window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2601,"title":"Chapter 2601 Thoughtful Lin Yuan!","paragraphs":["2601 Thoughtful Lin Yuan!","Lin Yuan felt a link form between the young girl and the fountain of faith in his divine kingdom while the woman directly became his believer!","It turned out that Su Yiren not only ensured that the regular citizens and homeless people in the Sand Island Continent were well fed but also dispatched a group of healing-type spirit qi professionals to heal them.","The homeless people and regular citizens in the Sand Island Continent did not possess many personal possessions, so the healing had to be free.","Lin Yuan felt that he should give Su Yiren more resources. She would definitely use them in the right places.","Lin Yuan and Eternal Source rushed to the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift while he observed the environment around him.","Even Eternal Source could not help but marvel at how the Sand Island Continent had changed.","Lin Yuan took out the Thoughts Letter Paper and saw that Su Yiren had been periodically reporting the situation in the Sand Island Continent and Dark Continent to him.","From what Lin Yuan just saw, the situation in the Sand Island Continent was even better than what Su Yiren had described.","Lin Yuan thought for a while before he sent a message to Su Yiren.","[Lin Yuan]: I am in the Sand Island Continent now. It is being managed well! I will have Wo Lun ship 1,500 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of various types, 5,000 tonnes of energy ores, 2,000 Bronze/Epic and 100 Bronze/Legend feys of various types, as well as 50,000 bottles of Grade 4 potions to you. Furthermore, I will leave Di Wanmi with you for now. If you need anything done, let her handle it.","Lin Yuan had his reasons for providing Su Yiren with so many resources.","All of these resources would be able to cause a stir in any federation. They were all top resources. It would be difficult for even a Class 5 Creation Master to produce them within 80 to 100 years.","There was no need for Lin Yuan to hide anything from his own people.","Since Su Yiren could manage two continents, Lin Yuan could provide her with a stable platform to do so.","After all, these resources were not that important to him.","Di Wanmi was the first Class 5 Creation Master subordinate Lin Yuan had gained. She represented invaluable strategic significance.","But now, Sky City had numerous Class 5 Creation Masters. The Goddess of Mercy could also be considered a member of Sky City.","As such, Di Wanmi was no longer as important as she used to be.","Lin Yuan could now produce Creation Master resources beyond the capabilities of Class 5 and 6 Creation Masters.","Although Di Wanmi was no longer as precious to Lin Yuan as she used to be, Su Yiren would be so delighted that her jaw might dislocate from smiling.","Su Yiren had contracted a Vitality Sloth in order to do her best as a manager. If she spent time sleeping, it would be difficult for her to achieve everything she needed.","Now, she only slept two hours a day while the other 22 hours were spent trying to recover the Dark Continent and protect the Sand Island Continent. It could be said that she had spent the past two months working tirelessly.","Su Yiren was accustomed to telling Lin Yuan about every single little achievement she made. It was her way of recording her achievements as well as demonstrating her value.","Just as Su Yiren was about to tell Lin Yuan about her results in the Dark Continent, she received a very long message from him.","Su Yiren was over the moon when she received this message. She loved it when Lin Yuan praised her.","But when she got to the bottom of the message, she placed both hands on the table to steady herself for fear she might faint.","The resource the Dark Continent lacked the most was energy ores. 5,000 tonnes of energy ores would be able to sustain development in the Dark Continent for almost two years.","Seventh Page War was horrible and had stripped the Dark Continent of almost all of its energy ores in the past few years. Thus, the Dark Continent did not have many left.","Lin Yuan needed to provide the Dark Continent with energy ores to help it develop continuously.","He had already provided Su Yiren with a significant amount of resources. She could not bring herself to ask him for more.","Besides the resources that were necessary for the Dark Continent’s development, Lin Yuan also provided her with 1,500 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls of various types as well as 2,000 Bronze/Epic and 100 Bronze/Legend feys of various types. These top resources would significantly raise the level of the Dark Continent’s experts.","The Dark Continent did not have many Creation Masters left, as any somewhat capable Creation Master had already fled. This was a massive blow to the Dark Continent’s foundation.","If Lin Yuan only provided the Bronze/Epic and Bronze/Legend feys, Su Yiren would not have the resources to nurture them. However, he also provided her with potions.","He was so thoughtful!","Furthermore, he also assigned a Class 5 Creation Master subordinate to her! Su Yiren could not be more aware of the significance of a Class 5 Creation Master!","Her grandmother had been a Class 5 Creation Master. Thanks to her, the fighting in the Dark Continent had stopped, and the seven federations could unite and grow together.","Since Lin Yuan had sent Di Wanmi to her, it meant he would not recall Di Wanmi anytime soon.","Having a Class 5 Creation Master meant she would have a stable source of high-class Creation Master resources. But more importantly, she would be able to motivate the people and give hope to the people in the Dark Continent who had chosen to submit to her.","Su Yiren could clearly tell that these people had been rather demoralized, and she had yet to devise an effective way to lift their spirits.","It was easy to talk about motivation but difficult to actually enact it!","But now, she finally had a good way of motivating them.","Su Yiren hurriedly sent a message to Lin Yuan to thank and assure him she would not let him down. She also became resolute in her plans to develop both the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent.","After checking the time, Su Yiren decided to hold the second imperial meeting since returning to the Dark Continent.","The previous meeting had been to cement her position as the ruler of the Dark Continent. Su Yiren hoped that this meeting would allow the Dark Continent to light up with hope.","She also wanted to eliminate all those who refused to cooperate. She did not want Lin Yuan’s resources to go to the likes of them!"]},{"number":2602,"title":"Chapter 2602 Wait for Just Ten Minutes!","paragraphs":["2602 Wait for Just Ten Minutes!","After making her decision and sending out the notification, Su Yiren said to two of the Samsara Realm Dictators Lin Yuan had left with her, “Shocking Flame and Piercing Horn, I will be relying on you later. Just kill whoever I tell you to!”","They felt concerned when Lin Yuan assigned them to Su Yiren, interpreting it as a form of exclusion. Although they weren’t the mightiest abyss demons in the Samsara Realm, they weren’t weak either.","Shocking Flame and Piercing Horn did not know why Lin Yuan had chosen them out of all the abyss demons.","Regardless of how important the jobs that Su Yiren gave them were, they would have more opportunities remaining by Lin Yuan’s side.","Although Shocking Flame and Piercing Horn had some grumbles, they dared not disobey Su Yiren. If they did and she complained about them, they would be doomed!","“Okay, please let us know of any requests that you have. We will do as you ask.”","Su Yiren felt herself relax. She had been struggling to figure out how to deal with the former associates of the Seven States of Darkness.","Su Yiren could only make this decision because of the resources Lin Yuan had provided.","Many of these former associates had worked with her grandmother and could be seen as her elders. They might have served her grandmother faithfully and for the benefit of the Seven States of Darkness in the past, but now they were working for Su Yiren and could influence how she managed the organization.","It was only at this moment that Su Yiren realized she had to be tough.","–","Su Yiren’s attendants had conveyed her orders, and she arrived promptly at the imperial meeting.","As she walked into the room for the important imperial meeting, she noticed that the long table, set to accommodate over 100 people, was only halfway occupied. About 20 to 30 individuals were still missing.","She had not contacted the ones she had sent out and were tied up to attend this imperial meeting. Everyone she had informed had more than enough time to arrive and take part in the gathering.","Their absence was evidently linked to their attitudes.","After Su Yiren looked around and made a note of who had not arrived, she told Shocking Flame, “If these people don’t arrive in the next ten minutes, you can go ahead and kill them. For the sake of the completeness of the imperial meeting, I can wait another ten minutes from the set start time.”","Su Yiren turned and sat down in her seat.","Her words caused the expressions of those there to subtly change. A few thought they were lucky for coming early and avoiding Su Yiren’s anger. Others sighed, waiting to see if she would follow through on her threat.","A group stood up, ready to ask permission to leave and bring those who hadn’t come yet.","As the new ruler of the Seven States of Darkness, there was no way that Su Yiren would make an empty threat. Those who had not shown up were in deep trouble!","Upon seeing those people standing and preparing to leave, Su Yiren knocked on the table and said coldly, “Whoever leaves now will go right to the end of the table when they return. You can leave if you want.”","Ranking was very important in the Seven States of Darkness. Their seat determined the amount of power that they wielded. Power equated to profit, and no one here wanted to risk losing profit.","Their reason for not turning up to the imperial meeting on time was very simple. All of them wanted to undercut her authority at this second imperial meeting. Thus, to them, arriving half an hour late would also be considered early!","After waiting for ten minutes, Su Yiren instructed Shocking Flame to close the door and began the meeting.","Since these people were willing to respect her enough to arrive at the imperial meeting on time, she was also willing to give those who were not fully cooperative a chance to change.","During the imperial meeting, Su Yiren outlined her expectations for the development of the Dark Continent and acknowledged those who had truly worked hard for her.","At that moment, cries of despair echoed outside the door.","Most of these cries were familiar, making it evident that Su Yiren hadn’t made idle threats. Those who had arrived late were now facing the consequences she had warned them about!","The room’s occupants grew visibly pale. Even those who had previously challenged her authority were forced to take her seriously. Regardless of whether they respected her, she had the power to end their lives effortlessly. If they continued to oppose her, they risked meeting the same fate as those outside the room.","Many absent from the imperial meeting had influential backgrounds, which had given them the audacity to skip it.","However, Su Yiren remained indifferent to their connections and pedigrees.","Once she made the aims of the Dark Continent’s development clear, Su Yiren tapped on the surface of the table and said seriously, “You are all holding pens and were taking notes while I was speaking. Liu Xi, collect all of their notes later. I want to see if they are clear on all of my requests!”","Su Yiren’s words caused the expressions of numerous people to change. Many of them had only been going through the motions and had not been taking notes seriously. A few of them were even doodling.","When Su Yiren saw this, she would definitely be displeased. If she wanted to kill someone to make an example out of them, they would definitely be picked!","Liu Xi was a poppy fruit from the Love Music Center that Su Yiren showed special favor to because she showed a very strong talent for governance. As such, Su Yiren brought her around as a close attendant.","When Liu Xi received Su Yiren’s orders, she stood up and smiled at the people sitting around the table as she said, “Your Majesty, I will collect them now! You weren’t speaking quickly at all. Those who are sincere would definitely have been able to follow. Those who are ingenuine wouldn’t know how to come up with something now even if they wanted to!”","Liu Xi then stepped away from Su Yiren’s left side and started to collect the meeting notes. She walked around the table until she arrived at Su Yiren’s right side and placed the notes neatly in front of her before she returned to her original seat.","Liu Xi knew that her words had offended many people, but she did not care. Su Yiren was the one who had given her her life as a poppy fruit. All she needed to do was follow Su Yiren’s instructions."]},{"number":2603,"title":"Chapter 2603 Changes in the Dark Continent!","paragraphs":["2603 Changes in the Dark Continent!","Liu Xi was linked to Su Yiren’s sacred source lifeform’s ability, so she could be considered a part of Su Yiren.","This was how every poppy fruit saw herself.","With everyone watching her, Su Yiren flipped through the meeting notes and separated them into three piles.","When she was done looking through all of the meeting notes, she knocked on the table and cleared her throat before saying, “Liu Xi, hand out this stack. All those who receive one, stand up.”","Liu Xi received the pile and distributed it.","There were a total of ten people who received a set, and none of them were worried as they stood there. They had made detailed notes of the arrangements that Su Yiren had outlined during the meeting.","Su Yiren could only be intending to reward them!","Once Liu Xi was done distributing the pile of notes, Su Yiren stood up as well.","Any federation with a Class 5 Creation Master would not follow the regular system and gain authority based on their ranking during imperial meetings. Instead, members of royalty would be established and become the federation’s core.","“From now on, the Seven States of Darkness will be renamed the Dark Federation. All those standing will become the Dark Federation’s members of royalty!”","Su Yiren’s words caused everyone in the meeting room to freeze. Everyone looked at each other regardless of whether they were sitting or standing.","Was it so easy to select members of royalty?","Four of the ten who were standing did not believe they were sufficiently powerful to handle the role of a member of royalty.","Members of royalty needed to hold up their titles with martial force. Otherwise, no one would listen to what they had to say!","If Su Yiren made them into members of royalty, she would definitely run up against significant obstacles in the future.","Nonetheless, it was good for them to be selected by Su Yiren!","At this moment, Su Yiren spoke again. “Besides announcing the members of royalty, I also need to make another announcement. The Dark Federation has a Class 5 Creation Master again! Those who are chosen to become members of royalty will be able to receive Class 5 Creation Master resources! Everyone will be given three Bronze/Legend feys and 30 Bronze/Epic feys to contract and nurture.”","Su Yiren’s words caused the meeting room to erupt into shouts. Her words were too astonishing.","It turned out that she had such impressive capabilities and even had a Class 5 Creation Master supporting her! It was no wonder she was confident enough to establish members of royalty!","Those whom Su Yiren had picked to be members of royalty pressed their lips together tightly. They had not expected this meeting to change their lives!","None of them had even been able to lay eyes on Bronze/Legend feys before! Now, not only could they contract such feys but would also be able to receive Class 5 Creation Master resources.","If they possessed Class 5 Creation Master resources, they would be able to surpass the rest rapidly and cement their positions as members of royalty.","Rather than saying that Su Yiren had picked members of royalty, it was more accurate to say that she was creating them.","Those who stood up were over the moon, while those who were not standing felt worse than if they were being punished. If they had known that such benefits were in store, they would have written down every word Su Yiren uttered! But now, it was too late, and all the positions had been assigned.","Moreover, they would no longer be able to enjoy any special treatment or authority in the Dark Federation once this meeting was over. They would have no power to influence any important decisions in the Dark Federation.","Su Yiren placed the last set of meeting notes in Liu Xi’s hands.","“Give this pile out. The ones who receive a set will be able to keep their family estates and continue leading their families. Those who did not receive a set of meeting notes belong in this pile. These people will have their family estates confiscated.","“However, I will give you a chance. From today onward, you will be sent to the Sand Island Continent, where you will be able to build up your families again.”","Su Yiren had made her arrangements in the span of two or three statements. It seemed as though she had made these statements casually, but they were actually decisions she had made after careful consideration.","To follow Lin Yuan’s order to develop the Sand Island Continent, she needed to shift some of her manpower there.","Normally, no faction from the Dark Federation would be willing to leave all they had accomplished in the Dark Continent and start over in the Sand Island Continent.","The Dark Continent had a tropical climate and was only lacking mineral resources. They had just as many resources as any other large continent.","On the other hand, the Sand Island Continent had a sand environment. Not only did it lack mineral resources, but it was also difficult to even procure food. The general view of the Sand Island Continent was that it was a barren land.","Su Yiren had to find a reasonable segue to carry out her plan, and this was her best chance. By sending these factions to the Sand Island Continent, it would be given a new lease on life.","Both those who had received meeting notes from the second pile and those who had not received one were very unhappy with Su Yiren’s arrangement.","However, Piercing Horn had already released his Samsara Realm Dictator aura, so no one dared to speak out. Anyone who had the audacity to speak now would end up with the same fate as those outside the room!","Su Yiren did not know she had picked up Lin Yuan’s habit of knocking on the table because of all her time with him.","“Is anyone displeased with my arrangement? This will be the last of such meetings, so you can speak if there’s anything that you don’t find satisfactory.”","Those who had complaints all felt shivers run up their backs. They all felt that she was baiting them. If they spoke now, there was no way they would receive a positive result.","As no one spoke, Su Yiren decided to end the meeting. But right before that, she said, “Those who I picked out as members of royalty will stay while the rest can leave. You should know what to do based on the instructions I just gave out!”","When Su Yiren was done speaking, she took out a piece of paper and mapped out her plans for the Dark Continent’s development.","The Iron Hammer, Divine Wood, and Great Lush Federations had all chosen their individual envoys.","Su Yiren used to be a Dark Envoy and intended to choose five Dark Envoys to participate in the upcoming Major Federation Meeting.","This would declare to the other federations that the Dark Federation had been revived. At the very least, the Dark Federation would not be pushed to the bottom of the pyramid like the Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations."]},{"number":2604,"title":"Chapter 2604 Demon Insect Palace!","paragraphs":["2604 Demon Insect Palace!","Su Yiren was very intelligent, and intelligent people always understood their own circumstances.","Back when she was still by Lin Yuan’s side, she had been more important than Luo Lan in terms of capabilities and function.","But now that she was overseeing the Dark and Sand Island Continents, she was no longer by Lin Yuan’s side. Thus, her status and function were the same as that of Luo Lan.","It was not just Luo Lan. Su Yiren also felt there was not much difference between her and Yi Huailong and Jin Qianxun. All of them were competing in the same field as they were all managing federations.","Although Su Yiren was managing more and larger federations, requiring more resources, she did not want the Dark Federation’s development to fall behind any of the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations. She did not care that the three federations had begun developing earlier than the Dark Federation.","She had picked ten members of royalty and assigned roles to them. Clearly, these ten people would play pivotal roles in the federation’s development.","Since she was the one who had chosen them, she would have to teach them slowly and personally.","After the rest left, Su Yiren gestured for the ten people to sit next to her.","Next, she distributed the meeting notes and said softly, “Your diligent recording of my expectations for the Dark Continent’s development was what earned you this chance. Now, I need to know where each of your skills lie.","“As members of royalty, you will not only receive the associated benefits but will also have to shoulder the required responsibilities and duties. From now on, someone will watch over you. I hope you won’t disappoint me and make me think I chose the wrong people.”","Everyone turned stern when they heard what Su Yiren said.","All of the people who were sitting there and had been taking notes seriously were those who had sincerely submitted to Su Yiren.","Now, Su Yiren was also promising them this mountain of benefits. There was no reason for those present not to do their best in carrying out the responsibilities and duties that came with being members of royalty.","It could be said that before today, none of these people believed they had such capabilities.","All of them reported their skills to Su Yiren, and she wrote them down seriously. Liu Xi also stood next to Su Yiren and made notes.","It took five hours for Su Yiren to fully digest and delegate the roles of these ten members of royalty.","Lin Yuan had sent her almost 20 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators, and Su Yiren decided to assign one to each member. This was to ensure their safety and watch over them as they performed their duties.","After sending them away, Su Yiren reached out and rubbed her temples as she felt a wave of exhaustion roll over her.","She was exhausted despite having contracted the Vitality Sloth. This was proof of how drained she was.","But as tired as she was, she did not head off to rest. Instead, she came up with three proposals to plan how she would develop the Sand Island and Dark Continents in the shortest amount of time.","...","While Su Yiren was drawing up her proposals, Lin Yuan had arrived at the entrance of the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift.","Currently, there were two Turning Wheel Realm Dictators standing next to the entrance to prevent anyone from the Sand Island Continent from entering the alien insect world.","The Turning Wheel Realm Dictators recognized Lin Yuan and Eternal Source.","Keira had become loyal to Lin Yuan and had absolute control over all the alien insects through their Genetic Locks.","Keira had purposefully and carefully memorized Lin Yuan’s appearance to ensure that no alien insect would mistakenly clash with him.","She could change the will of the alien insects by manipulating their Genetic Locks. The alien insect species now saw Lin Yuan as a god.","When the two Turning Wheel Realm Dictators saw Lin Yuan, they hurriedly knelt and paid their respects to him like alien insects with the inferior Class 3 Genetic Locks paid their respects to the female insects.","After Lin Yuan nodded to the two Turning Wheel Realm Dictators, he entered the alien insect world while riding on Eternal Source.","Before Lin Yuan had left, he had ordered Keira to relocate the alien insects’ nest near the entrance of the dimensional rift.","Keira had earnestly carried out Lin Yuan’s order.","Immediately after entering the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift, Lin Yuan spotted the insect empresses’ nests.","In the past few months, Keira had reorganized the alien insects with the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift at the center.","Now that Keira had successfully recovered, there was no need for the alien insects’ inheritance ground.","Keira had built a tall nest for herself, and alien insects were usually not allowed to enter. Even the insect empresses had to give their reports outside of the nest.","Eternal Source did not retract his aura while carrying Lin Yuan, so any alien insect that was somewhat powerful could sense Eternal Source and Lin Yuan’s presence.","With Mexa at the front, the alien insects gathered to welcome Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan could see alien insects bowing to him in every corner of his line of vision. The feeling left him breathless as he swept his gaze across this scene!","But soon, he furrowed his brow. He did not see Keira.","Keira should be even more excited than the insect empresses about his arrival.","Lin Yuan asked Mexa, “Where is Keira? Take me to her now.”","Mexa hurriedly said, “Lord Lin Yuan, Mother is in her Demon Insect Palace. We don’t have the right to enter the Demon Insect Palace, so we have no idea what she is doing at this moment. I can take you to the entrance of the Demon Insect Palace, and you can enter on your own!”","Lin Yuan was quietly shocked. He was witnessing the extent of control of the Genetic Locks over the alien insects.","Mexa had addressed Keira as ‘Mother’. From the attitudes of the other alien insects, it seemed that being able to call Keira ‘Mother’ was a privilege!","That was the truth. Keira had given Mexa this privilege because she had sensed that Mexa had distinguished herself to Lin Yuan. She had even given part of the might of the Demon Insect Lock Decoder to Mexa, making her more powerful than the other alien insects!","“Okay, take me to the Demon Insect Palace.”","Lin Yuan was not afraid that Keira had stopped cowering in respect for him. He had taken full control of her. As long as she was intelligent, she would know what the right attitude to take would be.","He was worried that something bad had happened to her."]},{"number":2605,"title":"Chapter 2605 Peace’s Request!","paragraphs":["2605 Peace’s Request!","If anything happened to Keira, Lin Yuan would suffer a great loss. After all, he had plans to use the demon insects heavily.","Lin Yuan intended to bring Liu Jie, but the latter had already entered the Midnight Palace’s seclusion. He was going to try and contact a few new insect-species carcinoma feys while transforming his current ones into fairies.","Since Liu Jie had already made his plans, Lin Yuan did not take him into the alien insect world.","With Mexa and the other insect empresses surrounding him, Lin Yuan arrived at the entrance of the Demon Insect Palace.","He took out the Spinning Chrysalis and instructed Mexa to protect it before he left it at the entrance of the palace.","Soon after, the Spinning Chrysalis rooted itself in the alien insect world’s ground. Then, a fuzzy carpet of fungi appeared below it and began spreading outward. The alien insects that made contact with the fungi swiftly fell under the Spinning Chrysalis’ control.","Now that the Spinning Chrysalis had begun working, Lin Yuan entered the Demon Insect Palace.","Once he entered, he heard Keira’s weak spiritual communication. “Lord Lin Yuan, I did not expect you to come at such a time. I am currently attempting to birth the first batch of demon insect eggs. The birthing process can’t be stopped once it starts. If it is forcefully halted, I might not be able to retain my status as a female insect! Is it possible for you to wait for me?”","Keira spoke with a nervous tone.","Demon insects abided by the law of the jungle, so those of lower status could not make those of higher status wait for them.","However, Keira was afraid that stopping the birthing process would cause her to suffer irreparable consequences. If she lost her function as a female insect, she would not only be unable to build up the demon insect species but might also lose the ability to activate the Demon Insect Lock Decoder!","There were numerous new demon insects who met with accidents and lost their female insect abilities.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the demon insects’ enemies had discovered this characteristic and constantly picked fights when the new females were laying eggs. Otherwise, the demon insects would not have deteriorated to such a degree!","Lin Yuan did not blame Keira. Instead, he asked seriously, “Given your current situation, do you need any help? You can speak freely. I will wait for you outside so you can relax and lay the eggs!”","Lin Yuan pulled out a chair and sat down. He took out the Thoughts Letter Paper and started communicating with the members of the Astronomical Parliament. He told them all about the main world’s current situation.","Lin Yuan had already gained an understanding of the Sleeper’s Revival plan, so he needed to ensure that the Astronomical Parliament’s members were prepared as well.","Su Yiren’s eyes widened when she saw Lin Yuan’s message, and she immediately made adjustments to her plans.","She was certain that the Dark Continent was not equipped to handle Tower Canon’s plan in its current state.","She intended to migrate every person from the Dark Federation to a location nearer to the Radiance Federation. The sooner she did this, the better she would be able to protect the Dark Federation’s citizens.","Since Lin Yuan had left the Sand Island Continent in her care, Su Yiren also needed to prepare for it.","When Yin Lin saw the message, she told her parents and grandfather about it. She did not leverage her identity as an Azure Envoy to report it to the Azure Federation’s imperial court.","Yin Lin had great faith in the friendship between the Radiance Federation and Azure Federation. There was no way that the Radiance Federation would hide such a matter from the Azure Federation.","As such, rather than trying to earn a reward from the Azure Federation, bringing the Azure Federation and Radiance Federation closer would be better.","Yin Lin did not know how the Azure Federation’s imperial court would react once they found out about this matter. But she was going to try to persuade her parents and grandfather to suggest to the imperial court to migrate the citizens of the Azure Federation.","The Azure Federation had struggled to even deal with the opening of the Class 6 water world dimensional rift. Given the circumstances, the best plan of action would be to band together.","Yin Lin had witnessed Lin Yuan’s strength.","If the Azure Federation united with the Radiance Federation, more federations would be induced to gather together with the Radiance Federation as well. They would eventually form a coalition of humans who would work together to take on Tower Canon’s evil scheme.","They would then take back their territories in the main world and move back once the storm had blown over.","Wo Lun, Bu Po, Luo Lan, and Peace had exactly the same thoughts.","Wo Lun did not feel strongly about the Violent Wind Federation. Since he had almost died once, nothing was more important to him than his safety. He was already prepared to relocate himself and his ship’s crew.","Wo Lun would not report such a matter to the Violent Wind Federation.","The Violent Wind Federation had a Class 5 Creation Master, so the opinions of peasants meant nothing. The decision-makers in the Violent Wind Federation’s imperial court might not believe him and might even arrest him.","Wo Lun did not want to deal with something so troublesome. After all, when things became serious, the Violent Wind Federation would catch wind of the news and decide.","Luo Lan’s thinking matched that of Su Yiren and intended to move the citizens of the Iron Hammer Federation nearer to the Radiance Federation. She also sent the information to Yi Huailong and Jin Qianxun.","Wo Lun and Luo Lan were able to make decisions on their own.","On the other hand, Bu Po had become the only remaining Spirit Mother reserve disciple but was not able to make decisions on the Spirit Mother’s behalf. He needed to tell the Spirit Mother about this matter.","But after their previous interaction, he did not need to be evasive in front of the Spirit Mother and could speak his mind.","After making their decisions, Wo Lun, Luo Lan, and Bu Po did not feel much pressure about this disaster.","However, Peace immediately felt crushed by the pressure.","There were very few places in the world with a higher death rate than the Broiling Rock Continent.","Peace was currently trying to develop the city and was seen as the Green Continent Goddess who could solve the city’s water scarcity issue.","But just because she could solve the city’s water scarcity issue, that did not mean she could deal with the dead spirits that rose from the ground.","The others could make migration plans, but Peace had only just made contact with the cities outside of the Green Continent City. She had no idea where the other members of the Astronomical Parliament were located and could not migrate to Lin Yuan’s location even if she wanted to.","If this was any other matter, Peace would handle it alone. But she knew she would not be able to address this situation on her own!","If she tried to address this situation, she would be jeopardizing the safety of the Green Continent City’s citizens!","Peace solemnly sent a message to Lin Yuan on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Peace]: Leo, after reading your message, I would like to migrate the residents of the Green Continent City to the Radiance Federation you mentioned! Are you able to zero in on the Green Continent City’s location in the Broiling Rock Continent so I know which direction to go toward?","When Lin Yuan saw Peace’s message, he did not panic."]},{"number":2606,"title":"Chapter 2606 Revival of the Demon Insects!","paragraphs":["2606 Revival of the Demon Insects!","Ever since Wen Yu arrived at the Grotto Continent, she told Lin Yuan she could clearly sense that she was nearer to Peace.","If that were the case, Lin Yuan would be able to meet Peace soon!","Wen Yu and Bei Xu were currently exploring the other side of the Barren Sea. They would eventually reach Peace’s location.","Lin Yuan believed that Peace was worried sick. Otherwise, given his understanding of Peace, she would never voluntarily ask him for help unless she had no other choice.","Lin Yuan intended to soothe the distraught Peace.","[Lin Yuan]: Peace, you don’t have to panic. I am aware of your situation. I will be able to help you with your situation soon.","Lin Yuan sent this message. But he remembered that Peace always lacked a sense of security and went on to explain things to her seriously.","[Lin Yuan]: Libra can locate you based on the constellations. We have already found Bei Xu. Previously, we were unable to find the Grotto Continent, where Bei Xu is located. This also goes for the Broiling Rock Continent. After arriving at the Grotto Continent, Libra noticed that she is nearer to you and is now able to sense you clearer than before. I will send Libra to meet up with you and help with the migration. Once the danger has been resolved, you can choose to continue developing in this thriving continent or return to the Green Continent City to continue striving toward your current goal!","Lin Yuan’s guess was right. His initial explanation had not been enough to assure Peace.","Peace always lacked a sense of security. Despite knowing Lin Yuan would never lie to her, she still found it difficult to feel assured by a simple explanation.","But Lin Yuan’s next message gave her solid assurance.","Peace finally relaxed and looked forward to Wen Yu’s arrival.","She could use this time to gather resources in the Green Continent City so as to prevent wasting resources when the time came to migrate.","After growing up in the Broiling Rock Continent, Peace saw wastage as the worst habit.","In other continents, resources could be easily found and harvested in the wild. But in the Broiling Rock Continent, resources were as important as one’s life!","After communicating with Peace, Lin Yuan spoke with the other members of the Astronomical Parliament before storing the Thoughts Letter Paper back in the spatial equipment.","The members of the Astronomical Parliament immediately began busying themselves with preparing for the impending crisis.","Bu Po hesitated for a while before he went to the Spirit Mother and solemnly described the situation.","Bu Po’s words immediately caused the Spirit Mother’s usual nonchalant expression to falter. “Little Po, are you sure that this information is accurate?”","Bu Po nodded seriously. “I can take responsibility for my words! You are the Spirit Mother of the Spirit Mother Federation, not me. What you choose to do after getting this information will not have anything to do with me. I won’t interfere. But if you choose to fortify the Spirit Mother Federation, I will leave with my sister. I hope you won’t force me to stay.”","Mountain Ridge Source was still on Bu Po’s body, so he had the confidence to communicate with the Spirit Mother without worrying that the latter would try to force him using martial force.","If what Bu Po said was true and this was Tower Canon’s plan, the organization behind him should be aware of this!","...","Lin Yuan had just kept the Thoughts Letter Paper away when he heard Keira calling him. “Lord, are you able to give me some pure spirit qi? If you do, I will do my best to repay you in the future!”","Once the words fell from her lips, Keira realized she had misspoken.","Her life and soul were now fully in Lin Yuan’s hands. Since she fully belonged to Lin Yuan, how could she speak of repaying him?","Normally, Keira should not require so much pure energy to lay the first eggs.","Lin Yuan had provided a significant amount of pure energy the last time.","Keira used the vitality to strengthen herself so her demon insect genes would improve. Thus, she had used up most of the spirit qi that Lin Yuan had given her.","She was only able to gain the chance to lay eggs so soon because her demon insect genes had been refined.","Keira brimmed with immense ambition and had injected the pure spirit qi into every egg that she had laid.","A demon insect that had revived had the greatest talent and potential. Their strength determined how strong the species they created would be. A strong demon insect would have hundreds of times the power of a weak one. They could not be compared!","This amount of pure spirit qi should have been sufficient based on Keira’s calculations.","However, she had overlooked her enhanced Genetic Lock, which would lead to increased egg production. She also intended to infuse pure spirit qi into the remaining eggs, ensuring the optimal development of the demon insect species.","Even though Lin Yuan had been casual about pure spirit qi, its worth was undeniable. Keira’s request seemed inappropriate and ignorant!","Additionally, it hadn’t been long since Lin Yuan generously provided her with a substantial amount of pure spirit qi.","If Lin Yuan perceived this as wasteful, it could lead to trouble for Keira!","While Keira felt increasingly anxious, Lin Yuan was elated.","Keira’s growing need for spirit qi indicated her increasing strength.","At present, what Lin Yuan lacked the most was time. Lin Yuan was delighted that Keira could quickly boost her power and enhance the insect species.","While Keira cherished pure spirit qi, Lin Yuan saw it as mere resources.","“Let me enter. This way, I can provide you with as much spirit qi as you need.”","Instead of immediately entering the Demon Insect Palace, Lin Yuan paused and directed his attention toward it, signaling that he awaited Keira’s input.","This action instantly filled Keira with a sense of respect for Lin Yuan."]},{"number":2607,"title":"Chapter 2607 Breaking the Demon Insects’ Historical Record!","paragraphs":["2607 Breaking the Demon Insects’ Historical Record!","Keira said gratefully, “Lord, I respectfully invite you to come in! I am extremely grateful for your help!”","The Genetic Locks brought the demon insect species into existence. Despite no Genetic Lock binding Lin Yuan and Keira, her loyalty to him equaled the security of such a bond. She had vowed allegiance to Lin Yuan with her soul.","Yearning for the admiration and favor of those one stood by was a common human desire.","Lin Yuan granted her plea and treated her with great respect. He committed to providing an ample supply of pure spirit qi, as much as she required.","Should her initial set of eggs be nurtured by pure spirit qi, the species she birthed could shatter historical records among demon insects!","Upon receiving Keira’s response, Lin Yuan entered the cave.","Before long, he encountered a feeble Keira lying on a stone platform.","Though the empress of demon insects, Keira consistently retained a human form, concealing her true appearance.","In actuality, Keira assumed the shape of an insect, a spider to be precise, boasting 16 legs.","Keira adamantly clung to her human form, regardless of her weakness, unless she faced imminent death.","Arranged beside her were four rows of insect legs, each housing 18 eggs, summing up to 72 eggs.","Evidently, the first quartet of eggs within the initial three rows radiated stronger auras than their counterparts.","Keira started softly explaining to Lin Yuan, “Lord, I am asking pure spirit qi from you so I can strengthen these eggs. This will ensure they remain strong after hatching. To us demon insects, the first batch—”","Before Keira could finish speaking, Lin Yuan took out a handful of spirit qi crystals and relaxedly crushed them.","A powerful wave of spirit qi immediately surrounded the eggs, and they began greedily absorbing the spirit qi around them.","Lin Yuan saw that the first four eggs in the first, second, and third rows were also absorbing the spirit qi. This meant that the eggs that Keira had strengthened before had not yet reached their full potential.","Lin Yuan asked, “It is probably beneficial for these eggs to absorb their fill of spirit qi, right?”","Keira was stunned.","Absorb their fill? What did that mean?","Lin Yuan’s question stumped Keira.","None of the records of the demon insects mentioned the eggs having or not having their fill of spirit qi.","She could not give Lin Yuan an answer to a question she knew nothing about.","However, it would definitely be beneficial to the demon insect eggs to absorb more spirit qi.","With the pure spirit qi that Lin Yuan provided, he could only give one or two spirit qi crystals to every egg.","Keira could only nod timidly since she had no answer to Lin Yuan’s question.","When Lin Yuan saw Keira nod, he demonstrated a mountain of wealth so gigantic that Keira would never forget about it.","A small mountain of spirit qi crystals appeared next to Lin Yuan. He reached his hand in and crushed a few of the spirit qi crystals.","Then, almost as though he felt that he was not crushing the spirit qi crystals quickly enough, he stepped on the ground, and hundreds of granules of sand appeared below his feet and shaped themselves into a large hand.","Three hands of sand were formed, and they gathered around one egg and started crushing the spirit qi crystals.","The eggs that craved pure spirit qi badly all swelled when the spirit qi made contact with their shells.","Keira could not help but gulp.","It turned out that such immense wealth existed in the world!","If she had become loyal to Lin Yuan when she was still in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the demon insects would not have deteriorated to such a degree!","As time ticked away, the mountain of spirit qi crystals by Lin Yuan’s feet shrunk and grew three times.","Keira realized with shock that this first batch of 72 eggs had absorbed their maximum capacity of pure spirit qi!","This allowed her to write in the future history books of the demon insects that demon insect eggs indeed had a maximum capacity of spirit qi they could absorb!","After absorbing their fill, the eggs would not reject spirit qi but would stop absorbing it.","Moreover, the eggs that had absorbed their fill would become crystalized and radiate verdant light akin to that of jade-colored glass!","After absorbing the maximum capacity of spirit qi, the demon insects that hatched from these eggs would be longer and able to fly immediately after hatching.","Lin Yuan nodded with satisfaction when he was certain that the demon insect eggs could not absorb any more spirit qi.","He looked at Keira and said sternly, “I made a huge investment in the demon insects because I hope you will be able to develop them into an elite army of soldiers for me. If you have any needs in the future, you can inform me immediately. Don’t hinder the development of the demon insects!","“There will be many possible situations where I won’t be able to reach you in time if you don’t give me advance notice. For example, if I hadn’t come this time, developing the eggs in the best direction would have been difficult for you.”","After receiving Lin Yuan’s warning, Keira immediately felt as though she was living in a magical world. Her master did not chastise her for using too many resources. Rather, he wanted her to use even more.","In the past, Keira would never have dared to dream that such a master existed.","She and the demon insects would be blessed if she could remain by Lin Yuan’s side.","Keira said happily, “Master, I will remember what you said! From now on, I’ll just let you know if I have any needs.”","Now that Keira had taken his words to heart, he did not give her any more orders.","Instead, he said, “Go and recover yourself. I promised the alien insects to provide them with the chance to trade bloodlines. I came for this reason. You are controlling the entire alien insect species through the Genetic Locks, so you can take the lead on this matter.","“Don’t forget that both parties must be willing before the alien insects trade with any lifeform. You can’t force them. You can also make records of the genes obtained by the alien insects in the Demon Insect Lock Decoder.”","Keira stood up and said, “Master, I am not that weak. I will go and carry out your order now!”","Keira bowed deeply to Lin Yuan before saying seriously, “Under your leadership, the demon insects will definitely achieve true prosperity! The demon insects will work hard to become your strongest weapons!”"]},{"number":2608,"title":"Chapter 2608 Attacking the Sky-Plundering Beast!","paragraphs":["2608 Attacking the Sky-Plundering Beast!","Keira was sincere and straightforward. Even if she had been hypocritical, she would have been honest only with Lin Yuan, avoiding empty promises.","In the past, when Keira was uncertain about Lin Yuan’s circumstances, she wouldn’t have dared to claim that she could transform the demon insects into elite soldiers for him.","The demon insects were formidable, but Lin Yuan’s ability to produce such pure spirit qi amazed Keira.","She didn’t know much about Lin Yuan’s background, but she believed that he could command thousands of species to submit to him if he wished.","Countless species waged wars to acquire more pure spirit qi, yet what they obtained paled in comparison to Lin Yuan’s purity.","Keira’s confidence in making such a claim to Lin Yuan only stemmed from the significant qualitative transformation of the demon insects.","Lin Yuan smiled, appreciating Keira’s passion and determination. If the demon insects could genuinely progress in this direction, all his invested resources would not be in vain.","As Lin Yuan escorted Keira out of the Demon Insect Palace, the other insect empresses awaited them at the entrance.","The usually highly respected insect empresses now sincerely bowed to Lin Yuan.","Keira found this behavior odd—the insect empresses had clearly noticed her but hadn’t acknowledged her presence.","Her Genetic Lock had already taken full control of these insect empresses!","Keira did not know what method Lin Yuan had used to supersede her Genetic Lock’s control.","This was enough to make Lin Yuan seem increasingly mysterious to Keira.","Lin Yuan knew that this was happening because he had taken control of the alien insect world through the Spinning Chrysalis.","Keira’s roots were not in the alien insect world, so she was not affected by the Spinning Chrysalis.","Lin Yuan had instructed her to handle the alien insect’s trading of genes with other lifeforms. As such, Keira stepped forward and took on the attitude of a matriarch.","She spoke with the insect empresses and gave a concise version of Lin Yuan’s orders. She emphasized that both parties had to be agreeable before the trade could take place so that not only the alien insects would benefit.","Keira knew that the Dictators from the other dimensional worlds would definitely agree to trade with the alien insects due to Lin Yuan.","However, the number and frequency of the trades depended on whether the alien insects were willing to satisfy the Dictators from the other dimensional worlds.","Otherwise, regardless of how much potential the alien insects had, Lin Yuan could not take the blood of other species in order to strengthen the alien insects’ power.","He would not be considered an excellent elite leader if he did that.","The lines of authority in the alien insects depended on genes. As such, the obedience and degree of submission to orders was far greater than that of other species!","Lin Yuan’s orders did not take long to spread and be disseminated.","All of the female insects became excited at the prospect of using the genes of other species to produce stronger male insects.","The female insects were always cruel toward male insects and saw them as tools.","But all of them were romantics and liked to seek comfort in the male insects they birthed. They would then take in the male insects they favored as concubini.","It sounded impressive to be a concubinus, but a female insect could have as many concubini as it wanted.","It would have many other options if it lost interest in its current concubini. It could either keep its concubini without showing favor to them or eat them to turn them into its energy source, ending their short-lived relationship.","In order to prevent something like that, the concubini always did their best to curry favor with the female insects. Once they lost the favor of the female insects, they would not only lose their status but also risk losing their lives.","The female insects would never pick other dimensional lifeforms to become their concubini.","But the female insects could absorb the genes of other lifeforms and morph them to produce new male insects that they chose to become their concubini. They could have fun while having full control over the relationship.","This was the same excitement as a poor person waiting to hit the jackpot overnight or a geeky homebody waiting for new figurines.","The alien insect world, though somewhat lacking, held its own treasures. Providing satisfactory compensation to the other Dictators for their trades wouldn’t be a challenge.","After fulfilling his promise to the alien insects, Lin Yuan promptly left.","The Sky-Plundering Beast had been in Lin Yuan’s company for a while. It had a fondness for wood-elemental energy, vitality, and spirit qi, as these aided in its growth.","Resources in abundance were at Lin Yuan’s disposal.","Lin Yuan crafted a ten-square-foot garden in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and filled it with Sky-Plundering Flowers, a favorite of the Sky-Plundering Beast.","He allowed it to feast on as many Sky-Plundering Flowers as it desired, promoting its rapid growth.","Nourished by the pure spirit qi within the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the Sky-Plundering Beast underwent a transformation, much like Genius had. It evolved from a regular beast into a Normal grade fey.","Before this transformation, Lin Yuan formed a contract with the Sky-Plundering Beast, as he had done with Genius and Chimey.","The energy needed for this contract was negligible, leaving Lin Yuan unaffected. This deepened the bond between Lin Yuan and the Sky-Plundering Beast.","Lin Yuan’s genuine care for the beast touched its heart.","Genius, Chimey, and the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope all befriended the Sky-Plundering Beast. After millennia of solitude, it was no longer lonely.","However, the journey to strength wasn’t easy for the Sky-Plundering Beast.","Lin Yuan didn’t want to elevate its grade and quality until it fully regained peak health, as this might affect its potential. Such a premature evolution could hinder the Sky-Plundering Beast from attaining the best abilities and exclusive skills.","The Sky-Plundering Beast was obedient and good-natured. However, after spending a long time underground, it became curious about the surface world and started to explore everything.","Lin Yuan supported this curiosity.","It was important for the Sky-Plundering Beast to learn about the world."]},{"number":2609,"title":"Chapter 2609 Evolve! Acid Corrosion Queen Bee!","paragraphs":["2609 Evolve! Acid Corrosion Queen Bee!","However, the Sky-Plundering Beast did not have good life habits. It would defecate wherever it wanted in the garden once it had eaten its fill of the Sky-Plundering Flowers. As such, Lin Yuan had no choice but to train it in the right way to act, just like one would do with dogs and cats.","This reminded Lin Yuan of when he first started nurturing Genius and Chimey, and he felt very nostalgic.","After leaving the alien insect world, Lin Yuan summoned Purple Afterglow, the Rememberling, and the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom out at the entrance of the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift.","Once Purple Afterglow, the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom, and Rememberling evolved to Suzerain/Myth, Morbius would be able to evolve to Suzerain/Myth and gain new abilities and exclusive skills.","The Endless Gems had unlocked Purple Afterglow, Rememberling, and the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom so Lin Yuan could see their complete abilities and exclusive skills.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to ask Purple Afterglow and Rememberling which one of them wanted to evolve to Myth Breed first, he heard Red Thorn’s voice in his head. “Yuan, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, that disappointment, is finally able to evolve to Fantasy Breed! It is showing signs of comprehending a Willpower Rune. Come and help it!”","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was always adoringly obedient toward Red Thorn, but the latter could not care less about it.","But it did care about the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee at crucial moments! Otherwise, it would not ask Lin Yuan to help the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was part of Lin Yuan’s earliest batch of feys. Although he had not formed a contract with it, he controlled it via Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish, which was hosted within it.","Lin Yuan had not found the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee externally from the wild.","When he helped Millstone Town to defend against the pinnacle Class 1 dimensional rift, the Mother of Bloodbath had found the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee in the dimensional hub.","When Lin Yuan first started fighting on Star Web, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee had been his secret weapon.","But as time passed, its importance to Lin Yuan faded.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee needed to comprehend a Willpower Rune from nature. However, it showed no signs of any changes even after such a long time had passed. This had caused Lin Yuan to slowly forget about its existence.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, this forerunner, was finally going to comprehend a Willpower Rune and successfully move forward!","Lin Yuan hurriedly let Red Thorn’s original body out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Red Thorn’s Mouth of Relinquish grew increasingly larger as its power climbed. It looked very terrifying and ferocious.","The three furnace-like Mouths of Relinquish squeezed together and let out roars.","Five ramets that had mutated grew out next to the three Mouths of Relinquish. The ramets’ vines grabbed dimensional lifeform body after dimensional lifeform body in preparation to feed them to the Mouths of Relinquish.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee emerged from one of the Mouths of Relinquish and flew up to the sky.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s appearance had changed radically.","At that moment, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee seemed more like an invisible assassin than the mother of a species.","It would not be effective for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to charge forward recklessly.","But now, while it was evolving to Fantasy Breed, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s body expanded, and its abdomen also started to change.","After the transformation, its abdomen took up a larger proportion of its body, and the two stingers on its posterior also shortened.","This made the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee seem more like a queen bee.","However, this caused Lin Yuan to knit his brows.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s abilities Wing Stealth, Bone-Penetrating Stingers, Queen Bee’s Premature Death, and exclusive skill Two-Strike Kill were all ferocious abilities that it could rely on to do combat.","In its current state, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s wings could not increase its flying speed and were smaller and rounder than they used to be. This would make it very difficult for the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to use them in battle.","Abilities like Parasitic Pupa required the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to break through its enemies’ defenses in order to place the pupa parasite in the target’s body, thereby injuring the target from the inside out.","The Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s body had stopped changing, and a Willpower Rune full of life entered its body.","Lin Yuan hurriedly used True Data to check on the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","[Fey Name]: Acid Corrosion Queen Bee","[Fey Species]: Vespidae/Bactrocera","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Poison","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Wing Stealth]: Flaps its wings at high frequency. The fast-flapping reflective wings allow the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee to be stealthy.","[Bone-Penetrating Stingers]: The super hard and impactful rotating stingers rapidly cause deep injuries.","[Parasitic Pupa]: The stingers on the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee’s forelegs can release a fast-hatching parasitic pupa into the target’s body while stinging.","[Acid-Swallowing Larvae]: With sufficient acid, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee will hatch numerous Acid-Swallowing Larvae that can be used as food for it to rapidly restore its consumed energy and venom reserves. At the same time, the Acid-Swallowing Larvae will replicate part of the Acid-Swallowing Queen Bee’s mother genes so that if the latter dies, the former can activate the genes to become the new mother.","[Acid Corpse Poison Bee]: A large amount of acid in the body is consumed to produce an Acid Corpse Poison Bee, which will reside in the body of a dead lifeform or dimensional lifeform and control the latter’s actions. These Acid Corpse Poison Bees will turn into Poison Silkworm Pupae again if the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee does not activate them.","[Queen Bee’s Premature Death]: After the queen bee dies, the two types of venom in its posterior stingers will combine to explode its body. During the explosion, the combined venom will shoot out, and the target that comes into contact with the poison will trigger Two-Strike Kill.","[Two-Strike Kill]: The two abdominal stingers contain two different kinds of acid-corrosion venom. If the abdominal stingers hit the same part of the target, the two types of venom will instantly disintegrate the target’s part.","[Parasitic Acid Bee Colony]: Momentarily combine with the parasite home. A colony of bees will be quickly produced from the acid in the home. The colony of bees will inherit all abilities and exclusive skills that do not involve procreation."]},{"number":2610,"title":"Chapter 2610 Praying Universe Soul Whale!","paragraphs":["2610 Praying Universe Soul Whale!","As a soul-type fey, the Remembrance Soul Whale could not use its body to take on the World Cleansing just like Blackie did. If any of the World Cleansing’s attacks made contact with its body, it would be heavily injured.","Lin Yuan looked at Eternal Source, and he immediately flicked his fingers toward the hole in the sky.","A gold and green screen immediately appeared in front of the gold and green screen. All of the lightning strikes hit this screen but could not cause any damage to it.","Half an hour later, no more lightning emerged from the hole, and the World Grace started forming in the hole.","Eternal Source flicked toward the hole again, and a beam of energy shattered the screen.","The World Grace passed through the hole and landed on Rememberling’s body.","In an instant, Lin Yuan felt as though constellations had appeared in Rememberling’s body.","It was clear that Rememberling’s body had not grown larger, yet the constellations made it seem vast.","When the star patterns appeared on Rememberling’s horn, they formed a road of stars. The star patterns leaped out from the horn and swirled around the road of stars.","Rememberling’s wings had also grown larger and heavier.","Although they had both evolved, Rememberling had not had as hard of a time as Blackie.","At that moment, the evolving Rememberling let out a low cry as though it was enjoying a comfortable massage.","Rememberling’s aura had changed, and Lin Yuan was certain that it had evolved.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Rememberling.","[Fey Name]: Praying Universe Soul Whale","[Fey Species]: Soul whale-species/single-horned whale-species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Soul","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[Soul Knot]: When faced with the body of a dead target, singing the whale song will combine all the hidden souls in the body and awaken the soul within the target. If there is enough soul in the target’s body, the memories in the soul will be activated.","[Whale Fantasy]: When faced with an attack, the body can be turned into soul power and spread out into the surroundings. This will be able to dodge any attack. When heavily injured, the soul will attach itself to the closest object. Once out of danger, the soul can re-solidify into its original form.","[Singing Soul]: The soul energy will be spent, and the soul’s past experiences will be recited. This will help to recover the soul’s memories.","[Whale Soul Tears]: After consuming the fragments of the soul and draining the energy within them, the energy can be released through the eyes as sacred items and be used to heal and nourish souls.","[Sacred Whale Song]: When the sacred whale song is sung, curses placed on the soul will be broken. The impurities in the soul will also be cleansed.","[Whale Horn Piercing Crystal]: The whale horn will pick out souls hidden within non-lifeforms. Rememberling’s soul energy will begin to mold the soul pieces until they solidify into crystals that cannot be returned to the main body.","[Soul Universe Guide]: The whale horn can communicate with and make prayers to the universe. The collected souls can be guided to its side and universe power will be used to guide the souls while protecting them and preventing them from dissipating.","Exclusive Skill:","[Burning Soul New Life]: By using spiritual ingredients full of soul power, the soul energy can be directed to and solidified in the soul. The soul energy can be used to recover damaged souls and return them to whole.","[Soul Remember Gift]: By combining with the collected dead souls, the dead souls will eventually become soul imprints once they are completely absorbed. When the soul imprint is applied on a lifeform of the same species, the lifeform’s comprehension ability will be raised, and they will be able to comprehend willpowers and laws more easily.","[Universe Prayer]: Cry out in unison with the universe space through its own bloodline. This will earn the chance to communicate with the universe space. After sincerely praying, the whale’s tears will be the guide that calls the universe’s thoughts and wills to it as a form of direct compensation.","Lin Yuan saw that Rememberling’s name had changed to the Praying Universe Soul Whale. But its species was still Soul whale-species/single-horned whale-species.","From its name, Lin Yuan was in amazement.","The star patterns and road of stars on Rememberling’s body all aligned exactly with the expansive universe!","Lin Yuan looked closely at Rememberling’s abilities and exclusive skills.","Its original abilities and exclusive skills had not changed, but it had gained Soul Universe Guide and Universe Prayer.","Soul Universe Guide was an ability it gained when it reached Suzerain, while Universe Prayer was an exclusive skill it gained when it reached Myth Breed.","The names were enough to know that Rememberling’s bloodline was why it evolved to the Praying Universe Soul Whale.","Lin Yuan had initially assumed that Rememberling would have no more chances to increase its power and that its set of exclusive skills and abilities were already perfect.","But as its bloodline continued to evolve, Rememberling had turned into a fey that would be seen as a treasure even in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Soul Universe Guide would allow Rememberling to use its horn to communicate with the universe and pray to it. It would search for souls in all spaces of the universe, and the found souls would be called to its side.","In order to prevent the soul from dissipating or weakening during the guiding process, it would also be able to use universe power to protect the guided soul.","When Rememberling was searching for a lifeform’s soul, the lifeform’s soul would not have to be present to be revived.","Universe Prayer was the base for the ability Soul Universe Guide.","Universe Prayer allowed Rememberling to cry in unison with the universe space through its bloodline. This deepened its connection to the universe and earned it the chance to communicate with the universe as equals.","Rememberling would use its tears as the medium to gain compensation from the universe.","The experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds would also lose their loved ones through accidents.","With Rememberling’s abilities and exclusive skills, Lin Yuan now had the leverage to negotiate with the true experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","When Rememberling was done evolving, it was very tired as all the energy had been used up to evolve its bloodline.","Lin Yuan took out a pile of spirit qi crystals and soul-type spiritual ingredients to rejuvenate Rememberling.","Once it had nourished itself, Rememberling fell into a deep sleep.","Lin Yuan brought Rememberling back into the Spirit Lock spatial zone and came down from the high of his joy.","Next, he turned his attention to the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom. He was going to evolve it next!","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom had also evolved to Diamond X/Fantasy V. The abyssal world’s Endless Gems allowed him to unlock the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s abilities."]},{"number":2611,"title":"Chapter 2611 Thought-Separating Flames!","paragraphs":["2611 Thought-Separating Flames!","In the past, Lin Yuan had not paid much attention to the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s abilities. This was because he was too busy and did not have much time to rest.","But now that he was continuously collecting the Endless Gems and unlocking more and more feys, Lin Yuan slowly lost the anxiousness he felt when he first unlocked the Jasmine Lily.","Now, he finally had the time to observe the Diamond X/Fantasy V Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom and see the new abilities/","[Fey Name]: Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom","[Fey Species]: Parasitic fungus species/flaming fungus species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Fire","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Seeping Flames]: The flames will seep into the target’s mind, spirit, and soul through the heart and brain. The spirit and soul will begin to burn. If the flames begin to die out, it can absorb the energy from the heart and brain to reignite itself.","[Body-Penetrating Flames]: When burning the mind, spirit, and soul, the flames will also burn the body. The damage will be translated from the elemental form to the physical. Before the fire in its mind, spirit, and soul was extinguished, the flames afflicting the body will continue to cause harm.","[Thought-Separating Flames]: When burning the target’s mind, spirit, and soul, if the target’s mind, spirit, and soul has any thoughts or feelings linked to another lifeform, the thoughts will become a guide that allows the flames to extend.","[Strengthened Spores]: The fungi produced will be strengthened and be able to absorb and take control of more energy. The fungi will be deeply rooted in the target’s soul and be more difficult to remove.","[Truth Colony]: When questioning a target, the precise answers given will grow a truth colony. When the colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a truth mushroom. When the truth mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be forced to tell the truth, making it easier to obtain true answers to questions.","[False Colony]: When questioning a target, every lie told by the target will produce a false colony. When the false colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a false mushroom. When the false mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be unable to break while questioning, preventing them from answering questions.","Exclusive Skill:","[Honesty Reflects the Heart]: The spores will host themselves deep within the target’s spirit and soul and determine the genuinity of the target’s exterior.","[Crumbled Parasitic Cycle]: The bacterial strain will be sacrificed. After being sacrificed, the energy around it will crumble, along with other energy-containing entities.","Lin Yuan could not help but let out a soft gasp.","Rememberling had already given him an enormous pleasant surprise. But the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom had delighted him just as much.","As a fire-type fey, the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was more skewed toward functions rather than attacking.","Rememberling was Lin Yuan’s safety net for those around him, while the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was the tool he used to obtain accurate and true answers.","He had gotten a taste of the benefits of the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom when he used it on Eighth Page Apoptosis.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom not only ensured that Lin Yuan would be able to obtain true answers but also placed extreme stress on the one being questioned.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom would definitely become useful when he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","When he first arrived at Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would not have much information about it. The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom would ensure that he only received accurate answers, allowing him to gain an understanding of Sky Beyond the Clouds as quickly as possible.","Each time Lin Yuan evolved his feys, he would be substantially pleasantly surprised.","Lin Yuan pondered over this seriously. He believed that this was directly linked to how he only used the best resources to nurture his feys.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s Elite ability, Body-Penetrating Flames, and Normal ability, Seeping Flames, would be able to work in perfect conjunction.","Seeping Flames allowed flames to enter the target’s spirit, mind, and soul to burn them. The target’s heart and brain would be the bases, and energy would be absorbed from the target’s heart and brain.","The flames would be reignited when they were weakened.","Body-Penetrating Flames would transfer the burning effects from the target’s spirit, mind, and soul to its body and intensify the flame damage.","More importantly, Body-Penetrating Flames made it more difficult to extinguish the flames on the body. This was because both the flames from Seeping Flames and Body-Penetrating Flames had to be quenched first.","Lin Yuan felt that only a wicked mushroom could produce the ability Thought-Separating Flames. A pure-natured mushroom would never be able to produce such an evil ability.","Any lifeform that was heavily injured and in a near-dead state would think about their loved ones, family, and friends. Exceptions were very rare.","The stronger the lifeform, the longer they would live and the more ties they would have in the world.","The ability Thought-Separating Flames would allow Lin Yuan to remove an entire lifeform’s network of relationships.","When the Thought-Separating Flames extended the flames through the links of relationships, the new targets would form new centers that would continue the effects of Thought-Separating Flames. This would cause the network to extend to both direct and indirect participants.","Moreover, Thought-Separating Flames would also be useful when Lin Yuan was trying to find a mole in a group.","If there were two moles in a thousand-men-team, he would only need to catch one of them. They would think of their partner before they died, causing the flames to be transferred to their partner and allowing Lin Yuan to catch the other spy.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was a bag of tricks for interrogation purposes!","Strengthened Spores might seem like a triggered ability and not considered strong, but it could actually be linked to the exclusive skill Crumbled Parasitic Cycle and lead to a lethal reaction.","Crumbled Parasitic Cycle involved the Engulfing Flames Mushroom sacrificing its fungi to remove an equivalent amount of energy from the target’s body. The energy would be removed in a continuous cycle, causing harm to the target from the inside out.","Strengthened Spores would raise the deadly effects of Crumbled Parasitic Cycle. It would also allow the fungi to become more strongly rooted in the target’s soul, preventing it from being removed.","If a fey’s ability was linked to an exclusive skill, its level would shoot upward."]},{"number":2612,"title":"Chapter 2612 Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom!","paragraphs":["2612 Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom!","Feys that could link their abilities and exclusive skills were stronger and more treasured than other feys.","Almost every ability could boost another ability or exclusive skill, allowing the abilities’ effects to be stacked on top of each other.","The Platinum ability, Truth Colony, added another mechanism to the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s questioning abilities.","Every time Lin Yuan asked a target a question and the target gave a precise answer, a truth mushroom would be grown.","The truth mushroom was similar to truth serums used to interrogate suspects in Lin Yuan’s previous life, forcing them to give accurate answers. This specifically targeted stubborn targets whose lips remained sealed even if they were on the brink of death.","The Diamond ability, False Colony, and Truth Colony’s abilities were direct opposites.","Every time a target gave a false answer during questioning, a false mushroom would be grown. The false mushroom would allow a target to hide their thoughts and prevent them from giving true answers.","This allowed the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom to gain the ability to resist probing. This ability was important to any faction and was definitely considered a foundational ability!","When he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he could feed a false mushroom to every white-clothed follower and feel assured that Sky City’s secrets would not be leaked.","Lin Yuan had rescued the white-clothed followers and nurtured them. They swore their loyalty to him on their Willpower Runes. Even if they had to sacrifice their lives, they would never hurt Sky City’s profits.","Furthermore, the Praying Universe Soul Whale was another protection level for the white-clothed followers. Even if they died, their souls would remain.","Once the Mother of Bloodbath’s sacred source lifeform became stronger, Lin Yuan could use the Jasmine Lily to work with the Ten Thousand Medicine Hot Spring and mold new bodies. This would be especially effective because the Jasmine Lily had reached Myth Breed and gained new abilities and exclusive skills.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was very timid and did not react much to Lin Yuan’s praise. After all, how much intelligence could a little mushroom have?","Lin Yuan ordered the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom to activate the World Cleansing and begin its evolution to Myth Breed.","The aura of a Diamond X/Fantasy V fey exploded forth from the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s body, and a hole opening immediately followed this in the sky.","Violent gales barreled out from the hole. Inky black clouds formed in the sky, and black hail fell out. Every piece of hail was in the shape of a water chestnut and was very lethal against fire-type feys.","Just like Rememberling, the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was useless when it came to defense and could not handle a single attack from the World Cleansing. A single attack would immediately damage its roots.","This was why functional-type Myth Breed feys were very rare in the wild.","This was a result of natural selection. Unless the functional-type feys could find a strong source of support when they evolved to Myth Breed, it would be very difficult for them to survive the World Cleansing.","If factions obtained more functional-type feys, they would definitely grow stronger.","Just like how he protected Rememberling, Eternal Source flicked his finger, and a green and gold screen appeared to block the falling black water chestnut-shaped hail.","After absorbing the World Grace, the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s body shrunk until it was only half the size of Lin Yuan’s pinky fingernail.","The flower patterns on its cap caused the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom to resemble a pillbug that was about to release its stink at any time.","The Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s appearance was just as beautiful as it had always been, and the color of its cap was even more brilliant than before.","However, its beauty could only be enjoyed if it was placed under a magnifying glass.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to begin examining the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom, he suddenly felt a special energy gathering around it.","It was very similar to the energy that had gathered around Chimey. This was a voice-spirit-type energy.","Could the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom have transformed after its bloodline evolved to Myth Breed and gained voice-spirit-type abilities and exclusive skills?","When he looked at its True Data, Lin Yuan saw that it was now called the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom.","The Suzerain ability, Interrogation Soul Flames, raised the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom’s interrogation abilities.","[Interrogation Soul Flames]: After confirming that the target has made more than three false statements, the target can be asked a question, and the soul with fungi rooted in it will be sacrificed. The target will have to tell the truth through the voiced spirit form.","Rather than saying that the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom was capable at interrogation, it would be more accurate to call it an executioner.","Interrogation Soul Flames could be used in conjunction with Crumbled Parasitic Cycle when Lin Yuan had exhausted all other interrogation methods and the target’s will was strong enough to continue to give false answers even after consuming the truth mushroom.","The fungi and target’s soul would be sacrificed, and the target in a near-dead state would have to tell the truth through the voiced spirit form.","This was another link between an ability and exclusive skill.","With Interrogation Soul Flames, Lin Yuan could receive whatever answer he wanted.","There were times when a question could clear up a cloud of doubts.","Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning was specifically meant to clear up doubts.","[Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning]: When a judgment cannot be made on an issue, one can be staked to question the sky and ask for a positive solution.","When Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to develop, he would not have as smooth of a time as when he developed in the main world. Inevitably, he would encounter danger, obstacles, and challenges.","Using Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning, Lin Yuan could tap into the roots of the sky and carve out an opportunity. This would allow him to make a judgment on a matter he alone could not decide on.","With Lin Yuan’s intelligence, he was always able to come up with ways to get himself out of sticky situations.","However, the guidance from Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning would be good to have around.","After evolving to Myth Breed, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s intelligence was still low. However, it could react appropriately to Lin Yuan’s words now."]},{"number":2613,"title":"Chapter 2613 Beautiful God Cutting Wings!","paragraphs":["2613 Beautiful God Cutting Wings!","Fungi-type feys were just like plant-type feys in that they could change form once they reached Myth III.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had reached the stage where its intelligence would skyrocket. In a few months, it could communicate normally with Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was excited to see what the little mushroom would grow into so he could see what kind of personality it had. After all, it was already evident that it had its own wicked intentions!","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom used to resemble a button. But now, there was no way that it would be able to function as a button!","Just as Lin Yuan was about to return the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it leaped onto his head and made itself comfortable on his hair.","Lin Yuan could sense that it really wanted to be with him. He had no objections to this and would not be burdened in any way by keeping it with him.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom weighed around the same as a large piece of dandruff. He would not feel any discomfort by letting it rest on his head.","Blood New Moon had brought the Mother of Bloodbath to the Heavenly Family Cottage’s headquarters to help it further tap into its Heavenly Family Fey bloodline.","Lin Yuan remembered that the Mother of Bloodbath loved resting on his head when it first became his Path Protector.","He had not seen the Mother of Bloodbath in some time and missed it. He wondered if the Mother of Bloodbath’s bloodline would have improved significantly once it returned from the Heavenly Family Cottage.","Now that Lin Yuan was done evolving the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, he turned his attention to Purple Afterglow.","He used his finger to beckon Purple Afterglow over, and it immediately flew over to land on the tip of his finger.","The light from the sunset engulfed the earth and slowly became one with Purple Afterglow’s body.","It was likely that such a beautiful sight had never appeared in the Sand Island Continent.","Although Purple Afterglow had many issues, its appearance was nothing to be scoffed at!","Ever since Purple Afterglow made its appearance on Star Web, it occupied the first place on the ranking of the most beautiful feys. It fully deserved this position.","It was unlikely that any butterfly-species fey could compete with Purple Afterglow when it came to beauty.","Perhaps only the content of legends and mysteries yet to be discovered stood a chance of being compared to Purple Afterglow.","“Purple Afterglow, it’s your turn to evolve. You have to do your best! Rememberling and the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s bloodlines improved after they evolved to Myth Breed! I will call the Kill Food Sky Butterfly over later so it can watch you evolve!”","Lin Yuan did not like to give his feys pressure but felt that some pressure was necessary. Otherwise, Purple Afterglow would be too laid back. It was so laid back that it might not be willing to do its best during its evolution.","Purple Afterglow’s mellow character did not come from meeting the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and gaining access to Lin Yuan’s almost endless supply of top resources. Even if this were not the case, Purple Afterglow would still act this way! This was largely related to its personality.","But regardless of Purple Afterglow’s many flaws, its beauty was sufficient to convince others to overlook them. They might even start to see its flaws as virtues!","Purple Afterglow did not have much passion or motivation because it knew from long ago that this evolution would very likely lead to an improvement in his bloodline.","Purple Afterglow had felt its bloodline pulsing ever since it evolved to Diamond X/Fantasy V. It was very smart and knew that it was of no help to Lin Yuan during combat.","Lin Yuan never relied on it for fighting. Thus, its individual strength would be irrelevant to Lin Yuan.","Purple Afterglow’s attitude reminded Lin Yuan of children from families of generational wealth. Since they could not help their elders, they decided to take a backseat.","But when it heard that Lin Yuan would bring the Kill Food Sky Butterfly over to watch it evolve to Myth Breed, Purple Afterglow’s motivation immediately sparked to life. After all, a man needed to look impressive before his wife.","Purple Afterglow had always been beneath Kill Food Sky Butterfly when it came to power, and this vexed it endlessly. Every time they were together, it would have to fly under the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Luckily, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly always looked at it with adoration. Otherwise, Purple Afterglow’s pride would prevent it from being together with the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Now that it would evolve to Myth Breed, this was a good opportunity for it to properly demonstrate its capabilities.","Lin Yuan summoned the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, and while the couple was flying lovingly around each other, he used True Data to check on the unlocked Purple Afterglow.","[Fey Name]: Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly","[Fey Species]: Flash-butterfly species/scaled-butterfly species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Silence Scale Powder]: Special scale powder with the ability to silence is released, and any target that comes into contact with the scale powder will be unable to use spiritual power abilities. The scale powder will also be absorbed into the target’s spiritual power. Each time the target uses spirit qi, their spirit qi will end up cracking.","[Flashing Scale Dance]: Its images will be formed from the scale powder released into the air. It will be able to flash back and forth between itself and the formed images. While it is traveling, it can absorb energy from its surroundings to quicken the production of scale powder.","[Scale Light Butterfly Image]: Scale powder in the wings will be used to refract light. When light fills its reflection, its charm will be boosted, and it will gain absolute control over butterfly-species feys.","[Beautiful God Hallucination]: When a target is attracted and sees one as a beautiful god, one will be able to adjust according to the target’s features and pick a lifeform to turn into the target’s definition of unsightliness. If the target and the lifeform have a positive connection, it will disappear momentarily. The target will attack the lifeform if they do not have a positive connection.","[Species Praised Beauty]: When attracting a target and receiving its worship, the target’s species will also be affected and instinctively feel positive about the Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly.","[Beautiful God Cutting Wings]: Flap its wings to produce sequential cutting attacks. A special Beautiful God Engraving will be formed on the target’s body. Every engraving requires 16 cutting attacks to be formed. The target with a formed Beautiful God Engraving will trigger its own emotions to the greatest extent. Anything related to energy will be prevented from moving in and out of the target’s body.","Exclusive Skill:","[Scale Powder Halo]: The scale powder has strong reflective abilities, and the reflection will affect the target that lays eyes on the powder. The target will start to feel dizzy and experience temporary blindness.","[Soul Beauty Goddess]: By activating the power of the spirit and soul, the beauty will be increased to a limitless level. The target will be attracted and fall in love. The target will want everything of the object of its love on its own body, and the target will want to collect everything connected to the object of its love.","Lin Yuan understood Purple Afterglow’s personality and did not use it for battle. All he wanted was to nurture it in the best way possible so that it did not get in the way of Morbius’ evolution.","Besides functional-type feys, attack- and defense-type feys were no longer of much use to Lin Yuan.","When it came to power, Lin Yuan could rely on Green Vine and fused with Dark Blue and the Abyss Red Lotus.","Suppose Lin Yuan fused with the Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil, which had evolved into a Satan, or the Purple Demon, which had evolved into an emperor sea demon. In that case, he might not achieve as much power as when he fused with Dark Blue and the Abyss Red Lotus. Nevertheless, he would still be much stronger than the feys he had contracted.","The feys that Lin Yuan contracted would not greatly help Lin Yuan now, aside from their special abilities.","Lin Yuan never held much expectations for Purple Afterglow, but it turned out that the abilities it gained came with special functions. It was a special fey with abilities that other feys could not replicate!","For example, the Elite ability, Flashing Scale Dance, could be linked with the Normal ability, Silence Scale Powder. Its effects did not seem strong, and butterfly-species feys might see the highlight as being able to absorb energy from the surroundings when traveling to quicken the production of scale powder. However, being able to form an image of itself from the scale powder in the air was an extremely strong method of attack and control for Purple Afterglow.","No lifeform would remain unmoved when it saw Purple Afterglow’s shining image filling the sky. This sight would only further bolster Purple Afterglow’s beauty to even greater heights!","Laying eyes on one beauty and a group of them would have a vastly different effect on those afflicted by lust.","Being able to flash back and forth from its images would elevate Purple Afterglow’s agility and allow it to flee from danger.","The Silver ability, Scale Light Butterfly Image, and Flashing Scale Dance would give Purple Afterglow amazing attraction capabilities.","However, Scale Light Butterfly Image raised Purple Afterglow’s attraction abilities to a greater extent than Flashing Scale Dance did, as it would allow Purple Afterglow to refract light from its scale powder to form a giant image of itself that other lifeforms could look up to. Purple Afterglow’s already incredible charm would be further elevated.","Lin Yuan could not imagine the effects if Purple Afterglow’s charm was further magnified.","Additionally, Scale Light Butterfly Image would allow Purple Afterglow to gain absolute control over butterfly-species feys. From now on, it could take control of any butterfly-species fey with ease, just like it had done with the Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies!","The Gold ability, Beautiful God Hallucination, was just a way of killing through beauty. Beauty would be used to attract and adjust to the target’s features.","Using beauty to adjust to a person’s perception was much more effective than trying to achieve an objective level of beauty as it was too reliant on desire that might not be lasting. However, one’s individual perception of beauty would never change.","By adjusting to the target’s features, Purple Afterglow could turn another lifeform into the target’s definition of unsightliness.","If both parties were linked by a spirit qi professional and contracted fey relationship, the target would not act under the influence of Beautiful God Hallucination.","But if they did not have this relationship, they would definitely turn on each other, regardless of how well they got along.","Lin Yuan pondered over the utilization of Beautiful God Hallucination, and his eyes lit up as it would be able to meddle with contracts.","The extent of this meddling was varied. When used, the ability would cause a spirit qi professional to immediately lose the protection of his fey, leaving him as exposed as a fish on a cutting board that could be fileted according to the wishes of the knife-wielder.","Even spirit qi professionals with a wealth of battle experience would be rendered helpless when they were suddenly faced with such an obstacle.","The Platinum ability, Species Praised Beauty, was even more ferocious!","Purple Afterglow could affect the target’s entire species while attracting it. The target’s entire species would instinctively feel positive about it.","If Lin Yuan needed to make a deal with another species in the future, he could capture one of its members and instruct Purple Afterglow to use Species Praised Beauty so that the entire species would become agreeable before he made a deal with them.","This would allow him to establish a closer connection with this species.","Purple Afterglow’s influence over other lifeforms was largely related to its genes. The more admiration the species had for Purple Afterglow, the more positively they would feel about it.","When he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would be able to use Species Praised Beauty to trade for many unexpected things.","If he could build a good relationship with the native factions from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan’s future exploration would be smoother.","The Diamond ability that Purple Afterglow gained was called Beautiful God Cutting Wings.","It was not easy to use this ability successfully even once, as strong targets could easily avoid the cutting attacks. Moreover, the target had to sustain 16 cutting attacks before the Beautiful God Engraving could be successfully formed. It would be very difficult for Purple Afterglow to strike an enemy 16 times successfully.","But if the target was unconscious or incapacitated, it would be easy to strike it 16 times!","Beautiful God Cutting Wings did not cause damage from the cutting attacks but the maximum magnification of the target’s emotions that the Beautiful God Engraving triggered.","This would work well in conjunction with Species Praised Beauty.","The Beautiful God Engraving that was formed from Beautiful God Cutting Wings would also be able to seal off all forms of energy from entering and exiting the target’s body.","This involved not only the vitality within the lifeform’s body but also spirit qi, elemental energy, source-type power, faith power, and more.","This meant that once the Beautiful God Engraving was successfully formed on the target’s body, it would be reduced to a cripple until the Beautiful God Engraving was removed.","The Beautiful God Engraving not only prevented energy from entering the body but exiting as well. The target would have no choice but to use its body to defend itself against enemies.","It could induce feelings of positivity in other species as well as block energy from entering or exiting a target’s body.","Purple Afterglow was just incredible!"]},{"number":2614,"title":"Chapter 2614 Beauty Reaches Every Species!","paragraphs":["2614 Beauty Reaches Every Species!","Lin Yuan was powerful and had the power to take on numerous enemies.","The captured enemies needed someone to watch them. If they did not, they would definitely cause trouble. This would be a waste of Lin Yuan’s subordinates.","But when Purple Afterglow used Beautiful God Cutting Wings to create the Beautiful God Engraving on a target, Lin Yuan would not have to assign many subordinates to watch over these enemies.","Lin Yuan had suffered for more than ten years after arriving in this world. But once he became a spirit qi professional, he struck the jackpot and reached the peak of Creation Mastery.","Using Genius, he also passed the test to become a Class 2 Creation Master and became the Moon Empress’ disciple.","Since then, everything had been smooth sailing for him.","This was largely related to Lin Yuan’s own power, but the protection from the Moon Empress could not be ignored either.","The Mother of Bloodbath had saved Lin Yuan many times, and it was the Moon Empress who had placed the Mother of Bloodbath as Lin Yuan’s Path Protector.","Otherwise, the Myth II Mother of Bloodbath and D-rank spirit qi professional Lin Yuan would never have been able to cross paths.","Once he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there would be no one to protect him—he would need to protect himself.","At that time, Beautiful God Cutting Wings would bring Lin Yuan a fair amount of convenience.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly and Purple Afterglow flew around each other in the sky. They looked like a flash of baby blue chasing after a streak of beautiful sunset purple. This breathtaking sight caused the desert outside of the Seaberry Federation to look romantically dazzling.","However, Purple Afterglow was not purely enjoying itself as it flew around with the Kill Food Sky Butterfly. It was also securing its own bloodline.","Once it sensed its relatively secure bloodline, Purple Afterglow stopped in midair.","When the Kill Food Sky Butterfly saw this, it did not cling to Purple Afterglow and dutifully put distance between them. It did not want to obstruct or disturb Purple Afterglow.","As Purple Afterglow flew around in the sky and dispersed its scale powder, it made for a beautiful sight.","Suddenly, a thick stream of purple light burst out from Purple Afterglow’s body and stained the sky purple.","All the people in the cities near the Seaberry Federation fell to their knees instinctively after spotting the purple-stained sky. They placed their palms together and began to pray earnestly.","The Seaberry Federation was considered relatively weak in the Sand Island Continent.","The people there lived lives so laboriously that those from wealthy federations would never be able to imagine such a reality. The people living there did not have any pastimes. A day that they did not spend working would be a day where they had to go hungry. They did not know what it was like to hope for anything.","All they could do was place their hopes on intangible gods.","The purple sky was the most beautiful phenomenon they had ever seen.","There was not much common knowledge to speak of in a federation where the average lifespan was only 20 to 30 years.","This sight caused many people to think that a god had descended on the Seaberry Federation, and it happened to be in the same direction as the tents that had been providing food to the people of the Seaberry Federation.","The people from the Seaberry Federation prayed with gratitude to this god and unknowingly increased their rate of supplying faith power to Lin Yuan.","As time passed, the purple in the sky did not fade and only became more concentrated.","There was a golden gleam within the purple that seemed to form thousands of wispy streaks. As the light danced around, every cascading wisp of light was surrounded by tens of rainbows.","The Seaberry Federation was enveloped in a beauty that could be appreciated in both heaven and on Earth. This beauty radiated from the very spot where the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift had once opened.","Even the insect queens guarding the entrance of the Class 6 alien insect dimensional rift became lost in this magnificent sight.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly stared at Purple Afterglow with gentle adoration.","Lin Yuan smiled at this. He now knew why Purple Afterglow said that its bloodline could take a step forward.","As he looked at this natural phenomenon, Lin Yuan could be certain that Purple Afterglow’s bloodline was transforming!","As Purple Afterglow continued to release its aura, a black hole appeared in the sky.","Crimson flames burst out from the hole and became entangled with the purple and gold sky.","Eternal Source proceeded to protect Purple Afterglow like he did with Rememberling and Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom.","Once the red flames were extinguished and the World Grace landed on Purple Afterglow’s body, it started to grow longer. Its wings became more flowy, and a layer of purple and gold light now bordered them. It looked as though there was a backlight shining on Purple Afterglow’s body.","The beauty of a butterfly-species fey depended on its shape and scale powder. There was not much relation to its patterns.","Color came from the scale powder, and too many patterns on the wings would cause the wings to look messy. This would be akin to attaching many accessories on an amazing piece of material.","Just as Lin Yuan thought that Purple Afterglow’s scale powder had turned purple and gold and that its evolution was complete, two sets of illusionary wings sprouted from its body.","The wings were 1.5 times larger than its body and flapped in tandem with its actual wings.","Lin Yuan used to struggle to come up with the words to describe Purple Afterglow’s beauty.","But once the illusionary wings grew out, Lin Yuan suddenly felt that it seemed to resemble the guard of a butterfly-species thearch.","The purple and gold coloring completely overhauled Purple Afterglow’s beauty and refreshed Lin Yuan’s assessment of beauty.","Lin Yuan hurriedly used True Data to check on Purple Afterglow and saw that its name had not changed. It was still called the Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly.","According to Morbius, only the most beautiful entities in the world could be considered beautiful gods or goddesses.","The names that Morbius gave all of its feys came from their bloodlines.","The Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly was the only Beauty Goddess Butterfly in the world, so Morbius saw no need to change its name.","The illusionary wings that Purple Afterglow gained after evolving to Myth Breed did not even reach the top three of its merits.","However, Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly’s type had changed from its initial flash-butterfly species/scaled-butterfly species to beautiful-goddess butterfly species/beautiful-goddess butterfly genus. This meant that it was no longer a flash-butterfly species at all and could pass on its new bloodline.","The Suzerain ability that Purple Afterglow gained was called Beauty Assessment Plundering.","[Beauty Assessment Plundering]: When one’s beauty stupefies a species and takes over that species’ assessment of beauty, it can set the standard with its own beauty and become the definition of beauty for that species. Besides itself, the species will not see any other lifeform as beautiful. It will detest and be repulsed by lifeforms that previously met their standards of beauty.","Lin Yuan was first stunned when he saw the description of Beauty Assessment Plundering. He suddenly felt that it could be effectively linked to Species Praised Beauty.","Species Praised Beauty would attract a target and utilize beauty to earn that target’s worship. It would then influence the target’s species and earn positive feelings from that species.","Beauty Assessment Plundering would turn Purple Afterglow into the standard of beauty for the species once it takes over their assessment of beauty.","This ability did not seem strong, but once Purple Afterglow took over a species’ assessment of beauty and altered it, the species would feel repulsed toward entities that previously met their standard of beauty.","This would not only make it more challenging for the species to procreate but might even cause the species to go extinct.","A species might go extinct due to its definition of beauty.","Purple Afterglow, this male butterfly, was looking more and more like the Death Demon Concubine Beast!","After observing Purple Afterglow’s Suzerain ability, Lin Yuan started observing the exclusive skill it had gained.","The exclusive skill Purple Afterglow gained from reaching Myth Breed was Beauty Reaches Every Species.","[Beauty Reaches Every Species]: Each time it receives the recognition of a species and becomes their standard of beauty, its charm will be eternally strengthened.","Beauty Reaches Every Species was very simple, but Lin Yuan was whooping with joy to himself.","Purple Afterglow’s beauty could be considered to be at the peak of the main world. But this might not be the case if it were in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","There might be even greater beauty out there.","Some of its abilities would be useless if it were less beautiful than its target.","However, Beauty Reaches Every Species would allow Purple Afterglow to continuously increase its charm and attraction. Because of this, Purple Afterglow would not have to worry about being less beautiful than another species in Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Even if it were not more beautiful now, it would not stay on the losing end after it increased its charm!","Purple Afterglow seemed very laid back, but it was very prideful when it came to its own beauty. When it arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Purple Afterglow would definitely try to become the most beautiful lifeform there.","Now that Purple Afterglow had evolved to Myth Breed, Lin Yuan did not have any other feys that he needed to evolve.","Lin Yuan had been spending most of his time in the dimensional world. Due to a lack of moonbeams, the Merciful Star Peony’s evolution had slowed. Moreover, just like the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee and Ethereal Jellyfish, the Merciful Star Peony needed to comprehend a Willpower Rune from nature.","Lin Yuan did not know when the Merciful Star Peony could evolve to Myth Breed.","Gray was able to evolve to Myth Breed. However, a higher priority for it now would be accumulating power rather than evolving.","Lin Yuan was willing to give Gray the chance to accumulate power. After all, accumulating power would never turn out to be a disadvantage.","Lin Yuan would be happy if Gray could become more mature and resistant to temptation before it evolved to Myth Breed.","The Sea Burial Lotus Flower was a carcinoma fey that Lin Yuan had nurtured into a fairy. It had expanded Lin Yuan’s horizons.","Silver Corona was currently only Diamond grade, but the sea of bone lotus flowers it had created would even be able to reduce a group of 100 Myth Breed feys into fertilizer.","The 16 Class 3 dimensional rifts had been spitting out waves of alien beasts for the past year. Yet, it had not been enough for Silver Corona to reach Diamond X.","Lin Yuan intended to take Silver Corona with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds so he could test its limits. He might be able to use Silver Corona to create a forbidden area that terrified even the native factions of the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Lin Yuan only gave himself a week to rest. Once he was done allocating the Samsara Realm Dictators and providing Su Yiren with resources, his break would come to an end.","He intended to return to the Spirit Lock spatial zone to fuse with and take control of the alien insect world’s tome.","That way, he could absorb energy from all five major dimensional worlds the next time that he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","Wen Yu had been communicating with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper. Lin Yuan learned from their correspondence that she had not found the Broiling Rock Continent, where Peace was located, but she could sense their stronger link.","This meant that Peace was located to the west of the Grotto Continent.","Wen Yu was very skilled at governance and excelled at military organization, as well as the allocation of resources.","With Dazzling Silver and the other four Samsara Realm Dictators, Wen Yu managed to find three Continent Vein Cores for Lin Yuan within the short span of a few days.","This delighted Lin Yuan.","Every continent on the other side of the Barren Sea had powerful federations.","The Continent Vein Cores could be found in the strongest federation of each continent.","Once the Moon Empress created the Major Federation Union, the federations would automatically hand over their Continent Vein Cores.","The Moon Empress had already told Lin Yuan she would handle this personally, so he did no need to worry. Lin Yuan never had to worry when the Moon Empress was handling things.","Frankly, Lin Yuan thought Morbius would evolve soon after Purple Afterglow evolved to Myth Breed and its grade would also increase from Diamond to Suzerain.","However, Morbius said it would need to sleep for around ten days before its grade would be increased.","Lin Yuan went to sleep full of hope. He looked forward to the accumulation meant to take on Tower Canon as well as Morbius’ evolution to Myth Breed.","Before he went to sleep, he contacted all of the subterranean Samsara Realm Dictators and instructed them to gather the Land Imps. They would then leave the subterranean world and move from the Iron Hammer Federation to Thick Soil City.","Thick Soil City was very close to the underground palace where the Space Tunnel was situated. It would make it easy for Lin Yuan to organize the Land Imps if they gathered at Thick Soil City.","Seven days would be just enough time for the Land Imps to travel!","Once he woke up, he would need to command these millions of Land Imps and organize them around the Radiance Federation. It would become the center around which the defensive fortifications would be constructed.","He would build a fortress that could remain standing amidst the ocean of dead spirits and even fend them off.","While Lin Yuan was sleeping...","In a time-worn castle, a woman with an icy demeanor yet gentle eyes knelt in the vast hall’s center. Her unwavering gaze fixated on a mural behind an ornate chair, the artwork in gradual flux, its details burgeoning with vibrancy.","Just a day earlier, constellations of stars had materialized around the colossal whale adjacent to the imposing figure at the drawing’s core. Simultaneously, the mushroom had dwindled in size, its intricate patterns multiplying."]},{"number":2615,"title":"Chapter 2615 Conflict in the Azure Federation!","paragraphs":["2615 Conflict in the Azure Federation!","A butterfly with an exquisite form had two illusionary wings sprouting from its back.","The circle around this imposingly dependable figure also started to spin. It was as though something was about to happen.","But when she saw this, the woman with the cold expression but gentle eyes started to bow sincerely and chant softly. Tears fell from the corners of her eyes and landed on the white jade floor of the vast hall.","\"The Totem God is finally about to evolve to the second form! It is now certain that Lord Saint has awoken!\"","The woman's expression suddenly hardened.","\"The eight ants from Tower Canon are probably going to wake up from their slumber soon as well. The cheek of them to wake up at the same time as Lord Saint! I hope the mortals from this Class 3 civilization won't impact Lord Saint. Otherwise, in spite of Lord Saint's order for Epoch God Palace not to affect the mortal world, we will have to step in to eliminate this Class 3 civilization!\"","Suddenly, the kneeling woman froze.","She had been thinking about other things while praying to the Totem God! This was a grievous sin!","The woman hastily started slamming her head to the ground to make up for her sin, leaving large pools of crimson and gold blood splattered all over the white jade floor.","The crimson and gold blood glinted with inexplicable life and contained laws related to the cycle of four seasons.","The sun had already risen and set numerous times outside of the hall, but the woman had yet to stop trying to repay for her sin.","?","...","Sky City had been started by Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu. The first one to join Lin Yuan was Liu Jie.","Liu Jie was Lin Yuan's retainer, but his presence had always been weaker than Wen Yu's.","Wen Yu was the manager of Sky City, while Liu Jie managed the white-clothed followers.","At first, Liu Jie was busy training the white-clothed followers. But eventually, the training reached a checkpoint and Liu Jie no longer had a role to fill. He became rather free.","Liu Jie did not want to become the mooch in Sky City, so he had been trying to improve himself in terms of his governance skills.","Wen Yu had been beside herself with work, so Liu Jie could not ask her to teach him when she was already this busy.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had taken Bai Qinghuan in so Liu Jie could learn from her.","Now, he could stand on his own two feet to a certain extent!","Ever since Wen Yu started managing the business related to the dimensional worlds, Liu Jie took over the governance side of Sky City.","At first, Liu Jie was very stressed. But he pulled himself up by the bootstraps, and after holding on for a month, he finally became accustomed to the job of managing Sky City. He also learned just how difficult Wen Yu's job had been.","After leaving the Midnight Palace and dealing with most of his tasks for Sky City, Liu Jie headed straight to Thick Soil City to help manage the Land Imps.","Ta Lei had been growing rapidly, but he was still too young. It was only with Su Yiren's help that he managed to secure his position as the City Lord of Thick Soil City.","?","Ta Lei was already strained by managing Thick Soil City's day-to- day affairs. He did not have the energy to manage the Land Imps as well.","Su Yiren was busy with the mountain of work required to manage two giant continents.","Even if Ta Lei wanted to ask her for help, he could not bring himself to do so. As such, he could only turn to Liu Jie.","Ta Lei could not have gone to Liu Jie for help and insisted on taking on the task himself.","After all, Luo Lan's people were helping to deliver the Land Imps, and they would definitely have the Land Imps under control. The leader of the Land Imps would not dare to step out of line.","However, Ta Lei was afraid of inconveniencing Lin Yuan.","Since he could not get in contact with Lin Yuan, he naturally got in contact with Liu Jie instead.","Ta Lei was much more familiar with Liu Jie than he was with Wen Yu. Lin Yuan had brought only Liu Jie with him when he went to the Startling Lines Continent to train.","Once he received confirmation that Liu Jie was coming to Thick Soil City to help, Ta Lei was finally able to relax.","Lin Yuan had left a special Diamond fey storage box with both Liu Jie and Wen Yu. Each of these Diamond fey storage boxes contained a large amount of Item-Storing Walnuts.","The Item-Storing Walnuts were meant to enable Liu Jie and Su Yiren to utilize the Space Tunnel in the basement of the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Although there were not enough Item-Storing Walnuts in the Diamond fey storage boxes to allow Liu Jie and Wen Yu to travel between the Radiance Federation and Grotto Continent, it was enough to allow them to travel between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent more than ten times.","...","By the time Liu Jie rushed to Thick Soil City, the first batch of Land Imps had arrived. Lin Yuan needed so many Land Imps they had to be sent in batches.","Lin Yuan had emphasized to Hollow Earth, Rock Underworld, and Mountain Furrow that a Samsara Realm Dictator had to lead each group of Land Imps.","In order to prevent the leading Samsara Realm Dictators from coming up with any schemes, he also assigned 20 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators who were fully subservient to him to watch over these Samsara Realm Dictators.","The Samsara Realm Dictator leading the first batch was named Dark River.","Dark River was a female Samsara Realm Dictator who came from the south mine district. Her looks ranked in the top three among the female subterranean Dictators. Her bloodline was that of the Bright Stone Witch and was considered to be extremely elite.","Yet, when Lin Yuan conquered the subterranean world, he had not paid any special attention to her. This had left her very dispirited.","Dark River believed that with her features and background, there was no reason not to favor her.","Not only did she have beauty, but she also had brains. Otherwise, she would not have been able to take over the richest mine district and reigned over it this entire time.","Dark River had decided that by hook or by crook, she would leave a good impression on Lin Yuan when she headed to the main world to deliver the Land Imps.","Alas, she was disappointed to find that Lin Yuan was absent when she arrived.","Liu Jie had not left a strong impression when Lin Yuan was conquering the subterranean world.","Although Dark River did not know who Liu Jie was, she could sense","that he was very weak. He could not even compare to the relatively more ferocious Apostles!","The subterranean world was similar to the other dimensional worlds in that nothing mattered more than power.","Given Liu Jie's power, he could not gain the respect of the Samsara Realm Dictator Dark River.","Although she looked down on Liu Jie, Dark River dared not show how she truly felt because she knew that Lin Yuan trusted Liu Jie. Otherwise, he would never have left such an important task in Liu Jie's hands.","Mountain Furrow, Rock Underworld, and Hollow Earth had repeatedly told the subterranean Dictators about how important this task was to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan could enable Samsara Realm Dictators to reach the Afterlife Realm. This ability left a deep impression on all the Samsara Realm Dictators of the subterranean world, Dark River included!","Since she could not perform in front of Lin Yuan, she could ensure she at least received the basic treatment deserving of a Samsara Realm Dictator.","But if she earned Lin Yuan's ire, she would not only miss out on the chance to reach the Afterlife Realm but might even lose the benefits given to Samsara Realm Dictators.","Dark River was well aware of what her place was.","Liu Jie was able to smoothly manage and organize the Land Imps. But there were just far too many Land Imps, and collating them all was impossible.","?","Liu Jie mulled over this situation and decided to use Bai Qinghuan's plan. He decided to organize the Land Imps according to their strength. Those who were stronger would manage the weaker ones.","This way, Liu Jie would only need to manage the few strongest Land Imps. This would allow him to commandeer all of the Land Imps when he was organizing the relocation as well as for future tasks.","The Dictator Land Imps could not be used to build the base. Even if they were assigned such a task, they had to be in charge of special roles. Otherwise, it would be a gross waste of their talents!","Thus, Liu Jie separated the Dictator Land Imps from the rest, and they became a special team.","These Land Imps who had attained extremely strong faith power would finally be allowed to become leaders.","Liu Jie chose 30 of the strongest Land Imps and assigned the rest to them as their subordinates.","Liu Jie told these 30 Land Imps in a stern and serious voice, \"You are being allowed to lead the teams of Land Imps because we trust you. From now on, you will be able to receive one earth-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearl every month. If you perform well, you might receive additional rewards!\"","The 30 Land Imps almost exploded with delight when they heard what Liu Jie said.","Normally, they would never have the right to touch resources like earth-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls. Lin Yuan usually only gave such resources to the Samsara Realm Dictators. Liu Jie had not made these decisions on his own accord. He had communicated extensively with Lin Yuan before he made these decisions. It was Lin Yuan who had decided to use heavenly- maiden-grade elemental pearls to motivate the Land Imps.","?","However, Lin Yuan had not provided a structured plan, and Liu Jie devised one according to Lin Yuan's goals.","A total of eight to nine batches of the Land Imps had arrived.","The more than 200 elite Land Imps would be sufficient to complete the task to perfection.","Liu Jie worked day and night in Thick Soil City. In his spare time, he communicated with Duan He and told him to return from training with all of the white-clothed followers in tow.","The main world was being shaken, and Tower Canon's Sleeper's Revival could begin anytime.","It was not appropriate for the white-clothed followers to continue training in the wild at such a time.","Moreover, Hu Quan had built the framework of Sky City on the Floating Island Whale's back. He did not lack subordinates or spiritual ingredients, but he did lack labor. The white-clothed followers would be just right to fill this gap.","If the white-clothed followers joined the building of Sky City, it would also be considered an accumulation of power.","Since Liu Jie found out that Lin Yuan's objective lay beyond the main world, he also changed his personal aim. He now also saw the world beyond the main world as the direction that he needed to work toward.","...","After the imperial meeting ended, the Moon Empress did not use the name of the Radiance Federation to establish the Major Federation Union. Instead, she established it jointly with the Azure Federation and Freedom Federation.","She sent invitations to every federation's imperial court, sending the main world into an immediate frenzy.","?","There was no way that any federation could go without joining a federation started by the three major federations.","The royalty of the other federations were all shocked that the meeting that established the Major Federation Union had been held in the Radiance Federation. The Freedom Federation had been the strongest of the three major federations all this time.","By all accounts, the establishment of the Major Federation Union should have been done in the Freedom Federation. There was no reason for it to have been held in the Radiance Federation's Royal Capital instead.","The other federations had many doubts about the Freedom Federation's lack of protest, and they began to guess the reason behind their compromise. This did not fit with their style at all.","However, these federations did not have the courage to ask the Mirror God and God of Fools about the reason.","They wondered whether something had happened between the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation.","But regardless of what the reason was, this matter allowed all the federations of the main world to know that the Radiance Federation would be the one sitting on the throne of the main world from now on.","Otherwise, the Freedom Federation would definitely have fought for something that directly involved authority over the main world! The meeting of the Major Federation Union was being held hastily.","After receiving the news, all the federations gathered their people and rushed to the Radiance Federation.","Once the Major Federation Union was established, the structure of all the main world's federations would be altered.","?","It was highly possible that a new ranking of the federations would replace the one established by the competition among the federation envoys during the Major Federation Meeting.","Hence, every federation intended to give their all in this matter that involved their potential benefits.","The leaders of the federations on good terms with the Radiance Federation were all jumping with joy to themselves.","The federations who had not interacted much or had no experience with the Radiance Federation were all planning ways to curry favor with the Radiance Federation.","The federations who had ties to the Freedom Federation's members of royalty were all discussing in an attempt to find out more about the situation.","The collaboration between the other federations and the Freedom Federation's royalty were all personal. They rarely collaborated in the name of their federations.","But when they contacted the Freedom Federation's royalty, none of the federations received a reply.","There were rumors that all of the Freedom Federation's royalty had rushed to the Radiance Federation upon hearing the news and were acting very strangely.","Given the circumstances, despite the lack of response from the Freedom Federation, the royalty of the other federations could guess what had happened.","...","The 12 aristocratic families of the Azure Federation held a meeting that lasted for two days. For the first time, there was a difference in opinion.","The Azure Federation was not fully united, and each of the 12 aristocratic families had their own individual sources of profits.","?","When their profits did not interfere with each other, they were very willing to respect each other's opinions.","But when there was a serious involvement of their profits, the aristocratic families were willing to clash violently with each other in order to preserve their personal profits!","It was said that 80 years ago, there were not 12 aristocratic families but 14 of them. However, two of the aristocratic families disappeared after a clash over profits!"]},{"number":2616,"title":"Chapter 2616 Morbius’ Evolution!","paragraphs":["2616 Morbius’ Evolution!","The internal battle in the Azure Federation had shaken up the entire main world in the past.","There were both benefits and drawbacks when it came to structuring a federation around families.","The benefits were that such federations would be more concerned about a federation’s development than federations under the control of royalty.","A family would be deeply rooted and intertwined with the federation, making them pay more attention to the development of the federation.","However, once there was a split in opinion among the families, the conflict that should have been about the federation’s strategy would become one about the families’ personal issues.","When families fought, their priority would be to secure their own profits, and they were willing to fight to the death for them!","Such conflict was the most evident among feys. Whenever two species fought, it always resulted in the death of one of the species.","The 12 aristocratic families all had fey bloodlines, giving them their beast patterns.","There were already signs of daggers preparing to be drawn at this Azure Federation imperial meeting.","“You decided to ally with the Radiance Federation and gave up on remaining neutral between the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation. I didn’t oppose this and went with your decision.","“We lost all the formidability of a major federation by following the Radiance Federation’s lead completely in the matter of the Freedom Federation. But I didn’t point out any doubts either. The favor that we owe the Radiance Federation can be said to be repaid. But now, you are suggesting we submit to the Radiance Federation. Yin Tong, what are you trying to do?”","An elder wearing a long blue robe with cloud patterns as well as a leopard crest on his chest stroked his beard and said seriously, “Lu He, watch what you say! Take a look at where you are! You will have to take responsibility for every word you utter in the Azure Federation’s imperial court!","“There are three things wrong with what you just said. Let me make things clear for you now!","“Firstly, you willingly participated in the vote during our imperial meeting to decide on forming an alliance with the Radiance Federation. No one coerced you through marital power; this was your voluntary choice. Therefore, you cannot claim you merely followed along.","“When you made your decision, it was in favor of the option most advantageous to the Azure Elf Cat species. Furthermore, the Azure Elf Cat species greatly benefited from aligning with the Radiance Federation within the Freedom Federation. If you have doubts about this, then the Azure Elf Cat species should relinquish these profits first.","“Secondly, you mentioned that the Azure Federation has repaid the Radiance Federation for their past assistance. This is entirely incorrect! Repaying the Radiance Federation remains an ongoing obligation for us.","“The Azure Federation found itself in a position of utter vulnerability when confronted with a crisis. The Freedom Federation explicitly refused to aid us during this critical juncture. Even when other federations boasting Class 5 Creation Masters observed our inability to handle the situation independently, they chose to remain passive observers.","“The Radiance Federation extended their helping hand precisely when we needed it most. Surely you recall what would have befallen the Azure Federation had they acted differently! Witnessing the fate of Fresh City in the Freedom Federation due to the Class 6 marsh dimensional rift serves as a stark reminder.","“The Radiance Federation rescued us; how could we ever repay such a debt? Our only chance to consider it repaid is if we, in turn, rescue them from a crisis. Have you lived so long that you’ve forgotten the fundamental principles of human bonds?”","Yin Tong, a man of few words, left Lu He utterly speechless with his recent statement. Beads of sweat formed on Lu He’s back.","Not swayed by Lu He’s expression, Yin Tong continued resolutely, “Lu He, our centuries-long camaraderie speaks volumes about our mutual understanding. You accuse me of aligning with the Radiance Federation, yet aren’t you the one consistently favoring the Freedom Federation? Is it not because of your ongoing dealings with certain members within the Freedom Federation?","“We convene here to resolve this issue, sparing niceties. Objectively suggesting that the Freedom Federation should be our ally over the Radiance Federation is nothing short of ignoring reality. However, if your stance is driven solely by personal gain, it reflects poorly on your character. Lu He, I’ve conveyed all that’s necessary. The floor is yours for rebuttal.”","Lu He’s lips twitched when he heard what Yin Tong said. He wanted to bite back but could not come up with a single word.","Everything that Yin Tong had said was true.","Although Yin Tong seemed to be pointing the finger at him based on principles, he was not wrong. If he tried to rebuke him, he would only be making specious arguments/","With so many people here, specious arguments would be exposed immediately and have no practical effect.","However, Lu He could not remain silent.","If he did not make a statement after being cornered by Yin Tong to such an extent, nothing he said during future imperial meetings would carry any weight!","With this thought, Lu He was about to speak when Fang Lingzhan patted him and said, “Old Lu, one should always set one’s sights as far into the future as possible. I’m sure you’re aware of this!","“The Freedom Federation is no longer the wielder of control. The one in control is now the Radiance Federation! Otherwise, why would the Freedom Federation have agreed to the Radiance Federation’s request and handed over so many resources? They even allowed the Radiance Federation to depart safely! I am also working with a few of the Freedom Federation’s royalty, but I agree with Yin Tong’s proposal!”","Fang Lingzhan was the leader of the Azure Soaring Eagle family, ranked among the top three of the 12 aristocratic families. It held a lot of sway in the Azure Federation’s imperial court.","Moreover, Fang Lingzhang was right in that the Azure Soaring Eagle family had always staunchly supported allying with the Freedom Federation.","He could only be changing his attitude now because he had considered the current situation and knew that the Freedom Federation was no longer the superpower they used to be.","However, the others did not agree with Fang Lingzhan. There were a few aristocratic families who were firmly against supporting the promotion of the Radiance Federation to the head of the Major Federation Union.","Because of Yin Lin, Yin Tong knew the most about the Radiance Federation out of the people present.","It was impossible to persuade the stubborn. Since they could not be persuaded, Yin Tong did not bother to do so. “Since we can’t see eye to eye, no one can make decisions for another. So, let’s not speak on behalf of each other. Let’s head to the Radiance Federation together so we can save ourselves from this senseless argument!","“If your minds aren’t changed even after you arrive at the Radiance Federation, you can make your stance clear to them then. I don’t feel any opposition toward this! But I suggest that you go and take a look at the Freedom Federation’s reaction first.","“Otherwise, if you end up impacting the Azure Federation’s profits, you will sin against the Azure Federation, which will be recorded in the history books! You will also end up erased from the Azure Federation, just like what had happened to those two families! That is my solemn warning for you!”","Yin Tong immediately ended the meeting after saying that.","It had not been Yin Tong’s intention to be so abrasive, but he saw no other option. If they had to argue to the point that a victor emerged, no one would be willing to back down, and the consequences would be irreparable! This was not what Yin Tong wanted.","These old men were stubborn, but none of them were fools. They would definitely understand their circumstances when it came to such small matters!","At that time, the Freedom Federation’s reaction would definitely change the minds of these old men!","The time of the Freedom Federation had passed. It was time for the spotlight to shine on the Radiance Federation!","Given the circumstances, all the smart people would know not to resist as there was no way that it would lead to a positive result!","...","Lin Yuan finally woke up from his slumber.","The first thing he did was take out his phone to check the time. He saw that he had been sleeping for almost nine days.","Although he had woken up, Morbius was still asleep.","Once Morbius woke up, Lin Yuan could witness Morbius evolve to Myth Breed!","Lin Yuan did not have to sleep again and could properly address all his business in the main world!","The Grotto Continent was in Wen Yu’s hands, so there was nothing for Lin Yuan to be worried about. The Moon Empress was handling the Major Federation Union. What Lin Yuan needed to do was use the Land Imps to build the base in the Radiance Federation.","Before Lin Yuan went to sleep, he left the matter of handling the delivery of the Land Imps to Liu Jie, and he had great faith in Liu Jie’s competency.","Indeed, Liu Jie had not disappointed Lin Yuan and had delivered the Land Imps in batches to the Radiance Federation.","There was no way that the Land Imps could be delivered through the Space Tunnel. After all, Lin Yuan did not have enough Item-Storing Walnuts to support such a method of transportation.","Luckily, the Startling Lines Continent was not far from the Radiance Federation, and the Island Whales could be used for long-distance deliveries!","Lin Yuan had already informed the Moon Empress and the Radiance Federation had sent more than 30 Island Whales who were already waiting in the Great Lush Federation’s harbor. All Liu Jie needed to do was move the Land Imps to the Great Lush Federation’s harbor once he had taken stock of them in Thick Soil City!","By the time Lin Yuan woke up, almost 40,000,000 Land Imps had been delivered to the Radiance Federation.","As such, there was no need for Lin Yuan to head to Thick Soil City. He could sit tight and wait in the Radiance Federation.","He needed an extremely large space in order to organize these Land Imps. It would not be easy to find such a space.","When the Moon Empress found out about Lin Yuan’s plan, she made advance preparations and dug out six mountains near the Royal Capital.","These six mountains were the Radiance Federation’s Royal Capital’s most famous vacation spots and were usually bustling with activity. Visitors from other cities always paid them a visit.","But special times called for special measures. The six mountains were not large enough to house all of the Land Imps. However, the Land Imps could alter the ground of the six mountains and create expansive underground spaces where they could reside.","Lin Yuan instructed the Land Imps to clean up the environment around the six mountains before they began building the underground spaces.","He had already prepared all of the resources. Once the Land Imps arrived, they could immediately begin working on the mountains and changing the environment of the Radiance Federation so as to prevent the dead spirits from breaching the Radiance Federation’s ground!","Lin Yuan’s idea seemed like a pie in the sky, but not only would the Land Imps be able to fulfill Lin Yuan’s plan, but they would even go beyond what Lin Yuan had asked in order to curry favor with him and demonstrate their value!","Once Lin Yuan was certain that the Land Imps had started working and could carry out his request, he immediately headed to the Radiant Moon Palace.","It had been a long time since Lin Yuan had the chance to sit down and have a good chat with the Moon Empress.","Both of them had been busy. But the invitations for the Major Federation Union had already been sent out. The Moon Empress could take a good rest for the next few days before the royalty from the other federations arrived.","The Radiance Federation’s establishment of the Major Federation Union should be extremely joyous. However, none of the Radiance Federation’s royalty looked happy because they were all aware of Tower Canon’s evil scheme.","With this impending disaster that was approaching the main world, the Radiance Federation’s members of royalty were all doing their best to protect the Radiance Federation.","Resources were rapidly being stocked up. The Radiance Federation’s royalty were not stingy with their personal resources, and this especially applied to Cicada Song!","Cicada Song had distributed almost all of his resources to the 32 City Lords so they could develop the City Guards to the maximum extent. This would not only involve increasing the City Guards’ power but also increasing their numbers. This would also ensure that every reserve guard obtained a Platinum fey.","If the dead spirits invaded the cities, the reserve City Guards would be the main pillar of strength that protected the Radiance Federation’s citizens!","The Radiance Federation’s royalty all released their own resources to elevate the Radiance Federation’s overall power, and the top resources given out by the Moon Empress had also allowed the royalty’s own power to increase significantly.","The veteran and top factions of the Radiance Federation had also improved substantially.","Now that Lin Yuan was back in the Radiance Federation, he should be helping the experts whose feys needed help overcoming their World Cleansings.","However, it was urgent that Morbius evolved its grade and quality.","Once Morbius evolved its grade and quality, not only would the spirit qi crystals be produced at a faster rate, but the amount of spirit qi contained in each spirit qi crystals would also increase.","Lin Yuan had just arrived at the foot of Leaning Moon Mountain when he heard Morbius’ voice in his head. “Partner, I can evolve at any time! Before I evolve, you will need to find a place for me that is completely empty. This evolution will cause a rather large commotion! I can promise that this evolution will benefit both of us significantly!”","Lin Yuan was delighted and immediately used the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation to travel to a remote location at the border of the Royal Capital and Ascending Dragon City."]},{"number":2617,"title":"Chapter 2617 14 Totem Seeds!","paragraphs":["2617 14 Totem Seeds!","The Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer had evolved here. It was also here that Lin Yuan had obtained the Kill Food Worm from the Cage of Brahma Insects’ Fan Jianyi.","Eventually, the Kill Food Worm had evolved into the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and found a partner in Purple Afterglow.","Lin Yuan felt slightly sentimental now that he was back here.","Now, he was going to witness Morbius’ evolution here.","Lin Yuan always felt that Morbius was very special. He could not regard Morbius under the same lens that he viewed everything else.","Regular feys would never have an exclusive skill when they were only Normal grade.","Even after reaching Diamond grade, Morbius could not see its own species on True Data. The section was still filled with three question marks.","He did not know if Morbius would finally be able to see its own species after it evolved to Suzerain/Myth.","Frankly, Lin Yuan did not want Morbius to see its own species too soon.","The later that Morbius gained access to its species, the more powerful it would be.","Each time one of the spirit-locked feys evolved, Morbius’ abilities changed when it evolved.","When Lin Yuan first acquired Morbius, its exclusive skill, Spirit Lock involved nurturing feys within the Spirit Lock spatial zone. These nurtured feys couldn’t possess a higher grade than Morbius itself. Morbius’ grade couldn’t evolve independently; rather, it would only advance through the evolution of the spirit-locked feys, gaining their initial abilities.","However, Morbius couldn’t acquire abilities through its own evolutions.","As Morbius’ grade increased, it could nurture another fey each time without any alteration to this grade increment method.","However, when Morbius reached Silver grade, Spirit Lock underwent an improvement. Now, there was no longer a restriction preventing Morbius from gaining abilities through its own evolution.","It was at that time that Morbius gained Spirit Qi Condensation.","After it gained Spirit Qi Condensation, a stone bowl appeared in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Periodically, a spirit qi crystal would be formed in the stone bowl. At the time, this was Lin Yuan’s only way of obtaining spirit qi crystals.","Later, after Lin Yuan used the Pure Land of Bliss to heal the Mother of Bloodbath when it evolved to Myth II, he accidentally allowed the Pure Land of Bliss to absorb the Mother of Bloodbath’s World Grace. From this, he obtained numerous spirit qi crystals.","Even until now, Lin Yuan could not be certain if this was because of the Pure Land of Bliss or because of Spirit Qi Condensation.","Although Spirit Lock no longer prevented Morbius from gaining new abilities, it could not gain a new ability every time it increased its grade.","Morbius’ gaining of abilities seemed to be coincidental.","When Morbius evolved to Diamond grade, it gained a new ability called Spirit Lock Filling.","Spirit Lock Filling’s effects would fill an empty spirit-lock slot so that Morbius’ evolution or improvement would not be affected. The ability could also be used for multiple grades. If a spirit-locked fey’s grade had reached the limit, Spirit Lock Filling could be used to remove the limit so that Morbius’ evolution would not be impacted.","This ability greatly increased Morbius’ margin of error. There was also no urgency for Lin Yuan to find a new fey to spirit lock now that he had contracted the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom. He could just use Spirit Lock Filling to fill the empty slot.","Lin Yuan had two Endless Gems he had not used to unlock the spirit-locked feys. One of them came from the subterranean world, while the other came from the alien insect world.","Presently, Lin Yuan did not have any good options for earth- or insect-species feys.","Lin Yuan did not want to force matters when it came to spirit-locking feys. When he spirit locked a fey, he had to ensure it would help with Morbius’ grade evolution and integrate perfectly into Lin Yuan’s combat system.","Lin Yuan intended to wait until Morbius evolved to Sovereign/Creation before he picked a fey to spirit lock.","After all, he had no idea how long he had to wait before Morbius could evolve to Sovereign/Creation.","Lin Yuan had become an A-rank spirit qi professional.","A-rank spirit qi professionals needed to cross an enormous gap in order to reach S-rank. This was not something that could be accomplished in a short span of time.","Lin Yuan told Morbius softly, “Partner, let’s begin! Do you need Eternal Source’s help when you are evolving?”","Morbius said cheerfully, “Partner, based on my memory, we are in a Class 1 world. The World Cleansings that appear in Class 1 worlds won’t be able to affect me, so there’s no need for you to worry.","“I said that I might cause a large commotion because I will be undergoing my evolution while containing the auras of six spirit-locked feys. The auras of the six spirit-locked feys will definitely alter the World Cleansing. However, there is no cause for concern.”","Once Morbius was done with its explanation, Lin Yuan felt his wrist grow hot, and Morbius started spinning as it flew off from Lin Yuan’s wrist.","There were ten Endless Gems embedded in Morbius’ indentations.","The treasures from the dimensional worlds had been produced after Morbius tempered the energy from the Endless Gems.","They could not be produced simply from piecing two Endless Gems together. Otherwise, powerful lifeforms from the dimensional worlds would already have formed contracts with the treasures and used them to take over the dimensional worlds.","Morbius had looked plain when it was on Lin Yuan’s wrist. But now, it looked extremely extravagant.","There were intricate patterns carved all over Morbius, and it seemed as though they could form the totems of all the creatures in the world when they were pieced together.","The patterns were so intricate they were almost hypnotizing, but when one focused, every line would become extremely clear.","When Morbius released its aura, a hole larger than that of regular World Cleansings appeared in the sky.","Lin Yuan looked at the hole and saw that there were smaller holes within the large one. The small holes were all overlapping, and one could not determine where they ended. It was impossible to tell where each one started and ended.","At that moment, the holes were all spewing the World Cleansing’s dark clouds, flaming clouds, lightning-filled clouds, poisonous clouds, lava, hail, thunderbolts, and rocks. Every type of World Cleansing that Lin Yuan had seen and not seen yet were all crashing down towards Morbius.","All ten Endless Gems on Morbius’ body lit up simultaneously.","They started absorbing the attacks from the World Cleansings according to their individual types.","Eternal Source used his aura to create a 500-square-kilometer cage around the area. Otherwise, the shocks would be throughout the entire Radiance Federation.","Normally, a fey’s World Cleansing would not last more than two hours if they had no one helping them and they had to endure all the attacks on their own.","However, Morbius’ World Cleansing lasted five days and five nights before it finally ended.","The World Grace of other Myth Breed feys always appeared as a white mist of energy.","But once Morbius was done with its World Cleansing, a waterfall of white fluid flowed out from the hole. The fluid-like World Grace crashed down on Morbius like violent rapids.","Lin Yuan almost bit through his tongue when he saw that.","Although he had already done all he could to quell the commotion that Morbius was causing, he had not expected Morbius’ World Grace to be so startling.","Morbius rapidly absorbed the waterfall-like World Grace.","Morbius was like a black hole, gobbling all of the World Grace.","But the white fluid World Grace was just the beginning, and Lin Yuan soon realized something was wrong.","The World Grace pouring out from the hole turned faint gold before intensifying into a deep gold.","It took three days before the World Grace stopped pouring out from the hole.","Once Morbius was done absorbing the World Grace, the rust-colored light around it exploded.","Lin Yuan saw that cracks had appeared on Morbius.","Morbius’ shape as a bangle had not changed, but a larger and collar-like Morbius had appeared.","The collar-like Morbius had 13 slashes, dividing the collar into 14 sections.","The collar was very plain and did not have many accessories attached to it.","But the rust-colored light made the plain collar seem quaint and stylish.","The collar and bangle spun around before returning to Lin Yuan’s body.","At that moment, Morbius, who looked similar to Lin Yuan, appeared in a spirit form next to him.","This was the first time that Morbius was appearing in the real world. Previously, it could only maintain its form in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Morbius looked at Lin Yuan, who was close by, and patted Lin Yuan’s left shoulder forcefully, just like Liu Jie would do.","“Partner, I can meet with you in this human form even if you’re not in the Spirit Lock spatial zone! Breathing the air of the real world feels much freer than holing up in the Spirit Lock spatial zone!”","Lin Yuan touched Morbius’ right shoulder and forcefully patted it.","At that moment, Lin Yuan and Morbius looked like a set of twins.","Lin Yuan could tell that Morbius was very happy and could not help but smile. “Partner, will you be able to slowly gain a tangible body as you continue to increase your grade and quality?”","Morbius was silent momentarily before it said with uncertainty, “That is possible, but I can’t say for sure what will happen after my evolution. The Spirit Lock spatial zone has been locked. A small portion of the World Grace I absorbed is being used to strengthen the Spirit Lock spatial zone. The renovation will take at least a month.","“I do have a piece of good news, which is that Klein Hub will also be strengthened alongside the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Once strengthened, Klein Hub will become large enough to transport Sky Sea!","“I have moved all of the lifeforms in the Spirit Lock spatial zone to the vicinity of the Pure Land of Bliss. They won’t be affected by the renovation of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","“I also intentionally used some of the World Grace to temper the Elemental Shellfish in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. The Elemental Shellfish will probably provide you with a pleasant surprise!”","While Morbius was speaking, Lin Yuan used True Data to check on it.","[Fey Name]: Morbius","[Fey Species]: ???","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Mystery","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[True Data]: All complicated information that is invisible to the eye is turned into data. Information that is turned into data might contain truth that cannot be distinguished on the surface.","[Calm Mind]: Passive ability. Effects of Calm Mind can be improved according to the fey’s grade. Calm Mind can stabilize the mind and has a certain probability of resisting negative conditions.","[Spirit Qi Condensation]: Gather the spirit qi in the air and Spirit Lock spatial zone. The gathered spirit qi will form spirit qi crystals that can enhance feys and source-type lifeforms.","[Spirit Lock Filling]: An empty spirit lock slot will be filled, and Morbius’ evolution and improvement will not be affected. Multiple grade slots can be filled, and a spirit-locked fey’s evolution limit can also be removed.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spirit Lock]: Morbius’ spatial zone can be used to nurture feys. The initial grade of the fey that Morbius’ spatial zone can nurture must not be higher than Morbius’ grade. Morbius isn’t able to increase its grade by itself, so its grade will be increased along with the fey’s grade that it nurtures.","[Pure Land of Bliss]: The Spirit Lock spatial zone will produce soil that is great for recovering near-death fey’s injuries. The grade of Morbius and the dying fey will determine the fey’s recovery time.","[Klein Hub]: Swallow and bind the dimensional hub that connects to the dimensional world into the Spirit Lock spatial zone. During the binding process, the lifeforms and items in the Spirit Lock spatial zone will enter the connected dimensional world. However, the dimensional world’s lifeforms will not be able to enter the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","[14 Totem Seeds]: The seeds of 14 totems can be given to 14 separate species. The 14 species will use their faith and power sources to incubate the totem seeds, enabling them to grow into totem trees. The species will then be engraved on the neck as totems. Once a species is carved onto the neck, the entire species’ lifeform rank will be raised and given a unique totem ability.","[Normal Spirit Lock]:","Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade): Suzerain I/Myth I","[Elite Spirit Lock]:","Five-Clawed Spirit Dragon: Suzerain I/Myth I","[Bronze Spirit Lock]:","Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly: Suzerain I/Myth I","[Silver Spirit Lock]","Praying Universe Soul Whale: Suzerain I/Myth I","[Gold Spirit Lock]","Perfect Touch Wisteria: Sovereign II/Creation V","[Platinum Spirit Lock]","Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom: Suzerain I/Myth I","[Diamond Spirit Lock]","(Spirit Lock Filling) (One-use only)"]},{"number":2618,"title":"Chapter 2618 Forage Moon: Six Moons!","paragraphs":["2618 Forage Moon: Six Moons!","Lin Yuan immediately looked happy when he heard what Morbius said.","Morbius’ words were nothing but good news to Lin Yuan.","After Sky Sea evolved to Myth Breed, its body became so large that Lin Yuan could not transport it back to the main world through Klein Hub.","After taking control of the Freedom Federation’s royalty, Lin Yuan could use the Class 6 marsh dimensional rift in the Freedom Federation as he pleased.","But if he used the Class 6 marsh dimensional rift to transport Sky Sea, he would end up exposing the secret of Sky Sea.","It was true that the Moon Empress had taken control of all of the Freedom Federation’s royalty. However, many people were still in the Freedom Federation, and he could not be certain that Tower Canon did not have spies hiding there.","Lin Yuan did not want to expose the secret of Sky Sea and give Tower Canon a chance to target it.","But if Klein Hub became large enough that Sky Sea could be transported through it, Lin Yuan could bring Sky Sea to the main world with no issues.","Hu Quan could then continue building Sky City on Sky Sea’s back in the main world.","This would save Lin Yuan the effort of having to enter the marsh world periodically to deliver resources to Hu Quan.","Besides increasing the size of Klein Hub and the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Morbius’ evolution also refined the Elemental Shellfish in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","There were more than 50 Elemental Shellfish in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","It was likely that the elemental pearls produced by these refined Elemental Shellfish would break through the current limits of the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","These highly pure elemental resources would allow Lin Yuan to increase his subordinates’ powers when it came to water, earth, wind, and fire elements. It was even possible that their bloodlines would be evolved.","Once Lin Yuan arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, these elemental pearls would allow him to rapidly break ground and launch his plans.","It was a shame that feys like the Ice Sealing Frozen Carps and Wood-Building Winged Sandflies, which could also produce highly pure elemental resources, did not produce resources in the same way that the Elemental Shellfish produced the elemental pearls. As such, there was no way to evolve them in the same way.","Lin Yuan had the Element Well and could further raise the purity of the elemental pearls.","The Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil would be blessed in the future!","With these extremely pure types of elemental energy, there was a high chance that the Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil would evolve again.","Lin Yuan had not had the chance to reach the peak of his happiness when Morbius’ new exclusive skill, 14 Totem Seeds, caught his eye. He also understood that the ring on his neck was a result of 14 Totem Seeds.","14 Totem Seeds allowed Lin Yuan to gain 14 totem seeds that he could choose to give to 14 different species. The species he chose would use their faith and sources of energy to nurture the totem seeds and grow them into totem trees.","When the totem trees were grown, the species would be added to the totem carving on his neck. The entire species’ life rank would also be raised, and they would gain a unique totem ability.","As of now, Lin Yuan did not know if there was a relationship between the totem abilities and abilities and exclusive skills. But he believed that an ability from Morbius would not be weaker than an exclusive skill!","For now, Lin Yuan did not know which species he should give the totem seeds to.","After thinking about it for some time, he picked the mermaids and Hundred Questions Beasts.","The Hundred Questions Beasts could gain Creation Master abilities after evolving and could also be nurtured to teach other lifeforms. This made them worth nurturing even when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan chose the mermaids because he could be considered one of them. If he gave a totem seed to the mermaids to nurture into a totem tree, Lin Yuan would also gain a totem ability. This way, he would be hitting two birds with one stone.","When Morbius saw Lin Yuan using True Data to check on it, it said with a smile, “Partner, my True Data ability became stronger after I evolved to Myth Breed! I will be able to display the data of all lifeforms of the spirit-fire level and below!”","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up.","The strengthening of True Data would improve Lin Yuan’s ability to check on other experts.","True Data also allowed Lin Yuan to assess whether the target possessed power beyond the spirit-fire level!","No matter how skilled at masking the target was, Lin Yuan would be able to see through them with ease!","Morbius’ evolution had caused a large commotion.","Luckily, Eternal Source was there to release his Afterlife Realm aura and block out the outside world. This kept the commotion from alerting the Royal Capital and Ascending Dragon City.","Moreover, all of the World Cleansing and World Grace had landed on Morbius and had not disturbed the surrounding environment in the slightest!","After the evolution, Lin Yuan did not linger here and left with Morbius. He rushed to the Radiant Moon Palace using Node Transportation.","Morbius was done with its evolution, and Lin Yuan could finally have a good chat with the Moon Empress!","...","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan did not know that something big had happened in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","This event had shaken up many of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ factions.","The Sky Beyond the Clouds was split into four universes: north, south, east, and west. There were millions of factions in the four universes.","The experts from the four universes had all witnessed 1/3 of the fates of the four universes being drained in the short span of a few hours!","The ‘hour’ was the most insignificant unit of measurement to the lifeforms from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The Sky Beyond the Clouds’ minions went into seclusion for centuries. If they came out before a millennium had passed, it would be considered a short period of seclusion.","This event went beyond the understanding of many factions, and the ‘holiness’ of Honor Absent Palace looked toward the dome in the direction of the East Universe.","A taboo legend surfaced in his mind as he looked at the cascading stars. The legend alluded to the winds of change.","Once the legend came to pass, there would be 14 species left that would become the pillars of every world.","...","The elder from Faerie Institution, which was located in the South Universe, was in his treehouse. He palmed the jade-like fruit in his hand as he mumbled, “If the legend is true, we faeries must secure one of the seeds!”","...","This event did not cause any obvious changes to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It only generated topics for conversation.","However, a large hidden storm was brewing below the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The factions with a certain amount of power were all yearning, fearing, and waiting for something.","...","The Moon Empress had found out about how Lin Yuan had arrived at the foot of Leaning Moon Mountain a few days ago but left in a hurry due to an unknown reason.","If the Moon Empress did not believe Lin Yuan could handle himself, she would have pursued this matter. She would be afraid Lin Yuan had encountered a problem he could not solve but was unwilling to ask her for help.","But the Moon Empress now knew how capable Lin Yuan was, so she did not probe into the matter. Instead, she waited silently in the Radiant Moon Palace for Lin Yuan to come to see her once he was done with what he needed to do.","Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress spoke for an entire day after he arrived at the Radiant Moon Palace.","Next, he used the few days of free time before the Major Federation Union began to take the Moon Empress to the subterranean and alien insect worlds to obtain their moons through her sacred source lifeform, Forage Moon.","With the main world’s moon included, Forage Moon had taken control of six moons.","If the Moon Empress wanted, she could release six moons into the sky simultaneously and cause hell to rain down on earth!","The Moon Empress detected Forage Moon’s current strength and recognized Lin Yuan’s significant contribution to her newfound power, far more than she, his Master, had ever assisted him.","This realization left the Moon Empress feeling a profound sense of shame. Nevertheless, there was nothing she could do about it. He had become too formidable!","Even if she did not want him to be strong-headed and wanted to insist on helping him, he was already astonishingly strong.","Previously, the Moon Empress feared she would not have the power to stand her ground. But now, with Forage Moon, she could take on the Mirror God and God of Fools during the Major Federation Union. Even if she did not already have them under her control, she could retain control as the head of the Major Federation Union.","...","In the evening, Lin Yuan returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion. Liu Jie would bring the last batch of Land Imps to the Radiance Federation tonight.","When the Land Imps were being gathered in the subterranean world, almost 40,000 Vein Land Imps had been discovered.","There were only 40,000 Vein Land Imps in the entire enormous subterranean world!","This showed just how lucky Lin Yuan had been to have encountered Heavy Mountain in the Class 3 subterranean dimensional rift in the Startling Lines Continent!","Lin Yuan did not instruct Rock Underworld, Hollow Earth, and Mountain Furrow to send the 40,000 Vein Land Imps to the Radiance Federation.","Vein Land Imps were much more capable of building than Land Imps. However, Lin Yuan felt that the Vein Land Imps’ talents would be better used digging up and tapping into mineral veins!","The 40,000 Vein Land Imps could work with the other subterranean Dictators and Apostles to rapidly discover and harvest from the mineral veins.","The Ten Thousand River Rock Willow could also help to locate the mineral veins.","Due to the existence of the Mine-Birthing Well, the subterranean world would never run out of mineral resources. Even if a large proportion of the mineral resources was harvested, the Mine-Birthing Well only needed some time for its effects to work before the mineral resources in the subterranean world’s mineral resources would be replenished.","The mineral resources in the main world were limited.","The Radiance Federation’s store of resources was only equivalent to that of one of the subterranean world’s four mine districts! This was an undeniable fact!","Even if the Major Federation Union could progress smoothly and the other factions were willing to follow the Radiance Federation’s lead, they would not be willing to cough up their own mineral resources to help the Radiance Federation build up their defenses. It would be better if the Radiance Federation drew on the subterranean world’s supply to source for resources for their defense.","Lin Yuan had not yet asked Hu Quan to draw up a blueprint for the Radiance Federation’s fortification.","Firstly, Hu Quan’s focus was on the construction taking place on Sky Sea’s back. The construction of Sky City on Sky Sea’s back was the foundation of Sky City itself. Secondly, Hu Quan’s skills lay in intricate designs and beautification rather than defense and fortification.","There were many Class 5 Spirit Craftsmen in the Radiance Federation, and the Moon Empress had already gathered all of them.","When the Class 5 Spirit Craftsmen understood the situation and learned of its urgency, they decided to carry out the building of the defenses in three stages.","The first stage had already been completed within five days.","Before Liu Jie returned to the Radiance Federation, he had handed over his work to the Moon Empress, who then held a discussion with Lin Yuan.","For the past few days, the Land Imps had already created many 50-meter-thick metal-type stone boards as per Lin Yuan’s request. There were layers of metal spiritual ingredients within each metal-type stone board.","Three layers of Crushing Soul Gold formed a thick mesh at the bottom that water could only penetrate.","The Land Imps were gifted at combining metal with metal, metal with stone, and stone with stone.","Once the final batch of Land Imps arrived, they could get into full swing!","Some of the Radiance Federation’s royalty suggested they should wait until the Major Federation Union began before they started building the base.","That would demonstrate their formidability to the other federations and show them just how powerful the Radiance Federation was!","However, after their discussion, Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress had decided against this.","The Radiance Federation’s formidability was already on display. Even the Freedom Federation had submitted to the Radiance Federation, so there was no need for the Radiance Federation to further demonstrate their formidability.","Time was required to enable safety. The other defensive work could wait to be built right before the disaster broke out, but the metal and stone boards had to be laid down first.","The Land Imps would not cause much disturbance to the Radiance Federation’s regular citizens while working underground. All they would feel was the occasional tremor.","...","The Land Imps quickly spread out, beginning at the Royal Capital and fanning across various locations within the Radiance Federation. Thousands of Land Imps positioned themselves at the Federation’s city borders. The unique metal-type stone boards were laid both inside and outside the territories.","As the metal-type stone boards covered every corner of the Radiance Federation, their deployment extended beyond its borders.","Upon Liu Jie’s return to the Radiance Federation, he reassumed leadership over the Land Imps. Immediately, he scoured the markets, selecting cooking ingredients to bring back to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","It had been a considerable amount of time since Liu Jie had last prepared a meal for Lin Yuan, and he felt a sense of unease over the delay.","Once back at the Return from Faraway Mansion, Liu Jie set about preparing a meal for Lin Yuan. Afterward, he had plans to journey to the Midnight Palace to establish contracts with the remaining insect-species carcinoma feys.","He intended to control these feys to combat the dead spirits effectively. As long as he didn’t restrain these carcinoma feys’ abilities, they would reach their full potential.","The insect-species carcinoma feys Liu Jie sought to command possessed the remarkable ability to consume soul fire, dead aura, bones, and toxins. These dead spirits would serve as a delectable feast for some of these feys!"]},{"number":2619,"title":"Chapter 2619 The Attacking Bai Qinghuan!","paragraphs":["2619 The Attacking Bai Qinghuan!","The thought of this filled Liu Jie with excitement.","This meant that Liu Jie would use his power to protect the Radiance Federation he loved. Furthermore, he wanted to show Lin Yuan how much he had grown!","For dinner, Liu Jie made grilled seafood, red braised meat, ribs, and passionfruit-roasted beef.","Since he and Lin Yuan were the only ones in the Return from Faraway Mansion and Lin Yuan did not have as large of an appetite as Wen Yu did, Liu Jie did not make too much food.","Lin Yuan was never the type to waste food. It was actually the opposite, as Lin Yuan was very frugal regarding food despite possessing numerous resources that would allow him to create batch after batch of experts.","Since Lin Yuan liked eating meat and all of the dishes were meat dishes, Liu Jie used fresh jujubes to make a jujube punch to serve as a drink and dessert.","Lin Yuan had been very busy. Aside from when he was sleeping, Lin Yuan rarely had the chance to have a proper meal.","Lin Yuan usually filled his nutritional needs with the Soldier Ration Radish leaves so that he would not have to use up his time eating.","Now that he was getting to eat Liu Jie’s food again after such a long time had passed, Lin Yuan was filled with contentment and bliss.","Little Flower and Little Grass were studying in the Spirit Qi Occupation School in the Royal Capital.","There happened to be a summer camp now, and Lin Yuan had registered for both Little Flower and Little Grass to attend.","Qin Lun had been sent to Qin Yu’s side two months ago, so he no longer lived in the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Luckily, there were still 20 Hundred Questions Beasts that Lin Yuan had yet to evolve in the Return from Faraway Mansion to manage the place.","The Return from Faraway Mansion was running smoothly, and Master Hong Shen was living right next to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Zhang Xiaobai, Xin Ying, Lu Pinru, and Tan Ran had already started participating in the qualifying rounds as the Dome Guild Club reserve team. They needed to pass the qualifying rounds before they were given the ticket to participate in the S Tournament’s elimination rounds.","It would be easy for the four of them to earn the ticket to participate in the S Tournament.","All of them were disciples whom Master Hong Shen had taught personally. Not even the main members of top factions were always lucky enough to have a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master as their master!","Lu Pinru and Wen Yu had created a fashion brand called Pinru’s Home. The brand was considered a luxury one and used luxury resources like elemental pearls, jade-textured wood, and various types of gems to adorn the clothes that the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce then sold. Sometimes, the top custom-made clothes were also auctioned off on Star Web. As a result, Lu Pinru was swimming in money.","Lu Pinru was the only one of the four who had joined Sky City.","After dinner, Liu Jie put the dishes away and sat beside Lin Yuan. He looked at him with a slightly worried gaze and asked, “Lin Yuan, is there really no way to reverse Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan?”","Lin Yuan did not reply to Liu Jie immediately. Instead, he handed Liu Jie a hot cup of Three Treasures Tea and said, “Big Brother Liu, if there was a way to reverse this, I wouldn’t be sitting here now!”","Two years had passed since Lin Yuan became a spirit qi professional.","He had been reborn into this world and would be turning 19 years old soon.","Even if he had turned 19 years old two years ago, it would be impossible for him to stop Tower Canon’s plan.","There was no way to reverse death aura in the ground that had seeped into ley lines as they would have immediately corroded them.","Even if Lin Yuan found out about this 19 years ago, all he would be able to do was do his best to set up defenses for the main world so that he would be able to prepare for Tower Canon’s plan in advance.","Liu Jie’s lips curled upwards when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","Liu Jie could imagine what the apocalypse that involved all the lifeforms that had ever lived in the world turning into dead spirits would look like. Such an apocalypse would last for thousands of years and might not end even after more than ten generations had come and passed.","The sixth epoch would begin with the apocalypse, and it would last long into the progression of the epoch.","Liu Jie did not want to see such a day arrive, but there was nothing he would be able to do about a situation that even rendered Lin Yuan helpless.","When he saw the expression on Liu Jie’s face, Lin Yuan handed him a jujube.","“Big Brother Liu, we have the ability to make change happen if we put in the effort. The only thing we can do is to face this crisis bravely. Luckily, we won’t be going into this crisis completely vulnerable but with advance preparations made.”","Morbius regained some of its memories after it evolved to Myth Breed. This allowed Lin Yuan to understand what a Class 1 world was and how a Class 1 world could be promoted to a Class 2 world.","The key point to promoting a Class 1 world to Class 2 is to combine that world with all the dimensional worlds that it was linked to.","Once a Class 1 world was combined with all the dimensional worlds it was linked to, its class would be promoted.","The key to combining the main world and the dimensional worlds was the treasures of the five dimensional worlds that Lin Yuan possessed.","If Lin Yuan wanted to, he could help the main world promote to a Class 2 world.","Since that was the case, Lin Yuan wondered if he could combine the main world with the five dimensional worlds after the Sleeper’s Revival plan began.","The dimensional worlds were separate from the main world’s ley lines. Thus, their ley lines would not be affected by the death aura after they combined with the main world.","Moreover, the dimensional lifeforms would also be able to effectively take on the dead spirits. Otherwise, given the number of humans and feys in the main world, there were far too few of them to be able to confidently take on the dead spirits.","This was why the Moon Empress was filled with despair and negativity when she learned about the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","Liu Jie nodded seriously. Since he could not prevent the disaster from happening, he could only do what Lin Yuan was doing, which was to try his best!","When Liu Jie went to the Midnight Palace, Lin Yuan left to observe the Land Imps’ work so he could assess the current situation and estimate how long it would take before the Radiance Federation’s defenses were completed.","Wen Yu was not the only one of Lin Yuan’s subordinates skilled at governance. Bai Qinghuan was also talented in this area.","However, their specific skill sets were different, as Wen Yu was skilled at resource allocation while Bai Qinghuan excelled at setting up attack and defense mechanisms.","Thus, Lin Yuan decided to bring Bai Qinghuan back from the Great Lush Federation. Weng Queji, the Class 5 Creation Master, came with her.","Bai Qinghuan had been assisting Jin Qianxun in the Great Lush Federation and managing the harbor’s construction.","Bai Qinghuan had given a fair amount of input for constructing the harbor. She insisted that it had to be large enough to host six Island Whales.","When Lin Yuan found out about this, he praised Bai Qinghuan but did not call for her and assign her to different tasks. This had left her feeling rather disappointed.","Bai Qinghuan had noticed some time ago that Lin Yuan did not care much for the Great Lush Federation. He was only concerned with the Great Lush Federation because of the harbor. Aside from providing resources, he basically allowed the Great Lush Federation to do whatever it wanted.","No matter how much she achieved in the Great Lush Federation, Lin Yuan would not notice it.","Bai Qinghuan had the Thoughts Letter Paper and could contact Lin Yuan. But she could never find a reason to do so. She could not contact him just to ask him to pay attention to her!","Just as she was reaching her wits’ end, an opportunity appeared in front of her.","As an official member of Sky City who had sworn her loyalty to Lin Yuan, she had learned about Tower Canon’s plan. Hence, she knew just how important this task that Lin Yuan had given her was! It just so happened that this was a task that she excelled at.","Bai Qinghuan did not make any promises to Lin Yuan. She intended to prove her value to him with the completion of the defense setup.","When she found out that Lin Yuan wanted an estimate of how much longer it would be before the metal-type stone planks were finished being laid down, Bai Qinghuan told Lin Yuan about her calculations.","“Young Master, based on the calculations I made according to the real-time circumstances, it will take around 35 days before all of the metal-type stone planks are done being laid down in the Radiance Federation, even with the 45,000,000 Land Imps involved in the project.","“This is because there are hard rocks in many places in the Radiance Federation that the Land Imps need to clear away before they can lay down the metal-type stone planks.","“Additionally, the metal-type stone planks need to be created, and it takes time to both create them as well as transport the materials. Aside from laying down the metal-type stone planks, building a metal wall around the entire Radiance Federation will only take ten days.","“The wall will be built outward, and there will be nine walls in total. The metal-type stone planks can also be laid down below the walls to prevent the dead spirits from invading externally!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Bai Qinghuan’s estimated time was shorter than what Lin Yuan had in mind, so this was good news to him.","Lin Yuan really liked someone like Bai Qinghuan, who could provide detailed answers to every question as well as anticipate what the person’s next question would be.","When Bai Qinghuan was done answering Lin Yuan’s question, she bit her lip and asked Lin Yuan seriously, “Young Master, we have built defenses underground, but I think that we need to cover more areas. We should also set up effective defenses for the sky!","“All of the dead spirits will indeed be rising from the ground, but some of them who are able to fly will be able to cross the seas and oceans to attack the Radiance Federation when we least expect it!”","Bai Qinghuan’s question was one that Lin Yuan had been ruminating over but had yet to come up with a good solution for.","They could separate the ground by using metal-type stone planks, but there was no way to build defenses for the sky!","Furthermore, the Radiance Federation was so expansive that Lin Yuan did not have enough experts under him to cover the entire area!","But once he found out how he could promote a Class 1 world to Class 2, Lin Yuan saw a way out.","Lin Yuan could use the Radiance Federation as the center as he began combining the five dimensional worlds with the main world. This would ensure no dead spirits rose in the vicinity of the Radiance Federation.","If these dead spirits wanted to reach the Radiance Federation, they must first cross the five dimensional worlds. This would greatly diminish their numbers.","The dimensional lifeforms would kill the dead spirits that could fly.","Dimensional lifeforms were very proficient at reproduction. For example, the alien insect species would even use each other as food.","The dead spirits might consume the dimensional lifeforms for sustenance as well!","This would give Lin Yuan the time to continue building the base even after the Sleeper’s Revival plan began.","The dead spirits below the Radiance Federation would be killed first, and the other federations could choose to rebuild themselves within the five dimensional worlds so they could team up with the Radiance Federation to take on the dead spirits.","This would address the issue of the lack of land as well.","This was the only plan that Lin Yuan could come up with that would solve the issue.","“I have a way to solve the issue of the attacking dead spirits. Hurry up and lay down the metal-type stone planks in the Radiance Federation!”","Bai Qinghuan was rather shocked. She did not know what Lin Yuan’s plan was. But she did not care what his plan was. All that she cared about was that she would be able to show her worth to Lin Yuan.","Bai Qinghuan was unempathetic by nature and did not care what happened to the main world.","She was only staying with Lin Yuan so she could earn his praise and become more important to him so he would treat her better!","“Young Master, I will make sure to do a good job!”","Many of the Spirit Craftsmen had negative opinions about the plan to lay down metal-type stone planks. They felt that it would affect the harvesting of underground resources.","The Spirit Craftsmen had reached Class 4 and 5 but were very short-sighted.","Land Imps that were Class 10 and below would have trouble breaking through the metal-type stone planks, but those above Class 10 would be able to easily break the metal-type stone planks to harvest the underground resources.","It would take tens of thousands of years to kill all of the dead spirits that rose up due to the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","However, the human world would not stop developing either. They could only stand a chance of solving their development issues with time.","“I only asked the Spirit Craftsmen to devise plans but did not discuss my decisions with them. Young Master, I can’t be bothered to give them an explanation. We might not even be able to survive, but they are trying to talk to me about harvesting and developing resources!”","Lin Yuan shook his head vexedly when he heard what Bai Qinghuan said.","It was unlikely that anyone’s heart was blacker than Bai Qinghuan’s.","Bai Qinghuan seemed to be complaining about the Spirit Craftsmen. Still, she was actually asking him to give her full authority over the construction of the Radiance Federation’s defenses so that she would not be restrained by anyone else.","However, this matter was of paramount importance. Lin Yuan could not allow Bai Qinghuan to call the shots on everything. He needed someone of substantial authority who would be able to restrain her."]},{"number":2620,"title":"Chapter 2620 The Spirit Lock Spatial Zone’s Evolution is Complete!","paragraphs":["2620 The Spirit Lock Spatial Zone’s Evolution is Complete!","“You don’t have to mind what the Spirit Craftsmen say. You can make the decisions as you see fit.”","Bai Qinghuan was happy when she heard this because she knew that Lin Yuan had understood the meaning behind her words.","But quickly, Lin Yuan’s tone changed. “Cicada Song, a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty, oversees city management. He’s quite visionary. You’ll be collaborating with him. If you excel, he’ll inform me.","“Bai Qinghuan, remember, this world is vast. Our current home is just a fraction of it. If you perform admirably, I might even take you to the Sky Beyond the Clouds with me!”","Bai Qinghuan had been worried when she heard that Lin Yuan would send her to work with a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","Working with a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty would place many more shackles on her than working with the Spirit Craftsmen. She could ignore the Spirit Craftsmen, but the Radiance Federation’s royalty could all be considered Lin Yuan’s elders. There was no way she could ignore what they said.","The member of royalty that managed the Radiance Federation’s cities had to have clear opinions and plans for every matter.","Bai Qinghuan knew that once she started working with Cicada Song, she would have to discuss every decision with him and that the final decision-making power lay in his hands.","However, what Lin Yuan said next caused all of Bai Qinghuan’s worries to evaporate.","He made her a sincere promise, and this allowed her to see light in her future.","If someone who yearned for a chance was promised a bright future, he would definitely do everything he could to grab onto the opportunity!","This summed up Bai Qinghuan exactly!","Bai Qinghuan worked hard to fight for the chance to gain authoritative control over the construction of the Radiance Federation’s base because she wanted Lin Yuan to see her capabilities. She fervently prayed that Lin Yuan would give her a chance.","She was very afraid that Lin Yuan would not be able to see her contributions and that all the merit would be attributed to the Spirit Craftsmen. This was why she had intentionally discriminated against them.","But now, Lin Yuan promised that if she did well, he would take her with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, allowing her to remain by his side.","This was what Bai Qinghuan dreamed of. If she remained by Lin Yuan’s side, it would mean that she was part of Sky City’s upper echelon.","Furthermore, given Lin Yuan’s power, he could bend the main world to his will. But he would have to encounter many challenges at the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Bai Qinghuan was skilled at military strategy, so Lin Yuan would definitely have to depend on her abilities. She would also have more chances to demonstrate and increase her worth.","“Young Master, I will complete the building of the base once I’ve run every decision past Cicada Song. Nothing will go wrong!”","Lin Yuan waved his hand to gesture to Bai Qinghuan to head back so she could continue her managing duties.","The last part of Bai Qinghuan’s response was amazing in a strange way.","By saying that she was going to run every decision past Cicada Song, it was as though she was saying that Cicada Song would be able to sway her decisions. It seemed as though she was pushing all the responsibility to Cicada Song. The last part she mentioned about how nothing would go wrong seemed to emphasize this intention.","Intelligent people were able to grasp your meaning easily, so speaking with them did not require much energy.","But when speaking with overly intelligent people, one would have to constantly wonder if more meaning was hidden between their words!","Lin Yuan had remained in the Radiance Federation these past few days. But he had dispatched out Zhou Luo, Endless Summer, as well as Duan He, who had just returned with the white-clothed followers.","Although the Radiance Federation had called for and was hosting this meeting of the Major Federation Union under its status as one of the three major federations, there were still some federations that were not going to be participating.","Hence, it would not be realistic to try and obtain all of the Continent Vein Cores from the Major Federation Union.","Lin Yuan instructed these people, who made up the backbone of Sky City to lead the tens of Turning Wheel Realm Dictators in collecting the Continent Vein Cores from the factions of the federations who were not able to participate in the Major Federation Union.","Some of these federations only had one or two Class 4 Creation Masters, much less a Class 5 Creation Master. There was no way that they possessed the Continent Vein Cores of the continent where they were located.","In such situations, the member of Sky City would have to search for the Continent Vein Cores on their own before bringing it back.","Lin Yuan was almost done making all of the necessary preparations. All he needed now was time.","He could only hope Tower Canon waited a bit longer before they began their Sleeper’s Revival plan.","Since all Lin Yuan needed to do from now on was come up with plans and strategies, he did not waste time and focused all of this time into nurturing his feys.","Lin Yuan was continuously evolving his feys so that he would be able to promote to S-rank spirit qi professional as soon as possible, and because he wanted to provide the cities with more Bronze grade high quality feys so that the City Guards and reserve City Guards would all be equipped with the best combat tools.","Lin Yuan continued evolving his feys as he waited for the Spirit Lock spatial zone to be unlocked.","Due to the Spirit Lock spatial zone being closed, Lin Yuan had to evolve his feys in the outside world using his own physique, and this took much longer than when he evolved his feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","According to his calculation, the Spirit Lock spatial zone would be opening in another two days.","At this moment, Lin Yuan received a message from Wen Yu.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, I found an extremely dry and hot area here on this side of the Barren Sea. However, it is not technically considered a desert but more like a grassland. The ground is fertile, and there is a high concentration of mud. The ground has just hardened because of the extreme lack of water. This environment is very similar to Peace’s description of the Broiling Rock Continent.","[Wen Yu]: The Astronomical Parliament can sense its members and their general location, but it cannot pinpoint exactly where the members are. I have a few strong Turning Wheel Realm Dictators with me. I don’t want to use such top combat power in searching for Peace. This will affect the speed of my search for the Continent Vein Cores!","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, I hope you can assign some Apostles to me so they can search for Peace and take her back to Sky Bearer City in the Grotto Continent!","Normally, Wen Yu did not like troubling Lin Yuan. However, she could tell which matters were of extreme importance.","Currently, the most important matter to Lin Yuan was the search for the Continent Vein Cores, and everything else came after.","Wen Yu felt that Lin Yuan was extremely kind for being willing to expend effort into searching for Peace.","Peace would be crushed by guilt if she found out that the search for the Continent Vein Cores had been impacted because of the effort spent searching for her.","Wen Yu believed that with Peace’s talent, she could only serve as a leader in the main world at best. There was no way that she would be given the chance to leave the main world with Lin Yuan when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Even if she did go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she could not offer any help.","By contrast, talents like Su Yiren and Yin Lin would definitely be able to accomplish significant achievements when they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","After reading Wen Yu’s message, Lin Yuan felt he needed to travel back to the Grotto Continent through the Space Tunnel.","Once the Spirit Lock spatial zone was unlocked, Lin Yuan intended to send a large group of his subordinates to the other side of the Barren Sea so the exploration and search for the Continent Vein Cores could be completed as soon as possible.","Lin Yuan did not want any entity on the other side of the Barren Sea the chance to fuse with any of the five dimensional worlds.","Even after they expanded to the other side of the Barren Sea, it would remain the most remote and desolate place in the main world.","Chu Ci had stayed with Wen Yu to train with her. Lin Yuan intended to leave Chu Ci with Wen Yu as it would benefit her greatly. Wen Yu could bring Chu Ci back with her once they were done exploring the Barren Sea.","Now that Thick Soil City’s operations were on track, Lin Yuan called Listen back so he could take charge of allocating the resources!","There were specialists in every field. Next to Wen Yu, Listen was the most capable of Sky City’s members at resource allocation!","Without Listen, it would be a struggle for Ta Lei to manage Thick Soil City.","Luckily, Listen had brought with him Qin Yu, who had been by his side for some time. Qin Yu would remain with Ta Lei to support him.","Before heading to the Grotto Continent, Lin Yuan went to the martial arts hall where the spirit qi professionals from various factions were waiting. They were waiting for help to evolve their feys.","Although the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s resources could not be accessed, Morbius’ exclusive skill, Pure Land of Bliss, was separate and could be used.","After the Spirit Lock spatial zone was expanded, it could easily accommodate all the spirit qi crystals.","After Morbius evolved to Myth Breed, the Pure Land of Bliss’ size increased to almost 500 square meters.","Lin Yuan could simultaneously help many feys to evolve their grades. Thus, he could accumulate spirit qi crystals much quicker than before!","Eternal Source could fend off every World Cleansing by flicking his finger. Thus, Lin Yuan would deal with the World Cleansings quickly.","However, it still took an entire day and a half before Lin Yuan finished absorbing the World Grace and Creation World Ley Lines.","This harvest of spirit qi crystals far exceeded Lin Yuan’s previous batch.","After all, the strength of the experts in the Startling Lines Continent could not compare to that of the Radiance Federation!","Lin Yuan was certain that he would be greeted by a giant harvest the next time he entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","At that time, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope would have a lot of work to do!","After helping the Radiance Federation’s experts successfully overcome their World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation, Lin Yuan went to the Space Tunnel near the Class 6 abyss dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan had opened the Space Tunnel that connected to the Grotto Continent because he wanted to give the Radiance Federation a way to harvest the resources from the other side of the Barren Sea.","However, one trip required an immense amount of spatial-type spiritual ingredients. Thus, regardless of what they found on the other side of the Barren Sea, the cost would not even out!","As such, Lin Yuan used the Space Tunnel himself.","But Lin Yuan did not see this as a waste as he would be able to obtain the Continent Vein Cores from the Grotto Continent on the other side of the Barren Sea. The Continent Vein Cores added to his tangible power. The more Continent Vein Cores he obtained, the higher the chances of victory for the Radiance Federation’s experts.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan could not leave Bei Xu to fend for himself.","Lastly, the Ethereal Jellyfish’s main tentacles could be regrown, but it took a long time.","After traveling through the Space Tunnel to arrive at the Grotto Continent, Lin Yuan was once again hit with the pains of long-distance travel.","When he regained clear consciousness, Lin Yuan continued seizing every moment to evolve feys as he waited for the Spirit Lock spatial zone to open.","Lin Yuan told Wen Yu that he was headed to the Grotto Continent but did not call her back.","Wen Yu was drawing up a map while she explored the other side of the Barren Sea.","Lin Yuan would follow Wen Yu’s map to send the Apostles and Dictators to Wen Yu.","The Spirit Mother Federation was always closed off and never associated with the outside world.","Although there was a Class 5 Creation Master in the Spirit Mother Federation, they had no Spirit Mother Envoys.","The Spirit Mother Federation had missed the Major Federation Meeting and was considered unique for a federation with a Class 5 Creation Master.","However, after Bu Po told the Spirit Mother about the circumstances, the Spirit Mother decided to head to the Radiance Federation to attend the first Major Federation Union meeting.","Wo Lun did not have any special feelings for the Violent Wind Federation.","But when the Violent Wind Federation received the invitation from the Radiance Federation, they rushed to the Radiance Federation after weighing the pros and cons.","Su Yiren, the ruler of the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent, also rushed to the Radiance Federation. But she intended on heading to the Iron Hammer Federation first to meet up with Luo Lan before they traveled together.","Recently, all the conversations on the Thoughts Letter Papers had been related to the Major Federation Union meeting.","When Wen Yu became certain that she had found the Broiling Rock Continent, she told Peace about this, finally setting Peace at ease.","The messages on the Thoughts Letter Paper seemed calm, but Lin Yuan knew this was just the calm before the storm.","While he was gathering information about Tower Canon, Tower Canon had to also be accumulating information about him and the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan had also sent a message to Eighth Page Apoptosis so he could contact Seventh Page War and Third Page Eternal Sin.","Every member of Tower Canon possessed somewhat different information. There was a chance that Seventh Page War and Third Page Eternal Sin possessed information that Eighth Page Apoptosis did not know about.","While Lin Yuan was keeping the Thoughts Letter Paper away, Morbius’ voice rang out in his ear, “Friend, the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s evolution is complete. Go in and take a look!”","Morbius’ voice always appeared in Lin Yuan’s head. But this time, Lin Yuan heard it in his ears.","Lin Yuan turned and saw Morbius standing next to him."]},{"number":2621,"title":"Chapter 2621 The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s Opportunity!","paragraphs":["2621 The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s Opportunity!","When he saw Morbius’ half-transparent body, Lin Yuan could not help but laugh. Nothing made him feel more at ease than this feeling of having his closest companion by his side.","Morbius’ ability to tangibly exist in real life proved to Lin Yuan just how significant its evolution was.","Morbius’ evolution made Lin Yuan feel that his hard work had not gone to waste.","Now, he was greatly looking forward to seeing the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s changes, so he immediately headed there. The Spirit Lock spatial zone should be where he was most familiar with, as he had spent the most time here in the past year.","However, once Lin Yuan entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone, he realized he was very unfamiliar with this place.","At first, the Spirit Lock spatial zone was only around 40 square meters large and was akin to a small storage room.","However, he kept this small storage room very tidy.","But regardless of how organized he was, the space was still cramped because the spirit pool and Lin Yuan’s worktable both needed to take up a certain amount of space.","Luckily, as Morbius’ grade continued to increase and the Spirit Lock spatial zone continued to grow larger, Lin Yuan was able to make better use of the space there.","After Morbius evolved to Diamond grade, the Spirit Lock spatial zone grew to 960 square meters.","This space was not only sufficient for Lin Yuan’s needs, but there was enough extra space for Lin Yuan and his feys to move around comfortably.","Lin Yuan had even made the indulgent move of placing a jade-textured white sandalwood recliner in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Hu Quan had made that recliner with details of mountains, rivers, plants, and animals carved all over it. The craftsmanship and love that went into creating it matched that of the red sandalwood longevity fishtank in the Return from Faraway Mansion.","After working under Lin Yuan for over a year, Hu Quan’s Spirit Craftsmanship improved significantly. Even laymen could tell just how high his Spirit Craftsmanship level was from his pieces!","When Lin Yuan slept in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, he lay on the recliner created by Hu Quan.","But now, the Spirit Lock spatial zone was like a miniature dimensional plane. Lin Yuan could no longer see where the Spirit Lock spatial zone ended.","Morbius said seriously, “Partner, this Spirit Lock spatial zone can be considered to be its somewhat complete form. Its size is related to the concentration of spirit qi. As the concentration of spirit qi increases, the size of the Spirit Lock spatial zone will increase. Although you can’t see where the Spirit Lock spatial zone ends, its area is not endless. If we had to calculate the size, it would be around the same size as the Xia Region!”","Lin Yuan was so shocked he could not speak. The place where he was born was now being used as a unit of measurement!","Lin Yuan had been feeling rather apologetic to the feys like the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope that had to spend all of their time in there. After all, the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s space was limited.","For fairies like Brocade Zither that did not require much space to move around, the size of the Spirit Lock spatial zone was not restrictive. But for the feys like the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Gray that needed more space to move and breathe, the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s size caged in their nature.","When a fey’s nature was dampened, it would lower its happiness level.","But now that the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s size had increased significantly, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Gray would take more than an hour to get across a space as large as the Xia Region.","The marsh world was going to be fused with the main world. Thus, Lin Yuan needed to make preparations in the marsh world.","Lin Yuan had considered moving resources into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, but the space had been too small then!","It took almost 50,000 square meters just to plant the Item-Storing Walnut Trees, Soldier Ration Radishes, and the Barren River Orchid Bud that needed to be nurtured by various types of marsh soil.","But now, the Spirit Lock spatial zone had become large enough to solve all of Lin Yuan’s concerns.","It would not just be the Item-Storing Walnut Trees, Soldier Ration Radishes, and Barren River Orchid Bud that would gain a new home, but Genius’ cats, the working space for the Hundred Questions Beasts, and even Sky Sea could be moved to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Regardless of Sky Sea’s size, it would not be larger than the Xia Region.","Lin Yuan intended to dedicate a space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone to Hu Quan so he could work there. He could take some Spirit Craftsmen with him to properly construct and decorate the space there.","The Sunlight King Lotus was housed in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, allowing it to be constantly flooded with light.","When Lin Yuan cultivated the Sunlight King Lotus, he had cultivated 99 of them.","The Sunlight King Lotuses that Master Hong Shen had nurtured could be put to use now.","Besides the Sunlight King Lotus, Lin Yuan had also obtained many plant-type feys that could create weather in the Divine Wood Federation.","Listen was still helping him to search for more of such feys.","However, due to the lack of space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan had been unable to display many of the feys that Listen had found.","If he displayed them now, he would not only be able to further beautify the Spirit Lock spatial zone but would also create an even more conducive environment for Gray to increase its power.","There was no way that the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope and Gray could manage the Spirit Lock spatial zone of this size. It would completely overwhelm them!","Rather than assigning humans to manage the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan preferred to nurture a group of feys who could change into human form.","He had discovered a special fey when he took control of the Great Lush Federation. It was called the Spirit Core Jasmine.","The Spirit Core Jasmine was a fey that required a large amount of spirit qi, but the spirit qi did not need to be of a high purity. Thus, it was not as finicky as other feys and could consume energy ores.","As long as it had sufficient energy ores, it could reproduce as quickly as ants!","If the Spirit Core Jasmine had access to sufficient energy ores, it could evolve to Myth III and change its form in only a few months.","After discovering the Spirit Core Jasmine, many main members of Creation Master families became crazed over contracting it. They had been under the impression they had stumbled on a treasure.","Alas, the Spirit Core Jasmine’s abilities were geared toward those of domestic feys. It would not gain combat abilities even after it reached Myth Breed. However, after it changed its form, it would become a skilled assistant that managed domestic governance and could nurture plants.","It would also emit a fragrance to the surroundings, the scent being similar to a high-quality banana.","This did not mean that the Spirit Core Jasmine could not kill other feys, but only that its combat power was a far cry from that of other Myth III feys.","After all, the Spirit Core Jasmine’s physique was also a factor.","No one could stand having a Myth III fey that a Diamond fey could defeat!","Furthermore, the Spirit Core Jasmine’s looks were plain even after it reached Myth III and evolved to human form. It could even be described as ugly!","Even if a spirit qi professional had warped thoughts and wanted to begin a romance with the Spirit Core Jasmine, they could not bring themselves to do so.","As a result, the popularity of the Spirit Core Jasmine in the Great Lush Federation rapidly diminished.","In every world, there were people with obsessive-compulsive personality types. In the Great Lush Federation, some disciples of secret aristocratic families contracted Spirit Core Jasmines and provided them with high-quality resources. They eventually discovered that the purer the spirit qi that the Spirit Core Jasmines absorbed, they would become more attractive when they transformed into human form. They would also become more skilled at nurturing plants. The fragrance they emitted could also nourish souls, soothe the spirit, and help to increase spiritual energy!","This discovery stirred up a renewed popularity for the Spirit Core Jasmine. But whoever wanted to nurture such a Spirit Core Jasmine would have to invest more resources into nurturing it than other feys.","Spirit qi professionals preferred to nurture feys that could fight rather than those that looked pretty and only had support-type functions.","Lin Yuan felt he could nurture some of the Spirit Core Jasmines in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","With the concentration and production of spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the Spirit Core Jasmines would be nurtured to Myth III quickly.","Then, taking care of all the plants and feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would fall to these Spirit Core Jasmines!","Lin Yuan immediately told Jin Qianxun what he needed.","Jin Qianxun would arrive at the Radiance Federation five days later to attend the Major Federation Union. At that time, he could deliver the resources that Lin Yuan wanted to him.","He also promised he would provide Lin Yuan with the best Spirit Core Jasmines.","Although Jin Qianxun was not considered an outstanding talent, he was still reliably competent!","It was not just the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s size that had increased. Both the spirit pool and Pure Land of Bliss were larger now as well.","The spirit pool was now only slightly smaller than the Submerged Flood Dragon Lake in the Return from Faraway Mansion.","The enlargement of the spirit pool proved two things. The first was that the energy ores in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had become stronger at producing spirit qi.","Energy ores were a very common resource in the main world. Spirit qi could be found in the main world’s air, and energy ores were not a nonrenewable resource.","With support from the main world, Lin Yuan could use as many energy ores as he wanted.","Thus, Lin Yuan placed even more spatial equipment next to the spirit pool and filled them with energy ores.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was very familiar with refilling the energy ores. It could continue performing this job!","Blackie’s Spirit Qi Imprint had changed when it evolved into the Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragon.","Lin Yuan could nurture feys with the dragon-species bloodline and use them to supply spiritual power to Blackie. This increased the accumulation of spiritual power in the Spirit Qi Imprint.","Lin Yuan had moved Blackie to the Submerged Flood Dragon Lake because the spirit pool had been too small.","Lin Yuan now felt that the spirit pool was large enough to move Blackie back in. The Spirit-Gather Goldfish that had awakened their dragon-species bloodlines could also be moved into the spirit pool.","This would not only increase the rate at which Blackie accumulated spirit qi, but the Spirit-Gather Goldfish would also be able to grow much quicker.","The Angelfish of Bliss did not produce their fish coats quickly. But if they were moved to the spirit pool, they could produce fish coats faster.","The spirit pool had already given Lin Yuan an enormous surprise. But the Pure Land of Bliss’ size had increased even more than the spirit pool’s.","The Pure Land of Bliss was now around the same size as the Return from Faraway Mansion. It was clear that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree had benefited significantly.","The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree had been around eight meters tall. But now, it was more than 100 meters tall. There was no limit to the height of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The roots of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree took up the center of the Pure Land of Bliss.","Multiple nests were formed from the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s circling branches.","Previously, when there was only one nest, Chimey was the only one using it. But now, Shiny could also nest in the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree. Gray also found a suitably-sized nest for itself.","When Gray rested in the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree, most of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree was shrouded in mist.","The gold leaves glinted under the light and resembled an ancient magical tree.","Lin Yuan heard Morbius say, “I noticed that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree is very suited to the root energy of the World Grace, so I gave it some. In my opinion, the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree is in a very similar condition to what Gray had experienced. It has reached the limit of a Heaven and Earth Fey and is very close to evolving into a Heavenly Family Fey.”","Lin Yuan was overjoyed and thought, It’s very difficult for feys without the Heavenly Family Fey blood to evolve into Heavenly Family Feys. If Gray’s evolution from a Heaven and Earth Fey into a Heavenly Family Fey is just a coincidence, then how do we explain what is happening to the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree? Is it possible that all the Heaven and Earth Feys in the world have the potential to eventually evolve into Heavenly Family Feys?","However, this was just Lin Yuan’s guess. He intended to discuss this with Purple Love when the opportunity arose.","If that was the case, Lin Yuan felt that he possessed enough resources to nurture more Heavenly Family Feys.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to examine the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s data, Chimey flew at him and said with carefree delight, “Yuan, I can feel that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree will be of much more help to me now that it’s larger!","“When I first evolved to Myth Breed, I felt that the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree was no longer useful to me. But now, it can increase the energy within strange flames! Each time it absorbs a mid-grade strange flame, it will be able to unleash an aura of a high-grade strange flame! I love the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree!”","Lin Yuan was shocked by what Chimey said. He had not expected the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s abilities to change in such a way after it absorbed the World Grace!"]},{"number":2622,"title":"Chapter 2622 Absolute Purity: Elemental Dolls!","paragraphs":["2622 Absolute Purity: Elemental Dolls!","From what Chimey said, the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s boosting of the strange flames would save on the energy within the strange flames.","When Chimey was done speaking, Shiny flew over and told Lin Yuan, “Yuan, the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree can also provide me with energy through the nest! This ability will benefit me significantly!”","Shiny flapped its wings while it spoke. It was very happy with the energy it could receive from the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree.","Gray told Lin Yuan softly, “Yuan, the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree wasn’t of any help to me previously. But the nourishment from the energy from the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree will allow me to absorb weather even quicker!”","Gray’s words led Lin Yuan to begin calmly looking through the data of the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree.","When he looked at the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s data in the past, its abilities and exclusive skills had always been support-type.","Thus, Lin Yuan always saw the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree as a special treasure.","This had not changed in its current data. However, all of its abilities and exclusive skills had improved.","The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree’s name had also changed after it absorbed a large amount of World Grace. It was now called the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree!","The Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree could only boost and nourish phoenix-species feys, but the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree could provide such benefits to all avian-type feys.","This greatly increased its value and strategic significance.","Lin Yuan brought Chimey, Shiny, and Gray to the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree and injected many strange flames into it.","Since he was certain that the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree could transform the strange flames into energy within the next six months, Lin Yuan did not need to pay attention to it.","Lin Yuan had obtained numerous strange flames after taking control of the abyssal world.","Fire-elemental energy was found in high concentrations in the abyssal world, so strange flames were created constantly.","Lin Yuan wanted to inject more strange flames into the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree but had already reached its limit.","Every leaf of the towering Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree had a strange flame attached to it, causing it to emit radiant light.","The light emitted by the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree was even more brilliant than the light from the Sunlight King Lotus. When it reflected off of the white sand of the Pure Land of Bliss, the light was blindingly white!","The Golden Lotus Brocade Pearl’s roots were not far from the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree. Brocade Zither was also a regular guest of the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree.","Shiny had a good relationship with Brocade Zither, Chimey, and Gray, and they were its playmates.","Lin Yuan had left some of them in Sky City so Master Hong Shen and Weng Queji could use them. At the same time, he had given some to the Moon Empress so she could have some in storage that every Class 3 and above Creation Master in the Radiance Federation could use them to help with their nurturing of feys.","In its free time, it either visited the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree’s branches or nuzzled up against the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia, which also sat on its branches.","The Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia had also benefited from the Celestial Destiny Chinese Parasol Tree’s evolution.","Lin Yuan did not need to strengthen his spiritual energy using the Cinnabar Osmanthus Haworthia’s fruits anymore.","Morbius could fully control its own strength now that it had evolved to Myth Breed. It no longer needed to rely on Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy.","After Morbius returned the spiritual energy to Lin Yuan, he suddenly realized he had sufficient spiritual energy to be considered a genius! It was just that Morbius had been using up so much of it that he was only left with a pathetically meager amount.","Lin Yuan could now use his spiritual energy to easily contract many feys. However, he did not intend on contracting any more feys from the main world. He intended to contract more feys from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","At that moment, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was feeling very conflicted next to the Element Well. It did not know whether it should sort these elemental pearls first or head over to greet Lin Yuan first.","The Elemental Shellfish were producing elemental pearls as quickly as a factory. Every Elemental Shellfish now produced elemental pearls at ten times their original rate.","Although the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was skilled at manipulating wind-elemental energy to sort the elemental pearls into their different types, there were many different grades of elemental pearls, and the wooden chests that Lin Yuan had prepared were almost all completely full.","For the past few days, while the Spirit Lock spatial zone had been evolving, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope finally finished sorting through the spirit qi crystals and counted all of them.","Thus, it stopped paying attention to the Elemental Shellfish. As a result, the elemental pearls piled up into a small mountain!","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was afraid Lin Yuan would think it was slacking. It was clearly a hardworking little antelope and did not want to be misunderstood by Lin Yuan! It was a cute antelope that worked hard! It was the best!","While the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope felt conflicted, Lin Yuan arrived next to it.","When he saw the pile of heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, he knew that the production rate had increased significantly.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan saw the small mountain of elemental pearls sway slightly before three elemental dolls emerged from the pile. They tiptoed down from the pile of elemental pearls.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the elemental dolls.","He saw that they were a sign of the highest purity.","This meant that the Heavenly Maiden Sleet elemental pearls had broken through again.","The Element Well could increase purity and allow Lin Yuan to gain access to elements of high purity.","But aside from the increment in purity, the purity of the entity was determined intrinsically.","If the Element Well could temper elemental energy at will, Lin Yuan would not have to nurture so many feys that could produce pure elemental energy!","The elemental dolls’ purity had reached 99%. So, once the Element Well tempered them, they would achieve absolute purity!","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was still filling the wooden chests with elemental pearls, so Lin Yuan squatted down and affectionately caressed its head. “The production of elemental pearls had increased significantly. Don’t use these wooden chests from now on. I will place a shelf next to the Element Well and fill it with custom Diamond fey storage boxes.","“From now on, you can concentrate on collecting the elemental pearls and spirit qi crystals. As for other tasks like laying down the coral jade and energy ores, they will be handled by others! Moreover, I will assign three helpers to you in a month.”","While Lin Yuan spoke, he saw that one of the elemental dolls was wind-type.","Lin Yuan held up the wind-type elemental doll and poured a cup of the Element Well’s water over it.","Soon, the elemental doll combined with the Element Well and turned into a glowing jade-textured fluid.","Lin Yuan held up the bowl to the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope’s mouth and said, “You have worked hard. Have a taste of 100% pure elements!”","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope quickly started lapping up the light green fluid.","Once the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was done drinking the bowl of elements, Lin Yuan saw many vortex-shaped light green patterns appear all over its body. Everlasting gusts of wind also started whipping around the bottom of its feet.","Lin Yuan had not formed a contract with the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope because it was already Silver grade by the time he encountered it, so he did not have sufficient spiritual energy to contract it. This was just an objective factor.","However, as a subjective factor, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope did not meet Lin Yuan’s standards.","But now, the ordinary Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had transformed into an amazing fey that went beyond others’ imaginations!","It was clearly made of flesh, but it possessed wind-elemental energy that was purer than that of element-type feys!","It looked as though the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope would be evolving soon!","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s manager and did not want to share its job with others.","However, after the Spirit Lock spatial zone became larger, the work was now too much for it alone!","Lin Yuan would definitely continue to garner numerous spirit qi crystals. The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was busiest every time Lin Yuan collected spirit qi crystals.","With the current production rate of the elemental pearls, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope would struggle to accomplish the job that Lin Yuan had given it.","Luckily, Lin Yuan would assign three helpers to it, thus alleviating some of its burden. As such, the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope did not protest.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was looking forward to the shelf that Lin Yuan talked about.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope liked collecting and gathering, and it liked to see the collected items organized neatly.","If the elemental pearls were placed haphazardly around, the Spirit Lock spatial zone would become very messy.","The custom Diamond fey storage boxes were all ring-shaped. All it needed to do was use its spiritual energy to link up with the Diamond fey storage boxes, and it could sort all the elemental pearls accordingly.","This would save it a lot of effort!","When it had to use the wooden boxes, regardless of how carefully the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope counted the elemental pearls, it sometimes made mistakes. The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope would then have to recount!","From the outside, the Element Well did not seem to have changed in any way. But its interior had expanded substantially, and it could also produce water faster now.","Begin Lady appeared in an illusionary form before Lin Yuan and leaped into the Element Well. It could not be happier with the enlargement of its new home!","Lin Yuan did not intend to do anything with the parts of the Spirit Lock spatial zone that he had yet to decorate or fill.","He walked over to Klein Hub and intended to move the army of Hundred Questions Beasts, Hu Quan, and Sky Sea to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan had been obstinate about keeping the Spirit Lock spatial zone a secret from everyone else because he lacked the ability to protect himself. If the secret of the Spirit Lock spatial zone was revealed, he would be in danger.","But now, very few people in the main world could threaten him!","Hu Quan was one of Sky City’s main members and was deserving of Lin Yuan’s trust.","Moreover, building the space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would not be easy.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone would continue to grow larger as the concentration of spirit qi increased.","Hu Quan would not be able to build up the space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone within a short period.","Furthermore, Hu Quan needed to focus on constructing Sky City on Sky Sea’s back. He would be spending a lot of time in the Spirit Lock spatial zone from now on!","The Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment would allow Hu Quan to bring many of his ideas into reality, and he liked nothing more than combining feys with scenery.","Lin Yuan looked forward to the designs that Hu Quan would come up with once he got a glimpse of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment.","Although Klein Hub did not look much larger than it was before, when he entered through it to its entrance in the marsh world, Lin Yuan thought, One Floating Island Whale? Even five Floating Island Whales can likely be squeezed through it to the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","Immediately after he entered the marsh world, Lin Yuan spotted the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and Purple Afterglow acting affectionately without caring if they were being watched. They did not care at all that he was basically their bachelor father!","The tens of Medusa Snake Demons were looking after the Item-Storing Walnut Trees in the near distance.","Scale Concubine had become the center of the group of Medusa Snake Demons and looked after all of them.","As Wendy’s mother, Scale Concubine was very respected in the marsh world.","Lin Yuan had thought about moving the Medusa Snake Demons into the Spirit Lock spatial zone so they could work as servants.","However, the Medusa Snake Demons were more skilled at combat than nurturing feys. They would not be as skilled at nurturing plants as the Myth III Spirit Core Jasmines in human form.","The Medusa Snake Demons had been assigned to look after the Item-Storing Walnut Trees and nurture the Soldier Ration Radishes in the marsh world.","Finding a lifeform in the marsh world that was as intelligent as the Medusa Snake Demon was difficult.","The Medusa Snake Demons bowed to Lin Yuan when they spotted him before continuing their jobs.","Scale Concubine did not move over to Lin Yuan’s side either. It knew it would be rude of it to move closer to Lin Yuan before he called it.","Lin Yuan had saved all of the Medusa Snake Demons. Otherwise, they would have become the playthings of the Drugged Snake Eagle.","More importantly, Lin Yuan had nurtured Wendy. Scale Concubine felt endless respect and gratitude toward Lin Yuan.","Genius sensed Lin Yuan’s presence, immediately emerged from the Hundred Questions Beasts’ secret space, and went to his side. With well-practiced actions, it climbed up to his shoulder. It could not care less that the army of Hundred Questions Beasts were all watching it."]},{"number":2623,"title":"Chapter 2623 The Floating Island Whale and Heavenly Family Fey!","paragraphs":["2623 The Floating Island Whale and Heavenly Family Fey!","Genius wrapped its tail around Lin Yuan before it meowed and said, “Yuan, I have missed you!”","Genius placed its head against Lin Yuan’s neck and began nuzzling him.","Lin Yuan and Genius had a very deep relationship that could not be described in words.","Feys usually knew who their parents were. They stayed with their parents and were cared for by them when they were young.","They would only be contracted by spirit qi professionals when they grew up and were able to be independent.","This was like how Lin Yuan had to wait until kittens had learned life skills from their mothers for the first two months of their lives before he could adopt them and bring them home.","However, the Hundred Questions Beast was the most lowly housekeeping beast in the main world, and almost every regular person could gain ownership of one. Thus, no one was willing to put too much effort into nurturing one.","Using Genius as an example, it never had the chance to know who its parents were. It did not even have a blurry memory to hold on to. A fey breeding base had taken it before it could even open its eyes.","In order to reduce the cost of supporting them, the Hundred Questions Beast would be sold within a month.","Due to the Hundred Questions Beast’s high intelligence, it could converse at a normal human level once it reached four months of age.","Thus, the Hundred Questions Beast could be nurtured postnatally.","Other feys always felt an attachment to their parents they would always feel but never mentioned it after spirit qi professionals contracted them.","However, to Genius, all of these feelings were associated with Lin Yuan. It was a love so deep that it permeated its bones.","Lin Yuan touched Genius’ small head with one hand as he lifted its chin with the other and said, “Genius, the Spirit Lock spatial zone has evolved. From now on, you can remain in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. You don’t have to stay in the marsh world anymore.","“I will ask Hu Quan to build a comfortable base for you and the Hundred Questions Beasts. You must have suffered in the marsh world!”","Lin Yuan was not trying to be polite. There was no need for window-dressing politeness when he communicated with Genius.","Although Lin Yuan never lacked resources, he had a million tasks on hand when he first entered the marsh world and was only at the beginning of his development.","There were not enough of the Spirit Craftsmen. After all, Lin Yuan had not picked many of them to relocate to the marsh world.","Thus, the Hundred Questions Beasts’ houses had never been renovated or updated although the army of Hundred Questions Beasts underwent two rounds of expansion!","There were more than 500 of the Hundred Questions Beasts squeezed into the small three-story building. Each one had less than ten square meters of space to work. Even illegal workshops had more space!","Each Hundred Questions Beast was worth as much as a pinnacle Class 3 Creation Master! Genius had nurtured those who had more talent into Class 4 Creation Masters!","Even the breeding room of a Class 1 Creation Master was more than 300 square meters large.","The breeding room designated to a Class 4 Creation Master by the Creation Master Association had two stories, and the interior mimicked that of the natural environment. Each floor would be more than 1,500 square meters large.","When Lin Yuan took the Creation Master exam, he had been stunned the first time he entered the breeding room of a Class 4 Creation Master.","But now that the Spirit Lock spatial zone was as large as the Xia Region, the Hundred Questions Beasts would not be given spaces as large as the allocations from the Creation Master Association but would be at least 80 square meters. Every room would also have a custom climbing rack, cat bed, and custom details.","Although the Hundred Questions Beasts would never betray him as they were under Genius’ control, Lin Yuan would still do his best to provide the Hundred Questions Beasts with the treatment that they deserved!","Genius’ eyes lit up like stars when it heard what Lin Yuan said.","But when it thought back to all of its cats and how much space they took up, Genius did not think they could all be moved into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The weakest of the cats had reached Diamond grade.","Most cat-species feys were loners and often fought when they had to live near each other.","When Genius first started managing the cats, it had to break up fights almost daily.","Those rowdy children could cause as much trouble as they wanted in the marsh world, but acting the same way in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would affect the other feys!","“Yuan, I only need to return to attend to the cats two to three times a week. This gives me a lot of time to stay with you in the Spirit Lock spatial zone!”","Lin Yuan smiled and patted Geniu. “We can move all the cats into the Spirit Lock spatial zone. I will ask Hu Quan to design a space for all the cats. Don’t worry. The Spirit Lock spatial zone has enough space. With all the pure spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, you won’t have to put as much effort into nurturing the cats!”","The cats were linked to Genius’ own power, so Genius often used the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to provide resources to the cats.","Lin Yuan also had to provide the army of Hundred Questions Beasts with spirit qi crystals that they would use to nurture the cat-species feys.","But once the cats moved into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan could save on a large amount of spirit qi crystals.","None of the cat-species feys were ordinary. They would require more infrastructure to be built in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The town that Lin Yuan lived in his previous life had not been large. But the Xia Region was around the same size as two cities from his previous life.","Every cat would receive a significant amount of space to move around in.","Once the Spirit Lock spatial zone was properly constructed and built up, it would resemble a city.","Once Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he could move those who wanted to relocate to the Sky Beyond the Clouds through the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When Genius heard what Lin Yuan said, it started to roll around in his arms.","It could finally remain by Lin Yuan’s side and did not have to separate from him! There was nothing else that Lin Genius wanted!","When Purple Afterglow was in the throes of expressing its love, it could ignore Lin Yuan. But the same did not go for the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly immediately approached Lin Yuan when it spotted him.","When it arrived next to Lin Yuan, it changed into human form while Purple Afterglow landed on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s lips.","Purple Afterglow’s beauty had been raised further after it evolved to Myth Breed.","Purple Afterglow noticed that the Kill Food Sky Butterfly adored it even more after its evolution. It really enjoyed this feeling.","Lin Yuan did not know what to do with this love-blinded butterfly.","Lin Yuan told the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, “Go and call Hu Quan, the Sentient Being Protective Dragon, and the Wailing Snake over. Tell Hu Quan to gather all of the Spirit Craftsmen in the marsh world as well.”","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly immediately left to search for the people Lin Yuan had asked for.","Purple Afterglow remained perched on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s lips.","...","Hu Quan had been wanting to discuss some matters with Lin Yuan but had not had the chance to meet with him. He also knew that Lin Yuan had been extremely busy of late and could not bring himself to disturb Lin Yuan.","Now that Lin Yuan was the one looking for him, Hu Quan intended to tell Lin Yuan about his plans for the construction on Sky Sea.","Hu Quan had drawn up a plan after taking over the construction involving Sky Sea.","With the three sets of Island Whale bones that Lin Yuan had given him, Hu Quan drew up the blueprints centered on them.","But when Hu Quan noticed Sky Sea’s ability, Whale Spout Empowerment, he realized that it expanded the realm of possibilities for Sky Sea and would allow it to carry even larger entities.","Whale Spout Empowerment could heal entities that were bonded to Sky Sea, and Whale Blood Screen added a layer of protection for everything on Sky Sea’s back. This double layer of protection allowed Hu Quan to come up with an even more ambitious plan for Sky City’s construction.","Since they were going to build Sky City and Sky Sea would continue increasing in size as it became more powerful, they should build the best version of Sky City right from the get-go so that Lin Yuan would not have to worry about renovating Sky City in the future.","Lin Yuan nodded. He liked a Spirit Craftsman like Hu Quan, who had his own ideas.","Lin Yuan was not a Spirit Craftsman, so he did not know their limitations. Thus, he could only offer suggestions to Hu Quan but could not make any demands. Hu Quan would then adjust his design based on feasibility factors.","Lin Yuan felt that this was a rare virtue. This was also why he continued relying mainly on Hu Quan, even though he could successfully recruit numerous Class 5 Spirit Craftsmen.","Sky Sea had already evolved to Suzerain/Myth I. It had not undergone the World Cleansing because it had evolved while it was in the marsh world. Thus, it had not gained its Myth Breed exclusive skills.","The word ‘fake’ was behind the Myth I segment in its True Data information.","When Sky Sea returned to the main world and activated its World Cleansing, it would become a real Myth Breed fey.","When Sky Sea evolved to Myth Breed in the marsh world, Begin Lady noticed that Sky Sea’s aura became highly similar to that of the Mother of Bloodbath and Purple Love.","There was a chance that Sky Sea could evolve into a Heavenly Family Fey once it returned to the main world and was able to reconnect with the sky.","As a faerie, there were definitely no issues with Begin Lady’s sensing abilities.","Since Sky Sea had a similar aura to that of a Heavenly Family Fey, it could transform when it evolved to Creation Breed even if it did not happen when it evolved to Myth Breed.","...","Lin Yuan did not try to leave Hu Quan hanging. “Uncle Hu, Sky Sea will be able to evolve again very soon. After this evolution, it will no longer undergo significant changes in the future.","“Once you see how Sky Sea transforms this time, you will have an idea of what you can do when building Sky City!”","Hu Quan needed time to gather Spirit Craftsmen as he had dispatched many of them.","Given that the whole marsh world was under Lin Yuan’s control, he did not need to restrict the Wailing Snake and Sentient Being Protective Dragon’s realm of activity.","The two of them were very far away, but the Kill Food Sky Butterfly finally managed to locate them. It would take more than a day to bring them back.","Sky Sea followed Hu Quan to where Klein Hub was located.","The sky of the marsh world was light green. It would turn purple at night, but it would not become black like the main world’s night sky did.","But now, all the natural light from the marsh world was being blocked by a giant creature, causing the marsh world to be shrouded in darkness.","This giant creature seemed to be carrying extreme pressure, and its cry shook the whole world.","If Sky Sea was not currently retracting its aura and controlling the winds around its body, the gale force would have shattered all of the plants, mountains, and stones around it. This was the fearsomeness that came with a gargantuan body.","This was why the Island Whale’s only method of combat in the sea was to use its body to slam into enemies. It was common for thearch-class experts to be killed by Island Whales when trying to use feys to hunt them.","Sky Sea was very swift. Although Whale Spout Empowerment, Lashing Spirit Tail Wings, and Whale’s Breath did not seem to be able to increase Sky Sea’s speed, they were actually capable of doing so.","Lin Yuan was only becoming more and more satisfied with Sky Sea. The latter was also looking at Lin Yuan with the same affection that Genius did.","When it came to affection, Sky Sea felt as strongly toward Lin Yuan as Genius did.","Sky Sea had suffered significantly in the Gao family. They had not noticed anything special about it. They had dismissed it as an egg that had undergone a negative mutation and would never be able to hatch.","It was Lin Yuan who had given Sky Sea a new lease on life and even used his blood to deepen their link.","Before Sky Sea evolved to Fantasy Breed, it was around the same size as Rememberling and could swim around Lin Yuan.","Only a few months had passed since Sky Sea had evolved to Myth Breed, but it had already come to accept its reality as a gargantuan creature. Hence, it dared not act too affectionately toward Lin Yuan. It was afraid that it would crush him even if it did not exert any strength!","Black wings spread out on Lin Yuan’s back, and he flew up to Sky Sea’s back before squatting down to touch the folds on Sky Sea’s skin.","Lin Yuan intended to take Sky Sea back to the main world and watch it evolve to Myth Breed. He would do all he could to help Sky Sea evolve into a Heavenly Family Fey!","Sky Sea could not be happier when it heard that Lin Yuan was taking it back to the main world.","Its main source of energy was spirit qi. Thus, the marsh world’s environment was not suitable for its long-term growth.","Sky Sea also badly wanted to return to the main world so it could undergo its World Cleansing. It could sense that its life rank would change once it underwent its World Cleansing.","It knew how many hopes Lin Yuan had for Sky City, and it wanted to be able to become a better vessel for Sky City through its evolution."]},{"number":2624,"title":"Chapter 2624 Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment!","paragraphs":["2624 Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment!","Sky Sea entered Klein Hub and reappeared in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He saw that the boundaries of the Spirit Lock spatial zone were also masked by blurry mist.","This was very similar to his divine kingdom.","An idea surfaced in Lin Yuan’s mind: Could Morbius’ Spirit Lock spatial zone be connected to the divine kingdom?","Lin Yuan did not know much about the divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom was at the beginning of its ‘big bang’ stage. He was pumping lots of faith power so that Truth could put it to use and enable the divine kingdom to develop rapidly.","However, during this stage of evolution development, the lifeforms could evolve in a million different and strange directions.","Lin Yuan always did his best to evolve his feys in the best direction. He had the same principle when it came to his divine kingdom. As such, Lin Yuan injected a large amount of faith power into the divine kingdom during this ‘big bang’ stage.","Only the species with the most potential were showing positive signs of development, and the most likely to evolve into the best species were left behind. This would inevitably cause Lin Yuan to use up more faith power.","However, Lin Yuan did not think utilizing faith power was a waste.","The lifeforms produced from this ‘big bang’ stage would become the roots of the divine kingdom’s future development.","If the divine kingdom did not establish its roots properly, how could it hope to continue developing in a stable manner?","Lin Yuan always felt reluctant when he gave faith power to Truth.","However, Truth was delighted.","Truth was Lin Yuan’s only holy spirit and had become his trusted aide.","If it became the holy spirit of a powerful divine kingdom, it could bask in glory and stand above all the rest in the future!","Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom was only at the beginning stage of its development. Hence, he had not yet explored the blurry space at the borders.","Lin Yuan felt that the nebulous space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone was very similar to the space beyond the divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan had already told Morbius about his guess.","After a moment of silence, Morbius shook its head lightly. It could not speak with certainty on this matter.","However, Morbius still did not know too much about itself. For example, it still could not see its own species!","Sky Sea’s fins fluttered and kicked up a gust of wind. This wind passed through the whale blood and shielded Lin Yuan’s body.","The wind left Lin Yuan feeling very comfortable.","This was a new way of communicating with Lin Yuan that Sky Sea gained after it grew to its giant size.","After receiving Sky Sea’s response, Lin Yuan went to his room in Sky Bearer City, where he summoned Eternal Source to take him to the surface.","Sky Bearer City’s buildings were built very close to each other. If Sky Sea was summoned out into Sky Bearer City, many buildings and infrastructure would be crushed by Sky Sea’s body.","The underground environment was not a conducive one for evolving a fey like Sky Sea, which belonged to the sea and sky.","The Grotto Continent’s entrance to the surface was guarded by three Turning Wheel Realm Dictators, who hurriedly made way when they saw Eternal Source and Lin Yuan.","These two were the last people that they would try to stop!","The other Turning Wheel Realm Dictators who had not been given any tasks were all envious of these three Turning Wheel Realm Dictators.","Even Samsara Realm Dictators rarely had the chance to appear before Lin Yuan, much less Turning Wheel Realm Dictators!","When Lin Yuan arrived at the surface, he looked into the distance and saw that the flat and barren land also had a unique beauty when it was blanketed by the setting sun’s light.","Lin Yuan hurriedly summoned Sky Sea out from the Spirit Lock spatial zone, where it had been waiting.","A sound akin to the cry of an ancient whale reverberated around the flat and barren land.","This added an air of magnificence and sacredness to the already present beauty.","The flat and barren land was already filled with sandy winds that left messy trails wherever they went.","The winds kicked up by Sky Sea caused the dust to settle, and everything became clear.","The sunset and falling dusk became a backdrop for Sky Sea and its outstretched wings.","It almost looked like Sky Sea was holding up the sky to Lin Yuan.","While it was flapping its wings, Lin Yuan felt as though Sky Sea could indeed become one with the sky.","At that moment, Sky Sea’s voice echoed in Lin Yuan’s mind. “Yuan, I want to try becoming a Heavenly Family Fey! However, doing so will require me to consume a large amount of spirit qi as well as wind- and water-elemental energy!","“My situation is very different from that of Gray. When Gray was an egg, it could accumulate spirit qi by being in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. It also innately possessed a trace of the Heavenly Family Fey bloodline.","“Its Heavenly Family Fey bloodline was hidden but was activated when it evolved. However, I don’t have the Heavenly Family Fey bloodline innately in me. What I am about to experience is a complete transformation of my life rank!”","Lin Yuan gave Sky Sea a very definitive answer and filled it with confidence.","A wooden chest that was around four-square-meters large appeared by Lin Yuan’s feet.","It went without saying that this was just a small portion of Lin Yuan’s store of resources.","Sky Sea suddenly raised its head and let out a deep whale cry.","A hole appeared in the sky. Sky Sea did not insist on using its own body to take on the World Cleansing.","Eternal Source stepped in to handle the World Cleansing, and the World Grace landed on Sky Sea’s body.","Sky Sea could be considered a real Myth Breed fey now!","However, Lin Yuan did not relax after Sky Sea evolved to Myth Breed. Rather, he finally began feeling anxious.","This was because Sky Sea was about to encounter a test from the sky. This would resemble the test that the Mother of Bloodbath had to face from the sun when it transformed into a Heavenly Family Fey.","The sky appeared to be peaceful, but there were too many natural phenomena taking place in the sky.","If Sky Sea wanted to hold up the sky, it would also have to hold up these phenomena!","Sky Sea would have to endure more than the Mother of Bloodbath did when it evolved into a Heavenly Family Fey!","Lin Yuan had a deep relationship with the Heavenly Family Cottage and learned a lot about Heavenly Family Feys from them.","There was a saying among Heavenly Family Feys—the more natural phenomena linked to a Heavenly Family Fey, the more potential it would have, but also the more difficult it would be for it to evolve. It required unimaginable resources to evolve such a Heavenly Family Fey’s power.","There were numerous such Heavenly Family Feys in the Heavenly Family Cottage, but they rarely managed to become one of its leaders.","The Heavenly Family Cottage had once tried to help a Heavenly Family Fey linked to numerous natural phenomena to become one of the leaders. But even after investing all of their resources, they could not cross that gap.","Lin Yuan was confident he could take care of Sky Sea’s needs, but not that he could help it to transform successfully.","The Mother of Bloodbath commanded the sun. This one natural phenomenon had already caused the Mother of Bloodbath extreme pain and put it in great danger.","Besides asking Eternal Source to protect Sky Sea, Lin Yuan could only provide it with resources.","The calm sky changed abruptly and was promptly embroiled in a windstorm. Rain, snow, and lightning gathered in the windstorm, and the changing power of day and night suddenly exploded into existence. More and more natural phenomena mixed in with the windstorm. It was as though the sky was the medium for the windstorm.","This sight caused Lin Yuan to hold his breath.","It could be said that Sky Sea had to endure a combination of the moon and stars, night and day, storming rain, lightning, and more.","The Mother of Bloodbath, Sacred Cry Moon Beast, Purple Love. White Phoenix, Gray, and the other Heavenly Family Feys had only had to endure a single-faceted test.","This was almost unbelievable!","As such, Lin Yuan believed that if Sky Sea could evolve into a Heavenly Family Fey, it could become the king of all Heavenly Family Feys.","However, the changes to the sky would only be the beginning.","Suddenly, the power of ferocious ocean waves materialized on the barren ground.","Good God! Was this another Blue Lotus?","Blue Lotus only had control over the seas. But Sky Sea controlled all the oceans of the world.","By being tested by both the sky and sea, it was as though the will of the main world itself was testing Sky Sea!","Eternal Source tried his best to contain all the explosions of natural phenomena, but he quickly realized that despite its Afterlife Realm power, it was having a hard time.","Eternal Source hurriedly told Lin Yuan about this, so the latter summoned the Abyss Great Emperor.","With the Abyss Great Emperor and Eternal Source fending off the natural phenomena, the event was finally contained to a certain extent. If the associated effects of these phenomena leaked out, innocent lifeforms would be harmed.","However, other Heavenly Family Feys would definitely be able to sense the changes in so many facets of nature.","The natural phenomena were still brewing, and Sky Sea flapped its wings while it waited for its test.","Morbius appeared next to Lin Yuan in its illusionary form and said softly, “Partner, with Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor here, Sky Sea will definitely be able to pass the test! You don’t have to be overly worried!","“These resources will definitely be of use to Sky Sea’s transformation. You have to trust in the culmination of all our work!","“Sky Sea can remain in the Spirit Lock spatial zone from now on. The spirit qi that it absorbs from the Spirit Lock spatial zone will be sufficient for its daily consumption! Sky Sea’s Myth Breed exclusive skill is rather interesting. When we get to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, this exclusive skill will remove the need for us to find and build a new base!”","Lin Yuan looked at Morbius curiously and checked on Sky Sea with True Data.","[Fey Name]: Floating Island Whale","[Fey Species]: Large-winged-whale-species/island-whale-species.","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (3/10)","[Fey Type]: Water/Wind","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[Whale Blood Screen]: Set fire to the essence blood inside its body and form a screen that can protect everything on its back.","[Water Vapor Whale Feelers]: Transform its feelers into water vapor and use them to gather nutrients from the environment to recover itself.","[Whale Spout Empowerment]: Through the blowhole in its head, it can shoot out energy from its energy and supply it to entities with compatible bodies to replenish their energy or fix them up in other ways.","[Lashing Spirit Tail Wings]: After being nourished by pure spirit qi, the wings and tail will be covered with skin that can filter out spirit qi. With every movement of the wings and tail, the spirit qi can be directed to its back to increase the concentration of spirit qi on its back.","[Flesh Solidification]: An additional mouth that is connected to the additional stomach will grow below the blowhole. The metal and rocks that enter the additional stomach will strengthen the flesh during the contraction and expansion of the additional stomach. The solidified flesh will not affect the growth of the whale’s bones.","[Whale’s Breath]: Gather energy that is compatible with its body and shoot it out at a target. Before the target escapes the breath’s lock, the breath will lock and track the target.","[Floating Whale Sinks]: When the things and lifeforms on the whale’s back are dying, a mournful cry of grief will be released. The sky will be like the ocean, and its body and soul will be the price paid to protect all the beings on its back.","Exclusive Skill:","[Floating Island Secret Realm]: A special space will be opened within the whale’s abdomen by swallowing wind-elemental energy. The higher the purity of the wind-elemental energy, the larger the space will be. However, the space will not exceed twice the size of the body. By swallowing water-elemental energy, the flesh will gain powerful fusion abilities that will enable the fats to stick to any lifeform, dead or alive, and drain nutrients from them. The purer the water-elemental energy, the stronger the fusion ability will be.","[Knotted Life Cohabitation]: Pick a lifeform on its back to fuse and share its life with. Before its life comes to an end, the target will not die. Before the target dies, it can continue living even if it sustains a serious injury.","[Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment]: A territory can be subsumed into its body and the body will become a part of this territory. The entities on its body can also be placed anywhere on this territory. The root power of the surroundings can be used to nourish the body and allow the body to be acknowledged by the environment.","When Lin Yuan saw Sky Sea’s Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment, he understood why Morbius said what it said. He also understood why Morbius believed that Sky Sea could overcome this test involving numerous natural phenomena.","Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment would enable Sky Sea to be acknowledged by its environment. Thus, Sky Sea could have an easy time when undergoing tests from nature in the future. It would not have to go through the risk of being on the brink of death each time."]},{"number":2625,"title":"Chapter 2625 What Kind of Earthly Paradise Is This?","paragraphs":["2625 What Kind of Earthly Paradise Is This?","When he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Sky Sea could pick a place and subsume it into its body so that it became a part of this place. This would indeed allow Lin Yuan to obtain a perfect place where he could settle down.","This place would allow Lin Yuan to enter and exit unseen at will.","Lin Yuan was very excited by the prospect of using the environment’s root power to gain its recognition.","Sky Sea had been recognized by the sea and sky and became the Heavenly Family Fey that commanded them.","If it could also become one with the mountains, rivers, and earth, could it break through its current limit and evolve into a Heavenly Family Fey that commanded the sky, sea, and land?","It went without saying this was just Lin Yuan’s guess and prediction. He would only reach a definite result after future experiments.","The description of Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment set Lin Yuan at ease.","Sky Sea’s body was continuously being degraded and damaged by the test from natural phenomena.","Once Sky Sea’s voice appeared in his mind, Lin Yuan immediately instructed Eternal Source to bring over two wooden boxes and poured out all the wind- and water-elemental pearls on Sky Sea’s back.","The Abyss Great Emperor brought over the Diamond fey storage boxes filled with spirit qi crystals and began pouring them out as well.","Lin Yuan did not feel reluctant to use so many precious resources so quickly.","Rather, it was Eternal Source who was complaining to himself.","It turned out that Lin Yuan had such an enormous store of pure elemental energy!","Eternal Source had received a fair amount of rewards from Lin Yuan since becoming his subordinate, but this was the first time he was getting such an unfiltered view of Lin Yuan’s wealth.","When he looked at Sky Sea, Eternal Source could not help but be reminded of Lift Marsh that gobbled up marsh soil.","After consuming so much marsh soil, Lift Marsh had grown larger than Sky Sea, but it did not have as many abilities as Sky Sea did.","When they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Sky Sea and Lift Marsh would become Lin Yuan’s two moving fortresses.","Eternal Source was certain Lin Yuan would take him with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He was confident of this! He was well aware of how important he was to Lin Yuan.","Eternal Source could not help but look forward to the life and adventures awaiting him in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","As an Afterlife Realm Dictator who grew up under the law of the jungle, Eternal Source did not like a life as stable as the one he was currently living. He preferred for his life to have more thrill and danger.","The immense store of resources that Lin Yuan possessed would be the core that sustained the development in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Due to Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment, Sky Sea had to endure a cleansing from multiple natural phenomena. However, it was in a relatively decent state compared to the Mother of Bloodbath, whose body had cracked when it was trying to evolve into a Heavenly Family Fey.","Sky Sea was transforming into a relatively peaceful state and intermittently absorbed elemental energy and pure spirit qi. Its body also steadily grew larger.","The transformation of Sky Sea’s body delighted Lin Yuan.","Its body had become a 1/3 larger than its original size even before its evolution was completed.","Lin Yuan was very glad that Hu Quan had not started working on constructing Sky City on Sky Sea’s back immediately.","Sky Sea would grow to at least twice its original size by the time its transformation was complete. As such, the original Sky City designs would have to be altered.","Although Sky Sea did not seem to be severely injured by the natural phenomena, but it was initially in extreme discomfort.","However, it quickly adjusted to the World Cleansing and bravely fought back against the natural phenomena while enjoying the feeling of transformation.","Sky Sea could clearly sense its body being strengthened with every passing second.","Half a day passed, and the test from the multiple natural phenomena started to dissipate slowly.","Sky Sea had successfully evolved into a Heavenly Family Fey.","It was larger than Lin Yuan had expected and was around 2.5 times its original size. Its body was more than 20 kilometers long and could be considered a truly gigantic beast! This was the largest lifeform that Lin Yuan had ever seen!","Previously, Lift Marsh had been slightly larger than Sky Sea. But now, Sky Sea was larger than Lift Marsh.","There was a limit to the types and quantity of marsh soil. Ever since Lin Yuan took control of the marsh world, he had not stopped searching for and collecting marsh soil. He had fed Lift Marsh every type of marsh soil at least once.","Lift Marsh was nearing its maximum size. It had a diameter of 15 kilometers and was the result of the mountain of earth-elemental pearls and marsh soil that Lin Yuan had injected into it.","It was also a miracle that was almost impossible to replicate.","Once Sky Sea was done with its evolution, Lin Yuan brought it into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","There was no limit to the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s height, so Sky Sea could fly around freely.","Lin Yuan was currently on the other side of the Barren Sea. He also had two Afterlife Realm experts who were using their auras to block out the surroundings. Otherwise, the members of Heavenly Family Cottage would have already made their way over there.","By the time Lin Yuan returned to the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Hu Quan had called over all of the Spirit Craftsmen and did a headcount of all of them.","The Spirit Craftsmen had been sent to the marsh world in two batches, and there were a total of 200 of them.","All of them were loyal to Sky City and had also dedicated their loyalties to Lin Yuan. They had been the first to raise their hands when Lin Yuan mentioned needing people to go under the radar.","Lin Yuan had been generously investing resources into these loyal men.","Hu Quan and Lin Yuan had been nurturing these Spirit Craftsmen for almost a year. Hu Quan was in charge of providing them with the techniques, while Lin Yuan was in charge of supplying the resources.","Some of these Spirit Craftsmen had only been pinnacle Class 2 when they first entered the marsh world. Most of them had been Class 3 Spirit Craftsmen, while only three of them were Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen.","But now, all of the pinnacle Class 2 Spirit Craftsmen had reached Class 3, while the intermediate and above Class 3 Spirit Craftsmen made up 75% of the entire group. There were now four Class 4 Spirit Craftsmen instead of three.","The only regret was that not a single one of them had managed to become a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman.","However, Lin Yuan knew nurturing a Class 5 Spirit Craftsman was not easy.","But if the 200 Spirit Craftsmen were given enough time, at least 10% of them could eventually become Class 5 Spirit Craftsmen.","Lin Yuan had given Bronze/Epic feys to all of these Spirit Craftsmen. He had even given Bronze/Legend feys to some of the more talented ones!","The high-quality Bronze feys were of great help to the Spirit Craftsmen during their constructions. They helped the Spirit Craftsmen to build even more beautiful structures.","Hu Quan, the teacher, was currently lecturing the 200 Spirit Craftsmen.","It was easy for a master to guide one disciple, but it would become difficult to guide many of them. The difficulty did not come from the teaching of techniques but because Hu Quan wanted to ensure that every single one of his disciples grew up with the right character.","Hu Quan had not placed much emphasis on this in the beginning. As a result, conflict had broken out among the Spirit Craftsmen.","It was inevitable for them to have their own selfish desires when it came to the allocation of resources.","After a few instances of conflict among the Spirit Craftsmen, Hu Quan began paying attention to combing out the mindsets of his disciples. The most effective way to go about this was to lecture them daily.","The Spirit Craftsmen who had their own opinions could seek him out after his lectures.","If this Spirit Craftsman had indeed been wronged, Hu Quan would right the wrong immediately.","But if there was something wrong with the Spirit Craftsman’s character, Hu Quan would sort out their character immediately.","Hu Quan would have to employ other means if he could not fix their character.","Hu Quan had kicked six Spirit Craftsmen out of the Heavenly Craft Pavilion in the past year.","Hu Quan did not intend to make an example out of anyone, but his actions had scared the other Spirit Craftsmen.","Hu Quan had taken full control of this team in the past year.","As Hu Quan looked at the 200 disciples he had personally brought up, he felt a strong sense of accomplishment.","After passing through Klein Hub to arrive at the marsh world, Lin Yuan did not interrupt Hu Quan’s lecture.","After Hu Quan was done with his lecture and it was confirmed that no Spirit Craftsmen needed to speak with him, Lin Yuan walked over to Hu Quan and said with a smile, “Uncle Hu, let me take you to a nice place. From today onward, you will be leading your team to decorate that place!”","Hu Quan looked surprised.","The Return from Faraway Mansion was filled with beauty, nature, and talented people. The marsh world also had a wonderful environment.","Lin Yuan had never praised the Return from Faraway Mansion or marsh world’s environments.","Hu Quan was very curious to see the environment that was deserving of being called ‘nice’ by Lin Yuan.","Hu Quan was one of Sky City’s core members and found out about the main world’s impending crisis from Lin Yuan. He also knew that Lin Yuan was gathering many Spirit Craftsmen from the Radiance Federation so they could build up the Radiance Federation’s base as a way of handling the impending crisis.","Hu Quan did not feel envious at all. Rather, he felt that Lin Yuan was depending on him.","At such a time, Lin Yuan did not ask him to lead the work in the Radiance Federation. Rather, he was instructed to attend to the construction on Sky Sea’s back.","The Radiance Federation was Lin Yuan’s responsibility, but Sky City was Lin Yuan’s roots.","The Spirit Craftsmen building the Radiance Federation’s base would only have the authority to come up with plans, but they could not make any decisions about key issues. The Land Imps would be the ones making those decisions.","Hu Quan hated it when he was unable to make decisions regarding his work. After spending a prolonged period carving and creating pieces, he also became unwilling to interact with society.","Now, Lin Yuan was going to assign him more jobs on top of the construction on Sky Sea.","Not only would this raise the capabilities of his entire team, but Hu Quan believed that his horizons would also be broadened.","Lin Yuan had gathered various precious ingredients from the dimensional worlds, including high-grade metal-type spiritual ingredients from the subterranean world.","Hu Quan felt he would finally have the chance to use those spiritual ingredients.","“Young Master, a place you call nice must be so. Did Sky Sea change after its evolution? I will draw up a new design for Sky City and instruct my men to begin the construction. Then, we can build up and decorate this place in an even more detailed and intricate manner! Young Master, I would like to know exactly how big this place is.”","Hu Quan had always addressed Lin Yuan by his name in the past. But after spending more time and interacting further with him, Hu Quan eventually started calling him ‘Young Master’ unconsciously. This was a demonstration of the respect he felt for Lin Yuan.","Hu Quan was extremely curious. He knew that Lin Yuan would take him to this place now, but he still could not help but ask Lin Yuan that question.","Lin Yuan did not leave Hu Quan hanging. He knew that Hu Quan was born in the Tide Region in Cloud Lake City.","The Tide Region was around the same size as the Xia Region. If they were compared closely, the Spirit Lock spatial zone might be slightly larger than the Tide Region.","“Uncle Hu, a space the same size as the place you were born should be large enough for you to unleash your prowess! However, several areas of this space will have dedicated uses. I will tell you everything about all the functions that I need!”","Hu Quan almost choked on his saliva when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","A space as large as the Tide Region? Lin Yuan was trying to create a small region! This would be much more challenging than when he had to build the Return from Faraway Mansion!","Hu Quan hurriedly said, “Young Master, let’s go and see this place!”","Lin Yuan grabbed the excited Hu Quan and said, “Slow down, Uncle Hu. Take these Spirit Craftsmen with you. You can’t start work if you go on your own!”","Lin Yuan’s words caused Hu Quan to realize he had acted out of turn.","Hu Quan coughed before waving his hand and saying to the Spirit Craftsmen behind him, “Line up behind me in the order of the numbers that I assigned you for this month’s test.”","Once Hu Quan was done organizing these Spirit Craftsmen, Lin Yuan was the first to step through Klein Hub.","Lin Yuan never allowed anyone else to pass through Klein Hub in the past. To Hu Quan, Klein Hub was akin to a forbidden zone.","Now that Lin Yuan allowed him through Klein Hub, it showed he trusted him even more!","Before Lin Yuan could think further, Hu Quan, experiencing such pure spirit qi for the first time, felt his cells stunned, then trembling.","A special item covered the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s ground. It seemed like green jade mixed with white jade, finer and smoother than green jade but more transparent than white. Spots of green within the white held endless life.","To Hu Quan, the vast Spirit Lock spatial zone was an uncut jade he could carve as he wished.","A dreamy paradise!","This pure spirit qi environment would benefit him and other Spirit Craftsmen, refining their bodies. It could also complement many fey types, letting them transform into their most beautiful forms.","This perfectly fit Hu Quan’s design passion of combining feys with the environment!","The Spirit Craftsmen who followed Hu Quan into the Spirit Lock spatial zone had all previously worked on the Return from Faraway Mansion. Additionally, after working in the marsh world for a year, they all gained considerable experience.","At that moment, all of their jaws had dropped.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment exceeded their realms of comprehension. Just what kind of earthly paradise was that?","Genius snuggled into Lin Yuan’s arms and blinked purposefully at him.","Lin Yuan immediately understood what Genius was trying to say.","Genius was hoping that Hu Quan could build their base as soon as possible so that the army of Hundred Questions Beasts would have a space to work and produce Creation Master resources! This would build up Lin Yuan’s arsenal of spirit fluids."]},{"number":2626,"title":"Chapter 2626 The Deposit Vegetable Pod!","paragraphs":["2626 The Deposit Vegetable Pod!","Lin Yuan had been very anxious about the construction of Sky City on Sky Sea’s back.","This was because Lin Yuan did not understand the Sleeper’s Revival plan’s aim, and he saw Sky Sea as his main strategic weapon against Tower Canon.","But now, he knew the true meaning of the Sleeper’s Revival plan. Tower Canon saw the entire main world as a tower defense game.","In land wars, Sky Sea that moved in the sky would not be of any use.","Lin Yuan’s sights were not only limited to the main world.","Sky Sea would only be of use in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan was not in a rush to have Hu Quan finish constructing Sky City on Sky Sea’s back.","Rather than begin building Sky City immediately, it would be more beneficial for Lin Yuan if the construction of the base in the Spirit Lock spatial zone was completed first!","Lin Yuan reached out and patted the soft fur on Genius’ back before he told Hu Quan, who was currently mesmerized by the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment, “Uncle Hu, if we call Sky Sea’s back Sky City’s base, this would be Sky City’s incubator. Or rather, this is the core world for Sky City’s members.","“I hope you will do your best to build everything that is meant to be placed here. That will ensure that everything produced in the base will be the best of the best! I will provide you with top resources! I will hand the resource list to you later, and Genius will provide you with knowledge on them so you will have a better understanding of the resources.”","In the past, Wen Yu was always the one who assigned tasks to Hu Quan. But she was now on the other side of the Barren Sea, helping Lin Yuan to search for the Continent Vein Cores.","Every member of Sky City skilled at governance had their own jobs to do and could not take charge of the design and construction of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan let out a soft breath.","It was clear that at the rapid rate that Sky City was developing, there were not enough members skilled in governance and interpersonal skills to go around!","However, when it came to constructing the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan could only trust friends like Wen Yu and Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan was very willing to depend on Bai Qinghuan, but he would never trust her as much as he did Liu Jie and Wen Yu.","Genius was like a daddy’s boy and understood Lin Yuan’s thoughts well. When it communicated with Hu Quan, it could offer some helpful suggestions on Lin Yuan’s behalf.","Hu Quan had been on a path of continuous breakthroughs and had surpassed the Class 5 Spirit Craftsman level. If he could match Night Leaning Moon’s skills in mechanics, he could be given the title of Class 6 Spirit Craftsman.","Hu Quan had the skills, but his experience was lacking. He did not recognize or understand many of the precious resources that Lin Yuan possessed. Thus, he struggled to combine them with his designs.","Lin Yuan handed the resource list to Hu Quan so that he could gain an understanding of these spiritual ingredients he had never seen or even heard of before.","Hu Quan could definitely flesh out his designs.","Hu Quan’s expression of mesmerization morphed into joy upon hearing that.","Lin Yuan had always treated him well and trusted him greatly. He even allowed him to handle resources as precious as Island Whale bones.","Lin Yuan was aware of all of this and was very grateful for the trust that Lin Yuan had in him.","Before entering the marsh world, Hu Quan always thought Lin Yuan had already given him the best resources he possessed.","But after entering the marsh world and gaining an understanding of the resources available there, as well as Lin Yuan’s status in the marsh world, Hu Quan finally learned he had only had access to relatively impressive resources. Only now was Lin Yuan giving him access to the most precious resources!","Hu Quan badly yearned to carve out a small world using these precious resources.","Being a Spirit Craftsman came with a certain level of OCD personality.","There were currently very few structures in this environment, and he could design and construct infrastructure with functional-type properties.","Hu Quan assured Lin Yuan, “Young Master, I have much more time to work now that I have contracted the Vitality Sloth! Feel free to let me know of any ideas you have. Once I understand the effects of these spiritual ingredients, I will build a base per your requests as soon as possible!","“You know that I love combining feys with the environment. Many feys need to be nourished by elemental energy. Is it possible for you to nurture a few high-quality Bronze Deposit Vegetable Pods? I would like to store the elemental pearls in them.”","The Deposit Vegetable Pods would not use up the elemental energy within the elemental pearls but could use the elemental pearl to nourish the lifeforms in the surroundings.","The Deposit Vegetable Pod was also very beautiful. It resembled a crystal legume that had jade vines.","Once the beans ripened, they would also leap out on their own. They would also serve as gorgeous accessories when paired with the elemental pearls’ radiance.","There were many feys in the world. Genius had read about plant-type feys like the Deposit Vegetable Pod in a book about Spirit Craftsmanship when it had been gathering information.","The Deposit Vegetable Pod started out as a cash crop. Its beans had a very similar taste to peas but were cheaper than peas.","However, the Deposit Vegetable Pod did not produce many beans and was quickly eliminated from the list of cash crops.","It was a Creation Master who had accidentally poured spirit fluid over the soil while nurturing the Deposit Vegetable Pod and managed to evolve to Flawless.","When the Deposit Vegetable Pod was evolved to Flawless, it could activate and use elemental energy to nourish the environment. However, this would drain its store of elemental energy.","The Class 2 Creation Master who discovered this wrote and published a thesis that caught the eye of a Class 4 Creation Master.","This Class 4 Creation Master was from Sea Sky Creation and was likely one of Ji Feng’s ancestors.","Class 4 Creation Masters had stronger capabilities and more resources to conduct experiments on feys.","When this Class 4 Creation Master evolved the Deposit Vegetable Pod to Gold/Epic, he noticed that it no longer drained whatever was placed within it when it was nourishing its surroundings.","This discovery had spurred the Class 4 Creation Master on, and he was motivated to invest more energy into evolving the Deposit Vegetable Pod.","After painstaking and exhausting efforts, he was finally able to nurture a new Silver/Legend Deposit Vegetable Pod that could use elemental energy to nurture its surroundings better than the Gold/Epic Deposit Vegetable Pod could.","This meant that the Deposit Vegetable Pod was a special fey that had stronger effects at lower grades and high qualities!","However, low-grade/high-quality feys were extremely difficult to nurture. At the very least, Class 4 Creation Master resources were required.","The resources would be better used to nurture the Elemental Shellfish rather than low-grade/high-quality Deposit Vegetable Pod.","The same amount of resources could produce more than ten elemental pearls. Three to four elemental pearls would be able to change an environment to a far greater extent than the Deposit Vegetable Pod could.","Thus, the Deposit Vegetable Pod was rarely brought up.","After Hu Quan mentioned the Deposit Vegetable Pod, Genius immediately sent all the information related to the Deposit Vegetable Pod to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow. Filling the Deposit Vegetable Pod with elemental pearls would indeed be very suitable for the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","Firstly, it would be very easy for Lin Yuan to nurture the Bronze/Legend Deposit Vegetable Pods.","Furthermore, he had a large number of high-quality elemental pearls. He did not have an urgent use for these elemental pearls, so storing them in the Deposit Vegetable Pods would not be a waste!","Lastly, the Deposit Vegetable Pod was beautiful enough to blend in with the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment.","Based on Hu Quan’s suggestion, it was clear he had put a lot of thought into the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s design.","“Uncle Hu, I will be able to provide you with 100 of the Deposit Vegetable Pods within two days. Rather than filling them with elemental pearls with outer radiance, I think that filling them with the elemental dolls will be a better choice.”","While Lin Yuan spoke, he took out two elemental dolls.","Elemental dolls had intelligence imbued into them from their elements.","The elemental pearl was still the core of the elemental doll. But being imbued with intelligence, the elemental pearl could contain emotions and manipulate movement.","If the Deposit Vegetable Pods were filled with elemental dolls, they would fly around the Deposit Vegetable Pods and produce a more pleasant sight than if the Deposit Vegetable Pods were filled with elemental pearls.","More importantly, the elemental energy in the dolls was much purer than that of pearls.","Using a combination of the Deposit Vegetable Pod and elemental dolls to nourish the environment would undoubtedly be much more beneficial for the other feys.","Hu Quan was no longer surprised by Lin Yuan’s capabilities.","When he previously asked Lin Yuan for resources, he prepared himself for a long wait. Yet, Lin Yuan delivered the resources to him within a few days.","Hu Quan had never seen the elemental dolls before and intended to ask Genius to explain them to him.","Hu Quan was not a Creation Master. As a Spirit Craftsman, he did not have the strong investigative and sensing abilities for spiritual ingredients that Creation Masters did.","Genius had used Connected Tails to send knowledge to Hu Quan more than once.","Hu Quan really liked how he could gain a sea of knowledge just from being linked to Genius’ tails.","“Young Master, tell me about the structures you want to build in advance. There is no limit to the height of this space. With my current mechanical abilities, I can use metal spiritual ingredients to build a high-speed elevator or spatial-type spiritual ingredients to build a transport vehicle.","“If you only need me to build tall structures, I think that the high-speed elevator will be more useful. After all, the transport vehicle will use up energy. But there won’t be this concern for a high-speed elevator. A mechanical core will be needed to build a high-speed elevator, and this mechanical core will produce energy on its own.”","When Lin Yuan heard what Hu Quan said, he could not help but be reminded of the skyscrapers from his previous life.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone was indeed enormous now. As Lin Yuan continued to develop, he would need to use more of the space. Thus, regardless of how large the Spirit Lock spatial zone became, it would be difficult for it to catch up to Lin Yuan’s needs.","Thus, he would be very willing to try building upward to maximize his utilization of the space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","“Uncle Hu, I would like you to build a base for Creation Masters. There isn’t a limit to its height, so it’ll all depend on your abilities. I need there to be 500 rooms, and each room has to be around 80 to 100 square feet.","“There also needs to be two sets of cat trees made of jade-textured wood. The work tables need to be around 60 centimeters in height. You can place around 20 centimeters tall futons below each work table. You don’t have to create the bottles used to concoct spirit fluids. I will purchase them from the Creation Master Association.”","Lin Yuan paused for a moment before looking at Hu Quan and smiling. “Uncle Hu, I’m sure you know why I have such a plan. I hope you will be able to complete it for me with perfection in mind.","“Additionally, dedicate a space to build a place for cat-species feys to live. It will house around 1,500 cat-species feys. The cat-species feys are able to adjust their form, so there’s no need for the space to be too big.","“Breeding bases will also be needed to grow the Soldier Ration Radishes and Item-Storing Walnut Trees. Move all the marsh soil meant to nurture the Soldier Ration Radishes and Item-Storing Walnuts from the marsh world to below these two building bases.","“The Barren River Orchid Bud can be grown between these two breeding bases! It will be able to benefit from the energy of the marsh soil under the two breeding bases.","“Don’t forget residences for yourself and the other Spirit Craftsmen as well. The conditions of your living spaces will remain the same. The only difference will be that it will now be in high-rise buildings. Every month, I will send you twice your base wages.”","Hu Quan earnestly made notes of all of Lin Yuan’s requests. He preferred to write everything down rather than rely on his memory. He had a good memory, but it was inevitable to miss out on some things when there were too many things to remember.","Hu Quan was not stupid. He had discovered the army of Hundred Questions Beasts in the past year that he spent in the marsh world.","He had been astonished when he first found out about the army of Hundred Questions Beasts.","If a species of fey could be nurtured into Creation Masters, this would spell massive changes for the main world.","This secret was enormous.","Hu Quan judged others based on his own values. He was afraid Lin Yuan would act against him when he learned he knew this secret.","It was not that Hu Quan did not trust Lin Yuan but that this secret was far too earth-shattering.","But now, Lin Yuan was bringing up this matter without hiding it from him.","Hu Quan was so touched that he came to a decision. He would never leave the Spirit Lock spatial zone for the rest of his life, aside from when Lin Yuan sent him out on jobs! He would also rein in the Spirit Craftsmen and ensure they caused no trouble.","There would be significant benefits concerning his quality of life and lifespan if he lived in this environment.","“Young Master, I have recorded everything that you said. I know why you have requested such designs, and I will enact them exactly as you requested!”"]},{"number":2627,"title":"Chapter 2627 Exclusive Skill: Sky Fate Attachment!","paragraphs":["2627 Exclusive Skill: Sky Fate Attachment!","“Once the 50 Land Imps that you send me follow my plan and build the frame, you can begin using the space. I will slowly carve and add in the additional details. After all, it will take more than just a year or two to finish a project involving a space as large as this!”","As a Spirit Craftsman, Hu Quan detested employers like that the most. He had encountered such an employer when he was younger. Since he had only been a Class 2 Spirit Craftsman then, he had ended up being horribly bullied by that employer.","Thus, from then on, Hu Quan developed the habit of making his expected deadlines known before he took on any job.","Despite knowing that Lin Yuan was not like that, Hu Quan could not kick this habit.","Low-class Spirit Craftsmen only had to fear being inconvenienced if their employers were regular people. But if their employers were figures of authority, many low-class Spirit Craftsmen would be able to attest to having experienced being bullied out of their deserved compensation by such employers.","Luckily, almost 30 years ago, the Radiance Federation’s constant reforms led to the establishment of the Spirit Craftsman Association, which put an end to such occurrences.","“Uncle Hu, all you need to do is build the frame. You can add in the details slowly in the future! A while later, I will assign some Myth Breed feys in human form to assist you. I will also send 50 Land Imps to you. They should be enough. There will be at least one Samsara Realm Dictator and five Turning Wheel Realm Dictators among these 50 Land Imps.”","Lin Yuan had only relocated a portion of the Land Imps from the subterranean world to the Radiance Federation. There were far too many Land Imps in the subterranean world. If they were all moved to the Radiance Federation, they would outnumber the Radiance Federation’s citizens.","Lin Yuan had only moved the cream of the crop to the Radiance Federation, but he had not moved the Land Imps like Sweet Vanquish, who fulfilled management roles.","Lin Yuan could send a team of Land Imps led by Sweet Vanquish to the Spirit Lock spatial zone to help Hu Quan.","Sweet Vanquish was very smart and knew he needed to strive to do the best that he could. Once his position as a leader was secured, he would do his best in the job that he was given.","Hu Quan immediately smiled brightly when he heard what Lin Yuan said. He had spent enough time in the marsh world to understand the significance of a Samsara Realm Dictator.","With Samsara and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators at his disposal when he was building the frame of the base in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, he might be able to complete the construction within a day or two!","Hu Quan did not give Lin Yuan any more assurances as Lin Yuan had an even deeper understanding of the power of Samsara and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators. Thus, he definitely knew how quickly the construction of the base would be able to progress with the help of the Land Imps!","Lin Yuan did not give out any more instructions past those involving the initial work that had to be done.","Instead, he planned on waiting until Hu Quan was done with the initial work before he assigned new work to Hu Quan based on the circumstances at that point.","One could only imagine how many years the catastrophic disaster stemming from Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan would last.","Hu Quan and the 200 Spirit Craftsmen would definitely be able to finish the required constructions in the Spirit Lock spatial zone during that time!","Once this disaster was dealt with and Tower Canon was defeated, it would be time for Lin Yuan to think about heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Lin Yuan was about to depart the Spirit Lock spatial zone when he heard Genius say seriously, “Yuan, I want to try evolving to Myth Breed! I will use the opportunity to ask the heavens for a way to become a Class 5 Creation Master.”","It had been accumulating its power for some time but felt it had reached its maximum capacity.","It was afraid that if it waited any longer, it would lose the courage to put its life on the line.","Lin Yuan was struck by what Genius said.","After Genius evolved from the Beast that Connects Everything to the Highest Access Fate-Knowing Beast, its Fantasy Breed exclusive skill changed from Connected Tails to Tail of Fate.","Tail of Fate was an expansion of Connected Tails. It retained the abilities of Connected Tails while adding the ability to link with the heavens.","Tail of Fate allowed Genius to combine all of its tails into one. It would then sacrifice its spiritual energy for the chance to access the will of the heavens and ask a question that it wanted the answer to.","Genius saw this ability as the key to becoming a Class 5 Creation Master.","Lin Yuan did not know how much spiritual energy Genius would have to sacrifice in order to receive an answer from the heavens on how it could become a Class 5 Creation Master. He was afraid something would happen to Genius in the process. Thus, he never told Genius to give this plan a try.","This was already the third time that Genius was expressing its wish to make an attempt at becoming a Class 5 Creation Master.","Lin Yuan had raised Genius and knew it was very strong-headed.","After a moment of silence, Lin Yuan rationalized that with Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor by his side, they would be able to step in even if the heavenly will ended up causing harm to Genius.","Genius had consumed numerous rainbow fish coats and grown many tails. It could use up these additional tails as it pleased to multiply its soul power and increase its comprehending powers!","Lin Yuan could not stop Genius from evolving because he was afraid something would happen to it. If he did that, he would be no different from an unreasonable parent. Lin Yuan did not want to become such a person.","Lin Yuan reached out and touched Genius’ soft fur. “Okay, we’ll try evolving you to Myth Breed and attempt to turn you into a Class 5 Creation Master!:","Genius meowed and excitedly wrapped its tails around Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had been afraid that an accident would befall Genius when it questioned the heavens that would affect its spiritual energy.","Genius was anxious to evolve because it wanted to be of more help to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan possessed pure spirit qi and elemental energy. He could also produce such resources.","He was able to accomplish 60% of a Class 5 Creation Master’s abilities. However, even using the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan could not accomplish the remaining 40%.","However, given that spirit qi and elemental energy were the foundation of everything, this gap was not as significant as it seemed.","Begin Lady could use its body to produce precious instruments, and this closed the gap between him and a true Class 5 Creation Master even further.","But there were a few special potions that could only be concocted by Class 5 Creation Masters. Lin Yuan would not be able to get his hands on them without going through a true Class 5 Creation Master.","The only true Class 5 Creation Masters that Sky City had were Di Wanmi, Yi Huailu, and Weng Queji.","Lin Yuan had left Yi Huailu in the Divine Wood Federation. The federation badly needed Yi Huailu for its development, and the Startling Lines Continent also needed a Class 5 Creation Master to hold down the fort.","Weng Queji could not produce enough potions to meet Lin Yuan’s needs.","The potions concocted by Class 5 Creation Masters could produce unimaginable effects when it came to increasing the production of feys.","Genius really wanted to help shoulder some of Lin Yuan’s burdens.","Genius was able to nurture the Hundred Questions Beasts into Class 4 Creation Masters when it was only a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master. This allowed the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to significantly increase their store of Class 4 Creation Master resources.","If Genius managed to become a Class 5 Creation Master, it might be able to use Connected Tails to produce a few Class 5 Creation Masters from the army of Hundred Questions Beasts!","If it could produce Class 5 Creation Masters, the resources that could be produced in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would be substantially improved.","This was why Genius felt so strongly about becoming a Class 5 Creation Master.","Lin Yuan treated Genius well, so Genius had to reciprocate!","Genius and Lin Yuan both liked to keep their true feelings to themselves instead of expressing them.","This was unlike Chimey, who twittered non-stop whenever it was in Lin Yuan’s arms.","Genius had tried to advise Chimey numerous times.","Chimey burped continuously daily as it drank the Grade 4 potions that Genius concocted. Otherwise, its bloodline would not have evolved so smoothly when it evolved to Myth Breed.","After Genius evolved to Myth Breed, Lin Yuan would not have any other feys he needed to help to overcome their trials anytime soon.","Dark Blue was currently refining the energy from within strange water and still needed some time.","Lin Yuan had only started nurturing Shiny. Coiling Dragon’s Valley had finally started producing dragon liver in batches. Dark Clouds Bird Shrine had also offered to supply Lin Yuan with a large amount of phoenix essence blood.","The Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil and Purple Demon still needed to build up their bloodlines.","The Merciful Star Peony’s grade could only be evolved after Lin Yuan used moonlight to temper himself. He currently did not have the time to do so. He intended to find the time to ask the Moon Empress to use Forage Moon’s six moons to temper him.","Not only did his physique improve rapidly, but the Merciful Star Peony’s grade and quality would also increase quickly. It might even mutate!","Weng Queji was entirely focused on the Bug-Consuming Thearch Emperor Lizards’ family.","Lin Yuan didn’t worry because a Class 5 Creation Master was constructing a fortress with six Bug-Consuming Thearch Emperor Lizards.","...","After leaving the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Genius, without any extra preparations, immediately used the second ability of Tail of Fate, Highest Access Tail.","Suddenly, Genius’ spiritual energy sea gathered. Its illusionary tails merged into one, shooting upward through the cloud-covered sky, carrying the spiritual energy sea.","World willpower activated instantly. The clouds dispersed, forming a deep vortex. The current clouds seemed unpredictable.","While looking at Genius, Lin Yuan’s lips tightened. Genius had suffered greatly during its evolution to Fantasy Breed. Its flesh had been taken apart, and it had nearly lost its life.","Due to that, Lin Yuan feared for Genius’ safety when it asked the heavens for a path to become a Class 5 Creation Master.","Only those who truly cared would experience a sense of loss.","What surprised Lin Yuan even more was that aside from the vortex of clouds formed by Genius’ communion with the heavens, everything else remained calm.","Genius hadn’t even utilized Tail Trigger.","Suddenly, an aura emanated from Genius, triggering World Cleansing instantly.","Genius’ World Cleansing was unique. Spiritual and soul fluctuations with an annihilative aura emerged from the sky’s opening.","Lin Yuan briefly wondered if this World Cleansing was specific to Genius or if all spiritual- and soul-type feys underwent it while evolving to Myth Breed.","Regardless, Eternal Source blocked this fierce World Cleansing with a finger flick.","Following this, the World Grace landed on Genius’ body.","Light emanated from Genius’ body and enveloped it.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Genius.","[Fey Name]: Highest Access Fate-Knowing Beast","[Fey Species]: Fantasy-cat-genus/fantasy-cat-species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[Memory Deduction]: When recalling something, it will be able to remember every minuscule detail. From this, it will be able to organize the information and infer the truth.","[Crowded Cat]: If it can control cat-species feys and convince the cats to crowd around it, it will be able to become affiliated with all of the cat-species feys’ elements and bodies. Every time the cat-species feys crowded around, it will be weak for some time.","[Spiritual Energy Expansion]: Transfer the spiritual energy into an emergency bank for the contractor. Even though the contractor cannot willfully use Spiritual Energy Expansion to increase his own store of spiritual energy, he can use it to defend himself against spiritual energy damage.","[Master of Cats]: As the new leader of cat-species feys, it can use spiritual energy to form contracts with other cat-species feys, control their lives, and share in their spiritual power.","[Soul Permutation]: Use and change different spiritual energies into soul power.","[Tail Trigger]: When using soul power, a tail can be sacrificed to increase the soul power. The spiritual energy inside the body can also be condensed to produce replacement tails to be used when there are no longer any tails left and Tail Trigger cannot be used.","[True Knowledge Analysis]: Use spiritual energy to envelop an entity, and the composition of the entity will be analyzed. Entities that have been combined will be analyzed separately. After the analysis, there will be a confirmation from the heavenly will to ascertain accuracy.","Exclusive Skill:","[Tool Transformation]: Capable of transforming into a tool for the contractor to use.","[Tail of Fate]: 1. Connected Tails: According to the number of tails, lives can be connected. The connected lives can share thinking and intention. 2. Highest Access Tail: Combine all the tails into one. If it craves for knowledge enough, it can sacrifice its spiritual energy to communicate with the heavens and request for an answer.","[Sky Fate Attachment]: The affiliation with heavenly will will be deepened, and the fate of the heavenly will will be attached to it to elevate its chances of success when concocting spirit fluids or when performing other actions."]},{"number":2628,"title":"Chapter 2628 The Army of Hundred Questions Beasts Expanded to the Limit!","paragraphs":["2628 The Army of Hundred Questions Beasts Expanded to the Limit!","Genius had not evolved from the Highest Access Fate-Knowing Beast despite reaching Myth Breed!","Lin Yuan was not surprised by this at all.","Genius’ bloodline had only evolved from the Beast that Connects Everything to the Highest Access Fate-Knowing Beast due to a coincidental opportunity that occurred during its evolution to Diamond grade.","The Highest Access Fate-Knowing Beast’s life rank was extremely high and was linked to the roots of the world. It had the same life rank as the Sky-Plundering Beast!","Morbius had already very seriously confirmed this with Lin Yuan.","When compared to Chimey that had grown up with Genius, Chimey could produce the sun from its body but Genius’ bloodline was still more elite!","This was why Lin Yuan wanted to give one of the totem seeds to the Hundred Questions Beast species.","It was very unlikely that Genius’ bloodline would evolve again before it reached Eternal or set its spirit fire alight!","Genius was currently swaddled by light. It had become a Suzerain/Myth fey and gained a new ability called True Knowledge Analysis.","Genius could analyze the structure and capabilities of an entity when it wrapped the entity in its spiritual energy.","This would not only allow Genius to use its spiritual energy to understand its target but also to communicate with the target’s roots.","In this aspect, there was some overlap between Genius and True Data’s ability. It could be considered a weaker version of True Data.","However, Lin Yuan was not at all disappointed by this overlap. Rather, he was very excited about it!","There were some special spiritual ingredients that Genius was unable to fully understand, given its current knowledge. Lin Yuan would need to examine the spiritual ingredients’ properties before Genius began using them. Due to this, Genius was unable to function fully independently from Lin Yuan.","But True Knowledge Analysis would allow Genius to stand on its own from now on!","Furthermore, True Knowledge Analysis could also discern between combined entities and analyze their capabilities individually.","Every Class 5 Creation Master had their own unique concoctions, and they would never divulge the recipes of those concoctions to others.","Before each recipe was considered complete, the Class 5 Creation Master would have to study it carefully and conduct many trials!","But if Genius got its hands on those potions, it could use True Knowledge Analysis to uncover the types and proportion of spiritual ingredients required to make these spirit fluids as well as what functions they had. In Genius’ hands, these potions were no longer secrets!","Furthermore, after analyzing their composition, Genius could use heavenly will to confirm if its analysis was accurate! This meant that Genius’ analyses would never be wrong.","True Knowledge Analysis was even more impressive than a Class 6 Creation Master!","The Moon Empress was a Class 6 Creation Master, and the one who had proposed the definition of a Class 6 Creation Master.","Lin Yuan could be certain she studied every potion that passed her eyes. However, it was difficult for her to come up with the exact recipe for every potion unless she had a large amount of the potion available that would allow her to conduct repeated experiments!","However, Sky Fate Attachment, which Genius attained after reaching Myth Breed, was even more astonishing than the Suzerain ability, True Knowledge Analysis.","Sky Fate Attachment would allow Genius to deepen its affiliation with heavenly will and use it to boost itself—its chances of success when concocting spirit fluids of performing any other actions would be raised!","The ‘other actions’ referred to those that only Class 5 Creation Masters could perform, such as creating precious instruments.","Lin Yuan could tell from Genius’ abilities and exclusive skills that it had found its own unique Class 5 Creation Master path.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of potions, the higher the grade, the more precious ingredients they required and the stronger their effects would be.","The world that Lin Yuan knew as the main world was only a Class 1 world, so the spiritual ingredients available there had limited effects.","Once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and came into contact with Class 2, Class 3, or even more powerful worlds, the spiritual ingredients available there would have even more incredible medicinal properties!","The higher the grade of potions, the lower the chances of a successful concoction.","Lin Yuan was not going down the traditional Creation Master route, but Genius was.","From now on, Genius could concoct spirit fluids with special effects as long as it had access to spiritual ingredients!","Even if Sky Fate Attachment only raised the chances of success by a hair, it would still save a sea of resources for Lin Yuan, both in concocting spirit fluids and creating precious instruments!","The concoction of spirit fluids was one matter, but the creation of precious instruments required spiritual ingredients that came from the bodies of sacred source lifeforms. If these spiritual ingredients were damaged during the forging process, it would be extremely difficult to replace them.","Lin Yuan let out a soft breath. Genius’ evolution had not put it in any danger, and the abilities and exclusive skills it had gained far exceeded Lin Yuan’s expectations. Lin Yuan was floored by every one of Genius’ evolutions!","The light that enveloped Genius slowly faded and revealed Genius’ body.","Genius’ body had not changed in size, but its fur was even fluffier than before. It also had nine tails now instead of eight.","Lin Yuan thought, Amongst all the feys, the fox-species determines the ranking of their bloodlines based on their tails. It almost seems as though Genius is evolving according to the fox-species bloodline!","But it was clear that the Hundred Questions Beast species that Genius represented was going down a completely different direction of evolution from fox-species feys as there were very few Hundred Questions Beasts besides Genius who sported so many tails!","This feature of having tails was the most obvious when it came to Genius’ evolutions.","The other Hundred Questions Beasts did not have abilities like Master of Cats either.","Perhaps, unlike the other Hundred Questions Beasts, Genius was a true miracle that Lin Yuan had managed to create!","Lin Yuan was very curious to find out how many tails Genius would end up with once it had reached its final stage of evolution!","By now, Genius had opened its eyes. The first thing it did was fix its eyes on Lin Yuan.","Genius moved over to Lin Yuan’s side and said in a child-like voice, “Yuan, I am now a Class 5 Creation Master. Once I enter the Spirit Lock spatial zone and begin teaching the other members of the Hundred Questions Beast army, most of them will be able to become Class 4 Creation Masters!","“I also discovered something. There are no defined gates to pass once one has become a Class 5 Creation Master. You can only continue studying and exploring the roots of all creatures! So, there is no need to define classes past Class 5 Creation Master. Based on my understanding of Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch, I am slightly stronger than them now!","“Once I become more familiar with concocting a few spirit fluids, I should be able to reach the level of a Class 6 Creation Master!”","Lin Yuan stroked Genius’ chin, and Genius purred happily.","From what Genius said, Lin Yuan now understood why the Moon Empress had once told him so seriously that the Creation Master path eventually came to an abrupt end, and it was very difficult to continue moving forward past that point.","But after learning about the existence of the Sky Beyond the Clouds from him, the Moon Empress then said that there was no end to a Creation Master’s path of growth.","When Creation Masters reached Class 5, their abilities would be improved based on their experience and familiarization with handling spiritual ingredients.","All those who were able to become Class 5 Creation Masters would possess potent spiritual energy and soul power! They would not differ much in terms of the level of control they had over spiritual energy.","“Genius, I will have to trouble you to stay in the Spirit Lock spatial zone for now to teach the army of Hundred Questions Beasts. Both your grade and quality have increased. Now that you are a Suzerain/Myth fey, it’s time to expand the army of Hundred Questions Beasts and group of cats!","“What do you think about this? I have purposefully nurtured more than 3,000 excellent Bronze/Legend cat-species feys. You can take your pick from among them!”","Genius meowed upon hearing that and said solemnly, “I intend on adding another 500 spots to the army of Hundred Questions Beasts. It will require all the effort I can muster to teach 1,000 Hundred Questions Beasts. Any more, and I won’t have the time to teach every single one of them!","“However, the Hundred Questions Beasts that have become Class 4 Creation Masters will be able to teach 100 Hundred Questions Beast students each on top of their daily concoction of spirit fluids. According to these numbers, there will be 1,000 core members of the Hundred Questions Beast army, as well as 100,000 peripheral members. They might struggle to teach the other Hundred Questions Beasts at first, but they will get used to it quickly!","“When we return and I inform Hu Quan about the properties of various spiritual ingredients, I will tell him about my ideas so he can come up with a design. As long as the structure is tall enough, the army of 100,000 peripheral Hundred Questions Beasts won’t take up too much space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","“Frankly, I think that giving every Hundred Questions Beast 80 to 100 square feet of space to work is too much space. Why don’t we—”","Before Genius could finish speaking, Lin Yuan interrupted it. “Genius, firstly, the Spirit Lock spatial zone will only continue to grow larger. With its current size, it can already fit ten million of the Hundred Questions Beasts! You don’t have to worry about space.","“Additionally, you can’t go back on matters you have already made promises on, especially as the leader of the army of Hundred Questions Beasts. Due to the contraction, the other Hundred Questions Beasts will remain loyal to you, but going back on your promises will definitely result in unrest.","“Why don’t we increase the size of the rooms for the main members to 120 square feet while the peripheral members will get 80 to 100 square feet? Hu Quan has been studying mechanics recently. He can build an elevator that will enable the building where the army of Hundred Questions Beasts will work to be thousands of meters tall.","“One building will be able to house more than 30,000 Hundred Questions Beasts, so three buildings will perfectly make up a base for the army of Hundred Questions Beasts. Once the construction of the base is complete, only you and the other Hundred Questions Beasts will be allowed to enter and exit. No one else will be allowed to enter under normal circumstances! I will assign ten Spirit Craftsmen to fix up and decorate the interior.”","Genius possessed an enormous amount of information but was not skilled at interpersonal experiences.","Genius could manage a group of 500 members, but when the group grew to 10,000 members or more, Genius couldn’t use its original method to manage the army of Hundred Questions Beasts.","Luckily, thanks to the Master of Cats ability, Genius had complete control over the army of Hundred Questions Beasts. Without this ability, neither Lin Yuan nor Genius would have expanded the army to such a large size.","As the army grew, more of them gained the abilities of Class 5 Creation Masters. This caused Lin Yuan’s production of Creation Master resources to become massive.","In the future, Lin Yuan’s Creation Master resources would go beyond spirit qi crystals and elemental pearls. He would also produce various types of potions!","“Genius, I will ask Listen to ship 500 Hundred Questions Beasts over. Once you have spoken to the army of Hundred Questions Beast and registered all those who have become Class 4 Creation Masters, I will personally lead them in picking out students.”","Lin Yuan’s approach would be rather tedious, but Lin Yuan did not think that this was a bad thing.","The Hundred Questions Beasts would essentially be picking disciples. Lin Yuan was willing to give them the chance to select their own disciples! This would incentivize them to do their best in teaching these disciples!","Genius would be fully responsible for everything in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Once the Wailing Snake and Sentient Being Protective Dragon secured themselves in the Pure Land of Bliss, the Spirit Lock spatial zone would not only be a paradise but also a place of blessing!","...","The Dictators and Apostles Lin Yuan sent to Wen Yu had arrived.","With these Apostles and Dictators, Wen Yu was confident she could gather all of the Continent Vein Cores on the other side of the Barren Sea within a month!","From her exploration, Wen Yu discovered there were federations on the other side of the Barren Sea as well, but there were no powerful cultures.","The figures in the federations that could be considered Creation Masters all held shockingly high positions and were treated almost no differently from gods! But in actuality, very few of them were truly capable.","While Wen Yu was interacting with these federations, she found out they held themselves in extremely high regard and were very arrogant toward her.","Thus, Wen Yu had no inclination to continue interacting with them.","She immediately moved on to exploring further locations after instructing Dazzling Silver and a few Turning Wheel Realm Dictators to grab the Continent Vein Cores.","Chu Ci was with Wen Yu. After a few short weeks of training, Chu Ci already felt as though she had experienced true growth!","This allowed Chu Ci to get a clear look at what the world she lived in was like. She no longer saw honing her combat skills as training. The experience she gained from such experiences seemed inconsequential now!","Chu Ci finally understood how Lin Yuan managed to grow so rapidly. He had blown right past his peers and was an unrivaled genius!","It was because Lin Yuan never lived in a comfortable bubble. He was constantly walking along the edge of a knife."]},{"number":2629,"title":"Chapter 2629 The Radiance Federation and Vast Sea Labyrinth Link Up!","paragraphs":["2629 The Radiance Federation and Vast Sea Labyrinth Link Up!","Since he was young, Lin Yuan always provided Chu Ci with the most comfortable and safe environments. With him around, Chu Ci never felt that she was missing out on familial love despite the death of their parents. Rather, with Lin Yuan’s affection, Chu Ci already felt she was being enveloped by sunshine and love.","Wen Yu decided that she would return 35 days later.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation through the Space Tunnel.","He planned on fetching Wen Yu 35 days later.","Lin Yuan felt he should refrain from using the Space Tunnel to travel as much as possible from the Radiance Federation to the Grotto Continent. Even someone as rich as him felt strained by the resources required for each trip.","It went without saying that Lin Yuan also asked Wen Yu to tell the human clusters on the other side of the Barren Sea about the impending disaster.","Because the Barren Sea separated them, the continents on the other side of the Barren Sea seemed to be disconnected, but their ley lines still linked them.","The disaster that was about to occur due to the Sleeper’s Revival would also affect the other side of the Barren Sea.","Lin Yuan would not be so callous as to send the federations on the other side of the Barren Sea to their deaths.","If these federations were willing to believe Lin Yuan, he would be willing to relocate them.","There was no way that Lin Yuan could facilitate such a large-scale migration.","Although the Spirit Lock spatial zone had become several times larger than its original size and the people from the other side of the Barren Sea could be transported through Klein Hub to the marsh world, Lin Yuan had many plans for the base in the main world and did not have time.","However, due to the Heavenly Family Cottage and the Radiance Federation’s awareness of Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan, the Radiance Federation finally linked up with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Lin Yuan had presided over this matter through the Moon Empress. The Radiance Federation was now working with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth was the secret ruler of the sea and controlled the most Island Whales of any organization in the main world.","The Island Whales could cross the Barren Sea, so the Vast Sea Labyrinth could be asked to relocate the federations that wanted to be relocated.","After Wen Yu communicated with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper and learned of his plans, she felt that he was too kind!","She felt there was no need for Lin Yuan to be concerned for the federations on the other side of the Barren Sea as their survival was irrelevant to Sky City’s profits!","Suddenly, Wen Yu remembered something that Mystic Moon had said. “With your intelligence, you would eventually be able to prove your capabilities to the Radiant Moon Palace. This is unquestionable. Although you were unable to complete the Moon Envoy test due to your injured roots and were sent to work beneath the four Moon Servants, you would eventually be able to distinguish yourself!","“I am unsure if I could take you in as my disciple after discovering your talents. But I definitely wouldn’t recommend that you become a Radiance Knight. Someone as calm as you is too rational and aloof to be able to think for the Radiance Federation’s sake.”","After Mystic Moon became Wen Yu’s master, they were always fully candid with each other.","Mystic Moon’s words did not trigger any negative emotions in Wen Yu, and she even agreed with him. She also felt faintly sweet.","This was because everything she had came from Lin Yuan. Without him, she would never have caught Mystic Moon’s notice.","She had only been able to grow to this point because she had experienced multiple transformations and awakenings.","Without Lin Yuan’s help and saving, she would have slowly sunk into dark despair and depression.","There was no way she would be enveloped in warm sunlight like she currently was!","If Liu Jie and Lin Yuan had not given her pressure or opportunities, she would never have been able to develop her talent in governance.","Lin Yuan’s spirit always attracted Wen Yu. It was exactly what she lacked.","Wen Yu always followed Lin Yuan’s instructions to the letter.","The federations on the other side of the Barren Sea were on relatively good terms with each other. This was because they were situated rather far from each other and had almost no contact.","With the scarcity of resources, the federations that had contact with each other had already battled each other to near destruction. One would either conquer the other or relocate further from the other.","Although the federations were in a relatively peaceful state with each other, their internal affairs were tumultuous.","The scarcity of resources was so serious that food supply had become a big challenge.","Furthermore, Creation Masters could nurture production-type feys and were very powerful. This allowed them to become the centers of their respective federations.","This living condition was very similar to that of the Grotto Continent and Broiling Rock Continent.","These continents were on the other side of the Barren Sea and happened to be miniature versions of the other side of the Barren Sea.","The factions on the other side of the Barren Sea were all riled up by the news brought by Wen Yu.","Firstly, Wen Yu was sufficiently powerful, yet they did not try to take over the federations by force. Thus, almost all of the federations believed what she said.","However, the federations all had different opinions about whether they would relocate to the other side of the Barren Sea.","Wen Yu left a Turning Wheel Realm Dictator in every federation. They would not only act as guides when the citizens of the federations did decide to leave but would also give them the freedom to make their own choices rather than being strong-armed into following the decisions of the Creation Masters.","Those who were made aware of the situation but still refused to leave could be left there to battle the dead spirits when the Sleeper’s Revival plan began.","Wen Yu gave out these tasks but did not forget that the most important matter at hand was searching for the Continent Vein Cores.","After discovering the Broiling Rock Continent, she did not waste any time and sent two Turning Wheel Realm Dictators off with resources to help Peace.","...","The millions of Land Imps in the Radiance Federation worked tirelessly, and the laying down of the metal-type stone boards was completed with no issues.","This was partly due to Bai Qinghuan’s supervision but also because the Land Imps were under the control of the subterranean world’s treasure, the Earth Source Cube.","Otherwise, lifeforms as sly as the Land Imps would never do their best in a job unless their lives were on the line.","Lin Yuan finally relaxed after the metal-type stone boards were laid down.","It could be said that now that the metal-type stone boards were laid down, the foundation for the defense against the Sleeper’s Revival plan was complete.","If the Sleeper’s Revival began before the metal-type stone boards were laid down, Lin Yuan would never be able to protect the Radiance Federation, regardless of his capability.","With the foundation of the defenses now complete, the Land Imps could send any powerful dead spirits that broke through the metal-type stone boards into the Dead Spirits Well that the Land Imps would soon construct. The spiritual ingredients meant for the Dead Spirits Well had been prepared before the metal-type stone boards had been fully laid down.","Now, they would begin laying down the metal-type stone boards outwards. Lin Yuan had been analyzing a way to join the five dimensional worlds with the main world.","However, Lin Yuan was unsure if he would be making the right decision by evolving this Class 1 world into Class 2.","Morbius had yet to recover relevant memories, and Lin Yuan was afraid he would cause problems by hastily combining the dimensional worlds with the main world.","But it seemed this would be his best chance of protecting the main world, so he needed to make a decision.","...","The representative groups from the various federations had gathered in the Radiance Federation.","All of them had arrived at the Radiance Federation feeling very troubled.","The location for the first meeting of the Major Federation Union was the Radiance Federation. This caused all the federations to begin guessing how the Freedom Federation had been convinced to give way.","The news from the Radiance Federation came so abruptly that the various federations had not had the time to come up with many guesses.","While on the way here, the federations’ representative groups and the federations they came from were all gathering information in a frenzy. But all they found out was that the Freedom Federation’s royalty had made a trip to the Radiance Federation.","This included the Mirror God and God of Fools. Could the Freedom Federation’s royalty have struck a deal with the Radiance Federation?","The heads of the various federations had a feeling that the sudden meeting of the Major Federation Union was related to that.","However, the Radiance, Freedom, and Azure Federations were all extremely tight-lipped about this matter and refused to let out even a peep.","The Radiance Federation was the head of the Major Federation Union, and the Freedom Federation and Radiance Federation had already discussed the Major Federation Union in advance. But, none of the other federations knew that the two federations had left the Azure Federation out of the loop.","The Azure Federation’s 12 aristocratic families had asked the Radiance Federation for information multiple times, but the Moon Empress had not told them anything in advance.","There was no airtight wall in the world. Even if there was, it was likely that Tower Canon had already placed moles within the various federations.","If the Moon Empress let out information in advance, Tower Canon would find out that their plan had been exposed and that the main world was coming up with a way to stop them. It would also lead to mass hysteria.","If the information was released during the Major Federation Union, the federations could react immediately and devise strategies to deal with the issue.","By sending all of their members of royalty to the Radiance Federation, the Freedom Federation had expressed sufficient sincerity.","The Mirror God and God of Fools had not tried to hide their presence at all while traveling on their fey carriage. This shocked all of the representatives of the various federations.","No matter how crucial this meeting was for the Freedom Federation, they could’ve simply sent one royal member, or at most, the Mirror God or the God of Fools. So, why did both of them come?","Were the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation going to fight during the Major Federation Union meeting?","...","The Moon Empress had been hanging on using rejuvenating spiritual ingredients. She had not rested in two weeks. Even birth-horoscope experts would get headaches if they remained tightly wound for a prolonged period.","The Moon Empress reached out and pressed her temples while listening to Cold Moon’s report.","Ever since Cold Moon left to train Chu Ci, Mystic Moon took up the responsibilities of both Moon Envoys. But now that Cold Moon was back, she resumed her duties.","Mystic Moon had always handled the internal affairs, while Cold Moon was more skilled at handling external affairs.","“Moon Empress, the Radiance Sacred Hall, which was chosen as the location for the Major Federation Union meeting, has been set up. I oversaw the entire process, and there were no issues!","“Of the federations we sent invitations to, only a few of them did not return with a response. A few of those who responded and are located relatively further away still haven’t arrived. But the rest have all been settled into envoy lodgings in the Royal Capital.”","The Moon Empress nodded before asking, “Did those federations located relatively further away say when they will be able to arrive?”","Cold Moon hurriedly replied, “The latest of them will be able to arrive by 5:00 a.m. today! I suggest that we hold the Major Federation Union meeting tomorrow afternoon.”","Cold Moon understood the situation and knew how urgent it was.","Otherwise, given the protocol for guests that the Radiance Federation usually had, they would have given these envoy groups a day to rest.","However, given the circumstances, not even the Moon Empress had time to rest. She had not slept in two weeks.","The Moon Empress was already extending the greatest sincerity and honor to these federation envoy groups by waiting for all of them to arrive before starting the Major Federation Union meeting.","“Cold Moon, tell all this to Cicada Song. Tell him to inform the envoy groups to gather in the Radiance Sacred Hall tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m.!”","The Moon Empress had been a bundle of worries. But luckily, she received a message from Lin Yuan saying the foundational defenses for the Radiance Federation had been completed.","Lin Yuan had invested heavily by using millions of Land Imps and secret spiritual ingredients from the subterranean world! Through this, he created a miracle that the Moon Empress would never have dared to dream of in the past.","In order to understand Tower Canon’s exact timeline of actions, the Moon Empress had sent the Mirror God and God of Fools to contact Tower Canon.","The Mirror God and God of Fools had failed to contact any of the real pages of Tower Canon, like First Page Crimson, but they were able to get in contact with Sixth Page Inverse Growth, who had worked with the Freedom Federation in the past.","The Moon Empress had asked the God of Fools and Mirror God to contact Sixth Page Inverse Growth because she had no other choice, but she ended up receiving unexpected benefits!","Sixth Page Inverse Growth had invited the Mirror God and God of Fools to head to Tower Canon’s headquarters two months later to listen in on a strategy meeting. They would also be invited to join Tower Canon then.","This meant Tower Canon would not make any moves within the next two months.","More than a month had passed since the Mirror God and God of Fools had contacted Sixth Page Inverse Growth.","The Moon Empress did not believe that Tower Canon would truly make the Mirror God and God of Fools part of the Eight Pages. If Tower Canon had this intention, they would already have gotten in contact with the Mirror God and God of Fools instead of waiting until now!","It was likely that Tower Canon was trying to eliminate the threats that the Mirror God and God of Fools, who were spirit-fire experts, posed.","Relocating the various federations within a month was a very tight timeline. But if it was handled immediately, a large-scale operation involving Platinum avian-type feys stood a high chance of success!","As long as these federations brought their citizens to the edge of their beaches, they would not have to shoulder the stress of migrations on their own.","Otherwise, even if they were given an entire year, there was no way that the federations could relocate all of their citizens!","Once they moved to the edge of their beaches, the Vast Sea Labyrinth would take over. They would use their Island Whales to transport the citizens to the Radiance Federation’s harbor.","The Moon Empress told Lin Yuan this decision so he would have time to prepare.","After the federations had been relocated to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan could decide whether to combine the five dimensional worlds with the main world."]},{"number":2630,"title":"Chapter 2630 World Emperor Grade!","paragraphs":["2630 World Emperor Grade!","Recently, Lin Yuan had been doing all he could to collect spirit qi crystals. Morbius had also absorbed its World Grace during its evolution to Myth Breed. As a result, Lin Yuan possessed an astonishing store of spirit qi crystals.","Since Lin Yuan did not have many opportunities to use these spirit qi crystals, he decided to use some to evolve Green Vine.","Green Vine had already been evolved to Sovereign/Immortal III. It was the strongest combatant Lin Yuan possessed that he had evolved through spirit qi crystals.","Rather than letting the spirit qi crystals sit in storage, it would be better to put them to use.","Feys that had reached Sovereign/Immortal were very foreign to Lin Yuan. He had not yet had the chance to interact with feys of such level.","He did have experts under him who possessed feys of such a level and had helped them to evolve said feys.","However, his method of helping them increase their power involved giving them World Crystals, the Immortal bodies cleansed by the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, as well as pure spirit qi and elemental pearls. All he needed to do was give them these resources, and the experts would know how to evolve their feys themselves.","Lin Yuan knew the Moon Empress had been busy with the Major Federation Union and had not had much time to rest.","The Major Federation Union meeting was going to begin tomorrow, so the Moon Empress would definitely take a good rest today. Lin Yuan did not want to disturb her rest.","Apart from the Moon Empress, Mystic Moon and Cold Moon also knew about the Sovereign/Immortal level. Cold Moon was currently unavailable as she was liaising with the teams from the other federations while Mystic Moon had remained in the Radiant Moon Palace to handle the internal affairs. Hence, Lin Yuan made his call to Mystic Moon.","Mystic Moon was currently instructing the spirit attendants as they helped to check the coronation costume the Moon Empress would be wearing tomorrow.","When Mystic Moon received Lin Yuan's call, a smile broke out on his gruff face.","During the early period, when he had only just become the Moon Empress' disciple, Lin Yuan would occasionally call Mystic Moon to ask him for help.","But ever since Lin Yuan became fully independent, he rarely called Mystic Moon. Mystic Moon made most calls to Lin Yuan.","The important figures of the Radiance Federation now communicated with each other solely through the Thoughts Letter Paper. If this was a critical matter, Lin Yuan would definitely have written to Mystic Moon.??????????????xt.??????","Now that he was calling, it meant that his question was not urgent.","\"Young Lord, the Moon Empress has also prepared clothes for you. Are you really not going to attend the Major Federation Union meeting?\"","Lin Yuan had told the Moon Empress with certainty that he would not be attending the Major Federation Union meeting some time ago.","Firstly, he was short on time and could not afford to expend energy on the Major Federation Union meeting. As he needed to take on Tower Canon soon, he had more pressing matters to attend to.","Additionally, he was still too young, and it would be a challenge for him to persuade the masses to follow his lead. After all, he could not go to every federation to prove himself to them.","Furthermore, his goals were no longer contained within the main world but had extended to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","\"Uncle Mystic, I really won't attend the Major Federation Union meeting. I am calling to ask you about the changes that can happen to feys during their evolution once they reach High Sovereign/ Immortal.\"","Mystic Moon was momentarily stunned by this. He did not understand why Lin Yuan, an A-rank spirit qi professional, would need to ask such a question.","Moreover, the Moon Empress usually cleared Lin Yuan's doubts. It would not be appropriate for him to go over her head to answer his question!","But the Moon Empress was currently resting. There was no way that Mystic Moon could disturb her over such a matter.","Yet, he also could not let Lin Yuan's question go unanswered!","After a moment of silence, Mystic Moon began explaining to Lin Yuan seriously, \"Young Lord, I'm sure you're familiar with the basics. The Immortal Breed comes before the Eternal Breed. Immortal Breed has levels up to Immortal IX, while the Eternal Breed has levels up to Eternal XII. Beyond Eternal XII lies an empty space known as Above Eternal. However, it's still quite a distance from reaching the birth-horoscope level.","\"Once you attain the birth-horoscope level, you can attempt to ignite your spirit fire. This process grants feys an additional exclusive skill as they evolve from Immortal to Eternal, but no new exclusive skills are gained afterward. The only change is the increase in their life rank. Moreover, there are no more defined grades beyond Sovereign X.\"","Lin Yuan nodded lightly at Mystic Moon's explanation.","The spirit-fire level was considered the peak of the main world. There were many few birth-horoscope experts in the main world, much less spirit-fire ones! Hence, it was understandable there were no more clearly defined grades and qualities above this level for feys.","However, according to how fey grades and qualities were defined, it seemed that Above Eternal, birth-horoscope, and spirit-fire levels were all transitional. This was because the feys would not gain any new abilities or exclusive skills at those levels.","Just as this thought was settling in Lin Yuan's mind, Morbius' voice echoed in Lin Yuan's head. \"Partner, you have the right idea. That should be how it works! Based on my examination of Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor, who are Afterlife Realm Dictators, I learned that lifeforms who surpass the spirit-fire level will be able to gain new abilities and exclusive skills!","\"If my memory is right, breaking through High Sovereign will lead to World Emperor. However, the divine kingdoms of feys and dimensional lifeforms are very different from yours.\"","Lin Yuan had not been shocked by what Mystic Moon said, but Morbius' words caused his heart to begin hammering in his chest.","It was likely that the World Emperor grade and divine-kingdom level referred to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Lin Yuan carefully made a note of these terms.","Lin Yuan was very curious to see the extent to which Green Vine could evolve given his current store of spirit qi crystals, and if it could break through to the World Emperor and the divine kingdom!","Lin Yuan only needed one fey whose quality had reached the divine-kingdom level, and he could gain an accurate understanding of a regular divine kingdom! He would find out just how it differed from his own divine kingdom that had formed from the shrine in his soul!","Mystic Moon's description was detailed. He sincerely tried to teach Lin Yuan, and it gave Lin Yuan an understanding of the levels above Immortal Breed.","After the phone call ended, Lin Yuan used Node Transportation to transport to the location where Morbius had evolved to Myth Breed. He intended to evolve Green Vine there.","Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor were Afterlife Realm Dictators, making them the equivalent of feys who had reached World Emperor and the divine-kingdom level. With them around, there was no need for Lin Yuan to worry about Green Vine's evolution.","Green Vine preferred to stay in fey form rather than human form. It differed from the Mother of Bloodbath and Endless Summer in this aspect.","Unless it had to be in human form for convenience's sake while it accompanied Lin Yuan, Green Vine preferred to remain elegantly rooted to the ground, swaying its vines around. Its different vines would crisscross, forming abstract shapes.","This caused Lin Yuan to wonder whether Green Vine, who had the appearance of a pretty woman, was actually an old woman with skewed tastes!","Ever since it could think independently, Green Vine never had to be concerned about its evolutions and could rely fully on Lin Yuan to supply the resources. Thus, it was not as enthusiastic and motivated about evolving as other feys. It was similar to a child who had been fed delicacies all its life and so was not excited by delicious food.","Lin Yuan reached out and touched Green Vine's vines, and it reciprocated by wrapping its vines around him before lifting him up.","This would come across to anyone else as though a tentacle beast was hunting its prey. But to Lin Yuan, this was the most basic form of interaction between him and Green Vine.","Lin Yuan exasperatedly patted Green Vine's vine and said, \"Okay, enough playing! I'm here to evolve your grade. I want to see how far you can go! From now on and for a long time, you will be the strongest of all my feys, so you will have to handle all combat- related matters!\"","Green Vine obediently set Lin Yuan back down on the ground as it said with fiery passion burning in its eyes, \"Don't worry, Yuan. Leave all the combat to me! I will do my best to increase my power and protect you!\"","Lin Yuan did not respond.","He did not need Green Vine to protect him but did not mind letting Green Vine continue thinking this. Only with such a mindset would Green Vine be filled with a sense of responsibility and work harder at increasing its power!","Lin Yuan felt that despite reaching High Sovereign/Immortal, Green Vine was still a greenhorn who had yet to experience any obstacles.","He intended to use this impending disaster involving dead spirits to properly train Green Vine.","The spirit qi crystals were all placed inside custom Diamond fey storage boxes. All of the custom Diamond fey storage boxes that Lin Yuan had were in the shape of rings. This made them very convenient to carry around.","Lin Yuan took out all of the Diamond fey storage boxes as he readied himself to feed them all to Green Vine during its evolution.","Many spirit qi professionals in Thick Soil City were still waiting to increase their power. If Lin Yuan made a trip back to Thick Soil City, he could top up his store of spirit qi crystals.","When the federations of the main world were all gathered in the Radiance Federation, those experts would become the 'garden' from which Lin Yuan could harvest spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan had plenty of ways to obtain spirit qi crystals. Thus, he did not need to worry he would be left without a way of replenishing his store of spirit qi crystals after using up all that he had on hand.","Green Vine changed into human form while it was absorbing spirit qi crystals.","At that moment, Green Vine's left arm was covered by an armor made of vines while its right leg had transformed into two vines.monopoly n0veIfulIbo0k There was a fiercely burning dark gold flame on its left shoulder. Once a fey reached Immortal Breed, the evolution from Immortal I to Immortal IX was meant to transform their bodies from human to humanoid forms. The objective was to blend fey features perfectly with the human form so they could wield their strongest attacks, even in humanoid form.","The body would have to go through nine transformations before reaching Immortal IX. This tempering process was excruciating for any fey.","Green Vine had reached Immortal III, and its body had already been tempered twice.","Perhaps it was due to having absorbed five of the dark gold scales that caused its body to be enveloped by dark gold flames that emanated the aura of annihilation, but Green Vine did not experience any pain during its Immortal transformations and overcame them with ease.","Green Vine's Immortal body became increasingly lustrous as the sacred fire burned. The Immortal body also intensified in color as Green Vine's power increased.","The High Sovereign II Green Vine evolved to High Sovereign X during this process.","According to Mystic Moon, feys would no longer be able to continue evolving past High Sovereign X even if they set their spirit fire alight.","Green Vine's quality also evolved from Immortal III to Immortal IX.","At that moment, Green Vine fully transformed into a human state. When it was Immortal III, Green Vine's humanoid state had looked rather ferocious. But now that it had reached Immortal IX, its Immortal body had attained perfection!","Green Vine was wrapped in an armor of vines, and there was a long dress composed of dark gold flames under the armor.","The vine whip it was holding had eight scars on it, each corresponding to one of the vines' capabilities.","Its dark green hair resembled curly vines that fell to Green Vine's waist. Its hair was its most frightening weapon.","Green Vine's body no longer had any weaknesses now that it had reached Immortal IX.","When he saw Green Vine serenely surveying its changes, Lin Yuan shouted, \"Green Vine, I still have many spirit qi crystals! Continue evolving past Eternal! Once you produce the Eternal Heart, you will gain a new exclusive skill. The Eternal Heart will also become your strongest combat method.\"","According to what Mystic Moon had said, the most lethal move that an Eternal fey could wield was producing its Eternal Heart and using it as an explosive against enemies.","It went without saying that producing the Eternal Heart and using it as an explosive would use up the energy within the Eternal Heart. This would hurt the fey's roots.","Hence, Eternal Breed feys would never produce their Eternal Hearts unless they had been pushed to the brink.","Every Eternal Heart had its own special ability that allowed the fey to transform in a unique way.","Lin Yuan wanted to know what ability Green Vine's Eternal Heart had and how it would transform Green Vine.","A fey had to cross a gaping distance to evolve from Immortal to Eternal, and it needed to be grilled by its inner demons. If it passed, it could only produce its Eternal Heart from its Immortal body.","When Immortal feys were tempered by sacred fire, they caused significant commotion. On the other hand, being grilled by their inner demons did not cause any commotion at all.","From the outside, with their eyes closed, they looked as though they were dreaming. But in actuality, being grilled by their inner demons was extremely perilous!","If they could not handle being grilled by their inner demons, their minds would become corroded, and they would devolve into lunatics."]},{"number":2631,"title":"Chapter 2631 Exclusive Skill: Vine Tempering Garrotte!","paragraphs":["2631 Exclusive Skill: Vine Tempering Garrotte!","Fortunately, most feys at that level had strong spirit qi professionals accompanying them. These professionals helped the feys endure the challenging ordeal posed by their inner demons. Consequently, over half of the feys who underwent this grueling confrontation with their inner demons managed to advance successfully to the Eternal Breed.","However, the situation was quite different for wild feys, who lacked contracts with spirit qi professionals. Their likelihood of successfully transitioning from the Immortal Breed to the Eternal Breed was less than 10%!","Lin Yuan had readied himself to assist Green Vine during its inner demons’ trial. When feys reached the Eternal stage, they became unable to handle the evolution trials on their own.","Upon hearing Lin Yuan’s words, Green Vine composed itself and began absorbing the spirit qi crystals. It sensed the security of its evolution toward the Eternal stage and the imminent transformation of its life rank. This was indeed a prime opportunity for it to augment its power.","While engrossed in absorbing the spirit qi crystals, Green Vine suddenly felt an overwhelming surge of power welling up within it. This burgeoning power brought along a multitude of thoughts and desires.","Simultaneously, Lin Yuan grappled with these very thoughts and desires, undergoing an experience mirroring Green Vine’s.","A long tug of war against Green Vine’s inner demons thus began!","With Lin Yuan’s help, Green Vine managed to emerge victorious in the tug of war and successfully evolved to Eternal. It was now a true Eternal Breed fey.","Green Vine should be considered Eternal I now.","Lin Yuan did not have the time to check the new exclusive skill that Green Vine gained after evolving to Eternal as he quickly moved on to help it with its second battle against its inner demons.","Now that they had already experienced it once, Lin Yuan and Green Vine both had an easier time during the second grilling by inner demons.","Green Vine’s path had been relatively simple thus far. Hence, its inner demons were all rather mild.","Nonetheless, after taking on 12 waves of attacks from the inner demons, Lin Yuan and Green Vine were psychologically exhausted, especially Lin Yuan, an A-rank spirit qi professional.","Green Vine’s body had become its Eternal Heart, which was able to help defend against the inner demons.","Luckily, after Green Vine produced the Eternal Heart, the burden that Lin Yuan needed to shoulder decreased substantially.","The evolved Perfect Touch Wisteria went over to Lin Yuan’s side and did not hesitate to place its inky green Eternal Heart in his hands. It was just like a child who was happily showing off its perfect test score to its parent.","When Lin Yuan held up Green Vine’s Eternal Heart, he saw that it resembled a dark green phantom quartz. The image of Green Vine’s original body could be seen within the crystal.","Green Vine said seriously, “Yuan, my Eternal Heart’s ability is Accommodation. It can be triggered in many different forms during battle. When I’m under attack, I can try accommodating the energy within the target’s attack and absorb it to replenish myself.","“My Eternal Heart will then analyze the target. The more energy I accommodate, the better understanding I will have of the target and the easier it will be for me to find a way to counter the target!”","Lin Yuan nodded lightly.","It appeared to be very simple if that was all there was to Green Vine’s Eternal Heart ability. Yet, it was not ordinary in the slightest.","It was actually the opposite in that it could even bring a powerful enemy to its knees. It was also possible for Accommodation to fully analyze a target after absorbing its energy, turning the tables of the battle.","Furthermore, Green Vine’s abilities mostly came from the abilities it gained from absorbing the eight entities.","Lin Yuan only chose the best options to fill these eight spots. Thus, it was very unlikely they would have overlapping properties as powerful entities usually had unique abilities that could not be replicated.","Examples would be the dark gold snake scales, faerie blood, and High Sovereign metals. All of them had completely different abilities.","Hence, if the Eternal Heart’s ability could only benefit a small number of entities, it would not be as useful as Accommodation, which could affect anything it came into contact with!","Lin Yuan returned the Eternal Heart to Green Vine.","Looking at Green Vine, he felt a strange feeling come over him.","Lin Yuan’s power had never been linked to his spirit qi professional rank. His power came from him using special methods to take control of other experts and make them submit to him.","But now, he was a spirit qi professional who had only recently reached A-rank but possessed a High Sovereign X/Eternal XII fey.","No one would believe that this was true if he told him about this!","Lin Yuan had only been a spirit qi professional for two years.","However, there were no shortcuts to increasing one’s spirit qi professional rank.","Lin Yuan could only stay the course and increase his power as he waited for the Sleeper’s Revival plan to begin and the dead spirits to rise up.","The battle against the dead spirits would be a long and drawn-out one.","During this time, Lin Yuan would definitely be able to raise his spirit qi professional rank.","As the war progressed, the alien and demon insects would be able to develop and grow.","Lin Yuan would also be able to use this time to build up the resources in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, so he would not have to worry about his supply of resources once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Green Vine, which was now his highest-graded fey.","[Fey Name]: Perfect Touch Wisteria","[Fey Species]: Strong armor wisteria species/long wisteria species","[Fey Grade]: High Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Eternal XII","Abilities:","[Forbidden Growth]: After contracting any lifeform, it can break the limit that comes with the contract. As long as it has sufficient energy, it will be able to continuously increase its power. When it has absorbed the maximum amount of energy, it will be able to comprehend a required Willpower Rune.","[Peak Sturdiness]: A large amount of the absorbed energy can be used up to increase the durability of the vines. When injured, the energy can also be used to repair the vines.","[Long Vine Application]: Choose two vines that will be applied to one vine. The vine with the two vines applied on it will be able to gain the two vines’ abilities.","[Paralysizing Vine Sap]: When damage is sustained, the vine sap with paralyzing effects can be sprayed out from the wound.","[Brutally Pushing Out of Soil]: When faced with the opponent’s defenses, the seeds’ sprouting strength can be activated to help break past the opponent’s defenses.","[Root’s Parasitic Restraints]: Pick a target, and the target’s body will become soil where roots will grow. The roots will absorb the target’s vitality to cause harm to the target.","[Splitting Illusionary Spikes]: When the illusionary spikes pierce a target’s body, the illusionary spikes will turn into a seed that will germinate in the target’s body and produce even more illusionary spikes.","[Avoidance Wedge]: Every time Green Vine is injured, a wedge will grow over its surface. Every three layers will turn into a sharp spike that will be able to increase the vines’ effects while boosting them.","[Combined Vines Defense]: Pick a target to apply to and help it to defend against external attacks. Green Vine’s own vitality will be sacrificed to protect the target it is applied to.","Exclusive Skill:","[Swallow Same Source]: Every vine will have the same grade and quality, but they can be separated to act as individual entities. Every vine can consume something and take control of its attributes. The swallowed entity cannot be spat out, but an even higher level item can replace it. (Once it gains attributes, the vine cannot be separated again.)","[Broken Vine Replacement]: When a vine is destroyed during combat, another vine can be picked to take on the damage instead to save the first vine.","[Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn]: The energy within the vines can be gathered at a certain spot. An illusionary thorn comprised of energy will sprout from this spot. The illusionary thorn will be undetectable.","[Tactile Vine Wood World]: All of the wood-type energy and vitality stored within the vines will be released. The wood-type energy and vitality will transform into a large number of vines. The vines will intertwine and form a world of vines. The main body will fuse with this world to attack targets. Before the wooden world is broken, all the damage sustained by the main body will be reduced and shouldered by the wooden world.","[Entire Body Medium]: Sacrifice the item that the vine had absorbed and release the source of the item through a medium. The released source will not have any knowledge but will possess all of its original power. (Compare the proportion of energy that the source comprises of within the item to determine how long the released source will be able to remain outside.)","[Vine Tempering Garrotte]: Use the long vines to garrotte other lifeforms. If the target’s bloodline is more elite than that of Green Vine, Green Vine can absorb the target’s bloodline to strengthen its own bloodline. This will also strengthen every vine that has absorbed an entity through Swallow Same Source.","Lin Yuan observed that Green Vine had acquired a new exclusive skill named Vine Tempering Garrotte. This skill would allow Green Vine to absorb the bloodline of a stronger target and use it to fortify its own bloodline. This unique ability would lead to a gradual enhancement of Green Vine’s bloodline.","Until now, Green Vine’s bloodline had remained unchanged, proving inferior to the bloodlines of numerous other Eternal Breed feys. It lacked the capacity to reinforce its bloodline by assimilating entities through its own bloodline.","However, a solution had finally emerged, providing a means to strengthen its bloodline effectively.","Additionally, it seemed that this method of enhancing its bloodline had no apparent limitations. As long as Green Vine didn’t reach the pinnacle of its bloodline, there would always be room for growth.","Vine Tempering Garrotte bore a striking resemblance to Green Vine’s Eternal Heart ability. Both involved augmenting the bloodline by absorbing another’s bloodline, but Vine Tempering Garrotte had a more ambitious undertone compared to Accommodation.","While Green Vine only alluded to utilizing Accommodation defensively during disadvantaged situations, Vine Tempering Garrotte seemed to carry a more avaricious implication.","After using Vine Tempering Garrotte to strengthen its bloodline, every one of Green Vine’s vines would be boosted.","There were not many feys with powerful bloodlines in the main world that Green Vine could hunt down. Most feys with powerful bloodlines were linked to spirit qi professionals from powerful factions.","It would not be convenient for Lin Yuan to evolve Green Vine’s bloodline. Once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, where lifeforms with elite bloodlines lived, Green Vine’s bloodline could be evolved immediately!","As he looked over his remaining spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan realized that Green Vine had used less than 10% of his store of spirit qi crystals to evolve to High Sovereign X/Eternal XII.","Although most of Morbius’ World Grace had gone to evolving the Spirit Lock spatial zone and splitting its body, Lin Yuan still ended up accumulating a significant amount of spirit qi crystals!","Lin Yuan was very curious to find out if the spirit qi crystals could help Green Vine reach World Emperor and the divine-kingdom level.","Lin Yuan asked seriously, “Green Vine, how is your condition now? Are you able to continue evolving your grade, or do you need to rest for a while first?”","Green Vine shook its head. “I can continue evolving now without any issues. If I reach that gate, I will let you know immediately and won’t insist on continuing to evolve!”","Lin Yuan smiled and said, “If that’s the case, you can continue absorbing spirit qi crystals!”","Green Vine immediately started absorbing spirit qi crystals again.","Lin Yuan learned from his communication with Mystic Moon that Above Eternal, the birth-horoscope, and spirit-fire levels did not come with new abilities or exclusive skills. Thus, they were still considered within the rage of Eternal XII.","This was akin to the detailed categories within a large segment.","...","While Green Vine absorbed spirit qi crystals, the Major Federation Union meeting continued for half a day.","In the Radiance Sacred Hall, leaders of various federations wore serious expressions as they grappled with the news revealed by the Moon Empress.","They struggled to believe her words. The main world appeared tranquil, but lurking in the darkness was a terrifying danger.","Tower Canon wasn’t unfamiliar to federations with Class 5 Creation Masters. However, factions with only Class 4 Creation Masters were clueless about it. This unheard-of organization was plotting to upend the entire main world, ushering in a new era.","These federation leaders were horrified by this plan and unsure how to address the issue. They felt powerless in the face of this crisis. Could they survive such a dire threat?","If victory seemed unattainable, the purpose of establishing the Major Federation Union came into question."]},{"number":2632,"title":"Chapter 2632 What is the Moon Empress Doing?","paragraphs":["2632 What is the Moon Empress Doing?","No one would be able to place an exact number on how many lives had been lost from the first to fifth epochs. Every inch of land in the main world had been the final resting spot of billions of lifeforms.","Humans were akin to a dim light that passed from epoch to epoch. Many dominant lifeforms had ended up extinct in the previous epochs.","It could be said that even the Freedom Federation and Azure Federation were depressed by this news, especially the Mirror God and God of Fools.","Both of them had worked with Tower Canon many times. It turned out that they had unknowingly aided in such a treacherous and amoral scheme!","The Mirror God and God of Fools looked at the Moon Empress, as well as the other members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty by her side.","Could it be that she had the means to take on such a disaster?","Both of them had already become loyal to her. Although they had not made their stances clear, they and the other members of the Freedom Federation’s royalty were all under the Moon Empress’ control.","The Radiance Federation could control the marsh world and make all the Samsara Realm Dictators submit to them. This was enough to prove the Radiance Federation’s formidable power.","However, the Samsara Realm Dictators would not be enough to fend off this disaster. The Samsara Realm Dictators could protect themselves, but not the regular people living in the federations. There was no way that the Moon Empress was unaware of that!","Nonetheless, the Moon Empress still held the Major Federation Union meeting. This meant that she already had a way to solve the issue.","The Mirror God and God of Fools were in disbelief. They had no idea what the Moon Empress could be planning.","The Moon Empress’ words caused the atmosphere to plunge into one of despair, and all the federation representatives lost hope.","If the Moon Empress wanted to establish the Radiance Federation’s position as the leader, she would have to give the other federations hope.","Thus, the Moon Empress’ next move would definitely be to reveal the Radiance Federation’s secret weapon.","The Mirror God and God of Fools were interested to see what the Moon Empress had up her sleeve!","They could use this opportunity to learn just how much power the Radiance Federation had accumulated all this time and how large the gap between their federations was.","Many federation representatives were shocked that the Spirit Mother had personally led the envoy team to the Radiance Federation.","The Spirit Mother Federation was the most closed-off of all the Class 5 Creation Master federations and rarely interacted with the outside world. They were often absent at Major Federation Meetings as well!","There was not much honor attached to the Spirit Mother Federation itself. Anything that could be considered a sense of honor had been used to safeguard the Spirit Mother’s position.","Yet, the Spirit Mother, who did not even attend the Major Federation Meetings, had chosen to participate in the Major Federation Union meeting headed by the Radiance Federation.","This seemed bizarre to the majority of federations.","The Spirit Mother was currently observing the Moon Empress. He felt her strength yet recognized her as a birth horoscope expert. She remained less powerful than the secret faction’s assigned expert, who was accompanying and protecting Bu Po.","The Moon Empress was one of the Radiance Federation’s most famous experts and had achieved impressive results during a Major Federation Meeting many years ago. It was also then that the Radiance Federation became the champion of the Major Federation Meeting for the first time.","An expert who had grown to power in such an exposed manner would not be able to hide her power to a significant extent.","Thus, the Spirit Mother could immediately be certain that the faction behind Bu Po was linked to the Moon Empress, but the link was not strong!","This made the Spirit Mother rather doubtful.","Given the Spirit Mother’s understanding of the Radiance Federation, there was no way that a secret faction was controlling the Radiance Federation.","The Radiance Federation’s members of royalty were strong-headed, and the federation’s development in recent years had been eye-catchingly obvious.","If a faction was controlling the Radiance Federation and trying to bleed them out, there was no way the faction would have invested so many resources to develop and strengthen the federation in the first place!","But the Spirit Mother would find it strange if the faction had been borne out of the Radiance Federation.","At that moment, the Spirit Mother had the exact same thinking as the Mirror God and God of Fools. He was also waiting to hear what the Moon Empress said next.","Luo Lan, Jin Qianxun, and Yi Huailong were the rulers of the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations, and they had been assigned seats that were next to each other.","The three of them were well-acquainted with each other and had been communicating often through the Thoughts Letter Paper during the past year.","Since Yi Huailong and Jin Qianxun knew that Luo Lan was on slightly closer terms with Lin Yuan, they sought her opinion in numerous matters despite the three of them technically being rivals.","The trio knew that the Moon Empress was Lin Yuan’s master—his status became clear once they arrived in the Radiance Federation. Thus, they were filled with curiosity toward the Moon Empress. Just what kind of person had managed to teach and produce such an outstanding disciple?","Due to being the ruler of both the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent, Su Yiren had a higher status than the Spirit Mother.","Lin Yuan had sent Di Wanmi, a Class 5 Creation Master, as well as many Samsara and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators, to Su Yiren.","Su Yiren possessed enough strength and resources to befit her status and handle her responsibilities.","When she saw that the representatives from the Azure Federation had yet to recover from their shock and that the Freedom Federation seemed to have no intention of asking questions,","Su Yiren pressed on her microphone and waited for three seconds before she asked, “I’m sure the first Major Federation Union meeting is not only meant to be a question-answering session. It is more important that we use this time to solve problems.","“So, Lordess Moon Empress, if you have any ideas, please guide us in the right direction that will give our millions of citizens the best chance of surviving the disaster of dead spirits!”","Su Yiren had intentionally addressed the Moon Empress as ‘Lordess’.","As the ruler of a federation, Su Yiren held equal standing with the Moon Empress at this meeting. As such, she did not need to address the Moon Empress that way!","Su Yiren had done so because the Moon Empress was Lin Yuan’s master. Out of respect for Lin Yuan, Su Yiren had to give the Moon Empress the proper respect as well.","From their previous interactions, Su Yiren sensed Lin Yuan’s respect for the Moon Empress.","By addressing the Moon Empress in such a way, she was also setting an example for the other federation rulers. Now, they would also know how to address the Moon Empress when they spoke.","When Su Yiren spoke, the Moon Empress smiled at her. She had heard Lin Yuan mention Su Yiren more than once.","Su Yiren was very important in Lin Yuan’s plans for Sky City. Although she was not as important as Wen Yu, she was still considered part of Sky City’s backbone, second only to Wen Yu and Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan mainly appreciated Su Yiren’s abilities.","Lin Yuan’s sights had always been set beyond the main world. Given Su Yiren’s impressive capabilities, he would likely take her to the new world.","While Su Yiren was observing the Moon Empress, the latter was doing the same to Su Yiren.","The Moon Empress had never spoken to Su Yiren in the past. But from what Su Yiren said, it meant that she understood the Moon Empress’ intentions.","The Moon Empress’ words were like an opening line, while Su Yiren’s question had captured the attention of the other federation representatives.","Many federation representatives echoed Su Yiren and hoped the Moon Empress could provide a way to overcome this crisis.","These federation representatives cursed Tower Canon more than once.","Just how much did this organization hate the world? Why did they have to bring forth such a disaster all of a sudden?","Furthermore, the Freedom Federation had worked with Tower Canon numerous times in the past. Could they be linked to Tower Canon’s schemes as well?","At that moment, the federation representatives could not be bothered to fear the Mirror God and God of Fools and began glaring at them.","If anyone looked at them in this way in the past, the Mirror God and God of Fools would have already lost their tempers. But they knew they did not have the right to fly into a rage before the Moon Empress.","Tower Canon had given the Freedom Federation two special precious instruments during a previous trade. They had said the precious instrument could gather death aura and asked them to collect all the death aura from the Freedom Federation.","The Mirror God and God of Fools had agreed without thinking too much about it.","It would benefit a federation greatly to have all of its death aura sucked out from it, as it would only help the federation to thrive. The growth of plants would be significantly improved!","At that time, neither the Mirror God nor God of Fools had asked why Tower Canon wanted to collect such a large amount of death aura.","The death aura the Freedom Federation had absorbed using the precious instrument had to have been an important step in the process of the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","Although the Mirror God and God of Fools always prioritized their own profits, they would not have traded with Tower Canon and would have even tried to put a stop to their plan if they had been aware of it in advance!","The Moon Empress waited for around a minute until she had the full attention of every federation representative present before she took out a sample of the metal-type stone board that Lin Yuan had given her. She placed the 50-centimeter-thick stone boards on the table in front of her and formed a small, sharp tower.","“This is a 50-centimeter-thick sample. There are more than 30 rocks within this stone board. Some of these rocks are intentionally meant to keep out dark souls like dead spirits. They are also very durable. Only dead spirits with Eternal power will be able to break through the metal-type stone boards. All dead spirits weaker than that will be kept below these boards!","“Aside from these rocks, the metal-type stone boards also contain more than 40 types of mesh metals. The mesh metals were packed tightly together. They cannot only keep death aura out but also have spatial-stabilizing properties!” the Moon Empress declared.","The Moon Empress said nothing else after describing the metal-type stone boards. She waited for the federation representatives to ask her questions about them.","A person’s will to fight could fade quickly, but confidence took a long time to build up.","Due to Tower Canon’s plan, the federation representatives had already lost all their confidence.","The Moon Empress wanted to help these people to build their confidence back up. As such, she could not be overly anxious.","The federation representatives stared at the sharp tower made of the metal-type stone boards. They found it hard to believe that this was being used as a building material.","One could only imagine the implications for a board like this that could block out dead spirits!","Creating the ingredients needed for this board was one matter, while putting it all together was another matter altogether. There was resource cost and time to consider.","Furthermore, there was no way to lay down all of them. Before the disaster of dead spirits began, there might not even be time to lay down all the boards to cover a small town!","What was the Moon Empress doing? How could she only begin thinking of building a dam now when the flood was almost upon them?","The Cleaning Burning Federation’s Duke Sparrow had been acquainted with the Moon Empress for a long time. There was no way she would scramble in the face of a crisis!","The other members of royalty would never agree if she was making the decision in such a condition.","However, Duke Sparrow still voiced his doubts. “Moon Empress, I don’t think boards like this are a practical solution. But if you need similar minerals and metal resources, the Cleaning Burning Federation is willing to supply them to the Radiance Federation for free!”","Duke Sparrow had not forgotten to extend an arm of friendship to the Radiance Federation while voicing his doubts.","After the first voice of doubt was raised, others quickly joined in. After all, they all believed there was no point in the Moon Empress bringing up this board now!","Even if 100,000 Spirit Craftsmen were given a month, they would not even be able to cover 2,000 square feet of space!","Regular Spirit Craftsmen would not be able to cut such materials that could block out feys that were Eternal and below, much less use them to form mesh structures!","The Moon Empress did not look displeased by the doubts. She had also brought up the same doubts when she first saw the stone boards. However, Lin Yuan had given her a shocking explanation that completely opened up her mind.","After all the federation representatives were done voicing their doubts, the Moon Empress raised her hand and stored the samples away before she said, “It’s very difficult to build these stone boards, and it takes a lot of finesse. However, the Radiance Federation is already fully covered by these boards. As long as no dead spirits above Eternal power appear, the Radiance Federation’s citizens will be safe!”","The Moon Empress’ words were like a tsunami sweeping everyone present.","Everyone, including the Mirror God and God of Fools, looked astonished. Even Su Yiren had not expected things to have progressed so swiftly!","Su Yiren suddenly felt a strange sensation, as if she were suspended in an unfamiliar emotion.","In the past, she always stayed updated about everything by Lin Yuan’s side.","Lately, her focus had been entirely on managing the Dark Continent. Her dream was to restore the Dark Continent’s glory and bring it back to the Seven States of Darkness.","However, the Dark Continent wasn’t part of Lin Yuan’s goals or plans. Lin Yuan respected her aspirations and determination, generously providing her with ample resources.","Yet, if she continued confining her ambitions to the Dark Continent, she would eventually find herself excluded from Sky City’s inner circle, no matter how much Lin Yuan acknowledged her skills.","In an instant, Su Yiren felt like she had emerged from being submerged underwater, breaking through to the surface."]},{"number":2633,"title":"Chapter 2633 Beginning of All the Federations’ Migration!","paragraphs":["2633 Beginning of All the Federations’ Migration!","She had no reason to insist on only remaining as the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent’s ruler.","There might be a deeper meaning to Lin Yuan placing Di Wanmi by her side!","At that moment, Su Yiren suddenly pivoted her ambition to only hoping that the Dark Continent could prosper and thrive while she remained by Lin Yuan’s side.","This was firstly because Su Yiren looked forward to seeing the beautiful world beyond the main world.","But it was also because the rewards and protection she could obtain by remaining by Lin Yuan’s side would be the best way to bring prosperity to the Sand Island Continent and Dark Continent!","There was no one who was without selfish desires.","Su Yiren had contracted the Absolute Love Poppy, and it allowed her to have a deeper-than-normal understanding of human nature.","Su Yiren never suppressed or went against the expression of human nature.","This was why she knew that she needed to be more grateful for her current position.","She had been going in the wrong direction all this time. She intended to get in contact with Lin Yuan once the Major Federation Union meeting was over.","From now on, Su Yiren intended to pivot away from trying to develop the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent to only try to nurture them properly.","The crisis of dead spirits would cause the entire main world to change, and all the major factions would be reshuffled.","Given that the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent were directly under Lin Yuan’s control, they would definitely be able to develop better than the other continents. The development of the Startling Lines Continent had proved that.","While Su Yiren was deep in thought, the other heads of federations were still all shocked by what the Moon Empress said.","But they knew there was no way the Moon Empress was lying. She would never lie at such a moment just to appease the crowd because such a lie could be exposed extremely easily!","The federation representatives all held their breaths as they waited for the Moon Empress to continue speaking.","“I don’t know when Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan will exactly begin, but according to the information we’ve obtained, it should be within the next month! The situation is of the highest urgency, and I took out the metal-type stone board to show that the Radiance Federation is prepared and to give you confidence.”","Before the Moon Empress could finish speaking, the atmosphere of the meeting became chaotic.","Everyone was fixated on the first part of what the Moon Empress said.","The Sleeper’s Revival would begin in the next month or two. This did not give them enough time to prepare at all!","Everyone present could tell that the Moon Empress wanted the major federations to relocate nearer to the Radiance Federation.","Ignoring the fact that they would forsake their historical roots, the key issue was that they couldn’t finish the migration within just a month or two, even if they wished to.","A sense of hopelessness descended on the federation representatives.","The Moon Empress had expected such a reaction from her words. She coughed and knocked on the table. This attracted the attention of all the federation representatives, and the Moon Empress said solemnly, “I wanted to establish the Major Federation Union because of my goal to safeguard the authority of every human federation. The creed of the Major Federation Union is to not bow or give up in the face of a crisis.","“After the meeting, every federation will receive a marked-out position. All you need to do is move your citizens to that position, and Island Whales will appear to take you to the vicinity of the Radiance Federation!","“This is an early gesture of sincerity of the Radiance Federation to show our thanks for your hard work and tenacity during the process of this crisis!”","The Moon Empress’ words altered the atmosphere of hopelessness.","If the Moon Empress’ words were true, the migration would be possible.","But just how many Island Whales were necessary to achieve this? Did the Radiance Federation have so many Island Whales at their disposal?","As one of the three major federations, the Radiance Federation was extremely powerful. This was unquestionable.","Nonetheless, dispatching 10,000 Island Whales at once was unbelievable!","But any less and there would not be enough to handle the migration.","The federation representatives had their suspicions, but none of them dared to doubt the Moon Empress’ words now.","The Radiance Federation’s formidability had been cemented. There was no need for them to cooperate with the Freedom Federation and Azure Federation. It was already the core of the Major Federation Union!","The Moon Empress also noticed this. She knew she did not need to continue bolstering support for the Radiance Federation.","Thus, she decided to give these federation representatives some confidence. “I want to ask all of you a question. Do you know of the faction that controls the sea clans?”","The Moon Empress’ question caused the federation representatives to begin pondering.","The powerful federations had the right to interact and trade with sea clans, but the federations without Class 5 Creation Masters dared not approach the sea.","Many federations had Class 4 Creation Masters who did their best to build up their fleets and nurture Island Whales in the hopes of trading with other federations, only to fail.","The humans in the sea had to encounter much more danger than the humans on land.","The Eight Clans of Sea Emperors sent expert after expert to take control of different parts of the sea.","But since the Moon Empress asked this question, it meant that the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors were not the true rulers of the sea.","The Moon Empress’ question blindsided many federation representatives. There were still many federation representatives who used the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors as their answer.","Those who did know who the true ruler of the sea was instinctively looked at the Mirror God and God of Fools, as well as the two leaders of aristocratic families from the Azure Federation. These four were the only ones present who could answer the Moon Empress’ question best.","The Mirror God and God of Fools represented the Freedom Federation and had succumbed to the Radiance Federation, putting them under the Moon Empress’ control. But this did not mean they had lost all of their previous scheming intentions.","When the Mirror God and God of Fools addressed the Azure Federation, they continued acting as arrogant as they always did.","After meeting eyes with the Mirror God and God of Fools, the two heads of families from the Azure Federation looked away.","It was then that the Mirror God said, “The true ruler of the seas is the Vast Sea Labyrinth.”","At first, the Mirror God also wanted to mention that the Moon Empress could only allocate so many of the Island Whales because of the Vast Sea Labyrinth. But he eventually decided to keep his mouth shut and supplied no more information besides the answer to the Moon Empress’ question.","Now that their positions had changed, the Mirror God knew to stay meek. This applied to the God of Fools as well. The two of them could not afford to go against the oath they had sworn to the Moon Empress. Moreover, after they swore their oath, the Moon Empress now controlled their souls. The two of them were completely helpless against her.","Although the two of them were members of royalty in name, they were actually no different from the Moon Empress’ servants.","But luckily, they still had their power. There was a lot that they would be able to do during the impending disaster on the main world. During the long war against the dead spirits, the two of them would have the chance to change the way that the Moon Empress saw them.","After hearing the Mirror God’s response, the federation representatives who had never heard of the Vast Sea Labyrinth before made a note of that name. They were all wondering why the Moon Empress had asked such a question!","The Moon Empress took over the conversation and said, “That’s right. The Vast Sea Labyrinth is the ruler of the seas! The Vast Sea Labyrinth will gather all the Island Whales in the sea and use them to migrate the federations’ citizens. Other oceanic feys can also be used as transport tools.","“No one will be left behind if you can arrive at the marked-out position. This is a strategy that the Radiance Federation has already discussed with the Vast Sea Labyrinth. They have given us their assurance!”","The Moon Empress’ words gave all the factions renewed confidence.","They all felt indebted to the Radiance Federation now as well.","The Freedom Federation had previously worked with Tower Canon to try to eliminate the human race. On the other hand, the Radiance Federation and Vast Sea Labyrinth were working together for the sake of the entire human race. What a difference this was!","Many federation representatives began expressing their gratitude to the Moon Empress.","The Moon Empress did not give them much time to express their thanks. She slammed her hand down on the table and said sternly, “Usually, we would be distributing the responsibilities of the Major Federation Union now. But it’s clear that no one will be able to focus on this now. Why don’t we do a cursory delegation of responsibilities for now? Go back and send out the news so you can make the preparations for the migration.”","Once the Moon Empress was done speaking, she instructed the two servants at the door to open it as a sign the federation experts could leave now.","The Moon Empress’ action once again won over the respect of the federation experts. Many matters should be discussed during the first Major Federation Union meeting, but it would take at least three days and nights to finish discussing all of them.","But given the emergency at hand, none of the federation experts wanted to waste this time.","If the disaster of dead spirits began earlier than expected, the three days would cost the lives of millions of citizens.","The Radiance Federation’s defenses had been fully set up, making them the human federation with the least worries.","Yet, they were still willing to think of the other federations.","Initially, the Moon Empress planned to mention the Heavenly Family Cottage. However, she reconsidered after witnessing the confusion among the federation representatives as the Mirror God referred to the Vast Sea Labyrinth. She realized that federations with only Class 4 Creation Masters, unfamiliar with the Vast Sea Labyrinth, likely wouldn’t know about the Heavenly Family Cottage either. So, bringing it up seemed pointless.","Revealing too much to the federations could diminish their caution and lead to unjustified optimism, which wouldn’t be favorable.","With a soft sigh, the Moon Empress acknowledged she had already done her best to address this crisis. The outcome now rested on these federations’ own abilities.","The two heads of aristocratic families from the Azure Federation present at the Radiance Federation were deliberating on a decision. The question arose: Should they elevate the Radiance Federation’s status?","Notably, the Moon Empress hadn’t proposed ranking the federations, hinting at her reluctance to establish a hierarchy within the Major Federation Union.","Concluding the meeting swiftly after outlining the impending disaster, the Moon Empress left the heads of aristocratic families feeling ashamed. They realized the Azure Federation wouldn’t have made such a choice in the Radiance Federation’s position.","Interestingly, these two leaders were the most opposed to placing the Azure Federation under the Radiance Federation.","At this moment, both of their opinions had changed.","The Azure Federation was aware of Vast Sea Labyrinth but had never been able to collaborate with them.","If the situation was as critical as the Moon Empress had described, it would be impossible for the Azure Federation to fend off the disaster by remaining where they currently were. Their only option would be to migrate!","The Azure Federation would also need help from the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s Island Whales in order to complete the migration.","These two heads of aristocratic families intended to tell the others about this when they returned so they could make a collective decision.","...","The Moon Empress immediately felt her tightly wound nerves relax once the Major Federation Union meeting was over.","However, the tasks related to the migration of the federations would be extremely laborious and problematic.","Firstly, the Radiance Federation did not have enough space to house so many citizens from other factions.","Even if they did, the Moon Empress could not allow them to settle down permanently in the Radiance Federation as this would encroach into the rights and resources of the Radiance citizens!","The closest continent to the Radiance Federation was the Startling Lines Continent.","The Startling Lines Continent was under Lin Yuan’s control. Given the Moon Empress’ understanding of Lin Yuan, she believed he would not be willing to ruin the environment of a continent he had taken over.","The Moon Empress intended to discuss with Lin Yuan where they could settle down these citizens from other federations.","Others saw her as the Radiance Federation’s decision-maker, but she needed to consult Lin Yuan when it came to making pivotal decisions.","This was because 90% of the Radiance Federation’s strength now came from Lin Yuan.","...","After the Major Federation Union meeting ended, Su Yiren did not stay in the Radiance Federation.","She was now the ruler of the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent. She had her own responsibilities to see through and arrange the migration of the Dark and Sand Island citizens.","While other federations might view the migration negatively, for the Sand Island citizens, it meant moving to a better environment. This would be great news for them!","The sea next to the Dark Continent had numerous harbors, so the migration process would be very simple.","But the Sand Island Continent was not bordered by the sea. The Sand Island citizens would have to move to the neighboring Spirit Mother Federation first before leaving via the Spirit Mother Federation’s harbor!","Su Yiren decided to use her relationship with Bu Po to strike up a conversation with the Spirit Mother.","She could meet the Spirit Mother’s requests. The Spirit Mother citizens would leave first before the Sand Island citizens.","However, she was worried that the Spirit Mother would try to pull some tricks.","But using her link to Bu Po, her communication with the Spirit Mother would go much more smoothly than if she did not have this connection.","Su Yiren called Lin Yuan before leaving the Radiance Federation.","She was used to communicating with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper. But this time, she felt that calling would be more formal.","At that moment, Su Yiren felt both clear-headed and nervous. She only hoped that her previous ambitions would not affect the way that Lin Yuan saw her!"]},{"number":2634,"title":"Chapter 2634 The Lifespan Mouse’s Development!","paragraphs":["2634 The Lifespan Mouse’s Development!","It did not take long for the call to connect.","Green Vine had already successfully set its spirit fire alight. Its spirit fire was a dark green one that brimmed with natural exuberance.","When one looked at it, one would get the same feeling as when looking at the Lifeform Sacrificial Fire. However, this spirit fire was actually a lethal killing machine.","Begin Lady used to remain by Lin Yuan and act as his bodyguard. But now, Green Vine was even stronger than Begin Lady!","Green Vine had reached the peak of the spirit-fire level and was only one step away from World Emperor and the divine kingdom.","Frankly, Green Vine had already absorbed sufficient spirit qi to attempt to evolve to World Emperor and the divine kingdom.","However, its level was still not very stable, and it needed some time to stabilize itself. If it forcefully tried to evolve now, it would be very difficult for it to take control of that power.","Once Green Vine had accumulated more strength and its level was stabilized, it could immediately attempt to reach the World Emperor and divine-kingdom level.","Eternal Source, who had been watching from the sideline, was struck by this sight.","His power had come from his slow accumulation, and every step had required an immense amount of effort.","In the beginning, there were even many times he had been in danger of losing his life. If he let his guard down even once or made the wrong call, he might even have ended up decomposed into fertilizer by the marsh world’s bacteria.","Meanwhile, Green Vine did not have to experience any risks as Lin Yuan had fully nurtured it from the beginning. Its power had also increased at an exponentially unimaginable rate.","Although there was only a small gap between his and Green Vine’s power, Eternal Source was not amazed by its power at all. Rather, he was amazed by Lin Yuan’s capabilities.","Lin Yuan was very pleased with Green Vine’s evolution.","Based on his communication with Green Vine, it would not need long before it could reach the World Emperor and the divine-kingdom level. Three months would be enough!","Green Vine’s power would be very useful against the dead spirits during the war.","Lin Yuan was in a great mood. His tone was also cheerful when he picked up Su Yiren’s call.","“Young Master, all of my thoughts recently have surrounded the Dark Continent, and I have completely neglected tasks related to you. I hope to guide Lin Hope and help him grow quickly before I assign a few dependable subordinates to support him!","“Liu Xi of the 14 Poppy Fruits is showing promise in internal governance. All she needs is some time to train, and she’ll be able to handle the affairs of both the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent on her own!”","Su Yiren had not overstated her appraisal of Liu Xi just because she was one of the 14 Poppy Fruits.","Liu Xi was the poppy fruit for whom Su Yiren had the highest hopes. Otherwise, she would never keep Liu Xi by her side.","This surprised and slightly frustrated him.","Su Yiren felt she had not been interacting with him often enough recently. She also had not contributed to setting up the Radiance Federation’s defenses. As such, she was worried his impression of her had soured.","This Major Federation Union meeting would definitely mention the defenses against the dead spirits. It was likely that this had fuelled Su Yiren’s concerns.","In fact, the only members of Sky City who had participated in setting up the defenses were Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and Bai Qinghuan, whom Lin Yuan was starting to rely more on. The three of them had been enough to manage the millions of Land Imps and perfectly completed the job. Not even Wen Yu had participated.","As for Lin Hope, whom Su Yiren mentioned, it was true that Lin Yuan had asked Su Yiren to help guide and teach him. However, he did not have any specific standards that he wanted her to meet.","At that time, Lin Yuan had just wanted to promise Lin Hope a better future.","He had saved him because he did not want to see a kind and innocent soul decayed by an environment filled with evil.","If Lin Hope was capable, Lin Yuan did not mind if Su Yiren handed him the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent to manage.","But if Lin Hope did not have such capabilities, he could be supported by capable aides. He did not need to be the sole ruler of the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent.","Su Yiren was very skilled at governance and the second-most capable at it amongst Lin Yuan’s subordinates. She was more useful to Sky City than Listen, who excelled more at business.","Lin Yuan would definitely take Su Yiren with him when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan would have asked her to do this even if she had not decided to shift her focus away from developing the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent.","He felt that he needed to give Su Yiren something to assure her. She was very quick at picking things up. She would tie herself up into knots over this matter if she was not assured.","“Yiren, the promise I gave you was genuine. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have given you so many resources or sent Di Wanmi to you. You have invested effort into both the Dark Continent and Sand Island Continent. At the very least, you have decreased the mortality rate in the Sand Island Continent.","“Now, make the preparations for the migration. We will have more than enough time to discuss other problems once the disaster of dead spirits breaks out. If my guess is right, this crisis will last centuries! It will be a brilliant victory if we manage to bring an end to this crisis within a millennium!”","Su Yiren pursed her lips when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","She was only finding out Lin Yuan’s expectations for the crisis of dead spirits now!","It turned out that he was estimating the war against the dead spirits to last centuries.","To special feys, a millennium was not a very long time. But to humans, ten generations could be born in a millennium.","When Su Yiren found out that Lin Yuan appreciated her talent for governance, she spent most of her time on management and no longer focused on increasing her power.","Su Yiren was not confident she would be able to live to see the war end.","Lin Yuan did not know that Su Yiren had such concerns. The lifespan of a human or all lifeforms was akin to a straight line that started from their birth and ended with their death. This was the cycle of life, and it also applied to Lin Yuan’s previous life.","But in this world, besides using the method of increasing one’s power to an extremely high level, Lin Yuan could also use the Lifespan Mouse to increase the lifespan of a lifeform.","The second time that Lin Yuan produced the Lifespan Mouse, he discovered that the Flower Branch Mouse with red tails could be bred. However, they would only reproduce after absorbing sufficient spirit qi.","Eventually, it would give birth to Lifespan Mice with orangey-red fur.","Although he did not know how the Flower Branch Mouse with red tails came about, he had proven that their genes did not result from a sudden mutation.","After the past six months, Genius’ studies were beginning to show some promise.","Genius noticed that when pure vitality was used to nurture a million Flower Branch Mice, only three to five of them would grow red tails.","It had been a very difficult selection process for Genius, but the number of Lifespan Mice in Lin Yuan’s possession had increased nonetheless.","Due to the difficulty of selection and the high standard of vitality required to nurture the young Flower Branch Mice, it was difficult to breed them in bulk. Thus, Lin Yuan’s supply was not endless. Still, he could give every white-clothed follower of Sky City a Lifespan Mouse so that they could attain a seemingly endless lifespan!","Besides Sky City’s members, Lin Yuan also left some behind that he meant to give to those who were close to him.","Nothing had brought Lin Yuan more joy in the last six months than the gains from studying the Lifespan Mouse.","All the pressure lifted off Su Yiren after her call with Lin Yuan.","“Don’t worry, Young Master. I will make sure to do a good job! I will also communicate with the Spirit Mother. I will report to you if something goes wrong during my communication with him! Given my understanding, he is not the easiest to talk to.”","Su Yiren had not said this to disparage the Spirit Mother. The Spirit Mother did not mean anything to Lin Yuan.","Su Yiren had said this to Lin Yuan because she was giving him advance notice. This would prevent any issues that possibly cropped up during her communication with the Spirit Mother from affecting the migration. She did not want Lin Yuan to think she only cared about the Dark Continent and was neglecting the Sand Island Continent.","A glint appeared in Lin Yuan’s eye.","“You can contact Bu Po about this and communicate with the Spirit Mother through him. If the Spirit Mother can’t see sense when it comes to this matter and tries to pull tricks, I will instruct the Samsara Realm Dictator protecting Bu Po to deal with the Spirit Mother. You don’t have to worry. Just focus on the migration!”","After speaking to Su Yiren for a while, Lin Yuan hung up and brought Green Vine back to the Return from Faraway Mansion while he returned to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Genius had already informed Hu Quan of all the functions and properties of the spiritual ingredients.","It was easier to come up with the design for a large base than a smaller one. The crux of a large base was its frame, while the key of a small base was the details and beauty.","Once Hu Quan was done drawing the design, he made a comprehensive list of all the materials he would need.","Lin Yuan received the list from Hu Quan and looked it over before he said, “You don’t have to trouble Listen to gather these materials. I will give them to you in Diamond fey storage boxes if I have them on hand. All you need to do is use whatever spiritual ingredients you require!","“There are some High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients in there as well. You can ask Genius about their functions. You can also use them in the construction of the base.”","Lin Yuan would not dare to say such a thing in the past.","Previously, Lin Yuan needed to use True Data to analyze the High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients before asking Genius to take notes on them.","But now that Genius had the ability True Knowledge Analysis, it could study and learn the spiritual ingredients’ properties on its own!","Otherwise, Lin Yuan really would not have the time to tell Hu Quan about all of the spiritual ingredients’ functions.","Hu Quan was floored by what Lin Yuan said.","He could use High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients, too?","In Hu Quan’s opinion, Suzerain metal-type spiritual ingredients were already considered very precious resources. They could be stocked up as strategic resources in the Radiance Federation.","Hu Quan had not even touched Suzerain metal-type spiritual ingredients many times in his life.","But now, Lin Yuan was allowing him free use of High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients. This was a little too far out of Hu Quan’s comfort zone.","But since Lin Yuan had said it, it meant that he had no lack of High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients. Since Lin Yuan had allowed him to use it, he had no reason to say no.","If High Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients could be added to the design for the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s base, Hu Quan would have to alter his current designs!","Although this would delay the construction, it would improve the result.","Hu Quan was also aware of the imminent crisis.","This disaster would last for an extremely long time. He had plenty of time to slowly carve out the ideal base for the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","If he had a few centuries, he would definitely be able to turn this space that was as large as a small region into an irreplicable divine haven!","Lin Yuan was about to continue discussing the construction of the Spirit Lock spatial zone with Hu Quan when his phone rang.","When he saw the call coming from the Moon Empress, he knew she was done with all that she needed to do.","Hence, he used Node Transportation to travel to the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace.","Lin Yuan had been bothered by something recently, which was whether to combine the five dimensional worlds with the main world to deal with the disaster of dead spirits.","Lin Yuan was struggling to make a decision for now. He knew that his decision would determine the safety of the main world.","What if, after the main world was promoted from a Class 1 world to Class 2, it would have to undergo a perilous trial just like during fey evolutions?","Since he could not make a decision himself, he decided to ask the Moon Empress for her opinion.","But before he could ask her, the Moon Empress presented him with a difficult problem that had yet to be solved but needed to be!","“Little Yuan, moving so many federations to the Radiance Federation will greatly strain the Radiance Federation. We don’t have the space for so many citizens. We are trying to save the whole world, but it shouldn’t come at the cost of the Radiance Federation’s basic rights!","“If we casually allow citizens of other federations to enter the Radiance Federation, it could lead to some risks, and there will definitely be conflict amongst the factions! But if we don’t take them into the Radiance Federation, there isn’t anywhere near the Radiance Federation that will be suitable to place them.","“Moreover, all the federations are separated by seas. There will also be countless dead spirits rising from the seas and making their way to the land!”"]},{"number":2635,"title":"Chapter 2635 The Imposing Moon Empress!","paragraphs":["2635 The Imposing Moon Empress!","Lin Yuan nodded at what the Moon Empress said.","Lin Yuan had already considered the possibility the Moon Empress would be unwilling to allow the citizens of other federations to migrate to the Radiance Federation’s territory.","If she allowed the citizens of other federations to move to the Radiance Federation’s territory, it would decrease the resources the Radiance Federation’s own factions could access.","Given that this was an issue of safety, the Radiance Federation’s royalty would eventually decide to drive these people out.","Lin Yuan had realized this long ago. This was why he was hesitating on his decision to combine the main world with the five dimensional worlds.","If there was enough space to settle down the citizens of other federations, there would be nothing for Lin Yuan to worry about!","Lin Yuan’s willingness to allow them to settle down in the Startling Lines Continent was not a factor, as the migration would also threaten the continent’s safety and affect the way of life there. Additionally, the Startling Lines Continent did not have enough space to house all of the citizens from the other federations.","Lastly, the area of sea between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent was not large, but there would still be an almost endless stream of dead spirits rising up from it and invading the Startling Lines Continent.","Thus, to address this issue, the only solution would be to combine the main world with the five dimensional worlds.","When the Moon Empress saw Lin Yuan nod, she fell silent for a moment before suggesting, “Little Yuan, why don’t we get in contact with the Vast Sea Labyrinth and ask them to station people nearby the Radiance Federation?","“We can cover the bottom of the sea with the metal-type stone boards and cover an area as large as five continents around the Radiance Federation. Otherwise, once these federations have relocated only to find there is no suitable place for them to settle, they will definitely argue that it is Radiance Federation’s responsibility to find a solution!”","The Moon Empress had come to this difficult decision because she was not aware of the possibility of combining the main world with the dimensional worlds. She saw no other option.","But Lin Yuan felt that it would be difficult to fulfill the Moon Empress’ suggestion.","Firstly, it would be difficult to organize this with the Vast Sea Labyrinth. It was a gargantuan faction and managed thousands of times the number of sea clans than there were members in human factions.","Every action the Vast Sea Labyrinth took would cause every clog in the system to move. There was no way several segments could be isolated to work with the Moon Empress.","Once the Vast Sea Labyrinth learned about Tower Canon’s plan from the Radiance Federation, they were very willing to work with the Radiance Federation. They did not hesitate before they agreed to help the Radiance Federation with the migration of the other federations’ citizens and had arranged to deploy their entire fleet of Island Whales.","The Heavenly Family Cottage was indeed a positive connection, but a larger reason was the wisdom of the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s decision-makers.","If the Vast Sea Labyrinth agreed to the humans’ request this time, they would be able to ask the humans for a favor in the future.","Lin Yuan intended to be present during future interactions with the Vast Sea Labyrinth so he could make contact with the strongest hidden faction in the sea.","Furthermore, there was no way to lay down the metal-type stone boards in the sea.","However, the Land Imps were all very afraid of water and could not reach the bottom of the sea.","The Radiance Federation could only be covered by metal-type stone boards in a month because millions of Land Imps had worked together to accomplish the task.","Lin Yuan did not intend to leave the Moon Empress hanging. “Master, I need to seek your opinion on something. It could involve unknown dangers that might put the main world at extreme risk. But this would also be able to perfectly solve the problem you just mentioned.”","Lin Yuan was about to explain to the Moon Empress in greater detail when she beat him to the punch and said calmly, “Little Yuan, this crisis of dead spirits is already disastrous for the main world. We don’t even know if the main world will be able to survive!","“It won’t make much of a difference to throw in a few more issues. If the main world ends up encountering other catastrophes, it might affect not just us but the dead spirits as well! Moreover, this might be able to solve our current problem.","“Little Yuan, why are you hesitating?”","Lin Yuan was momentarily stunned by what the Moon Empress said. From this matter, he had gotten a full blast of her imposing side.","The path he had been going down had been too smooth. Thus, Lin Yuan wanted every one of his decisions to only result in the best consequences. He did not want to undertake even a hint of risks.","But the fact was that risks were part of life.","Almost every elder generation of experts had made it this far after overcoming significant risks. They saw it as a tool they could harness.","For example, when they were dealing with carcinoma feys, the Spirit Guards would use carcinoma feys and fight fire with fire.","The Moon Empress’ words dispelled Lin Yuan’s worries.","She was right! Why was he hesitating?","Furthermore, promoting a Class 1 world to Class 2 was a very good thing in itself.","After making this decision, all of Lin Yuan’s anxiousness disappeared.","Although he did not need to come to a decision now, Lin Yuan still explained the situation to her.","“Master, do you know that worlds can be evolved just like feys?”","Lin Yuan’s words immediately caught the Moon Empress’ attention. She had never heard this question before.","If anyone else said this to the Moon Empress, she would think that they were trying to pull her leg. After all, she was already part of the highest echelon that stood on the top of the world. It was unlikely for there to be anything to exist that she had not even heard of!","Yet, since these words had come from Lin Yuan’s mouth, the Moon Empress had no choice but to believe it to be true as he had already grown to an extent that she found hard to fathom.","The Moon Empress shook her head. She felt a sense of familiarity and absurdity at the same time.","Two years ago, when Lin Yuan had just become her disciple, he would ask her questions in the inner palace of the Radiant Moon Palace. She would then answer them.","But now, their roles were reversed. Despite still being his master, she was now the one who needed to be taught by him!","This was enough to prove just how much he had grown in the past two years.","“If the main world is combined with the five known dimensional worlds, we will be able to promote the main world from Class 1 to Class 2!","“I have already taken control of the five dimensional worlds and intend to join them to the main world with the Radiance Federation at the center. Once the joining is complete, the citizens from other federations can settle down anywhere within the dimensional worlds.”","The Moon Empress’ eyes lit up when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","She had never heard of such a thing before, but his explanation allowed her to understand the process.","If what Lin Yuan said was right and the citizens from other federations were settled down in the dimensional worlds that had been combined in the main world, the five dimensional worlds’ ley lines could slow down the invasion of dead spirits. After all, the Sleeper’s Revival had only contaminated the main world’s ley lines and not the ley lines of the dimensional worlds.","As such it was feasible to house the main world’s lifeforms in the dimensional worlds!","The Moon Empress was intelligent, so there was no need for Lin Yuan to go too deep into an explanation or elaboration on the profits.","However, dimensional lifeforms had low intelligence and were very ferocious. The Moon Empress was afraid that these dimensional lifeforms would attack the citizens of other federations who migrated into the dimensional worlds.","There was a difference in power between different federations. Not every federation was as powerful as the Azure, Freedom, and Radiance Federations. The federations without a Class 5 Creation Master were not even as strong as some of the Radiance Federation’s cities.","As such, it would be difficult for these federations to fend off the dimensional lifeforms.","Although dimensional lifeforms were not intelligent, they knew how to gather up and attack when they were presented with delicious morsels!","When he heard the Moon Empress’ concerns, Lin Yuan replied with a smile, “Master, my control of the dimensional worlds does not only extend to the powerful experts but the weak dimensional lifeforms as well!","“I have taken full and systematic control of the dimensional lifeforms. You don’t need to worry that they will attack the humans! Rather, these dimensional lifeforms will even be able to protect them from danger.”","The Moon Empress felt a heavy weight lift off of her. At that moment, just like Lin Yuan, she no longer felt as much stress.","If the humans could set up good defenses, they would only need to endure the disaster and do their best to survive!","There was no need for her to seal herself away in darkness. Anxiousness would only be damaging for a decision-maker.","Suddenly, the Moon Empress remembered that Tower Canon also controlled a dimensional world. It was called the dead world, and Lin Yuan had mentioned it before.","The Moon Empress sensed a strong connection between the dead world and the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","Lin Yuan had overheard the Mirror God and the God of Fools mentioning that Tower Canon had once exchanged death aura with the Freedom Federation.","The Freedom Federation had delivered the death aura to Tower Canon in a special vessel.","Tower Canon had never engaged in such a trade with the Radiance Federation.","Upon learning this, the Moon Empress deliberately probed the death aura within the Radiance Federation. She discovered that Tower Canon hadn’t collected any death aura from the Radiance Federation.","Tower Canon aimed to use death aura to corrupt ley lines and trigger a crisis with dead spirits. However, the main world lacked sufficient death aura for this purpose. Consequently, it was highly likely that Tower Canon obtained their death aura from the dead world!","Lin Yuan had merely mentioned involving the five dimensional worlds in the main world’s advancement. He hadn’t mentioned the dead world at all. This strongly suggested that the dead world wasn’t part of the main world, and Tower Canon likely comprised experts from another world.","Having grasped this, the Moon Empress ceased asking further questions.","If she could deduce this, so could Lin Yuan. As she couldn’t manage this situation, there was no need for her to contribute to his burden!","The Moon Empress personally cooked a meal. After dinner, she asked, “Little Yuan, are you staying in Leaning Moon Mountain tonight?”","Lin Yuan finished his cup of tea before saying with a smile, “Master, I intend to go to the Startling Lines Continent to make some advance preparations. I should be back within a week. I hope you’ll take me to meet with the people from the Vast Sea Labyrinth when I get back. I have some things to discuss with them. This will allow me to decide exactly where to join the five dimensional worlds!”","The Moon Empress did not force Lin Yuan to stay as she knew that he was the busiest of them all. Moreover, no one could help him with what he needed to do!","Once ley lines were contaminated by death aura, there was no way to reverse the process.","Lin Yuan wanted to draw up this map so he could pinpoint a place to designate as a training ground for the troops.","This would allow the humans to gain an understanding of the dead spirits in advance and get a sense of just how many dead spirits would appear. This was the only way to make the best estimate of how long the crisis of dead spirits would last.","They would also be able to predict whether the dead spirits would rise up all at once or in waves.","They would stand a better chance of overcoming this trial only if they gathered as much information as possible.","“Little Yuan, do you intend to join the main world with the five dimensional worlds immediately after making contact with the five dimensional worlds?","“My suggestion is that you wait for the citizens of other federations to arrive in the Radiance Federation first. This will prevent them from interfering when the worlds are being joined.","“Additionally, you mentioned that you are collecting a faith-related power. You will be able to use this opportunity to gather faith from every human in the main world. The best way to gather faith is always to demonstrate unbelievable might and spin a miracle out of a seemingly hopeless situation!”","The Moon Empress paused before adding, “Once all the federations have migrated to the Radiance Federation, it is likely that some secret factions will try to establish communication with us. If any of them seem special, I will let you know.","“Little Yuan, again, I’m just going to remind you not to overwork yourself!”","The Moon Empress raised her hand and helped Lin Yuan to adjust his collar. She did this for him whenever he left for a long trip. But each time she did it, her mindset was completely different!"]},{"number":2636,"title":"Chapter 2636 Rotted Bones into Fireflies!","paragraphs":["2636 Rotted Bones into Fireflies!","Lin Yuan transported himself through the Space Tunnel to the Divine Wood Federation. He arrived in the underground palace that Hu Quan had painstakingly built.","Hu Quan had used a metal-type spiritual ingredient called Gilded Light Silver to surround the underground palace.","Gilded Light Silver had strong damping and fortification effects, and Lin Yuan could move the underground palace into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He also had plans to build a palace in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","This was firstly because the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s size would only increase as it continued to evolve. Moreover, when Morbius evolved into Myth Breed, the Spirit Lock spatial zone grew from a room into a small world. Having a palace there would befit this change in grandeur!","Hu Quan had asked Lin Yuan both about the construction and design of this palace, and Lin Yuan had added his own input.","Lin Yuan’s ideal palace was one that Hu Quan would carve out over a long period.","Silver Corona’s bone lotus flowers outside the underground palace were in prime bloom at the moment. Silver Corona flew over and sat down on Lin Yuan’s shoulder when it saw him.","Silver Corona had not seen Lin Yuan in a very long time.","Although Lin Yuan had used a different method to contract Silver Corona than he did his other feys, this did not change the fact that it was a lifeform he had contracted!","Silver Corona felt rather uneasy after seeing all the other feys being evolved to Suzerain/Myth.","Recently, it had been consuming dimensional lifeforms non-stop and was only a step away from reaching Myth Breed!","Silver Corona never expressed its emotions strongly. But at this moment, it held Lin Yuan’s face and nudged it with its own.","“Yuan, I reached Diamond X three months ago and have successfully evolved to Fantasy Breed! My bloodline is now the top amongst the six-winged fairies! Once I reach Myth Breed, my bloodline will be able to reach pinnacle six wings at the very least, or maybe even eight wings!”","Silver Corona had been very proud of the strength of its bloodline. But when it thought about Red Thorn’s bloodline, all of that pride crumbled away.","Although Silver Corona and Red Thorn were six-winged fairies and could be considered equals, Silver Corona always felt timid before Red Thorn.","It was certain that Red Thorn could become an eight-winged fairy when it evolved to Myth Breed! If it could not take that step when it evolved to Myth Breed, it would never be able to catch up to Red Thorn!","Silver Corona’s words caused Lin Yuan’s eyes to light up.","Silver Corona had finally evolved to Fantasy Breed! Unlike the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee, it had not been stuck at Diamond X/Legend for a long time.","Lin Yuan immediately used True Data to check on Silver Corona.","[Fey Name]: Sea Burial Lotus Flower (Silver Corona)","[Fey Species]: Water Willow/Water Bone Lotus","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Fairy","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy IV","Abilities:","[Spotted Coral]: When trained according to the spots on the coral jade, different effects are generated.","1. Nurture Spot Style: Nurture the spots that were absorbed from the spotted coral jade in the Bone Lotus Flowers. The Bone Lotus Flowers will use a living being’s life and soul to nurture the spots to give them vitality. The spots with vitality can use the living being’s original strength to increase the strength and stamina of the Bone Lotus Flowers.","2. Burial Spot Style: Place the spots in between the Bone Lotus Flowers. The spots will eat the Bone Lotus Flowers and become bone insects. The bone insects will retain the spot’s abilities and can deal with attacks on the Bone Lotus Flowers according to their abilities. The external lifeforce will be absorbed, and their soul can also be absorbed when the external lifeforce is still weak.","[Bone Powder Mist]: The Bone Lotus Flowers will vomit out the living being’s bones that could not be digested. The bone powder will fly up into the sky and stay in the coral spots once it reaches a set thickness of layer.","[Blood Bone Insect Drunk]: While the bone insects eat, they enter a drunken state. When they’re in a drunken state, they will not feel any pain. The circulation of their root power will also slow down.","[Blooming Lotus]: The Bone Lotus Flowers’ structure will change and split into main lotuses and branch lotuses. The branch lotuses will strengthen combat power, while main lotuses will lose all combat power. Every time the main lotuses blooms, the spots will use the vitality they absorbed to produce a skeletal insect. The skeletal insect can consume them to repair the damage done to the body.","[Arrival of Grant of Death]: When the hermit’s dead servants cannot stand up against the enemies, they will change into the grants of death that place death penalties on the targets’ souls.","[Soul Parasite Rebirth]: The soul will be hosted in the main lotus. The main lotus will make a copy of the aura of the lifeform’s soul and vitality. When the target’s body and soul are damaged, the main lotus can be sacrificed while absorbing vitality and soul power to enable the target to be reborn. Once reborn, the target will be in a very weak state, and its soul and roots will also be diminished.","Exclusive Skill:","[Hermit’s Dead Servant]: The Bone Lotus Flower will absorb the target’s body when attacking it. 1% of the target’s power will be injected into the target’s soul to cause the target to be pregnant with its dead soul. The dead soul will consume itself, and when the Bone Lotus Flowers gain 36 hermit dead servants, every hermit dead servant will be able to create a layer of mist over the Bone Lotus Flowers.","[Rotted Bones into Fireflies]: Both vitality and death aura will be absorbed simultaneously. The vitality will turn into fireflies that will mend the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers. The death aura will increase the strength of every Bone Lotus Flower. If there is a pile of rotting bones below the Bone Lotus Flowers to supply nutrients to them, as long as the main lotus is alive, rotting lotuses will be produced from the rotting bones and energy will be saved!","Lin Yuan noticed that Silver Corona had reached Fantasy IV! All it needed to do was absorb sufficient energy, and it might be able to evolve to Fantasy V soon!","But what delighted Lin Yuan the most about Silver Corona’s True Data description was not its grade and quality but the exclusive skill it gained after reaching Fantasy Breed.","For all the lifeforms in the main world, the dead spirits crisis would be a cataclysmic calamity. But for Silver Corona, it would be a delicious feast.","Rotted Bones into Fireflies allowed Silver Corona to absorb death aura, meaning that the dead spirits would become part of its meals.","If he didn’t intervene during the disaster and let all the lifeforms in the area die, there was a high chance that Silver Corona would—after gathering power for centuries—become the savior who ended the dead spirits crisis!","With limited food available and Silver Corona’s ever-growing hunger, its food supply would eventually run out.","When Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he planned to plant Silver Corona by the entrance.","His original idea was to wait until he reached the Sky Beyond the Clouds before continuing to nurture Silver Corona. Once the five dimensional worlds merged with the main world, there wouldn’t be any more dimensional rifts opening up!","But now, Lin Yuan changed his mind. He could use this dead spirits crisis to nurture Silver Corona and help it to grow!","Lin Yuan found himself struggling to imagine the degree to which Silver Corona could grow by the time the dead spirits crisis ended.","Rotted Bones into Fireflies allowed Silver Corona to sustain itself using death aura. The death aura would turn into fireflies that tended to the sea of flowers. It would be able to achieve the greatest dream of plant lifeforms, which was to never wither!","Given the current size of the sea of flowers, it would not fit in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Even if it did fit, Lin Yuan did not want to leave Silver Corona in the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","Spirit qi was no longer of much help to Silver Corona. Regardless of how large the Spirit Lock spatial zone became, Lin Yuan did not want to waste its resources.","The sea of bone lotus flowers could not be moved once they had spread out. Silver Corona could recover a portion of the energy by forcing the flowers to wither, but most of the energy would still be lost!","The only way to move Silver Corona would be to instruct Sweet Vanquish and the other Samsara Realm Land Imps to integrate iron boards into the ground and shift the entire palace with all the bone lotus flowers along with it!","This would be no small undertaking and not even Lin Yuan would come to such a decision easily.","Suddenly, an idea formed in Lin Yuan’s mind. Why not plant Silver Corona in the seabed between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent? The environment at the seabed would be much more comfortable for Silver Corona than on land!","When Lin Yuan first found Silver Corona, it had been a plant-type carcinoma fey growing in the sea.","Lin Yuan’s gift to the Vast Sea Labyrinth would be planting Silver Corona in the sea between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent. It would be a way of thanking them for supplying the Island Whales to help the humans with their crisis.`","If Silver Corona’s main body was separated from the sea of bone lotus flowers, its consumption rate would decline. Thus, Silver Corona did not head to Thick Soil City with Lin Yuan and stayed put to continue increasing its power and to strive to evolve to Myth Breed.","Lin Yuan had made sure to remind Silver Corona not to rush to evolve to Myth Breed but to focus on accumulating its power instead so that it could use the dead spirits to evolve to eight wings before attempting another breakthrough.","Silver Corona nodded obediently when it heard that. It also preferred to grow its fourth pair of wings during its evolution to Myth Breed rather than trying to evolve to Myth Breed as soon as possible!","That way, it would not have to keep its head down around Red Thorn when they were both by Lin Yuan’s side in the future!","...","The first thing that Lin Yuan did after arriving in Thick Soil City was head to the City Lord’s residence. There was one of the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacle nodes there.","He did not need to be inspected before he entered Thick Soil City. Otherwise, given how infrequently he came to Thick Soil City, there was no certainty the guards could recognize him!","Lin Yuan had already informed Ta Lei he would be coming, and the former was waiting for him in the meeting room with Qin Yu.","After a short interlude of faint spatial fluctuations, Lin Yuan’s body appeared in the meeting room.","When Qin Yu first arrived to help Ta Lei, they had been around the same height. But now, Lin Yuan realized Qin Yu was already taller than Ta Lei by almost a head! His originally stick-thin body had also filled out with muscle.","Lin Yuan patted Qin Yu and Ta Lei’s shoulders. It had to be hard on them to manage all the operations of a mega city like Thick Soil City!","Su Yiren had brought up Ta Lei. She determined that he possessed some talent for governance but was only suited to maintaining the status quo. He was not capable of dealing with risky endeavors or breaking new ground.","This might sound like she was undermining him, but she was already being very generous!","There always had to be a member of the Astronomical Parliament in the main world. Ta Lei was very suited to watching over the entire main world from Thick Soil City.","Rather, it was Qin Yu who took Lin Yuan by surprise.","Qin Yu had only spent a few months following Listen around before he came to assist Ta Lei. Previously, he ran a small fey store and had not had any opportunities to train himself at all.","But after going to Ta Lei, Qin Yu had managed to endure the change in environment and had not caused any trouble. A few months later, he was already very adept at his responsibilities!","Even Lin Yuan did not think he could match up to Qin Yu in terms of adaptability and rate of learning.","Someone like Qin Yu only needed someone to nurture him, and he would definitely become capable of big things!","Lin Yuan placed Qin Yu at the highest rank of priority to be nurtured amongst Sky City’s members.","Both Ta Lei and Qin Yu had been saved by Lin Yuan when they were on the brink of death, so they felt immense gratitude and respect towards him.","Lin Yuan had not only saved Qin Lun and Ta Lei but was also nurturing Qin Yu’s younger brother, Qin Lun.","Because of Lin Yuan, Qin Lun did not need to brave the cold selling plum branches in order to earn money to buy medicine.","Before Lin Yuan saved Qin Yu, his biggest dream had been to send Qin Lun to school.","Now, Lin Yuan had fulfilled that dream.","Lin Yuan had saved Ta Lei and changed his entire tribe. Now, they did not have to be bullied by anyone and were seen as the leaders of Thick Soil City!","The help that Lin Yuan had given their families was more impactful than saving their lives.","Lin Yuan’s patting of their shoulders indicated he acknowledged them. This thrilled both Ta Lei and Qin Yu.","Ta Lei knew that Lin Yuan was very busy and immediately began talking about official business.","“Teacher, I have organized everyone in Thick Soil City. When will we, just like the Divine Wood Federation and Iron Hammer Federation, be able to migrate? Sister Luo Lan has arrived at the Great Lush Federation’s harbor, and the Island Whales have begun moving.”","After discussing with the Moon Empress, Lin Yuan decided to combine the main world with the dimensional worlds.","Now, aside from those in Thick Soil City, no humans were found in the Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan was silent momentarily before saying, “You don’t have to move the people out of Thick Soil City. I will turn the entire Startling Lines Continent into an impenetrable fortress within 20 days. Before the crisis of dead spirits begins, I will send at least 10 Samsara Realm Dictators and 100 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators to guard and protect Thick Soil City!”"]},{"number":2637,"title":"Chapter 2637 Chef Supreme’s Limit!","paragraphs":["2637 Chef Supreme’s Limit!","Ta Lei and Qin Yu were all aware of the magnitude of the impending catastrophe. It was beyond anything they could dream up!","But as long as Lin Yuan said that he was confident in keeping Thick Soil City safe, the two of them believed him without hesitation.","Ta Lei and Qin Yu voiced their stances,","“Master, we will stand by Thick Soil City. We are ready for any of your instructions!”","“Young Master, I will do my best to assist Ta Lei and complete Thick Soil City’s organization!”","Ta Lei always addressed Lin Yuan as ‘Master/Teacher’, and Lin Yuan had only corrected him once. Since this was how Ta Lei wanted to address him, there was no need to try and change him. However, there was no actual master-disciple relationship between the two of them.","It was true that Lin Yuan had helped Ta Lei to become a Class 3 Creation Master, but all of the knowledge had come from Genius.","There were numerous others who received the same treatment as Ta Lei. For example, Bei Xu and Bu Po had also been taught and guided by Lin Yuan and Genius. However, the two of them did not see Lin Yuan as their Master like Ta Lei did.","At first, Qin Yu had been very nervous when he found out that Ta Lei addressed Lin Yuan that way. If Ta Lei was truly Lin Yuan’s disciple, it would mean that he was his ‘little master’!","But as time went on, Qin Yu realized that was not actually the case.","Ta Lei saw Lin Yuan as his Master, but Lin Yuan did not see Ta Lei as his disciple.","After realizing this, Qin Yu became much more relaxed in his interactions with Ta Lei. He stopped following Ta Lei’s decisions completely and would give his own opinions to initiate discussions with Ta Lei.","Ta Lei was very conservative, but Qin Yu was more daring. Thus, he could make up for Ta Lei’s flaws.","Despite slowly realizing that he was more capable than Ta Lei, Qin Yu did not feel any derision or arrogance toward Ta Lei. He continued to view them as equals.","Qin Yu knew that Lin Yuan had only placed him there to train him but would not leave him with Ta Lei permanently. He would eventually be assigned somewhere else!","What Lin Yuan said next shocked and excited Qin Yu.","“From now on, Ta Lei will manage Thick Soil City on his own. Qin Yu will be in charge of the Startling Lines Continent’s defensive base that will be built outside of Thick Soil City.","“The Samsara and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators will go with Qin Yu. Ta Lei, if you have any needs, you can contact Qin Yu! The two of you must have become close with each other after working together for such a long time.”","Qin Yu nodded seriously. He knew that his chance was finally there!","When he was by Ta Lei’s side, he could only support Ta Lei but did not hold any decision-making power. Regardless of how well-run Thick Soil City was, it was all due to Ta Lei’s effort and not his own.","But now that Lin Yuan was going to send him to manage the defensive base outside Thick Soil City, he could finally call the shots!","The achievements he made in the future would definitely allow him to shine in Lin Yuan’s eyes.","Lin Yuan assigning the Samsara and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators to him was also a sign that he deemed him to be more capable than Ta Lei.","Ta Lei also understood that. However, he was not the type to be competitive and found happiness in stability.","He was only able to grow to such an extent within such a short time because Su Yiren and Luo Lan had helped him. At the same time, he was determined not to let Lin Yuan down.","Ta Lei was always aware of his capabilities. Just like Bei Xu and Bu Po, he came from nothing. But unlike them, he did not have much tenacity. To put it bluntly, he was just a laid-back character!","Regardless of how hard he worked, the shortcomings of his character limited him to only being capable of properly looking after Thick Soil City!","A while ago, Ta Lei had been extremely troubled by this and complained to Su Yiren and Luo Lan about it.","Both of them had given him the same reply, which was not to overextend himself beyond his limits. Doing things right was more important than doing more things!","After taking their advice, all Ta Lei wanted to do now was to do his best in his role as Thick Soil City’s City Lord.","It could be said that of all the members of the Astronomical Parliament, Ta Lei had the least prospects. His path had essentially ended there.","But Lin Yuan believed that Ta Lei was enough. Otherwise, he would not have allowed him to manage Thick Soil City on his own!","From the way that he was treating Ta Lei, all the members of the Astronomical Parliament knew that Lin Yuan was extremely kind.","“Master, if I need anything, I will let Qin Yu know! If he needs me, I won’t hesitate to help either!”","Lin Yuan handed a copy of Bai Qinghuan’s plan to Qin Yu.","Once Sweet Vanquish and the 15,000,000 Land Imps arrived by Qin Yu’s side, all he needed to do was act according to this plan!","After handing things over to Qin Yu, Lin Yuan started helping the experts to evolve their feys’ grades and qualities.","The Pure Land of Bliss now covered one square kilometer. With this size, Lin Yuan estimated he could help at least 500 feys with their World Cleansings. This would save a lot of time and increase the rate at which he accumulated spirit qi crystals!","Nonetheless, this still occupied Lin Yuan for two days.","Firstly, this was because Lin Yuan had established this system in the Startling Lines Continent much earlier than he had in the Radiance Federation. Additionally, it was much easier to evolve plant-type feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline than regular plant-type feys.","Now that he had amassed another mountain of spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan once again had a wealth of resources at his disposal. His method of using his resources to nurture experts who would then give even more resources back to him was a sustainable one! Through this method, his store of resources would only snowball.","Lin Yuan learned from Keira that pure spirit qi and elemental energy were also considered invaluable resources in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","He wanted to snowball as many resources as he could so they could help him in his endeavors in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The experts gathered in Thick Soil City had come from the Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations. Lin Yuan noticed that they got along well, and there was no friction between them. This pleased him greatly.","By the time Lin Yuan left, Sweet Vanquish had already led the 15,000,000 Land Imps to the Startling Lines Continent and met up with Qin Yu.","Sweet Vanquish dared not show any disrespect toward Qin Yu.","Given that Lin Yuan had assigned the management of such a massive operation to Qin Yu alone, it meant that Lin Yuan had to have great trust and belief in Qin Yu’s abilities. Otherwise, Lin Yuan would never have made such a decision!","With Sweet Vanquish so cooperative toward Qin Yu, it went without saying that the Land Imps under him were even more obedient!","Qin Yu had not contracted a Vitality Sloth because he did not see himself as just being talented at internal governance. With his Polar Night Blue Sky Scorpion beast patterns and the Polar Night Blue Sky Scorpion that Lin Yuan had helped him to contract, Qin Yu felt that only utilizing his talents in internal governance would be a waste of the trust and resources Lin Yuan had invested into him!","Qin Yu knew that Lin Yuan was extremely powerful—more powerful than Qin Yu could ever imagine.","Nonetheless, Qin Yu still placed his hopes on eventually becoming Lin Yuan’s bodyguard.","...","Once Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, he continued gathering the spirit qi crystals before he handed a large batch of resources to the Moon Empress so that she could allocate them as she saw fit.","Lin Yuan had already told the Moon Empress about his goals, so she would definitely know what to do with these resources!","Even if Lin Yuan had the time, he did not want to waste it on networking with the other federations. He preferred to use the time to produce more resources in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","...","With the Land Imps’ help, Hu Quan was basically done building the living area for the Hundred Questions Beasts! The details of the interior and other decorations would only be completed a long time later.","Hu Quan would lead his subordinates in doing up every room later on. But now that the rudimentary version of the base was complete, the Hundred Questions Beasts could begin using it.","Genius and the Hundred Questions Beasts it had selected went to the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce’s breeding base and selected 100,000 young Hundred Questions Beasts. These young Hundred Questions Beasts could not even open their eyes yet and were all newborns.","All of them had unattractive fur colors and could not be considered beauties. If they were sent to the market, it was unlikely they would be picked and bought. After all, one only needed to spend another 200 Federation dollars, and they could buy a much more attractive Hundred Questions Beast! Even the poorest family only had to tighten their belts, and they would be able to scrape 200 Federation dollars together!","Once these Hundred Questions Beasts were moved into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, they would be carefully nurtured by the matured Hundred Questions Beasts.","...","Lin Yuan could not help but think that despite the unfortunate circumstances of their births, these Hundred Questions Beasts ended up being the luckiest of their peers!","Just as Lin Yuan was about to go into the Spirit Lock spatial zone to take a look at the Soldier Ration Radishes that had been moved into the Spirit Lock spatial zone and were being looked after by the Medusa Snake Demons, he received a message from the Moon Empress.","[Moon Empress]: Little Yuan, the people from the Vast Sea Labyrinth have arrived in the Radiance Federation and have something to discuss with us. If you have time tonight, why don’t you come with me to meet them?","Normally, the Moon Empress did not bring up interactions with other factions with Lin Yuan because she knew he was not invested in such matters. She informed him now because he had mentioned wanting to interact with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Lin Yuan smiled when he saw the Moon Empress’ message.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, I am heading to the Radiant Moon Palace now to meet with you! It just so happens that I need to ask your opinion on something.","Lin Yuan had cleansed his body of impurities numerous times. He had also consumed the Earth Center Fine Milk. Thus, his genetic model had long exceeded average human limits. Lin Yuan’s body could not be cleaner.","Moreover, the spirit qi clothes that he wore also repelled dust.","But after not showering for almost a week, Lin Yuan still drew a warm bath in his room in the Return from Faraway Mansion before heading to the Radiant Moon Palace.","...","The Moon Empress was seated at a table and looked at the thick stack of documents in her hand before handing most of them to Cicada Song. She knew that Cicada Song was more capable than her when it came to internal governance.","The Spacetime Elder only showed her favor because she had the highest Creation Mastery and was the strongest expert among all the Radiance Federation’s royalty. Lin Yuan was another contributing reason.","The Spacetime Elder had contracted the Lifespan Mouse and attained an endless lifespan.","Although he had relinquished his position and did not need to worry about anything anymore, he was still trying to protect the Radiance Federation.","Ever since the Moon Empress found out about the existence of the Sky Beyond the Clouds from Lin Yuan, her sights were also no longer restricted to the main world. She did not want to spend all of her time on internal governance because it would delay her increment in power.","They were in the midst of a crisis. Once the dead spirits emerged and things started progressing as planned, the Moon Empress intended to hand everything to Cicada Song so she could focus on increasing her power.","Recently, the Moon Empress had been busy, but she had also been troubled by one matter—Chef Supreme had sent a message saying he would reach his limit within the next five years.","Chef Supreme was around the same age as the Spacetime Elder. While the Spacetime Elder had been establishing the Radiance Federation, he had suffered numerous hidden injuries. The same went for Chef Supreme as well.","Chef Supreme’s contributions could not be ignored when it came to building the Radiance Federation that allowed the Moon Empress and Bamboo Monarch to grow in such an outstanding manner!","Chef Supreme had provided the Moon Empress and Bamboo Monarch with resources continuously after noticing their potential.","This was why the Moon Empress and Bamboo Monarch had such deep respect for Chef Supreme.","Now that she learned Chef Supreme was not long for this world, the Moon Empress, who had attained an endless lifespan, felt intense sorrow.","She knew that Lin Yuan was very close with Chef Supreme’s disciple and daughter. Thus, after some thought, she decided not to hide this from him.","There was no way that Chef Supreme’s people would tell Lin Yuan about this. If she did not tell him either, he would be filled with regret if he was not able to see Chef Supreme one final time!","The Lifespan Mouse’s existence was a miracle in itself.","When the Moon Empress last spoke to Lin Yuan, she learned he only had three Lifespan Mice left after giving one to the Spacetime Elder.","She never thought about asking Lin Yuan to give a Lifespan Mouse to Chef Supreme.","If there were still only three Lifespan Mice left and Lin Yuan wanted to give one to Chef Supreme, the Moon Empress would advise him to think twice before giving away something so precious.","The Moon Empress intended to listen to Lin Yuan’s question once they met.","She would tell Lin Yuan about Chef Supreme after they were done meeting with the people from the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","This would prevent him from showing his grief when they met with the Vast Sea Labyrinth and cause them to misunderstand that the people from the Radiance Federation were weak and incapable.","Lin Yuan’s question for the Moon Empress was indeed related to the Lifespan Mice.","Although he could not produce the Lifespan Mouse in large batches, as long as he was willing to nurture the army of Hundred Questions Beasts, he would still have an endless supply of the Lifespan Mouse.","Lin Yuan’s question was not about how to use the Lifespan Mice. He would never ask such a ludicrous question.","An endless lifespan would cause many issues for the main world. But Lin Yuan was no longer restricted to the main world."]},{"number":2638,"title":"Chapter 2638 The Vast Sea Labyrinth’s Request!","paragraphs":["2638 The Vast Sea Labyrinth’s Request!","Even if it caused disruptions, it would be the Sky Beyond the Clouds that would be affected. Given the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ level, small disruptions like this would not mean much! They might even have similar treasures themselves.","For example, Keira used her own bloodline to create the alien insect species. She also managed to use reincarnation to extend her own lifespan by thousands of years.","This would be akin to possessing pills of immortality when your family and friends had to contend with death. At that point, no one would be thinking about whether the immortality pills violated natural law!","Lin Yuan wanted to ask the Moon Empress if she needed the Lifespan Mice. If she did, he would be able to nurture the Lifespan Mice and supply them to the Radiance Federation.","In the face of this crisis that would affect the entire main world and trigger a changing of epochs, it would be necessary to have people with endless lifespans to see the main world through the entire event!","Lin Yuan’s current power had reached the peak of the main world, but he did not know much about the main world’s bigshots. Rather, he was more familiar with factions like the Heavenly Family Cottage, which was composed fully of Heavenly Family Feys.","For example, in the Radiance Federation, besides the Moon Empress, Night Leaning Moon, and Chef Supreme, Lin Yuan had only met and exchanged words with the Bamboo Monarch, Cicada Song, and the Spacetime Elder a few times. There were even members of royalty whom Lin Yuan had never seen before.","He had never met a single bigshot from another federation.","As such, it would be much more suitable for him to give the Lifespan Mice to the Moon Empress so she could distribute them accordingly.","After Lin Yuan sat down, the Moon Empress poured out a cup of tea for him and asked softly, “Little Yuan, do you have anything to ask me? I have time now, so I can help you with anything you might need.","“The federation representatives who left will need some time to relocate their citizens to the Radiance Federation. Even after they do, Cicada Song will be administering the operation!”","Lin Yuan hurriedly shook his head.","The Moon Empress was his Master, and he would only go to her with questions. He would never assign tasks to her.","“Master, do you remember the Lifespan Mouse? It is the fey that both you and the Spacetime Elder have contracted.”","The Moon Empress’ expression changed when she heard what Lin Yuan said. She began closely observing the expressions on his face.","Was Lin Yuan bringing up the Lifespan Mouse because he knew about Chef Supreme’s lifespan coming to an end?","But the Moon Empress could not discern any pain from his expression.","If Lin Yuan intended to give the Lifespan Mouse to Chef Supreme, he should not be acting so calmly.","But if he did not know about Chef Supreme’s limited lifespan, why would he bring up the Lifespan Mouse to her?","The Moon Empress nodded to indicate she remembered the Lifespan Mouse.","To the Moon Empress, the Lifespan Mouse was a precious treasure that no amount of resources could replace.","The Earth Center Fine Milk had a place on the list of most precious treasures, but it could only increase one’s lifespan by a year or two. Moreover, its effects would be discounted after the first use!","Even Class 2 Creation Masters could utilize spiritual ingredients that contained vitality, much less Class 5 Creation Masters.","Thus, using the Lifespan Mouse to increase one’s lifespan came at a very small cost!","When the Moon Empress nodded, Lin Yuan smiled and asked, “Master, do you need the Lifespan Mice? Uncle Mystic and Auntie Cold still have long lifespans, but they can eventually use the Lifespan Mouse. Why don’t we use this time before the crisis of dead spirits to help them—”","Before Lin Yuan could finish speaking, the Moon Empress sternly cut him off.","“Little Yuan, I’m sure you know how precious the Lifespan Mouse is. I am aware of your affection for Mystic Moon and Cold Moon, but you should keep such a resource to yourself and use it for your own needs! They are my left and right arms, but not yours.","“Liu Jie and Wen Yu are your left and right arms! If you have a surplus of the Lifespan Mice, you can give them to Liu Jie and Wen Yu rather than Mystic Moon and Cold Moon.","“When you go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, don’t reveal the existence of treasures that can extend lifespans, like the Lifespan Mouse, unless it’s absolutely necessary. There’s no way to tell what people are truly thinking. You should try your best to prevent anyone from coming after you because of the resources you possess!”","The Moon Empress had never said such things to Lin Yuan before. It was similar to what mothers in Lin Yuan’s previous life told their children before leaving for university. Only those who truly cared about you would say such things!","The Moon Empress believed she could protect Lin Yuan in the main world. But she would not have this confidence once he left for the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","It was possible that when they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, their positions would be switched. He would have to be the one to protect her instead!","Lin Yuan smiled at what the Moon Empress said before he took out a thermos box made of crystal. It contained 20 Lifespan Mice that were covered by orangey-red fur.","The Moon Empress looked shocked when she saw this box of Lifespan Mice. But she was also happy.","Lin Yuan noticed the happiness in her eyes and realized there was someone who badly needed the Lifespan Mouse!","“Master, the Lifespan Mouse can be nurtured. However, the process is very tedious and requires both effort and resources. I managed to nurture a few. I am leaving these Lifespan Mice with you. I’m sure you understand my meaning. You can give them to those who need them.","“I think Uncle Mystic, Auntie Cold, your four Moon Servants, and four tea attendants should have Lifespan Mice reserved for them!”","Lin Yuan paused before he asked the Moon Empress with a serious expression, “Master, if your friend’s lifespan is coming to an end and you don’t have enough of the Lifespan Mice, feel free to ask me for more!”","From Lin Yuan’s words, the Moon Empress knew he had noticed something in her gaze.","Since there was no lack of the Lifespan Mice, all problems could be solved!","Since Lin Yuan was willing to give away the Lifespan Mice, Chef Supreme definitely had the abilities, power, and track record to make him deserving of receiving the Lifespan Mouse!","As such, the Moon Empress started telling Lin Yuan about Chef Supreme.","“Little Yuan, the Kitchen Fragrance Palace sent word that Chef Supreme only has around five years left in his lifespan. He personally declared during an imperial meeting that he would enter seclusion to concoct more potions to maximize his value. He also said to send any dangerous tasks his way first!”","When the Moon Empress’ lifespan was ending, her main emotion had been indignance. But Chef Supreme was much more resigned and accepting. The past few centuries of his life had been exciting enough.","Chef Supreme was very cavalier, but the same could not be said for the others. Tian Feng was on good terms with Chef Supreme and had shed a waterfall of tears.","“Little Yuan, I will send the Lifespan Mouse to Kitchen Fragrance Palace in your name. If you aren’t busy, you can deliver it there yourself, too!”","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he said softly, “Master, I think you should help me to deliver it. Once we meet with the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s people and settle our discussions with them, I have many other plans that I need to see to.”","The Moon Empress instinctively tousled the top of Lin Yuan’s head. He had only just celebrated his 19th birthday but did not sound like a 19-year-old at all.","“Little Yuan, no matter how busy you are, don’t forget to take care of yourself! If you overstrain yourself and damage your roots, you will need to make up for it when the time comes for you to awaken your birth horoscope!”","The Moon Empress’ tone was solemn.","She had experienced what it was like to have seriously damaged roots, which caused her to suffer unexpectedly when she tried to awaken her birth horoscope. It was natural that she did not want Lin Yuan to go through the same experience.","The Moon Empress had brought this up with Lin Yuan more than once.","Because of his injured roots, the Class 5 Creation Master Weng Queji was still unable to awaken his birth horoscope, even with Lin Yuan’s help.","Hence, Lin Yuan was well aware of the consequences of damaging his roots. He would never knowingly harm himself.","“Master, don’t worry. I won’t overextend myself.”","It was true that Lin Yuan was busy, but he could squeeze out pockets of free time.","He did not want to go to the Kitchen Fragrance Palace personally because he was afraid of being profusely thanked by Uncle Li and Auntie Zhang.","Regardless of what happened, Lin Yuan felt he would never be able to repay Auntie Zhang and Uncle Li for all they had done for him when he was younger.","Although Lin Yuan and Chu Ci could have survived without Auntie Zhang and Uncle Li, the two of them had brought warmth into Lin Yuan’s life. Because of them, he felt as though he still had people to rely on, even during the toughest times!","Lin Yuan would not know how to respond if they thanked him.","Aside from the Moon Empress, Uncle Li and Auntie Zhang were the elders whom Lin Yuan respected the most. Not even Mystic Moon and Cold Moon could compare to them.","“Master, why don’t you send three Lifespan Mice to the Kitchen Fragrance Palace? His daughter and son-in-law can contract the other two.”","The Moon Empress could not help but grin.","Lin Yuan’s suggestion once again proved what a sentimental person he was.","Those who only cared about profits would think of his sentimentality as stupid. But the Moon Empress admired this about him because she was the same.","In the past, the Moon Empress always asked Lin Yuan to wear the version of the coronation costume she had prepared for him when they met with members of other factions. This was so the other factions would know he was her disciple.","But she did not ask him to do so this time.","If the people from the main world learned about everything Lin Yuan had done, they would no longer talk about him as the Moon Empress’ disciple. Rather, they would talk about her as Lin Yuan’s Master.","Meanwhile, in a building situated in the Radiance Federation’s imperial court...","Three strange men were seated around a table. All of them were staring austerely at the resources the Radiance Federation had just given them.","The three of them were the true rulers of the sea clans, the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s leaders. All three of them had married members of the Heavenly Family Cottage and were notorious within the Vast Sea Labyrinth for being afraid of their wives.","But the three Heavenly Family Feys who married them knew that their fear actually came from a place of adoration and respect.","In actuality, the Heavenly Family Cottage could not compare to the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s might!","The Vast Sea Labyrinth had been ruling over the sea clans for millennia, and they controlled all of the resources produced in the sea. They owned thousands of the Island Whales the humans were so eager to nurture but found difficult to do so.","Although the Heavenly Family Cottage also had a long history, they had very few members. There were less than 100 Heavenly Family Feys in the entire world!","The three of them had already noticed changes happening to the ley lines at the bottom of the sea.","However, they had not thought much of it and were feeling great regret over that mistake. If they had discovered Tower Canon’s plot a little earlier, they might have been able to reverse this disaster.","They were also furious thinking about how they had previously worked with Tower Canon. Their cooperation with Tower Canon had been a major driving force in the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","Although the three of them were unaware of Tower Canon’s plot, they still felt guilty. They felt remorseful toward every lifeform in the main world.","Otherwise, the Vast Sea Labyrinth would never have neglected to make even a single request of the Radiance Federation during their negotiation.","The tall, skinny man with long black hair and an air of elegance around him asked the two other men, “First Brother and Second Brother, why are we hesitating? We must ask the Radiance Federation for help! The Radiance Federation has more power than they are letting on. I have investigated this!","“It’s true that a 50-centimeter-thick layer of metal-type stone boards has covered the bottom of the Radiance Federation. The sea clans are in greater danger than the humans! We also need to cover the bottom of the sea with these special metal-type stone boards. Otherwise, we won’t be able to take cover anywhere when the dead spirits rise from the sea!","“Don’t forget that all lifeforms lived in the sea during the first and second epochs. They only started making their way to the land during the third epoch.”","The black-haired man spoke in an agitated tone. Few things in this world could send a leader of the Vast Sea Labyrinth into a state of panic.","However, this matter was grave and concerned the survival of the sea clans.","The man with short and curly light-blue hair and two light-blue moles at the corner of his eye said, “Third Brother, you must maintain your composure at all times! We have come to the Radiance Federation to ask for their help. We have already demonstrated sufficient sincerity. Without our thousands of Island Whales, the humans would never have been able to successfully complete their migration.","“According to Sister Purple Love, the Radiance Federation is easy to communicate with. Moreover, we are on the same side as the humans in the dead spirits crisis. However, First Brother should still be the one to lead the conversation and decide what conditions we set for the humans!”","The silver-haired man with a burly physique and black scales on his face smiled wryly.","His brother was thinking about things way too simply!","Now that they were racing against time, asking the Radiance Federation for such help would be no different from trying to rob them of their means of survival."]},{"number":2639,"title":"Chapter 2639 What Did the Moon Empress Mean by This?","paragraphs":["2639 What Did the Moon Empress Mean by This?","There was no way that the Radiance Federation would be willing to share freely in the face of such a crisis. If they could, he would not be as troubled as he was now!","“Second Brother, we are not here to negotiate with the Radiance Federation but to request their help! Let’s stop with the discussions. As long as the Radiance Federation is willing to help us, we will do our best to meet their conditions!","“Watch your words when we meet with the Moon Empress later. Do not make the Radiance Federation feel like we are threatening them with the favor we have done for them!”","The short blue-haired man with two light green moles by the corner of his eye hurriedly said, “Big Brother, when have we ever been pushed to such a degree? Our sea clans will be the main troops in dealing with the dead spirits crisis that will befall the entire world.","“There will be many more dead spirits rising from the sea than the land. It’s obvious that our jobs will be harder—”","The rest of his words were cut off.","“Second Brother, you have to get one thing clear. The humans don’t need the sea clans’ help to face this crisis! If we hadn’t become aware of the Radiance Federation’s might and gotten a glimpse of their capabilities, we wouldn’t have been so easily convinced to help them with their migration!","“We control all of the sea clans in the sea, but the Radiance Federation is not directly affected by whether the other federations live or die. We are helping the other federations and not the Radiance Federation.","“The humans have always fought with each other. When have they ever decided to band together to form an alliance? If we’re only talking about the Radiance Federation, we do not have much of an upper hand!","“Don’t forget that you have also done your own investigation and confirmed that it’s true that metal-type stone boards have been laid down below the entire Radiance Federation! This means that the rumor about the Radiance Federation taking over the subterranean world is true. Otherwise, how could so many Land Imps be activated to help the Radiance Federation with this operation?","“Second Brother, your view of things is too superficial. Ice Flow sees things much clearer than you can!”","The elegant man with long black hair that reached the ground also sighed.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth was currently being forced to take action. They would inevitably have to surrender some control to the Radiance Federation. All they could do was hope that the Radiance Federation did not go overboard!","Frankly, there was nothing the Vast Sea Labyrinth could do even if the Radiance Federation chose to go overboard.","He had sought out Purple Love in the hopes she could act as a bridge that protected them. But she had turned him down.","This told Ice Flow that Purple Love cared more about her relationship with the Radiance Federation than she did with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Previously, the Moon Empress had already gone to see the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s three leaders in a very formal manner. Hence, she did not need to be equally ceremonial this time. Instead, she took Lin Yuan directly to where the three leaders were staying.","The three figures stood up when the Moon Empress entered with Lin Yuan behind her. The Moon Empress greeted them.","The three of them knew of Lin Yuan but did not know why the Moon Empress had brought her disciple with her. It was not suitable to have a junior present at such a meeting!","From their expressions, the Moon Empress could tell that the Heavenly Family Cottage had not told them about Lin Yuan.","The three leaders’ faces fell. The Moon Empress’ words sounded like she was not taking them seriously or joking.","What did the Moon Empress mean by this?","Normally, the three of them would have immediately flown into a fit of rage. They might have even declared the Radiance Federation to be an enemy.","This treatment was akin to one showing genuine sincerity when visiting a prestigious family, only to be greeted by a trivial member of the family. This crossed the line!","Alas, the Vast Sea Labyrinth needed to ask the Radiance Federation for help. As such, the three of them were in no position to throw a tantrum.","The three of them calmly met the Moon Empress’ eyes before they each reached out their hands to Lin Yuan.","The well-built man with black scales on his face was the first to extend his arm. “My name is Ice Wave. I am one of the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s leaders. These two are my younger brothers. This is Ice Flow, and this is Ice Clarity.”","Lin Yuan smiled as he shook Ice Wave’s hand before doing the same with Ice Flow and Ice Clarity.","Next, he took out three brocade boxes and handed one to each of them. “The Radiance Federation hasn’t been able to make contact with the Vast Sea Labyrinth because we have been much too busy recently. This is a gift from the Radiance Federation to our friends and also a small gesture from Master and me.”","The three of them felt less aggravated when they heard what Lin Yuan said. They realized Lin Yuan was no normal human young man. Otherwise, he would not have been able to say something like that.","It would not be polite for them to open the brocade boxes in front of those who had gifted them to them.","Ice Wave, Ice Clarity, and Ice Flow stored the brocade boxes away before they thanked Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress.","Frankly, the three of them did not think much of the contents of the brocade boxes.","They might have a higher regard for these gifts if they had come from the Moon Empress. But since the young man had prepared them, they likely contained some spiritual ingredients or potions concocted by Creation Masters.","Once Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress were seated, Ice Wave did not beat around the bush and immediately brought up the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s problem.","There was no need to hide such a matter.","If the Radiance Federation truly intended to help the Vast Sea Labyrinth with their issue, they would do so immediately after he brought it up. But if they never wanted to help the Vast Sea Labyrinth in the first place, it would not matter what he said.","In the face of such a disaster, every second was tied to the survival of many sea lifeforms. If the Radiance Federation was unwilling to help, the Vast Sea Labyrinth could make other preparations as soon as possible rather than being sitting ducks.","In actuality, Ice Wave believed that with the Moon Empress’ intelligence, she would already have deduced their reason for coming.","The Moon Empress broke out in a cold sweat when she heard about the sea clans’ situation.","Ice Wave spoke with extreme sincerity and did not try to hide anything about the problem that the sea clans were facing.","If she had not already spoken with Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress would have no way of helping the sea clans and would have no choice but to disappoint Ice Wave.","The sea clans were in a much tougher situation than the humans were in.","As Ice Wave had said, all lifeforms in the main world lived in the sea from the first to third epoch.","The Moon Empress did not see this meeting as a deliberation with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","This was firstly because the Vast Sea Labyrinth had already shown sufficient sincerity. They did not need to try and gain the upper hand over the Vast Sea Labyrinth. Secondly, there was nothing that Vast Sea Labyrinth could do to force Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan purely wanted to help all the sea clans and rescue the entire main world.","This was why the Moon Empress had allowed Lin Yuan to take the lead in this discussion.","If she intended to deliberate, the Moon Empress would have helped Lin Yuan to make contact with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Lin Yuan coughed softly. This cough struck Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity. The three of them knew that this cough and this young man’s response could determine the fate of all the sea clans.","The three of them all felt a sense of foreboding.","This young man’s expression had not changed in the slightest after hearing what they said. He did not seem to be mulling over the pros and cons of helping them.","Could it be that the Moon Empress had predicted they would be asking for help and was unwilling to make a decision herself for fear of hurting the relationship between the Radiance Federation and the Vast Sea Labyrinth? Thus, she was pushing her disciple to make the decision instead?","Ice Wave took a deep breath. He had anticipated a result where the Moon Empress refused to help them.","The Radiance Federation didn’t need to help the Vast Sea Labyrinth, and this would not be easy help to provide either.","Even if the Radiance Federation refused to help, Ice Wave had no intention of recalling the Island Whales.","It would be better not to go back on his word!","They did not currently have any other use for the Island Whales as the sea clans did not need to use them for transportation.","Ice Flow and Ice Clarity had the same thoughts as Ice Wave.","Since the three of them had already prepared themselves for the worst, their first emotion after hearing what Lin Yuan said was not happiness. Rather, it was disbelief!","“You have guessed right. The Radiance Federation has indeed taken control of the subterranean world and can allocate the Land Imps. But based on what you have said, I don’t think sending the Land Imps into the sea to lay down the metal-type stone boards is the best course of action.","“The seabed is much harder than land. The Land Imps are afraid of water and can’t work properly at the bottom of the sea. As opposed to this plan, there are better ways to protect the sea clans.”","Ice Flow, Ice Clarity, and Ice Wave blinked a few times.","Although this young man had not explicitly agreed to help, he did say there were better ways to protect the sea clans.","Ice Clarity, the most anxious of them, hurriedly asked, “What do you have in mind? There are tens of millions of lifeforms living in the sea. It won’t be easy to protect all of them! If there isn’t a place where the sea clans can be sheltered from the dead spirits’ invasion, they will eventually be swallowed by the dead spirits.”","Although Ice Clarity had an impulsive streak, he had highlighted the key issue the sea clans were facing.","His words reminded Lin Yuan there would be no way to solve the sea clans’ issue if they could not find a safe haven for them.","Normally, Ice Flow was the one who liaised with other factions on the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s behalf. He knew that humans liked to leverage whatever advantage they had.","Ice Flow thought that Lin Yuan would also try to corner them. Yet, he said, “The sea clans are asking for too little. A safe haven won’t be enough to keep them safe from the dead spirits crisis.","“Besides the subterranean world, the Radiance Federation has also taken control of the water world. We have a way to combine the water world with the main world. All the sea clans can move into the water world. At that time, due to the water world’s lack of ley lines that have been infected by death aura, we can build defenses there.","“Additionally, the Dictators, Apostles, and other dimensional worlds in the water world can also become the sea clans’ companions and help them fend off the dead spirits’ invasion. Does my plan meet your satisfaction?”","Lin Yuan had spoken in a straightforward manner. Even someone dim-witted could understand him.","However, his words went beyond the three brothers’ comprehension. All at once, astonishment, excitement, and exhilaration rushed into their heads, causing them to feel dizzy!","If what this young man said was true, all their problems would be solved!","The sea clans would be able to live in the water world.","They had also encountered water world dimensional rifts in the past.","At that time, the water world dimensional lifeforms and sea clans were bitter enemies. But now, they were about to become comrades.","Although the three brothers were shocked, they did not think the Radiance Federation was lying.","The Moon Empress was sitting right here, and she had not rebuked anything her disciple had said.","If the Radiance Federation had any intention of lying to the sea clans, it would be pointless and result in the sea clans eventually seeking revenge on them. The sea clans would never accept being lied to!","Ice Wave, Ice Flow, and Ice Clarity forcefully composed themselves before they thanked the Moon Empress and Lin Yuan and asked, “How does the Radiance Federation intend to combine the main world with the water world? Will we need to do anything during this process?”","Lin Yuan did some calculations before he said, “About 15 days later, the other federations will have migrated to the Radiance Federation’s vicinity. At that time, the Radiance Federation will combine the main world with the dimensional worlds.","You can start relocating the sea clans to the Radiance Federation immediately. This will help more sea clans reach the Radiance Federation before the crisis of the dead spirits occurs. Ensuring this is the primary task for the sea clans.","“After merging the water world with the main world, I will arrange for the two main factions of the water world, Grace Sacred Hall and Mermaid Forbidden Sea, to establish contact with you.","So far, everything that Lin Yuan had done had been in secret. Once he was done weaponizing the Radiance Federation, he became assured.","There was no way they could hide the migration of the federations from Tower Canon.","Tower Canon’s inaction meant they cared more about triggering the start of the Sleeper’s Revival plan than stopping the migration.","Since they could not hide this from Tower Canon, they could cause as large of a commotion as possible.","Even if Tower Canon tried to take action against them, they would not be able to know what to do immediately.","Lin Yuan was racing against Tower Canon for time. He could also use this time before the dead spirits crisis began to find more information about Epoch God Palace.","As feys and the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s leaders, Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity had very long lifespans. They likely knew more about Epoch God Palace than Eighth Page Apoptosis did!"]},{"number":2640,"title":"Chapter 2640 Red Thorn Evolves!","paragraphs":["2640 Red Thorn Evolves!","Lin Yuan said solemnly to the three of them, “I want to ask you a question. I hope you will tell me the answer if you know it!”","Ice Wave, Ice Clarity, and Ice Flow all pulled serious expressions.","With how grave Lin Yuan’s expression was, the three of them would respond with utmost seriousness regardless of what his question was.","Ice Flow was the least calm of the three, but his brain was also the most active one!","He had already sensed the Moon Empress had not sent her disciple to lead the meeting with the Vast Sea Labyrinth because she wanted him to be the one to make the tough decisions—he had the capabilities to head such a meeting.","Although Purple Love had not spoken much about Lin Yuan, Ice Flow had heard about him from his wife.","The person on the best terms with the Heavenly Family Cottage was actually not the Moon Empress but someone close to her. It was likely that this referred to Lin Yuan!","Ice Flow was aware of the Moon Empress’ abilities. She had awoken her birth horoscope not long ago, and the Sacred Cry Moon Beast had only just reached Above Eternal. If she could, she would have already tried to take down the Freedom Federation long ago rather than waiting until now!","All the changes to the Radiance Federation that began two years ago happened to coincide with the time the Moon Empress took in her disciple.","With this thought, a chill ran up Ice Flow’s back when he looked at Lin Yuan again. Once this thought formed, Ice Flow only became increasingly certain it was the truth.","When Ice Wave heard what Lin Yuan said, he said seriously, “If it is something I know about, I will definitely lay it all out on the table without holding anything back! Feel free to ask whatever you want! Even if the matter concerns the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s deepest secrets, I will reveal them to you!”","As such, Lin Yuan asked softly, “Have you heard of Epoch God Palace?”","Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity’s expressions all changed when they heard this question. They had indeed heard of Epoch God Palace.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth held a deep history, and their privileges stemmed from ancestors. Despite never encountering Epoch God Palace directly, its existence was recorded in their ancient texts. It was a mysterious and fearsome organization. When they communicated with them, they couldn’t fully grasp the Epoch God Palace’s capabilities.","Records also suggested that Tower Canon once clashed with Epoch God Palace, attempting to steal their time-related artifact. But an Epoch God Palace leader intervened, and that generation of Tower Canon’s Eight Pages vanished.","Among the vanished, First Page Crimson reappeared unexpectedly, catching everyone’s attention, especially Ice Wave’s. He had witnessed First Page Crimson’s formidable power during a previous interaction. This drove him to study Tower Canon’s history through ancient records, gaining his current knowledge.","Ice Wave shared all this with Lin Yuan, confirming Lin Yuan’s suspicions. First Page Crimson belonged to Tower Canon’s initial Eight Pages.","This confirmation hinted that the initial Eight Pages, who controlled the dead world, had come from the Sky Beyond the Clouds for an unknown reason.","It was likely that this applied to Epoch God Palace as well!","However, Lin Yuan could not shake the feeling that Epoch God Palace was not safe. There was a high possibility that Epoch God Palace would become an even more difficult enemy to deal with than Tower Canon!","Luckily, he had uncovered Tower Canon’s plan. However, he did not have a single clue about Epoch God Palace’s plans or goals!","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was sure they were working toward a goal. Otherwise, they would not have remained hidden and waiting in a corner of the main world for so long.","Now that he was confident he would be able to tackle the dead spirits crisis, Lin Yuan decided to begin searching Epoch God Palace’s experts and make contact with them!","He had heard about a fight between Epoch God Palace and Tower Canon from Ice Wave. This alone was enough.","After answering Lin Yuan’s question, Ice Wave seemed to muster up an immense amount of determination before he told Lin Yuan about the deal he had made with Tower Canon in the past.","Ice Wave felt much more relaxed after confessing his mistake.","The Moon Empress knitted her brow when he heard what Ice Wave said.","He had helped Tower Canon to collect death aura from the bottom of the sea, and it was because of this large amount of death aura that the Sleeper’s Revival plan was able to commence smoothly.","Lin Yuan also frowned. But his brow relaxed quickly.","Firstly, he knew that removing a large amount of death aura from a piece of land would be beneficial for the lifeforms that lived on it. Ice Wave had made that decision because he was a true king of the sea clans and was trying to improve their quality of life.","Furthermore, Tower Canon’s plan had been shrouded in secrecy, and Ice Wave had not been aware of it. His only crime would be carelessness and neglecting to check thoroughly.","Even if he had not made the deal with Tower Canon, the latter would have found another way to gather the death aura from the bottom of the sea.","There were also a few of the Radiance Federation’s 32 major cities that had their death aura unknowingly drained.","Ice Wave could have hidden what he had done from the Radiance Federation but chose to reveal it of his own accord. This was enough to prove his sincerity in working with the Radiance Federation.","“What has passed has passed. I only hope that going forward, the Vast Sea Labyrinth will do its best in the war against the dead spirits. We have discussed all that we need to discuss.","“Why don’t we leave the details for later, once you are done relocating the sea clans? The Radiance Federation will help the sea clans defend against the dead spirits! Not only will we supply you with Land Imps, but we’ll provide you with resources as well.”","Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity looked deeply into Lin Yuan’s eyes. He had not mentioned anything about profits at all. He was purely trying to use his abilities to save the sea clans and help them overcome this crisis!","This magnanimity caused the three of them to feel extremely ashamed!","After the three of them left, the Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan with gratification.","It turned out that this was how he conducted deliberations!","From Lin Yuan’s interactions with the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s three rulers, the Moon Empress got a sense of how Lin Yuan interacted with others during his path of growth, especially with the Dictators from the dimensional worlds.","It was at that moment the Moon Empress realized that Lin Yuan was smiling.","She was rather curious. What was there to be happy about now?","Lin Yuan heard Red Thorn asking him which part of its body it should evolve. It only asked this question when it was about to evolve its grade.","Among all of Lin Yuan’s feys, Red Thorn’s evolution was the slowest. It had been stuck at Platinum IX/Fantasy V for three months with no signs of evolving to Diamond grade.","But in actuality, Red Thorn’s power had far exceeded its expected potential!","A Platinum/Fantasy V source-type lifeform could use the Tongue of Relinquish to control an Afterlife Realm corpse and wield it as a living weapon. Not even Platinum feys possessed such abilities!","Moreover, Red Thorn was now a pinnacle six-winged fairy and was showing signs of evolving to eight wings.","If Red Thorn could grow a fourth pair of wings when it evolved to Diamond grade, it would be able to set a new record in history for fairy source-type lifeforms.","“Master, I have a fey that is about to evolve. I need to find a wide and quiet place. Once I have helped it to evolve its power, I will go with Ice Wave and the rest to the Vast Sea Labyrinth. The sea clans are supplying the Island Whales to help us humans with our migration. I am going to help them to repay them!”","The Moon Empress nodded before raising her hand and helping him to adjust his collar again.","“Since becoming a Class 6 Creation Master, I have made achievements of my own in the past year. I have nurtured a special fey that can increase the amount of spirit qi that spirit qi professionals can contain in their bodies. It will be able to help spirit qi professionals promote their spirit qi professional rank quicker.","“After nurturing this fey once by accident, I haven’t been able to nurture a second one, even using the same method. Once you return, you can form a contract with this fey. From then on, you will no longer be hindered by your spirit qi professional rank!”","Lin Yuan looked delighted when he heard what the Moon Empress said.","It could be said that the only thing holding Lin Yuan back was the promotion of his spirit qi professional rank.","After he contracted this fey, his spirit qi professional rank would reach S+ at least while the dead spirits crisis was going on.","From then on, the evolution of the grades of Lin Yuan’s feys would no longer be limited!","Lin Yuan did not stand on ceremony with the Moon Empress. A fey that could help a spirit qi professional to increase their rank faster would not be of much use to an expert like the Moon Empress.","“Master, that will be a big help to me! The promotion of my spirit qi professional rank is what I am lacking the most now!”","The Moon Empress was very glad she could help Lin Yuan.","She reached out and patted the hair on top of Lin Yuan’s head.","“Little Yuan, I know that even with the impending dead spirits crisis, your power will not fall back to the level of the Radiance Federation. But remember to always keep your movements hidden, no matter where you are! Tower Canon’s Eight Pages will definitely be watching you at all times. Don’t give them the chance to target you! I will be waiting in the Radiance Federation until you return.”","Lin Yuan nodded at the Moon Empress before transporting himself through Node Transportation to a remote area outside of Ascending Dragon City.","This was not the same place where Morbius had increased its power.","Morbius’ evolution had caused far too much commotion. Lin Yuan had been afraid that Morbius’ large amount of World Grace would catch the attention of the higher beings in other worlds and cause them to zero in on the main world.","When Begin Lady and Celestial Sight underwent their Heaven’s Trials, Lin Yuan had confirmed that the Heaven’s Trials were controlled by those higher lifeforms!","Lin Yuan composed himself and summoned Red Thorn, fairy form and original body.","Lin Yuan had not looked at Red Thorn’s data in a long time, and he used True Data on it.","[Fey Name]: Red Thorn (Six-Winged Fairy) (Thousand Eyes Relinquish)","[Fey Species]: Rafflesia genus/fairy species","[Spirit-Lifeform Grade]: Platinum (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Wood","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Mouth of Relinquish]: Secretes vigorous digestive fluids with powerful corrosive properties, allowing a faster speed to absorb the energy in the food. The Tongue of Relinquish inside the mouth is able to increase the digestion speed by several times. It can also secrete a special corrosive fluid from the flesh and blood that it consumed. When the Tongues of Relinquish pierce a target, the tip of the tongue can be cut off and left in the target’s body. While the target remains alive, the tip of the tongue will control the target’s spirit and soul. After the target dies, the tip of the tongue can control and manipulate the target to make it appear as though it was still alive.","[Brutal Carnivore Vine]: The vines contained digestive fluids that grew in midair, and the sharp teeth on the inner side of the vine could grind off and collect flesh and blood energy.","[Eye of Relinquish]: Eyes formed by using blood and flesh energy. Each eye contains a huge amount of blood and flesh energy. When the number of Eyes of Relinquish on every Mouth of Relinquish is maintained below 60, they are merely able to store energy. When the number of Eyes of Relinquish is above 60, those Eyes of Relinquish that are above 60 can be turned into an energy ray at any time.","[Sea of Flowers State Transition]: By quickly using up the stored-up energy, the sea of flowers’ child ramets’ attacking power and mobility can be improved several times. The child ramets’ weapons will also morph in a way that increases their functionality.","[Demon Spirit Curse Kill]: Whenever any of the ortet’s ramets touched an enemy target and breaks through a target’s defense, the target will be cursed. Every curse carries a negative effect that would be stacked with every additional attack.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spore Growth]: Spits a huge amount of spores, which can absorb the energy or flesh energy supplied by Red Thorn, out of its spore cavity to quickly grow ramets and child ramets that are controlled by the ortet.","[Wither Glory]: Red Thorn can rapidly absorb the energy from the soil and pour the energy into the sea of flowers. As long as the soil has the roots of the child ramets and ramets, the withered sea of flowers would reach its prime state.","Lin Yuan stared at Red Thorn’s data for a moment. He felt it had reached the pinnacle of capabilities for a lifeform that fought by establishing a land formation and expanding it.","There was no other way in which Red Thorn’s sea of flowers could be improved.","Even if Lin Yuan found a minute detail and tried to evolve it, its benefit would be negligible.","Given the circumstances, Lin Yuan felt he should pivot away from evolving Red Thorn’s sea of flowers.","Since Red Thorn could control the Abyss Great Emperor through the Tongue of Relinquish, Lin Yuan felt he could evolve that part during Red Thorn’s next evolution!"]},{"number":2641,"title":"Chapter 2641 Tongue Pouch Births Demons","paragraphs":["2641 Tongue Pouch Births Demons","While Lin Yuan was increasing Red Thorn’s power, he never stopped thinking about what the best method would be. It did not take long for him to arrive at an answer.","However, Lin Yuan did not know whether the abilities and boost that Red Thorn received from the evolution of the Tongue of Relinquish would meet his expectations.","Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish could control other lifeforms because it had swallowed the seed in Ji Feng’s body.","The seed came from a plant called the Gardener Konjac. At that time, Lin Yuan did not know where the Gardener Konjac came from. But slowly, he became certain it came from the dead world that was still largely foreign to the main world.","The Gardener Konjac was a dimensional lifeform that Second Page Revival had been actively nurturing. But for an unknown reason, Second Page Revival later disappeared.","According to Eighth Page Apoptosis, Second Page Revival had disappeared around the time she went with Sixth Page Lashing to a joint operation with the Freedom Federation envoy group to the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan had already asked the Moon Empress and confirmed that Second Page Revival’s disappearance was not related to the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan always found this to be strange.","Although the Tongue of Relinquish’s abilities came from the Gardener Konjac, its power now fully came from the corpses it controlled like the Abyss Great Emperor. It did not actually have much to do with the Gardener Konjac’s genes!","The main reason was that Red Thornb had raised the Gardener Konjac’s abilities.","Otherwise, why did the Gardener Konjac only have so few top experts under its control when it was in Second Page Revival’s hands? Why did it only control emperor-class experts with Myth Breed feys like Ji Feng?","Lin Yuan wanted to strengthen Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish because he wanted to see the extent to which Red Thorn could raise the Gardener Konjac’s genes.","Lin Yuan reached out and halted the flying Red Thorn before saying seriously, “Red Thorn, I know you have been waiting for this day for a long time and that you have accumulated enough power. When you evolve to Diamond grade, choose to evolve your Tongue of Relinquish!","“While you are evolving, I will instruct someone to provide your main body with a large number of corpses so you can replenish your vitality. I have already extracted a significant amount of pure wood-elemental energy from the Wood-Building Winged Sandflies’ larvae.","“I will feed you the wood-elemental energy as well as the almost 1,000 units of pure fairy bloodlines supplied by the Goddess of Mercy!","“The Goddess of Mercy caused too much bloodshed while trying to obtain these fairy bloodlines. When you absorb them, create a new history for the fairy species, and bring glory to them, you will have made those deaths worth it!”","Red Thorn nodded earnestly.","Normally, there was nothing that Red Thorn liked more than to cling to Lin Yuan. It rarely acted as seriously as this.","When Red Thorn found out that the Goddess of Mercy had been nurturing fairies to kill them and turn them into toys once they were fully grown, it immediately started to hate the Goddess of Mercy.","It had been keeping this fury to itself and had not expressed it to Lin Yuan.","No lifeform would not become enraged by the knowledge that someone was killing its kind and turning them into toys.","This contributed to Lin Yuan’s decision not to keep the Goddess of Mercy by his side and send her to the water world to live with the other mermaids instead.","“Yuan, I do not need so many fairy bloodlines for my evolution. I sense that I will need less than 300 fairy bloodlines to reach eight wings. After I evolve to eight wings and reach that gate, I will need to accumulate power for some time before my bloodline can experience another breakthrough.","“During that time, the remaining fairy bloodlines can go to Silver Corona, Elegance, Brocade Zither, and the rest!","“Brocade Zither does not have much potential, and it would have been difficult for it to become a four-winged fairy. But after living in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and being nourished by the pure spirit qi for a prolonged period, as well as absorbing a significant amount of energy from the Pure Land of Bliss, it can now evolve to four wings. All it needs now is an opportunity! If it absorbs a few units of fairy bloodlines, it will be able to evolve into a four-winged fairy!”","Usually, Red Thorn rarely interacted with Brocade Zither. However, it did look out for Brocade Zither.","Lin Yuan smiled and nodded. “Red Thorn, I can supply you with as many fairy bloodlines as you need. Just relax and evolve!”","Red Thorn flew to the center of the three Mouths of Relinquish and wrapped its body with its three pairs of wings before falling into slumber.","Soon, explosive roaring noises could be heard within the three large Mouths of Relinquish. The roaring resembled that of the eruption of a small volcano.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and released 30 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators before instructing them to take Diamond fey storage boxes to Red Thorn’s Mouths of Relinquish to supply it with the corpses of dimensional lifeforms.","Normally, Lin Yuan only fed the corpses of Class 5 and 6 dimensional lifeforms to Red Thorn. However, the Platinum Red Thorn could already consume Class 7 to 8 dimensional lifeforms that were the equivalent of Myth Breed feys!","Numerous dimensional lifeforms died in the dimensional worlds daily, and Lin Yuan had intentionally collected all of them.","This not only provided Red Thorn with good quality food, but Lin Yuan also did not need to kill whenever he needed to feed Red Thorn.","When the corpses filled with blood energy entered the Mouths of Relinquish, the sounds coming from the three furnace-like Mouths of Relinquish became even more uproarious.","Each time the Mouth of Relinquish contracted and expanded, it grew larger.","As the Mouth of Relinquish had a relatively flat shape, it did not seem tall. However, it was around the size of a small sports stadium.","The Eye of Relinquish did not become much larger as it was not the focus of the evolution like the Mouth of Relinquish was. Nonetheless, it still became larger and brighter. It was clear that it now stored much more energy than it did in the past!","The roaring noises lasted for almost five hours before they stopped. As the Tongue of Relinquish was currently wrapped up in the Mouth of Relinquish, Lin Yuan could not see its current state.","But as the Mouth of Relinquish opened and closed, Lin Yuan saw that there was a pouch-like item below the Tongue of Relinquish.","Lin Yuan walked into the part where the three Mouths of Relinquish met.","Lin Yuan had just instructed the 30 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators to feed the fairy bloodlines and wood-elemental energy to Red Thorn.","When he arrived at the part where the three Mouths of Relinquish met, he saw that Red Thorn had grown another pair of wings just as he had predicted. However, this set of wings seemed to be extremely premature.","Lin Yuan was not a fairy, so he could sense that Red Thorn’s bloodline had evolved. Still, he could not tell if it had any influence over other fairies.","Silver Corona was not with him. Otherwise, he would use Silver Corona as a test subject.","Lin Yuan used Morbius to check on Red Thorn.","[Fey Name]: Red Thorn (Eight-Winged Fairy) (Thousand Eyes Relinquish)","[Fey Species]: Rafflesia genus/fairy species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Wood","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Mouth of Relinquish]: Secretes vigorous digestive fluids with powerful corrosive properties, allowing a faster speed to absorb the energy in the food. The Tongue of Relinquish inside the mouth is able to increase the digestion speed by several times. It can also secrete a special corrosive fluid from the flesh and blood that it consumed. When the Tongues of Relinquish pierce a target, the tip of the tongue can be cut off and left in the target’s body. While the target remains alive, the tip of the tongue will control the target’s spirit and soul. After the target dies, the tip of the tongue can control and manipulate the target to make it appear as though it was still alive.","[Brutal Carnivore Vine]: The vines contained digestive fluids that grew in midair, and the sharp teeth on the inner side of the vine could grind off and collect flesh and blood energy.","[Eye of Relinquish]: Eyes formed by using blood and flesh energy. Each eye contains a huge amount of blood and flesh energy. When the number of Eyes of Relinquish on every Mouth of Relinquish is maintained below 60, they are merely able to store energy. When the number of Eyes of Relinquish is above 60, those Eyes of Relinquish that are above 60 can be turned into an energy ray at any time.","[Sea of Flowers State Transition]: By quickly using up the stored-up energy, the sea of flowers’ child ramets’ attacking power and mobility can be improved by several times. The child ramets’ weapons will also morph in a way that increases their functionality.","[Demon Spirit Curse Kill]: Whenever any of the ortet’s ramets touched an enemy target and breaks through a target’s defense, the target will be cursed. Every curse carries a negative effect that would be stacked with every additional attack.","[Tongue Pouch Births Demons]: When a corpse is being consumed, it can be stored in the tongue pouch and nurtured. If the corpse’s power is intact, it can be nurtured into a special lifeform that contains a fairy bloodline. Its previous power will be retained, and its power can also be increased when tempered by blood energy.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spore Growth]: Spits a huge amount of spores, which can absorb the energy or flesh energy supplied by Red Thorn, out of its spore cavity to quickly grow ramets and child ramets controlled by the ortet.","[Wither Glory]: Red Thorn can rapidly absorb the energy from the soil and pour the energy into the sea of flowers. As long as the soil has the roots of the child ramets and ramets, the withered sea of flowers would reach its prime state.","Currently, Red Thorn had evolved to Diamond I, but its quality had not changed. Nonetheless, after reaching eight wings, its abilities had all been strengthened!","Given that it had chosen to evolve the Tongue of Relinquish, it gained a new ability called Tongue Pouch Births Demons.","In spite of his wealth of experience, Lin Yuan still could not help but slap his leg out of excitement when he saw Tongue Pouch Births Demons.","Tongue Pouch Births Demons significantly increased the Tongue of Relinquish’s ability to control corpses.","The Tongue of Relinquish took control of corpses by inserting its tongue tip into the corpses. The tongue tip would then fix up the corpse before activating its cells and manipulating its movement.","Now that the Tongue of Relinquish had evolved, Tongue Pouch Births Demons could store a corpse in its tongue pouch and nurture a lifeform with a fairy bloodline.","The lifeform would also retain all the abilities from when it was alive. Just like a living lifeform, it could also be nurtured to increase its power while it was inside the tongue pouch. This made it no different from a living lifeform.","Although the corpses in the tongue pouches would still be dead entities that Red Thorn controlled, their powers could continue to increase!","The Abyss Great Emperor was currently Lin Yuan’s strongest powerhouse. But it fell short of Eternal Source because he could continuously increase his power while the Abyss Great Emperor could not.","But now, the Abyss Great Emperor also had the chance to increase its power.","At that moment, Red Thorn woke up and started flapping its four pairs of wings.","Red Thorn sensed its new pair of wings before it dove into Lin Yuan’s arms.","There was nothing that fairies prioritized more than their bloodlines, and Red Thorn was no exception.","However, Lin Yuan did not know that Red Thorn was not only happy because of its bloodline. It was also largely related to Silver Corona.","Previously, Red Thorn and Silver Corona were six-winged fairies. Although Red Thorn’s bloodline was slightly more elite than Silver Corona’s, it could not exert much influence over Silver Corona. Thus, it could not chase Silver Corona away from Lin Yuan’s side.","This always triggered Red Thorn’s possessiveness.","But now that it had eight wings, it could use its bloodline to overcome Silver Corona’s bloodline.","Red Thorn did not know why it always had the uncontrollable urge to compare itself with Silver Corona when they were actually on good terms.","It was because they had extremely similar abilities and could produce seas of flowers.","Silver Corona was also highly favored by Lin Yuan in the beginning, and he had used Shatter Spatial Stones to open up tens of dimensional rifts for it.","Red Thorn had been rolling in jealousy for some time!","Red Thorn said softly, “Yuan, I can use my tongue pouches to nurture promising corpses in the future! Every Tongue of Relinquish will be able to grow two tongue pouches at the most. The tongue pouches can be used as long as they are empty.","“Moreover, there isn’t a limit on the corpses being controlled. But the stronger the corpse, the more time it will take for the tongue pouch to transform it!”","With feys like the Engulfing Flames Heart Mushroom and Source Sand, which did not have high intelligence, Lin Yuan always needed to deduce their abilities after each evolution through True Data.","But with fairies like Red Thorn, which were even more intelligent than humans, the latter would volunteer answers to Lin Yuan’s questions.","It was not easy for Lin Yuan to find any more strong corpses from the main world unless he killed the real Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","But once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, it was likely that there would be powerful experts abound.","Before Red Thorn grew the tongue pouches, the World Emperor experts that it controlled using its tongue tips could be easily recognized by experts they had ties to. Once they were recognized, Lin Yuan would be targeted by the experts’ kin.","Luckily, with the tongue pouches, Lin Yuan did not need to worry about that anymore."]},{"number":2642,"title":"Chapter 2642 Opening of the Five Black Coffins!","paragraphs":["2642 Opening of the Five Black Coffins!","Once the corpses were nurtured, they would become lifeforms similar to fairies.","In a nutshell, Tongue Pouch Births Demons could be used to create a species out of the experts’ corpses!","Moreover, the species of corpses that Red Thorn created would become even stronger weapons than the alien insects!","The alien insects could use the bloodlines of other species to strengthen themselves but could not attain the abilities of the species they took over.","If Lin Yuan’s sights were still restrained to the main world, he would not be this elated about Red Thorn attaining Tongue Pouch Births Demons.","But now that his sights were set on the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he realized that many of his feys’ abilities and exclusive skills would become extremely useful!","Lin Yuan pulled himself back to reality. Regardless of how much he was looking forward to heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the most important matters he needed to address now were dealing with Tower Canon, helping the main world to overcome their dead spirits crisis, and carrying them through the sixth epoch.","“Red Thorn, how long will it take for you to use the tongue pouch to transform the Abyss Great Emperor?”","Given that Red Thorn controlled the Abyss Great Emperor, it completely understood his circumstances.","Red Thorn fell silent momentarily before replying, “Yuan, it will take me at least three months to transform the Abyss Great Emperor. After all, I am still only Diamond grade. My bloodline might have reached eight wings, but the effects of my abilities are still strongly correlated to my grade!","“However, you can still use the Abyss Great Emperor even while I’m transforming him in the tongue pouch. He can continue to protect and fight for you.”","Lin Yuan’s happiness showed on his face, and he said, “Red Thorn, why don’t you use the tongue pouch to transform the Abyss Great Emperor now? I am looking forward to seeing what he becomes three months later!”","Red Thorn snapped its fingers and ordered the Abyss Great Emperor to enter one of the Mouths of Relinquish.","Once the Abyss Great Emperor fully entered the Mouth of Relinquish, the tongue pouch closed around him.","Red Thorn stuck out its tongue and said softly, “However, after transforming the Abyss Great Emperor, he might look rather strange the next time you summon him.”","Lin Yuan shook his head to indicate he did not care. As long as the Abyss Great Emperor did not become weaker, he did not care what he looked like.","Now, Lin Yuan did not have any more feys that needed to be evolved for the foreseeable future.","He had told the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s three leaders he would be heading there.","Ice Wave needed to oversee the entire operation of migrating the sea clans. Ice Clarity was rather impulsive and would not be appropriate for working with Lin Yuan. Hence, Ice Wave assigned the task of receiving Lin Yuan to Ice Flow.","Ice Flow had also been the one who first interacted with the Radiance Federation.","Ever since Lin Yuan contracted the Ethereal Jellyfish, he began placing its tentacles all over the Radiance Federation to create spatial nodes. These spatial nodes were not meant to be used solely by Lin Yuan but were also for the convenience of all of Sky City’s core members.","Ice Flow’s facial features were very elegant, and his long black hair looked rather out of place. Nonetheless, none of the people around noticed he was a fey in human form.","Ice Flow reached out his hand and greeted Lin Yuan with a smile, “Thank you for being willing to come with me to help the sea clans.”","Lin Yuan smiled back at Ice Flow to say ‘you are welcome’.","From Morbius, Lin Yuan could see that Ice Flow was a pinnacle spirit-fire expert and was only a small step away from reaching World Emperor and the divine kingdom. He was much stronger than the Mirror God and God of Fools!","Lin Yuan did not know much about how much power the Spacetime Elder had and could not make a comparison to him.","But it was possible that Ice Flow was the strongest expert in the main world below the World Emperor and divine-kingdom level.","When he met Ice Flow and the other leaders of the Vast Sea Labyrinth, they talked the most about the issues they were about to face. The Vast Sea Labyrinth had been desperate for the Radiance Federation’s help. As such, at the time, Lin Yuan had not asked about the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s power.","Lin Yuan stood next to Ice Flow and looked out at the sea as he asked, “How many pinnacle spirit-fire experts like you does the Vast Sea Labyrinth have? Does the Vast Sea Labyrinth have World Emperor and divine kingdom experts?”","Ice Flow froze when he heard what Lin Yuan said. He instinctively felt that Lin Yuan’s question was rather inappropriate as it involved the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s core secrets.","However, after considering the relationship between the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the Radiance Federation, Ice Flow decided to answer Lin Yuan’s question. However, he was soon stunned by the latter part of what Lin Yuan said.","He heard Lin Yuan mention the World Emperor and divine-kingdom level. Were these the levels above High Sovereign and the spirit-fire level?","This was the first time Ice Flow learned about the terms for the levels above spirit fire.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth’s legacy went back much further than that of the humans.","Every generation of the Vast Sea Labyrinth had been recorded in the Coral Records. So, one only needed to look through the Coral Records to learn about the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s entire legacy.","There was no mention of the World Emperor and divine-kingdom level at all in Vast Sea Labyrinth’s legacy.","Ice Flow wondered, Can it be that humans already have such experts?","As overwhelmed as he was feeling, Ice Flow still appeared extremely calm and said seriously to Lin Yuan, “There are a total of 14 spirit-fire experts in the Vast Sea Labyrinth. We don’t have a single World Emperor and divine-kingdom level expert!”","Lin Yuan was startled.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth truly lived up to their role as the rulers of the sea. It turned out that they had 14 spirit-fire experts! These were pinnacle spirit-fire experts to boot!","The first Major Federation Union meeting had commenced smoothly. Presently, there were only four known human spirit-fire experts. There was one in the Radiance Federation, two in the Freedom Federation, and one from the Azure Federation.","The sea clans had more than three times the number of spirit-fire experts than the humans!","They did not need to bother comparing their number of birth-horoscope experts!","Lin Yuan took a deep breath. It was no wonder that the Vast Sea Labyrinth had never bothered to take the human factions seriously. They were indeed powerful enough to sneer at the human factions on land.","Lin Yuan did not respond to Ice Flow’s question immediately. He controlled Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor, who were Afterlife Realm Dictators. Their power was equivalent to that of World Emperor and divine kingdom-level experts.","However, neither of them were humans.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was human.","Lin Yuan looked into Ice Flow’s eyes, and they glinted as he said, “To be honest, I have two subordinates of that level!","“When we head to the Vast Sea Labyrinth together, I will send around 100 Turning Wheel Realm Dictators that are the equivalent of Above Eternal feys to summon ocean currents and help you with your migration.","“I can also open a Space Tunnel that will allow the sea clans to enter the marsh world, where they can remain for some time. Once I release the sea clans into the marsh world, they will be able to relocate to the Radiance Federation’s sea.","“However, if you organize the migration on your own, only the powerful lifeforms will be successfully relocated. The weak lifeforms will definitely end up losing their lives to the dead spirits crisis! I didn’t mention this previously, but it’s not too late to bring it up now.”","Lin Yuan did not stop walking while he spoke.","He looked around and saw that everyone on the harbor looked concerned and anxious.","Usually, when they faced disasters, the Radiance Federation’s royalty preferred to take the full brunt of the effects on their own and did not want to affect the weaker spirit qi professionals and regular people.","But during this disaster that triggered the changing of epochs, the Radiance Federation’s royalty decided after much contemplation not to keep it under wraps and reveal the situation to all of the Radiance citizens. This was so they could all make their own preparations and receive this calamity together.","The Radiance Federation’s royalty made this decision because they were all aware they could not handle this crisis on their own. It would require the combined efforts of all the Radiance citizens!","Currently, the Radiance citizens were all accumulating resources in order to take on the impending disaster.","The harbor was much more crowded than usual. But these were just people gathered together. None of them were showing any interest in chatting with each other while they were moving resources. This was a silent crowd full of bottled-up emotion.","Lin Yuan could not help but sigh. He had already done all he could to help the Radiance Federation with this crisis. There was nothing else he could do!","Ice Flow had frozen in his steps when he heard what Lin Yuan said. But he quickly snapped out of his trance and caught up with Lin Yuan.","Ice Flow solemnly told Lin Yuan, “Thank you for all you are doing for the sea clans. If we are able to tide over this crisis, the sea clans will do whatever you ask of us!”","Lin Yuan did not say anything. He knew that Ice Flow was not making empty promises but could not take Ice Flow seriously.","Firstly, he did not know how long it would take for the dead spirits crisis to pass. Secondly, Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity could make promises with short-term repercussions, but the same could not be said for long-term promises!","But given Lin Yuan’s current situation, there was no way he would need help from the sea clans.","“Let’s go. We can talk about other matters in the future.”","Lin Yuan had walked to the end of the harbor and raised a leg to walk into the sea.","Lin Yuan’s action startled Ice Flow.","This was a deep harbor, not a regular place. The water could reach a depth of 2 kilometers. Otherwise, there was no way that the Island Whales would be able to dock there.","Once Lin Yuan lowered his leg, he would fall into the sea!","The water was full of dark undercurrents that would quickly pull Lin Yuan to its dark and deep depths.","Ice Flow was about to manipulate the water to grab Lin Yuan when he saw the water rise up and gather around Lin Yuan’s feet, holding him up.","The water was moving very similarly to when he controlled it.","Ice Flow could sense that the sea water was voluntarily gathering around Lin Yuan.","The seawater was gathering around Lin Yuan before Ice Flow had ordered it to do so. This deeply shocked Ice Flow.","Ice Flow looked at Lin Yuan incredulously. He did not know how Lin Yuan was more affiliated with and have a stronger control over water than he did!","Ice Flow had heard that Blue Lotus had given her Heavenly Family Blessing to a young human. But even if Lin Yuan was this human, this should not be how it manifested!","Lin Yuan turned back to look at Ice Flow as he quipped, “Let’s hurry. Every moment that we are late will cost the lives of many sea lifeforms!”","Lin Yuan raised a hand and a current rose from the surface of the water.","Ice Flow stepped on the current that Lin Yuan had formed and manipulated it to carry him toward the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Numerous regular people and spirit qi professionals on the harbor saw Lin Yuan and Ice Flow’s actions. Although they were all shocked by this sight, they did not act on their shock.","Experts had been arriving in Ascending Dragon City recently, and tens of the Island Whales had also been dispatched from the harbor.","Seeing the Island Whales expanded these people’s horizons.","Their eyesight was not good enough. Otherwise, they would have noticed Lin Yuan performing the extraordinary act of summoning and riding on water currents.","...","While Lin Yuan and Ice Flow were headed to the Vast Sea Labyrinth, a few soft giggles emerged from a castle.","A girl dressed in a long black skirt and holding a back candle stopped flipping through the book in her hands.","The light from the purple flame burning atop the black candle became the brightest light source in the large hall. It even blanketed over the light from the glowing birth horoscopes hanging above the large hall.","The girl turned towards the eight black coffins behind her.","The first, third, fourth, fifth, and sixth black coffins flew open simultaneously. The seventh coffin shook a few times but eventually did not open.","The girl’s gaze became even deeper when she saw the five open black coffins.","“Violet Light Green, Cavity Orchid, and Wave Glow, it’s been too long!”","The girl strode to the fifth coffin and hugged the girl within, who had seven-colored eyes and hair. Her action was full of love and devotion.","However, this girl with rainbow eyes and hair adjusted her skirt before deftly pushing Second Page Warbler Candle away with her slender fingers and saying coldly, “Crimson told you to manage the situation. But you caused so much trouble! The human federations and sea clans ended up finding out about the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","“Warbler Candle, you have truly disappointed me. Back then—”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow was not done speaking before she was interrupted by the short young man in the black coffin next to her."]},{"number":2643,"title":"Chapter 2643 Welcome, Lord Thearch!","paragraphs":["2643 Welcome, Lord Thearch!","“Falling Rainbow, what has happened has happened. We already settled that matter. Warbler Candle has also paid the price for that incident. Why are you still dragging it up? Moreover, we were the ones who she let down back then, not you.”","She waved her hand and swept away the hair that had fallen across her forehead before she walked out of the black coffin and asked First Page Crimson, “Crimson, How much longer will it be before Concubine Winding and Eye Shadow wake up? If they need more than two months, we can begin the plan now! After all, the dead world has already infected this world’s ley lines with enough death aura.”","First Page Crimson frowned under his black and red cloak and was silent for a moment before he said, “Seventh Page Concubine Winding will need 17 more days, while Eighth Page Eye Shadow will need 35 more days. I suggest you wait until they are awake before you combine the dead world with the main world. Otherwise, they will lose out on a lot of benefits.”","First Page Crimson had just finished speaking when Sixth Page Wave Glow, who had long hair resembling ice crystals and a more beautiful countenance than most women, said resolutely, “I don’t think we should begin the plan now. It doesn’t matter if the humans and sea clans know about our plans and set up defenses against it. It won’t affect the plan’s progression.","“I care more about what Crimson said about the humans taking control of the marsh and water worlds. If they can control the marsh world and water world, they will be able to control the alien insect, subterranean, and abyssal worlds, too!","“I am worried that humans will find a way to combine the five dimensional worlds with this world to promote this Class 1 to Class 2. If that happens, it will throw a wrench into our plans!”","Sixth Page Wave Glow’s words had hit the nail on the head.","First Page Crimson shook his head and said, “I can’t answer your question because I have also been sealed and recuperating in the black coffin. I haven’t been able to look in detail into human factions. But I can be certain that something anomalous has happened to the human world.","“Otherwise, given my understanding of the human world before I went to sleep, they shouldn’t have such capabilities! I suspect that this is related to Epoch God Palace. Only they possess such capabilities!","“As for Tarot Round Table, who have implanted spies into Tower Canon, they are nothing more than a group of noisy insects trying to cause trouble. They don’t have such capabilities either!”","Second Page Warbler Candle only looked away from Fifth Page Falling Rainbow now.","Second Page Warbler Candle looked at First Page Crimson seriously and said, “I began secretly watching Epoch God Palace a week ago. This matter is not related to them at all! They haven’t changed and still seem to be waiting for something. They wouldn’t have needed to wait until now if they wanted to try something. They could have acted when we first started injecting death aura into the ley lines.","“First Page Crimson, did Epoch God Palace frighten you off a thousand years ago?”","First Page Crimson ignored Second Page Warbler Candle.","Before the others awoke, First Page Crimson interacted with Second Page Warbler Candle because he had no choice.","But now that the others had awoken, there was no need for First Page Crimson to continue doing so!","First Page Crimson was not fond of Second Page Warbler Candle at all.","Third Page Violet Light Green did not want to interact with First Page Crimson and the other four. She picked up a comb with several eyeballs embedded into it and began combing her hair. The eyes opened and shut continuously while she was combing her hair with the comb.","Once she was done combing her hair, she began dressing herself up with accessories and was completely nonchalant towards the discussion that needed to take place.","When she saw Sixth Page Wave Glow looking at her, Third Page Violet Light Green said apathetically, “You can make the decision about such trivial matters. You don’t have to seek my opinion! This way, if you insist on starting the plan now, I won’t be left without a way to explain myself to Concubine Winding and Eye Shadow when they wake up.”","Eye Shadow was not the type to be petty. But if Concubine woke up and found out she had been stiffed, the situation would become very difficult to deal with!","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s selfish behavior had displeased many of them.","Third Page Violet Light Green and Sixth Page Wave Glow had both expressed their opinions. Second Page Warbler Candle never got involved and always followed Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s lead.","First Page Crimson looked at Fourth Page Cavity Orchid. “Cavity Orchid, have you made your decision?”","Fourth Page Cavity Orchid blinked. Given the circumstances, regardless of what she said, she would end up offending someone. Fourth Page Cavity Orchid did not want that to happen.","Hence, she smiled at First Page Crimson and said, “Crimson, I’ll follow your lead. Your decision is my decision! I have only just woken up, so unlike you, I don’t know much about what’s happening.”","First Page Crimson looked away from Fourth Page Cavity Orchid.","Fourth Page Cavity Orchid never liked to get on the wrong side of anyone, yet she also refused to allow herself to be advantaged in any way.","She had said that despite already knowing what his choice was.","If the eight of them had not tried tripping each other up and caused the sacred instrument that contained death aura to become damaged, they would not have needed to attempt to make a grab for Epoch God Palace’s vessel! They also would not have had to slumber for thousands of years.","If the dead spirits crisis could have been brought forward a few thousand years, this Class 1 world would have already been combined with the dead world and taken over the roots of this Class 1 world.","What a waste! A waste!","“Then let’s wait until Concubine Winding and Eye Shadow wake up. We can return to the black coffins and continue recuperating—”","Before First Page Crimson could finish speaking, he was interrupted by Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s furrowed brow.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow did not attempt to go against First Page Crimson’s decision. This decision had been made collectively by all of them. If she tried to go against it, she would be offending the majority.","However, she noticed that she had lost her link to the Secret of the Dead that had been within the Tower of Falling Rainbow.","“What is my Tower of Falling Rainbow now? Why can’t I sense the Secret of the Dead now that I’m awake?”","First Page Crimson frowned.","They only established Tower Canon after coming to this world. They saw the eight towers as part of their legacy and passed it down from generation to generation of the Eight Pages.","The subsequent generations of Tower Canon had been unable to use the power of the Secrets of the Dead in the towers.","Based on First Page Crimson’s understanding, the Tower of Falling Rainbow should be in Fifth Page Truth’s hands.","He had not known where Fifth Page Truth was and only found out from Third Page Eternal Sin that he had died.","But if Fifth Page Truth had died, the Secret of the Dead should have transported the Tower of Falling Rainbow back to Tower Canon!","The Secrets of the Dead were linked to the dead world’s roots, and the dead world was a dimensional world linked to a Class 2 world.","“Falling Rainbow, you can send people to find the Tower of Falling Rainbow, but I suggest you return to the black coffin to rest up. Once Concubine Winding and Eye Shadow wake up and we begin the plan, we will have to remain in the dead world and won’t have the opportunity to recuperate any further.”","Once he was done speaking, First Page Crimson entered the black coffin and closed the door.","Second Page Warbler Candle blew out the flame of the candle she held with a gentle breath before saying, “Falling Rainbow, I don’t need to spend any more extended periods of time recuperating. I can help you to search for the Tower of Falling Rainbow!”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow scoffed softly.","“I will send my own people to conduct the search! The people I send will also be able to help me gain an understanding of the current happenings in this world! Otherwise, we’ll have to ask First Page Crimson everything, and he’s unwilling to share.”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow walked out into the large hall, and Second Page Warbler Candle hurriedly followed her.","Third Page Violet Light Green and Sixth Page Wave Glow entered their black coffins. The light in the large hall filled the space once again after Second Page Warbler Candle left.","The faint light from the chain of birth horoscopes seeped out into the beautiful and dead silence.","...","Lin Yuan stepped on the jets of water.","Due to his mermaid thearch bloodline, Lin Yuan instinctively felt more comfortable in the sea than on land.","Lin Yuan had been busy for such a long time, and as he traveled on the sea, he felt the same carefreeness he felt while on vacation.","However, Lin Yuan found it difficult to relax fully.","Neither the humans nor sea clans’ migration was complete. Lin Yuan was afraid that he would predict the timeline wrongly.","Ice Flow told Lin Yuan, “We will be able to reach the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s palace in a day. I will lead you into the depths then while you hold this pearl. This comes from the 10,000-year-old giant clam and will allow you to breathe underwater.”","Lin Yuan received the pearl and nodded before tossing it back to Ice Flow. “I can enter the depths of water without external help. You don’t need to make such preparations for me.","“On the way here, I saw many sea clans gathering together under the lead of the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors. I am curious to know how the Vast Sea Labyrinth sends out your orders.”","Ice Flow did not try to keep secrets and responded. “When any member of the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors is given authority over a piece of the sea, they will also receive a messenger shell. No matter where they are, they can receive orders from the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors’ headquarters through the messenger shell.","“The Vast Sea Labyrinth just needs to send our orders to the leaders of the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors. After we selected the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors, they rapidly increased their numbers and strength because of the abundance of resources they possess.","“Now, there aren’t enough sea territories to allocate to every member. This is why there has been so much fighting among the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors in the past 1,000 years!","“First Emperor Dragon Shark Clan has already become the new fountainhead of the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors. Many human federations believe the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors to be the leaders of the sea clans. But in truth, they are nothing more than chess pieces that are under our control!”","Lin Yuan now understood why the Vast Sea Labyrinth cared so little about the First Emperor Dragon Shark Clan’s extinction. They never cared about any of the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors.","He could sense from Ice Flow’s words that the Vast Sea Labyrinth was very unhappy with all the fighting that had been going on among the Eight Clans of Sea Emperors.","The human federations were much more independent than the sea clans. They would never be able to act collectively after just one order was issued.","Although this Major Federation Union meeting was successful, many federations had not been in attendance. It was very likely that those who had not gone to the Radiance Federation were still unaware of the dead spirits crisis.","There was nothing that Lin Yuan or the Moon Empress could do about that.","By this time, Lin Yuan and Ice Flow had arrived at the sea near the Azure Federation.","The sea near the Azure Federation had already been cleared, and there were no traces of toxins left. This would not have been possible in such a short span with just the experts from the Azure Federation. The mermaids had helped secretly as well.","Suddenly, Ice Flow furrowed his brow deeply together, and he looked astonished. He noticed that there were almost 100 spirit-fire lifeforms nearby. Moreover, there were thousands of enormous sea beasts behind these 100 spirit-fire lifeforms.","From the auras of the sea beasts, they were likely water world dimensional lifeforms.","Ice Flow was very familiar with the aura of water world dimensional lifeforms.","Ice Flow knew that a Class 6 water world dimensional rift had opened in the sea near the Azure Federation. These dimensional lifeforms must have come out from there!","Ice Flow had heard that Lin Yuan had taken control of the water world and wanted to combine the water world with the main world so that the sea clans could be relocated there.","Ice Flow looked at Lin Yuan.","Regardless of how he thought about it, Ice Flow could not shake the feeling that these spirit-fire mermaids and giant sea beasts were there to cause trouble.","As a mermaid thearch, Lin Yuan could sense where lifeforms with the mermaid bloodlines were located.","He smiled and told Ice Flow, “These are the helpers I will be sending to help the sea clans with their migration. They have been waiting for me for a long time. They will be coming with us to the Vast Sea Labyrinth.”","While Lin Yuan was speaking, the mermaids and sea beasts had moved over to his side.","The king-class mermaids had ridden water currents to the surface of the water. But the instant they spotted Lin Yuan, they all folded their tails and knelt on pillars of water. They dared not meet his gaze and said softly, with utmost respect, “Welcome, Lord Thearch!”"]},{"number":2644,"title":"Chapter 2644 Contact with Tarot Round Table!","paragraphs":["2644 Contact with Tarot Round Table!","After the king-class mermaids were done with their greetings, it was the sea beasts’ turn to greet Lin Yuan.","Many of the sea beasts present had reached the Turning Wheel Realm as well. All of them knew that Lin Yuan had the mermaid bloodline in his body.","At first, the sea beasts from Mermaid Sacred Hall always butted heads with the mermaids. But now, they were very respectful toward mermaids of comparable power. Although they would not keep their heads down around the mermaids, they could get along relatively amicably.","The battle between Grace Sacred Hall and Mermaid Forbidden Sea was a fight between the mermaids and sea beasts. There were no mermaids in Grace Sacred Hall, while there were sea beasts in Mermaid Forbidden Sea. But those sea beasts had always been on friendly terms with the mermaids.","The sea beasts were all lined up neatly around the mermaids.","Because of Lin Yuan, the mermaids had become the leading species of the water world, and their status had naturally inflated.","Although Lin Yuan did not have the power to give the mermaids more authority than the sea clans, he knew what the mermaids and sea beasts were thinking.","The mermaids were much more united than the sea beasts, so allowing the mermaids to lead the water world would lead to more stability.","Moreover, it was true that Lin Yuan had the mermaid bloodline in his body and was a mermaid thearch.","When the mermaids appeared, shock appeared on Ice Flow’s face.","Mermaids also used to be in the main world, but their numbers were always very small.","However, mermaids were naturally affiliated with water-elemental energy and known for being extremely beautiful in their human form. Thus, they used to be regarded as auspicious entities in the sea.","Mermaids could not be found in Class 1 to 4 water world dimensional rifts and were only seen occasionally in Class 5 dimensional rifts.","Ice Flow knew that the mermaids came from the water world, but they never expected them to be such a populous species in the water world and so powerful!","The mermaids and sea beasts addressed Lin Yuan as ‘Lord Thearch’.","Ice Flow knew that the mermaids prioritized their bloodlines.","The way that they addressed Lin Yuan caused Ice Flow to realize that Lin Yuan’s strong control over water came from him having the mermaid bloodline in his body!","His bloodline was strong enough to induce the sea beasts to kneel to him. This was sufficient to prove that his bloodline was extraordinary!","Ice Flow now knew that it was not the Radiance Federation who had taken control of the water world but the Moon Empress’ disciple!","Given that the Moon Empress’ disciple had the ability to take control of the water world, he had to also be the one who had taken control of the Moon Empress’ disciple.","At this instant, the way that Ice Flow looked at Lin Yuan changed. Now, he fully believed all that Lin Yuan had said before. Aside from astonishment and satisfaction, he also felt brimming faith.","Ice Flow bowed deeply to Lin Yuan. “With help from these mermaids and sea beasts, the migration of the sea clans will undoubtedly be much smoother! Lin Yuan, thank you for your help! We will remember this favor and be sure to repay it!","“In a previous conversation with the Moon Empress, she mentioned faith power. Unless I’m mistaken, I believe that she was trying to gather it for you! If that’s the case, I will dedicate all of the sea clans’ faith to you! We three brothers will also become your believers!”","Ice Flow was not trying to be polite to Lin Yuan. If that was his intention, it would not have been necessary to say what he just said.","Lin Yuan could tell that Ice Flow was sincere because once he was done speaking, Lin Yuan could sense that a glowing dot of light that represented Ice Flow’s faith had appeared in the fountain of faith in his divine kingdom. This meant Ice Flow was now linked to him and supplying him with faith!","Lin Yuan smiled.","He did not have to make any requests of Ice Flow, and the latter had said all that he said of his own accord. This caused Lin Yuan to have a good impression of Ice Flow, and by extension, the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","It was true that Lin Yuan needed faith power. But he had not expected the Moon Empress to have helped him to lay the groundwork with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","The Moon Empress had always looked out for and took very good care of him.","Lin Yuan told Ice Flow, “I do need faith power. We’ll do as you said. But every matter is separate. I’m not helping the sea clans because I’m after your faith. In this matter, you are the ones helping me. I will not allow you to help me for free!","“I have a significant amount of pure spirit qi and water-elemental energy. I can help the sea clans to reach the full extent of their power by evolving the sea beasts’ grades and qualities. But I will need a portion of the sea beasts’ World Graces. It will amount to 3-4% of their World Graces. This will not affect your feys in any way. This promise will stand for as long as I am in the main world. What do you think?”","Ice Flow was listening intently to what Lin Yuan said, but he thought that Lin Yuan would seek compensation for helping the sea clans. Yet, it turned out that Lin Yuan would be providing the sea clans with such immense benefits!","Ice Flow was stumped and at a momentary loss for words!","Human factions needed resources, but the fey factions that made up sea clans lacked Creation Master resources even more than human factions did!","Although some powerful feys possessed similar abilities to Creation Masters, it was much easier for humans to become Class 5 Creation Masters than feys!","Fey factions possessed extremely little Class 5 Creation Master resources as human Creation Masters usually served federations, and they almost never released their Creation Master resources to others. It was challenging for human federations to share their Creation Master resources with each other, much less with feys!","Fey factions used to want to trade for resources with human Creation Masters, but the humans had asked for remuneration that the feys could not pay. This was because the humans tried to trade for a mountain of spiritual ingredients from the feys, most of which came from the feys’ own bodies.","The feys found it difficult to strip the corpses of their ancestors to trade for the human Creation Masters’ potions. This was in spite of the fact that the fey factions’ own Creation Masters did not concoct their potions.","However, the feelings that came with their own kind doing this and human Creation Masters doing this were completely different!","Numerous sea clans were stuck at a certain level.","If these sea clans’ experts could all increase their power, the sea clans’ overall power would increase by at least five times its current level!","The sea clans were made of fey factions, and their experts lived for much longer than humans did.","With such long lifespans, fey powers could reach a rut at any point in their lives. Most of them would stay in the rut for their entire lives!","Ice Flow did not know how many resources Lin Yuan had that enabled him to make such a promise.","But since Lin Yuan had made such a promise, he would definitely have the capabilities to back it up!","This was a good opportunity for the sea clans to rise up.","Ice Flow did not bother to stand on ceremony with Lin Yuan and hurriedly said, “Lin Yuan, I don’t know how to thank you. You are the savior of all the sea clans! You mentioned wanting 3-4% of the World Graces and Creation World Ley Lines. Even if you ask for 20%, 30%, to 80%, the sea clans would be willing to give it to you!","“I will go and make the arrangements now and prepare a name list of the sea clans for you.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","If a member of any human faction was present, they would not understand the promise that Lin Yuan had made. From anyone else’s perspective, it seemed as though he was doing nothing more than tossing away resources!","But in actuality, he was accumulating his own store of resources.","Lin Yuan’s mention of him being in the main world allowed Ice Flow to understand that Lin Yuan’s goals were beyond the main world and that he intended to leave.","Ice Flow thought of himself as the strongest leader in the main world when, in fact, he was nothing more than an ignoramus!","Ice Flow suddenly felt as though he had been defeated by youth.","At the same time, he began wondering about Lin Yuan’s identity. All of a sudden, he questioned whether Lin Yuan was human. But how could he have the mermaid bloodline in his body if he was?","Lin Yuan could not be more than 20 years old. This made him a young man by human standards. But by fey standards, he was a baby!","Ice Flow had many questions, but he did not ask Lin Yuan any of them.","Instead, he began thinking about how he could tell his brothers about this.","His brothers would not have any issues with him giving Lin Yuan the faith of all the sea clans, even if Lin Yuan had not promised them anything in return, much less now that he was going to be substantially benefiting the sea clans.","The members of sea clans were all terror-stricken by the dead spirits crisis.","If Ice Flow announced this good news, morale would pick up rapidly.","Now that Lin Yuan had come to an agreement on this matter with Ice Flow, he was overjoyed.","He knew that it would be easier to collect spirit qi crystals from the sea clans than the humans.","Due to the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s characteristics, Lin Yuan could still increase its power with spirit qi crystals, although it had already reached the World Emperor and divine kingdom level.","On this trip to the Vast Sea Labyrinth, Lin Yuan wanted to establish a good relationship with the sea clans so that they would be able to work well with the humans to take on the dead spirits crisis. But his other purpose was to seal this deal with the sea clans.","Everything was going very well, and it could be said that Lin Yuan’s trip to the Vast Sea Labyrinth was complete.","He had not given Ice Wave and Ice Clarity the chance to meet with him during this trip, and he dove into helping the sea clans.","Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity were very thankful for this.","The three of them should have welcomed Lin Yuan with the proper etiquette, but they knew that every moment wasted would cost the lives of millions of sea lifeforms.","From the fact that Lin Yuan had not bothered to ask about it either it meant that he genuinely wanted to help the sea clans and did not have any selfish desires.","Before they were done feeling touched, Ice Wave and Ice Clarity heard of Lin Yuan’s promises from Ice Flow.","Ice Wave and Ice Clarity had to digest for a moment before they accepted this fact.","The two of them already saw Lin Yuan as the sea clans’ savior. But now, it seemed that he was also their lucky charm!","Because of him, the sea clans would be able to prosper.","If Lin Yuan was just a regular human, Ice Wave and Ice Clarity would have begun suspecting his motives when they heard this news.","But everything made sense when they found out about Lin Yuan having the mermaid bloodline in his body.","Lin Yuan was aware that humans and the sea clans never got along. This was because the humans were always fishing for feys from the sea. The humans might see nothing wrong with this, but it was no different from murder to the sea clans.","The sea clans only worked with the humans because they had no choice. They would never have made such a compromise if they had any other choice.","Ice Flow, Ice Clarity, and Ice Wave had expressly emphasized Lin Yuan’s saving of the sea clans during the migration of the sea clans. This was to encourage all members of the sea clans to dedicate their faith to Lin Yuan.","As the rulers of the sea, Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity possessed absolute authority.","The order from the three of them and the fact that he had saved all the sea clans allowed Lin Yuan to garner a large amount of faith power from the sea clans.","Lin Yuan spent almost 20 days in the Vast Sea Labyrinth. Once the last batch of sea clans were sent away, Lin Yuan did not allow Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity to meet with him before he used Node Transportation to transport himself to the Radiance Federation.","Now that the sea clans’ migration was done, Lin Yuan had achieved his goal.","After checking the time, he estimated that Wen Yu was done with her exploration of the other side of the Barren Sea. It was time for him to fetch her and Chu Ci!","Once he was done fetching Chu Ci and Wen Yu, the migration of the human federations to the Radiance Federation should also be complete.","Lin Yuan would then combine the main world with the five dimensional worlds with the Radiance Federation at the center!","The main world would be promoted from a Class 1 to Class 2 world before the dead spirits crisis even began.","Lin Yuan had remained in contact with the Moon Empress and Wen Yu the entire time while he was in the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","He knew that a faction called Tarot Round Table had come to the Radiance Federation and asked to work with the Radiance Federation.","They said that they knew many secrets about Tower Canon.","The Moon Empress should have agreed to their request. However, they were being rather overbearing.","She could not agree to Tarot Round Table’s request, so she told Lin Yuan about the situation and let him make the decision once he was back!"]},{"number":2645,"title":"Chapter 2645 Lin Yuan’s Deadly Aura!","paragraphs":["2645 Lin Yuan’s Deadly Aura!","Lin Yuan always felt that even if a person did not know how to be sensitive to changing times, they should know not to cross the line.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth was doing a very good job now.","Initially, they compromised on their profits as a show of sincerity to the Radiance Federation. This allowed them to gain Lin Yuan’s wholehearted willingness to save them.","Otherwise, even if Lin Yuan was still willing to help the sea chains with their problem, he would not have put in as much effort. He also would not have sent the 100 water Turning Wheel Realm Dictators and 1,000 regular Dictators to help the sea clans migrate.","Lin Yuan’s action allowed the water experts and the Vast Sea Labyrinth to become acquainted sooner than they would have. This would enable them to work together even better in the future.","Although all of Lin Yuan’s decisions were geared toward achieving a win-win situation, he had actually allowed the Vast Sea Labyrinth to obtain incomparable benefits.","Because of Lin Yuan’s promise, the sea clans’ top combat power would be increased by at least 50%!","Lin Yuan liked a faction like this that knew how to be flexible, was rational, and knew where the lines were.","Lin Yuan felt no inclination to help the federations who had received the Radiance Federation’s invitation but were unwilling to attend the Major Federation Union meeting.","He had heard of Tarot Round Table from Eighth Page Apoptosis.","He did not have a good feeling about this secret human faction that was composed of tens of top experts.","Tarot Round Table had been investigating Tower Canon all this time and clearly knew many of their secrets. Yet, they had not done anything and, in a way, allowed Tower Canon to infect the main world’s ley lines with death aura.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth had previously worked with Tower Canon, but this did not color Lin Yuan’s opinion of the Vast Sea Labyrinth or cause him to become angry at them.","Firstly, the Vast Sea Labyrinth had been unaware of Tower Canon’s plan. Lin Yuan understood Ice Flow, Ice Wave, and Ice Clarity. If they knew Tower Canon aimed to extract the death aura, unleash the dead spirits crisis, and trigger the changing of epochs, they’d have refused to cooperate and tried to stop it.","But based on what Tarot Round Table had told the Moon Empress, Lin Yuan knew they had been aware of Tower Canon’s plan. However, all they did was continue watching silently as they tried to gather even more information to continue working toward their goals.","Lin Yuan did not know what Tarot Round Table’s goals were, but it was a fact they had consciously remained on the sidelines. This meant they truly did not care about the survival of the main world’s lifeforms.","Thus, the Radiance Federation would take a completely different attitude toward Tarot Round Table than they did with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Lin Yuan felt that it was reasonable for the Azure Federation to have remained neutral between the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation. After all, they needed to look out for their own profits.","But safeguarding one’s profits was not a good enough reason for remaining on the sidelines in every situation!","Lin Yuan already felt extreme displeasure toward Tarot Round Table.","But Tarot Round Table had not made contact with the Radiance Federation because they wanted to help in the war against the dead spirits but to negotiate with them.","Tarot Round Table had already stated their conditions. This was their price for telling Lin Yuan everything they knew about Tower Canon.","It seemed that Tarot Round Table was a mercenary group greedily trying to secure their benefits in a mad frenzy now that they sensed imminent danger!","The Moon Empress believed that if Tarot Round Table had three spirit-fire experts, six birth-horoscope experts, and more than ten Above Eternal experts, agreeing to their requests might not be a bad idea!","Tarot Round Table possessed almost equivalent top combat power to all three major federations combined!","It would not be unreasonable for them to occupy 20% of the leadership positions in the Major Federation Union.","However, the Moon Empress did not want to hand over the policymaking authority to them. They would have the final say in most proposals if she did that.","The three major federations and other federations with Class 5 Creation Masters would all occupy leadership positions in the Major Federation Union. This was a sealed deal.","The Azure Federation was in alliance with the Radiance Federation but had not become fully subordinate to them. On the other hand, the Freedom Federation could be considered a branch of the Radiance Federation.","The other factions were unaware that the Freedom Federation’s royalty had already sworn their loyalty to the Moon Empress. There was no way that the Freedom Federation would reveal this voluntarily.","Thus, regardless of what happened, the Radiance Federation would occupy more leadership positions than Tarot Round Table.","While the Moon Empress was discussing with Lin Yuan, she took a grudgeful tone toward Tarot Round Table. Regardless of how strong Tarot Round Table was, the Moon Empress did not like how conniving they were.","It was likely that the Tarot experts had lost their humanity to the passage of time.","Lin Yuan chuckled coldly. There was no way he would be sharing even a shred of the policymaking authority with Tarot Round Table. They did not deserve it!","If Tarot Round Table could be content with just 20% of the leadership positions and did not insist on having policymaking authority—and if they were willing to invest their full sincerity into helping with the defense against the dead spirits crisis by assigning their experts to help the weaker federations with any abrupt dangers that cropped up—Lin Yuan could force himself to have a conversation with them.","But if they continued to be this greedy or came up with more unreasonable requests, Lin Yuan would not be opposed to teaching them a lesson.","Lin Yuan rarely used martial force against others, but this did not mean he was fully against this method.","While rushing back to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan used up his spirit qi numerous times. The journey left him dusty, but traveling using Node Transportation was much faster than other modes of transport.","Once he entered the inner palace of the Radiant Moon Palace, he saw the Moon Empress sitting there with an austere expression. Her brows knitted tightly together.","Lin Yuan walked briskly over to the Moon Empress and asked softly, “Master, has something gone wrong with Tarot Round Table, or have they made an unsavory request?”","The Moon Empress had not expected Lin Yuan to arrive so quickly.","In the past, she would not have discussed issues with him. But she had no choice but to tell him about the issues related to Tarot Round Table so that he could solve them.","Even the Spacetime Elder would seem weak when he faced the Tarot experts. Lin Yuan was the only one who could stand toe-to-toe with them.","The Moon Empress rarely encountered people as arrogant as the Tarot experts.","The Leaning Moon Mountain had a total of two main palaces. The Moon Empress usually lived in the Radiant Moon Palace and met with other members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty in the Radiant Moon Palace as well.","The Four Moon Servants only used the Resting Moon Palace when they returned with their teams. Night Leaning Moon occasionally stayed there, too.","The Moon Empress only allowed the people closest to her to use the Resting Moon Palace and would never have allowed the people from Tarot Round Table to stay there of her own volition.","Given that the people from Tarot Round Table still ended up staying there in spite of the Moon Empress’ unwillingness, the reason was obvious without being explicitly said.","Lin Yuan laughed coldly and asked softly, “Master, are the people from Tarot Round Table making things difficult for you?”","Lin Yuan’s voice was laced with lethal intention.","The Moon Empress was stunned by what Lin Yuan said. It sounded as though he wanted to stand up for her.","The Moon Empress could not remember the last time she felt this way. Perhaps that old fellow had stood up for her when she first became his disciple.","However, he had been an alcoholic and was only sober a few times a year. He had died by the time she became a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. He had not even been around to see her become a Radiance Envoy.","The Moon Empress smiled and said, “Little Yuan, the people from Tarot Round Table did not make things difficult for me. It’s not so easy to push me into a corner. They insisted on staying on the Leaning Moon Mountain. I’m sure you can understand that this is one of their ways of demonstrating their formidability.","“They also wanted me to call you back as soon as possible. They have not only been looking into Tower Canon but have also investigated a fair amount of the Radiance Federation’s recent happenings. They have likely obtained information about you. I don’t know the exact intel they have on you, but they see it as their bargaining chip.","“Little Yuan, if they cross the line in your interaction with them, you don’t have to force yourself to suffer for the sake of helping the main world with its disaster. They don’t have experts who are above the spirit-fire level!”","The Moon Empress should not have said that, as it went against her status. But simultaneously, she was worried about Lin Yuan and did not want him to suffer.","She could already see how greedy they were. If Lin Yuan kept giving way during the negotiation with Tarot Round Table, they would just end up climbing all over him.","Lin Yuan stood up. “Master, I will go and meet with Tarot Round Table! I really want to know what intel they have on me!”","A year ago, if such a powerful faction had obtained information about Lin Yuan, he would have been worried regardless of how important the information was.","Being targeted by a powerful faction like Tarot Round Table would undoubtedly have caused a lot of trouble for him.","Back then, Lin Yuan’s secret weapons were insufficient to deal with Tarot Round Table.","But now, the Abyss Great Emperor and Eternal Source would both be able to easily keep the four spirit-fire Tarot experts in check.","In Lin Yuan’s eyes, Tarot Round Table was nothing more than meat on a chopping board. Although the meat was rather tough, cutting through would not be impossible.","Lin Yuan was curious to know what information Tarot Round Table knew about him that they believed would be enough to keep him under their thumb!","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was certain that Tarot Round Table did not know too much key information about him. Otherwise, they would not have been foolish enough to have the confidence to come to try to negotiate with him!","Tarot Round Table might seem powerful to others, but they were nothing more than a replaceable garnish to Lin Yuan. He had not considered them when he first started coming up with his plan to protect the main world and had still successfully carried out his plan.","The people from Tarot Round Table were trying to refrain from exerting any effort and take control of him. Even if they were willing to help out in the war against the humans, they would never listen to his instructions.","Red Thorn had only just evolved to Diamond grade. It happened to need assets to use Tongue Pouch Births Demons on.","Lin Yuan thought, Tarot Round Table should hope that they do not give me the chance to obtain assets for Red Thorn!","The Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan seriously while he was speaking as she tried to discern from his gaze if he was trying to console her.","She saw that his gaze was very level and that his deadly aura had not diminished at all after hearing about Tarot Round Table’s intentions. Instead, it had intensified.","The Moon Empress was confident that Lin Yuan had the power to handle Tarot Round Table and was not worried about them.","“Little Yuan, go ahead and do what you need to do. Don’t forget to prioritize your own safety at all times. The spirit-fire Tarot experts have definitely contracted sacred source lifeforms and all of them have different abilities. Take everything seriously, and never be careless!”","The Moon Empress was not the emotional type and hated such people.","But at that moment, when Lin Yuan was about to head to the Resting Moon Palace to meet the Tarot experts, she ended up becoming such a person.","She was just too worried about Lin Yuan’s safety.","But she knew that if he really ended up clashing against the Tarot experts, she would not be of any help to him because she had yet to set her spirit fire alight. She might even become an inconvenience to him.","Otherwise, she would definitely have gone with him so she could hear the information firsthand!","Lin Yuan nodded seriously when he heard what the Moon Empress said. He made sure to make mental notes of everything that she said.","This was because he knew that the Moon Empress had his best interests at heart and because she had more experience than him.","The Moon Empress’ advice was also her way of imparting experience to him.","However, Lin Yuan truly was not overly concerned about the Tarot experts.","The Tarot experts only had the equivalent power of the subterranean world’s top combat power. They also did not have as many Above Eternal experts, who were the equivalent of Samsara Realm Dictators.","Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor were not the only weapons in Lin Yuan’s arsenal.","When Lin Yuan fused with the Abyss Red Lotus in the past, he was already able to suppress all the abyssal Samsara Realm Dictators."]},{"number":2646,"title":"Chapter 2646 You Don’t Deserve to Be Threatened By Us!","paragraphs":["2646 You Don’t Deserve to Be Threatened By Us!","At that time, the Abyss Red Lotus had only taken control of three dimensional worlds. But now that he had taken control of five, Lin Yuan would be even stronger after fusing with it!","Lin Yuan said, “Master, don’t worry. I will be back very soon!”","Before leaving the inner palace, Lin Yuan released the Abyss Great Emperor, who Red Thorn’s tongue pouch was transforming.","He did not give the Moon Empress time to respond before he transported himself to the Resting Moon Palace’s entrance.","As the Moon Empress looked at the Abyss Great Emperor, tears started welling up uncontrollably in her eyes.","It went without saying she knew what Lin Yuan’s intention was. He had left this abyss demon with powers above the spirit-fire level here to protect her.","In actuality, he was already intending to burn all bridges with Tarot Round Table.","However, Tarot Round Table had four spirit-fire experts, and Lin Yuan was afraid they would come to the Radiance Moon Palace to harm her while he was battling it out with Tarot Round Table.","From the way that Lin Yuan chose to leave one of his experts with her during such a crucial time, the Moon Empress could tell how much he cared about her. This affection could not be communicated through words. It could only be expressed through actions!","At first, the Moon Empress did not intend to head to the Resting Moon Palace as she feared she would inconvenience Lin Yuan. But now, she decided to take this abyss demon with her as she headed to the Resting Moon Palace’s entrance.","This way, she and this abyss demon could step in immediately if any issues erupted!","Now that she had taken control of six moons, the power that Forage Moon afforded her already went beyond the birth-horoscope level, allowing her to take on spirit-fire experts. She was not being overconfident about her powers as the Spacetime Elder had made this judgment.","Once Lin Yuan arrived at the Resting Moon Palace’s entrance, he released Eternal Source and sauntered into the Resting Moon Palace.","The Leaning Moon Mountain was his home, and the Resting Moon Palace was a part of it. There was no need for him to be mindful of others in his own home!","The Tarot experts already saw themselves as invaluable assets and had demanded to stay in Resting Moon Palace.","However, Lin Yuan never thought much of these Tarot experts.","Once he entered the palace, a shrill voice echoed. “Are the Moon Empress’ servants so ill-mannered? How dare you enter the residence of a valued guest without permission?”","Lin Yuan was so enraged that he started to laugh.","Lin Yuan did not get angry often, and he was only angered to the point of laughing a few times a year!","“The mistress is the one who decides if the guest is a valued one. This is the first time I’m hearing a guest make that determination on their own! Didn’t you insist on staying in the Resting Moon Palace because you were waiting for me?”","If Eternal Source revealed such overwhelming power from the get-go, the Tarot experts would change their plans out of fear of Eternal Source’s power.","After Lin Yuan was done speaking, the female voice did not respond. However, an elderly male voice wafted out from the Resting Moon Palace’s inner palace. “What’s wrong? Doesn’t the Radiance Federation see Tarot Round Table as valued guests?","“The Radiance Federation couldn’t stop us even if we wanted to enter your imperial court! The Radiance Federation should take it as a sign of our greatest respect that we’re willing to stay in the Resting Moon Palace!","“Since you’re here, come in. The Resting Moon Palace is a rather pretty place, but the beverages are lacking. The Moon Empress sure doesn’t know how to treat her guests. She didn’t even serve us the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar!”","The elderly man’s voice was relaxed and casual. It was a stark contrast from the girl’s piercing screech.","But when Lin Yuan heard this elderly man’s voice, the deadly aura in his gaze intensified.","The imperial court was prohibited territory to any federation. No one could enter it without an invitation!","Despite regarding the Vast Sea Labyrinth as their most treasured collaborator, the Radiance Federation had only arranged to meet with their three rulers in a small palace situated away from the central area. They had not been allowed to set foot into the main palace!","Yet, this old man not only had the gall to say he wanted to enter the Radiance Federation’s imperial court but also said there was nothing that the federation could do to stop him!","Evidently, he looked down on the Radiance Federation and saw them as insignificant bugs!","If Lin Yuan had the capabilities to restrain such arrogant characters, he could dismiss them as having bad attitudes. But if Lin Yuan was unable to restrain this person and the Radiance Federation did something that displeased Tarot Round Table, their next step would be to threaten the Radiance Federation’s imperial court!","Lin Yuan would not brush off this elderly man’s words as empty threats, as Tarot Round Table had a reputation for such behavior!","Their forceful entry into the Resting Moon Palace was a warning to the Radiance Federation.","Since Tarot Round Table was harboring such thoughts, they were nothing more than a ticking bomb in relation to the Radiance Federation.","The Moon Empress had made a sacrifice for the Radiance Federation’s sake by allowing them to stay in the Resting Moon Palace. Yet, they complained about the beverages she served and wanted to drink the Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar.","Lin Yuan could not be bothered to waste words on these people. He did not respond to what the elderly man had said and asked, “I heard that you have come into possession of a significant amount of information about me. Just what is this information about?","“Since we’re here to negotiate, let’s get right to it! The Radiance Federation established the Major Federation Union intending to save all humans. We have been continuously sharing our resources with others and with no selfish intent. I’m sure Tarot Round Table has learned of this during your investigations!","“I don’t care what you’re trying to achieve by occupying the leadership positions in the Major Federation Union, but regardless, you should tell the Radiance Federation about Tower Canon to make our own preparations!”","Lin Yuan did not want to continue speaking with Tarot Round Table.","If they could not help Lin Yuan understand Tower Canon, he would have already seized control of and begun grilling this ticking time bomb!","Lin Yuan would not need to be present to interrogate Tarot Round Table as Eternal Source could do it in his place.","With the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, Lin Yuan could ensure he would receive the answers he sought. But doing so would only waste more time.","Since the Tarot experts believed that he was in the palm of their hands, they would not have set up any defenses against him.","Thus, it would probably be easy for him to obtain information from them!","Lin Yuan’s lips twitched.","Not only were Tarot Round Table scheming after authority in the Major Federation Union, but they were also trying to control him and turn him into their puppet!","“Since you want me to serve you, I need to ask two questions. Once you answer them, it will give me a proper understanding of Tarot Round Table.”","The elderly man spoke again. “It looks like you’re easier to communicate with than we expected! Ask away. As long as it doesn’t encroach into Tarot Round Table’s key secrets, we can share some information with you!”","Lin Yuan immediately said, “I have already asked my first question, but you didn’t answer me. I am curious to find out what secrets you know about me and what you plan on using to threaten m—”","A sharp voice interrupted Lin Yuan. “You don’t deserve to be threatened by us! We are well aware of your sister’s situation. You are also on good terms with Chef Supreme’s daughter and son-in-law.","“You were most likely only able to increase your power so quickly because of your sacred source lifeform. Your power only skyrocketed when you left the Radiance Federation for the Startling Lines Continent.","“Due to an unknown reason, you managed to obtain the mermaid mermaid bloodline and absorbed it into your body. You used your mermaid bloodline to convince the Freedom Federation’s Goddess of Mercy to collude with you.","“Your Path Protector has deep ties with the Heavenly Family Cottage and used secret means to kill Fifth Page Truth in the Startling Lines Continent. This is just a portion of what we know about you. You have no secrets we don’t know about!”","Lin Yuan relaxed. He had been concerned about what secrets Tarot Round Table knew about him!","It was true that their investigation into him had been very thorough. They had found out about many key points in his journey of growth.","Unfortunately, they still had no clue about his biggest secret, Morbius. It seemed he had done a good job of hiding it!","Although it seemed as though they had investigated him fully, they had only scratched the surface.","This caused Lin Yuan to lose interest in the information that Tarot Round Table knew about Tower Canon.","Furthermore, they had crossed his line.","Tarot Round Table first mentioned Chu Ci, Uncle Li, and Auntie Zhang because they wanted to hit his weaknesses. They wanted him to know that if he did not agree to their request, Chu Ci, Uncle Li, and Auntie Zhang would end up suffering or losing their lives.","After asking his first question, Lin Yuan suppressed his angry urges and asked, “What do you know about Tower Canon? I don’t think you need to leverage any information you know about Tower Canon. The humans have already done all we can to defend against Tower Canon. There isn’t anything else we can do to improve.”","Lin Yuan’s words caused the inner palace to fall silent momentarily.","The shrill female voice that Lin Yuan first heard when he entered screeched. “Tarot Round Table spent a lot of effort investigating Tower Canon. If the Radiance Federation wants to know about them, you must pay us!","“The Radiance Federation will not be getting any information from us so easily! Even if we are given spots in the Major Federation Union’s leadership, the Major Federation Union will have to purchase or trade information from us!","“We sent our people posing as the Eight Pages to infiltrate Tower Canon. You can’t even imagine the full extent of what we know!”","Tarot Round Table finally broke the last strand of interest that was keeping Lin Yuan involved in this conversation.","Tarot Round Table had sent someone posing as the Eight Pages to infiltrate Tower Canon? This meant they would have the same status as Eighth Page Apoptosis. Hence, they probably only knew as much as he did.","Moreover, Lin Yuan could already guess which of the Eight Pages had been moles.","Eighth Page Apoptosis had fled with Seventh Page War and Third Page Eternal Sin.","Seventh Page War was a unique plant-type fey. If she had joined Tower Canon to find out more about their secrets, she would not have left to conquer the Dark Continent!","This meant that Tarot Round Table’s mole had to be Third Page Eternal Sin!","By now, Lin Yuan had arrived at the inner palace. As he swept his gaze across the 30-odd people, it eventually landed on a familiar figure.","The Spirit Mother was a member of Tarot Round Table. Lin Yuan had not seen this coming at all!","Based on Eighth Page Apoptosis’ description of Third Page Eternal Sin, the short-haired girl looking at him with amused interest had to be Third Page Eternal Sin!","Lin Yuan did not have the best impression of the Spirit Mother, but it was not bad either.","He asked the Spirit Mother, “Your Excellency, instead of staying with the Spirit Mother Federation and helping with its migration, you’re here trying to grab one of the Major Federation Union’s leadership positions. Normally, your status as a Class 5 Creation Master would have already guaranteed you a seat.","“Your Excellency, I would like to ask if you’re representing Tarot Round Table and residing in the Resting Moon Palace signifies that your profit will be tied to that of Tarot Round Table from now on?”","The Spirit Mother had not expected to be called out by Lin Yuan or to even be remembered by him.","The Spirit Mother had no idea what Lin Yuan looked like, but he had been astounded by Lin Yuan’s growth journey.","Lin Yuan’s growth journey reminded him of Bu Po.","Lin Yuan had asked the Spirit Mother this because he had previously spoken with the Spirit Mother and knew he cared for the Spirit Mother Federation.","Lin Yuan also wanted to give the Spirit Mother a chance. But it seemed that the Spirit Mother could not understand his meaning and looked at him curiously.","“I am indeed the Spirit Mother, but I am also a Tarot member. Naturally, I will stick by them no matter what happens. Since you know who I am, let me introduce you to the rest!”","Lin Yuan snarled coldly, “There’s no need for introductions. I’m not interested in getting to know a bunch of people who are headed for death!”","The moment he spoke, a familiar aura that even terrified Eternal Source burst out from Lin Yuan.","Previously, Lin Yuan was unable to fully control his aura when he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus. But now, he could completely control his aura and restrict it to the inner palace!"]},{"number":2647,"title":"Chapter 2647 Lin Yuan Gets Violent With a Girl!","paragraphs":["2647 Lin Yuan Gets Violent With a Girl!","Lin Yuan was pleasantly surprised by this ability to restrain his aura.","Normally, he did not have many opportunities to use the abilities that came with fusing with the Abyss Red Lotus. Thus, each chance he got was an opportunity for him to test and learn more about his capabilities.","When he first fused with the Abyss Red Lotus, his terrifying power had been felt in every corner of the subterranean world He had felt rather embarrassed by this.","Since he could not control his aura when he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus, his location would be exposed immediately once he used his power against Tower Canon.","But now, this issue had been perfectly addressed.","Two minutes ago, the people from Tarot Round Table saw Lin Yuan as merely easy pickings. But now, the tables had turned and he was the strong hunter that could kill the prey that was the experts from Tarot Round Table with one swipe of his claw.","Lin Yuan’s aura caused the experts from Tarot Round Table to freeze. But almost immediately, their faces morphed into astonished bewilderment!","Lin Yuan’s aura exceeded the comprehension of all the experts from Tarot Round Table!","Now that Lin Yuan wielded the might of the five dimensional worlds, if he was measured against Eternal Source, his power would be beyond the Afterlife Realm.","His power likely exceeded the World Emperor grade and reached an unprecedented level!","This was power that the experts from Tarot Round Table could only behold. They could never have imagined that it truly existed!","This was akin to a Myth Breed fey seeing itself as outstanding and constantly paraded around Fantasy Breed feys. But now, it was suddenly encountering an Immortal Breed fey and was receiving a shock to its system.","The experts from Tarot Round Table were all silent.","Lin Yuan had already used the Abyss Red Lotus’ black roots to capture all the experts from Tarot Round Table.","Lin Yuan hissed to the Spirit Mother, “On account of Bu Po, my impression of you isn’t completely bad and I was willing to give you a chance. But you chose to let that chance go. So you have no one to blame but yourself!”","Just as Lin Yuan was about to instruct the Abyss Red Lotus to use its roots to strike, the elderly voice rang out again.","But this time, his voice had lost all of its previous composure and was solely filled with panic.","“Without Tarot Round Table, the Radiance Federation and Major Federation Union’s plan to take on Tower Canon will be doomed to fail! Don’t assume that Vast Sea Labyrinth will be willing to help you wholeheartedly just because you’re working together! Such kindness doesn’t exist in this world! If the humans could coexist with the sea clans, there wouldn’t be federations that are unable to share their cultures because they lack Island Whales!”","The elderly man’s words made sense and Lin Yuan could not find anything wrong with it.","However, the elderly man only said this because he was not aware of the power that Lin Yuan possessed or that he intended to fuse the five dimensional worlds with the main world. The dimensional worlds from the five dimensional worlds would all contribute their strength towards defending the dead spirits crisis.","Lin Yuan was not the type to believe the promises of others easily. If he was, he would have either succumbed to an evil plot some time ago or be constantly bullied.","But in fact, he rarely experienced drawbacks during his journey of growth.","Lin Yuan’s relationship with Vast Sea Labyrinth was not based on trade. He was saving them. So, Vast Sea Labyrinth would definitely do their best to work with the humans and tackle the dead spirits crisis.","Lin Yuan had the power to control all of the sea clans.If any of them had straying thoughts, all he needed to do was weed them out.","Those who knew Lin Yuan saw him as the kind of person who preferred to keep a low profile. But in actuality, he was just cautious and preferred to keep his power and background a secret.","This was because previously, he did not believe that he possessed power that warranted showing off. But now that he did, the way he carried himself during his activities had significantly changed.","“What you said is correct based on what you know. But you have no idea that your corpse might become useful in defending against the dead spirits crisis.”","Lin Yuan looked up at the girl whose eyes shimmered intermittently and asked, “You must be Third Page Eternal Sin, right?”","Lin Yuan’s words sent a shiver running up Third Page Eternal Sin’s body.","If Eighth Page Apoptosis saw this, he would definitely suspect that this was not the real Third Page Eternal Sin.","When a lifeform encountered a power beyond its comprehension in its world, its world would quickly collapse and it would devolve into a state of fright.","Lin Yuan’s words made Third Page Eternal Sin feel as though she had found the string of hope she could cling to for survival.","She was the spy that Tarot Round Table had sent to infiltrate Tower Canon and she knew a fair amount about them. In the eyes of both the Radiance Federation and humans, she posed significant value. If she used what she knew about Tower Canon as a bargaining chip, she should be able to ensure her survival.","With this thought, Third Page Eternal Sin hastily nodded.","When he saw Third Page Eternal Sin nod, Lin Yuan said seriously, “I will ask you a few questions. Remember not to lie to me! I’m sure you are aware of what the consequences will be if I find out that you lied!”","Lin Yuan spread the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores on Third Page Eternal Sin’s body.","He covered the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores with his aura so Third Page Eternal Sin did not notice them landing on her body.","Lin Yuan did not tell Third Page Eternal Sin that Eighth Page Apoptosis was already under his control.","He was not going to ask Third Page Eternal Sin about Tower Canon as he had already heard everything from Eighth Page Apoptosis. Given that they were both part of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, it would not make sense for her to know more than Eighth Page Apoptosis.","Before Lin Yuan made his move, he still wanted to give some of Tarot Round Table’s experts a chance. After all, minority opinion was sometimes drowned out by the majority in a team.","“What is Tarot Round Table’s real goal for coming to the Radiance Federation? You’re not just after the leadership positions so you can stand a better chance of surviving the dead spirits crisis, right?”","Instinctively, Third Page Eternal Sin wanted to lie.","Someone who used to keeping up a facade always found it difficult to tell the truth!","But when the lie reached the tip of her tongue, Third Page Eternal Sin hurriedly pushed it down.","She realized that this young man was able to ask her questions so calmly because he had obtained some secret or important information.","This young man seemed to be familiar with the Spirit Mother and had mentioned Bu Po. Bu Po seemed to be the reserve disciple who the Spirit Mother had picked to be his successor.","Third Page Eternal Sin suddenly suspected that there was a spy in Tarot Round Table.","Despite knowing that she would anger the young man, Third Page Eternal Sin said honestly, “We want the leadership position in the Major Federation Union because we want each of us to have control over a federation. The Spirit Mother is in charge of the Spirit Mother Federation and gets to enjoy being worshiped by the entire Spirit Mother Federation. We also want to lead such lives! Moreover, once the dead spirits crisis breaks out, there will be nowhere to hide. The Radiance Federation is the best option as a safe haven!”","Lin Yuan’s blood boiled.","The Spirit Mother was able to lead the Spirit Mother Federation because he was born there. He only joined Tarot Round Table later in life when he became more powerful and was given an opportunity. As such, he would definitely prioritize the Spirit Mother Federation’s development.","On the other hand, the other members of Tarot Round Table felt no sense of belonging to any of the federations. If they took control of a federation, they would treat it the same way as someone who bought a new house and decided to fix up the garden. Their goal would be to groom the federation according to their tastes.","If Tarot Round Table carried out their objective, the citizens of the federations they chose would be in dire straits!","Lin Yuan furiously asked his second question.","“Has anyone objected to this plan?”","Third Page Eternal Sin instinctively looked around at the other members of Tarot Round Table.","Most of the experts from Tarot Round Table thought that Lin Yuan would provide them with a way out after threatening them.","Their fate hung in the balance of Third Page Eternal Sin’s answer.","Third Page Eternal Sin knew that she should not lie to Lin Yuan. But she still could not stop herself from saying, “There were indeed people who opposed this idea.”","Once Third Page Eternal Sin was done speaking, Lin Yuan received feedback from the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s exclusive skill Honesty Reflects the Heart.","Since Third Page Eternal Sin’s denial was a lie, it meant that every member of Tarot Round Table was evil.","If even one of them had opposed this, Third Page Eternal Sin would not have been deemed to be lying.","Lin Yuan had opened up a way out for her and was holding the door open.","While Third Page Eternal Sin was waiting for Lin Yuan’s reply so she could bring up what she knew about Tower Canon, she noticed that Lin Yuan’s left fist was still tightly clenched.","Aside from Eternal Source, all other signs of life disappeared from Resting Moon Palace’s inner palace.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and released Red Thorn’s main body.","Red Thorn looked at the corpses and said to Lin Yuan excitedly, “Lin Yuan, every Tongue of Relinquish has two tongue pouches. Aside from the Abyss Great Emperor, there is still space for the corpses of another five experts. These corpses are still in very complete condition and all the feys have been trapped in the spiritual spatial zone. Once I turn them into fairies, they will be able to control their feys, sacred source lifeforms, and precious instruments to do battle! However, it might take a little longer to transform them!”","Lin Yuan did not mind and nodded. Regardless of how long it took Red Thorn to transform these corpses, it would not take longer than the Abyss Great Emperor.","One batch would take two to three months at most.","Every three months, an expert would be added to the army that defended against the dead spirits crisis. This would not make a significant impact on the dead spirits crisis that would last for hundreds or thousands of years.","Red Thorn placed the corpses in the Diamond fey storage box that Lin Yuan had specially made for it. It was in the shape of a small red flower bud clip. Red Thorn liked it immensely! The long red ribbons that hung from the sides of the clip reminded Red Thorn of the old days with Lin Yuan.","After Red Thorn stored the corpses away, Lin Yuan returned Red Thorn’s main body to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He allowed Red Thorn to sit on his ear and he listened to it hum.","Lin Yuan did not leave Resting Moon Palace’s inner palace immediately. There were too many signs of life left behind by Tarot Round Table’s experts. Lin Yuan saw this as he had dirtied Resting Moon Palace.","Lin Yuan let out a few of the Hundred Questions Beasts and assigned them to perform their natural abilities as housekeeping beasts. The Hundred Questions Beasts quickly cleaned up Resting Moon Palace until it was spick and span.","Lin Yuan only walked out of Resting Moon Palace when he was certain that it was completely clean.","Eternal Source silently followed Lin Yuan. His gaze when he looked at Lin Yuan was filled with even more admiration than before. He was even leaning towards worshipping Lin Yuan!","Eternal Source always knew that Lin Yuan was kind and generous and rarely showed the might of a powerful being.","He had not killed many Dictators in the subterranean world. He had not even made an example out of anyone!","Frankly, Eternal Source preferred cruel and merciless leaders to warm and kind ones.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan’s eventual aim was the Sky Beyond the Clouds. If he maintained such a soft nature, he would eventually be taken advantage of.","But now, Eternal Source was finally getting to see the deadly and decisive side of Lin Yuan. This also allowed Eternal Source to understand that Lin Yuan was kind to his own people. He did have a vicious side that he showed to outsiders but up until now, he had not had many opportunities to display it.","Lin Yuan noticed the change in Eternal Source’s attitude but did not comment on it. After all, he always acted true to himself.","Taking the big picture into consideration, Lin Yuan would probably not have killed all the experts from Tarot Round Table if Red Thorn had not obtained the ability Tongue Pouch Births Demons when it evolved to Diamond grade. Instead, he would have allowed them to live despite knowing that they would not be easy to manage. He would have forced them to swear their loyalty to him. This would only be because this would enable him to save more lives during the dead spirits crisis.","This might have caused him to seem weak to Eternal Source who lived by the law of the jungle but Lin Yuan’s actions reinforced his goal.","Lifeforms of different levels, species, and who lived in different environments naturally had different ways of thinking.","Lin Yuan was not looking down on Eternal Source. But with Eternal Source’s stubborn forcefulness, even if he somehow managed to exceed the main world’s limits and make it to the Sky Beyond the Clouds on his own merit, he would either end up joining a faction or becoming the subordinate of another expert. He did not have the chops to build and lead his own faction!","Previously, Lin Yuan thought that humans were much weaker than dimensional lifeforms as it was much more difficult for them to increase their power and their bodies were also much frailer.","But now, he suddenly felt that humans were much more guileful. This might be the advantage that they had over dimensional lifeforms!"]},{"number":2648,"title":"Chapter 2648 The Moon Empress’ Sense of Security!","paragraphs":["2648 The Moon Empress’ Sense of Security!","This natural advantage was what allowed humans to rule over the land and all the feys that lived on it, as well as stand toe-to-toe against the sea clans!","Lin Yuan’s mermaid bloodline might seem stronger than his human one but he saw his human bloodline as his true bloodline.","“Eternal Source, I will be sending the Abyss Great Emperor away to transform him. During this time, you can stay in the Radiant Moon Palace! Don’t forget to make my master’s safety your top priority. If you do this well, I will help you take another step forward! The Afterlife Realm won’t be the ceiling of your power.”","Eternal Source was ecstatic when he heard what Lin Yuan said. It meant that he was an important asset to Lin Yuan. Otherwise, he would not assign him such an important task.","Eternal Source had been feeling rather enlightened ever since he reached the Afterlife Realm. Now that he had reached the Afterlife Realm, he could see the vast majesty of the world that had opened up to him!","He had been the strongest Samsara Realm Dictator in the marsh world. Confidence was not something he lacked.","But now, there was a fact that he needed to accept. This fact was that he would not be able to move on from the Afterlife Realm through his own effort and potential.","Truthfully, he was only able to reach the Afterlife Realm with Lin Yuan’s help as well.","He knew that without the pure source-type power that Lin Yuan had given him, he would not be able to reach the Afterlife Realm even after another few thousand years passed.","Lin Yuan’s trust in him was one matter. But Lin Yuan was also willing to provide him with benefits. This proved that Lin Yuan truly saw him as a close subordinate.","Given that Lin Yuan was willing to provide him with the resources to evolve past the Afterlife Realm, he would also be willing to continue nurturing him to even greater heights.","“Young Master, don’t worry. As long as I’m alive, I will not allow any danger to befall your master.”","Eternal Source did not give a guarantee because he knew that Lin Yuan was a pragmatic person.","He could not make any grounded guarantees when his opponent was the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","But by saying this, it showed his earnesty and resolution.","Eternal Source had learned a fair amount after his extended interactions with humans.","The way that he addressed Lin Yuan had also changed from ‘Lord’ to ‘Young Master’. This came from his observation that only those who were truly close to Lin Yuan called him by his name. Eternal Source yearned to enter that inner circle.","Lin Yuan patted Eternal Source’s shoulder. He was very satisfied with Eternal Source’s answer.","Lin Yuan would take Chu Ci into the Spirit Lock spatial zone and she would live there safely until Tower Canon was dealt with. The pure spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would also strengthen Chu Ci’s power.","It made no difference whether one contracted the Lifespan Mouse earlier or later in life. But if one formed a contract with it earlier, they would be able to retain the looks of their younger self!","Once Chu Ci and Wen Yu were back, Lin Yuan intended to give Chu Ci, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and his other close ones a Lifespan Mouse each so they could accumulate as much lifespan as possible.","Due to the limited supply of the Lifespan Mouse and because Lin Yuan had already given the Moon Empress many of them, the non-key members of Sky City such as the white-clothed followers would not be able to contact the Lifespan Mouse anytime soon.","However, Lin Yuan had already sent instructions to collate the ages of all the white-clothed followers. He would make sure that every one of them contracted the Lifespan Mouse before they came to the end of their lifespans.","Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest still needed to train and this dead spirits crisis would be the best training environment.","Based on Lin Yuan’s understanding of Chu Ci, it was likely that she also intended on using the dead spirits crisis to train herself.","However, she was still too young and weak. She did not have the capabilities to be a leader. Lin Yuan would only be able to lay his worries to rest if he knew that she was in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Apart from Chu Ci, the Moon Empress was Lin Yuan’s closest loved one.","As a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty who was also overseeing operations of the entire Radiance Federation, there was no way that she would agree to take shelter in the Spirit Lock spatial zone during such a time.","Lin Yuan could think on behalf of Chu Ci and tell her what to do but he could not do the same to the Moon Empress.","Assigning Eternal Source to protect the Moon Empress was the most that he could do for her.","The strongest protector that Lin Yuan could send was an Afterlife Realm expert like Eternal Source.","With Eternal Source protecting the Moon Empress, even if Tower Canon secretly ambushed her, Lin Yuan would be able to use the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation to transport himself to the Moon Empress’ side immediately while Eternal Source was fending Tower Canon off.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan had patted Eternal Source’s shoulder but this time, Eternal Source felt a greater sense of security than he ever felt before because Lin Yuan had given him assurance.","Before Lin Yuan exhibited his power, Eternal Source assumed that he was the strongest combat power that Lin Yuan had.","But as he spent more time by Lin Yuan’s side and learned more about the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he knew that his power would not seem as impressive there.","When Eternal Source found out that Keira was a lifeform from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he immediately began communicating with her.","Most of Eternal Source’s unease appeared after Keira appeared.","Keira had sensed Eternal Source’s unease but she still told him about her circumstances. This was the only way to convince Eternal Source to empathize with her.","Keira was only trying to become acquainted with Eternal Source. Whether this gave him a sense of security or made him more anxious was his own problem.","When he arrived at the entrance of the Resting Moon Palace, Lin Yuan saw the Moon Empress standing there with the Abyss Great Emperor. There was anxiousness written all over her face and she kept peering into Resting Moon Palace.","Lin Yuan had never seen the Moon Empress in such a state.","Before the Moon Empress could move over to his side, he reached her first and said softly, “Master, you don’t have to worry. I have handled Tarot Round Table. You don’t need to worry about them anymore!”","The Moon Empress had arrived at the Resting Moon Palace after Lin Yuan and she had been waiting by the entrance for less than an hour.","Yet, he had already settled the matter!","Indeed, the Moon Empress could not sense any energy fluctuations coming from within Resting Moon Palace’s inner palace and thought.","It looks like there’s no need for me to step in. Otherwise, I would still be able to feel some energy fluctuations.","The Moon Empress was finally able to relax when she saw Lin Yuan.","But given the magnitude of this matter, the Moon Empress still asked Lin Yuan, “Little Yuan, did Tarot Round Table make more unreasonable requests? You can tell me if they tried to threaten you. I’ll help you to come up with a plan. If I fuse with Forage Moon, I will be just as strong as a spirit fire expert!”","The Moon Empress looked at Lin Yuan kindly. He could see determination in her gaze.","He did not know what it meant for Forage Moon to fuse with the Moon Empress. But it would require a huge price for a birth horoscope expert to unleash spirit fire power!","Lin Yuan hurriedly told the Moon Empress, “Master, Tarot Round Table did make some insane demands. They wanted each of them to occupy a federation. The Spirit Mother of the Spirit Mother Federation is also a member of Tarot Round Table. They want to be worshipped by a federation the same way that the Spirit Mother is worshipped by the Spirit Mother Federation. But they had no intention of shouldering the responsibilities that come with it. From their intentions, it’s clear that their final goal is to take control of the entire human world and gain more decision-making authority in the human world.”","The Moon Empress froze when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","If Tarot Round Table truly had such intentions, it was unlikely that there was anyone in the human world who be able to oppose them.","The Mirror God and God of Fools from the Freedom Federation had both set their spirit fire alight. With them and the Radiance Federation’s Spacetime Elder, there would only be three spirit fire experts.","The Moon Empress had not included the spirit fire expert from the Azure Federation.","It would not be strange if the Azure Federation chose to side with Tarot Round Table after learning of their power.","Even if the Azure Federation, Radiance Federation, and Freedom Federation banded together and the four spirit fire experts were able to stand up to Tarot Round Table, Tarot Round Table had far too many birth horoscope experts.","Before the Moon Empress’ worries could grow, Lin Yuan said seriously, “Master, I have eliminated all of the people from Tarot Round Table! You know that I have taken control of Di Wanmi’s corpse and am continuing to use her as a Class 5 Creation Master. I can use a similar method to control the people from Tarot Round Table. They will become just as obedient as Di Wanmi and contribute to the defense against the dead spirits crisis!”","Lin Yuan immediately began describing to the Moon Empress everything he had done and thought of in the Resting Moon Palace. This would prevent her from becoming worried because of any misunderstandings she had.","Astonishment spread across the Moon Empress’ face.","At this moment, Lin Yuan’s image in the Moon Empress’ mind was once again refreshed.","But regardless, the Moon Empress knew that Lin Yuan was her disciple.","She turned and helped him to adjust his already-neat collar before she waved and said, “Little Yuan, the other members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty also knew about Tarot Round Table’s experts staying in the Resting Moon Palace. I will hold an imperial meeting to tell them about what happened. You...”","The Moon Empress had been filled with happiness after learning about the power he possessed.","But at the same time, she felt the slightest hint of bitterness.","She was the master yet she was being protected by her disciple!","The Moon Empress had only been able to enjoy the feeling of guiding Lin Yuan and holding question-and-answer sessions with him for a little over a year.","At this moment, the Moon Empress sensed that Eternal Source was standing behind her. He seemed to be intending on following her.","She turned to look back at him before she shifted her gaze over to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan smiled and waved at her as he said, “Master, Eternal Source will be your bodyguard from now on. He will protect you! Don’t worry about me. My safety is assured!”","When the Moon Empress heard the first part of what Lin Yuan said, she was about to turn him down when she heard the second part of what he said and could not stop herself from taking in a sharp breath.","She waved back silently to Lin Yuan.","When she turned back, the smile on her face was faint but her heart was extremely warm.","The warmest feeling she had ever experienced in her life thus far came from this disciple of hers.","After the Moon Empress left, Lin Yuan got in touch with Qin Yu.","All the Land Imps had been sent to the Startling Lines Continent and were being managed by Qin Yu.","These Land Imps had the experience of building the Radiance Federation’s base so Qin Yu did not need to spend a lot of time guiding them.","However, he did need to supervise them.","The building of the Startling Lines Continent’s base was extremely important and Lin Yuan needed to check on the progress.","Moreover, he was done with his discussion with Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Lin Yuan needed to create a space near the Radiance Federation to house the sea clans before the experts from Vast Sea Labyrinth arrived.","Vast Sea Labyrinth’s biggest worry was that they would arrive at the Radiance Federation and the dead spirits crisis would begin before Lin Yuan combined the main world with the five dimensional worlds. If that happened, the migration of the sea clans would be for naught.","Lin Yuan knew why Ice Flow, Ice Clarity, and Ice Flow made many requests despite knowing that doing so would give the humans more advantage over them.","Lin Yuan was very willing to show his sincerity to this partner who would be helping him to take on the dead spirits crisis.","Moreover, Lin Yuan already intended on building a platform at the bottom of the sea so the Sea Burial Lotus Flower would be able to create a sea of Bone Lotus Flowers there and use the dead spirits crisis to increase its power.","Ever since Lin Yuan gave this important task to Qin Yu, Qin Yu had treasured this chance.","Every day, he reported everything that happened before he went to bed.","Hence, he was very detailed in his answers to Lin Yuan’s questions.","In this regard, Qin Yu did a much better job than Ta Lei.","Previously, Lin Yuan always felt that Ta Lei’s competence was lacking because he had no one to help him. But now, it seemed that this was not the case as Qin Yu was also alone with no one to help him.","The laying down of the metal-type stone boards in the Radiance Federation had already been completed.","Lin Yuan sent a message to Qin Yu.","[Lin Yuan]: Ah Yu, it looks like you have a good grip over the 15 million Land Imps. I will send you another 12 million Land Imps around three days later. Bring Sweet Vanquish with you to receive them.","Qin Yu was over the moon when he received Lin Yuan’s message.","The more jobs Lin Yuan assigned to him, the more he felt validated in his capabilities.","[Qin Yu]: Young Master, that is no problem at all. The Land Imps you sent me have done so well. The laying down of the metal-type stone boards in the Startling Lines Continent is already almost 80% complete. I intend on finishing the project with these 15 million Land Imps. I will send the 12 million Land Imps to the bottom of the sea to lay down the metal-type stone boards there. I hope you can assign some experts from the sea clans to me. I need them to create an environment that will be conducive for the Land Imps to work in! I noticed that in spite of the Land Imps’ cowardly natures, they will do whatever they can to play sly tricks and find loopholes. If we don’t provide them with a comfortable environment, their speed will decline and I’m worried that they will take shortcuts."]},{"number":2649,"title":"Chapter 2649 Easily Gained Faith!","paragraphs":["2649 Easily Gained Faith!","[Qin Yu]: I have sent out all of the Dictators you sent me to watch the Land Imps work.","Lin Yuan could not help but be impressed by Qin Yu when he saw the message.","Lin Yuan felt that it was very praiseworthy that Qin Yu could pick up on the Land Imps’ issues while he was leading them.","[Lin Yuan]: The first batch of sea clan experts should be near the Startling Lines Continent by the time the 12 million Land Imps reach you. I will instruct them to make contact with you and they will do their best to assist you with the construction!","Now that he was done communicating with Qin Yu, Lin Yuan returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","He took out a piece of paper and began concentrating on drawing up a layout so he could visualize how the five dimensional worlds would be connected to the main world.","Lin Yuan intended to finish all the preparation work before he fused the worlds.","For someone like Lin Yuan who always liked to be ready as early as possible, he was never careless when it came to preparation work.","He knew that the coming few days would be the last peaceful ones for a long time.","Wen Yu sent a message to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, I am done investigating all the land on the other side of the Barren Sea! I told every federation ruler here about the dead spirits crisis. Many of them were very rude to us. A few of them outright ordered their men to attack me without giving me the chance to speak. Thanks to Dazzling Silver and the rest, there haven’t been any serious injuries. Naturally, there were some who were willing to listen and asked for help with their migration. Miss Chu Ci, Bei Xu, and I have collected every Continent Vein Core. There are a total of 21 of them. They are all in my possession.","Lin Yuan’s face lit up.","Although Wen Yu had made sure to mention Chu Ci and Bei Xu, Lin Yuan knew that they had not provided her with much help. Rather, she would have had to go the extra mile to take care of the two of them.","Wen Yu had managed to obtain 21 Continent Vein Cores. This was not only more than what Lin Yuan had been expecting but she also completed the task sooner than he had expected.","[Lin Yuan]: Wen Yu, I am in the Radiance Federation now. I will immediately travel to Sky Bearer City through the Space Tunnel. Let’s talk more when we meet!","Lin Yuan stored away the completed layout diagram before he immediately headed to the Space Tunnel situated at the entrance of the Class 6 marsh dimensional rift.","He believed that he would have no need to head to the other side of the Barren Sea again after this trip to Sky Bearer City!","It was already Lin Yuan’s biggest act of kindness for him to tell the human federations on the other side of the Barren Sea about the news of the impending dead spirits crisis. He had even offered them the opportunity to relocate. If the rulers had been willing to relocate, Lin Yuan could have relocated every citizen from the federations to the Radiance Federation where their survival would be assured.","Lin Yuan did not have the time for Wen Yu to try to persuade the federations who attacked her without giving her the chance to say her piece. After all, he had to incur costs and it took up time for him to relocate the federations’ citizens.","When he arrived at Sky Bearer City, Wen Yu was waiting for him by the entrance.","Once she spotted him, Wen Yu began telling him everything that had happened.","When she was done with her report, Wen Yu said softly, “I discovered a total of 37 federations on the other side of the Barren Sea. After hearing my warning, only nine of them have agreed to relocate. The other 28 seem to have absolutely no inclination to relocate. There are even a few who, after hearing my repeated warnings, said they wanted to work together to take me down! Young Master, how should we handle these nine federations?”","Wen Yu’s beginnings came from the Radiant Moon Palace and she used to be a moon attendant.","Although moon attendants did not have much real authority in the Radiant Moon Palace, it was still a very prestigious position. They represented the Radiant Moon Palace whenever the Radiance Federation interacted with other factions.","With her prestigious upbringing, Wen Yu was able to see things with exceptional clarity.","It was because of this that she did not ask about the other 28 federations at all. Even if Lin Yuan wanted to save the 28 federations, they did not deserve to be saved by him.","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment before he asked Wen Yu, “What is the population size of the nine federations?”","Wen Yu immediately answered, “These nine federations who agreed to relocate are all considered the weaker ones among all the federations on the other side of the Barren Sea. Rather than saying that I managed to convince them, it would be more accurate to say that they are just seizing any opportunity to change their fates! These nine federations have a combined population that is smaller than the Radiance Federation’s major cities. But it won’t be easy to relocate them.”","Lin Yuan nodded gently.","If the nine federations had a combined population that was smaller than one of the Radiance Federation’s major cities, it would take around two days to relocate all of them.","Two days later, most of the people from the federations participating in the Major Federation Union would have arrived in the Radiance Federation’s vicinity.","By the time the people from the nine federations were relocated, it would also be time for Lin Yuan to return to the Radiance Federation and begin the process of combining the main world with the dimensional worlds!","Lin Yuan released the Land-Lifting Marsh Turtle from the Spirit Lock spatial zone. It had become a mobile piece of land.","Lin Yuan could move the people from the nine federations to the Land-Lifting Marsh Turtle’s back and send them to the marsh world.","Even if the Land-Lifting Marsh Turtle could not move all the people at once, it would be done in two or three trips.","The only part of the plan that would take up time was moving all the people from the nine federations onto the Land-Lifting Marsh Turtle’s back.","Lin Yuan received the 21 Continent Vein Cores from Wen Yu and placed them all next to the Abyss Red Lotus. The Abyss Red Lotus’ roots soon wrapped around the 21 Continent Vein Cores.","He would be able to tap into the power in the Continent Vein Cores when he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci and saw that she had become tanner after baking in the sun on the other side of the Barren Sea. But the light oat coloring made her seem more energetic than before.","Lin Yuan reached out and pressed down on the stray strands of hair on Chu Ci’s head that were sticking out as he asked with a smile, “Previously, you were constantly talking about wanting to go to train. So how was your time training with Wen Yu?”","Normally, Chu Ci would become jittery with excitement when Lin Yuan asked her such a question.","But now, she felt strangely calm when she answered his question.","After a moment’s contemplation, Chu Ci said seriously, “Big Brother, I was able to get a good look at this work during my time with Sister Wen Yu! I used to think that we had a tough childhood. But now, I don’t think we can call our childhoods tough at all!”","Lin Yuan looked at Chu Ci with satisfaction. She was finally beginning to understand that this world was filled with pain and hardship. It could be said that it was only at this moment that she truly began understanding this world.","Chu Ci was only 17 years old. This made her old enough to learn the fact that living in this world was arduous.","Lin Yuan’s gladness did not last long before he heard Chu Ci say seriously, “Big Brother, I heard from Sister Wen Yu that there will be a dead spirits crisis arriving very soon. I want to...”","Before she could finish speaking, she was cut off by Lin Yuan.","“Chu Ci, you will have plenty of opportunities to grow. I will definitely be taking you with me to another world in the future! I hope you can grow in a safe environment instead of a perilous one. I will find a safe place for you to stay and where you can increase your power. The dead spirits crisis will last for a very long time. It won’t be too late for you to continue training once you become sufficiently strong!”","Lin Yuan spoke in a decisive tone. There was no one in this world who knew Chu Ci better than Lin Yuan did.","Chu Ci was very strong-headed. If he did not shoot her down, she would bite down on any shred of hope and refuse to let go.","Chu Ci had called him ‘Big Brother’ twice. It was likely that she would be calling him ‘Lin Yuan’ again after what he just said.","Chu Ci looked back at Wen Yu after she heard what Lin Yuan said.","Lin Yuan’s eyebrow twitched. She was actually trying to find supporters!","Wen Yu smiled and shook her head when she met Chu Ci’s gaze, signaling that she could not help. She said to Chu Ci, “Young Master is just worried about you. Don’t forget that without the protection of Dazzling Silver and the rest, the two of us would have already died many times over! The dead spirits crisis won’t be like our expedition for the Continent Vein Cores. It will be much more dangerous!”","Chu Ci pursed her lips and looked at Lin Yuan.","Chu Ci’s emotional intelligence was not the only way in which she had grown after her training with Wen Yu. She had also gained experience and character.","As such, she could understand that Lin Yuan had made such a request because he cared about her.","“Big Brother, I know already! I will sit tight and increase my power until it reaches a level that is satisfactory to you. But once I reach that level, you have to allow me to join the fight against the dead spirits crisis!”","Chu Ci spoke with great sincerity.","Chu Ci was not insistent on participating in the dead spirits crisis.","However, her brother and master were both helping to protect the main world by fighting the dead spirits crisis.","Chu Ci also wanted to share Lin Yuan’s burden and make things easier for them.","Lin Yuan was a transmigrator and the education from his previous life gave him a traditional personal value system.","However, the only family that Chu Ci had ever known was Lin Yuan. Apart from him, the only people she had in her childhood were Auntie Zhang and Uncle Li. Thus, there were very few people who she cared about in this world. Cold Moon, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the others only entered her life later.","Nonetheless, she only wanted to protect these precious people who were part of her small circle. She felt no noble obligation to save the world.","When Lin Yuan heard what Chu Ci said, he could not help but hug her.","His little sister had finally grown up!","Now that he was done speaking with Chu Ci, he realized that Bei Xu was nowhere to be seen. As such, he asked Wen Yu, “What is Bei Xu doing now?”","Wen Yu immediately answered, “Young Master, I wanted to train Bei Xu so I left him behind to gather the people from the nine federations. He has not come back to Sky Bearer City yet. Thanks to the many Dictators that you assigned to me, I was able to move the people from the nine federations nearer to the Sky Bearer City very quickly.”","Lin Yuan waved at Wen Yu and Chu Ci.","“Let’s go. It’s time for us to lead this people in their migration!”","Sky Bearer City was situated below the Grotto Continent and it made Lin Yuan feel very suffocated. He only relaxed when he arrived at the surface.","Wen Yu pointed northwest.","“The people from the federations are arriving from the northwest direction. If the Island Whales are sent to fetch them, they will be able to climb onto the Island Whales’ backs very quickly.”","Lin Yuan shook his head. He did not send the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s Island Whales to fetch the citizens from the federations on the other side of the Barren Sea.","Firstly, the other side of the Barren Sea was far too remote. Even if the Island Whales were able to locate them, it would waste too much time.","Secondly, Vast Sea Labyrinth had been accumulating resources and had thousands of the Island Whales. Nonetheless, there still would not be enough Island Whales to move all the people from the federations.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had other means of relocating the federation citizens.","Bei Xu was keeping in contact with Wen Yu and knew that Lin Yuan would be arriving soon. Hence, he kept looking in the direction that she had left in.","Once he spotted Lin Yuan, Bei Xu stood up and started waving at him.","Bei Xu was not the kind of person who was afraid of hardship. Rather, he liked tasks that came with some difficulty as they would allow him to train himself.","However, the task that Wen Yu had given him was really challenging him.","Even if these people were easy to manage, he did not have the experience of managing millions of people. Moreover, these millions of people came from nine different factions. It was inevitable that there would be friction when they were all gathered together.","It would not be as easy as Qin Yu managing the Land Imps.","Wen Yu had assigned numerous experts to protect him but they were not able to help him to manage these people like how Sweet Vanquish could help Qin Yu to manage the Land Imps.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and waved at Bei Xu.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan realized that immediately after he arrived, faint glowing dots of light that represented the faith from many people from the nine federations.","This slightly confused Lin Yuan. But he quickly came up with a reason for this","It was likely that Wen Yu and Bei Xu had been treating these people very well during the migration process.","Wen Yu had stocked up on the Soldier Ration Radishes and probably distributed them to these people. The Soldier Ration Radishes prevented the federation citizens from starving to death.","Lin Yuan had witnessed the cruel environment of the Grotto Continent and Broiling Rock Continent. The biggest dream of the regular citizens living on the other side of the Barren Sea was to have a proper meal.","It was because of this reason that all of them had pinned their hopes onto him."]},{"number":2650,"title":"Chapter 2650 The Second One to be Eliminated!","paragraphs":["2650 The Second One to be Eliminated!","Those who had been put through life’s wringer would be more easily enamored by an unknown, powerful being. This enamorment would eventually turn into faith!","Lin Yuan had been trying to come up with a way to earn the faith of the people from the nine federations. Now, he found it.","He released Lift Marsh.","To the people from the nine federations, Lift Marsh was a mammoth creature beyond their collective wildest dreams!","Lift Marsh raised its head and let out a roar that rippled through the sky and pushed apart the clouds. Suddenly, there was not a cloud to be seen in the previously cloud-covered sky!","Lift Marsh’s ability to do this did not come from having an ability similar to Chimey’s. It only possessed abilities related to earth elements.","It was able to do this because it was a giant lifeform. Any movement in its body was bolstered by its qi. It had used the strength from its qi to drive all the clouds out from the sky.","Lift Marsh could be considered the equivalent of a Turning Wheel Realm Dictator in an actual battle setting. However, at merely the Turning Wheel Realm, it would suffer if it only depended on its qi and body to do battle.","But Lin Yuan had not nurtured Lift Marsh for combat purposes.","All the various marsh soil that he had fed to Lift Marsh had not gone to waste! They had all gathered on its back. From now on, he could nurture any plant-type fey he wanted on Lift Marsh’s back.","Once Lift Marsh grew even larger, Lin Yuan could move it into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Even Lin Yuan, who saw Lift Marsh often, could not help but be awed by its size, much less the humans from the nine weak federations who came from the other side of the Barren Sea!","At the instant that he summoned Lift Marsh, Lin Yuan could sense the fountain of faith in his divine kingdom filling up with even more flowing dots of light. The first few dots of faith that came from the people from the nine federations were also steadily growing larger.","Lin Yuan spread the black wings on his back and flew up to Lift Marsh’s head.","At this moment, he could be described as a celestial being who had descended to earth.","He looked at the people from the nine federations and said seriously, “You might see this migration as a risk, but I want to tell you that it is actually an opportunity for you to transform. I won’t say anything more. You can see for yourselves!","“Move onto the giant turtle’s back in groups of three federations! Remember to be as quick as you can. I will only give you two days to complete your migration. If you aren’t done in two days, the leaders of the nine federations will be left behind here to be feasted on by dead spirits!”","If a federation could survive independently without Lin Yuan’s help, they would only follow him because their leaders trusted him. But this was the complete opposite situation.","Lin Yuan seemed to hold the leaders of the nine federations captive, but they were convinced by and trusted him.","All of them knew that they held no value to this celestial-like young man. Since they had no value, he did not need to scheme to entrap them.","Furthermore, none of them were hiding any exceptional treasures. Weak federations like them all had to provide offerings to the powerful federations.","There was no need for this celestial-like young man to lie to them.","If they could not complete the migration in two days, they would really be abandoned here! Hence, all the rulers of the nine federations began focusing on the tasks surrounding the migration.","They were all in the same boat. Thus, it did not matter which federations were part of the first group to migrate!","Lin Yuan had come up with this arrangement because he had been afraid that the nine federations would begin fighting over who would be the first to migrate. He also did not want his deadline to unnecessarily cause the regular people to panic.","The rulers of the nine federations did hold absolute authority over their own federations, and their citizens quickly lined up into long rows.","Lift Marsh usually stayed in the marsh world. It rarely had the chance to be close to Lin Yuan ever since it became an Apostle. It also had not known Lin Yuan for as long as Wendy, Rising Lizard, and White Pavilion. Hence, it really enjoyed the opportunity to be close to him.","Lift Marsh raised its head continuously to stare affectionately at Lin Yuan. Due to the largeness of its body, it could not move too physically close to Lin Yuan. Otherwise, it would dive into Lin Yuan’s arms each time it saw him, just like Wendy did.","Since the people from the nine federations saw Lin Yuan as a celestial being, they saw Lift Marsh as a celestial turtle that could move the earth and sky!","Lift Marsh’s clear affection for Lin Yuan deepened these people’s fearful respect for him.","The sand below their feet was whipped up and formed thousands of long staircases that led from the ground to Lift Marsh’s back. All these people needed to do to relocate was walk up the staircases!","As he watched the people from the first three federations walking up the staircases, he realized that these nine weaker federations did have something going for them. They were relatively united.","During their journey here, many people collapsed due to exhaustion and sickness despite being supplied with the Soldier Ration Radishes by Wen Yu. These weaker people and elderly were all being supported by younger or middle-aged people as they climbed up the stairs. Some of them would even carry the weak on their backs.","Lin Yuan could not be more pleased to see this!","Peace had also led the people of the Green Continent City to relocate.","Due to the emergence of the dead spirits crisis, Peace could no longer carry on with her Green Continent Goddess Plan. This was her only option.","She much preferred staying with Lin Yuan and his companions over suffering in the harsh environment of the Broiling Rock Continent. However, she was rather disappointed that her dream of building up Green Continent City was ruined.","The first person from the Astronomical Parliament whom Peace met in real life was Wen Yu. It only took a few words with Peace for Wen Yu to understand Peace’s ambitions.","Ta Lei could only serve as the City Lord of Thick Soil City because his capabilities were limited.","Meanwhile, Peace’s management of a large city was an underuse of her capabilities. Her horizons and dreams restricted her.","There was no way that someone like her could leave the main world with Lin Yuan.","Wen Yu believed that Peace had her own uniquely impressive capabilities. Otherwise, she would not have been able to perform her role as the Green Continent Goddess of Green Continent City as well as she did without being exposed by anyone. If Peace could apply her methods elsewhere and was properly guided, she would definitely be able to achieve great things.","But at that moment, Lin Yuan had long passed the stage of needing and searching for talents.","Although he still wanted to surround himself with talents, it was clear that he did not want to force the members of the Astronomical Parliament. Once Lin Yuan heard about Peace’s ambitions, he would immediately provide her with a way to attain the future she wanted.","Wen Yu already knew of Lin Yuan’s plan to give every member of the Astronomical Parliament the Lifespan Mouse.","As long as they had the Lifespan Mouse, their life would not be in any danger. The members of the Astronomical Parliament would be able to continue living even after the dead spirits crisis came to an end.","No matter how many preparations he made for the dead spirits crisis, the world would be razed to the ground by the time it ended. At that time, there would be a million things to do.","Peace would have the chance to build a federation and make her dreams come true then.","Wen Yu was the practical kind. Now that she knew where Peace’s heart lay, Wen Yu no longer concerned herself with Peace. After all, there were endless things she needed to think about and do.","The fewer people she needed to worry about, the more brain space would be freed up to increase Wen Yu’s productivity.","Wen Yu did not tell Lin Yuan about what she learned. If she told Lin Yuan about this, it would seem as though she had something against Peace.","With Lin Yuan’s intelligence, he could sense Peace’s thoughts once he met and interacted with her.","Lin Yuan did not stay here to oversee the migration of the nine federations. He had intentionally appeared as though he was a celestial being because he wanted to collect faith. It would still be Bei Xu who managed the migration.","The people from Green Continent City were in the center of the crowd of people from the nine federations. Since they were all going to be migrated, Lin Yuan did not give the people from Green Continent City special treatment.","If he gave them special treatment, it would cause them to be seen as the enemy by the other people from the nine federations. This would not be beneficial for the people from Green Continent City.","Wen Yu had already moved Peace to Sky Bearer City.","If time was not as tight as it was, Lin Yuan would have gone to meet with Peace when he first arrived in Sky Bearer City. Nonetheless, it was not too late to meet with her now.","Lin Yuan led Wen Yu and Chu Ci into Sky Bearer City and to the room where Peace was resting.","Peace had never left the Broiling Rock Continent and its dehydrated environment filled with fire-element energy.","When she left the Broiling Rock Continent, Peace thought that she had entered heaven.","However, what she saw as heaven was nothing more than a desolate area that could barely support life.","Peace had gotten a full blast of how terrible the world could be. This also solidified her will to bring happiness to Green Continent City!","Peace immediately walked up to Wen Yu and Lin Yuan happily when she saw them.","Peace could sense that Wen Yu was more friendly with her now. But this friendliness was not linked to any deep emotions.","On the other hand, Peace already saw Lin Yuan as her family.","Lin Yuan’s explanation of her name had given her much relief and the strength to carry on.","“Leo, we are finally meeting! You are younger than I imagined. You also have great skin and are very handsome.”","This was the first time that Lin Yuan was hearing someone compliment him in such a straightforward manner.","This caused him to feel rather shy.","Lin Yuan smiled before he said to Peace, “It must have been tough on you!”","Peace shook her head and hurriedly said, “Leo, the environment in the Broiling Rock Continent might be cruel, but I didn’t find it difficult at all! My biggest dream was to protect the Green Continent City, provide it with water, and allow its people to never have to worry about water again.”","Lin Yuan was slightly stunned when he heard what Peace said.","After a moment of silence, he said with a smile, “Once you arrive on the other side of the Barren Sea, you will realize that water isn’t that precious of a resource. Aside from a few places, most places experience rain every few days. There are even some places where it rains all year! But you will be able to continue your dream of protecting Green Continent City even if you are in a different location!”","Wen Yu could not help but shake her head slightly when she heard what Peace said.","If Peace did not make her wishes fully clear and Lin Yuan did not promise to fulfill them, it would not be too late!","When they arrived on the other side of the Barren Sea and Peace’s horizons were broadened, she would inevitably reassess her dreams.","But now, she had forced herself into a box. Even if she decided to change her dreams and direction in the future, she could not tell Lin Yuan about it.","Lin Yuan would never rely on or appreciate a person who altered their dreams.","At this moment, Peace had locked in her future.","Wen Yu felt that Peace would become the second person after Ta Lei, who would be eliminated.","Luckily, just like with Ta Lei, Lin Yuan would ensure that Peace’s future in the main world would be a happy one.","After chatting with Peace, Lin Yuan and Wen Yu left Peace’s room.","Once they were outside Peace’s room, Lin Yuan could not help but sigh.","Wen Yu said solemnly, “Young Master, as the Astronomical Parliament’s Stars continue to increase, there can be hundreds of members! Aside from Bei Xu, Su Yiren, and Wo Lun, Yin Lin, Bu Po, and Luo Lan haven’t made any concrete plans.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Although he had told the members of the Astronomical Parliament about the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he had never asked about their thoughts.","Su Yiren, Luo Lan, and Bu Po all held important duties in their individual federations. Su Yiren had expressed her wishes to him, but Lin Yuan would not ask the other three how they felt. Instead, he would wait for them to take the initiative to tell him about their dreams and ambitions, just like Peace had done.","However, Lin Yuan was surprised to learn that Wen Yu was aware of Wo Lun’s decision.","Wo Lun had the least presence amongst the Astronomical Parliament’s members, but his contributions had been tremendous!"]},{"number":2651,"title":"Chapter 2651 Long Time No See, My Path Protector!","paragraphs":["2651 Long Time No See, My Path Protector!","Wo Lun was the oldest member of the Astronomical Parliament.","The Astronomical Parliament might seem secretive, but the members had an average age of around 25 years old. Wo Lun was the only one who was older than 40 years old, and he significantly increased the average age of the group.","However, 40 years old was not particularly old for a spirit qi professional.","As a sailor, Wo Lun naturally craved risks and liked to search for treasure on the open sea.","Aside from when Wo Lun was saved by Lin Yuan, joined the Astronomical Parliament, and later received the Blue Ring Sea Octopus, he did not receive much help from Lin Yuan.","When Wo Lun found out that Lin Yuan wanted to establish a trade route for the Startling Lines Continent, he immediately left his federation and headed to the Startling Lines Continent to help the Great Lush Federation build the harbor and port.","However, Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan caused all his efforts to go to waste.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan remembered Wo Lun’s effort.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of Wo Lun, the adventure addict definitely preferred the Sky Beyond the Clouds over the main world.","“Wen Yu, did Wo Lun say anything to you?”","Wen Yu smiled and said, “Young Master, when we were building the harbor, Wo Lun told me he hoped to have the chance to stay by your side to train and experience adventure! You had not yet revealed the Sky Beyond the Clouds, then. Although Wo Lun doesn’t like to speak much, he does take clear stock of everything that happens.”","Lin Yuan nodded and did not continue the topic.","Everyone had their own ambitions, and the members of the Astronomical Parliament were all individual entities. Since they had made their decisions, Lin Yuan would not try to force or pressure them.","The migration via Lift Marsh went very smoothly, and the nine federations were successfully migrated within three days. Lin Yuan had already brought all of them into the marsh world.","Compared to the Barren Sea, the marsh world was a prospering haven!","The people from the nine federations had never seen such fertile and rich land. The fertile land meant one thing—they could live without going hungry when they lived here.","The faith the people from the nine federations felt toward Lin Yuan shot upward again!","On the second day, before the people from the Green Continent City were relocated, Peace requested to stay with Green Continent City to manage the situation.","Lin Yuan did not turn her down and allowed her to stay with the people from Green Continent City in the marsh world.","Now, the migration was complete, and he had found what he needed to find.","Lin Yuan traveled back to the Radiance Federation to meet with the Moon Empress.","Next, he was going to fuse the main world with the five dimensional worlds and promote the main world to a Class 2 world.","When Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, he saw that many citizens from other federations had arrived at the Radiance Federation.","When the Moon Empress found out that Lin Yuan wanted to combine the five dimensional worlds with the main world, she stopped objecting to the relocation of the other federations’ citizens to the Radiance Federation.","But in a few short days, there would be inevitable friction.","Luckily, the City and Spirit Guards were well-trained and knew how to resolve such conflict.","...","At that moment, seven black coffins were pushed open in a bright ancient castle.","A female body with ice-blue eyes and snow-white skin with a faint gray hue walked stiffly out of one of the coffins.","There were no signs of movement from the eighth coffin.","...","Once Lin Yuan spoke with the Moon Empress, the latter wanted to help him earn more faith power and thus suggested that he wait for another day before he began the process.","The people who were arriving from other federations would only be settled in the Radiance Federation a day later.","Compared to the human federations, the sea clans moved slightly quicker.","The sea clans had already gathered in the sea near the Radiance Federation.","If one threw a brick into the sea, the brick would hit thousands of sea clan members while it sank.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth had considered the issue of a lack of oxygen when all the sea clans were gathered in a small area. As such, they planted many oxygen-producing plants around the area where the sea clans were gathered.","Ice Flow, with whom Lin Yuan was the most familiar, arrived in the Startling Lines Continent first.","After discussing with Qin Yu, Lin Yuan sent around a million wind-elemental sea lifeforms to create an area at the bottom of the sea where the Land Imps could lay down the metal-type stone boards.","Lin Yuan took out the five dimensional worlds’ treasures: the Abundance Treasure Tree, Tide Herb Treasure Conch, Spinning Chrysalis, Earth Source Cube, and Demon Evil Tablet.","He would place these dimensional treasures at the location where the main world would be connected to the dimensional worlds. Then, all Lin Yuan needed to do was activate the dimensional treasures, and the main world would be combined with the dimensional worlds.","Lin Yuan sent out Eternal Source and the Abyss Great Emperor to place the five dimensional treasures at the locations where he had marked out.","The five dimensional treasures contained the might of the dimensional worlds. Only Lin Yuan and the people he gave authority to could use the treasures.","It could be said that all preparations were complete!","Lin Yuan looked out the window all night but did not manage to get a wink of sleep.","Despite knowing it was his only choice and that this way would allow him to protect the most number of lifeforms from the main world, promoting a Class 1 world to Class 2 still undoubtedly came with risks. Unfortunately, no one could say what these risks were.","Lin Yuan was not the only one who did not get a good rest that night. The Moon Empress did not rest properly either.","The Moon Empress had spoken to Lin Yuan in such a categorical manner because that was truly how she felt. But she also did not want to place too much pressure on Lin Yuan.","Even if something really ended up going wrong, it would be because she had so strongly pushed Lin Yuan toward that decision. She decided to take all the pressure onto herself.","Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress were unable to sleep because of their worries. On the other hand, Ice Flow, Ice Wave, Ice Clarity, and the other experts from the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the members of sea clans were unable to sleep because of how excited they were.","Although there were sea plants that could produce oxygen, this did not change the fact that there were far too many sea beasts in the seas surrounding the Radiance Federation. With this high concentration of sea beasts, it was inevitable that some weak sea beasts would grow weaker and lose their lives.","There was no one who did not want to live in a better environment than they currently did. If the situation dragged on, it would begin to take a strain on even the stronger sea beasts!","The citizens of other federations who had moved to the Radiance Federation were also looking forward to a miracle.","After all, the news brought back by the federation representatives had been almost unbelievably shocking.","Once they received the news, even the most hesitant leaders decided not to waste any more time and immediately activated the entire federation to begin the migration.","This migration had cost the federations almost all of their resources, and their wealth had shrunk considerably.","All they could do was wait for an extraordinary miracle to save all of them, and the Radiance Federation was the only one that had hope of creating such a miracle!","The leaders of the federations had wondered if the information from the Major Federation Union had been false. But it was very easy to verify this issue. The federation only needed to send their Immortal experts to investigate the ley lines.","Some continents’ ley lines were nearer to the surface than others, and the people living on top of those lines had heard strange sounds from below them. They also felt their bodies being contaminated by death aura. It caused them to age at a much faster rate.","All of this verified the Radiance Federation’s information.","Once the people from the other federations relocated to the Radiance Federation, they were extremely thankful to the Radiance Federation. If the Radiance Federation had not revealed the news, not even the Immortal experts would be able to escape when the dead spirits crisis broke out.","Promoting the main world from a Class 1 world to Class 2 would affect all the lifeforms in the main world.","...","The next morning, Lin Yuan went to the Radiance Federation’s imperial court to meet with Purple Love, Blood New Moon, and the Mother of Bloodbath, who had just arrived at the Radiance Federation.","All of the Heavenly Family Feys from Heavenly Family Cottage had already arrived in the Radiance Federation.","Since the main efforts of the main world’s defense against the dead spirits crisis would be concentrated in the Radiance Federation, the best choice for Purple Love would be to come to the Radiance Federation with the Heavenly Family Feys!","So many things were happening in the Radiance Federation that Purple Love also intended to lend a helping hand.","The Radiance Federation and the Heavenly Family Cottage were already allies.","Furthermore, because of Lin Yuan, there were already deep ties between them.","Lin Yuan had told Purple Love about his intention to promote the main world from Class 1 to Class 2.","At first, he thought that the cautious Purple Love would object to his idea.","Yet, Purple Love shared the Moon Empress’ opinion and was very supportive of the idea of promoting the main world!","A large reason behind the Moon Empress’ support was that she wanted to support and affirm Lin Yuan. However, Purple Love spoke fully based on her own opinions!","“Lin Yuan, just think about it. No human spirit qi professional doesn’t want to increase his rank. There isn’t much danger surrounding a spirit qi professional raising their rank. But it is very dangerous for feys to evolve!","“Yet, have you ever encountered a fey who decided not to evolve out of fear of this danger? Promoting the main world from a Class 1 world to Class 2 is a great opportunity for the main world and all its lifeforms. Since the challenge has been presented, all the lifeforms of the main world need to do is accept this challenge!","“After being promoted to a Class 2 world, the main world will grow larger, the lifeforms will live longer, and every creature will be blessed. If anyone opposes your idea, it will only be because they are narrow-minded and short-sighted. You are doing something great. Why should you care about what those people think?”","Lin Yuan realized he had misunderstood Purple Love all this time.","Purple Love was not conservative. She only stayed below the radar all this time because she wanted to give the Heavenly Family Feys a safe place to live and prevent them from being bothered by the outside world.","Before Lin Yuan could speak, Purple Love smiled and continued. “The Heavenly Family Cottage will stand by your side and address all problems together with you.”","Purple Love looked at the Mother of Bloodbath, who was standing next to Blood New Moon and staring calmly at Lin Yuan.","The Mother of Bloodbath had recently been with the Heavenly Family Cottage to learn about its legacy. This was the first time that it had seen Lin Yuan in a long time.","Purple Love shot a look at Blood New Moon and pulled him out of the room before he could say anything to Lin Yuan.","The Mother of Bloodbath walked over to Lin Yuan and handed him a bag of fried chicken. “Taste this. Auntie Flame made it, and it is crispy and delicious!”","After seeing Lin Yuan after such a long time, the Mother of Bloodbath realized that Lin Yuan had matured significantly. They had only been apart for six months, but his aura had already changed completely. This had to be because Lin Yuan had grown exponentially in the past six months.","The Mother of Bloodbath felt a wave of regret. It was Lin Yuan’s Path Protector. Although it did not have the power to carry out its duties, it should still stay with him and watch him grow.","Its power had grown substantially in the past six months, but it was clearly nothing compared to Lin Yuan’s growth.","In just a little over a year, Lin Yuan had grown from a fledgling to the cream of the crop of the main world.","A year ago, the Freedom Federation envoy group had gone to the Radiance Federation and spectated the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. The Mother of Bloodbath had been present when Lin Yuan took on the Freedom Federation envoy group.","The Mother of Bloodbath was curious to find out what Lin Yuan had experienced in the past six months. It wanted to sit down and listen to Lin Yuan tell it about everything that had happened in the past six months. But it knew that was not the right time because Lin Yuan had something very important to do.","When it first joined this man, he had been like a blade of grass that any gust of wind could have snapped off.","But now, he had grown into a towering tree sheltering the millions of lifeforms in the main world.","Lin Yuan received the fried chicken from the Mother of Bloodbath.","The Mother of Bloodbath had not changed its gluttonous nature.","As Lin Yuan looked at the Mother of Bloodbath, he felt a sense of being reunited with an old friend.","The Mother of Bloodbath had saved his life twice.","It was also thanks to the Mother of Bloodbath he managed to find a loyal lapdog for Red Thorn in the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee!","Lin Yuan took a bite out of a drumstick, and sweet and fresh juices exploded in his mouth, bombing his taste buds with delicious flavor. This was just as good as Liu Jie’s work. It was no wonder it came so highly recommended by the Mother of Bloodbath!","Lin Yuan looked at the Mother of Bloodbath with bright eyes before reaching out his right hand.","“Long time no see, my Path Protector!”"]},{"number":2652,"title":"Chapter 2652 The Evolved Main World!","paragraphs":["2652 The Evolved Main World!","As a spider-species fey, the Mother of Bloodbath was naturally cold.","It was inaccurate to say that some feys could lord over others feys solely based on their bloodlines.","High-level feys had bloodlines with different emphases. Thus, their bloodlines could not only be compared in terms of power.","However, the Sky Sundial Jade Spider was the only fey that could control a celestial body, and it was the sun!","The Mother of Bloodbath’s mother, Jade Sundial, and Blood New Moon were extremely cold as well.","This especially applied to Blood New Moon, who had the bloodlines of two different spider-species feys. When the two bloodlines overlapped, they made his personality even more frosty.","However, this frostiness was relative, and he was rather warm toward lifeforms.","The colder a lifeform seemed, the stronger the affection they would feel towards their loved ones.","This was exemplified by how Jade Sundial took care of all the Heavenly Family Feys in the Heavenly Family Cottage and Blood New Moon’s fierce love for his wife and daughter.","Although the feys in Heavenly Family Cottage all treated the Mother of Bloodbath well, objectively speaking, the two most important people in the Mother of Bloodbath’s life were Endless Summer and Lin Yuan.","The Mother of Bloodbath could not be happier that it had found its parents and was now able to experience the joy of being with its family.","However, the time and companionship it shared with Endless Summer in their younger days and all the times Lin Yuan was willing to give up everything to save it were the things that the Mother of Bloodbath truly cherished!","The Mother of Bloodbath gently placed its hand over Lin Yuan’s. Its normally icy hand grew slightly warm.","“Lin Yuan, it’s been too long! I won’t be leaving again! But looking at you now, I don’t think I can continue calling myself your Path Protector!”","Lin Yuan shook his head.","“Mother of Bloodbath, the duty of a Path Protector is not just to protect a person. Moreover, as my Path Protector, don’t you want to know that I’ve grown? Besides, you have already protected me plenty of times. Let’s do battle side by side from now on!”","The Mother of Bloodbath looked hopeful.","It had experienced a life of trying to survive daily in a harsh environment, so it was passionate about increasing its power.","The Mother of Bloodbath also strongly desired to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Its power had also completely transformed in the past six months.","Lin Yuan immediately used True Data to check on the Mother of Bloodbath.","[Fey Name]: Mother of Bloodbath","[Fey Species]: Tarantulas/jade-spider-species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Natural (light)/Blood","[Fey Quality]: Creation VIII","Abilities:","[Execution Sting]: Through the eight sharp chelicerae, the blood and light energy will be injected into the target to control their blood while simultaneously purifying them.","[Eyes of Senluo]: The spider eyes look directly at the core of the blood inside the target and anticipate the target’s next movements based on the blood flow. At the same time, the spider eyes can look through the target to a certain extent.","[Funeral of Light]: After killing a target with a strong enough soul, the target’s soul can be momentarily controlled by light energy. Once the light dries up with soul energy, the target can become a temporary controllable zombie.","[Spider Form Attachment]: Condense its own blood energy into a blood core, which can overload the attacks from the outside world. When the spider core is shattered, the light energy within can restrain a target.","[Blood Control]: Call down belts of sunlight from the sun to restrain and attack targets while activating the blood energy in the target’s body. The flow of fresh blood in the target’s body can be momentarily controlled.","[Hug of Dawn’s Light]: Take in energy from the sun and swallow it to temporarily increase its power. The light energy can also be used to slowly heal injuries.","[Sun Light Drapery]: Activate the stored energy in the body during combat. A jade sundial with the carving of a sun on it will appear behind the Mother of Bloodbath. Every time the energy in its body is used, half of the energy will be taken from the sun. The jade sundial will defend against damage caused by the outside world.","[Hanging Sun Net]: With the sun at the center, its energy will be used up to activate the sun’s energy. The energy from both entities will form a net. The target trapped in the sun net will be restrained temporarily before being released to the surface of the sun.","Exclusive Skill:","[Desire Spider Form]: Increase its affinity for light energy so that the body will not reject excessive light energy but will transform it into hair that can store the light energy. After the devoured light energy tempers inside the body, light energy can be absorbed directly into the body.","[Concealed Spider Shadow]: Stop the flow of its own blood energy, conceal its aura, and transform it into the form of ‘nothing’. It can then use the sun as its eyes to survey the surrounding environment.","[External Blood Bone]: The chelicerae will be fused into other young feys’ bodies so they can become its blood bones. The strength of the external blood bone cannot be higher than the strength of the target being pierced. The dark-type curses or negative soul-type effects of the target can be purified.","[Rich Light Trial]: When causing damage to a target, the target will also be injected with light elements that will have a deadly purging effect.","After Lin Yuan was done looking at the Mother of Bloodbath’s data, he immediately looked astonished.","The Mother of Bloodbath was now a Sovereign X/Creation VIII fey! In just half a year, the Mother of Bloodbath had evolved from a Myth Breed fey to a pinnacle Creation Breed fey!","Unlike Green Vine, the Mother of Bloodbath could not increase its power quickly. Due to the exclusive skill External Blood Bone, it took the Mother of Bloodbath much longer to increase its power than other feys of the same grade.","Clearly, the Mother of Bloodbath had worked hard during the time it spent in Heavenly Family Cottage. The Heavenly Family Cottage had also been willing to provide it with resources.","It was clear that the Mother of Bloodbath had asked him such a question because it assumed that he would not expect it to have improved to such an extent in the past six months.","But it was not just the Mother of Bloodbath who had improved in the past six months. Lin Yuan had been growing continuously as well. In fact, he had improved even more than the Mother of Bloodbath!","When Lin Yuan last looked at the Mother of Bloodbath’s data, it did not have the abilities Sun Light Drapery, Hanging Sun Net, and the exclusive skill Rich Light Trial.","With these two abilities and exclusive skill, the Mother of Bloodbath’s defense and deadliness would increase significantly during battle.","This especially applied to Hanging Sun Net. It could send entities from the net to the sun! The sun was hot enough to even roast Eternal Breed lifeforms to death!","Lin Yuan and the Mother of Bloodbath always talked freely.","He did not hide his knowledge since he knew the Mother of Bloodbath’s power now.","“Mother of Bloodbath, you improved so quickly! I can’t believe that you’re Sovereign X/Creation VIII now! I believe that you’ll be able to reach Immortal Breed very soon!”","The Mother of Bloodbath was not surprised that Lin Yuan had seen through its power.","However, it could not attribute its rapid improvement in the past six months solely to its hard work and the resources from Heavenly Family Cottage. Another significant reason was that the Blood Brew Grapevine had reached Myth Breed.","Due to the fine base that Lin Yuan had laid down for the Blood Brew Grapevine, its production capacity significantly increased after it reached Myth Breed.","The Heavenly Family Fey in the Heavenly Family Cottage, who was the most skilled at cooking and the Mother of Bloodbath addressed as Auntie Flame, had also used the Blood Brew Grapes to produce a wine. This wine could speed up the rate of absorption of blood energy. Without this wine, the Mother of Bloodbath would only have reached Sovereign V/Creation VI now!","Lin Yuan and the Mother of Bloodbath did not spend much time catching up before the Mother of Bloodbath left the imperial court with Lin Yuan.","At this moment, the Radiance Federation was reaching its full capacity of people it could contain. Lin Yuan needed to combine the main world with the five dimensional worlds now and promote the main world to a Class 2 world!","Most of the sea clans and federations had arrived.","Lin Yuan could not afford to wait for those relocating at too slow of a pace.","After all, once he combined the dimensional worlds with the main world, these people only needed to reach one of the dimensional worlds, and they could avoid the effects of the dead spirits crisis. The dimensional lifeforms would not attack the citizens of the human federations.","Black wings opened on Lin Yuan’s back, and he flew up into the sky above the Royal Capital.","At the instant that he activated the Abundance Treasure Tree, Tide Herb Treasure Conch, Spinning Chrysalis, Earth Source Cube, and Demon Evil Tablet, a brilliant rainbow appeared on top of Lin Yuan’s head.","All the light landed on Lin Yuan’s body, and he seemed to be wearing a jacket made of rainbows.","At this moment, all the lifeforms in the Radiance Federation could not stop themselves from looking up at Lin Yuan in the sky.","Under the waterfall of light, Lin Yuan’s body appeared increasingly clear and stalwart. It had an unspeakable aura of sacred mightiness. It was as though he represented the will of the entire main world.","The instant that Lin Yuan was draped in the rainbow jacket, the five dimensional worlds began fusing with the main world.","Just like rivers that joined up with the sea, the main world started to expand.","This caused the earth to begin shaking, and giant waves rose from the sea.","Luckily, the fusing of the main world and dimensional worlds did not cause too many negative effects.","The sea clans that were gathered in the Radiance Federation’s vicinity immediately entered the water world’s sea. It was as though they were being set free!","The citizens from other federations were all watching this with astoundment. All of them raised their heads and looked at the celestial-like young man.","Most of the federation experts knew Lin Yuan.","Firstly, this was because Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple. Secondly, Lin Yuan’s stunning performance during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection had already made Lin Yuan a celebrity and household name among the younger generation!","Lin Yuan’s fame was not restricted to the Radiance Federation. The other federations had also heard of him.","However, it was only at this moment that most of the citizens of the Radiance Federation and other federations were truly witnessing Lin Yuan’s full might.","Lin Yuan thought that fusing the main world with the five dimensional worlds would take some time. Yet, it was done within three hours!","This was also a historic change for the dimensional lifeforms of the five dimensional worlds. From now on, the term ‘dimensional lifeform’ would no longer apply.","Perhaps there were still clear differences between dimensional lifeforms and feys now. But once the epochs changed, most of the dimensional lifeforms would begin transforming into feys.","When the Class 1 world was done fusing with the dimensional worlds, Lin Yuan realized that no other change was taking place and everything was calm.","According to Morbius, the transformation of a Class 1 world to Class 2 would come with a sort of shift. However, Lin Yuan had not sensed any shift. Rather, he felt anticlimactic.","Given that he had no prior experience with this, Lin Yuan did not know where the problem had occurred.","...","Lin Yuan did not know that seven black coffins had just opened simultaneously in the ancient castle where the true Eight Pages of Tower Canon were residing.","First Page Crimson, Second Page Warbler Candle, Third Page Violet Light Green, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, Sixth Page Wave Glow, and Seventh Page Concubine Winding stepped out with grim expressions that soon morphed into elation.","“Someone has evolved this Class 1 world into a Class 2 world! Luckily, we anchored the dead world to the top of this Class 1 world. Otherwise, this Class 1 world would be undergoing the Trial of World Molding! A Class 1 world undergoing the Trial of World Molding to promote to a Class 2 world will definitely attract the attention of experts from that place.”","Fourth Page Cavity Orchid bit her finger as she said with suppressed excitement, “Previously, we were only trying to take over a Class 1 world. But now, we have the chance to take over a Class 2 world! This opportunity is right in front of us. There’s no reason for us not to take it! Let’s begin planning now. I will give some of my root power to Eye Shadow so she can wake up sooner.”"]},{"number":2653,"title":"Chapter 2653 Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s Awakening!","paragraphs":["2653 Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s Awakening!","The Eight Pages of Tower Canon had been working together for thousands of years, and all had their own self-serving thoughts.","Given that they all had to work together, it was inevitable that they would scheme against each other.","However, a few members had genuine ties, albeit this only existed between a few specific members.","Some members could not see eye-to-eye with each other.","No one opposed Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s suggestion. As long as they could ensure that","Eighth Page Eye Shadow would awaken; there was nothing wrong with bringing the plan forward. In truth, they were all still here because they were waiting for Eighth Page Eye Shadow to awaken.","Moreover, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid would be giving her own resources to Eighth Page Eye Shadow, and this did not harm the profits of the other members.","They were all fully focused on the main world’s evolution.","“It looks like the humans from this earth do have some capabilities! We have underestimated them!”","First Page Crimson slowly furrowed his brow when he heard what Second Page Warbler Candle said.","He felt that Second Page Warbler Candle was no different from an idiot. She remained devoted to Fifth Page Falling Rainbow even after that incident.","Aside from him, Second Page Warbler Candle had been awake the longest and had the best grasp on the circumstances of the human factions. On the other hand, Third Page Violet Light Green, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, Sixth Page Wave Glow, and Seventh Page Concubine Winding had not been awake for long and had yet to gain an understanding of the level of power the humans wielded.","Due to her abilities, Second Page Warbler Candle had used Second Page Revival as her eyes and ears. Thus, Second Page Warbler Candle had to better understand the main world than him.","Had Second Page Warbler Candle really never wondered why the human factions could rise abruptly and take control of the dimensional worlds?","Two years ago, the human factions had been terrified of the opening of the dimensional rifts. Aside from the Freedom Federation, who had taken the suggestion of Tower Canon and began harvesting resources from the marsh dimensional world, the Radiance and Azure Federations had not shown any inclination to enter and explore the Class 6 abyss dimensional rift and Class 6 water world dimensional rift.","Previously, First Page Crimson had only been aware that the Dictators from the five dimensional worlds attached to this Class 1 world were helping the humans. However, he had no idea that the humans had already assumed full control of the five dimensional worlds.","One needed to obtain the treasure of a dimensional world in order to take control of it. This required time. Thus, it was clear that the humans had been secretly carrying out their plan to take control of the dimensional worlds.","This caused First Page Crimson to feel as though he was in the open while his opponent was hiding in the shadows. He felt as though he was falling into a trap, and he did not like this feeling at all.","Third Page Violet Light Green noticed the change in First Page Crimson’s expression and raised her head before she asked softly, “Crimson, did something happen? We are all here. If there’s an issue, tell us about it so we can find a way to solve it together!”","First Page Crimson decided that he needed to explain the situation to the rest.","But before he could finish speaking, Second Page Warbler Candle cut him off. “The strongest human has only set his spirit fire alight. A spirit fire expert isn’t worth much. Do we really need to hold a meeting just to discuss this?","“First Page Crimson, I can understand why you’re afraid of Epoch God Palace, but I never thought that you would be afraid of humans, too! Don’t forget about the power we wield!”","Second Page Warbler Candle scoffed, making it clear that she was completely unbothered by the humans from this world.","At this moment, even Third Page Violet Light Green, the group’s most cautious, felt that First Page Crimson was being worried over nothing.","First Page Crimson was actually concerned about the humans from this world! The humans from this world were nothing more than nutrients for the dead world.","Third Page Violet Light Green patted First Page Crimson’s hand.","“Crimson, has any divine kingdom expert emerged among the humans?”","First Page Crimson shook his head as he was unsure of the answer. After all, he had no way of ascertaining the actual amount of combat power that the humans wielded.","The humans’ actions had proven that his information was false.","Now, Tower Canon’s Sleeper’s Revival plan was about to begin. First Page Crimson could not ignore the plan to investigate the power of the human factions.","Frankly, he believed that this should have been Second Page Warbler Candle’s job.","Second Page Warbler Candle had not made use of her abilities to fulfill her role as the scout. He had to do almost everything himself after he woke up.","What had Second Page Warbler Candle been doing in all that time?","The more he thought about it, the angrier First Page Crimson became at Second Page Warbler Candle.","However, he managed to control himself. There was no need to fall out with Second Page Warbler Candle when the plan was about to begin.","“I guess I was just overthinking! Let’s just hope the humans aren’t hiding too many secrets.”","At this point, a thought struck First Page Crimson, and he told Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Sixth Page Wave Glow, “The two of you need to pay attention to Epoch God Palace’s movements to find out if the promotion of this Class 1 world to Class 2 is related to them.”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Sixth Page Wave Glow’s expressions became austere at the mention of Epoch God Palace.","“Crimson, we will pay close attention to them once the plan begins. We will also find out if Epoch God Palace is trying to disturb our activities! They have been in this world longer than we have. Just what are they waiting for? If Epoch God Palace didn’t exist in this world, we wouldn’t be having such a hard time.”","Sixth Page Wave Glow had voiced what everyone else was thinking.","There was no faction in this world that Tower Canon detested more than Epoch God Palace!","However, all they could do was resent them. They could not actually seek out Epoch God Palace and attack them.","The conflict with Epoch God Palace that took place thousands of years ago had prevented Tower Canon from successfully finding out what Epoch God Palace’s secret weapons were. To add insult to injury, Tower Canon had been forced to go into slumber all these thousands of years.","Epoch God Palace was definitely Tower Canon’s archenemy!","Fourth Page Cavity Orchid had already arrived next to the eighth coffin and placed her hand on it.","A river of energy flowed out from Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s body and into the black coffin.","The black coffin started to ring before the door opened.","A short, pale, and skinny girl looked at Fourth Page Cavity Orchid with gleaming eyes before she waved at Fourth Page Cavity Orchid in an almost shy manner.","This girl’s looks were not considered stunning, but her aura was extraordinary. It made one feel enthralled.","First Page Crimson greeted Eighth Page Eye Shadow before he said, “Now that Eye Shadow is awake, we can activate the death aura in the ley lines now!”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow followed behind First Page Crimson and intended to activate the death aura alongside the other Eight Pages. But suddenly, a thought struck her, and she said, “I still haven’t found my Tower of Falling Rainbow. After trying to sense it, I realized I have lost my connection to it. It must have been stolen and hidden away by someone! I have no clue who owns my Secret of the Dead now.”","Seventh Page Concubine Winding said, “I haven’t retrieved my Tower of Concubine Winding. The only ones with towers are First Page Crimson, Second Page Warbler Candle, and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid. We don’t need the Secrets of the Dead to activate the death aura in the ley lines.","“Once we are done, we can find a time to search for your Tower of Falling Rainbow! As long as your Secret of the Dead is still in this world, we can find it. We will only need the Secrets of the Dead at the last step when we fuse the dead world with this Class 2 world!”","Seventh Page Concubine Winding was always good-natured. But at this moment, she was frustrated with Fifth Page Falling Rainbow as well.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had way too many issues. Although Second Page Warbler Candle had made the mistake all those years ago, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had also been deeply involved. Second Page Warbler Candle had been the weapon, while Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had wielded the weapon.","Seventh Page Concubine Winding was much angrier at Fifth Page Falling Rainbow than she was at Second Page Warbler Candle!","When Seventh Page Concubine Winding was done speaking, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid chimed in. “Let’s settle what needs to be done first. If you weren’t impatient and insisted on starting the plan now, I wouldn’t have used my roots to awaken Sister Eye Shadow.”","Eighth Page Eye Shadow glared at Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, and boundless evil flashed in her pretty eyes. However, her lips remained curled in a smile.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow ignored Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s expression and shot a murderous look at Seventh Page Concubine Winding. That mouth of hers sure excelled at driving wedges!","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow cared so much about the Tower of Falling Rainbow because she felt that something must have gone very wrong for her to be unable to sense it. Whoever had hidden the Fifth Page Falling Rainbow away had to be remarkable!","The insect who had been looking after the Tower of Falling Rainbow, Fifth Page Truth, had to be dead by now!","After multiple teleportation trips, the Eight Pages of Tower Canon arrived at a place full of prohibitions.","The ley lines that had started out gold and glittery had turned gray and black. But there was still a large amount of death aura being injected into the already-saturated ley lines.","The roiling gray and black ley lines started to screech, and it was as though the earth itself was crying out.","The Eight Pages of Tower Canon nodded with satisfaction when they saw the color of the ley lines.","After all these years of preparation and waiting, it was finally time to reap their harvests!","Second Page Warbler Candle greedily took a deep breath of all the death aura permeating the air.","“All we need to do now is release some of the dead world’s roots and combine it with the ley lines, and our plan will begin! I suggest that we inject more of the dead world’s roots so that the dead spirits will be awakened faster than expected! This will especially apply to the high-grade dead spirits!”","First Page Crimson did not rebuke Second Page Warbler Candle because he agreed with her.","He could also use this opportunity to see just how capable the human factions were!","This would also let the humans and sea clans trying to make their best preparations know that merely fleeing would not allow them to escape the revival of the dead spirits!","First Page Crimson looked at the other Eight Pages and asked, “What do you think? At first, I only intended on injecting a day’s worth of the dead world’s roots. Let’s inject three day’s worth instead!”","The other members of Tower Canon had no objections because every single one of them was thinking the same thing.","Three days was indeed a good choice. It would hasten the revival of dead spirits while threatening the humans and sea clans and allow them to realize just how stupid their ideas were!","...","Tower Canon had begun the final preparations, and so had Lin Yuan.","The Land Imps were skilled at construction and had become even more skilled after all their time building bases! Thus, their productivity was extremely high.","The sea clans and human federations had all started the final stage of their migration.","The dimensional lifeforms from the dimensional worlds had also established battle lines at the boundaries where they were connected in preparation for the invasion of the dead spirits.","The Land Imps’ construction was in full swing, and all the preparations were complete.","But now, Lin Yuan was facing a serious problem, which was that the dead spirits were themselves full of death aura.","Once a large amount of dead spirits were killed, they would sink into the ground and contaminate the earth. As time went on, the contamination would affect the ley lines that had been fine previously.","Now, he urgently needed to find a way to neutralize the death aura.","Silver Corona could consume death aura, and the Mother of Bloodbath could transform death aura. However, they were both only singular entities. Regardless of how strong they were, they could not handle all of the death aura.","What he needed was a fey that he could give to every soldier fighting on the frontlines.","Otherwise, if the death aura was allowed to soak the lifeforms for too long, the lifeforms’ lifespans would also be affected.","It was very difficult to solve this issue, especially because it involved nurturing a fey. Lin Yuan knew that this would take a very long time.","Luckily, once Lin Yuan became aware of Tower Canon’s plan, he sent the army of Hundred Questions Beasts off to do research.","Finally, the research was showing signs of achieving results.","Some of these feys nurtured by the army of Hundred Questions Beasts indeed had relevant and beneficial abilities. However, they could not reproduce easily.","As a result, it would take two to three months before there were enough of these feys that could absorb death aura to be sent to every soldier in the battle.","Lin Yuan needed a fey that could be nurtured in large quantities within a month!"]},{"number":2654,"title":"Chapter 2654 Dead Decay Earthworm!","paragraphs":["2654 Dead Decay Earthworm!","Although Weng Queji was a Class 5 Creation Master, he rarely met with Lin Yuan.","Whenever Weng Queji came to see him, Lin Yuan knew that Weng Queji either needed resources or had achieved results in his research.","Lin Yuan last gave Weng Queji resources a month ago.","He provided Weng Queji with an immense amount of resources each time. There was no way that Weng Queji could finish using up all the resources within a month. Thus, it was more likely that Weng Queji had accomplished something with his research.","Lin Yuan hurriedly asked Wen Yu to bring Weng Queji to his room.","Upon reaching Lin Yuan, Weng Queji did not waste time speaking and immediately summoned a small pink worm. There were purple and black star-shaped spots over the pink worms that elongated when the worm stretched its body.","Weng Queji spoke with his voice quivering with excitement, “Young Master, this worm is able to absorb death aura. Although its absorption abilities aren’t strong, it can digest the death aura quickly. It can also reproduce very quickly. We don’t have to wait for it to reproduce on its own and cut it up to manually produce more of it ourselves!”","At first, Weng Queji joined Lin Yuan because he wanted to find a place to rest and take shelter in his later years.","But after he spent some time with Lin Yuan, Weng Queji got a glimpse of a wider world. Despite being a Class 5 Creation Master, he was an ignoramus compared to Lin Yuan.","Previously, he had known nothing about the dimensional worlds. But in the past six months, he had many opportunities to enter the dimensional worlds.","Most importantly, Lin Yuan was trying to save the world. This act triggered the righteous streak within Weng Queji.","Moreover, Lin Yuan had just given him the Lifespan Mouse.","From now on, all he needed to do was provide the Lifespan Mouse with vitality, and his own lifespan would be lengthened continuously. Essentially, he had gained an endless lifespan! He no longer had to worry about his age.","Weng Queji’s appearance had not changed in just a short few days, but his previous geriatric aura had completely disappeared.","Weng Queji had also done research when he was under Fifth Page Truth. His research then had also attained significant positive results.","However, he never shared the fruits of his research with Fifth Page Truth.","A Class 5 Creation Master’s selfishness could not be seen from the outside.","Weng Queji had completed his research of this death aura-consuming worm so quickly because it had been a failed product of his fey evolution experiments. When he realized that his failed product could be of use, he immediately conducted further experiments on it and brought it to Lin Yuan once it met his satisfaction.","After hearing Weng Queji’s description, Lin Yuan immediately began examining the worm.","He saw that this fey known as the Dead Decay Earthworm could not only consume death aura but could also clean bones and corpses!","If there were too many dead spirits, the troops only needed the slightest of fey nurturing knowledge, and they would be able to cut the Dead Decay Earthworms’ bodies to manually reproduce them.","“Elder Weng, you have done a big favor for the entire world!”","When Weng Queji heard this, he knew Lin Yuan intended to use this fey.","Weng Queji hurriedly took out a large porcelain tank that was filled with the Dead Decay Earthworms.","“Young Master, when I was experimenting on cutting the Dead Decay Earthworm, I discovered that they can only reproduce naturally if not cut into more than four segments! If they are cut too many times, they will need the help of spirit fluids and guidance to reproduce.”","Wen Yu stood next to Weng Queji and took notes intently while he spoke.","She knew that the Dead Decay Earthworms would soon be nurtured in large quantities by the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters before they were sent into battle.","Everything that Weng Queji said would be helpful knowledge for the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters, who would be nurturing the Dead Decay Earthworms. It would provide the low-class Creation Masters with guidance and help them to nurture the Dead Decay Earthworms as quickly as possible.","Lin Yuan received the porcelain tank from Weng Queji and took out ten of them to keep for himself before he handed the tank to Wen Yu and said with utmost solemnness, “Wen Yu, give the Dead Decay Earthworms to Master!”","Previously, Lin Yuan liked to do everything himself, especially when it came to nurturing feys.","But as time passed and Lin Yuan grew, he came to understand something. It was not always a good thing to do everything himself!","Every person excelled in their own way. A leader needed to delegate the right task to the right person.","Lin Yuan kept ten of the Dead Decay Earthworms for himself to ensure that if there was an accident that caused all the Dead Decay Earthworms to die, he would still have some left that he could use to replace those that died.","Tackling the dead spirits crisis would take center stage for the next few millennia. Thus, they would need more than just one fey to handle all of the death aura and dead spirits corpses.","Lin Yuan would not instruct the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to stop nurturing the other feys just because he now had the Dead Decay Earthworms.","Wen Yu was well aware of the significance of the Dead Decay Earthworm. She carefully held the porcelain tank before using Dance of Paper to travel to the Radiant Moon Palace.","The Moon Empress had also been researching feys that could absorb death aura.","The Radiance Federation had three Class 5 Creation Masters. They should have nurtured numerous special feys in the past few centuries. Most of the time, these special feys could solve issues, or they could serve as the foundation to nurture other feys that could solve the issues at hand.","However, the Moon Empress, Chef Supreme, and the Bamboo Monarch had not nurtured any unorthodox or bizarre feys because they had been focusing on common resources that could be distributed to the other members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","Otherwise, the Radiance Federation’s top combat power would not have evolved so quickly and closed the gap between the Radiance Federation and Freedom Federation while surpassing the Azure Federation!","The Moon Empress had been sleeping as little as necessary but had not been satisfied with her progress. Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch had not reported any successes either.","While the Moon Empress was feeling rather vexed, Mystic Moon knocked on the door of her breeding room.","Normally, no one dared to disturb the Moon Empress when she was in her breeding room.","When she heard the knock, the Moon Empress froze, and she immediately assumed that something had happened. She anxiously left the breeding room, “Mystic Moon, has something happened to Little Yuna?”","Mystic Moon had been beside himself with anxiousness. However, he could not do anything about his anxiousness as he could not help the Moon Empress.","But now, there was finally a fey that could absorb death aura!","With this, the Moon Empress no longer needed to hole up in the breeding room after she was done with her official tasks.","The Moon Empress quickly said, “Mystic Moon, let me take a look at this fey! Since Little Yuan sent this fey to me, I should be the one to nurture it!”","Mystic Moon placed the porcelain he received from Wen Yu in front of the Moon Empress.","The Moon Empress looked at the earthworms inside, and uncontrollable excitement spread across her face.","“This really came in the nick of time! Mystic Moon, go and inform the Bamboo Monarch and Creation Master to gather all of the Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation.","“Then, tell Cicada Song to use the name of the Major Federation Union to gather all the leaders of the federations and sea clans and instruct them to send people to nurture this earthworm. We must ensure that this earthworm can be used on a large scale within the next two weeks before the dead spirits crisis begins!”","Lin Yuan had always admired the Moon Empress’ execution abilities. The operation of nurturing the Dead Decay Earthworm was rolled out swiftly.","Since the five dimensional worlds had already been fused with the main world, Lin Yuan returned all the Samsara Realm and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators.","However, Eternal Source remained by the Moon Empress’ side to protect her as her personal bodyguard.","The dimensional lifeforms were the first line of defense against the dead spirits crisis.","The dimensional lifeforms were very wild and difficult to control. But luckily, Lin Yuan had absolute control over all of them.","When Wen Yu was managing a few of the dimensional worlds, she had assigned every Samsara Realm to be the leader of an army. This gave them some stakes in the form of authority and thus maintained stability.","The Samsara Realm Dictators only needed to receive orders, and the orders would be perfectly communicated down the ranks.","Now, it was time to put the system to the test.","Lin Yuan prepared for the beginning of the dead spirits crisis while simultaneously giving orders to the Hollow Earth, Rock Underworld, and Mountain Furrow to instruct them to organize all the Land Imps and resources in the subterranean world.","Lin Yuan needed to build bases in the dimensional worlds as soon as possible.","Given that the ley lines in the dimensional worlds were unaffected and no dead spirits would emerge from them, there was no need to cover the ground with metal-type stone boards. This significantly lowered the amount of work and challenge of the task.","Each team consisting of 10,000 Land Imps could finish building a city within a day.","Hollow Earth, Mountain Furrow, and Rock Underworld were the strongest subterranean Samsara Realm Dictators, and all of them were obsessed with wealth.","Even if the consumption of the precious metal-type spiritual ingredients would not be able to increase their own powers, they would not give them to their subordinates. Instead, they would store it away for themselves.","They also used the Ten Thousand River Rock Willow to seek out the mineral veins produced by the Mine-Birthing Well and took over control of the subterranean world’s resources.","As a result of this, the subterranean world had much fewer regular Apostles and Dictators than the other four dimensional worlds.","Lin Yuan did not even know where he should begin to criticize such actions!","Luckily, their decisions had created an abundant store of metal-type spiritual ingredients that could be used to build the bases.","Lin Yuan assigned the job of overseeing the dimensional worlds to the white-clothed followers.","The white-clothed followers still needed more training before they could stand on their own two feet. This was a good chance to train them.","Bai Qinghuan had done a good job of building the Radiance Federation’s base and had finished Lin Yuan’s plan a week ahead of his expectations.","Because of this, Lin Yuan also assigned her to oversee the second phase of base construction.","Bai Qinghuan was both excited and overjoyed by Lin Yuan’s reliance on her.","Now that Lin Yuan was assigning her a large task on the heels of her recent completion of another giant task, it meant that Lin Yuan recognized her skills.","It did not matter to Bai Qinghuan whether she did a good job or not. What mattered to her was whether Lin Yuan recognized her abilities! If Lin Yuan did not acknowledge her, it would not matter how good of a job she did.","Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress, and the others who knew of the dead spirits crisis were all worried about the future of the main world. They were afraid that the only thing that would be left in the wake of the dead spirits crisis was a space devoid of life.","Regardless of how much preparation Lin Yuan made, he could not be fully confident that he had perfectly solved the issue. He was still worried.","Before the dead spirits crisis began, Lin Yuan had no way of knowing the exact strength of the dead spirits crisis.","However, Bai Qinghuan was not worried at all. All she felt was boundless thrill and excitement!","Bai Qinghuan saw the dead spirits crisis as a sandbox game, allowing her to demonstrate all her skills.","Bai Qinghuan did not care about any lifeform in the main world or about the survival of the federations and various species.","Lin Yuan already knew that Bai Qinghuan had psychopathic tendencies. She was always merciless and utterly self-serving! The only way to control her was to scare her into submission before offering her benefits that would keep her in check.","When Lin Yuan dispatched Bai Qinghuan, he always placed Zhou Luo and Endless Summer by her side.","Zhou Luo was steadfast, and Endless Summer was composed. Both of them knew why Lin Yuan stationed them next to Bai Qinghuan.","Once she stepped out of line, they would immediately discipline her.","Moreover, as long as Lin Yuan provided Bai Qinghuan with benefits and allowed her to see a bright future for herself, she would be very easy to control!"]},{"number":2655,"title":"Chapter 2655 The Erupted Dead Spirits Well!","paragraphs":["2655 The Erupted Dead Spirits Well!","At the moment that Lin Yuan was done communicating with Bai Qinghuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper, he sensed that the entire Radiance Federation had started trembling. It was as though there was something underground that was slamming into the Radiance Federation!","Lin Yuan’s heart skipped a beat. He realized that the dead spirits crisis was beginning! Tower Canon was starting their Sleeper’s Revival plan!","Lin Yuan was not the only one who could feel the tremors. Every lifeform present in the Radiance Federation could clearly sense it.","The Radiance Federation had already released the news of the dead spirits crisis. Every citizen in the Radiance Federation was aware of this event. All of them had accumulated resources to prepare themselves to face the dead spirits crisis.","Nonetheless, they could not help but be gripped by fear.","The movements became more violent, but the tremors did not intensify. At this point, the sounds underground had exceeded 100 decibels.","Although he had laid down the metal-type stone boards, Lin Yuan could not be certain that his defenses were sufficient as the dead spirits would be emerging from underground.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had placed Land Imps and sufficiently capable experts in every city. If the metal-type stone boards in any area were damaged, the Land Imps would be able to build the Dead Spirits Wells and use them as funnels to concentrate the direction from which the dead spirits emerged.","Aside from the Dead Spirits Wells that would be built after the metal-type stone boards were broken, Bai Qinghuan also built vents in advance. These would serve as proxy Dead Spirits Wells.","??","The area in a 100-kilometer radius around these proxy Dead Spirits Wells had already been cleared. This way, even if the might of the dead spirits crisis was underestimated, it would not cause harm to the environment and citizens in the area.","The dead spirits crisis was no light matter. The metal-type stone boards were indeed very capable of restraining the dead spirits. But if no vents were created and the dead spirits were somehow able to find a gap, the entire Radiance Federation would turn into a pressure cooker that had been sealed tight.","The Dead Spirits Wells would serve as the depressurizing valve on pressure cookers that prevented explosions from happening.","By now, dead spirits should already be rushing out of the Dead Spirits Wells.","It would not be long before the battle progress was reported to him, and Lin Yuan could assess the danger level of the dead spirits crisis.","At this moment, Lin Yuan was very glad that he had worked overtime and had not wasted any time.","The consequences would be unthinkable if the Radiance Federation’s defenses had not been completed!","The dead spirits crisis affected not only the land but the sea as well. Lin Yuan did not keep the decision-making power over the sea to himself. Instead, he allowed the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the Samsara Realm Dictators from the water world to take charge. Each party held an equal share of power.","Since the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the sea clans had migrated over and taken up the water world’s resources, the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s rulers were reasonably disadvantaged when it came to deliberating with the Samsara Realm Dictators from the water world.","But it went without saying that this was also because the Vast Sea Labyrinth respected Lin Yuan. They knew he was the true ruler of the water world’s dimensional lifeforms.","Zuo Ming and You Zhe took turns overseeing all the Dead Spirits Wells situated to the west of the Royal Capital.","It happened to be Zuo Ming’s shift today. At the instant that the ground began to shake, Zuo Ming instantly issued the order.","Hence, the Spirit Guards and City Guards on sentry duty were already in position and surrounding the Dead Spirits Wells. They were waiting for the Dead Spirits Wells to erupt.","No one had an exact grasp of what the dead spirits crisis would entail. After all, this was the first time such a calamity took place in the world! They had zero frames of reference!","Even if they wanted to build a simulation, they had no input that they could use to simulate an outcome.","Thus, Zuo Ming had trained the City Guards and Spirit Guards using the same method as when wild feys and dimensional lifeforms attacked cities in the past.","Zuo Ming had used the strictest methods to train these Spirit Guards and City Guards. But he still felt that it was far from enough!","Zuo Ming had sent out his order instantaneously, and the Spirit Guards and City Guards had acted swiftly.","The Spirit Guards and City Guards did not even have time to take in a breath before the first wave of dead spirits burst forth from the Dead Spirits Wells.","The dead spirits were not only singular entities. There were also specters that existed in soul states.","Luckily, the Dead Spirits Wells had many Soul-Revealing Crystals embedded into them. The Soul-Revealing Crystals could reveal the silhouettes of the specters. This allowed the City Guards to use their feys to take down the specters!","The Dead Spirits Wells only had a diameter of ten meters each. However, the number of dead spirits that were surging out had far exceeded everyone’s initial expectations.","Luckily, there were more than enough reinforcements, and the sentries could be rotated out hourly to rest.","The battle between the main world and dead spirits had officially begun!","There were emperor-class and thearch-class experts guarding every Dead Spirits Well.","Because of the large amounts of Creation Master resources that Lin Yuan had provided the Radiance Federation, the number of emperor-class and thearch-class experts in the Radiance Federation had increased significantly.","These emperor-class and thearch-class experts would not bother with the low-grade dead spirits as the Spirit and City Guards would handle them. The emperor-class and thearch-class experts focused on the dead spirits that were Diamond grade and above.","The initial wave of dead spirits had been overwhelming, and the troops from the Radiance Federation, emperor-class and thearch- class experts, as well as Zuo Ming, had all been shocked.","But once they became accustomed to this magnitude, the Radiance Federation’s troops were able to adjust slowly.","However, this did not make Zuo Ming happy in the slightest.","This was because he knew that this was only the beginning. This was the new normal.","The troops were only just holding on. In a week, they would be exhausted.","The death aura was spreading continuously. They would not cause much harm to lifeforms in the short run, but as the lifeforms absorbed more and more of the death aura, the Radiance Federation’s troops would quickly grow old and decay. They might even become dead spirits themselves!","Luckily, there were Corpse-Consuming Vines planted in the five- kilometer radius around the Dead Spirits Wells.","These Corpse-Consuming Vines had been brought in from the marsh world. In past experiments, they proved to not only be unaffected by death aura but would even thrive in an environment rich with death aura.","These Corpse-Consuming Vines could handle the dead spirits that were Bronze grade and below.","The Corpse-Consuming Vines would reproduce and grow stronger after consuming the dead spirits.","After a day passed, not only had the Corpse-Consuming Vines not been destroyed by the dead spirits, but they were even stronger than they had been a day ago. The Corpse-Consuming Vines would definitely be a major killing machine of dead spirits!","Unfortunately, the Corpse-Consuming Vines could only handle the dead spirits’ corpses. They could not absorb the death aura from the dead spirits.","Zuo Ming intended to tell all this to You Zhe when he arrived to take over for his shift.","Zuo Ming knew that the hardest workers in the Radiance Federation were the Creation Masters.","The Creation Masters were all working overtime to either nurture the feys that could be used in the dead spirits crisis or concocting healing potions.","Once the current circumstances were reported, it would only add more stress to the Creation Master.","Nonetheless, Zuo Ming believed that he needed to bring this matter up!","Moreover, he needed to ask Chief Guard Ye to contact the Moon Empress so this matter could be regarded as one of the highest priorities!","There were an endless number of dead spirits surging out of the Dead Spirits Wells, but there were not unlimited troops in the Radiance Federation.","If the issue of the death aura was not addressed, the Radiance Federation would not last even a decade.","Suddenly, a blue beast-shaped dead spirit that was almost four meters long spewed flames comprising of death aura at an emperor-class expert.","Half of the emperor-class expert’s lion-species fey’s body was burnt to a crisp. A large amount of death aura entered the emperor-class expert’s fey’s body.","Zuo Ming immediately killed this dead spirit that was the equivalent of a pinnacle Creation Breed fey.","This was the first emperor-class expert injury of the day!","Zuo Ming hurriedly sent someone to take the emperor-class expert’s fey to the healing team so it could be healed.","At this juncture, every emperor-class expert and thearch-class expert were extremely precious.","If the emperor-class experts and thearch-class experts’ feys died, the emperor-class and thearch-class experts’ spiritual energy would be damaged.","If that happened, it would take a long time before the emperor- class and thearch-class experts could return to battle.","Zuo Ming personally killed numerous beast-shaped dead spirits that were the equivalent of Creation Breed feys.","He realized the beast-shaped dead spirits could emulate elemental energy using death aura.","The elemental energy emulated from death aura could affect the elements just like regular elemental energy. 2","When the attacks made contact with a living creature, their deadliness came from the death aura contaminating and decaying the body.","It was difficult for healing-type feys to heal such injuries. The healing type had already told Zuo Ming about this numerous times. If humans, or rather all living creatures, wanted to tackle the dead spirits, they would need to nurture feys that could effectively heal bodies that were infected with death aura.","Zuo Ming had noted down all of these discoveries.","The dead spirits crisis had only just begun. Now was the time to discover issues and find ways to fix them.","Zuo Ming rubbed his temples. His mind was more exhausted than his body was.","At this moment, Zuo Ming’s subordinate, who had only just left, came running back.","Zuo Ming furrowed his brow. He thought that something had happened to the healing team.","The healing team had already reported numerous problems to him, all of which he had noted down.","The only way to address the issue would be for the Creation Masters to nurture appropriate feys and hand them out to be contracted by the healing-type spirit qi professionals.","The issue would naturally solve itself once the healing-type spirit qi professionals began nurturing the feys that could heal death aura- related injuries.","“Lord Zuo Ming, Lord Lin Yuan say that he wants to come and take a look at the Dead Spirits Wells, as well as deliver resources. You...”","Before his subordinate could finish speaking, he was interrupted by Zuo Ming, “Elder Qiu, if Lord Lin Yuan wants to come to check on the Dead Spirits Wells, why didn’t you just bring him over? What was the point of reporting this to me? Did you think that I would turn Lord Lin Yuan down?”","Zuo Ming saw Lin Yuan for the first time at the Guard Ye Banquet. Zuo Ming saw Lin Yuan as a junior, just like how he saw Liu Jie. However, he would never dare to treat Lin Yuan like a junior!","Zuo Ming was not alone. No one in the entire Radiance Federation would dare to treat Lin Yuan like a junior!","Lin Yuan was the world’s true savior in this dead spirits crisis.","Zuo Ming did not know how Lin Yuan managed to create such a miracle at his young age. But this did not get in the way of him feeling admiration for Lin Yuan.","Elder Qiu could not help but scratch his head awkwardly.","“I was going to bring Lord Lin Yuan over, but he said that he wanted to observe the procedures of battle. You are the commander. He told me to come to report to you! I couldn’t go against his wishes.”","Elder Qiu spoke with praise and respect for Lin Yuan.","Anyone who had ever been to battle knew that only one commander could wield absolute authority.","Yet, in spite of his young age, Lin Yuan was not only aware of this but even knew how to act accordingly.","This was enough to show his exceptional character!","Zuo Ming urged anxiously, “Now, you have come to ask me. Go and bring Lord Lin Yuan over here now!”","Elder Qiu rolled his eyes.","He had been with Zuo Ming for such a long time. They had worked together for decades. But this was the first time that he had seen Zuo Ming in such an anxious state!","It was likely that Zuo Ming had many things that he wanted to report to Lin Yuan.","This thought pained Elder Qiu.","Once Lord Zuo Ming reported the situation to Lin Yuan, the stress would be shifted onto Lin Yuan’s shoulders.","Damn that Tower Canon! Why did they have to go and try to destroy the world?","Even if they had a means of tackling the dead spirits crisis, many lifeforms would have to lose their lives during the transition to the sixth epoch!","When Lin Yuan followed Elder Qiu to the Dead Spirits Wells, he could sense the extremely high concentration of death aura around him.","Luckily, Weng Queji had nurtured the Dead Decay Earthworms. In the past two days, the Dead Decay Earthworms had already been bred at a rapid rate.","Lin Yuan had come to check on the Dead Spirits Wells because he wanted to gain an understanding of the dead spirits crisis. If he found that the humans were not sufficiently equipped to handle the dead spirits crisis, he would do what he could to help them.","Additionally, he wanted to put the first batch of Dead Decay Earthworms to use and see if they could help address the issue of the death aura. If the Dead Decay Earthworms could not achieve the intended effect, there would be no point in nurturing them.","Lin Yuan asked the gray-haired man next to him, “How many injuries and deaths have there been in the past day?”"]},{"number":2656,"title":"Chapter 2656 Lin Yuan’s Rewards!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2656 Lin Yuan’s Rewards!","Qiu Kaixuan answered honestly, “Lord Lin Yuan, there are indeed some deaths and injuries. However, the death rate isn’t high. Most are just severely injured. Although we have prepared many medical teams, the regular healing-type feys are limited in their abilities to treat injuries caused by dead spirits. I’m sure Lord Zuo Ming also intends to report this issue to you!”","Lin Yuan immediately frowned. The issue he had been worried about had indeed come to pass!","It was truly not easy to handle dead spirits.","The dead spirits’ attacks could cause significant harm to living creatures that could not be healed via traditional methods.","This issue had dawned on Lin Yuan a day ago.","Although Lin Yuan had just arrived at the Dead Spirits Wells, the Moon Empress had already sent people to capture some dead spirits and deliver them to the Radiant Moon Palace. She then distributed the dead spirits among Creation Masters so they could research the dead spirits.","After their experiments, the Creation Masters realized that the dead spirits’ attacks could cause devastating damage to living creatures. Moreover, traditional healing methods could not stem the death aura’s infection of the body’s muscles and tissue.","The Creation Masters informed the Moon Empress of their discovery, and she instructed them to begin researching solutions before she relayed the discovery to Lin Yuan.","It had become a matter of utmost importance to develop feys that could effectively heal death aura.","Lin Yuan had come to test out the Dead Decay Earthworms. Once they were determined to be actually useful, Lin Yuan would immediately send the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to stop their research into feys that could consume death aura and divert their efforts to researching healing-type feys instead.","The Dead Spirits Wells would not stop spewing dead spirits. Lin Yuan needed to find a way to heal the Radiance Federation’s troops. Otherwise, as the death aura continued to contaminate their bodies, the size of the Radiance Federation’s army would only shrink!","“Apart from the healing situation, have you discovered anything else? You can tell me anything you think is important. As long as it affects the safety of the Radiance Federation’s troops, I will address it immediately! We can try our best to find ways to tackle issues that don’t seem to have a solution! All of the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters have been activated. They will support the Radiance Federation’s troops and solve any issue that crops up.”","Qiu Kaixuan felt a sense of warmth wash over him when he heard this.","Lin Yuan’s words were evidence of the Radiance Federation’s upper echelon’s attitude towards their troops.","Qiu Kaixuan believed that with the support from the top Creation Masters, regardless of how dangerous the dead spirits crisis was or how long it went on, victory would never be an impossibility!","Qiu Kaixuan was Zuo Ming’s subordinate who was in charge of organizing information. He was aware of all the problems that the Radiance Federation’s troops had encountered during the battle against the dead spirits.","However, Zuo Ming had to be the one to report all of this to Lin Yuan. If he told Lin Yuan everything now, Zuo Ming would have nothing to report later.","“Lord Lin Yuan, our intelligence team has reported all of the issues we encountered over the course of this past day. Lord Zuo Ming will tell you all about them when you see him! He is currently waiting for you at the commanding watchtower!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Zuo Ming had done well by assigning the intelligence team to collate and organize all the problems. When the problems were recorded, it would be easier for the humans to gain a detailed understanding of the dead spirits crisis.","The earlier they discovered the problems, the sooner they could solve them and ensure the safety of the Radiance Federation’s troops. This would minimize the damage done by the dead spirits.","However, one day’s worth of observation was not enough to gain a comprehensive view of all the issues of the dead spirits crisis.","There would be more types of dead spirits emerging.","The battle against the dead spirits had only just begun. There could be new problems arising anytime.","Lin Yuan had already resolved himself to deal with all the problems and challenges.","He caught sight of Zuo Ming standing in front of the commanding watchtower, who had just killed two Creation Breed dead spirits.","Black wings sprouted from Lin Yuan’s back, and he flew over to Zuo Ming.","Lin Yuan did not immediately ask Zuo Ming for updates on the current circumstances like he had done with Qiu Kaixuan.","Although Qiu Kaixuan had not gone into detail, he had told Lin Yuan everything that was important.","Now, the most important thing for Lin Yuan to do was distribute the Dead Decay Earthworms and solve the most pressing issue on the troops’ plate.","When Zuo Ming saw Lin Yuan, he hurriedly bowed respectfully, “Lord Lin Yuan, welcome. Please proceed with your observation and assessment of the Dead Spirits Wells.”","Lin Yuan was still only a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. He was not even a Radiance Envoy. But to Zuo Ming, he was no different from a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","Otherwise, he would not have invited Lin Yuan to observe and assess the Dead Spirits Wells.","Lin Yuan took out four Silver fey storage boxes from his spatial equipment and handed them to Zuo Ming before he said with utmost seriousness, “Senior Zuo Ming, these four fey storage boxes contain the Dead Decay Earthworms. The Dead Decay Earthworms can take apart the corpses of the dead spirits and absorb their death aura. Open one of the fey storage boxes and distribute the Dead Decay Earthworms within so they can handle the corpses of dead spirits.","“As for the remaining three fey storage boxes of Dead Decay Earthworms, make sure that every Radiance Federation soldier receives the Dead Decay Earthworm during the changing of shifts. Then, we can see if the Dead Decay Earthworms can make an actual impact!”","Zuo Ming could not stop his cheeks from spreading with delight. Lin Yuan was really here to provide them with whatever they needed!","The most urgent issue for the Radiance Federation’s troops was to deal with the corpses of the dead spirits and lower the concentration of death aura in the air.","At first, Zuo Ming had not intended to report this matter to Lin Yuan.","Yet, without him needing to do so, Lin Yuan had already brought him the solution in the form of the fey known as the Dead Decay Earthworm.","Even if the Dead Decay Earthworms could not fully fix the issue, they would definitely be able to help take some of the heat off. This would make things easier for the Radiance Federation’s troops and increase their battle endurance.","Zuo Ming immediately sent his men to distribute the Dead Decay Earthworms as per Lin Yuan’s orders.","Once the first Silver fey storage box was delivered to the battleground, its contents were poured out.","Zuo Ming had asked Lin Yuan and confirmed that the Corpse-Consuming Vines would not harm the Dead Decay Earthworms. This set his worries at ease. If the Corpse-Consuming Vines would also attack the Dead Decay Earthworms, the Dead Decay Earthworms would not have the time to consume the dead spirit corpses before they were gobbled up by the Corpse-Consuming Vines!","Lin Yuan was much more anxious than Zuo Ming. Zuo Ming was only hoping that the Dead Decay Earthworms would be able to alleviate some of the pressure, while Lin Yuan was hoping that they would lead to a miracle.","This would free up the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters and the army of Hundred Questions Beasts so they could move on to addressing other issues. They would no longer need to continue researching the feys that could digest dead spirit corpses and absorb death aura!","The Dead Decay Earthworm did not feel hunger or fullness. As long as there was food, it would begin eating and digesting.","These Dead Decay Earthworms had only just been born from being cut from other Dead Decay Earthworms. Thus, they could not even be considered feys.","When the Dead Decay Earthworms made contact with the dead spirit corpses, they immediately sprung into action and chomped on the dead spirit corpses while they crawled around.","Although it was difficult for the Dead Decay Earthworms to make headway in the ocean of dead spirits at first, once they absorbed some death aura and slowly grew stronger, they were eventually able to use their sharp teeth to break apart the dead spirits’ bodies and move through the sea of dead spirits.","The Dead Decay Earthworms were not picky. Any part of the dead spirits’ body that contained death aura would become part of their meal.","When the Dead Decay Earthworms were sent into the battleground, Lin Yuan instructed Zuo Ming to send out the order for the Radiance Federation’s troops to cut the Dead Decay Earthworms once they grew longer than 15 centimeters so they could produce even more of the Dead Decay Earthworms!","As the Dead Spirits Wells continued to spew dead spirits, many Dead Decay Earthworms would be killed. They might also be accidentally killed when the humans were fighting with the dead spirits.","However, as the Radiance Federation’s troops enabled the Dead Decay Earthworms to reproduce, the Dead Decay Earthworms’ numbers would not shrink but would grow.","The Dead Decay Earthworms could absorb some of the death aura in the air but not a significant quantity of it.","Nonetheless, this flaw did not warrant criticism as the death aura in the environment would quickly be fully absorbed due to the sheer quantity of the Dead Decay Earthworms.","With the Dead Decay Earthworms consuming the death aura from the dead spirits crisis, no more death aura was released from the Dead Decay Earthworms into the air.","Lin Yuan waited and watched the Dead Spirits Wells for an entire day.","Eventually, he concluded that the Dead Decay Earthworms would be able to fully handle the task of clearing the dead spirit corpses and suppressing the death aura.","Moreover, the Dead Decay Earthworms could also be linked to the Corpse-Consuming Vines.","The Dead Decay Earthworms would build nests under the Corpse-Consuming Vines and use their roots to hide from the dead spirits.","The Dead Decay Earthworms’ by-products would fertilize the Corpse-Consuming Vines and increase the speed of their growth.","Even if many powerful dead spirits burst forth from the Dead Spirits Wells and damaged the line of defense comprising of the Dead Decay Earthworms and Corpse-Consuming Vines, all they needed to do was spread some of the Corpse-Consuming Vines’ seeds and release some of the Dead Decay Earthworms.","As the Corpse-Consuming Vines killed and consumed the dead spirits, they produced fruits that were full of seeds. All the Radiance Federation’s troops needed to do was pluck these fruits and gather them before drying them. When the dried fruits were crushed, they would be able to attain a large amount of seeds.","At that moment, Lin Yuan could finally relax.","After a day of observation, Lin Yuan noticed many urgent problems that needed to be solved.","One of these issues was the healing. Another important issue was the increase of the Radiance Federation’s troops’ power.","Lin Yuan intended to invest some of his resources into the Radiance Federation’s troops so they could become stronger as quickly as possible.","He would tackle the dead spirits crisis by fueling war with warfare.","Now that he had come to this decision, Lin Yuan bid goodbye to Zuo Ming before he went to check the other Dead Spirits Wells.","Due to the overwhelming number of dead spirits that had burst through the metal-type stone boards, the Radiance Federation had built an additional 137 Dead Spirits Wells. 130 of them had been built instantly, while the other seven had been after a time lag as the eruption of dead spirits had been too powerful, and the Land Imps had been unable to build them instantly. This delay had resulted in substantial damages.","Luckily, the experts had sealed off these areas in advance. Otherwise, the consequences would have been dire.","This combat result exceeded Lin Yuan’s expectations as it protected most of the Radiance Federation’s citizens.","Lin Yuan investigated all the Dead Spirits Wells around the Royal Capital and distributed all of the Dead Decay Earthworms.","The other cities also received urgent deliveries of the Dead Decay Earthworms from Ostrich Logistics.","The Dead Decay Earthworms were immediately sent into battle once they were nurtured.","When Lin Yuan was done with his investigation, he reported all his findings to the Moon Empress.","He now ascertained the subsequent research direction for the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters.","Once Lin Yuan was done telling the Moon Empress about the situation, he gave her three Diamond fey storage boxes.","“Master, the resources in these three Diamond fey storage boxes will be able to help spirit qi professionals increase their power. The troops who are fighting the dead spirits all volunteered for the job. All of them answered the call to enter the battle.","“I hope that these resources can reach these troops and help them increase their power as quickly as possible, thereby increasing the power of the Radiance Federation. We will strengthen them via the method of fueling war with warfare!","“From now on, I will continue to supply them with resources. I suggest that we come up with a comprehensive reward and punishment system. Those who do well will receive high-quality feys. These troops deserve a good future for their willingness to give their all in protecting this world.”","The Moon Empress could not help but gulp twice when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","She lapsed into momentary silence when she saw the three Diamond fey storage boxes full of resources that Lin Yuan was holding out.","The Moon Empress was once again stupefied by the resources that Lin Yuan possessed.","If these resources were given to the Radiance Federation’s troops on the frontlines of battling the dead spirits, they would grow stronger rapidly.","This would not only prevent the Radiance Federation’s army from shrinking but would also raise their motivation."]},{"number":2657,"title":"Chapter 2657 The Attacking Dimensional Lifeforms!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2657 The Attacking Dimensional Lifeforms!","The Moon Empress knew rewards were the most effective way to spur fighting spirit and motivation. However, it was not easy to shoulder the cost of such generosity.","Even if the Radiance Federation was squeezed dry of all of its resources, it would not be able to afford the cost of all the rewards that Lin Yuan was offering! This was because the rewards he was offering were of a very high level.","Even if the Spirit-Mouthed Peonies were disregarded, the Moon Empress had no idea where and how Lin Yuan got his hands on the hundreds of thousands of Bronze/Epic and Bronze/Legend feys!","It would take hundreds of Class 4 Creation Masters decades in order to produce so many high-quality Bronze feys, and this was only if they worked tirelessly.","Yet, the rewards Lin Yuan offered so casually were even more precious than these.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was providing the Radiance Federation with such precious resources.","Previously, Lin Yuan had also given the Moon Empress a large amount of resources intending to raise the Radiance Federation’s overall power.","However, most of these resources had gone to the Radiance Federation’s factions so they could increase their power.","The resources were meant for the troops fighting the dead spirits this time.","This would not only raise their motivation but would also increase their power in a very short period.","Lin Yuan’s contribution to the Radiance Federation would bring about structural change.","From now on, there would be even more members of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation fighting for the opportunity to join the Radiance Federation’s troops in battling the dead spirits.","With this, the Radiance Federation would not have to worry about recruiting for their frontlines.","Although being stationed near the Dead Spirits Wells and fighting the dead spirits would indeed come with danger, the opportunities were greater.","All they needed to do was work hard and do their best to protect the Radiance Federation, and they would have the opportunity to gain a high-quality Bronze fey that would enable their power to catapult upwards. As long as they conscientiously nurtured their high-quality Bronze feys, they would definitely be able to achieve impressive results!","It could be said that the main reason for most spirit qi professionals becoming stuck at a certain level of power was that they had not managed to acquire a fey with high potential in their early days.","The rewards that Lin Yuan was offering allowed the Moon Empress to see a limitless future for the Radiance Federation.","“Little Yuan, I will call for an imperial meeting just to discuss and implement this reward and punishment system. If you already have an idea in mind, you can tell me about it now!”","Lin Yuan hurriedly shook his head and said honestly, “Master I don’t have any ideas. You can make the decision during the imperial meeting! I went to the Dead Spirits Wells today to check on the situation and have noted what we need to research and put work into going forward. Wen Yu will organize them before handing the information to you!","“The Creation Masters will definitely have their work cut out for them for the next few decades! In order to prevent them from becoming bitter, I will also provide the Creation Masters with additional resources.”","The Moon Empress said seriously, “Little Yuan, you don’t have to worry about the Creation Masters. I might not be able to provide as many resources as you, but I can keep these Creation Masters in line with no issues!","“The Radiance Federation is in a state of emergency. The Creation Masters are a part of the Radiance Federation, so they want to protect it! They also work hard and hope the dead spirits crisis will pass as smoothly as possible!”","Lin Yuan did not spend too much time in the Radiant Moon Palace. When he left, he headed to the sea clans to see how they were doing.","The sea clans’ battle with the dead spirits was much more intense than the Radiance Federation, which only had to deal with the dead spirits coming from the hundreds of Dead Spirits Wells.","Dazzling Silver had sent a message to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper asking him for help.","There were far too many dead spirits in the sea. It was difficult for just the sea clans and water world dimensional lifeforms to deal with all of the dead spirits.","The sea was filled to the brim with dead spirits.","Luckily, the death aura released by the dead spirits only affected the sea clans who came from the main world. The sea beasts and mermaids were considered dimensional lifeforms and thus undisturbed by the death aura.","Some sea beasts liked to consume the dead spirits and could digest and absorb the death aura. They even attained new abilities from absorbing and digesting the death aura!","This was extremely good news for Lin Yuan.","The dimensional lifeforms were much stronger than the feys and humans living in the main world.","The Dead Decay Earthworms could not live underwater.","If the sea clans were also troubled by the death aura, Lin Yuan would have no means of helping them for the foreseeable future!","After all, Lin Yuan’s army of Hundred Questions Beasts and the Creation Masters had to serve the humans first.","The battles happening at the borders between the main world and dimensional worlds were much more intense than the battles in the sea.","The tsunami of dead spirits flooded into the dimensional worlds. The dead spirits had already fully invaded the alien insect, abyssal, subterranean, and marsh worlds.","However, the invasion of the dead spirits had also been met with strong counterattacks by the native dimensional lifeforms.","Firstly, more than 80% of the marsh world was comprised of a marshy environment. The ground was dark, but when one stepped foot on it, half of one’s body would sink in immediately. If one could not save oneself or was pulled out by anyone else, they would eventually sink fully into the mud.","The specters were fine as they were in a soul state. However, most of the dead spirits in solid form had become stuck in the marsh and ended up as food for the Marsh Crocodiles.","There were many Marsh Crocodiles in the marsh world. They could be found almost everywhere where there was marsh.","If they could not find food, the Marsh Crocodiles would even feast on each other.","But now, the Marsh Crocodiles finally had the opportunity to fill their stomachs.","The waves of dead spirits were torn apart in the marsh. The death aura could affect the Marsh Crocodiles to a certain extent, but their bodies could quickly adjust to the death aura.","The Marsh Crocodiles were accustomed to hunger, and this was the first time that they were experiencing what it was like to have an endless supply of food.","The dead spirit corpses in the marsh became nutrients for the fungi in the marsh world. The fungi broke down the dead spirit corpses.","The dimensional lifeforms like the Drugged Snake Eagle and Medusa Snake Demon that liked to consume souls feasted on the floating specters.","Specters had much tougher souls than regular souls.","Initially, the marsh world dimensional lifeforms had been anxious about the dead spirits crisis. But now, they saw it as a gift.","In a few days, the marsh dimensional lifeforms came to an unspoken shared sentiment: they hoped that the dead spirits crisis would never end! If it ended, when would they have another chance to fill their stomachs daily again?","Some dimensional lifeforms were killed by powerful dead spirits, but death was a part of life for the dimensional lifeforms. It was normal in the dimensional worlds for there to be death during the hunt for food.","Because of Lin Yuan’s orders, some Apostles and Dictators would quickly kill these more powerful dead spirits.","The death of every powerful dead spirit was good news for the weaker dimensional lifeforms.","With the dead spirits as a source of food, low-class dimensional lifeforms like the Marsh Crocodiles and Marsh Fireflies were able to reproduce rapidly.","Lin Yuan was stunned for almost five minutes after he heard this.","He never thought that the dead spirits crisis would become a blessing for the marsh world!","The marsh world was not considered outstanding amongst the five dimensional worlds.","The abyssal world was doing just as well, or maybe even slightly better than the marsh world.","The abyss demons were very adaptable. Lin Yuan had tested this some time ago.","This was because the abyss demons from the abyssal world were not fire-type by nature. They only came to become fire-type because of the influence of the Abyss Red Lotus.","The abyss demons’ strong adaptability allowed it to change itself according to its environment.","After the abyss demons consumed the dead spirits, many abyss demons started exhibiting attributes of the dead spirits.","This change in type would allow the abyss demons to absorb death aura and use it as a source of strength.","Suppose Lin Yuan could not research and produce feys like the Dead Decay Earthworm, after a few hundred years of evolution. In that case, the abyss demons might be able to take the job of cleansing their environment of death aura.","The dimensional world that was performing the best against the dead spirits was the alien insect world that Keira was leading.","Food was the alien insects’ greatest need.","If the lack of food did not restrict the size of the alien insect species, there would already be enough of them to fill every corner of the world!","After Lin Yuan gave Keira the Soldier Ration Radishes in the Diamond fey storage boxes, the size of the alien insect species had grown significantly.","When the dead spirits invaded, Keira commandeered the alien insect empresses and alien insect queens to lead the alien insects into battle.","They eventually discovered that the dead spirits were edible.","They might not taste very good, but they could provide the muscles with energy.","After realizing this, the alien insects started to treasure their food.","The alien insects like the Acid Tapeworm could even use the strong acid produced in their abdomens to preserve the dead spirits and prevent them from spoiling.","Some absurd female insects even wanted to make the dead spirits their mates and insisted on taking the dead spirits’ genes to produce offspring with them. The female insects’ strong reproductive ability caused many dead spirits to unwittingly become fathers.","As such, many alien insects with dead spirit attributes were born, and they became effective tools for targeting the dead spirits.","There were even some female insects who fought each other in order to mate with powerful dead spirits.","If Keira had not interfered in the infighting between the alien insects, the various alien insect species would definitely have begun viciously fighting among themselves over resources.","The dimensional world that was faring the worst against the dead spirits was the subterranean world.","Most of the lifeforms in the subterranean world consumed minerals and metals. This meant that dead spirits could not become part of their diet.","As a result, the fighting was the most intense between the subterranean dimensional lifeforms and dead spirits.","Because of this, Lin Yuan had no choice but to send some alien insects and abyss demons that could live in the subterranean world’s environment to the subterranean world to help them fight the dead spirits.","The impressive performance of the alien insect, abyssal, and marsh worlds greatly boosted Lin Yuan’s confidence.","It was likely that Tower Canon’s Eight Pages had not expected that the dead spirits crisis they had been planning for so long was now serving as a food source for these dimensional lifeforms!","Compared to the dimensional lifeforms, the humans were extremely poor at acclimating!","However, the humans had boundless creativity.","Immediately after Lin Yuan entered the water, a group of dead spirits charged at him.","Lin Yuan could not tell which epoch these dead spirits came from.","They were not strong. The strongest of them was only Silver grade.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and created a current that tore apart the dead spirits.","Ice Flow knew that Lin Yuan was coming to observe how the sea clans were faring against the dead spirits, so he had been waiting for Lin Yuan.","Ice Flow could not help but immediately ask Lin Yuan for help upon seeing him.","Some sea beasts from the dimensional worlds could consume the dead spirit corpses and absorb the death aura. However, there were not many of such species, and they were insufficient to catch up to the rate at which the dead spirits were emerging.","There were already many members of sea clans who were in bad condition because their bodies had been infected by death aura.","If this issue was not solved, the size of the relatively weaker sea clans would gradually grow smaller.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth would have solved their issues on their own if they were capable of doing so. But since they lacked the capabilities, they had no choice but to ask Lin Yuan for help.","From Ice Flow’s pleas for help, Lin Yuan could feel his frustration as the ruler of the sea clans.","At this moment, Lin Yuan thought of the Sea Burial Lotus Flower.","The sea’s death aura was the best nutrient source for the Sea Burial Lotus Flower.","Lin Yuan could instruct Dazzling Silver, Light Green Umber, Blue Umber, Red Beauty, and the other emperor-class mermaids to watch over Silver Corona.","As Silver Corona grew freely in the sea, the places it covered would no longer be affected by the death aura, and the sea clans would be safe!","A carcinoma fey that had previously been hated by the sea clans to the point that they would chop it down immediately after glimpsing it would now become their savior.","“I do have an idea. It will be able to clear out all the death aura in a certain area. However, this will not solve the root of the problem. Regardless of how effective this method is, it will never be able to protect all of the sea clans!","“I need to make sure that you are aware of this. The humans are also grappling with the death aura during our battle against the dead spirits. The death aura has injured many human experts.","“Our Creation Masters will need to find a way to help the humans first. Once they have solved the problems the humans face, we will attend to the sea clans immediately!”","Lin Yuan gave the unpleasant news first. He was speaking nothing but the truth.","Ice Flow really liked Lin Yuan’s candid style of communication.","If Lin Yuan could provide the sea clans with a space that was free of death aura, it would already be extremely helpful for the sea clans as the injured troops could use that area to rest and recover.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth was aware to a certain extent of what was happening over on the human side. They knew that the humans were not having an easy time either.","There were some members of sea clans who had Creation Master abilities."]},{"number":2658,"title":"Chapter 2658 Silver Corona and the Dead Spirits Wells!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2658 Silver Corona and the Dead Spirits Wells!","The Vast Sea Labyrinth’s Creation Masters would never provide the humans with resources before they ensured that everything was stable and going well with the sea clans.","Lin Yuan had shown his greatest sincerity by promising the sea clans he would help them with their issues once he solved the humans’ problems.","“Lord Lin Yuan, you are the savior of the sea clans. Regardless of what becomes of the sea clans or how much time passes, we will never stop seeing you as a deity and dedicating our faith to you!”","Lin Yuan was reluctant to fully believe him and raised his eyebrow. He indeed needed the faith power from the sea clans.","However, Lin Yuan would not make too many demands of the sea clans just because he wanted their faith.","Lin Yuan was helping the sea clans because he hoped that the sea clans would be able to stand by the humans and take on the dead spirits crisis together. There was no way he was after self-serving profits because he had provided them with much more benefits than they had provided to him.","“Ice Flow, when you return, go and tell Ice Wave and Ice Clarity to help me find a 500-square-kilometer space at the bottom of the sea where the metal-type stone boards have been laid down. It is also necessary to ensure that this space will be growing larger in the future.","“I will be placing a carcinoma fey that has evolved into a fairy there. It can not only help to clear away the dead spirit corpses but also consume the death aura in the sea. In the future, you can collect the dead spirit corpses and throw them into the sea of flowers produced by the fairy.”","Lin Yuan did not speak praise of Silver Corona’s abilities.","He was hoping that the dead spirits crisis would enable Silver Corona’s power to grow rapidly.","It was a challenge for the sea clans to clear the dead spirit corpses. Although some of the water world dimensional lifeforms could consume the bodies of dead spirits, their digestive capabilities were limited.","If the sea beasts could consume all of the dead spirit corpses, the sea clans would not be as troubled as they were!","The water world dimensional lifeforms were less capable of digesting the dead spirits than the abyssal world, marsh world, and alien insect world dimensional lifeforms, but the abyssal, alien insect, and marsh worlds’ dimensional lifeforms could not live underwater. Thus, they were unable to help the sea clans.","If the sea clans tossed all of the dead spirit corpses that the sea beasts could not consume into the sea of flowers produced by Silver Corona, Silver Corona would be able to increase its power rapidly and expand the area of the sea of bone lotus flowers.","Silver Corona might be able to address some of the sea clans’ problems, but it could not fix the root cause.","Once the humans no longer lacked Class 5 Creation Master resources, Lin Yuan would ask the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to do research into aquatic lifeforms that could tackle both death aura and the dead spirit corpses.","It was possible that while the army of Hundred Questions Beasts was researching healing type feys that could heal bodies infected by death aura, they would stumble on a fey that could handle the dead spirit corpses and death aura in the sea!","Ice Flow hurriedly asked Lin Yuan, “None of the areas where the metal-type stone boards have been laid down have been used. The aquatic lifeforms rarely need to live at the bottom of the sea. The coral reefs can’t be moved. Only a small amount of coral polyps can be removed to grow new coral reefs. The coral polyps are very important, and we are in no rush to plant them at the bottom of the sea.","“You can place the fairy anywhere the metal-type stone boards have been laid down. We will use the fairy as the center and arrange for the aquatic lifeforms to build their homes around the sea of flowers. We will also arrange for dedicated people to place the dead spirit corpses in the sea of flowers. I will personally communicate with your fairy to provide the fairy with the best environment to increase its power.”","As one of the sea rulers who has been alive for thousands of years, Ice Flow could easily comprehend what Lin Yuan was trying to say.","It was clear that Lin Yuan was hoping that the sea clans would help to increase this fairy’s power while he was helping the sea clans clean out the death aura.","The sea clans had no other means of repaying Lin Yuan. As such, they would do their best to meet all of his requests.","Moreover, helping Lin Yuan would also help the sea clans to change their environment.","When Lin Yuan heard what Ice Flow said, he did not bother with additional courtesies. He created a current and sent it to the bottom of the sea. He did not try to find the safest area. Instead, after careful deliberation, he decided to find an area where there were many Dead Spirits Wells.","This was similar to when he first started nurturing Silver Corona and opened many dimensional rifts so that waves of dimensional lifeforms could emerge continuously. The endless waves of dimensional lifeforms allowed Silver Corona to increase its power quickly.","Otherwise, Silver Corona’s sea of flowers would not have grown so strong so quickly!","Lin Yuan would now emulate that strategy and use these Dead Spirits Wells to feed Silver Corona’s power while reducing the strain on the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the water world dimensional lifeforms.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth could use the coral polyps to build new coral reeds to protect the absolutely safe areas.","Using knowledge from his previous life, Lin Yuan knew how important coral reefs were to the development of the lifeforms in a world.","The Dead Spirits Wells were much more dangerous than the dimensional rifts.","The strongest dimensional lifeform that could emerge from a Class 3 dimensional rift was the equivalent of a Diamond grade fey. On the other hand, dead spirits of any strength could burst forth from the Dead Spirits Wells.","With Silver Corona only being Diamond grade, it could still not kill many powerful dead spirits on its own.","If these powerful dead spirits were allowed to wreak havoc on the sea of bone lotus flowers, they would cause extensive damage.","Lin Yuan did not want this to happen.","If a powerful dead spirit damaged the sea of flowers, Silver Corona would have to fix it, and this would slow the rate at which Silver Corona increased its power.","However, this situation was avoidable.","Lin Yuan only needed to station one or two Turning Wheel Realm Dictators next to every Dead Spirits Well. The Turning Wheel Realm Dictators were strong enough to handle the more powerful dead spirits.","As Silver Corona grew increasingly stronger, Lin Yuan could open more Dead Spirits Wells to provide Silver Corona with even more nutrients.","When Ice Flow said that Lin Yuan could have his pick of areas, he assumed that Lin Yuan would pick the safest place for his fairy. He never expected that Lin Yuan would pick the area near the Dead Spirits Wells.","“Lord Lin Yuan, the safest area is over there. Let me take you over there! There is definitely enough space there for your fairy to grow the sea of flowers!”","Lin Yuan shook his head and asked Ice Flow seriously, “Is this where there are the most Dead Spirits Wells? Take me to the place where there are the most Dead Spirits Wells. I will place my fairy in the area where there are the most Dead Spirits Wells. This will take the most pressure off of the sea clans. It will also give the sea clans a space to nurture the coral reefs!”","Ice Flow was momentarily at a loss on how to reply to Lin Yuan.","If what Lin Yuan said was true, millions of the sea clans’ troops would be freed up!","The sea clans had only just moved to the water world and urgently needed to build their abodes.","The millions of sea clans troops would be able to improve the sea clans’ environment in a very short span of time.","Ice Flow had already thanked Lin Yuan so many times that he felt that the meaning of the word had paled.","This time, Ice Flow did not begin thanking Lin Yuan repeatedly. Instead, he intended to tell his brothers about what had happened so all the sea clans would become aware of the help that Lin Yuan was giving the sea clans.","Lin Yuan needed faith power so the Vast Sea Labyrinth would take the initiative to help him gain the faith of all the sea clans. This was the best way to repay Lin Yuan!","One of the areas where the metal-type stone boards had been laid down had 60 Dead Spirits Wells on it. It was the most contaminated part of the sea.","When Ice Flow brought Lin Yuan to that area, they saw the sea clans and dimensional lifeforms battling ferociously against the dead spirits.","Ice Flow felt that the battle here was too intense. From his conversation with Lin Yuan, Ice Flow had found out about this fairy’s power. It would be very difficult for a Diamond grade fey to make its home here.","Just as Ice Flow was about to take Lin Yuan to another area with fewer Dead Spirits Wells, he heard Lin Yuan say seriously, “I will give you ten days to clear this area. I will be assigning a Turning Wheel Realm Dictator to every Dead Spirits Well to support you. Once all the sea clans have left this area, I will move the sea of flowers over here and anchor it to the top of the Dead Spirits Wells.”","Ice Flow looked deeply into Lin Yuan’s eyes before he bowed forcefully and left to relay the news to Ice Wave and Ice Clarity.","Ten days was a short deadline to clear out the millions of members of sea clans. But it could be accomplished with the help of tens of Turning Wheel Realm Dictators!","The sea clans would be conducting a second large-scale relocation.","After this migration, the sea clans could begin using the coral polyps to build coral reefs once they were done preparing their environment.","Ice Flow had already resigned himself to the reality that the dead spirits crisis would last for a few millennia before it came to an end.","The area where the water world had fused with the main world would be the sea clans’ home from now on.","Unless the dead spirits crisis came to an end, the main world’s ley lines would continue to be infected by death aura, and dead spirits would continue to rise from the ground.","There was no way that the sea clans could live in the main world’s seas.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth fully controlled the sea clans. Thus, the orders issued by the Vast Sea Labyrinth could be disseminated quickly.","The sea clans were able to clear out within nine and a half days.","The sea clans’ army formed a large circle and began attacking the dead spirits in that formation to prevent them from escaping.","Once all the sea clans had fled, Lin Yuan instructed Lift Marsh to lift the area in the Startling Lines Continent covered by the sea of bone lotus flowers and bring it into the sea.","The Bone Lotus Flowers seemed awkward and bulky on land. They could not move with the large piece of land under them.","But in the sea, every Bone Lotus Flower seemed to come alive as they were able to twist their bodies to glide and swim through the sea.","Although it had lived on land for a long time, this did not change the fact that Silver Corona was an aquatic carcinoma fey.","Since Silver Corona could control the sea of flowers and move freely in the sea, Lift Marsh’s job was done now that it had delivered Silver Corona to the sea.","Silver Corona followed Lin Yuan’s instructions to the right area before it spread its sea of flowers over the more than 60 Dead Spirits Wells. The sea of flowers also covered all of the dead spirits in the area.","The sea of bone lotus flowers started to move rapidly as they began attacking the dead spirits.","The sea of bone lotus flowers was much stronger than the Corpse-Consuming Vines when it came to battling the dead spirits.","Silver Corona used Rotted Bones into Fireflies and rapidly absorbed all the death aura around it.","The death aura refined the strength of every Bone Lotus Flower. The rotting bones that could nourish the Bone Lotus Flowers were also formed beneath the Bone Lotus Flowers.","As long as the main lotuses were not destroyed, they could rapidly produce new flowers using the rotting bones.","Even if the dead spirits damaged the sea of flowers. the effects of Rotted Bones into Fireflies would prevent the sea of flowers from shrinking too much.","As long as Silver Corona could secure itself in this area and the accumulation of rotting bones increased, Silver Corona could quickly expand the size of the sea of bone lotus flowers.","The sea clans were all amazed as they watched Lin Yuan order Lift Marsh to bring over the sea of flowers that eventually blanketed the dead spirits.","Lin Yuan hurriedly garnered a large amount of faith power. The number of glowing dots of faith in the fountain of faith increased, and those that already existed also grew brighter!","The Turning Wheel Realm Dictators were stationed above the sea of flowers and dealt with the powerful dead spirits that the sea of flowers were not strong enough to handle.","Silver Corona sat on Lin Yuan’s shoulders and swung its legs, looking extremely happy.","Silver Corona was used to having big meals. But it was still bursting with joy over this enormous feast.","This was the first time that Silver Corona was absorbing death aura. It could not only digest the dead spirits but also filter the sea of death aura. This meant that not only would the sea of bone lotus flowers be free of death aura, but it would also be able to cleanse a radius of at least 5,000 square kilometers around it.","The area that had been the biggest issue for all of the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s troops and the water world’s dimensional lifeforms now became a haven.","Dazzling Silver led Blue Umber and Red Beauty over to Lin Yuan. They bowed and said, “Lord Therach, if dead spirits as strong as Samsara Realm Dictators or even stronger appear, it will be difficult for just these Turning Wheel Realm Dictators to deal with the situation. I intend on leaving Blue Umber and Red Beauty here to protect the sea of flowers.”","Dazzling Silver had been spending time with Wen Yu of late. While she protected Wen Yu, she also learned a lot about strategy and interpersonal relationships.","In the past, Dazzling Silver would definitely try to single-handedly undertake the job of guarding the sea of bone lotus flowers as a means of proving her worth."]},{"number":2659,"title":"Chapter 2659 Attack of the Hundred Sequence!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2659 Attack of the Hundred Sequence!","But now, Dazzling Silver was getting better at thinking from a managerial standpoint. She liked to analyze managerial issues from a manager’s perspective and understood what Lin Yuan needed was not powerful Samsara Realm Dictators.","He had many Samsara Realm Dictators under him, but he always showed a preference for those who were capable of accomplishing tasks.","This was why East Glow was so heavily relied on by Lin Yuan despite only having just become a Dictator.","Lin Yuan nodded and replied, “Samsara Realm Dictators must indeed guard this sea of flowers. You are currently the strongest water world dimensional lifeform, so you can be the one to make the arrangements for this matter!","“Dazzling Silver, you must ensure this sea of flowers is well protected. It is essential for my future plans, so no carelessness or mistakes will be tolerated!”","Lin Yuan was nurturing Silver Corona to eventually take it to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Hence, he wanted it to grow the most and the best that it could.","With Silver Corona’s sea of flowers sitting on the Dead Spirits Wells, it would easily be damaged by powerful dead spirits if attention was taken off of it.","Lin Yuan still said what he said despite knowing that Dazzling Silver would definitely take good care of the sea of flowers because he wanted to put pressure on her.","This was the first time that Dazzling Silver was hearing Lin Yuan speak of a matter with such solemnity.","Dazzling Silver hurriedly gave Lin Yuan her guarantee.","Once Silver Corona was done producing the sea of bone lotus flowers, Lin Yuan was done with all he needed to do in the water world.","The other human federations were all living in the dimensional worlds and did not have to worry about battling the dead spirits.","After they relocated, they focused their efforts on constructing infrastructure, leaving the Radiance Federation to take the full brunt of battling the dead spirits.","After all, the Radiance Federation was part of the main world, and its ley lines had also been severely contaminated.","It was good that the other human federations could immediately delve into building infrastructure after they migrated without having to burden themselves with the invasion of the dead spirits.","If the dead spirits also rose out of the ground in the dimensional worlds, it would be difficult for the other human federations to fight them.","The Moon Empress had already distributed resources. Once the experts from the human federations received the resources, they immediately began increasing their power.","The Moon Empress had made a request when she gave out these resources. Any expert with feys that were about to experience the World Cleansings or Trials of World Creation had to wait for Lin Yuan to collect a portion of their feys’ World Graces or Creation World Ley Lines.","Most of those human federations upheld their promise to the Moon Empress, but there were still a small portion of them who went against their word.","Thus, the Moon Empress sent the knights under the Moon Servants to keep a lookout while they were patrolling in the other federations.","If they discovered any expert who broke this agreement, not only would the Moon Empress reduce the amount of resources that the federation that the expert came from received, but she would punish the experts by requesting their federations to compensate the Radiance Federation three times the amount of resources that they had received.","Ever since he returned from checking on the sea clans, Lin Yuan had been in the Spirit Lock spatial zone using spirit qi crystals to nurture promising feys to high-quality Bronze.","These feys would be given to the Radiance Federation’s troops.","The troops that were able to fight the dead spirits on the Radiance Federation’s behalf would be able to use their service to trade for a significant amount of resources, and they were capable enough to nurture these high-quality Bronze feys.","Regardless of what happened, they would be able to nurture the high-quality Bronze feys to Suzerain/Myth in the next few decades and provide Lin Yuan with a large amount of spirit qi crystals.","The dead spirits crisis would definitely last for a long time!","Aside from using the spirit qi crystals to nurture feys, Lin Yuan also took a look at how Hu Quan was progressing with decorating the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Since Lin Yuan assigned the Land Imps to Hu Quan, the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s construction began progressing rapidly.","Hu Quan was already done with building the living and working spaces for the Hundred Questions Beasts. The size of the Hundred Questions Beasts would soon reach the millions.","The millions of Hundred Questions Beasts, which were the equivalent of Class 3 and 4 Creation Masters, would definitely be able to solve numerous issues for Lin Yuan.","The Moon Empress usually never left Leaning Moon Mountain. But now, she spent almost all of her time in the imperial court. She attended numerous imperial meetings each day to solve a variety of issues.","The Radiance Federation wanted to set up a reward and punishment system for the troops who were fighting the dead spirits. They also needed to attend to the federations who were asking for help.","There were many federations who asked to borrow resources from the Radiance Federation because they lacked resources of their own to build bases. Not every federation was able to pay back what they borrowed. The Moon Empress did not hesitate to lend resources to such federations even if she knew they could not pay them back.","This imperial meeting was initially meant to discuss the formation of the troops around the Dead Spirits Wells.","At first, there were 15 teams assigned to every Dead Spirits Well, and they took shifts to defend the Dead Spirits Wells.","But now that they had the Dead Decay Earthworms, there was no need to station so many troops to each Dead Spirits Wells.","The Moon Empress was currently in the midst of a discussion with the other members of royalty about how many troops should be part of the new and smaller formations.","It was not easy to make such an order. They had to conduct careful tests. Otherwise, there was a high chance that the wrong decision would result in unimaginable damage!","The Radiance Federation’s royalty were fully responsible for the safety of their troops. Otherwise, they would not have held three imperial meetings with this matter as the main agenda!","Night Leaning Moon proposed to reduce the number to nine teams. Eight of the nine teams would battle the dead spirits in three-hour shifts while the last team would be on standby. If, at any instance, the eruption of dead spirits from the Dead Spirits Wells was too violent, the team on standby could step in to help.","Night Leaning Moon was the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards. Thus, she had more experience than the other members of royalty when it came to organizing troops.","Night Leaning Moon felt that after all the resources that Lin Yuan was providing the troops to help them fight the dead spirits, it was only right for her to put some pressure on the troops. This way, the dead spirits crisis would become an opportunity for them to train themselves.","It would not be long before the Radiance Federation’s troops’ overall power multiplied.","Liu Wencheng rarely gave his input during recent imperial meetings. Because of the dead spirits crisis and the fusing of the five dimensional worlds with the main world, no more dimensional rifts opened in the main world.","The schools had all lost their best training environments. Liu Wencheng was currently requesting that every city set a Dead Spirits Well aside to serve as a training site for the students.","The fifth epoch was now a thing of the past. The dead spirits crisis had triggered a changing of epochs.","The Radiance Federation would need to adjust to the changing times if it wanted to continue developing in the new epoch.","It was very important that the students gained an understanding of and were able to make contact with dead spirits during their education.","Liu Wencheng was very anxious to begin introducing classes related to dead spirits from the elementary school level.","He was the only member of royalty who managed Radiance Sacred Hall. Thus, he had to handle this matter all on his own.","The other members of royalty were also very busy, and he could not bring himself to bother them.","The group that was the most representative of the Radiance Federation was the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","At such a time, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence needed to set the example and become involved in the defense and rescue efforts of the various cities.","Liu Wencheng used this imperial meeting to bring up this matter.","“As all of you know, I have been busy trying to change the education system. I suggest every city provide schools with one or two Dead Spirits Wells. I have already brought up this matter with Cicada Song and Night Leaning Moon, and they have supported this decision!","“The earlier we incorporate education on the dead spirits, the better. This way, the schools under Radiance Sacred Hall will be able to nurture the best soldiers for the Radiance Federation. Otherwise, these students won’t be able to move directly from school to the battlefield.","“Aside from changing the education structure, I would like the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to become flag bearers and be sent to the various cities to protect them.","“Furthermore, now that the Major Federation Union is established, there is no longer any need for the Major Federation Meeting. However, the Radiance Federation should still maintain the tradition of selecting Radiance Envoys.","“When the Radiance Hundred Sequence members are sent to the various cities to help with the battle against the dead spirits, I will pick five of the best-performing members and recommend that they become Radiance Envoys. As long as they can defeat the current Radiance Envoys, they will be able to become official Radiance Envoys!”","After Liu Wencheng spoke, every member of royalty, including the Moon Empress and Night Leaning Moon, were all stunned.","There were no issues with any of Liu Wencheng’s suggestions. The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were the faith of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation. Each of them had celebrity status in the Radiance Federation. It was only right that they took up the necessary responsibilities during such a catastrophe.","However, the Radiance Hundred’s royalty could not bear to put the Radiance Hundred Sequence in such danger.","There was a high chance that the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would end up losing their lives when they were sent to various cities to fight the dead spirits.","Normally, no one treasured the Radiance Hundred Sequence more than Liu Wencheng. It was truly surprising that such a suggestion had come from him!","While the other members of royalty were silent, Iron Prison said, “I support this decision. This is exactly the time when we should be bolstering confidence. The best way to do that is to send the Radiance Hundred Sequence into battle.","“Since the Moon Empress is going to pump resources into the troops on the frontlines, the Radiance Hundred Sequence will also be eligible to claim some of these resources if they were sent to battle.”","Liu Wencheng was thankful that Iron Prison was the first one to voice his support.","But it was not long before Liu Wencheng furrowed his brow.","What did Iron Prison mean? Did he think I was trying to help the Radiance Hundred Sequence gain some of the resources meant for the frontline troops?","Even if Iron Prison did not have such an intention, it was easy to misunderstand his meaning.","However, Iron Prison had no inkling of this at all.","Cicada Song shot Iron Prison a silent look before he helped Iron Prison to add on, “Iron Prison is hoping that this opportunity will help the Radiance Hundred Sequence to grow. The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence are also part of the Radiance Federation’s troops.","“I hope that after this, the experience they gain will enable the Radiance Hundred Sequence to become true leaders of the Radiance Federation and that their influence will extend past just the younger generation.”","Liu Wencheng’s expression lightened significantly after he heard what Cicada Song said.","Iron Prison did not have any of the intentions that Liu Wencheng thought he did.","When Liu Wencheng made his decision, the Moon Empress had not yet announced her decision to provide resources to the Radiance Federation’s troops!","Although the members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty were silent, none felt any opposition toward Liu Wencheng’s decision. The strongest emotion they felt was that the idea was rather radical.","Luckily, experts were guarding every Dead Spirits Well.","These experts could help to look out for the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence!","The Moon Empress said decisively, “That is a good idea. Wencheng, you can pass on this decision as an announcement! The Radiance Hundred Sequence should set an example for the Radiance Federation at such a time.”","The Moon Empress intended to tell Lin Yuan about this to check if he was available. If he was busy with other matters, he would not need to spend time on this assignment for the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Every second of Lin Yuan’s time was very precious.","Lin Yuan had saved not only the Radiance Federation, but also the main world. No one had done more for the main world than Lin Yuan.","However, at the end of the day, the Moon Empress still hoped that he could become a Radiance Envoy and stand in the same position she used to stand in!","If Lin Yuan did not participate in this assignment for the Radiance Hundred Sequence, he would lose the eligibility to become a Radiance Envoy.","After all, the selection for the Radiance Envoys had to be fair. Otherwise, the original meaning would be lost.","Since Liu Wencheng was willing to send the Radiance Hundred Sequence out to train, the Moon Empress decided to give him a helping hand.","Every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had been carefully chosen. They had all been enjoying the best resources the Radiance Federation offered. The best use of these precious resources was to give them to the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Aside from the resources that Lin Yuan had given her, the Moon Empress also had a large store of high-class Creation Master resources that she had concocted herself.","She had initially been saving these resources for Lin Yuan, but she now knew that he did not need her resources.","If that were the case, there would be no harm in her giving the resources to the Radiance Hundred Sequence!","As such, the Moon Empress said seriously, “I will establish a prize pool. The resources will be allocated to the Radiance Hundred Sequence members.","“The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence will be able to attain the resources based on their contributions. The stronger they are, the more resources they’ll receive.","“We haven’t conducted this year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. The dead spirits crisis is no reason to stop the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection from happening.","“Let’s hold the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection before we send out the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to the cities to help with the fight against the dead spirits! This will also give us a chance to distract the citizens and boost their morale!”"]},{"number":2660,"title":"Chapter 2660: Prologue of the Sequence!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2660: Prologue of the Sequence!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Moon Empress had received many reports from Cicada Song lately.","Cicada Song managed all 32 of the Radiance Federation’s cities, so he had been gathering intel on the situation in the 32 cities.","The information had been passed through so many ranks and gone through so many revisions that it was only a few lines of simple statements by the time it got to Cicada Song. Nonetheless, he was aware of the meaning behind the statements.","Because he understood the meaning, he repeatedly sought the Moon Empress out to update her on the situation. He hoped she would see these issues as important and find solutions.","Once the Radiance Federation’s troops obtained the Dead Decay Earthworms, it became manageable for them to fight the dead spirits crisis.","However, it was difficult for the low-rank spirit qi professionals and regular people to gain confidence from this.","The regular people and low-rank spirit qi professionals made up 90% of the Radiance Federation’s population. The Radiance Federation’s endurance would be transformed if their morale could be boosted.","Liu Wencheng’s suggestion would be the best way to raise morale, and the Moon Empress was happy to support this.","Cicada Song finally relaxed.","After the Moon Empress was done speaking, Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch also expressed their stances.","The Bamboo Monarch said seriously, “I also have many high-class Creation Master resources. I will give some of them to the Radiance Hundred Sequence to nurture them.","“We shouldn’t stop at selecting the Radiance Envoys. We should pick out new Radiance Knights, too! Some of the resources I provide will go to the newly chosen Radiance Knights.”","The Bamboo Monarch’s words did not have a discursive tone. Instead, he had already made a decision.","This was because the Radiance Knight candidates had even more potential than the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Additionally, the Radiance Envoys were the flag bearers for the Radiance Federation, but they would need to be supported. The Radiance Knights existed to serve the Radiance Envoys!","Another reason was that the Bamboo Monarch knew that his disciple Gu Lang stood no chance of becoming a Radiance Envoy. It would be very difficult to defeat the current generation of Radiance Envoy.","It was likely that the only person who stood a chance was the Moon Empress’ disciple Lin Yuan. Not even the Spacetime Elder’s granddaughter was a shoo-in. It was most likely that Gu Lang would become a Radiance Knight.","The Bamboo Monarch did not want the disciple he had invested so much effort into to become a marginal character among the younger generation. After all, Gu Lang was not even a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Chef Supreme did not have as many considerations as the Bamboo Monarch.","He was willing to provide resources to aid the Moon Empress’ endeavor because he knew that he owed her and Lin Yuan his life.","Before he contracted the Lifespan Mouse and gained an endless life, Chef Supreme thought that he had reached the end of his lifespan. Yet, because of that tiny mouse, he had regained his life! He was now able to say that he had a truly immortal life!","He guessed that the Moon Empress and the Spacetime Elder had also resolved their lifespan issues by contracting the Lifespan Mouse.","The Moon Empress and Lin Yuan were his saviors, and Chef Supreme was very thankful to them.","If not for the fact that he had not had the opportunity to meet Lin Yuan recently, Chef Supreme would definitely have expressed his sincere thanks to Lin Yuan.","“I will provide the Radiance Hundred Sequence and Radiance Knights with the same amount of resources as the Bamboo Monarch. They can be added to the Moon Empress’ prize pool as well! I am rather curious to see what position the Moon Empress’ disciple attains in this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection!","“He was restricted to Sequence #91 the last time because it was his first Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. I think he stands a good chance of vying for Sequence #1 with Xia Qing!”","Liu Jie was the current Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. However, Chef Supreme did not mention him because he was aware of the relationship between Liu Jie and Lin Yuan. They were not competitors.","In actuality, Liu Jie was not weak at all.","Chef Supreme had gained a detailed understanding of Liu Jie. He disagreed with Night Leaning Moon’s method of helping Liu Jie use the Insect Queen as the final weapon. This was because he had seen too many cases of carcinoma feys destroying the main world.","By controlling carcinoma feys, Liu Jie was essentially holding a timed bomb.","Chef Supreme had warned Night Leaning Moon of this numerous times and had even argued with her over it.","It was only later that he found out about the Firefly Demon Fetuses that Liu Jie had obtained and that they could transform carcinoma feys into fairies. Their potential became boundless when they transformed into fairies with high intelligence and could follow Liu Jie’s orders.","It was only then that Chef Supreme’s idea of Liu Jie changed. It could be said that unimaginable accomplishments were in store for Liu Jie’s future!","The dueling stage was not convenient for Liu Jie to exhibit his abilities. If he was given a large open space where he could unleash his abilities, it was possible that even Lin Yuan would be no match for him.","However, given the relationship between Liu Jie and Lin Yuan, there was no way that Liu Jie would compete with Lin Yuan!","This was just like back then when Night Leaning Moon refused to compete with the Moon Empress.","It was a pity that Iron Prison had not been competent enough. Otherwise, Night Leaning Moon might not have been able to become a Radiance Envoy.","Chef Supreme could not help but smile a small smile while he reminisced.","Half of the people sitting on these 13 seats had been nurtured in their early days by resources provided by him. Now, these people who he had watched grow up had become pillars of the Radiance Federation.","In the past, such emotions would have brought him joy but also slight woe.","Now, he did not feel even a hint of sadness. He no longer had to fear being eliminated due to his lifespan coming to an end!","The fact that the Moon Empress was willing to give him the Lifespan Mouse meant that it was not exceptionally precious. It was likely that the rest of the Radiance Federation’s royalty would eventually receive the Lifespan Mouse of their own.","The older one became, the more one feared separation. Chef Supreme did not want to look around him one day just to realize that they had all gone.","Ever since he gained an endless lifespan, Chef Supreme not only worked harder than before at concocting spirit fluids and researching feys that could be used in the dead spirits crisis but also spent his free time playing chess with the Spacetime Elder and chatting about the past.","The Moon Empress smiled when she received Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch’s support.","The Radiance Federation’s three Class 5 Creation Masters were still very much united. This unity had not been worn away by time.","This proposal that Liu Wencheng had brought up had received full support. None of the Radiance Federation’s royalty opposed it. Not even Iron Prison, who always had issues to pick out, had anything to say this time.","All left to do now was for Liu Wencheng to proceed with the plans.","As a member of royalty, no one knew better than Liu Wencheng how to carry out such plans.","Now that they were done with this interlude, the Moon Empress brought up the main topic and described everything happening with the dead spirits crisis.","Although not every member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty was a Creation Master who needed to concern themselves with nurturing feys, it was still necessary to have a grasp on what was happening. This would enable them to make the right decisions when handling their tasks.","This especially applied to Liu Wencheng. He needed to understand the risks that he would be putting the Radiance Hundred Sequence through by sending them in to help with the dead spirits crisis.","The Moon Empress was not against sending the Radiance Hundred Sequence to help with the dead spirits crisis, but she needed to ensure their safety and minimize the possibilities of any injuries that could happen while they were carrying out their tasks!","Once Liu Wencheng understood what was happening, he would definitely assign experts from Radiance Sacred Hall to guard the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","The imperial meeting lasted for an entire day before it finally ended.","Unless something drastically changed with regard to the dead spirits crisis, there would be no need to hold another imperial meeting for the foreseeable future!","After the imperial meeting ended and the other members of royalty left, Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch stayed back.","The Bamboo Monarch sternly said, “Moon Empress, I have been managing the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters. There is something I must tell you. Most of these Creation Masters are far too arrogant. This attitude will not be beneficial for the nurturing of feys during the dead spirits crisis!","“I think that we need to do something to change their attitudes. The others might be unable to do anything about this, but the three of us can!”","Chef Supreme shook his head. Chef Supreme did not think that it would be easy to handle such a situation.","As a Class 5 Creation Master, the Bamboo Monarch should be well aware of how such a situation could arise.","Creation Masters were creators. If Creation Masters had not been nurturing feys and producing resources, the humans would not possess a third of the power they currently possessed.","As a result, Creation Masters were usually arrogant. It would be strange to come across one who did not think highly of themselves.","If they began enforcing strict restrictions on these Creation Masters, there was a high chance that this would backfire on them and cause the Creation Masters to go on strike.","The Radiance Federation could not afford such a consequence! It was not just the Radiance Federation. No faction would be able to handle such a situation.","Hence, Chef Supreme did not want the Bamboo Monarch to take the risk of something like that happening.","The Moon Empress fell silent when she heard what the Bamboo Monarch said.","She had also noticed this issue. Even if the Bamboo Monarch did not bring this matter up, she would have eventually.","But the difference between them was that the Moon Empress would have thought deeply before she brought up this matter.","The dead spirits crisis would last for thousands or even tens of thousands of years. During such a long period, many generations of Creation Masters would come and go.","There was indeed a need to change the Creation Masters’ attitudes. Otherwise, as they were given more authority, it was inevitable that they would carry more weight in decision-making!","Since it was going to be a reform, there would definitely be obstacles.","But with Lin Yuan’s resources, the Moon Empress now had the means to overcome those obstacles. Otherwise, she would never have decided to support the Bamboo Monarch’s decision.","Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch were done expressing their opinions and were currently looking at the Moon Empress seriously as they waited for her reply.","The Moon Empress gently knocked on the surface of the table. This was not one of her habits. Instead, it was one of the things that Lin Yuan did when he was thinking.","Slowly, the Moon Empress had incorporated Lin Yuan’s habits.","“I support Chef Supreme. The Creation Masters do need to change their attitudes. Their actions should also be restained. But I don’t think we should depress their statuses. I think you understand why I’m saying this. Bamboo Monarch should be the one to handle this.","“Chef Supreme, you can support him! If you encounter any difficult issues, you can let me know and we can talk it through together! I hope we can pass through the dead spirits crisis as peacefully as possible and that the legacy of humans doesn’t come to an end here.”","Lin Yuan was in the Spirit Lock spatial zone working hard at nurturing feys when his phone suddenly rang. He was surprised to see that the call was coming from the Moon Empress.","Normally, the Moon Empress preferred to communicate with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper instead of calling him.","Lin Yuan picked up the call and heard the news about the upcoming Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","As a previous Radiance Hundred Sequence member, Lin Yuan should participate in the selection.","Lin Yuan was using spirit qi crystals to nurture feys but could hand over the job to Genius.","This would not take him too much time. Rather, it would be no different from a spirit qi professional sending his fey into combat.","Lin Yuan had gotten almost no rest in the past year.","Participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would be a form of relaxation for him.","Once this selection was over, Lin Yuan also intended to follow Radiance Sacred Hall’s order to be sent to one of the major cities to help in the defense against the dead spirits.","He was done with the preparations for the dead spirits crisis. All he could do now was wait for Tower Canon to make their move. There was no way he could dig them out to confront them while they were hiding in the shadows.","Moreover, rather than battling Tower Canon now, Lin Yuan preferred for them to stay in hiding for longer. The longer they hid, the stronger he would grow.","All Lin Yuan needed now was time. The more time he had, the more ripe source fruits he would possess and the more Afterlife Realm Dictators he would have in his arsenal. Every Afterlife Realm Dictator would be a key weapon against Tower Canon.","Red Thorn would also be able to take control of more Tarot experts.","“Master, I will wait for news from Radiance Sacred Hall and do my best to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. Will there also be selections for the Radiance Knights and Radiance Envoys? I would also like to see how everyone has grown.”","Lin Yuan was referring to his friends like Gu Lang, Liu Jie, Gao Feng, and An He.","He also wanted to use this opportunity to give resources to his friends to help them increase their power.","Lin Yuan felt that the real Eight Pages of Tower Canon would be appearing soon.","There was also no way that the dead spirits crisis was this easy to handle. Lin Yuan could not shake the feeling that something big was stewing!"]},{"number":2661,"title":"Chapter 2661: The Elemental Paper Evolves!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2661: The Elemental Paper Evolves!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Moon Empress was rather surprised when she received Lin Yuan’s response.","She had not expected him to decide to join the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","In her opinion, with his power, he should be interested in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Lin Yuan was still young. She did not want him to have to carry such a heavy burden at his young age. The Moon Empress hoped that he would be able to live a normal life.","However, she knew that she was unable to provide him with this.","This was because he was growing too quickly, and she could not force him to change his mind. No one could take over the responsibilities that he was currently carrying.","Moreover, the dead spirits crisis had already begun. No one could be replaced in such an environment.","Chef Supreme’s disciple, Zong Ze, the Bamboo Monarch’s disciple, Gu Lang, Long Lamplight’s disciple, An He, and the Spacetime Elder’s granddaughter, Xia Qing, all had their own heavy burdens to bear.","Liu Wencheng’s decision would be a way for the older generation to hand down their responsibilities to the next generation. The next generation would carry on their legacy and hold up the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress ended their call once they were done speaking.","It was not long before Wen Yu and Liu Jie heard the news that he had returned.","The two of them immediately headed to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Based on what the Moon Empress said, the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would be taking place very soon.","When Chu Ci heard what Lin Yuan said, increasing her power became her main goal. She no longer chased after a seat in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","If she had attained a place in the Radiance Hundred Sequence this year and was sent to a city to train among the Dead Spirits Wells, Lin Yuan would be beside himself worrying about her.","In the course of Lin Yuan’s difficult life, he had experienced many dangers.","He was never afraid of taking on danger himself, but he was very afraid of putting Chu Ci through any sort of danger. This was the cross that all older brothers had to bear.","If Chu Ci remained in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, she could focus on raising her spirit qi professional rank.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie had both reached the limits of the B-rank spirit qi professional level and could be promoted to A-rank at any time.","Part of the reason they were able to promote their spirit qi professional rank so quickly was that they had consumed the Platinum Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar and cleansed their bodies of impurities. They had also consumed the Diamond Silver Stamen Gold Luster Cassia nectar, cleansing their souls of impurities.","Furthermore, the two of them were often nourished by pure spirit qi.","Pure spirit qi was effective not only on feys but also on humans.","However, highly pure spirit qi was so precious that not even Class 5 Creation Masters had tested it on humans.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie could be promoted to A-rank spirit qi professional at any time and evolve their feys to Myth Breed.","Liu Wencheng had very strong execution abilities. He had sent out the news by the same afternoon. Every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had received the news.","Even people like Wen Yu, who were expected to become Radiance Knights, had been informed.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion immediately after receiving the news.","The selection was going to begin in three days, and Liu Jie felt down the entire time.","He had been stuck at pinnacle B-rank spirit qi professional for some time. Other spirit qi professionals were stuck here for three to four months at the longest, but Liu Jie had been stuck for six entire months.","If he was not stuck here and unable to advance, he would have become an A-rank spirit qi professional sooner than Lin Yuan had.","There was nothing bad about Lin Yuan promoting his spirit qi professional first.","Liu Jie was delighted by Lin Yuan’s increase in power.","However, he was Lin Yuan’s retainer, and when he became a B-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan had only been a C-rank spirit qi professional. Now, he had been surpassed by Lin Yuan!","Liu Jie was certain that he would not be able to promote his rank before the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","He was sure that once he promoted his spirit qi professional rank, the Insect Queen would immediately evolve to Myth Breed.","Liu Jie had not had the opportunity to test himself against Lin Yuan. Lin Yuan would have to battle him before replacing him as Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Liu Jie badly wanted the opportunity to have a proper brawl with Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie could use the opportunity to assess the distance between himself and Lin Yuan.","In contrast to Liu Jie, who was solely focused on his spirit qi professional rank, Wen Yu was much calmer.","She had been thinking about what her advantages were.","Her advantage did not come from her power. She was only eligible to become a Radiance Knight because of the Elemental Paper’s special abilities.","The Thoughts Letter Paper that came from the Elemental Paper had already become the Radiance Federation’s highest level’s main mode of issuing directions.","She was eligible to become a Radiance Knight with just the Thoughts Letter Paper!","Faceless Paper, Paper Flower Funeral, Paper of Ten Thousand Forms, and Truth Form Paper were not any weaker than Thoughts Letter Paper as well! There just were not as many opportunities to use them.","Since she was aware of her advantages and knew that she was irreplaceable, Wen Yu was not concerned at all.","Because of her composed demeanor, she could sense the spirit qi in her body begin to transform at the instant she stepped into the Return from Faraway Mansion.","When Lin Yuan sensed the increase in Wen Yu’s rank, he did not immediately go to her to congratulate her. This was because he knew that it was best if a spirit qi professional could remain undisturbed when they had just evolved their spirit qi professional rank. If they were bothered, it was possible that their promotion would be halted.","After waiting for around 12 minutes and ascertaining that the spirit qi ripples had slowed, Lin Yuan stepped out of the main building and congratulated Wen Yu with a broad grin, “Wen Yu, congratulations on becoming an A-rank spirit qi professional! You are one step ahead of Big Brother Liu! He should also reach A-rank in the next day or two!”","Although Wen Yu was in no rush to become an A-rank spirit qi professional, she was still happy to become one.","“Young Master, because of my spirit qi professional rank, my Elemental Paper has been stuck at Diamond X/Fantasy V. But now, it can finally evolve its grade and quality!","“Young Master, I would like to ask you to help to evolve the Elemental Paper’s grade and quality. I want to see what new abilities and skills it will gain!”","Lin Yuan replied, “Let’s go. We’ll evolve the Elemental Paper’s grade and quality now so it can reach Myth Breed! I am also curious to see what new abilities and exclusive skills it will gain when it reaches Myth Breed!","“Big Brother Liu is going to the Midnight Palace. By the time we’re done, Big Brother Liu should be back. The three of us haven’t gathered together in a long time. Let’s see if his skills have improved!”","Wen Yu’s stomach immediately started rumbling when he heard what Lin Yuan said, and her cheeks flushed beetroot red.","It had not been long since Wen Yu finished her last meal. But at the mention of Liu Jie’s cooking and the memory of his dishes, Wen Yu could not help but feel ravenous.","Wen Yu had not had Liu Jie’s cooking for a long time. She was really looking forward to tonight’s dinner.","Aside from being able to eat Liu Jie’s dishes, Wen Yu also looked forward to the feeling of sharing a meal with Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","They had eaten together just like this two years ago.","Two years ago, Wen Yu would never have been able to imagine that Sky City would grow to such a magnitude.","Lin Yuan did not take Wen Yu too far to evolve the Elemental Paper. All they did was find an empty space outside of the Royal Capital.","Lin Yuan had been helping spirit qi professionals evolve their grades and qualities. He was very familiar with the process of helping a fey evolve to Myth Breed.","This time, he did not summon the Abyss Great Emperor. Instead, he summoned White Speak.","White Speak also had the power to fend off the World Cleansing.","Previously, White Speak had been left in the marsh world to manage the Marsh East Circle alongside East Glow.","But after the main world was fused with the marsh world, Lin Yuan decided to keep White Speak and East Glow by his side.","After training together, Lin Yuan noticed that East Glow and White Speak greatly excelled at governance than Everything did. This was why Lin Yuan relied on White Speak and East Glow more than he did Everything despite her being stronger than them.","Once the main world was fused with the dimensional worlds, there was no longer any difference between dimensional lifeforms and feys. The dimensional lifeforms were all eventually assimilated into the humans and feys.","By keeping White Speak and East Glow by his side, he could take some of the burden of managing Sky City off of its human members.","White Speak had been feeling very downtrodden of late.","In the past, Lin Yuan used his often and always kept him by his side. But ever since Lin Yuan conquered the marsh world, Eternal Source had replaced him.","Compared to Eternal Source, he was nothing but a small insect. He did not even have the right to compete with Eternal Source.","During his time in the Marsh East Circle, White Speak began focusing on improving his management abilities once he calmed down.","But after the marsh world was fused with the main world and White Speak returned to Lin Yuan’s side, he felt like a concubine who had regained the king’s favor!","From the fact that Lin Yuan was beginning to use him again, White Speak knew that he could remain by Lin Yuan’s side as long as he did not make any mistakes.","White Speak also had experience helping feys to overcome their evolutions. He was familiar with the process.","Lin Yuan said, “Wen Yu, summon the Elemental Paper!”","With a light wave of her hand, a shower of paper flowers shot out from Wen Yu’s hand.","Lin Yuan immediately used True Data to check on the shower of paper flowers.","[Fey Name]: Elemental Paper (Blossoming Paper Flower)","[Fey Species]: Elemental-species/paper species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Dance of Paper]: Transform the body into a piece of paper that is immune to physical attacks. However, it is especially vulnerable to elemental attacks. The paper has a teleporting power. The teleportation can be used every three seconds and has a radius of 20 kilometers.","[Paper Crane’s Promise]: The paper will be stacked to form a paper crane that can send messages. The paper crane will be engraved with the aura of the person receiving the message. If a person other than the receiver touches the paper crane, it will burst into flames. The paper crane has a teleporting power that is 30 times more powerful than that of Dance of Paper.","[Thoughts Letter Paper]: The paper will absorb the target’s blood and form a temporary contract with the target. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to communicate with each other using their thoughts, as their thoughts will automatically appear as words on the paper. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to read the words together.","[Faceless Paper]: An imaginary paper will appear in front of the target, and it can take the shape of the target[s appearance. As long as the Elemental Paper is not destroyed, the imaginary paper will be undamaged even if the target is killed.","[Paper Flower Funeral]: The paper will be folded into a flower that will form an imprint when it lands on a target. Even if the target is hidden, cloned, or affected by elements, the paper flower imprint can be used to sense the target’s location.","[Paper of Ten Thousand Forms]: The paper can pretend to be a person, fey, mountain, city, sea, or even sky. While in the imitation state, the entities hidden behind the paper can enjoy absolute defense.","Exclusive Skill:","[Hear Heaven’s Secrets]: The contractor will become a book of secrets that is linked to the flying piece of paper. When the book’s pages are turned, it can transfer any knowledge within to the flying piece of paper.","[Truth Form Paper]: While the paper is flying around, soul power can be used to form a piece of paper that can investigate the truth. When questioning a target, the paper will be folded into a flower if the target is telling the truth, and it will break apart if the target is lying.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was looking at the Elemental Paper’s data. But he still could not help but be amazed by what he saw.","He believed that the Elemental Paper’s strategic value would not be hampered in the slightest, even if the abilities and exclusive skills it gained when it reached Diamond/Myth were useless.","Objectively, the Elemental Paper had the greatest strategic value out of any source-type item Lin Yuan had ever come across! It was just as strategically valuable as Genius!","Wen Yu’s Elemental Paper formed a secret network of information that was absolutely secure.","Wen Yu also had the ability to take back the Thoughts Letter Papers she had given away.","Thus, she did not have to fear the Thoughts Letter Papers falling into the hands of enemies!","Wen Yu took a deep breath before tossing the paper into the sky.","The paper spread out across the sky, and in an instant, a rain of paper began descending from the sky. Every slip of falling paper was folded into a white rose.","The energy and aura emanating from the Elemental Paper activated the sky, and a hole appeared in the sky.","White Speak was prepared to step in at any time to take on the black hole in the sky that was the Elemental Paper’s World Cleansing."]},{"number":2662,"title":"Chapter 2662: Paper World Carrier!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2662: Paper World Carrier!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Wen Yu had only contracted three feys but the Earth Rush Golden Lotus and Sunlight Egret did not have combat abilities either. A pure support-type spirit qi professional like Wen Yu was the most worried about evolving her feys.","But now, Wen Yu did not have to worry at all because she knew that Lin Yuan would be there to help her with all of her problems. As long as he was by her side, she felt as though she always had someone to lean on and motivate her.","If not for Lin Yuan and Liu Jie, Wen Yu would never have pushed herself this far to continuously work hard at improving. She would also have never become capable enough to manage entities like the Astronomical Parliament and dimensional worlds!","As the paper flowers danced in the air, the sky and ground were enveloped in beautiful ivory.","Although Wen Yu knew that the Elemental Paper was the source of her strategic value and made her irreplaceable, she still hoped that it could surprise her when it evolved to Myth Breed.","This was because she knew that one could never allow oneself to become satisfied if one wanted to remain by Lin Yuan’s side. Just the slightest of pauses could result in one being overtaken by another.","Wen Yu understood how Liu Jie felt.","He had already taken control of so many insect-species carcinoma feys, and more than ten of them had transformed into fairies. Yet, he was still desperate to continue improving himself.","This was all because he wanted to remain by Lin Yuan’s side and because he wanted to prevent himself from one day being relegated to the back ranks, where he could only watch his former comrades from afar.","Given that Lin Yuan’s goal was the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she and Liu Jie could not restrain their considerations to the main world. They needed to look even further.","Wen Yu did not have a clear idea of the Sky Beyond the Clouds, so she did not know what to expect.","After all, not even Lin Yuan had been there yet.","Regardless, she could only prevent herself from being replaced if she continuously raised her value!","Peace’s development was halted by her desire to focus on protecting the Green Continent City.","Ta Lei did dream big and wanted more than just to be the City Lord of Thick Soil City. However, his capabilities were lacking, and it was already a stretch for him to manage Thick Soil City. There was no helping those who were limited by their lack of talent!","Wen Yu was terrified that she would end up with the same fate as Ta Lei.","By now, the boisterous flames were erupting from the black hole in the sky with full force and were soaring toward the paper flowers.","White Speak possessed the equivalent power of a birth horoscope expert.","Although Lin Yuan had not kept him by his side recently, he had still been very generous in his resource provision!","White Speak threw his fist toward the black hole in the sky.","His fist turned into a jet of water that soon expanded into a waterfall that enveloped all the fire. The waterfall slowly absorbed all of the flames until the last spark to emerge from the black hole had been extinguished, and the World Grace descended.","The World Grade landed on the newly formed bouquet of flowers formed by the Elemental Paper.","The white flowers bloomed and began folding over themselves continuously in the sky until they had created an even larger bouquet.","But this time, there were not just paper flowers. There were also paper cranes flittering amongst the flowers.","If a girl held such an enormous bouquet, there was no doubt that she would become the envy of every other unwed female at a wedding.","It just so happened that Wen Yu was holding this bouquet of flowers.","The streams of light rippling across the paper flowers were so brilliant that it was impossible to tear one’s eyes away.","As he sensed the changes to the Elemental Paper’s aura, Lin Yuan knew that it had evolved from Diamond X/Fantasy V to Suzerain/","Myth.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Elemental Paper.","[Fey Name]: Elemental Paper (Bouquet of Flowering Cranes)","[Fey Species]: Elemental-species/paper species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[Dance of Paper]: Transform the body into a piece of paper that is immune to physical attacks. However, it is especially vulnerable to elemental attacks. The paper has a teleporting power. The teleportation can be used every three seconds and has a radius of 20 kilometers.","[Paper Crane’s Promise]: The paper will be stacked to form a paper crane that can send messages. The paper crane will be engraved with the aura of the person receiving the message. If a person other than the receiver touches the paper crane, it will burst into flames. The paper crane has a teleporting power that is 30 times more powerful than that of Dance of Paper.","[Thoughts Letter Paper]: The paper will absorb the target’s blood and form a temporary contract with the target. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to communicate with each other using their thoughts, as their thoughts will automatically appear as words on the paper. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to read the words together.","[Faceless Paper]: An imaginary paper will appear in front of the target, and it can take the shape of the target[s appearance. As long as the Elemental Paper is not destroyed, the imaginary paper will be undamaged even if the target is killed.","[Paper Flower Funeral]: The paper will be folded into a flower that will form an imprint when it lands on a target. Even if the target is hidden, cloned, or affected by elements, the paper flower imprint can be used to sense the target’s location.","[Paper of Ten Thousand Forms]: The paper can pretend to be a person, fey, mountain, city, sea, or even sky. While in the imitation state, the entities hidden behind the paper can enjoy absolute defense.","[Paper World Carrier]: Its own body will become a carrier for other entities. The entities can be restructured to enter the paper world. When portions of the paper are broken apart, the entities stored within will be released. The paper carrier can be used to transport entities through Paper Crane’s Promise.","Exclusive Skill:","[Hear Heaven’s Secrets]: The contractor will become a book of secrets that is linked to the flying piece of paper. When the book’s pages are turned, it can transfer any knowledge within to the flying piece of paper.","[Truth Form Paper]: While the paper is flying around, soul power can be used to form a piece of paper that can investigate the truth. When questioning a target, the paper will be folded into a flower if the target is telling the truth, and it will break apart if the target is lying.","[Floating World Ever-Changing]: One’s body will be separated. As long as a piece of paper still exists, the owner of the paper can be revived through the remaining piece of paper.","Lin Yuan was immediately attracted by the Elemental Paper’s new exclusive skills and abilities.","Previously, the Elemental Paper had the same strategic significance as the Island Whale. But now that it had evolved to Myth Breed, its strategic significance was the equivalent of the Floating Island Whale!","The Elemental Paper’s strategic significance was extraordinary to start with.","Lin Yuan never expected its new abilities and exclusive skills to raise its already outstanding strategic significance!","Paper World Carrier allowed the Elemental Paper to split into pieces of paper that could be used to store both items and living creatures. Once the paper ripped, whatever was contained within would be released.","The Elemental Paper could deliver goods or troops across long distances.","If the ability’s benefits stopped there, Lin Yuan would not appraise it with such high strategic significance.","The most important factor was that Paper World Carrier could be used alongside Paper Crane’s Promise.","When Wen Yu used Dance of Paper, the effects could already affect a limitless expanse of space. Yet, Paper World Carrier was almost 30 times more effective!","Although the main world’s area had enlarged after fusing with the dimensional worlds, Wen Yu could still use Paper World Carrier to rapidly transport resources and troops to the necessary areas.","Now, no one in the main world could come close to Wen Yu regarding allocating and managing troops.","This was extremely important given the ongoing dead spirits crisis!","Compared to Paper World Carrier, Floating World Ever Changing seemed weaker.","But to Lin Yuan, Floating World Ever Changing was a stroke of genius!","Wen Yu’s strategic significance was incomparable.","She had always been hiding in the wings, so outsiders were unaware of her strategic value.","But once she was exposed, she would immediately become the target of assassination attempts and schemes.","This especially applied to when they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds as Lin Yuan could not yet be fully confident that he would be able to ensure her safety there as well.","But now that the Elemental Paper had Floating World Ever Changing, all Lin Yuan needed to do was place a portion of the Elemental Paper in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, and Wen Yu would be reincarnated there even if something bad happened to her.","Aside from Wen Yu’s own method of protecting herself, Lin Yuan’s Praying Universe Soul Whale and Floating Island Whale would also be able to shield her.","While Lin Yuan was looking through the Elemental Paper’s new abilities and exclusive skills, Wen Yu was also sensing the changes that had taken place due to the Elemental Paper’s evolution to Myth Breed.","Wen Yu could not hide her elation. It was obvious from her sparkling gaze that she was well aware of the elevation of her strategic significance due to the Elemental Paper’s evolution to Suzerain/Myth.","As the Elemental Paper continued to evolve, Paper World Carrier’s effects would also grow stronger.","“Young Master, Lord Liu Wencheng will be sending spirit qi professionals to the major cities. I can request to use the Elemental Paper’s Paper World Carrier to transport the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.”","Wen Yu was not the type to show off. Part of her reason for doing this was that she hoped to do more for the Radiance Federation. Additionally, she wanted to prove her strategic significance and value to the Radiance Federation. This way, no one would see her as undeserving of her post once she became a Radiance Knight and began assisting Lin Yuan in that capacity!","Lin Yuan smiled and nodded. He checked the time before he said to Wen Yu, “Wen Yu, let’s go back. Big Brother Liu should be back soon. Hold on to this brocade box. It contains law source crystals. You can use them to quickly evolve the Elemental Paper’s grade and quality.","“I believe that once you reach S-rank and the Elemental Power But after they spent more time together, she became used to his trait of being generous with those around him.","She also knew that the best way to replace him would be to do her best to manage Sky City and assist him in shouldering his responsibilities.","“Young Master, I will try my best to increase the Elemental Paper’s power as quickly as possible! The Earth Rush Golden Lotus and Sunlight Egret will soon be able to evolve as well. I will ask White Speak to help me then, too.","“I have already been unofficially selected to become part of the next generation of Radiance Knights. Since I don’t have combat abilities, there’s no need for me to be tested.","“Young Master, you will have to battle the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence multiple times. Big Brother Liu already mentioned that he’s excited to have a proper fight with you during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.”","Wen Yu paused for a moment before she continued in a regretful tone, “Young Master, if I was also a combat-class spirit qi professional, I would also want to have a good brawl with you!”","Spirit qi professionals often strengthened their bonds with each other through combat. Those who were truly close often battled and trained with each other.","For example, the Moon Empress and Night Leaning Moon often tested their skills against each other in their youth.","However, Night Leaning Moon would never do her best, and this frustrated the Moon Empress endlessly.","Eventually, the Moon Empress stopped asking Night Leaning Moon to train with her and asked Ji Changdeng to be her new battle buddy.","Only then did Night Leaning Moon become serious when she trained with the Moon Empress.","Unlike Liu Jie, Wen Yu was unable to fight with Lin Yuan. This was increases once again, it will be able to amaze us in even more ways!”","When Wen Yu first joined Lin Yuan, she was always embarrassed to accept anything that he gave her.","one of her regrets.","The glimmer of excitement immediately appeared in Lin Yuan’s eyes.","His past two years had been a long journey, but he had not had many opportunities to sharpen his sword against his peers.","Lin Yuan enjoyed the thrill of battle. Otherwise, he would not have climbed Star Tower in his early days of growth.","Lin Yuan really wanted to have a good fight with Liu Jie so he could see if he could defeat Liu Jie without using any of his secret weapons.","It was not just Liu Jie. Gu Lang, Zong Ze, Xia Qing, and An He were also formidable foes.","Due to the direction that Gao Feng had chosen, he was a support-type spirit qi professional, just like Wen Yu, and had no combat abilities.","However, it was said that Cicada Song had used a special method to turn Gao Feng into an A-rank spirit qi professional.","With Myth Breed feys, Gao Feng had no issue securing a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence despite not being skilled at combat!","A Fantasy Breed could not compare to a Myth Breed fey.","When Lin Yuan brought Wen Yu back to the Return from Faraway Mansion, they saw Liu Jie busy at work in the kitchen.","The Mother of Bloodbath followed him around and stared yearning at all the delicious dishes he was cooking.","If not for the fact that the drumsticks in the pot were yet to be fully cooked, the Mother of Bloodbath would have already tasted one.","Liu Jie looked at the Mother of Bloodbath with slight irritation. He took out a large platter of roast meat from his spatial equipment and handed it to it.","“Have this first. The drumsticks cooking in bamboo shoots and abalone juices will only be done 20 minutes later. You can have the first taste once it’s done!”","When he turned to hand the Mother of Bloodbath the platter of roast meat, Liu Jie caught sight of Lin Yuan and Wen Yu.","His stern expression morphed into a gentle smile."]},{"number":2663,"title":"Chapter 2663 Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2663 Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Jie had worked harder than anyone else this past year. He spent most of his time evolving his insect-species carcinoma feys.","He could tell that his personality had changed. He was now more bloodthirsty and apathetic.","But at thiat moment, he felt as though he had regained his original self.","His companions were his strongest source of warmth and strength, and Lin Yuan and Wen Yu were his most important companions.","Liu Jie badly missed the carefree time they spent together in the Return from Faraway Mansion.","When this thought struck him, Liu Jie was stunned for a moment before he smiled.","Perhaps he was the only one who saw that time as carefree. Even then, Lin Yuan had been silently increasing his power.","After the wave of warmth passed over him, Liu Jie suddenly felt the spirit qi in his body begin to surge and densify.","Liu Jie entered a mystical and mysterious state.","His hand dropped the plate of roasted meat that it had been holding. The meat fell to the ground and dirtied the previously clean floor.","With the Mother of Bloodbath’s power, it could have easily picked up the plate when Liu Jie dropped it. But it did not do so.","Instead, the Mother of Bloodbath suppressed its aura as it was afraid of getting in the way of Liu Jie promoting his spirit qi professional rank.","Lin Yuan and Wen Yu had blissful expressions. Both of them had been looking forward to Liu Jie promoting his spirit qi professional rank.","Once Liu Jie’s spirit qi professional rank was raised, Elegance’s power would also increase. It would evolve from Diamond X/","Fantasy V to Suzerain/Myth and gain another ability.","This meant that it would be able to produce another kind of insect. The new exclusive skill would allow all the insects it already controlled to become stronger.","Moreover, when Elegance became stronger, its control over insect-species carcinoma feys would also be strengthened!","The insect-species carcinoma feys that Liu Jie had transformed through the Firefly Demon Fetuses and regular insect-species carcinoma feys would all become more powerful.","The increase in the carcinoma feys’ powers would be the equivalent to the difference between a Class 4 dimensional rift and a Class 5 dimensional rift. It was a difference that only those who had experienced it could fully comprehend!","Liu Jie’s spirit qi professional promotion increased his power in a much more well-rounded manner than Lin Yuan’s had.","Lin Yuan’s power was more geared towards the functions of his feys.","Lin Yuan did not focus on power when he contracted feys. Rather, he prioritized their functions.","But in terms of pure power, Liu Jie was ahead of Lin Yuan.","It could be said that it was unlikely that anyone in the world could compete with Liu Jie in terms of power!","The title ‘Fifth Day Disaster’ was not an exaggeration!","The Mother of Bloodbath, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu tiptoed upstairs while trying to impact their environment as little as possible.","The process of a B-rank spirit qi professional evolving to A-rank took some time.","When Liu Jie was done, he would call out to Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, and the Mother of Bloodbath.","Once he returned to his room, Lin Yuan took out the Thoughts Letter Paper and communicated with Bai Qinghuan.","When he confirmed that everything was going well with Bai Qinghuan’s building of the base, he contacted the Samsara Realm Dictators stationed in the dimensional worlds.","The dimensional lifeforms had been assigned to different dimensional lifeforms as troops. The Samsara Realm Dictators were the generals who led their army of dimensional lifeforms to battle against the dead spirits.","Every Samsara Realm Dictator had been given a Thoughts Letter Paper. They normally used it to send reports and communicate with Lin Yuan. This made it easier for Lin Yuan to gain an understanding of how the war against the dead spirits was progressing.","If Lin Yuan wanted to work, he would have endless options of tasks to work on.","In the past, Lin Yuan would have tried his best to do everything himself. But now, he had learned to delegate tasks to others.","Su Yiren, Luo Lan, and Yin Lin were helping Lin Yuan to keep an eye on the dimensional lifeforms and the war against the dead spirits. If any issue cropped up, the three of them would immediately alert Lin Yuan.","Regardless of whether Lin Yuan had the ability to handle all these tasks himself, it was very time and energy-consuming to balance everything on his plate!","The dead spirits crisis did not help only Lin Yuan to grow. Every member of the Astronomical Parliament was also doing their best to improve.","Just as Lin Yuan was done being updated on the dimensional lifeform progress in taking on the dead spirits crisis, someone knocked on his door.","Lin Yuan knew that the only person who could be knocking on his door now was Liu Jie, who had successfully promoted his spirit qi professional rank!","Immediately when he opened his door, Lin Yuan was greeted by the excited Liu Jie, “Lin Yuan, my Elegance can finally evolve its grade!”","Liu Jie had been a pinnacle B-rank spirit qi professional for longer than Lin Yuan and Wen Yu combined. Thus, he felt extremely anxious to be able to evolve his feys’ grades.","“Big Brother Liu, Elegance should be able to evolve to Myth Breed anytime, right? Why don’t we evolve Elegance first! We’ll eat after that. There are many new restaurants in the Royal Capital.","“Long Tao told me about a few that Zhao Xiaochun has praised. When you’re done evolving Elegance, your insect-species carcinoma feys and fairies will need to be evolved. Let’s properly increase your power before the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection!”","Liu Jie shook his head. “I’m in no rush to increase my power. If the grade is stuck, I won’t be able to improve by much, anyway. The chicken drumsticks soaking in abalone juices that I have cooking on the stove has reached a boil. I can make a few more dishes, too.","“You, Wen Yu, and the Mother of Bloodbath haven’t had my cooking in some time. I can use this opportunity to show you my new skills! We’ll eat, chat, and have a much more comfortable time than if we go out to a restaurant!”","Lin Yuan did not try to force Liu Jie.","What Liu Jie said had been right. Regardless of how anxious he was to increase its power, there was no need to do it right this moment.","There were still a few days to go before the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection took place. This was enough time for Liu Jie to increase the overall power of his feys!","“Big Brother Liu, we shall trouble you then. Frankly, none of the chefs in the restaurants mentioned by Zhao Xiaochun can ever hold a candle to your skills!”","Although Lin Yuan was not completely insensitive and possessed a certain emotional quotient, he was not the type to overcompliment others. He only said those things about Liu Jie because this was how he truly felt!","Lin Yuan had tasted many famous Royal Capital restaurants and even experienced a confrontation in the Spirit Food Pavilion.","None of the chefs from Kitchen Fragrance Palace who had been taught some of Kitchen Fragrance Pavilion’s skills could compete with Liu Jie.","The only one who could stand toe-to-toe with Liu Jie was Zong Ze, who had received full knowledge of all of Kitchen Fragrance Palace’s skills!","If Liu Jie was not a spirit qi professional but instead decided to open a restaurant, it would definitely be just as famous as Spirit Food Pavilion!","Liu Jie was not the type to show off, but he liked it when Lin Yuan and Wen Yu complimented his culinary skills.","He did not cook just to fill the stomachs of his companions. Instead, he wanted to bring them happiness.","“Lin Yuan, I have a fair amount of ingredients left. The Mother of Bloodbath is a bottomless pit, and Wen Yu also has a large appetite. I will use a secret recipe to cook a 25-kilogram grouper and ribs marinated in seafood and winter bamboo duck soup.","“Let’s have a real feast tonight! We can evolve Elegance when we’re done eating! I have prepared the genetic model needed to complete the Diamond abilities.”","Liu Jie took out a dragonfly with six-colored wings and a long tail.","This insect-species fey was not foreign to Lin Yuan at all because he was the one who recommended the Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly to Liu Jie.","Ever since the Cage of Brahma Insects discovered that Lin Yuan was the Moon Empress’ disciple, they showed Lin Yuan every special insect-species fey they nurtured. This was their way of currying favor with him.","Lin Yuan did not turn down their gestures, and they eventually presented him with a pleasant surprise.","The Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly did not have combat abilities, but it was a superior support-type fey.","The Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly could increase the strength, speed, defense, and elemental energy of several insect-species feys. This meant that it had strengthening effects on both the interior and exterior aspects of feys.","It could strengthen feys who relied on their bodies for battle, like the Execution Blade Insect and Shield Ladybugs. It could also benefit feys who depended on elemental abilities in combat, such as the Flowing Plasma Electricity Insect and the Electromagnetic Chrysalis. Additionally, it could enhance the performance of feys that utilized elemental powers for scouting, like the Lonely Night Hurricane Moth.","Liu Jie was always very serious in his selection of the feys that would become part of Elegance’s genetic model.","Ever since Lin Yuan helped Liu Jie to obtain the Hurricane Owlet Moth, Liu Jie began using Elegance to take control of insect-species carcinoma feys. He stopped considering any other type of insect-species feys.","However, the fey that would be used to complete Elegance’s Diamond genetic model also ended up coming from Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan smiled at Liu Jie and said, “Big Brother Liu, that is a great decision. The Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly is very suitable for you. It will not only be able to support Elegance’s army of insects.","“Still, it can also support armies of carcinoma feys and insects, such as the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle that relies on its body for battle.”","Liu Jie summoned Elegance.","Elegance gave Liu Jie a peck on his cheek before it hid behind him.","Elegance had not seen Lin Yuan in some time. Although it was still familiar with Lin Yuan, it felt shy after seeing him again after such a long time.","Liu Jie gave the Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly to Elegance.","“Elegance, this is the fey for your Diamond genetic model. You need to complete your abilities first before you can evolve to Myth Breed!”","Elegance held the Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly to its chest, and it sunk into its body.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Elegance.","[Fey Name]: Insect Queen","[Fey Species]: Insect-species/fairy-species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Spiritual","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy V","Abilities:","[Execution Blade Insect]: Eight hooked insect legs will grow out of the body. The sense of taste, smell, and mouth will be degraded. The insect legs have extremely strong sensing ability. The hooked legs’ sharp end has mouths connected to the inner organs. When the legs pierce a target, the mouths will emerge and break through anything hard within the target’s body.","[Vibrating Armor Ladybug]: Its back will open and have a strong defense against attacks. Its back will also start to vibrate violently and reflect physical attacks. If targeted by elemental attacks, the vibrating back would be able to dodge a portion of the elemental damage.","[Flowing Plasma Electricity Insect]: The insect will spit out large amounts of plasma that will start to flow. The flowing plasma will have strong paralyzing effects. It will cause long-lasting electric-related damage to the target.","[Electromagnetic Chrysalis]: In a chrysalis state, it will be able to speed up the plasma accumulation rate. The plasma will be quickly released. In the moth state, it can use plasma to manipulate electromagnetic fields and control targets from a distance away.","[Lonely Night Hurricane Moth]: Flapping its wings can generate strong winds that it can manipulate to attack a target. Its wings will produce special scale powder that perfectly blends with the night or camouflage in the day.","[Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly]: It can boost other insect-species lifeforms and increase their speed, strength, defense, as well as storage of energy. When it is necessary, it can become a shield and take on a deadly attack on behalf of one of the feys it has boosted.","Exclusive Skill:","[Blast Recovery]: The Insect Queen will select a portion of the insects it produced and explode them. The explosion timings can be adjusted based on the positions of the insects. After the blast, the Insect Queen will regain some of the protein and spiritual power.","[Swarm Frenzy]: When the insect swarm is in a frenzied state, its speed will skyrocket. In the frenzied state, the insect swarm will be bloodthirsty and be able to replenish their vitality using the blood within the target.","Lin Yuan saw that Elegance now had a sixth ability!","“Big Brother Liu, Elegance will need to pick another insect-species fey for its new genetic model once it evolves to Myth Breed. I will get in contact with the Cage of Brahma Insects and other human federations to gather all precious and special insect-species feys. You can pick the most suitable one out of them!","“Judging from your current situation, you are done choosing all the insect-species carcinoma feys to be turned into fairies by the Firefly Demon Fetuses. Since you have made this decision, you should be done picking the direction for Elegance’s abilities!”","Liu Jie nodded seriously.","Liu Jie had experienced a period of feeling lost. It was Lin Yuan who gave Liu Jie the chance and courage to persevere in his journey.","As he continued to grow, Liu Jie became more aware of the importance of staying strong in his decisions.","He already had a clear plan for his future development.","If Lin Yuan helped him collect all the precious insect-species feys in the world, he would be able to find what he needed!","Lin Yuan had just witnessed Wen Yu’s improvement. Now, he was witnessing Liu Jie’s increase in power.","He genuinely loved the feeling of watching his companions improve!"]},{"number":2664,"title":"Chapter 2664: Death -Cleansing Scale Snake!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2664: Death -Cleansing Scale Snake!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Every dish Liu Jie made was a favorite of Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, and the Mother of Bloodbath.","During this meal, a significant amount of their stress evaporated.","They had all been busy tackling the dead spirits crisis, and it had been a huge drain on their mental constitutions. This was especially so because all four of them occupied extremely important roles in the dead spirits crisis.","While they ate, the four of them sipped on the Three Treasures Tea and chatted idly.","For the four of them, this was one of the few opportunities for respite.","At first, Liu Jie did not participate much in the group with Lin Yuan, Gao Feng, Gu Lang, Zong Ze, and the others.","But ever since he got to know a few of them better and formed friendships with them, he became interested in the news they sent.","“Zong Ze, Gu Lang, An He, and Gao Feng have all promoted their spirit qi professional rank. Zong Ze’s Fiery Sky Hou fused with tens of special strange flames, and its bloodline has transformed. It might be able to kill other Myth Breed feys with just its breath now.”","Lin Yuan smiled and nodded.","“Zong Ze is not the only one whose power has increased significantly. Gu Lang’s Cuttlefish of Days Past’s bloodline has also evolved after it evolved to Myth Breed. I heard that Zong Ze and Gu Lang had a fight, but it ended in a draw,”","Wen Yu was not especially interested in what Lin Yuan and Liu Jie were talking about.","She was not close with Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and the rest. Gao Feng was the one she was the most familiar with.","She could not beat Zong Ze and Gu Lang with brawn, but they might not be a","match for her in terms of strategic significance, even if they joined forces.","Now, Wen Yu no longer felt inferior to anyone.","Liu Jie was also aware of the event that Lin Yuan had mentioned. Zong Ze and Gu Lang never failed to test their skills against each other whenever the opportunity arose.","All of them had encountered various different opportunities in the past year and achieved astonishing leaps in power.","Aside from Lin Yuan, Liu Jie was also looking forward to battling Zong Ze, Gu Lang, An He, and the rest.","However, regardless of how much they had improved, it was unlikely that they would be able to defeat him.","After he contracted the special insect-species carcinoma feys, he was able to establish his formation much faster than he used to.","The four of them chatted until nightfall, and Liu Jie did not ask Lin Yuan to help him evolve Elegance to Myth Breed.","Liu Jie asked himself if he was able to handle the World Cleansing.","Elegance was the only source-type lifeform he had truly contracted. However, the insect-species carcinoma feys and fairies Elegance controlled also needed to be evolved alongside Elegance.","Liu Jie did not want to waste too much of Lin Yuan’s time.","It would take at least a day or two to evolve Elegance as well as all the entities it controlled.","It was true that Lin Yuan was busy. The army of Hundred Questions Beasts had just produced a type of healing-type fey that could neutralize death aura.","Although it had not shown overwhelmingly positive results during the experiments, just like the Dead Decay Earthworm, it could help take some of the strain off the humans. At the very least, it would reduce the shrinkage of the troops caused by death aura infections!","Lin Yuan intended to nurture these healing-type feys as soon as possible and deliver them to the Moon Empress so she could distribute them to the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters, who would then nurture them on a large scale. This was so the healing-type spirit qi professionals would be able to contract them as soon as possible.","This was far more important than Lin Yuan going with Liu Jie to evolve his feys. If he was even slightly late, it could lead to the deaths of thousands of the Radiance Federation’s troops!","With White Speak by Liu Jie’s side to protect him, Elegance and other carcinoma feys would definitely have no problems during their evolutions.","When Lin Yuan returned to the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Genius and the feys were already waiting for him next to the work table.","The fey was a snake that was around one meter long and had gray and green patterns on its body.","It was extremely active and slithered around the work table without stopping. Genius had to grab it with its tail to prevent it from slithering off of the work table.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the small snake. He saw that its ability, Healing Cleansing, could indeed neutralize death aura.","However, the small snake’s healing method was to bite the area infected by death aura and suck it out. One would have to be bitten by this small snake to be healed by it! This was an even more ridiculous method than being slathered in the Spitting Turtledove’s spit.","In order to test its skills, Lin Yuan slit his palm and injected death aura into the wound.","It did not take long before the flesh on Lin Yuan’s left forearm turned brown. The pain of the infection caused Lin Yuan to shudder.","Genius’ heart ached as it watched Lin Yuan. But there was no denying that this was the best method to test the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake’s healing abilities.","Lin Yuan had the human bloodline. If the test was done on a fey like the Black Back Mountain Boar, predicting the healing effects on humans would be difficult.","Lin Yuan grabbed the Death -Cleansing Scale Snake and held it to his palm.","Before Lin Yuan could instruct Genius to communicate with the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake, it began eagerly latching to his palm.","This caused Lin Yuan to look surprised.","Obviously, the Death -Cleansing Scale Snake was very attracted to death aura.","Otherwise, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake would not be acting this thirsty toward Lin Yuan’s palm, which had been infected by death aura.","Even a starving wolf would not eat the flesh infected by death aura. The Creation Masters had confirmed this.","Genius looked at the Death -Cleansing Scale Snake that was biting Lin Yuan’s hand. His brown hand started to return to its original color.","Genius said to Lin Yuan, “Yuan, the army of Hundred Questions Beasts have been testing how different healing-type feys react to death aura. They have only found four feys that aren’t averse to death aura.","“I conducted many experiments on these feys using death aura. The other three couldn’t hold on and died within two days. Only the Tree-Scaled Snake, the most normal healing-type fey of them all, mutated and transformed into the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake!","“Almost every Tree-Scaled Snake I experimented on mutated. So it wasn’t due to one Tree-Scaled Snake being an anomaly. The Death-Cleansing Scale Snake’s method of healing is a little biolent, but it does get the job done.","“After all of the research done by the army of Hundred Questions Beasts, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake has shown the best results.”","Genius was very serious when it explained the process of nurturing the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake to Lin Yuan.","It needed to wait for him to decide whether to use the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake.","Lin Yuan had used his own body to test the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake’s healing effects.","After his experiment, Lin Yuan was satisfied with the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake’s healing abilities.","Regardless of anything else, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake was able to cleanse death aura from an infection. It could even heal the wound on top of neutralizing the death aura.","In terms of its effects, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake was satisfactory.","It was likely that the troops submerged in danger would not mind letting the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake bite them.","“Genius, leave ten of the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes as samples and pack up the others.”","As it was a snake species fey, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake could not reproduce as quickly as the Dead Decay Earthworm.","But after being nurtured by the Creation Masters, every female snake could lay eggs at least four times annually. This meant that its reproduction rate would be increased by 30 to 40 times.","Moreover, if they used death aura to nurture the Tree-scaled Snakes, they could obtain an endless supply of the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes.","The Death -Cleansing Scale Snakes that were produced through reproduction, as well as mutation, would all be sent into the battleground once they evolved to Gold grade.","“Yuan, give me ten minutes. I have around 5,000 of these mutated","Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes. I expected them to be able to make some sort of positive impact, so I instructed the army of Hundred Questions Beasts to evolve them to Bronze/Legend using spirit qi crystals. They should be done evolving in another 20 minutes!”","Lin Yuan carried Genius and said seriously, “Genius, let me thank you on behalf of all humans.’","If these 5000 Bronze/Legend Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes were delivered to the healing-type spirit qi professionals, it would save at least 5000 lives!","Lin Yuan would evolve the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes slightly more before he distributed them to the Radiance Federation’s spirit qi professionals.","The Death -Cleansing Scale Snake would be the main source of strength for healing troops before a better alternative for healing and neutralizing death aura was found!","Genius leaped into Lin Yuan’s arms.","“Yuan, you don’t have to be so polite with me! I am not that noble. I only did so because I understand how you think!”","Genius was a Hundred Questions Beast that had been scorned from the moment it was born and was almost abandoned. The first person to show it warmth was Lin Yuan.","Hence, everything that Genius did was for Lin Yuan’s sake.","If Lin Yuan did not care about whether humans lived or died, Genius would not care either.","Suddenly, a thought struck Genius, and it said seriously, “Yuan, I discovered that the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake has a strong affiliation with water. The Tree-Scaled Snake is already able to live in water. I believe that the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake will also be useful to the sea clans.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up. It would be great if that was true!","If it were, many sea lifeforms would be healed and saved!","However, Lin Yuan would not immediately give the Death -Cleansing Scale Snake to the sea clans. He first had to ensure that there were enough for the humans. He would only help the sea clans once he ensured that there were enough Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes to meet the humans’ needs.","After the 5,000 Bronze/Legend Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes were stored in a Diamond fey storage box and handed to Lin Yuan, he went to the Radiant Moon Palace and gave the Diamond fey storage box to the Moon Empress.","When the Moon Empress looked inside the fey storage box, she could not stop excitement from blossoming on her face.","Lin Yuan had just provided the Dead Decay Earthworm and solved one of the Radiance Federation’s issues.","After only a few days, he nurtured a healing-type fey that could cleanse death aura.","From now on, the Radiance Federation’s no longer had to research feys. All they needed to do was nurture the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake!","The dead spirits crisis had only just begun, but two of the biggest issues had already been solved.","Now that medical treatment was handled, the humans could begin truly tussling with the dead spirits.","During the last imperial meeting, the Moon Empress had decided to reduce the number of subsequent imperial meetings. After all, all they would do during the imperial meetings was discuss the same issues that could not be solved! The Radiance Federation’s royalty’s time would be better spent handling sudden emergencies.","But now that they had the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake, it was necessary to hold another imperial meeting.","The Radiance Federation’s royalty would have to work together to distribute the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes.","The first batch of spirit qi professionals to contract the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes would be the cream of the crop.","The Death -Cleansing Scale Snakes would also have to be distributed to the other human federations once it was ensured that there were enough to go around in the Radiance Federation.","Given that the humans were on the brink of life and death, it was not the time to gatekeep and be selfish!","The Moon Empress did not say anything else to Lin Yuan. Instead, she hurriedly left to hold the imperial meeting.","The Moon Empress knew that she needed to enable the healing-type spirit qi professionals to contract the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes as soon as possible to protect the Radiance Federation’s troops to the greatest extent.","Lin Yuan’s job was done now that he had handed the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes to the Moon Empress. What happened next would be up to the operating system in the Radiance Federation.","When Lin Yuan returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion, Liu Jie had already left to evolve Elegance.","Elegance’s evolution went swimmingly. It had already evolved to Suzerain 1/Myth 1.","Elegance and the other insect-species carcinoma feys had managed to fend off the World Cleansing’s attacks, so none of them made contact with Elegance’s body.","This was the first time that White Speak was learning about Liu Jie’s combat style. This combat style reminded White Speak of the insect queens in the alien","insect dimensional rift.","But in actuality, the insect queens could not produce insects as quickly as Liu Jie could.","Liu Jie focused on sensing the exclusive skills Elegance gained after evolving to Myth Breed.","Liu Jie was very happy with both of Elegance’s exclusive skills.","Liu Jie had been afraid that after Elegance evolved, the exclusive skills it gained would not suit his chosen path.","This was the reason for Wang Zhong needing to make fundamental changes. But even after six months, he still did not manage to find a suitable new combat style. As a result, his combat power fell significantly.","After sensing Elegance’s exclusive skills, Liu Jie finally relaxed. At the same time, he was filled with prodigious joy.","Elegance truly knew him well!"]},{"number":2665,"title":"Chapter 2665: Gathering in the Return from Faraway Mansion!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2665: Gathering in the Return from Faraway Mansion!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Jie would only leave the outskirts of the Royal Capital and return to the Return from Faraway Mansion a day later.","Elegance’s evolution to Myth Breed allowed it to gain an exclusive skill that was very helpful for combat. The insect-species carcinoma feys under its control had also all increased in power.","His increase in power made Liu Jie even more excited to battle Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie knew that when it came to power, he could never hope to compare to","Lin Yuan.","He only wanted so badly to battle with Lin Yuan because he wanted to prove his determination!","Liu Jie wanted to show Lin Yuan how he had improved.","This was the same way that Wen Yu felt pressed to demonstrate her strategic value!","With the exclusive skill that Elegance gained, Liu Jie’s insect-species carcinoma feys and the fairies had changed in ways that might be able to cause Lin Yuan to stumble during battle!","When Lin Yuan returned from the Radiant Moon Palace yesterday, he received a call from Gao Feng.","“Ah Yuan, I didn’t expect you to have done so much while I was in seclusion! I just came out of seclusion. Let’s have a get-together! I haven’t had Zong Ze and Liu Jie’s cooking in a very long time. I miss them so much! Liu Jie is with you, right? I will get in contact with Zong Ze. If we are all available, we can have a meal together!”","Lin Yuan smiled and said, “No problem. We went to Zong Ze’s place the last time. Let’s do it at my place this time!”","Lin Yuan could tell that Gao Feng had not changed at all. He did not feel hostility toward him and was still his old self.","Frankly, Lin Yuan was also missing Zong Ze, Gao Feng, and the rest. They could use this opportunity to have a proper gathering before they headed to the Radiance Sacred Hall!","Since Lin Yuan had set his mansion as the location for this gathering, it meant that he was the host.","Lin Yuan intended to contact Gu Lang, An He, and his new friend Xia Qing to invite them to this gathering at the Return from Faraway Mansion.","They could decide for themselves if they wanted to come. They should all be very busy at such a time. Lin Yuan would not force them to come if they could not make the time.","When Gao Feng heard what Lin Yuan said, he smiled and said, “It looks like we’ll be able to enjoy another feast of flavor! I heard that Zong Ze had improved substantially. He is probably preparing to fight you and Xia Qing for a spot as a Radiance Envoy.”","Gao Feng spoke in a very casual tone.","This was because he had no intention of vying for a spot as a Radiance Envoy.","He did not have the power to allow him to do so, even if he wanted to.","Additionally, just like Wen Yu, he was already unofficially selected as a Radiance Knight.","He was also irreplaceable due to the Memory-consuming Eight Tunes Box.","As a support-type spirit qi professional, he only needed to ensure he had abilities that no one could replicate or replace! There was no need for him to come up with ways to defeat enemies because support-type spirit qi professionals always went into battle with a team, and the team needed to protect their support-type teammates.","Lin Yuan smiled and shook his head.","He was already standing at the top of the main world and was the savior of the main world.","It was possible that even the Moon Empress would not be a match for him in combat.","Hence, there was no question that he could secure one of the Radiance Envoy spots!","Lin Yuan knew that the Moon Empress wanted him to become a Radiance Envoy and also intended to do so.","As a transmigrator born into this world, Lin Yuan already saw himself as a part of the Radiance Federation.","He had already decided to take on the duty of safeguarding the Radiance Federation back when he first participated in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","He had upheld that decision ever since then.","After hanging up the call with Gao Feng, he received a call from Zong Ze before he could call Gu Lang and An He.","When he picked up the call, Lin Yuan heard Zong Ze’s happy voice on the other end.","The more he got to know Zong Ze, the more he felt that Zong Ze had schizophrenic tendencies.","This was not a wrongful accusation.","Those who understood Zong Ze would think that he was cold and aloof. This made people want to stay far away. But once one got to know Zong Ze better, one would realize that he had a cold exterior but warm interior.","Normally, those with cold exteriors and warm interiors were like cups of warm water. However, Zong Ze was more like a cup of lava.","Lin Yuan only saw Zong Ze as a friend, but he had no idea that Zong Ze saw him in a special way.","His curse had afflicted Zong Ze for a very long time. Lin Yuan was the one who saved him from this curse.","But as he spent more time with Lin Yuan, he found himself becoming more taken with Lin Yuan’s personality.","Otherwise, he would not see Lin Yuan with the same level of importance as Gu Lang after only knowing each other for such a short time.","“Lin Yuan, congratulations on all your achievements and improvements! You will soon become a Radiance Envoy and participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. You’ll probably be setting off for the Radiance Sacred Hall the day after tomorrow.","“I was just on the phone with Gao Feng. Since we have time now, why don’t we all gather together? It’ll also give you the chance to taste my upgraded skills!”","Lin Yuan smiled and said, “Zong Ze, you can come anytime. You can stay here too. Big Brother Liu has just become an A-rank spirit qu professional. He is currently increasing the power of Elegance and his other insect-species carcinoma feys. He’ll only be back later. Gao Feng will be here tomorrow. I will also contact Gu Lang, An He, and Xia Qing.”","On the other end of the call, Zong Ze was beaming toothily.","If Chef Supreme saw Zong Ze now, he would definitely wonder if his disciple had hit his head and was experiencing mental issues. He had never seen him smile like this in all his years of knowing Zong Ze!","“Lin Yuan, Gu Lang and An He are with me. I’ll take the two of them over with me. They are insisting that I train with them!”","Previously, An He had not been on good terms with Gu Lang and Zong Ze. Lin Yuan brought them together and allowed them to slowly turn from enemies to friends.","It could be said that Lin Yuan was the center of the group.","Zong Ze paused momentarily before continuing, “We aren’t too familiar with","Xia Qing. You can contact her!”","Zong Ze was telling the truth. He, Gu Lang, and An He were not close to Xia Qing.","This was because she never used to take them seriously. She had extremely high standards and never thought much of them.","She only noticed Liu Jie because Liu Jie had protected Cold Frost City.","The only ones Xia Qing took seriously were Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","If anyone else called to invite her, she would definitely turn them down. But not if the call came from Lin Yuan!","Lin Yuan just mentioned that Liu Jie had become an A-rank spirit qi professional and that Elegance had evolved to Myth Breed.","Elegance was a very unreasonable fey. It was the only fey that Liu Jie could contract.","When its grade was low, it had been very weak. But once it evolved to Gold grade and its three abilities allowed it to control and produce armies of insects, its power became astonishing.","Otherwise, Liu Jie would never have been able to become part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence with just one fey.","When Elegance evolved to Myth Breed, every insect that Elegance controlled skyrocketed in power.","Zong Ze could not be fully confident that he would be able to defeat Liu Jie’s Suzerain/Myth Insect Queen.","Moreover, Elegance was no longer Liu Jie’s strongest source of power!","Liu Jie’s true source of power were the Diamond alien insects and Myth Breed insect-species fairies.","Zong Ze was envious of his friends’ improvements but never resented them.","Zong Ze had remained by Chef Supreme’s side for the entire month before his lifespan was supposed to come to an end.","Zong Ze thought that Chef Supreme was going to leave him, and he had been devastated and miserable. To him, Chef Supreme’s death was no different from the death of his parents, as he had grown up by Chef Supreme’s side.","Zong Ze had a strong will, but he could not help but cry when he was alone at night.","Later, the Radiant Moon Palace sent over a fey called the Lifespan Mouse. Once Chef Supreme formed a contract with it, his lifespan was no longer limited.","Zong Ze later found out that the Lifespan Mouse had come from Lin Yuan.","This caused Zong Ze to feel even more grateful to Lin Yuan.","“I will go and get more ingredients. I know what all of you like to eat! If the Mother of Bloodbath is there too, I can prepare some roast meat too. Otherwise, the little dishes I make might not be enough to satisfy the Mother of Bloodbath’s appetite!”","Zong Ze had a vivid memory of the Mother of Bloodbath’s appetite.","Unlike Liu Jie, Zong Ze was not used to making dishes with large portions. He preferred making small, intricate dishes that were always a feast for the eyes. The dishes he made could usually be finished with one mouthful.","As a result, no one felt full and was always left wanting more after eating his dishes. Luckily, he always made a large variety to ensure his guests were full.","The only thing that Zong Ze could think of that would satisfy the Mother of Bloodbath’s appetite was roasting a large animal.","Due to the relationship between Zong Ze and Lin Yuan, he immensely respected the Mother of Bloodbath after discovering it was Lin Yuan’s Path Protector. He began seeing the Mother of Bloodbath as his senior.","Otherwise, he would never consider the Mother of Bloodbath’s feelings when he was preparing ingredients!","Phone calls were not soundproof. With the Mother of Bloodbath’s power, it easily overheard Zong Ze and Lin Yuan’s conversation.","When it heard that Zong Ze was coming over, the Mother of Bloodbath could not help but become excited, and its gluttonous spirit sparked to life!","Zong Ze and Liu Jie were equals when it came to their culinary skills. The Mother of Bloodbath loved both of their food.","After it became used to Liu Jie’s food, the Mother of Bloodbath only became interested in other food if it came from Zong Ze.","“Lin Yuan, I’ll go and see Zong Ze so I can help him carry the items.”","Lin Yuan knew what the Mother of Bloodbath was thinking and plotting. It was worried that Liu Jie would not prepare sufficient ingredients or that the ingredients would not suit its tastes.","Liu Jie was almost done evolving his feys. The Mother of Bloodbath could use this opportunity to indulge as much as it wanted.","Liu Jie had already made more dishes than usual last night, and all of them had been large portions.","However, it had still not been enough for the Mother of Bloodbath.","Zong Ze heard the Mother of Bloodbath’s voice through his call with Lin Yuan. Thus, he asked Lin Yuan for the Mother of Bloodbath’s number.","Once he was done with his call with Lin Yuan, Zong Ze called the Mother of Bloodbath and arranged for a place to meet.","Meanwhile, Lin Yuan called Xia Qing and invited her.","Ever since the Dead Spirits Wells were constructed, Xia Qing had been busy battling the dead spirits.","She was only forced to return to her usual residence because she needed to participate in the upcoming Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and would have to report to Radiance Sacred Hall two days later.","Xia Qing would never have agreed if an invitation had come from anyone else at such a time because she felt that the time would be better spent killing more dead spirits!","But since the invitation was coming from Lin Yuan, it was a different story.","At first, Xia Qing had only been curious about Lin Yuan. She wondered how he had managed to acquire all his power at his young age.","Only when Lin Yuan killed the Freedom Envoy Liu Yifan she formed a positive impression of him.","When the positive emotions settled, Xia Qing first thought that she had developed romantic feelings for him. This caused her to panic slightly.","But after she cleared her mind, she realized that her emotions did not come from a place of romance but rather deep respect.","This respect had only just taken root in Xia Qing and Lin Yuan went on to accomplish many great things. All the great things he did nurtured the respect she felt into a towering tree!","To only discuss recent events, Xia Qing personally experienced the dangers of battling the dead spirits and understood the Radiance Federation’s troops’ circumstances better than anyone else.","The environment concentrated with death aura stripped away all of the troops’ vivacity, and after the death spirits injured them, the death aura contaminated their bodies. Since regular healing-type feys could not heal these injuries, they had no choice but to amputate the contaminated parts or resign themselves to death.","Xia Qing had been very stressed about this.","Yet, Lin Yuan managed to solve both of these issues within the short span of a week!","How could a person like this not draw respect out of Xia Qing?","“I only just returned from the Dead Spirits Wells. I’ll go over to see you once I clean myself up! I can’t cook, but I can bring some ingredients.”","Xia Qing was not good at expressing herself. However, she felt just as grateful to Lin Yuan as Zong Ze did. This was because Lin Yuan had saved her grandfather, her only remaining family.","After he invited Xia Qing, Lin Yuan stretched.","At this moment, Lin Yuan intended to rest and have a good time with his friends. He would wait calmly for Tower Canon to make their move.","He knew that Tower Canon would never allow the dimensional lifeforms to continue fending off the dead spirits or for the dead spirits to become fuel for the dimensional lifeforms!"]},{"number":2666,"title":"Chapter 2666: Epoch God Palace and the Radiance Federation!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan had his own reasons for making such a prediction.","Tower Canon had been recuperating in the shadow for thousands of years and only just managed to implement their Sleeper’s Revival plan.","They must have anticipated many of these present issues.","Given that they could not allow the Sleeper’s Revival plan to end before achieving its purpose, they had to have more moves they were waiting to use!","Lin Yuan’s approach towards taking on his enemies was always to address the issues as they cropped up. Hence, he did not fear Tower Canon at this present moment.","When Tower Canon made their move, it would also allow Lin Yuan to get a better look at their true capabilities!","He would eventually have to take them on. He was already prepared to face the real Eight Pages of Tower Canon in battle.","“Xia Qing, you don’t have to bring any ingredients. Just come and eat! Zong Ze has gone with the Mother of Bloodbath to get ingredients. With the Mother of Bloodbath buying the ingredients, they will definitely end up with more than they need! ”","Xia Qing did not insist and said, “I’ll go over once I’m done packing.”","Xia Qing was the straightforward type, so she did not stay on the line to chat with Lin Yuan.","She knew of the Mother of Bloodbath. But when she was first acquainted with the Mother of Bloodbath, she had no idea that the Mother of Bloodbath was Lin Yuan’s Path Protector. Instead, she knew it as a member of theHeavenly Family","Cottage.","Lin Yuan was also the reason for the alliance formed between the Radiance Federation and Heavenly Family Cottage.","With Xia Qing’s position and status, it was not difficult for her to find out such information.","She could no longer measure just how much Lin Yuan had done for the Radiance Federation.","At first, the only role models in Xia Qing’s mind were her parents and grandfather. Now, she had another – Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was the idol of many youths in the Radiance Federation, but Xia Qing would never lose sight of her aim as a fan. She would only silently try to follow in his footsteps. She would not try to outdo him, just to become someone like him.","After inviting Xia Qing, Lin Yuan yawned.","He had been busy and on the edge for many days. A few days of rest were like a luxury to him. Lin Yuan was not the type who could live without working.","While he was waiting for his friends in the Return from Faraway Mansion, Lin","Yuan communicated with Bai Qinghuan and Qin Yu through the Thoughts","Letter Paper. They told him about the progress of the construction of the fortresses in the dimensional worlds.","After the Elemental Paper evolved to Suzerain/Myth, Wen Yu left to see Mystic Moon so she could tell him about her new abilities.","Paper World Carrier was extremely important to the Radiance Federation now.","Both the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes and Dead Decay Earthworms needed to go through a logistical process to be dispatched.","These resources were delivered by humans who always had to perform careful checks to ensure that nothing was wrong before they could be delivered to the next stage.","There were no problems with this method, but the efficiency was lowered.","With a lower efficiency, it could cost the lives of many troops who were fighting by the Dead Spirits Wells.","These issues would be eliminated by using Paper World Carrier to transport the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes and Dead Decay Earthworms. Wen Yu would be able to quickly deliver the resources to the troops on the frontline.","Mystic Moon was shocked, to say the least, after he learned of Wen Yu’s ability.","He had already been stunned by the Elemental Paper’s previous abilities. Yet, it was able to bring him an even greater surprise after evolving into Suzerain/Myth!","Mystic Moon immediately reported Wen Yu’s new abilities to the Moon Empress.","After learning of this, the Moon Empress immediately instructed Wen Yu to send out the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes and Dead Decay Earthworms that the Creation Masters had nurtured.","This was originally a very large undertaking. But with the Elemental Paper’s Paper World Carrier, Wen Yu could easily complete this job. She was not at all challenged by merely delivering resources.","Wen Yu returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion once she was done with the task.","When she returned, Liu Jie was still not back from evolving the feys. However, Zong Ze, Gu Lang, An He, and the Mother of Bloodbath had all arrived.","The three of them had initially intended to buy more ingredients. But when they saw how the Mother of Bloodbath was picking ingredients, they realized that their idea of ‘more’ was not the same as that of the Mother of Bloodbath. Its idea of ‘less’ already exceeded its idea of ‘more’!","As the Mother of Bloodbath swept through the market for ingredients, they quickly filled up half of a Diamond fey storage box.","Zong Ze gulped when he saw this.","Even if he worked his hardest and used all the skills that Kitchen Fragrance Palace had imparted to him to turn these ingredients into dishes, he would not be done using all of them even after working in the Return from Faraway Mansion’s kitchen for five decades.","Zong Ze had always known that he was a good cook. Gu Lang always gobbled down large portions of food that he made.","But Gu Lang’s appetite was not considered large compared to the Mother of Bloodbath!","Unbeknownst to Zong Ze, the Mother of Bloodbath had already held itself back.","At the thought of Zong Ze and Liu Jie’s cooking skills, the Mother of Bloodbath wanted to eat everything and anything they could make. After all, there was unlikely to be any ingredient in this world that the two of them did not know how to turn into a dish.","There were no disadvantages to buying more, just to be prepared!","When the three of them saw Wen Yu, they greeted her before Zong Ze made a beeline to the kitchen and began preparing his feast.","When the three of them saw Lin Yuan, they could not stop themselves from taking turns to hug him.","After being reunited with their friends after such a long time apart, all of them were overwhelmed with emotions.","A merry gathering began in the Return from Faraway Mansion. Xia Qing arrived soon after Wen Yu returned.","Meanwhile, on the other side of the sea...","An ancient castle on an island was swallowed by a dimensional rift leaking black miasma. The concentrated death aura flowed in all directions and rapidly withered everything alive on the island.","Eight strange figures were sniffing the air with yearning.","The death aura that was extremely lethal to living creatures was nourishment for these eight figures.","After the eight of them spent a long time tasting the death aura, Third Page Violet Light Green tossed a bright red fruit in one hand as she said with amusement, “The humans have indeed produced a hero! They are actually able to control all of the dimensional lifeforms from the dimensional worlds to fend off the dead spirits!","“I underestimated lifeforms from these five dimensional worlds. They managed to consume the death aura and turn it into nutrients. If we don’t do something, the dead spirits crisis will come to a standstill!”","While she spoke, Third Page Violet Light Green did not look anxious at all. Rather, her tone contained derision.","Seventh Page Concubine Winding narrowed her eyes and said nonchalantly, “The humans probably think that they have won this stage of the dead spirits crisis! The humans sure are naive. They can hold back the dead spirits from invading by laying down the metal-type stone boards. Using the Dead Spirits Wells can funnel and redirect the dead spirits.","“The humans’ actions are indeed helpful for this initial stage of the dead spirits’ revival. But in another two months, the dead spirits will explode out, and it won’t be as easy for the humans to stop them then! Let’s continue trying to fuse the dead world with this Class 2 world.","“As long as the dead world becomes connected to this Class 2 world, we will be able to open the death dimensional rift in this world anytime! Then, the humans will truly find out what it means to be swarmed by dead spirits!” First Page Crimson could not help but frown.","Seventh Page Concubine Winding was not the type to behave ostentatiously, but she despised humans with every fiber of her being.","This was because she came from a higher-class world. It was natural for her to look down on lifeforms from a lower-class world.","First Page Crimson had felt the same way when he first woke up.","However, First Page Crimson recently had gotten the increasingly strong feeling that something was wrong.","There was no way for humans from a Class 1 world to surpass the boundaries of a Class 1 world.","The hero that Third Page Violet Light Green mentioned should not exist in this main world!","This was an anomaly for a Class 1 world.","Usually, for a Class 1 world to fuse with a dimensional world, a Class 6 dimensional rift would have to open in the Class 1 world and lead to a","catastrophe. Eventually, the energy from the two worlds would connect, and repeated calamities would guide the dimensional worlds to combine with the Class 1 world.","This was why every Class 2 world needed to recuperate for a very long time before it could begin thriving.","Otherwise, there would be no need for the Sky Beyond the Clouds, which had the duty of maintaining order in the worlds to protect Class 2 worlds!","But this Class 1 world was far too peculiar that First Page Crimson could not help but come up with a suspicion.","Seeing as things were progressing exactly along his suspicions, First Page","Crimson could not help but say, “We can’t let our guard down. I suspect that other lifeforms from higher-class worlds have arrived in this world and are putting up obstacles for us! How else could a Class 1 world undergo such momentous changes in just two years?","“This is a key juncture during the main world’s fusion with the dead world. We can’t leave now. Otherwise, I would personally go to investigate the Radiance Federation and find out if someone is supporting them!”","First Page Crimson’s words caused Second Page Warbler Candle to frown slightly.","Second Page Warbler Candle was the second one of the Eight Pages to wake up after First Page Crimson. She had even investigated and observed this Class 1 world on First Page Crimson’s behalf.","She believed that the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection was when all the changes began.","One of the young men from the Radiance Federation had distinguished himself during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Second Page Warbler Candle could not help but shake her head when this thought entered her mind.","That young man was not even a B-rank spirit qi professional. He was only able to defeat his opponents by using his mermaid bloodline.","Second Page Warbler Candle had seen everything clearly through Second Page Revival.","That young man was not the only person in the main world who had evolved his bloodline using the mermaid bloodline. The Goddess of Mercy was another example.","Second Page Warbler Candle just could not find it in herself to attribute all the changes in the Class 1 world to Lin Yuan.","But it was true that it was only after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection that the Radiance Federation transformed its position and managed to overtake the Freedom Federation to become the dominant faction of the main world!","Second Page Warbler Candle could not understand how the Heavenly Family Cottage and the Vast Sea Labyrinth were suddenly on such good terms with the Radiance Federation.","The old fellow from the Radiance Federation had indeed set his spirit fire alight, but the Heavenly Family Cottage and Vast Sea Labyrinth were on a completely different level!","While Second Page Warbler Candle was frowning and deep in contemplation, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid said indifferently, “Crimson, don’t you think you’re overthinking? When we first arrived in this world, it sensed our presence, and the world willpower sealed off this world.","“So no one else could have come to this Class 1 world after us! They would have already eliminated us if they could break the world willpower.","“How could they allow us to awaken from our slumber? Crimson, you have become careful and cautious ever since Epoch God Palace defeated us. This isn’t beneficial for our objective of invading this Class 1 world!”","Second Page Warbler Candle never got along with First Page Crimson. Second Page Warbler Candle always liked watching the other Eight Pages disparaging First Page Crimson.","But at this moment, Second Page Warbler Candle felt that Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s thoughts were too simple.","Second Page Warbler Candle did not want to side with First Page Crimson, but her thoughts aligned more with his. At the same time, she wanted the other Eight Pages to take the faction behind the Radiance Federation seriously.","Second Page Warbler Candle decided to bring up Epoch God Palace.","“We don’t know what Epoch God Palace’s motives are for remaining in this Class 1 world. It’s clear that they don’t belong here. Since they arrived here before we did, do you think they’re behind the anomalies?”","Second Page Warbler Candle’s words had a greater effect than First Page Crimson’s words.","The previous encounter with Epoch God Palace had caused the Eight Pages of Tower Canon to become extremely fearful of them.","It was true that Epoch God Palace had not interfered even once in the Sleeper’s Revival plan.","But this did not mean that they were not secretly helping the Radiance Federation.","If this matter was really related to Epoch God Palace, it would be very bad for Tower Canon!","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow was silent for a moment before she said, “I think we should try making contact with Epoch God Palace so we can get a better idea of what they want from the main world. If both our goals are in agreement, they might be able to help us!”","Sixth Page Wave Glow scoffed.","“Do you really think that Epoch God Palace will be willing to work with us? If you think it’s possible, you can be the one to make contact with them! I hope you manage to win their cooperation.”","Sixth Page Wave Glow resented Fifth Page Falling Rainbow because the incident she and Second Page Warbler Candle had caused had set the Sleeper’s Revival plan back by thousands of years.","Sixth Page Wave Glow was about to retort when she was interrupted by Eighth","Page Eye Shadow’s soft voice, “There’s no need to make contact with Epoch God Palace. We have already begun fusing the dead world with this Class 2 world.. We can’t turn back now! Even if a bottomless chasm is waiting for us at the end of the road, we have no choice but to walk on!”"]},{"number":2667,"title":"Chapter 2667: The Main World’s Protector!","paragraphs":["Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Eighth Page Eye Shadow rarely spoke, but each time she did, she said things that the other Eight Pages could not ignore.","“That’s right. It’s just as Eye Shadow says. The relationship between Tower","Canon and Epoch God Palace can never be mended. The only way would be if Tower Canon had never targeted Eye Shadow all those years ago. Tower Canon still doesn’t understand Epoch God Palace’s full capabilities.","“Given the circumstances, there’s no way that Tower Canon can take on Epoch God Palace. I only hope that Tower Canon’s actions don’t lead Epoch God Palace to come up with any ideas or think we are trying to ruin their original plans.","Otherwise, Tower Canon and Epoch God Palace will have to clash once again.”","A moment later, First Page Crimson said, “Since we know that there’s no way back. We need to make sure that we get it right. Let’s teach the lifeforms of this world that resistance is futile!”","While First Page Crimson spoke, the enormous crevice behind him continued to leak death aura that contaminated the main world’s roots.","Slowly, the rift became quieter, as though it was emulating the foreboding calm before the storm.","By the time Liu Jie returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion, it was already abuzz with activity.","After greeting Gao Feng, Xia Qing, Gu Lang, and An He, Liu Jie entered the kitchen to join Zong Ze.","The Mother of Bloodbath’s mouth watered as it watched Zong Ze and Liu Jie.","Zong Ze and Liu Jie worked very well together. Every time they finished cooking a dish, they would take out a portion of it to keep the Mother of Bloodbath at bay.","The Mother of Bloodbath happily snacked on what they gave it while Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, Gao Feng, Gu Lang, and Xia Qing began chatting on the sofa.","This was the first time that Xia Qing was making Wen Yu’s acquaintance, but she was always friendly towards girls.","Furthermore, Xia Qing understood Wen Yu’s abilities and knew that she was in charge of delivering information to the entire Radiance Federation. It was also she who had solved the Radiance Federation’s resource transportation issues.","Xia Qing could not help but be curious about Wen Yu.","Suddenly, a feeling arose in Xia Qing, and she looked at Lin Yuan.","It seemed as though everyone in his orbit was exceptional.","Previously, Wen Yu was merely a moon attendant working in the Radiant Moon Palace. She did not possess any capabilities that allowed her to stand out.","But after meeting Lin Yuan, she managed to transform completely in just two years.","The moon attendants were chosen by the Radiant Moon Palace’s four tea","attendants. The four tea attendants had a very good eye for talents.","If Wen Yu was truly this amazing, they would not have kept her as a regular moon attendant!","With this thought, Xia Qing quickly shook her head.","She did not know how Lin Yuan managed to grow to such an extent, but she still saw him as the same person he had been a year ago during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","An He took a few sips of the Three Treasures Tea.","“Lin Yuan, your tea tastes much better than my Master’s sea! The osmanthus flavor is fragrant and strong without being bitter. It also has refreshing capabilities. Having a cup of this by the window during winter would be absolute bliss!”","An He was not exaggerating. This was genuinely how he felt.","Wen Yu was the one who had created the Three Treasures Tea. Its name came from the three ingredients it was made of.","Wen Yu had conducted many experiments before she finally decided to toss in the dried flowers of the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus to complement the bitterness.","The pairing of the osmanthus flower and plum flowers made the drink even smoother and more refreshing.","The Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ flower petals also provided an invigorating effect.","Lin Yuan’s Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus grew up in the Pure Land of Bliss and was nourished by the pure spirit qi for a few months before he brought it to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","It could be said that very few feys in the world could produce resources that the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus could.","An He only started working hard recently.","In the past, he would never leave the house if he could help it. When he was at home, his favorite activity was to drink tea and look out the window at the scenery.","As he sensed his recent growth, An He felt rather regretful.","If only he had not been so laid back in the past, he would already have reached a much higher level than he was now.","Presently, there was still a gap between himself and Zong Ze and Gu Lang. With this thought, An He could not help but sigh heavily.","Otherwise, given his character, he would already have asked Gu Lang and Zong Ze to train with him.","Wen Yu could not help but smile when she heard An He praise the Three Treasures Tea.","She was very proud of the Three Treasures Tea, and both Lin Yuan and Liu Jie liked drinking it.","Amidst her day-to-day activities, regardless of how busy she was, she would produce a batch of Three Treasures Tea whenever she got her hands on the Cinnabar Sweet Osmanthus’ flowers.","Lin Yuan said happily, “Wen Yu is the one who concocted the Three Treasures Tea. If you like it, she can give you some before you leave. An He, how has your growth been coming along?”","If anyone else had asked him this question, An He might not respond honestly.","But since It came from Lin yuan, An He (110 not try to nide anything ana replied, “Lin Yuan, you know of all my feys. They need pure earth-elemental energy in order to evolve their bloodlines. Master has been very busy trying to achieve a breakthrough.","“With scarce resources, they have all gone to him to help him in this endeavor. My power hasn’t increased by much since we last met, but I have improved my combat skills.”","An He’s voice sounded rather bitter.","When he was picking out his feys, he had only thought about picking the strongest ones. He had not considered the difficulty of nurturing them at all.","An He’s words resonated with Gu Lang as he was facing the same situation with his feys.","But he had the advantage of having Bamboo Monarch, a Class 5 Creation Master, as his master. Bamboo Monarch had provided him with significant help. Otherwise, it would also be difficult for him to increase his power.","Xia Qing did not react much.","Her increase in power had also been stalled due to a lack of resources, but she was already accustomed to this.","After fighting on the frontlines for so long, she understood the world’s ways and how precious high-class Creation Master resources were.","The Creation Masters were always the irreplaceable kingpins of the world as they were the only ones who could produce resources and create experts. Gao Feng was the member of the group who was the most familiar with Lin","Yuan.","It was clear that Lin Yuan had asked An He this question because he wanted to help them after hearing about their needs.","Gao Feng had not made many friends in his life. Being born to a top faction, Gao Feng had watched people scheme and play tricks all his life. Many of his fellow faction members had parted ways after plotting against each other. Hence, he had long learned to put up a wall against potential friends.","Furthermore, after choosing the path of a support-type spirit qi professional and being unable to find a team, he had lost even more hope in the bonds of friendship.","Only after he met Lin Yuan did Gao Feng learn what friendship was like.","Zong Ze, Gu Lang, An He, and the rest who Gao Feng eventually became friends with were all people he got to know through Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan rapped his finger on the table twice before saying to An He, Gu Lang, Gao Feng, and Xia Qing with utmost seriousness, “Tell me exactly what resources you’re lacking, and I’ll supply you with them. After this meal, we’ll make sure that all of your powers reach a new level before the Radiance Envoy selection begins.","“That way, the Radiance Envoy selection will truly become interesting. I will also be able to use these upcoming fights to raise the spirits of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation!”","Lin Yuan’s words caused a shock to bloom on Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and Xia Qing’s faces.","None of them thought that Lin Yuan was lying.","They were all disciples of members of royalty, and Xia Qing was the Spacetime Elder’s granddaughter. They all knew that Lin Yuan was the one who supplied all those vital resources to Federation.","Given that Lin Yuan was able to supply resources to all of the Radiance","Federation, it went without saying that he could do the same for them.","Zong Ze, Gao Feng, and An He had already received Lin Yuan’s help in the past.","If Lin Yuan had not raised the Fiery Sky Hou’s powers, Zong Ze might have already been killed in the abyssal world.","Xia Qing, An He, Gu Lang, and Gao Feng all knew the implications of Lin Yuan’s words.","The four of them did not bother being overly courteous and just bumped fists with him.","There was no need to be explicit about one’s emotions amongst friends. Action was much more important.","If, in the future, Lin Yuan ever needed any of them to take on an enemy with him, none of them would hesitate to agree to fight to the death alongside him!","There was one thing Lin Yuan said that was right: something had to be done to raise the morale of the Radiance Federation’s citizens. There was no better way to do this than to exhibit their power during the Radiance Envoy selection. This would give all of the Radiance Federation’s citizens a sense of security.","Gu Lang said softly, “Lin Yuan, Zong Ze is still in the kitchen. He’ll tell you what resources he needs once this meal is over. When the time comes, all of us must put on a good fight. It will be a performance where we show all that we’re capable of!”","Lin Yuan smiled and nodded.","He was always sincere in helping his friends. Thus, he did not like it when they stood on ceremony with him as it made them seem distant.","Gu Lang, An He, Xia Qing, and the rest were undeniably the cream of the crop. Once they received resources, their powers would definitely skyrocket.","It was not just the Radiance Federation that needed to be riled up and motivated. The same went for the other federations in the main world.","Lin Yuan intended to discuss with the Moon Empress about helping the other federations regain their hope after the Radiance Federation’s morale had been raised.","Otherwise, if a dimensional lifeform could not kill a dead spirit, the humans from the other federations would be so filled with fear and panic that they would have no idea how to take on the mantle and continue the battle.","Gao Feng had yet to visit the Dead Spirits Wells and see the dead spirits for himself. He was very curious about the dead spirits.","“Lin Yuan, can you share updates on the dead spirits? I am very curious to find out what types of dead spirits there are! I came here immediately after coming out of seclusion, so I haven’t had the chance to fight a dead spirit yet.”","Xia Qing looked at Gao Feng and began speaking before Lin Yuan could get a word out, “Every lifeform that has ever lived in this world can be turned into a dead spirit. They come in many forms, and it’s hard to measure them through statistical data because new types are popping out at every second.","“The best way to gain an understanding of the dead spirits is to head to a Dead Spirits Well and fight the dead spirits yourself. The environment around the Dead Spirits Wells is very dangerous and not for the weak-hearted.","“There could be death happening around you at any moment. Once the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection comes to an end, Radiance Sacred Hall will make the arrangements.","“The Radiance Envoys, Radiance Knights, and Radiance Hundred Sequence will be sent to the various cities and stationed around the Dead Spirits Wells to help with the fighting. I hope that all of you will be prepared. I fought by the Dead Spirits Wells for almost three days and only barely escaped death numerous times. If the other experts there didn’t save me, I would already be dead!”","Xia Qing spoke calmly, but her words allowed Gao Feng to get a clear picture of the dangers of the dead spirits.","Gu Lang nodded knowingly.","“I came out of seclusion early, so I trained by the Dead Spirits Wells for two days. The most dangerous part is that the dead spirits you kill will release death aura that can infect your body. Healing-type feys can’t treat these injuries. The death aura is also very concentrated in the air around the Dead Spirits Wells and will eat away at your vitality.","“Luckily, Lin Yuan has just provided a short-term solution to all these problems. With the Creation Masters’ continuing hard work, these issues will be solved very soon.”","Once Gu Lang was done speaking, Liu Jie and Zong Ze began serving the dishes.","The Mother of Bloodbath did not join the rest at the table. Instead, it stayed in the kitchen to work on the roast meat that Liu Jie and Zong Ze had specially made for it.","Given that the Mother of Bloodbath was Lin Yuan’s Path Protector, Lin Yuan’s friends were its seniors.","The rest of them would be unable to comfortably chat if it joined them at the table.","The Mother of Bloodbath did not have many friends. While it had been growing, its only real friend was Endless Summer.","The Mother of Bloodbath spent a long time being on its own.","Thus, it really hoped that Lin Yuan would be able to make as many friends as possible.","Lin Yuan did not remember the last time they had gathered together.","After this meal, everyone at this table would embark on a new journey.","During the beginning of the sixth epoch, Lin Yuan made a silent wish. He prayed that after the sixth epoch ended, the seventh epoch that followed would be filled with peace and joy so that none of the lifeforms in the main world would have to endure any more suffering.","Lin Yuan did not tell the others about his wish. This could be because of the belief in Lin Yuan’s previous life that saying a wish out loud would cause it to not come true or because this was not the right time to say it.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan would work hard to make his wish come true.","Once they defeated Tower Canon and stability returned to the main world, Lin Yuan would head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds under the name of being the main world’s protector and continue protecting the main world from there.","With this thought, Lin Yuan suddenly frowned.","There was another secret faction in the main world that was stronger than Tower Canon—Epoch God Palace.","The words ‘Epoch God Palace’ had already become a source of headaches for Lin Yuan.."]},{"number":2668,"title":"Chapter 2668: Nurturing Shiny!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2668: Nurturing Shiny!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan already had a certain level of understanding of Tower Canon. They were not completely foreign to him. Thus, he was not at a total loss about how to take them on.","On the other hand, he was utterly unfamiliar with Epoch God Palace.","If he had not heard about them from Eighth Page Apoptosis, he might not have known that such a secret organization existed in the world.","Any powerful organization needed to be guided by a goal in order to function.","Taking Sky City as an example, if they did not have any goals, Wen Yu and Liu Jie might not mind, but the white-clothed followers would not feel any sense of security.","An organization without a clear goal would lose all of its value. Hence, Epoch God Palace definitely had an objective.","Lin Yuan had also considered the possibility of Epoch God Palace being a foreign entity just like Tower Canon. What else could explain why Tower Canon had suffered such a humiliating loss to Epoch God Palace?","This thought made Lin Yuan lose his appetite.","However, he did not share his thoughts with anyone else for fear of affecting them.","Even if he did tell Xia Qing, Zong Ze, and the rest about his concerns, they","could not offer any solutions.","Lin Yuan would still end up having to handle everything on his own.","Therefore, where was the point in him sharing his worries?","Lin Yuan felt that if the opportunity arose, he needed to do a deep dive into Epoch God Palace.","Since Epoch God Palace was currently staying quiet, he would make the first move to reach out to them.","After coming to this decision, Lin Yuan added Epoch God Palace to his schedule.","Tower Canon had already pushed the main world into chaos. Lin Yuan prayed that Epoch God Palace was not planning something similar.","If Epoch God Palace had the same intentions as Tower Canon, the main world’s lifeforms would be sent into another disaster immediately after the dead spirits crisis.","During the meal, Wen Yu and Liu Jie noticed Lin Yuan’s demeanor change.","Lin Yuan was the type to look after others. After being the sole caretaker of Chu Ci in their younger days, Lin Yuan was very thoughtful in everything he did.","But he had only taken a few bites of the food on the table and was quiet most of the time. It was evident that he was ruminating over something.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie had been with Lin Yuan for a long time, so they knew him best.","Although Gu Lang, Zong Ze, Gao Feng, An He, Xia Qing, and the rest were his friends, they were not always by his side, so they could not pick up on when he was acting out of character.","After the meal, Lin Yuan broke his silence and returned to his usual manner.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu exchanged a look. It seemed that whatever issue was occupying Lin Yuan’s mind was a very difficult one to crack.","If it was an easy task, Lin Yuan would not be keeping it to himself.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie intended to ask Lin Yuan about this once Zong Ze and the rest left. Even if they could not provide actual help, they could help to take on some of the emotional burden.","Lin Yuan passed around a platter of fruit that could cut through the discomfort of unctuous flavor before turning to tell Zong Ze what he had just said to the rest.","Zong Ze’s gaze sparkled as he listened to Lin Yuan.","It was all because of the Heavenly Maiden Sleet elemental pearl given by Lin Yuan that the Fiery Sky Hou was able to evolve to its current state and transform its bloodline to one that allowed it to stand over Gu Lang’s fey with the barren bloodline.","Not even Chef Supreme was able to produce such a treasure.","Previously, Zong Ze assumed that the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls had come from the Moon Empress. But now, he knew that it came from","Lin Yuan himself.","Lin Yuan had already invested a large amount of Creation Master resources into the Radiance Federation, but none of it had been at the same level as the Heavenly Maiden Sleet elemental pearls. However, they were all Defined Life at least. Thus, the Radiance Federation’s experts’ feys still substantially evolved their bloodlines.","The rest of them also had the means to obtain such resources. It was clear that Lin Yuan intended to provide them with higher-level resources.","Zong Ze and the rest accepted Lin Yuan’s gesture and did not stand on ceremony with him.","They also possessed the Thoughts Letter Paper, albeit the access parameters for each one were different. They could only exchange messages with the people linked to the Radiance Federation but could not reach the experts who were part of the Astronomical Parliament or Sky City.","All of them wrote down what they needed on their Thoughts Letter Papers, and Lin Yuan received all their messages.","Wen Yu was the one who suggested using the Thoughts Letter Paper to collate the resource lists. She made this suggestion because she knew just how many resources each of them needed.","If one of them did not need many resources, those who needed more would be embarrassed to openly ask for what they needed.","This way, with everyone directly reporting their needs to Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper, there was no need to worry about such issues, and all of them could make their requests without holding back.","As Lin Yuan read through their lists, he got a sense of the levels that Zong Ze, Xia Qing, and the rest’s feys with the barren bloodlines had reached.","He quickly packed the resources in brocade boxes and distributed them.","After receiving the resources, Zong Ze, Xia Qing, and the rest would have to go into seclusion for a day or two to evolve their feys’ bloodlines. Once they were done, all of them would reach new heights of power.","Lin Yuan also intended to go into seclusion for a while.","Long Tao was also supposed to be present at this gathering, but he was currently in charge of overseeing Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s affairs.","Recently, he had slowly taken on more and more duties within Coiling Dragon’s Valley. He now handled many responsibilities that usually belonged to the head of the family.","At first, he felt very out of his element.","The head of a top faction had an endless list of tasks to attend to every day.","Although he did not have to handle everything personally, he still needed to supervise. It required some extra effort to ensure that the elders listened to his orders.","Luckily, Long Tao was given the title of Young Leader at a young age and was also part of the Radiance Federation’s most elite team, the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Thus, he captured the faith and loyalty of most people in the family, and it did not take long for him to weed out the minority who stood in his way.","When he had merely been the Young Leader, Long Tao had been extremely respectful to the elders in his family.","But now that he held the role of the head of the family, his duties had changed, and so had his perspective.","The head of a family needed to wield absolute authority!","His father had also faced obstacles when he was the head of the family. As a result, he had been unable to change the family in the direction that he wanted.","Because of Long Tao’s relationship with Lin Yuan, Coiling Dragon’s Valley was part of the Moon Empress’ camp and had replaced Whale Ocean Commerce to become one of the Radiance Federation’s three top factions.","Given his relationship with Lin Yuan, no one in the family dared to oppose Long Tao’s plans.","Hence, all Long Tao needed to do was adjust to the life of being the head of a family.","Long Tao never understood why his father’s powers had increased so slowly after he became the head of the family.","But now, he knew the reason.","If he occupied the position of the head of the family for too long, he would have to neglect increasing his power as well.","Two years ago, Long Tao would have been willing to make such a sacrifice for his family.","However, after his interactions with Lin Yuan, Long Tao came to realize that power was the center of everything. Without power, nothing else mattered.","Long Tao had been nurturing young aides in his family that he could trust to help him develop the family.","It went without saying that these aides would have to use their actions to prove their loyalty to him in order to win his trust.","Long Tao’s capabilities were unquestionable. His grandfather and father admired his ruthless actions.","However, the two of them were unaware that he cared more about increasing his own power than managing the family.","It was said that one should never forget those who had been kind to them.","Long Tao was still grateful towards Lin Yuan and continued to instruct the Coiling Dragon’s Valley members to nurture dragon-species feys and supply Lin Yuan with dragon livers.","He also used the relationship between Coiling Dragon’s Valley and Dark Clouds Bird Shrine to help Lin Yuan obtain large amounts of main phoenix-species feys’ blood and even some essence blood.","Long Tao had already delivered all of these resources to the Return from","Faraway Mansion some time ago and handed them to Master Hong Shen.","Master Hong Shen immediately gave Lin Yuan the dragon liver and phoenix blood when he returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion. He had even processed the dragon liver to remove the membrane covering them that was difficult to digest.","Lin Yuan had contracted Shiny long ago but had not had the chance to nurture it.","Now, he could finally nurture it!","The longer he waited, the more Shiny’s confidence fell!","Since he would be competing for a spot as one of the Radiance Envoys, there was no reason not for Lin Yuan to wield a fey with the barren bloodline. During the dead spirits crisis, feys with the barren bloodline were still the Radiance Federation’s secret weapon.","Lin Yuan looked at Zong Ze, Xia Qing, and the rest and invited them, “Why don’t you go into seclusion here? We can all head to Radiance Sacred Hall together when you’re done.","“Although you won’t be participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection will be immediately followed by the Radiance Envoy and Radiance Knight selections. As per Radiance Sacred Hall’s request, you will need to be present to watch.”","Xia Qing, Zong Ze, and the rest gratefully accepted Lin Yuan’s invitation. Wen Yu immediately waved over a few servants to set up training rooms for them to evolve their feys.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had built a sufficiently large building. Otherwise, they would not have been able to build so many training rooms.","At first, every training room’s walls were embedded with a layer of radium to prevent any battles or fey nurturing processes taking place in the training rooms from damaging them.","But as Lin Yuan grew increasingly stronger, and with the large amounts of high metal-type spiritual ingredients that he obtained from the subterranean world, Hu Quan instructed his disciples from Heavenly Craft Pavilion to work with the high-class Land Imps to renovate the training rooms’ wall.","Once the walls were embedded with the Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredient Strong Jade Soft Steel, it would be difficult for even Immortal experts to leave a mark on the walls.","The Strong Jade Soft Steel was stronger than most Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients.","When Lin Yuan was nurturing the Perfect Touch Wisteria six months ago, he did not have many Sovereign metal-type spiritual ingredients. But now, they were common goods to him. He could have as much of it as he wanted!","Once Zong Ze, Gao Feng, Xia Qing, and the rest entered the training rooms to nurture their feys and sacred source lifeforms, Lin Yuan picked another training room and prepared to enter.","At this moment, Lin Yuan heard Wen Yu call out to him, “Young Master, were you preoccupied with something during the meal? You can share it with Big Brother Liu and me if it’s convenient. Regardless of what it’s about, we will face it together with you!”","Wen Yu would never have dared to say something like this a year ago. Although she was his assistant, she was actually his servant.","However, Lin Yuan never saw her as a servant.","But as she spent more time with him, Lin Yuan became not just her Young Master but also her family.","Now, as a member of his family, Wen Yu wanted to share his burdens.","Liu Jie nodded earnesty. Wen Yu had said out loud exactly what he was thinking.","Lin Yuan did not try to hide the truth from Wen Yu and Liu Jie.","He was not trying to find someone to share his burdens. There was no one who could help him shoulder this burden. He only told Wen Yu and Liu Jie about this because he could sense their sincerity.","“Aside from Tower Canon, there is another secret and more powerful organization called Epoch God Palace. They have been hiding in the shadows all this time. I don’t know what their goal is. But from how things look, they have no intention of interfering with Tower Canon’s plan.”","Liu Jie and Wen Yu looked astonished.","This was the first time that they were hearing of Epoch God Palace.","Wen Yu pursed her lips. She knew that if such a powerful secret organization did not side with the humans, the humans and sea clans could be ruined!","It was no wonder that Lin Yuan’s expression was so grim.","Wen Yu could not come up with any way to address this matter. The only thing she could do was stick by Lin Yuan and face Epoch God Palace with him when they eventually made their move.","Liu Jie took a deep breath and said with a smile, “Young Master, regardless of what Epoch God Palace’s goal is, we must do whatever it takes to protect the Radiance Federation and all of the lifeforms in the main world! That was our goal from the very beginning. All we need to do is follow it to the end!”","Lin Yuan reached out and patted Liu Jie and Wen Yu’s shoulders before he smiled and nodded.","What a coincidence. This was exactly how he felt, too!","Since he did not know what lay on the road ahead, all he could do was keep up the passion and weather all storms that came his way.","He had grown enough to stand up on behalf of the Radiance Federation and humans to shield all the lifeforms in the main world from the imminent storms.","Lin Yuan never wanted to be a savior. He never had any ambitions of saving the main world.. He had only made it to this point in his life because he felt a sense of belonging to this world and saw it as his home!"]},{"number":2669,"title":"Chapter 2669: Shiny’s Comprehensive Evolution!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2669: Shiny’s Comprehensive Evolution!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Once he was done speaking with Liu Tie and Wen Yu, Lin Yuan entered his own training room. Just like the two of them, he had his own personal training room.","Each of their training rooms was tailored to their individual needs. Wen Yu primarily used her training room to organize information. As a result, it was no different from an office.","Liu Jie used his to train Elegance’s insect armies. Thus, his was the largest training room, and the ground had various geographical terrains built into it. The walls and ground were also fortified with thick layers of metal-type spiritual ingredients.","Lin Yuan had yet to use his training room for fighting. He usually used it to nurture feys or to read in. He still kept up the positive habit of reading.","This time, just like many other times in the past, Lin Yuan was going to use his training room to nurture a fey.","Frankly, Lin Yuan had been looking forward for a long time to nurture Shiny.","But before now, he had lacked dragon liver. Lin Yuan preferred to evolve it at once rather than strengthening it incrementally!","Lin Yuan summoned Shiny, and the large, majestic golden bird appeared. He raised his hand, which grabbed his arm like a landing pad.","Shiny turned its sharp beak to the side and used the soft feathers on its neck to brush against Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","In the past, it would nuzzle up against his neck. But in one instance, its feathers had cut the skin on his neck.","This was not because Lin Yuan’s skin was too soft and not tough enough. Lin Yuan’s genes had been refined, and he was an A-rank spirit qi professional. Hence, his skin was much tougher than that of most humans.","But the fact was that Shiny was a bird that used its body for combat. Although it was only Bronze grade, the feathers on its neck, which were the softest ones on its entire body, were also very lethal.","Shiny was very mischievous and liked to play all over the marsh world.","If Shiny was a human, it would definitely be an adventurer who loved traveling!","Lin Yuan rarely saw Shiny when he went to the Spirit Lock spatial zone. But whenever he did, it would cling to him. It was just as attached to Lin Yuan as Genius and Chimey were!","With its Barren bloodline, Shiny was very intelligent.","It flapped its wings a few times and lifted its claws off of Lin Yuan’s arm before flying in circles around him.","Shiny had also been waiting for this day for a long time.","During the entire time that it had been stuck at Bronze grade, Shiny had yearned to grow its power.","It knew that Lin Yuan was finally going to nurture it.","Lin Yuan looked at Shiny and could not help but smile.","Regardless of how bad things got in the outside world, being here with his feys always healed and relaxed him.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Shiny.","[Fey Name]: Golden Wings [Fey Species]: Barren-species/feather-winged-species","[Fey Grade]: Bronze (9/10) [Fey Type]: Wind [Fey Quality]: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Snapped Neck Falling Death]: When its sharp claws make contact with a target, the target’s neck will be snapped. Simultaneously, the Golden Wings will extract the target’s soul and absorb it into its feathers. The soul will imbue the storm patterns on the feathers with intelligence.","[Flowing Wind Claws]: When the wind elements in the Golden Wings’ feathers are released into the environment, it will be able to control the surrounding winds and manipulate it to attack its opponent. The attacked target will feel like claws are slashing it. After attacking a target, the Golden Wings will also be able to inject wind elements into its target through explosions and cause double the amount of damage.","Exclusive Skill:","[Unset State]: When interacting with another fey, the Golden Wings can copy the fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities. Unset State will then turn into the copied exclusive skill and triggered ability. The abilities can only be switched out once every lunar cycle.","[Wind’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all wind elements, it will become the eye of a hurricane and control all of the surrounding wind elements. It will become the master, while all other winds will become its disciple.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was looking at Shiny’s data. But every time he did, he could not help but marvel at the might of a fey with the Barren bloodline! It was possible that not even Platinum avian-type feys would be able to defeat Shiny!","Shiny’s exclusive skill, Wind’s Descendant, gave it absolute control over wind elements. It was a controlling type of exclusive skill.","Snapped Neck Falling Death and Flowing Wind Claws would allow it to cause significant damage to its enemies.","Snapped Neck Falling Death had an instant death effect and could take control of souls. Lin Yuan had never seen such an ability in other feys.","Clearly, the Moon Empress had chosen carefully before giving him Shiny’s egg. It was impossible that every fey with the Barren bloodline had equally fearsome abilities as Shiny!","Lin Yuan waved to Shiny.","“Shiny, stop flying. Go and stand on the table.”","Lin Yuan placed a large block of red sandalwood on the table in the breeding room.","It was very easy for Shiny to grab hold of the block of red sandalwood. It would be difficult for Shiny to eat if it had to stand on the table.","Shiny folded its wings in midair before landing on the block of red sandalwood.","Its sharp claws pierced through the jade-textured red sandalwood, leaving slashes in the wood.","If anyone else in the main world saw this, they would gasp and think that this was such a pity!","However, this did not mean anything to Lin Yuan because this piece of red sandalwood was completely ordinary two days ago. After spending two days in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it only became jade-textured.","Shiny perched on the block of red sandalwood and bobbed its head excitedly.","Lin Yuan took out the fresh dragon liver that Long Tao had given him before slathering it in phoenix blood.","In Shiny, a more delectable meal could not exist.","All Lin Yuan needed to do was provide Shiny with pure spirit qi and wind-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls while it ate, and its power would spring upwards!","With the temptation of such a meal and the prospect of increasing its power right in front of it, Shiny did not lose sight of everything else and begin obsessing over the food like feys with low intelligence would do.","Instead, it let out two sharp cries that sounded like a mix of metal scraping against each other and a bird screech before it waved its wings at Lin Yuan and began elegantly eating the food in a gentlemanly manner.","Lin Yuan took out a box of spirit qi crystals and a box of wind-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls and placed it next to Shiny’s meal. This way, Shiny could eat them whenever it wanted!","Lin Yuan backed into a corner. All he needed to do was wait until Shiny was done eating the various spiritual ingredients so he could help it with the next steps!","Shiny ate happily. There was no need for it to stomp and crush the dragon liver before eating it like the other wild beasts had to do.","Shiny pecked at the dragon liver, and it broke apart as easily as tofu.","Shiny’s power rose rapidly since the dragon liver came from main-dragon-species feys and the phoenix blood came from main-phoenix-species feys.","As its power rose, Shiny became increasingly majestic. The color of its feathers intensified.","Its feathers were individually exquisite, and each looked like a piece of art.","Lin Yuan could not help but shiver at the ferocious aura emanating from it.","When he looked at Shiny, he felt as though he had returned to a primeval world and was looking at a peak hunter feasting on its haul.","Shiny ate one elemental pearl or spirit qi crystal with every beakful of the dragon liver.","Lin Yuan stood quietly to the side as he watched Shiny’s power grow.","Shiny did not grow larger each time it evolved its grade. When it evolved to Platinum grade, it had even shrunk to the point that its wingspan was only around three meters.","However, the decrease in its size did not hamper Shiny’s forcefulness. Rather, it became even more ferocious!","At this moment, Shiny let out a cry before manipulating the wind-elemental energy to form a voice. “Yuan, I have reached Diamond/Fantasy Ill! I will need some time to digest my power. Once I consume the remainder of the dragon liver and phoenix blood, I will reach Diamond X/Fantasy V.","“I would like to stay at this level for a while before I move on to evolve to Suzerain/Myth. If I evolve my power to too great of an extent, my combat abilities might not catch up to my body’s strength. I won’t be able to cope with my physical changes!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","With Shiny’s intelligence, it could determine the most beneficial route of evolution for itself.","Since Shiny had chosen the most beneficial path for itself, there was no way that its contractor would object.","Spirit qi professionals all preferred intelligent feys. This was because intelligent feys were able to communicate effectively with their spirit qi professionals and tell them about their needs. If spirit qi professionals evolved feys based on their own judgment, they could sometimes accidentally negatively impact the feys’ potential.","Lin Yuan told Shiny seriously, “Shiny, you can remain at Diamond X/Fantasy V then! Two days later, I will take you to participate in a few fights so you can get used to your own power. We’ll evolve you to Suzerain/Myth once you’re ready!” Shiny paused for a while before it sincerely thanked Lin Yuan.","Shiny’s contract with Lin Yuan was formed through spiritual energy, soul, and bloodline. It was linked to his mind and could clearly sense what he was thinking.","Lin Yuan wanted to take it to participate in the Radiance Envoy selection.","If Shiny wanted to compete with other feys with the Barren bloodline, it would have to be evolved to Suzerain/Myth.","But if something went wrong during its evolution, Shiny would have to take responsibility for itself.","As Lin Yuan’s fey, it would also have to be responsible for answering to him. If it was the only one involved, it would be more than willing to immediately evolve to Suzerain/Myth so it could do battle for Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan heard this, he ignored the fact that Shiny’s feathers had become even sharper after evolving to Diamond grade and patted its abdomen. He immediately felt a pang of pain in his palm.","“Shiny, with our relationship, there’s no need to thank me! I used my best resources to nurture you. You should trust in your own power! Moreover, we are not just acting for the short-term. We need to look further into the future!”","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Shiny.","[Fey Name]: Golden Wings","[Fey Species]: Barren-species/feather-winged-species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (1/10) [Fey Type]: Wind [Fey Quality]: Fantasy Ill","Abilities:","[Snapped Neck Falling Death]: When its sharp claws make contact with a target, the target’s neck will be snapped. At the same moment, the Golden Wings will extract the target’s soul and absorb the soul into its feathers. The soul will imbue the storm patterns on the feathers with intelligence.","[Flowing Wind Claws]: When the wind elements in the Golden Wings’ feathers are released into the environment, it will be able to control the surrounding winds and manipulate them to attack its opponent. The attacked target will feel like claws are slashing it. After attacking a target, the Golden Wings will also be able to inject wind elements into its target through explosions and cause double the amount of damage.","[Rapid Wind Whistle]: By flapping its wings to activate wind-elemental energy, the Golden Wings will simultaneously let out a roar that causes physical and elemental damage to a designated target. A headwind will also lower the target’s speed. Each time a headwind is released, its own speed will be increased.","[Hurricane Added Protection]: A vicious hurricane shield will be added to one’s own body. Every time elemental damage is inflicted on it, the hurricane shield will absorb the damage before reflecting it. The hurricane shield can also absorb wind-elemental energy from the surroundings to replenish the wind-elemental energy in its body.","[Folded Wings Wind Valley]: With the Golden Wings at the center, an environment charged with wind-elemental energy will be formed.","Wind-elemental energy will be continuously produced in this environment. When it makes a sacrifice to this territory, the wind-elemental energy will be absorbed into its bloodline and trigger a one-time explosion.","[Disappearing Wind Attack] :","Exclusive Skill:","[Unset State]: When interacting with another fey, the Golden Wings can copy the fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities. Unset State will then turn into the copied exclusive skill and triggered ability. The abilities can only be switched out once every lunar cycle.","[Wind’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all wind elements, it will become the eye of a hurricane and control all surrounding wind elements. It will become the master, while all other winds will become its disciple.","Lin Yuan was stunned by what he saw. He was momentarily at a loss about how to appraise Shiny.","The four new abilities it had gained were almost too comprehensive!"]},{"number":2670,"title":"Chapter 2670 Descent of the Dead Dimensional Lifeforms!","paragraphs":["2670 Descent of the Dead Dimensional Lifeforms!","Every fey had clear aptitudes. This was common knowledge in the fey world.","This was especially evident when the feys reached Fantasy Breed. Because they only had a few abilities and exclusive skills, their aptitudes could be clearly discerned.","Once the fey reached Immortal Breed and gained more abilities and exclusive skills, their aptitudes could become buried by the slew of other abilities.","Taking Chimey as an example, its abilities looked perfect, but it was actually inept at defense. It was also lacking controlling abilities!","However, because Lin Yuan had contracted many feys, their abilities could complement each other’s aptitudes and make up for their flaws.","Shiny’s abilities could be considered fully comprehensive.","The ability Snapped Neck Falling Death was an extremely strong deadly ability that could extract souls.","Flowing Wind Claws allowed it to manipulate wind-elemental energy from all directions. If Shiny released its wind-elemental energy into the environment, it could both restrain and cause damage to targets.","The Silver ability Rapid Wind Whistle would allow Shiny to channel all the wind-elemental energy in its surroundings to produce a roar. The wind-elemental energy would produce overclocked reverberations that could cause physical and elemental damage to a designated target.","When headwinds were added as well, the target’s speed would be lowered while its own speed would be raised. This was also considered a form of control.","Snapped Neck Falling Death, Flowing Wind Claws, and Rapid Wind Whistle were all mainly deadly and controlling abilities. Although they were powerful, they could not be described as comprehensive.","The Gold ability Hurricane Added Protection gave Shiny an additional shield in the form of a hurricane. The hurricane shield would be able to absorb energy from elemental attacks aimed at Shiny before reflecting it.","This meant that it would be able to send an enemy’s attack back at it and was considered a defensive ability.","Furthermore, the hurricane shields could absorb the wind-elemental energy from the surroundings to rejuvenate themselves and increase their endurance.","With just these four abilities, Shiny’s abilities could now be described as comprehensive.","The Platinum ability Folded Wings Wind Valley would create an environment around Shiny that was charged with wind-elemental energy. This environment would become an endless source of wind-elemental energy that Shiny could tap into.","This was the strongest replenishing ability that Lin Yuan had come across.","There were very few feys that had abilities that could create elements.","If the concentration of elements in an environment fell too low, it would affect a fey’s ability to use element-type abilities.","But with the ability Folded Wings Wind Valley, Shiny would not have to worry about being held back by its environment as it would be able to create its own source of wind-elemental energy wherever it went.","Folded Wings Wind Valley was not just a powerful endurance ability. If Shiny offered up a sacrifice and created a territory, the wind-elemental energy in Folded Wings Wind Valley would trigger Shiny’s bloodline and enable it to set off even stronger power.","This ability boosted Shiny’s comprehensive abilities even further and added an explosive aspect.","Disappearing Wind Attack allowed Shiny to enter the wind and use the wind to protect itself. As long as the wind was not fully dissipated, Shiny would be able to hide within it.","Wind was fluid. When Shiny turned into wind, it could appear at any corner of an ongoing battle to attack the target.","This might come across as a defense ability, but was also a powerful assassination ability.","The exclusive skill Unset State allowed Shiny to copy another fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities.","Given that the abilities could be swapped out every lunar cycle, Unset State made Shiny’s set of abilities even more well-rounded.","This also allowed Shiny to be linked with other feys as well as Lin Yuan.","The other exclusive skill Wind’s Descendant was the main enabler for Shiny being able to control wind elements. It assured its status relative to the wind elements.","Lin Yuan looked at Shiny that had its head lowered as it mulled how it should begin consuming the dragon liver, phoenix blood, and wind-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls. A thoughtful expression spread across his face.","Lin Yuan did not know what level Gu Lang, Zong Ze, and the others’ feys with the barren bloodline had reached. Nonetheless, he felt that Shiny stood a good chance of taking the Myth Breed feys with the barren bloodline on!","At this moment, Lin Yuan heard Wen Yu’s voice in his head.","Wen Yu was currently calling Lin Yuan in her capacity as the mistress of the Astronomical Parliament.","This was so that he would be able to receive the message instantly regardless of where he was and what he was doing.","Wen Yu knew that he had entered his training room to nurture his feys.","Given that she was willing to disturb him to send him a message, it had to be of the utmost importance! This was because using the Astronomical Parliament to send a message would come at the cost of willpowers.","During an Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting, one of the members could sacrifice willpower.","Up until now, Lin Yuan was the only one who had supplied the willpowers and laws.","If the Astronomical Parliament was a luxury boat, Lin Yuan was the engine.","Without Lin Yuan, the Astronomical Parliament would not be able to properly utilize its power!","Now, Wen Yu no longer had any more willpowers to sacrifice.","As such, she immediately sent a message to him through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, the dimensional lifeforms have sent news. Over the last two hours, many Samsara Realm Dictators have reported the appearance of many special dead spirits. These special dead spirits are spreading a plague-like death aura that is different from that of the others. The dead aura isn’t released from their body after they are killed.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, I have spent the last few days conducting research into the types of dead spirits and recorded all the information using the Elemental Paper’s ability Hear Heaven’s Secret. I don’t think they used to be a lifeform from one of the main world’s past five epochs. Rather, they are purely dead lifeforms like the Pilgrimage Corpse Bird and come from the dead dimensional rift!","[Wen Yu]: The death aura within the Pilgrimage Corpse Bird had also been very concentrated. It could also use death aura to contaminate other targets and the environment. The regular dead spirits did not have such abilities!","The information that Wen Yu used Hear Heaven’s Secret to record was always accurate.","When Wen Yu wanted to utilize the information, she could easily make detailed comparisons and amendments.","When Lin Yuan saw Wen Yu’s message, he placed the Thoughts Letter Paper on the table.","He pondered for a moment before he called the Moon Empress and told her everything that he had just heard from Wen Yu. He also asked the Moon Empress if such lifeforms had appeared near the Dead Spirits Wells.","Those lifeforms had already invaded the dimensional worlds. There was a high chance that they would eventually make it into the Radiance Federation and cause damage there.","They were only just beginning to nurture the Dead Decay Earthworms. Although they were very easy to nurture, it was difficult to produce enough of them within such a short span of time to meet the Radiance Federation’s needs.","If many of such dead spirits exploded onto the scene in the Radiance Federation and began spreading death aura, it would be disastrous for the Radiance Federation!","Although Lin Yuan was not certain if something like this would definitely happen, prevention was better than cure. Nothing bad could come out of being prepared and having added precautions!","When the Moon Empress heard what Lin Yuan said, a similar expression to what had appeared on Lin Yuan’s face appeared on hers as well.","She now looked extremely stern. She knew the exact implications of what Lin Yuan were saying.","“Little Yuan, I will immediately hold an imperial meeting to declare the news. Then, we will direct all of our forces towards nurturing the remaining Dead Decay Earthworms to prepare ourselves for the worst!”","Lin Yuan responded solemnly. “Master, I will be able to produce ten million Dead Decay Earthworms soon. The other Creation Masters in the federation can do their best to nurture these Dead Decay Earthworms.","“In order to prevent any anomalies from happening, the Radiance Federation’s Dead Decay Earthworms should be prevented from reaching outsiders. We need to make sure to meet the Radiance Federation’s needs first before we help the others. This will ensure that there will definitely be at least one safe haven in the main world!”","The Moon Empress nodded with relief and gratefulness.","She had echoed his thoughts.","The Moon Empress felt that they needed to help their own before they helped others!","“Little Yuan, I understand what you mean.”","The Moon Empress hung up the call.","Lin Yuan let out a long sigh of relief.","Wen Yu had definitely done a detailed analysis. Otherwise, she would never have made such a conclusion. The Wen Yu that Lin Yuan knew was not the kind of person who made baseless conclusions.","If she was such a person, he would never rely on her as much as he did!","Everything was quiet on Tower Canon’s side. Lin Yuan was already certain that the lifeforms from the dead world were part of Tower Canon’s counterattack.","Lin Yuan had seen the dead lifeforms for himself. The death aura they released was more than a hundred times more potent than that of dead spirits.","Luckily, Weng Queji’s research had produced a fey like the Dead Decay Earthworm that could absorb death aura, and the Hundred Questions Beasts had produced the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake.","Otherwise, regardless of how capable Lin Yuan was, it would be difficult for him to save the Radiance Federation from these dead spirits.","Shiny was currently eating spiritual ingredients in Lin Yuan’s training room. If Shiny needed him for anything, it could contact Lin Yuan through their contract.","Lin Yuan pushed open the training room’s door and saw Wen Yu and Liu Jie standing by the entrance with stern expressions.","Lin Yuan told them seriously, “I have already informed Master. She will hold an imperial meeting soon to look into this matter and try to come up with a solution. On our end, we will get in contact with the Samsara Realm Dictators and tell them about the situation.","“Let’s observe the impact that the contamination from the dead dimensional lifeforms has on the five dimensional worlds!”","Wen Yu had panicked when she received the reports from the Samsara Realm Dictators. She had no way of tackling this issue.","Wen Yu had used the Elemental Paper to transport the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes and Dead Decay Earthworms. As such, she was well aware of how much the Radiance Federation lacked these two feys. Each time she delivered them, it was like trying to put out a fire with a drop of water.","It would be very difficult for the Radiance Federation to handle the dead dimensional lifeforms’ invasion now.","Amidst her panic, she had no choice but to send a message to Lin Yuan. Otherwise, if she could handle it on her own, she would never choose to disturb him while he was nurturing feys.","In the end, immediately after receiving her message, Lin Yuan came up with the best plan of action.","Lin Yuan was her main source of support at any and all times.","“Young Master, after receiving the reports from the Samsara Realm Dictators, I told them to wait for the Thoughts Letter Papers. I will contact them now and organize information based on their reports. Then, we can analyze the information and get a better understanding of what’s happening on the ground.”","Liu Jie nodded silently by the side.","Wen Yu’s Elemental Paper might not be capable of combat, but it was very skilled at combat.","If Lin Yuan had to listen to every single Samsara Realm Dictator’s report to understand what was happening in the five dimensional worlds, it would take at least a day.","But if Wen Yu used Hear Heaven’s Secret, she would be akin to an organizing machine. She could effectively and efficiently organize all the information and transcribe them with ease!","When Lin Yuan was done speaking to Wen Yu, he turned to tell Liu Jie, “Big Brother Liu, send a copy of Wen Yu’s information to the Radiant Moon Palace and another set to the Midnight Palace.","“We need to learn all that we can to boost our chances of victory. The Radiance Federation needs to understand what’s happening in the dimensional worlds in order to come up with the best defenses!”","Liu Jie nodded seriously. “Lin Yuan, I will deliver the information once Wen Yu is done organizing it. We might need to delay the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection!”","Lin Yuan shook his head.","Lin Yuan did not agree with this. He felt that it was all the more important that they boosted the Radiance Federation’s citizen’s fighting spirits now so all of them could band together to protect their homeland!","Hence, it was imperative that they went through with the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection!","The fact that Liu Jie did not notice this meant that he still needed to hone his outlook even further.","This dead spirits crisis was indeed a calamity, but it was also a whetstone that would accelerate the increase of the main world’s power!","Wen Yu knew that they were very pressed for time, so she had already entered the Hear Heaven’s Secrets’ state.","There were light yellow papers flying all over the room, each of them printed with neat lines of words.","Wen Yu had already started collecting the information from the Samsara Realm Dictators!","Lin Yuan watched her quietly and prayed that the dimensional worlds were able to put up a good fight against the death aura!"]},{"number":2671,"title":"Chapter 2671 Hope Amidst Despair!","paragraphs":["2671 Hope Amidst Despair!","The rustling of the paper reverberated throughout the two floors of the mansion. The sound would not affect Gu Lang, An He, Xia Qing, Gao Feng, and the rest, who were in the midst of increasing their power.","Lin Yuan prepared himself mentally as he listened to the sound of the paper flying around him. Regardless of what conclusion the information pointed to, he would have to face it.","Rather than going to every single dimensional lifeform Dictator to ask them for updates, reading Wen Yu’s information would not only allow him to understand the situation immediately, but he would also be able to make the best judgment about the biggest issue caused by the dead dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan did not have to wait for long. Wen Yu soon returned to human form.","She placed her hand in front of the stacks of word-filled paper, and they immediately flew into the air.","Eventually, three sheets of paper formed in her hand, and she handed it to Lin Yuan while saying dryly, “Young Master, this is the result of my consolidated and organized information. Things aren’t looking good in the dimensional worlds!”","Lin Yuan did not reach out to receive the three sheets of paper. Instead, he sat down and said, “Wen Yu, summarize it and tell me that version!”","Wen Yu poured out a cup of soothing Three Treasures Tea for Lin Yuan before she said, “The only dimensional world that hasn’t been too seriously affected is the alien insect world. The alien insects are still able to absorb the death aura from the dead dimensional lifeforms.","“The insect empresses are very interested in the dead dimensional lifeforms and have begun experimenting with procreation with them. Some of the insect queens and insect empresses are even fighting with each other for the chance to reproduce with the dead dimensional lifeforms!”","Lin Yuan thought, The alien insects are actually fighting over the dead dimensional lifeforms as though they’re resources!","The demon insects indeed had very strong bloodlines. Just a hint of their bloodline managed to enable the alien insects to hold their own against the dead dimensional lifeforms.","But based on what Wen Yu said, this might be the only piece of good news.","While Lin Yuan was thinking, Wen Yu continued giving him the report.","“Based on Carlos and Caroline’s reports, many Cowardly, Horn, and Bone Demons began decaying after being infected by concentrated death aura. Some of them are even showing signs of transforming into dead lifeforms.","“The Burning Flame Demons and Succubi are unaffected by the death aura. The Burning Flame Demons can burn up the death aura, while the Succubi can wield the death aura in combat after absorbing it!","“Some Succubi are even displaying abilities related to death aura. However, the Burning Flame Demon and Succubi are very rare species, while the Horn, Cowardly, and Bone Demons are the majority!”","When Lin Yuan heard that the Succubi could wield the death aura and use it as part of their mutated abilities, an idea appeared in his head.","Could it be that the death aura had stronger effects on dimensional lifeforms that were physically stronger? Meanwhile, dimensional lifeforms that had strong soul energy could withstand and adapt to the death aura.","The Succubi and Burning Flame Demons were known for their high intelligence. On the other hand, the Cowardly, Horn, and Bone Demons were fools that were only able to fight by instinct until they reached Class 10 or became Apostles.","Lin Yuan did not immediately bring up his idea. Instead, he continued listening to Wen Yu.","“The abyss demons had to do an internal cleanup. Carlos and Caroline are afraid that the Cowardly, Horn, and Bone Demons who were infected by death aura would turn into dead spirits and attack the other abyss demons.","“The Abyss Wombs produce Abyss Worms at a set rate. After the abyssal world was fused with the main world, the 18 levels combined into one. Carlos and Caroline gathered up the ten Abyss Wombs and began protecting them.","“According to the rate at which the Abyss Wombs produce the Abyss Worms, the abyssal world won’t be able to hold on for long. Rather than saying that they are reporting to me, it would be more accurate to say that they were pleading with me for help!”","At this point, Wen Yu paused before she continued. “The marsh world is in a similar situation to the abyssal world. It is also experiencing serious negative impacts. There are many species in the marsh world, like the Drugged Snake Eagle and Medusa Snake Demon that possess strong venom. They have all been strengthened by the death aura.","“The Medusa Snake Demon’s natural skill is petrification. But after absorbing the death aura, its petrifying gaze has changed to a deadly gaze. Not only will the target be petrified but their souls will be damaged as well. Unlike in the abyssal world, many of the intelligent species in the marsh world have increased in power.","“However, the Marsh Crocodiles are only able to withstand low concentrations of death aura. Once the concentration increases, they will immediately begin transforming into dead spirits and fall under the control of the dead dimensional lifeforms. The Marsh Crocodiles that used to be the marsh world’s soldiers are now the most uncertain variable.”","Lin Yuan’s expression could not help but change when he heard this.","This was because the marsh world was the first dimensional world that he had taken control of.","Lin Yuan spent the longest time in the marsh world and understood the Marsh Crocodiles’ significance to the marsh world.","The Marsh Crocodile’s position in the marsh world’s ecosystem was irreplaceable. It was a source of food for countless lifeforms in the marsh world.","Many of the weak lifeforms that made up the Marsh Crocodiles’ diet also used the Marsh Crocodiles’ undecayed corpses as a food source.","The Marsh Crocodile was a hunter and a producer of food. They made up more than half of the total number of lifeforms in the marsh world.","The transformation of the Marsh Crocodiles into dead spirits might not mean much to the powerful dimensional lifeforms, but it would lead to starvation in the marsh world. The powerful lifeforms would be able to last for a long time, but the low-level dimensional lifeforms would not make it past five days.","With this thought, Lin Yuan interrupted Wen Yu’s report, “Wen Yu, use the Elemental Paper’s ability to fill 100 Diamond fey storage boxes with the Soldier Ration Radishes and deliver them to Hornless Dragon Source. Instruct him to distribute the Soldier Ration Radishes accordingly. For now, ensure that the weak marsh dimensional lifeforms will be able to survive.","“We can find other solutions later. After delivering the Soldier Ration Radishes, instruct East Glow to lead a team of around 50 Dictators to evacuate the Marsh Crocodiles that had yet to be infected by the death aura. This will ensure that the marsh world’s life cycle isn’t halted.”","Wen Yu seriously noted down everything that Lin Yuan said.","She was silent for a moment before she continued telling Lin Yuan about the situations in the water world and subterranean world.","Compared to the situations in the water world and subterranean world, the marsh world and abyssal world were having very easy times!","The sea beasts in the water world could not adapt to consuming dead spirits and digesting death aura.","They had been able to hold on when the death aura was not so concentrated.","But now, they were incapable of taking in and digesting the death aura from the large amounts of dead dimensional lifeforms.","Although some of the Dead Decay Earthworms were given to the sea clans, they were far from enough to help the sea clans and water world dimensional lifeforms withstand the death aura.","A large proportion of the water world had already been contaminated, and countless members of sea clans and water world dimensional lifeforms had died in the death aura.","There were only a few species of water world dimensional lifeforms that were unaffected by the death aura. However, none of them mutated.","The mermaids were even more susceptible to the death aura than regular sea beasts. There were many mermaids who had lost their lives while being submerged in the death aura.","Rather than saying that the mermaids were giving a report, they were asking Lin Yuan for help.","The only thing that the mermaids could rely on was Lin Yuan, who was a thearch.","Lin Yuan could not help but purse his lips as he listened to Wen Yu’s report on the water world. He was pained by the injuries suffered by the mermaid species.","Alas, he did not know what to do. If he had a solution, he would not hold back from using it.","Lin Yuan always preferred prevention over cure. The sea clans were fending off the dead spirits together with the water world dimensional lifeforms.","The sea clans that were controlled by Vast Sea Labyrinth were helpless against the dead dimensional lifeforms. The sea aura was much more potent against the sea clans from the main world than the dimensional lifeforms.","Given that Wen Yu chose to bring up the water world first, it meant that the situation in the subterranean world was even more serious!","According to the previous tests, the subterranean dimensional lifeforms had the weakest resistance against death aura.","“Young Master, many of the dimensional lifeforms from the subterranean world that encountered the dead dimensional lifeforms have been afflicted by the death aura. Some of the Apostles who were infected by the death aura have begun to decay.","“Luckily, you relocated some of the Lan Imps. Otherwise, with the invasion of the dead dimensional lifeforms and dead spirits, most of the Land Imps would end up dead. Many of the younger Land Imps who were left behind have died after their bodies were infected by the death aura.”","Lin Yuan’s spirits fell when he heard what Wen Yu said. But he was not surprised.","He had already expected such a result for the subterranean world and had instructed the Dictators from the other dimensional worlds to lead teams to provide aid to the subterranean world. The aid teams would be arriving around a day later, and the subterranean world’s circumstances would take a turn for the better then.","The challenge would be helping the seas!","The subterranean world had powerful dimensional lifeforms going to help them, but Lin Yuan had no way of helping the lifeforms in the sea. After all, dimensional lifeforms that were more adept at terrestrial combat would only be headed toward their deaths if they were sent to the sea.","While he was being updated on the dimensional worlds, Lin Yuan could also ascertain if his guesses were right or wrong.","If it was true that a dimensional lifeform that had a soul that was a sufficiently high level would stand a chance of mutating in an environment filled with death aura, the Land Imp should have also mutated as it was an intelligent dimensional lifeform that had a soul level that was the equivalent of that of the Medusa Snake Demon.","Yet, the Land Imps had not mutated at all.","This situation refuted Lin Yuan’s hypothesis.","Just as Lin Yuan was racking his brain to try and come up with a solution, he received a message from Keira through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","After laying the demon insect eggs, Keira had been recuperating and rarely contacted Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan read the contents of Keira’s message, he could not stop the delight from spreading across his face.","[Keira]: Master, I have only just woken up and learned of the issues that this world is currently facing. Can you provide me with some special dead lifeforms? The death aura is a special energy, so it can be consumed and absorbed by the demon insects. If I am supplied with such special energy, I can use it to nurture the demon insects. This might not only solve the dead spirits crisis but would also be an opportunity for the alien insects to prosper!","Lin Yuan was so ecstatic he almost started trembling.","He almost forgot! The alien insects were just appendages borne from the demon insect bloodline.","The alien insects already had a naturally high resistance to the death aura. They were even able to use the death aura to improve themselves.","The demon insects had to be even stronger than the alien insects!","At first, Lin Yuan had been so panicked that his head started to spin when he heard of the hell that had broken loose in the dimensional worlds. He had not been able to think of Keira at all.","If what Keira said was true, the demon insect species would definitely become a killing machine during the dead spirits crisis!","Since Tower Canon had already made their move, it would not be difficult to find the dead dimensional lifeforms.","Hence, Lin Yuan decided to send Dictators to capture a large number of the dead dimensional lifeforms and deliver them to Keira’s nest.","He hoped that the demon insects would be able to procreate quickly enough to bring him a big surprise!","Lin Yuan had no idea just how excited and happy Keira was after she woke up and learned what was happening.","As a demon insect, Keira could not care less about whether the humans lived or died.","The humans’ existence and survival meant nothing to Keira. Keira only cared about the demon insect species’ development and how Lin Yuan felt about her.","Lin Yuan had provided her with a large amount of resources. It was possible that not even the Sky Beyond the Clouds would be able to supply such resources.","If Keira wanted to reinvigorate the demon insect species, she needed to secure even more resources. The best way to do this was to gain Lin Yuan’s favor so he would willingly hand over the resources. Otherwise, she had no other way of obtaining such resources.","Moreover, allowing the demon insects to consume the dead dimensional lifeforms’ bloodlines and producing alien insects that could use death aura would also be a means of padding the demon insect species’ storage of genes.","She had just woken up and needed to start everything over from the beginning.","One of her main priorities now was to pad the demon insect species’ storage of genes.","Keira did not know if her suggestion would be agreeable with Lin Yuan.","After sending the message, Keira nervously waited for Lin Yuan’s response.","At that moment, she received Lin Yuan’s reply.","[Lin Yuan]: You can let me know of any resources required by the demon insect species. Do everything you can to develop the demon insect species and fend off the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms that are releasing death aura!"]},{"number":2672,"title":"Chapter 2672 Demon Insects and Dead Spirits!","paragraphs":["2672 Demon Insects and Dead Spirits!","Keira read the message from Lin Yuan, and elation immediately spread across her face. This was exactly the response that she had been hoping for!","Lin Yuan was giving her an open path to resources. She could ask him for resources whenever she needed them.","With Lin Yuan providing her with pure spirit qi and pure vitality, there was no limit to the demon insects’ development.","It was possible that this branch of demon insects would be the last breakthrough for the foreseeable future. She would be the one to rewrite the history of the demon insects!","There were many demon insect tribes in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and every demon insect queen ruled over her own demon insect tribe.","The four demon insect empresses occupied the West Universe and made up one of the six major factions there.","Although the demon insects were linked by the same foundational genes, they subsequently absorbed very different genes, causing their abilities to differ greatly.","Before her incident, Keira was a normal demon insect queen. Unfortunately, she fell into a scheme.","The reincarnated Keira had no plans to seek revenge because she knew what her priorities should be.","But as her faction of demon insects developed and grew under her, when she went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and fought for a position as a demon insect empress, she would also have the opportunity to take her revenge.","[Keira]: Master, I still need more spirit qi to develop the demon insects. The spirit qi will help with the fusing of the embryos with the death aura. The purer the spirit qi I absorb, the more complete the fusion will be, and the better the alien insects will be able to manipulate the spirit qi to target the environment. The alien insect species has already collected a large amount of genes from this world. I will select some of the genes from the genes storage to become part of the evolved demon insects’ genetic model.","Keira’s message to Lin Yuan had been slightly cunning. She only mentioned wanting spirit qi but did not explicitly mention pure spirit qi.","Pure spirit qi was nothing more than a commodity to Lin Yuan. He could produce as much of it as he wanted.","However, Keira was unaware of this and thought that pure spirit qi was the most precious resource.","Keira was afraid that Lin Yuan would think that she was greedy.","Nonetheless, she still included the fact that the purer the spirit qi, the more complete the fusion between the embryos and death aura would be.","Those of high ranks usually were not turned off by such a roundabout way of asking for resources.","Keira had been observing Lin Yuan. The longer she observed him, the more certain she became that he was not a lifeform from a Class 1 or 2 world. This was because the secret weapons that he possessed surpassed even that of Class 3 worlds.","She was really curious to know which faction Lin Yuan’s legacy came from. Why were they taking such good care of a Class 1 world? It was because of the care that Lin Yuan was showing this Class 1 world that she managed to meet Lin Yuan!","If the other demon insect empresses found out that she had received such an opportunity after being reincarnated, they would all be dying of envy!","When Lin Yuan received Keira’s message, he was silent for a moment before he said,","[Lin Yuan]: Let the alien insect empresses manage the alien insect world. As for you, come to the Radiance Federation right now! You can have as much pure spirit qi as you want. Once you’re here, I’ll help you to evolve in the best way!","Technically, the most efficient method to produce the demon insects was for Keira to produce them on the spot.","The quantity of spirit qi crystals that Keira possessed was enough to tide her over until Lin Yuan sent a Dictator to send more to her.","However, Lin Yuan did not do that and instructed Keira to come to the Radiance Federation because he was going to protect the Radiance Federation first. This would prevent the dead dimensional lifeforms from causing widespread damage and contamination even if they managed to make it to the Radiance Federation.","Of all the lifeforms in the main world, the Radiance Federation was the only one that was still in its original position.","Once the Radiance Federation was conquered by the dead spirits, it would become the largest Dead Spirits Well, and the dimensional worlds would be barraged by the dead spirits from every direction.","Hence, Lin Yuan was making the best decision in terms of both an emotional and strategic angle!","Since he had decided to bring Keira over, Lin Yuan would only be able to make further decisions once she was here. This was because he did not know whether the demon insects would truly be the solution to the dead dimensional lifeforms in the way that Keira had described.","Thus, Lin Yuan did not tell the Moon Empress about this plan.","The Radiance Federation still needed to try coming up with other plans! The more strategies they came up with, the better protected the Radiance Federation would be.","Lin Yuan heard that Chef Supreme had raised the idea of managing the Creation Masters. It would definitely be challenging to manage the Creation Masters. It was indeed time to put some pressure on the Creation Masters and stir up a sense of urgency in them!","The dead spirits crisis had only been going on for two weeks, but many changes had already taken place in the Radiance Federation.","The entire era would change in accordance with the sixth epoch.","The sixth epoch had begun with death and pain, but at least it was over.","Once it was confirmed that the demon insects produced by Keira could handle the death aura and dead dimensional lifeforms,","Lin Yuan would reallocate the Samsara Realm Dictators in the four terrestrial dimensional worlds. He would no longer assign them only to the respective dimensional worlds they came from. Lin Yuan intended to mix up the Samsara Realm Dictators from different dimensional worlds and ensure that each of them had an army under them.","Lin Yuan would set up eight departments in every dimensional world, with two branches being formed from dimensional lifeforms from one dimensional world.","This way, there would be no part of the combined territories that were more susceptible to the dead dimensional lifeforms!","Otherwise, as time went on, the marsh world, abyssal world, and subterranean world would fall while only the alien insect world would grow stronger.","At this moment, Lin Yuan was very glad that Wen Yu had organized the dimensional worlds’ troops in a tree structure where every Samsara Realm Dictator had their own team.","Otherwise, there was no way that such a migration could be carried out successfully!","...","As the night grew deeper, the falling rain washed the Radiance Federation’s Royal Capital.","This should be the best time to sleep, but the light in the Radiance Federation’s meeting room was still on.","The 13 members of royalty were sitting in front of the table and staring stoically at the information that the Moon Empress and Night Leaning Moon had just handed out. The information contained the reports on the five dimensional worlds that had been delivered over by Liu Jie.","Even the Moon Empress, who was already aware of the terrors of the dead spirits crisis, had not anticipated the dimensional lifeforms to be having such a nightmarish time!","When the dimensional rifts first opened, these dimensional lifeforms had been the enemies of the humans. Every time they appeared, they consumed lifeforms from the main world.","But now, they had become the shields that were protecting the humans.","Alas, this shield that the humans were depending on was about to shatter.","The 13 members of royalty felt their throats go dry as they read through the information. They were at a loss about what to say.","They could not allow the issue to sit without addressing it.","The Moon Empress was the first to speak, “Since this situation is our reality, let’s discuss ways to tackle it!”","The Moon Empress was just done speaking when Cicada Song added, “The Dead Decay Earthworms and Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes have already been distributed. The Dead Decay Earthworms and Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes can only hold the fort down for so long.","“After all, the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake isn’t as easy to nurture as the Dead Decay Earthworm. The only thing we haven’t used is the power of the members of royalty. If we are really left with no other choice, we can enter the battle ourselves and lend all the strength we have to the Radiance Federation!","“In the past, I made it a point to only come up with the best solutions. This has become a habit. But we have already done all we could in order to face the dead dimensional lifeforms. I haven’t changed. I am still always ready to contribute everything I have to the Radiance Federation. I am sure that everyone here feels the same way.","“The dead dimensional lifeforms have yet to appear in the Radiance Federation, so we still don’t have a clear idea of just how deadly they are.","“Moon Empress, your disciple has been the one solving all the issues ever since the dead spirits crisis began. Why don’t you call him over to participate in this imperial meeting, too? This might be the only way to save the Radiance Federation!”","When Cicada Song spoke, he was rather self-mocking and vexed. But what he said was the truth.","If Lin Yuan had not sent this news, the Radiance Federation would still be overjoyed over the discovery of the Death-Cleansing Scale Snake and Dead Decay Earthworm, completely ignorant of the impending dangers!","However, Cicada Song’s words caused the Moon Empress to frown.","He was not only the savior of the Radiance Federation but also of the humans and other millions of lifeforms in the main world.","Lin Yuan had been silently lending his strength to the main world, and this was enough pressure on its own.","But if he joined the imperial meetings too, it would only add more pressure onto his shoulders.","With the immense pressure that he was already under, the Moon Empress did not want to increase his burden.","But what Cicada Song said was right. If none of them had any solutions, they would have no choice but to rely on Lin Yuan.","At this moment, the Moon Empress received a message from Lin Yuan on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, I might have a way to deal with the dead dimensional worlds. If this method is effective, the main world will become unaffected by the death aura! However, we should always be careful. I’m not sure if this method will work, but chances are high that it will. You don’t have to be too worried.","[Lin Yuan]: Nonetheless, it will still be best to continue having the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters find ways to treat the death aura. This way, even if my method doesn’t show positive results, the Radiance Federation still has the research to fall back on!","Lin Yuan knew that the Moon Empress had to be very anxious after finding out about this. He decided to tell her everything because he was afraid that she would be overwhelmed by her anxiousness.","In all honesty, Lin Yuan knew that the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters would not be able to solve the problem of the dead dimensional lifeforms given that they did not even understand them.","Lin Yuan had spent the past two years building up his arsenal and increasing his store of secret weapons. If the dead spirits crisis had taken place six months ago, the main world would have been completely devoured.","Lin Yuan did not fully understand Keira and the demon insect.","Keira was his servant, but they had not interacted much yet.","However, Lin Yuan did not think that Keira would lie to him about such matters.","She was not strong yet. But the alien insect empresses would deliver the demon insect embryos, and they would soon reach the Radiance Federation.","It was possible that the dead dimensional lifeforms would appear in the Radiance Federation before Keira arrived.","Even if they did not appear before then, Lin Yuan had already sent out the instructions. Any Samsara Realm Dictator whose team had captured a dead dimensional lifeform was ordered to send it to the Radiance Federation with an Apostle as an escort. The delivery had to be done under the strictest and most secure conditions to prevent the dead dimensional lifeform from releasing death aura in the Radiance Federation.","Some of the Moon Empress’ panic subsided when she saw Lin Yuan’s message.","Frankly, there was no way that the experts in the main world could counter the death aura.","The moonbeams released by the Moon Empress could cleanse the death aura to a certain extent, and the Mother of Bloodbath had some abilities and exclusive skills that could take control of dead spirits and cleanse them.","But in the grand scheme of things, individual powers did not make much of an impact. There was no way they would be able to cleanse every single dead spirit!","Although the Radiance Federation had slowly stabilized after the initial eruption of the Dead Spirits Wells, there were still new Dead Spirits Wells being built. The Land Imps were also continuously adding and fortifying the metal-type stone boards.","Previously, the Moon Empress believed that humans would definitely be able to succeed in anything they put their minds to. But in the face of a large-scale catastrophe, even spirit fire experts could not be of much help!","There were many Samsara Realm Dictators that were the equivalent of spirit fire experts in the dimensional worlds. Some Samsara Realm Dictators could even be stronger than spirit fire experts. Yet, none of them could even take on the dead spirits that were just above average in power on their own.","The right thing for the Radiance Federation to do was to continue researching ways to produce feys that could deal with the dead spirits in the long term.","The Moon Empress became more relaxed when she heard about the situation from Lin Yuan.","However, she did not tell the other 12 members of royalty about this.","Chef Supreme’s suggestion to manage the Creation Masters had been pushed to the side because the Moon Empress did not want destabilizing changes happening within the Radiance Federation at the onset of the dead spirits crisis.","But now, she changed her mind.","Anything could happen during the battle with the dead spirits. Stability did not exist.","Thus, given that none of them were able to come up with an effective solution to deal with the dead dimensional lifeforms, all they could do was spark the Radiance Federation’s spirits to the greatest extent so the Creation Masters could unleash their full potential to protect the Radiance Federation.","The only way that the Radiance Federation could fulfill their duty of being the leader of the Major Federation Union was by finding an effective solution to deal with the dead spirits and having the ability to continuously replenish resources.","The clash between the dead spirits and humans had only just begun. There was no guarantee that the humans would end up as the losers.","The Moon Empress did not want the seventh epoch to be a playground of death ruled by the dead spirits!"]},{"number":2673,"title":"Chapter 2673 Five Female Demon Insect Eggs!","paragraphs":["2673 Five Female Demon Insect Eggs!","The Bamboo Monarch had told the Moon Empress about this privately. He had not brought it up in the presence of the other members of royalty.","The Moon Empress had set the Bamboo Monarch’s suggestion aside, and he thought that she, like Chef Supreme, was against his idea.","Yet, she ended up bringing it up during an official imperial meeting.","“The dead dimensional lifeforms’ invasion into the main world could be the end of the Radiance Federation. But we will be able to find a solution. Since no one is able to come up with a good idea, let’s move on to another topic.","“I suggest changing the Creation Master Association so that it is no longer independent and self-managed. Let’s set up an official department to recruit Creation Masters under the Radiance Federation’s name. The recruited Creation Masters will do research under this department and increase the efficiency of the Creation Masters. What do you think of this idea?","The Moon Empress had similar ideas in the past, but she had not developed them.","Since Chef Supreme brought up this suggestion, the Moon Empress decided to focus on that.","After an investigation, they discovered that many Creation Masters claimed to be researching ways to cleanse the death aura but were secretly concocting potions and selling them on Star Web.","This might not be the main reason behind the slowdown in the Radiance Federation’s research, but it was definitely a contributing factor.","The Creation Masters’ undisciplined attitude made the Moon Empress unsure of the Radiance Federation’s future. She needed to build another anchoring force. Otherwise, all of the pressure would land on Lin Yuan’s shoulders.","Lin Yuan was the savior of the main world, not its slave.","Lin Yuan had already done enough. The Moon Empress did not want his load to become even heavier!","The Bamboo Monarch immediately voiced his agreement when he heard what the Moon Empress said.","The Bamboo Monarch had formed such ideas long ago, but he had not run it past the other members of royalty or gotten the approval of the Moon Empress, who was a Class 6 Creation Master. As such, he had not been able to carry out the plan!","To the outside world, he and Chef Supreme might seem to be on equal standing with the Moon Empress. But in actuality, the Moon Empress’ abilities had far surpassed their own. The Moon Empress’ Class 6 Creation Master power was not fabricated.","Now that the Moon Empress had proposed and supported this idea, it was very likely that it would be able to proceed smoothly.","There were many Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation. Every Class 4 Creation Master possessed endless creation powers. If their abilities could be united, it would only lead to a positive result for the Radiance Federation!","Furthermore, doing this would not cut into the Creation Masters’ profits. Rather, after banding together and working for the Radiance Federation’s sake, their powers might even improve!","“I agree with the Moon Empress’ suggestion! At least 60% of the Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation aren’t doing the research that was instructed. A small portion of Class 4 Creation Masters are even serving top factions instead. If we are able to combine their abilities, we will be able to stand a better chance of taking on the dead spirits crisis!”","Chef Supreme sighed. This was easier said than done.","If they made such a choice, the Radiance Federation would have to suffer the consequences for a long time.","But if they were able to properly execute this plan, they were making an investment now to reap the benefits in the future!","The Moon Empress was not the type who liked to gamble. Since she had brought up the suggestion, it meant that she had full confidence to see it through.","Chef Supreme would not be able to rest easy if this matter was left to the Bamboo Monarch to handle. But he had complete faith that the Moon Empress would be able to do a good job. However, given the Moon Empress’ ruthless methods, the disobedient Creation Masters were going to have some pain in their future!","Chef Supreme also agreed with the Moon Empress’ suggestion. At such a time, he, the Moon Empress, and the Bamboo Monarch could not be on different sides as that would indicate opposing opinions.","If there were opposing opinions, Tian Feng and the other members of royalty who preferred to err on the side of safety would definitely voice their opposition.","Given that this matter concerned the Creation Masters, if all three of them were in agreement, no one else would have the right to contradict them.","The Moon Empress had made the suggestion, and it was followed by agreement from Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch.","The meeting room fell silent for a moment before other voices of agreement chimed in.","Cicada Song waited until he was sure that no one was going to argue and was silent for a long time before he said, “Moon Empress, once such a change takes place, the quantity of Creation Master resources in the Radiance Federation will fall by at least a third of its current level. This will probably last for six months or more. I hope that all of you are prepared for this.”","Cicada Song was not going against the Moon Empress’ decision. He actually believed that she was doing the right thing. This strict method would minimize the negative impacts on the Radiance Federation to the greatest extent.","However, Cicada Song was used to thinking about the consequences.","The other members of royalty had to be made aware of the severity of the consequences in order for them to cooperate with the Moon Empress, Chef Supreme, and the Bamboo Monarch’s subsequent plans.","Chef Supreme and the Bamboo Monarch did not speak. Instead, they turned to look at the Moon Empress.","The Bamboo Monarch had not voiced this suggestion publicly because he was unable to afford the consequences.","But now that the Moon Empress was bringing it up, it meant that she was able to handle the consequences.","The Moon Empress gently knocked on the table twice before saying resolutely, “Regardless of how little Creation Master resources the Radiance Federation has this year, I will be able to make up for it.","“I believe that as long as we work together, we will be able to endure the rough period, and eventually, the dust will settle!”","The Moon Empress paused before she continued. “Elder Liu, you have already informed those involved of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection, but you haven’t sent out an announcement to the entire federation. I suggest delaying this matter by a week before going ahead with the original plan.”","Liu Wencheng nodded and said, “I will send out word of the delay. Moon Empress, let me know if you have any other requests, and I will do my best to accommodate you!”","The Moon Empress did not request the delay because she wanted to use the time to gather the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters. Gathering the Creation Masters’ did not clash with the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection. She made this request because she wanted to give Lin Yuan time.","Firstly, Lin Yuan could use this time to test if his plan was effective. Secondly, the Moon Empress knew that given Lin Yuan’s current situation, he could not miss this event.","Lin Yuan had shone the brightest during the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. He had even eliminated a Freedom Envoy.","After that, Lin Yuan became an idol in the eyes of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation. He became even more popular than the Radiance Envoys.","If he was absent, the Radiance Federation’s citizens would definitely notice and wonder why. This would affect the objective of the event.","The event’s objective was to raise the Radiance Federation’s fighting spirit. Otherwise, they could have held these selections privately.","The Moon Empress did not mention the dead dimensional lifeforms again, but the others guessed that she had already found a solution. Otherwise, she would not have changed the topic!","At this moment, the Radiance Federation’s royalty were all doing their best to increase their power. They wanted to be able to use their own power to come up with solutions when the Radiance Federation was in danger.","After the imperial meeting ended, the Moon Empress returned to the Radiant Moon Palace.","She, the Bamboo Monarch, and Chef Supreme established a research institute for the Creation Masters and requested for every Creation Master in the Radiance Federation to join!","The Moon Empress was busy trying to bring together the Radiance Federation’s Creation Masters’ strength while also waiting for a response from Lin Yuan.","Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Xia Qing, Gao Feng, and An He left the training rooms on the second day. All of them had increased their feys’ powers.","After hearing that the selections would be postponed, none of them stayed in the Return from Faraway Mansion to disturb Lin Yuan.","Zong Ze and Gu Lang agreed to head to the Dead Spirits Wells to battle the dead spirits so they could gain an understanding of their strength.","Xia Qing decided to return to the imperial court to stabilize her two feys.","Her spiritual energy had mutated by accident.","While in seclusion, Xia Qing’s ability had also moved past A-rank spirit qi professional. Although she was still a distance away from becoming an S-rank spirit qi professional, she knew that her mutated spiritual power would allow her to wield Suzerain/pinnacle Myth feys!","Gao Feng intended on going to see Cicada Song to help him with some of his work.","An He was going to see his senior brother and fight with him as a means of training his own combat skills.","On the fourth day, Lin Yuan finally caught sight of Keira rushing towards him.","Keira said to him with utmost respect, “Master, on the way here, I captured more than ten dead dimensional lifeforms. They are appearing with increasing frequency. I selected five insect eggs, and they consumed the dead dimensional lifeforms before I guided them to hatch. These are the female insects I hatched.”","Keira took out the Diamond fey storage box that Lin Yuan had given her and released the five demon insects.","The appearance of the five demon insects gave Lin Yuan a fright.","Perhaps it was because of the genetic model from the dead dimensional lifeforms, but the five female demon insects had black bodies shrouded in thin black mist. They looked like spiders with slender legs, but unlike spiders, they had 12 legs.","The five female demon insects had generally similar genetic models, but their details differed vastly.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the five demon insects. He saw that they did not have any set abilities or exclusive skills.","This was very similar to when Lin Yuan used True Data on Keira.","This did not mean that Morbius’ investigative abilities had gone wrong. Rather, the demon insects that used their genetic models to do battle were already the best weapons in themselves.","In this aspect, they were very similar to dimensional lifeforms.","This was also further proof that the alien insects came from the demon insects’ genetic model.","When she saw that Lin Yuan was not saying anything, Keira began to introduce the five female demon insects, “Master, you can provide these five female insects with an environment concentrated with death aura to test their powers. What do you think of this?”","Lin Yuan nodded. This was exactly what he was planning to do.","Just on her way here, Keira had managed to notice that the dead dimensional lifeforms were appearing in increasing frequency.","Lin Yuan was very aware of this because he had been receiving updated news from the Samsara Realm Dictators.","Now, the entire main world was in a state of emergency.","If this issue was not solved within the next two months, the entire main world would be doomed!","Death aura could flow and spread.","In two months, given the rate at which the dead dimensional lifeforms were appearing, the concentration of death aura in the environment could even overtake that of spirit qi!","Tower Canon’s attack was not one-fold. Rather, they had launched an assault that would destroy the Radiance Federation!","Lin Yuan mulled over this and decided that the best place for the five demon insects to unleash their abilities would be near a Dead Spirits Well. The eruption of dead spirits from the Dead Spirits Well would provide a good simulation for the demon insects to battle.","With this thought, Lin Yuan contacted the Moon Empress.","When the call went through, Lin Yuan immediately noticed how weary the Moon Empress’ voice was. This made his chest ache.","But he could not tell her to rest now.","If there was any opportunity to rest, the Moon Empress would not have allowed her exhaustion to show.","The only thing that Lin Yuan could do for the Moon Empress would be to set her mind at ease.","Lin Yuan said to the Moon Empress, “Master, the aid I intend on sending to deal with the dead dimensional lifeforms has arrived. I need a Dead Spirits Well to test their efficacy. Do you have time to spare? If you do, you can come with me to observe the experiment!”","The Moon Empress’ expression froze momentarily, and she immediately set down what was in her hands and said excitedly, “Little Yuan, dead dimensional lifeforms have appeared in Dead Spirits Well C33 in the north area of the Royal Capital. Why don’t we use that area for your test? I will head there now and personally clear the area. The troops in Area C33 will be sent to help Area C32. I will send Mystic Moon to fetch you an hour later.”","Lin Yuan hurriedly said, “Master, there’s no need to trouble Uncle Mystic. I will ride my fey and head over an hour later. I am not far from the Dead Spirits Well in Area C33. It will take less than ten minutes for the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to take me there.”","After she was done speaking, the Moon Empress hung up.","Frankly, Lin Yuan was rather nervous. Even if the five female demon insects managed to handle the dead spirits from the Dead Spirits Well, this might not be indicative of a solution. Lin Yuan was not just trying to handle one Dead Spirits Well, but all the dead spirits that were running amok in the main world.","Keira had been observing Lin Yuan’s expression. When she saw how concerned he looked, she said assertively, “Master, once you see the five female demon insects, you will definitely be so happy that you’ll feel like you’re flying!”"]},{"number":2674,"title":"Chapter 2674 The Amazing Demon Insects!","paragraphs":["2674 The Amazing Demon Insects!","Keira had never heard of the idiom ‘every potter praises his own pot’ but that was exactly what she was doing at the moment.","However, while the potter could not guarantee that every pot would be of the same quality, Keira could ensure the strength of the demon insects.","To the lifeforms in the main world, the dead world crisis was a calamity. But to Keira, there was nothing special about the dead world crisis. This was not because she was aloof to the plight of the main world but because she had seen too many similar events in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Thus, these circumstances were not cause for much interest to her.","The demon insects could easily produce a branch species that was capable of creating such an event.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie, who were standing behind Lin Yuan, did not trust this strange and boastful lifeform. What she was saying sounded almost too good to be true, to the point that it was likely a scam!","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he said to Keira seriously, “Keira, if your demon insects can help to solve my issue, I will enable you, or rather the demon insects, to evolve. Come with me. It will soon be time for you to dazzle with your true abilities!”","Lin Yuan could sense Keira’s confidence. Her self-assurance gave him significant ease.","The demon insects were much more intelligent than humans. If Keira did not have absolute confidence, she would not have made such claims. She was well aware of the price that she would have to pay for lying to Lin Yuan. With their contract in place, he could easily eliminate her and put an end to the demon insects.","Keira had witnessed the impact of the dead spirits crisis on the alien insect world.","The boundary between the alien insect world and main world had a much more serious outbreak of dead spirits than here around one of the Radiance Federation’s Dead Spirits Wells.","Keira mentioned that the demon insects had a glittering battle record back at the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He prayed that the demon insects could recreate their success from the Sky Beyond the Clouds and bring salvation to the main world.","Lin Yuan released the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","Keira did not use any other demon insect eggs. She led the five female demon insects and quickly climbed onto the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s back.","Wen Yu said to Lin Yuan seriously, “Young Master, let me and Big Brother Liu come with you! Ever since the dead spirits crisis began, all I’ve been doing is organizational work.","“My knowledge of the dead spirits crisis is solely based on data and information that was reported to me. I haven’t seen and experienced the dead spirits personally. I can use this opportunity to collect even more data!”","Lin Yuan nodded. He had also intended to take Liu Jie and Wen Yu with him.","They might not be able to provide much help, but it was necessary for them to understand what the main world was currently facing. Otherwise, they could make mistakes in the instructions they gave out.","Given the dead dimensional lifeforms’ impact on the main world, it was clear that Tower Canon had intended for the invasion of the dead dimensional lifeforms to be a lethal move. However, they had not anticipated Keira’s presence.","If they had anticipated Keira’s presence and were capable of putting up a defense, they would have already done all they could to kill her.","With just a few flaps of its wings, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly arrived at the Dead Spirits Well in Area C33.","The Moon Empress and Cicada Song had come together and moved all of the Radiance Federation’s soldiers to the Dead Spirits Well at Area C32.","Despite it clearly being the middle of the afternoon, a moon appeared in the sky.","The moonbeams were like a waterfall that fell in a 50-kilometer radius around the Dead Spirits Well at Area C33 and trapped all the dead spirits within. If any of the dead spirits within tried to pass through the cage of moonbeams, they would be instantly vaporized by the moonbeams. The moonbeams also cleansed the death aura.","The Moon Empress herself was worth millions of troops, and she could ensure that this Dead Spirits Well was no longer affecting the environment around it or endangering the citizens in the area.","But human strength was limited. Millions of troops could secure tens of Dead Spirits Wells, but the Moon Empress could not.","The Moon Empress needed to use her own energy to create the moon in the sky and unleash moonbeams.","If she was capable of holding down the fort on her own, she would not be as troubled by the dead spirits crisis as she was!","Although the Moon Empress had attained an endless lifespan after contracting the Lifespan Mouse, she would be willing to give up her immortality if it meant that she would be able to save the Radiance Federation! From the first day she became a Radiance Envoy, the Moon Empress had been ready to lay down her life for the Radiance Federation.","The Moon Empress sensed the number of dead spirits that were trapped by the moonbeams and let out a deep sigh.","This was just one day’s worth of dead spirits and death aura from one Dead Spirits Well.","This was not the first time that the Moon Empress was stepping in to take control of a Dead Spirits Well. There were numerous instances where the Dead Spirits Wells had shown signs of collapsing, and the Moon Empress had to step in to handle the situation.","She could clearly notice that the weekly quantity of the dead spirits bursting out from the Dead Spirits Wells had increased! The dead spirits were now surging from the Dead Spirits Wells at around 1.3 times their initial rate.","This allowed the Moon Empress to confirm one thing, which was that the dead spirits were being awakened slowly and would be emerging in waves.","This would continuously increase the pressure on the Radiance Federation’s troops that were stationed around the Dead Spirits Wells. It was possible that the metal-type stone boards would eventually crack.","To prevent the metal-type stone boards from eventually breaking, the Radiance Federation could not stop building more of the Dead Spirits Wells.","Could the Radiance Federation really handle all that pressure?","The Moon Empress could not remember the last time she felt this helpless.","The Moon Empress never liked relying on others. However, given the circumstances, she had no choice but to place all her hopes in Lin Yuan.","When the Moon Empress turned to look behind her, she saw Lin Yuan riding the Kill Food Sky Butterfly toward her.","She waved at him. It was only when the Kill Food Sky Butterfly got nearer that the Moon Empress spotted Keira and the five bizarre female demon insects.","Lin Yuan bowed at the Moon Empress and Cicada Song before getting right to the point, “Master, open a hole in the cage of moonbeams that the dead spirits can pass through. This will allow me to test my plan out!”","This was not the first time that Cicada Song was meeting Lin Yuan. But every time they made contact, his impression of Lin Yuan was refreshed.","It could be said that Cicada Song had watched Lin Yuan grow up. However, Lin Yuan’s growth had not been characterized by steps but by leaps and bounds. Each jump was extremely wide.","This young man in front of him might have already surpassed him in power long ago.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was still humble and respectful toward him. This was a very rare virtue for a young man!","Although Cicada Song was very composed and unshakable now, his youth had been wild.","With a wave of the Moon Empress’ hand, the moon in the sky lit up, and the ribbons of moonbeams slowly parted like a curtain.","The sea of dead spirits enveloped in death aura charged out.","Lin Yuan’s heart skipped a beat with initial shock before he said to Keira, “Keira, it’s time for you to perform!”","Keira’s lips twitched. She wondered if Lin Yuan had misunderstood something.","She asked Lin Yuan to test these five female insects’ powers. Why did he bring them here? How was this enough to test the five female insects? She wanted to show off for Lin Yuan, but he had provided her with such a small stage.","She felt that he was underestimating her. Did he think so little of the demon insects’ power?","Keira felt that it was necessary for her to prove what the demon insects could do.","But regardless of how daring she was, Keira would never dare to speak against Lin Yuan.","With this thought, Keira said despondently to the female insect next to her, “Doom, send out an offspring with a Class 3 Genetic Lock to handle these dead spirits and death aura! Remember to do a good jog. Not even a hint of death aura can be allowed to remain!”","Keira scrunched her nose.","“The death aura around here is of a relatively high concentration. While you’re at it, cleanse all the death aura in the area!”","The female insects that Keira had produced were of a similar intelligence to her.","Being a highly intelligent lifeform, Doom knew of the best way to demonstrate her abilities.","Since Keira had picked her first, this was a prime opportunity for her to prove herself.","Just like Keira was trying her best to get Lin Yuan to acknowledge her, the female insects that Keira had produced were also trying to win her trust and affection.","In a family with many children, regardless of how fair the parents tried to be, it was inevitable for there to be favorites.","Doom raised one of her spidery legs up, and a hair as long as her leg shot out. A purple and black egg shot out from the area where the hair was connected to her leg.","The egg shot into the sea of dead spirits.","At this instant, Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress, Cicada Song, Wen Yu, and Liu Jie could sense that the sea of dead spirits was waning.","When they took a closer look, they saw that every dead spirit had a purple and black maggot that was around a centimeter long on it. The maggots were gobbling the dead spirits’ bodies and bones at an almost unimaginable rate.","It was as though the sea of dead spirits was being eaten and swallowed.","The dead spirits that the Moon Empress had trapped for some time could not catch up to the rate at which the millions of maggots were eating them.","Once the maggots were done eating the dead spirits, many of them crawled into the Dead Spirits Well.","The ever-cool-headed Moon Empress and Cicada Song could not stop their jaws from dropping. They found it hard to believe that the annihilation of so many dead spirits had come from a spider lifeform merely lifting its leg.","The insect lifeform that Lin Yuan had called Keira had mentioned an offspring that had a Class 3 Genetic Lock.","If this insect lifeform was like the alien insects, there should also be offspring with Class 2 and Class 1 Genetic Locks that had even more powerful genes.","At this instant, hope sparked to life in the Moon Empress and Cicada Song’s eyes.","It was at this moment that the black and purple maggots ran out of dead spirits to consume and began eating each other.","This reminded Lin Yuan of a game in his previous life called Eat Fish.","The maggots grew visibly larger each time they ate one of their counterparts. Soon, they turned into half-meter-long cocoons.","All of this happened in the blink of an eye. The insects worked like a rapid machine.","Eventually, the ground was covered with over 4000 cocoons that were around half a meter long.","Less than 30 seconds later, the cocoons broke open, and a spider lifeform that was slightly smaller than the mother insect crawled out. They let out piercing screeches as though they were heralding their new life.","Soon, it was as though the death aura permeating the air was being attracted as they entered the demon insects’ bodies.","The demon insects drank up the death aura in the air, and the death aura became their source of energy.","The newly born demon insects with Class 3 Genetic Locks were extremely capable of absorbing death aura. The Moon Empress could sense that all the death aura in a 50-kilometer radius was quickly being pulled to this spot.","The spider lifeforms were gathered together now, but they would be able to make just as large of an impact when they spread out. This meant that as long as there was one of these insects in a 50-kilometer radius, there was no need to be concerned about there being death aura present in the area.","This was much more effective than using the Dead Decay Earthworms to cleanse the death aura!","Keira glared at Doom. She was not very satisfied with Doom’s performance. This was because Doom had not prevented the first few demon insects from being consumed. Otherwise, there would have been one to two times more of the newly born demon insects with Class 3 Genetic Locks.","If Lin Yuan was dissatisfied with her demon insect genes because of this, it would be extremely bad for Keira!","Lin Yuan would have opportunities to take control of other demon insect queens when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Based on Keira’s gaze, Doom realized that she had been careless.","As Keira’s offspring, Doom did not even have the right to rebuke her.","Keira could kill these female insects she had produced with just as much ease as Lin Yuan could do to her.","In order to prove the demon insects’ value, Keira hurriedly said, “Master, some of the demon insects have gone beneath the Dead Spirits Well. They are reproducing there. A few demon insects with Class 3 Genetic Locks can form a miniature colony.","“As long as none of the dead spirits that appear are overly strong, they won’t be able to make it out from the Dead Spirits Well! Doom only used one egg that she had prepared in advance. There weren’t enough dead spirits here for the insects to consume, so they had no choice but to reproduce through consuming each other.","“If the number of dead spirits is increased by ten times and is accompanied by a large amount of death aura and dead dimensional lifeforms, the demon insects will truly be able to demonstrate our capabilities.","“If you want to test the demon insects’ abilities, I hope you can bring me to the boundary between one of the dimensional worlds and this Class 2 world. It is only at a place like that that the demon insects will be able to properly perform!”","Keira spoke with an anxious tone, but she had not lost any of her confidence.","However, Wen Yu and Liu Jie no longer felt that she was boasting.","The two of them had only just managed to recover from their stupefaction."]},{"number":2675,"title":"Chapter 2675 Insects Take Over the Startling Lines Continent!","paragraphs":["2675 Insects Take Over the Startling Lines Continent!","Liu Jie and Wen Yu had been with Lin Yuan for a long time. They were more resistant to the shock that came with witnessing such feats than the Moon Empress and Cicada Song were.","Keira’s abilities were astounding.","Although Keira said that she was limited by her environment and could not unleash her full power, Liu Jie and Wen Yu were already certain that Keira would be able to fend off the dead spirits crisis.","Although the dead spirits crisis would continue progressing, the amazing demon insects would be able to minimize the impact on the main world to the greatest extent.","However, it went without saying that this also depended on whether Tower Canon had any new moves to play that would deter the demon insects.","Lin Yuan looked at Keira and said seriously, “I will give you the chance to wield your full abilities soon so we can gain a full understanding of the demon insects’ abilities! Until then, do your best to push the five female demon insects to reproduce as quickly as possible.”","Lin Yuan handed a Diamond fey storage box to Keira.","Lin Yuan knew what Keira wanted and why she was willing to work so hard for him, to the point that she had rushed from the alien insect world to the Radiance Federation within three days.","Keira had not yet replenished the energy she had used up to produce the demon insects.","Keira did not like leaving her nest before she fully recuperated.","She decided to rush to the Radiance Federation in spite of this because he had absolute control over her. He controlled her soul so she could not go against any of his requests.","Additionally, she hoped that he would give her resources that she could use to develop the demon insects.","Keira was an open book to Lin Yuan.","At first, Lin Yuan was displeased that she had only laid five eggs, but he did not show his displeasure. He felt that Keira was not treating his orders with enough seriousness.","But now, it seemed that he had underestimated the abilities of Keira’s female demon insects.","Lin Yuan turned to say to the Moon Empress and Cicada Song, “Master and Lord Cicada Song, you have just witnessed the demon insects’ abilities in countering the dead dimensional lifeforms.","“Up until now, Tower Canon has been the only one attacking. It’s time for us to show Tower Canon that we aren’t to be trifled with!”","In the battle with Tower Canon, Lin Yuan had been the one reacting to the moves made by Tower Canon.","But now, Lin Yuan wanted a change.","If he stayed in his current position, he would not be able to dig deeper into Tower Canon’s secrets. Tower Canon would never exhibit all of their secret weapons if they were able to decide on the attacks.","Lin Yuan needed to be able to see through Tower Canon.","There would be two possible results to trying to see through Tower Canon.","Firstly, Tower Canon would put up a fight and push back with force. The two sides would end up utilizing their secret weapons and pit them against each other in a good fight.","The other possibility would be that after witnessing the humans’ powers, Tower Canon would retreat back to the shadows to gather more power. This would give the humans more time to develop.","Regardless of which consequence it was, Lin Yuan could accept it.","But rather than the latter outcome that seemed to be more beneficial for him, the Radiance Federation, and humans, Lin Yuan preferred the former.","It was no longer Tower Canon that truly terrified him, but Epoch God Palace.","According to Eighth Page Apoptosis, Tower Canon had lost the battle against Eighth Page Apoptosis thousands of years ago. It had resulted in Tower Canon recuperating for the past few thousands of years while Epoch God Palace had been able to continue developing.","Lin Yuan hoped that after this catastrophe, he would be able to draw out Epoch God Palace and have the chance to make contact with them.","As things stood, he had no means of making contact with Epoch God Palace.","Lin Yuan let out a silent sigh. Just what was he going to do with Epoch God Palace?","His army was making waves in the main world, yet Epoch God Palace was showing no signs of trying to make contact with him. Were they really so strong that they could ignore all of this?","Lin Yuan pursed his lips, and an overwhelming wave of thoughts and emotions took over his mind.","The Moon Empress and Cicada Song hurriedly nodded, and she said seriously, “Little Yuan, if you are going to head to the boundary of the dimensional worlds and the main world where the battle with the dead spirits is the fiercest, take Eternal Source with you! Keeping him with me is limiting his movements anyway!”","Lin Yuan shook his head and smiled before he said, “Master, I have other experts who are just as strong as Eternal Source, so you don’t have to worry about me! I already accounted for Eternal Source staying with you to protect you!","“It won’t affect my plans at all, so you don’t have to worry! Once I take Keira to unleash the full power of the demon insects, I will bring back with me numerous demon insects, and they will set up nests in the Dead Spirits Wells. Then, stability will return to the Radiance Federation!”","Lin Yuan instructed the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to immediately take him, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, the five female demon insects, and Keira to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","The Space Tunnel under the Return from Faraway Mansion was the nearest access point to the Startling Lines Continent.","The situation in the Radiance Federation was grave, and Lin Yuan needed to save all the time he could.","The Startling Lines Continent was the training ground that Lin Yuan had prepared.","Qin Yu and the millions of Land Imps had been working in the Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan had not hesitated to pour in resources and turn the entire Startling Lines Continent into a metal bucket. There were only ten Dead Spirits Wells in the entire Startling Lines Continent, each of which was guarded by two Samsara Realm Dictators.","The citizens in Thick Soil City led very similar lives to the citizens in the Radiance Federation. Both had almost no injuries or damage because they had someone standing in front of them to shield them.","But it went without saying that during such a crisis, some minor injuries were inevitable.","Lin Yuan had heard Listen mention in the past about how capable Qin Yu was. But at that point, he had only heard about Qin Yu’s capabilities from others.","However, now that he had given Qin Yu a task, Lin Yuan discovered that he was truly a talent when it came to execution capabilities!","Execution capabilities were very different from governance abilities.","Although governance abilities had slightly more value to a faction, execution abilities could not be absent if a faction wanted to develop well!","Lin Yuan had many people under him who were capable of execution, but based on his observations, Qin Yu could easily make it into the top three!","Recently, Lin Yuan often received news from Ta Lei and Qin Yu through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Ta Lei also gave him periodic updates on the situation in Thick Soil City.","Lin Yuan had supplied sufficient powerful dimensional lifeforms to the Startling Lines Continent to ensure its safety so Ta Lei did not have much to worry about.","After Ta Lei’s previous report, Lin Yuan suggested that Ta Lei look around the Startling Lines Continent to see if there were any areas that needed to be renovated.","This was both a test and an opportunity that Lin Yuan was giving Ta Lei. He wanted to see if Ta Lei had not only grown in age but also in perspective and acumen.","Alas, the suggestion that Ta Lei made two days later wholly disappointed Lin Yuan.","Ta Lei felt that it was a waste to use a large amount of metal-type spiritual ingredients.","After hearing this, regardless of whether Ta Lei had any insinuations towards Qin Yu, Lin Yuan felt that Ta Lei was very narrow-sighted.","The Land Imps were able to control minerals. They could not only blend minerals but also separate them. Thus, any minerals used in the Startling Lines Continent would not go to waste.","All Lin Yuan needed to do was order the Land Imps to gather all the resources, and he would be able to retrieve all of them in a very short span of time. The only thing that would be used up was the Land Imps’ time.","If Ta Lei was not even able to see this, it would be very difficult for him to make any strategic advancements in the future!","The construction of the defenses in the Startling Lines Continent was basically complete. However, it would not be Sky City and the Radiance Federation’s troops that would be training there but the demon insects that naturally consumed the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms.","The Startling Lines Continents’ seemingly impenetrable defenses would only hinder the female demon insects.","While riding on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, Lin Yuan sent a message to Qin Yu.","[Lin Yuan]: Qin Yu, stop renovating the Startling Lines Continent. Relay my message to the other teams of Land Imps and tell them to stop what they’re doing. Once I arrive, we will meet at the underground palace at the center of the Startling Lines Continent. Then, we will start dismantling all of the defenses that have already been constructed.","Lin Yuan’s message to Qin Yu was very sudden, and it affected many of the plans that Qin Yu had already prepared. Nonetheless, he did not feel any begrudment and immediately replied.","[Qin Yu]: Young Master, when will you be arriving? I will try to make the arrangements at the underground palace as per your instructions before you arrive!","Once again, Qin Yu demonstrated his impressive execution abilities to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan nodded in satisfaction when he received Qin Yu’s response.","By now, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly had arrived in front of the Return from Faraway Mansion. Lin Yuan sent his response.","[Lin Yuan]: I will appear in the underground palace five minutes later. Go ahead and make the arrangements! After this trip to the Startling Lines Continent, there won’t be much for you to do there because it will enter a state of stability. You can leave things there to Ta Lei. I will be taking you with me back to the Radiance Federation. Qing Lun has grown much taller recently. He asks about you each time I see him. I am sure he will be delighted to see you back in the Radiance Federation!","In consideration of the sadness of separation felt by the two brothers, Wen Yu had prepared Thoughts Letter Papers for Qin Lun and Qin Yu so the two of them could still converse whenever they wanted.","However, there was still a big difference between conversing through the Thoughts Letter Paper and being reunited in real life!","When Qin Yu, who was clutching the Thoughts Letter Paper, read Lin Yuan’s message, a genuine smile spread across his cold and handsome facial features.","It was not just Qin Lun who missed Qin Yu. Qin Yu missed his brother badly as well.","Qin Yu knew that Lin Yuan had sent him to oversee the construction of the defenses in the Startling Lines Continent because he wanted to train him.","Although he did not know why Lin Yuan suddenly wanted to dismantle the defenses that had been so carefully and painstakingly constructed, he guessed that he had passed the training.","If he had not passed, he would have been sent to Thick Soil City to manage it alongside Ta Lei.","Qin Yu composed himself. The gratitude that he felt towards Lin Yuan intensified. The consideration that Lin Yuan had for him touched him to the point that he felt the faint urge to cry.","In the past month that he had spent managing the Land Imps, Qin Yu had gained absolute authority over them. Now, not even the Samsara Realm Land Imps dared to defy him.","Previously, there were a few Land Imps that did not take Qin Yu’s instructions seriously, and Qin Yu immediately asked Lin Yuan to swap them out. Qin Yu’s authoritative manner taught the Land Imps the consequences of getting on his bad side.","Furthermore, when the Land Imps found out that Lin Yuan was coming, they swiftly carried out Qin Yu’s instructions and gathered at the underground palace.","Lin Yuan had already arrived at the underground palace.","The underground palace’s construction had been completed long ago. Qin Yu did not damage the underground palace while he was renovating and setting up the Startling Lines Continent’s defenses. Instead, he buried the metal-type stone boards under the underground palace. It could be said that the underground palace was even more fortified than Thick Soil City!","Lin Yuan summoned the Land Imps that he had previously sent to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","He instructed them to use metal-type stone boards to envelop the entire underground palace before moving it up to the surface.","This way, he would be able to move the underground palace into the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","With the Spirit Lock spatial zone being as large as the Xia Region now, he would have no problems storing the underground palace there.","Hu Quan could not have done a better job of creating the underground palace. He had even hand-carved all of the etchings on the walls.","If the underground palace was moved into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it could be used as a resting place for the lifeforms working in the Spirit Lock spatial zone once Hu Quan was made some alterations.","When the Land Imps used the metal-type stone boards to envelop the underground palace, the defenses were weakened, and the dead spirits immediately seized the opportunity.","Given that the metal-type stone boards had been laid down in even thicker layers in the Startling Lines Continent than the Radiance Federation, the pressure building up beneath the Startling Lines Continent was even greater than that of the Radiance Federation.","A hole opened up right in front of Lin Yuan.","But without him needing to give any orders, Keira looked at Doom.","There was no need to use all five female demon insects to deal with one eruption of dead spirits.","Keira was not pleased with Doom’s recent performance.","When Doom noticed Keira looking at her, she immediately realized that this was her chance to remedy her mistake.","Doom lifted the third and fourth legs on her left flank and shot out four insect eggs. Two of the eggs were purple and black, while the other two were slightly larger and blue and purple.","Previously, one of the insect eggs produced enough insects to take over and handle the eruption of dead spirits. This time, the might of four insect eggs instantly buried the blast of dead spirits, and the situation was under control in an instant.","At first, Doom thought she had done well. She had no idea that Keira had already cursed her multiple times to herself, This idiot! It handled the dead spirits instantaneously! It didn’t put on any show or demonstrate the effects of a clash!"]},{"number":2676,"title":"Chapter 2676 Sea of Insects Under the Startling Lines Continent!","paragraphs":["2676 Sea of Insects Under the Startling Lines Continent!","What if Lin Yuan felt that these dead spirits were easy to deal with? The other experts he had under his control were also capable of killing dead spirits!","At this point, Keira’s gaze on Doom was downright nasty.","Doom had not managed to understand what Keira wanted. This meant that she had gone against Keira’s wishes twice.","This made Keira livid.","If Lin Yuan did not currently need the female insects that were born from consuming the dead dimensional lifeforms’ genes, Keira would have already taught Doom a lesson to appease the fury she felt.","While Keira was stewing in her anger, Lin Yuan sincerely complimented her, “The demon insects is indeed strong. There are many more dead spirits beneath the Startling Lines Continent than the Radiance Federation.","“When the Land Imps go to remove the metal-type stone boards, the five female insects can quickly reproduce, and Wen Yu will deliver the demon insects with reproductive abilities to various parts of the main world.”","Keira finally relaxed when she heard Lin Yuan’s praise. Her displeasure towards Doom also subsided significantly.","If Lin Yuan removed the metal-type stone boards from the entire Startling Lines Continent, the demon insects would definitely be able to unleash the full force of their combat power and show Lin Yuan the fierceness of the demon insects.","It was because she knew that Lin Yuan really wanted to protect the main world that Keira had decided to allow the five demon insect eggs to absorb the dead dimensional lifeforms’ genetic model before reproducing. Otherwise, she would have just laid two to three eggs.","“Master, now that I am aware of your goal, the demon insects will do our best to reproduce in a way that will benefit your goal! Compared to the alien insects, we demon insects have much stronger reproductive abilities!”","Keira made this guarantee while she instructed the other four demon insects to send the insect eggs underground and begin consuming the dead spirits there.","Occasionally, a newly born demon insect with a Class 3 or 2 Genetic Lock would emerge from the hold. All of them had the demon insects’ reproductive abilities.","Each time a newly born demon insect appeared, Wen Yu used the Elemental Paper’s ability to send it to a certain area in the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan had started dealing with the dead spirits in the Radiance Federation even before Qin Yu had arrived with the Land Imps!","By now, Lin Yuan fully believed what Keira had said.","Due to his contract with Keira, Lin Yuan could sense where the demon insects were located.","The demon insects already occupied a space underground that had a diameter of over 60 meters and had begun reproducing and colonizing.","The five female demon insects had only sent their eggs into the hole but had not entered personally. If they had, their power and reproductive abilities would be even stronger!","He had already found a counter for the move that Tower Canon had just made. Lin Yuan was very curious to find out if Tower Canon would come up with another move to try and fix this.","Lin Yuan did not have to wait for long. Qin Yu and the Land Imps had already rushed over.","Qin Yu bowed deeply when he saw Lin Yuan.","“Young Master, as per your instructions, I have brought all the Land Imps over from the Startling Lines Continent. Do you want them to start removing the metal-type stone boards now?”","Lin Yuan nodded and replied, “That’s right. Let them begin removing the metal-type stone boards now! Remember to start from the center and move outwards. Keira will communicate with you on how fast the removal should proceed.”","Lin Yuan looked at Keira.","She was the demon insects’ strongest female and was capable of controlling all the demon insects.","The demon insects she produced only listened to her. Given the circumstances, it would be the most appropriate for her to be the one to communicate with the Land Imps. This would ensure that the rate at which the insect army was consuming the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms matched the rate at which the Land Imps were removing the metal-type stone boards.","If the Land Imps removed the metal-type stone boards quicker than the rate at which the demon insects reproduced, the dead spirits and dimensional lifeforms would become a danger for the humans living in Thick Soil City.","Lin Yuan had put a lot of effort and resources into building Thick Soil City, so he did not want anything to happen to it.","With Keira’s intelligence, she was able to communicate smoothly with the Land Imps.","These Land Imps were all under Lin Yuan’s control. He never neglected to provide them with benefits. Otherwise, they would not be as submissive and willing to work hard. All of them knew that there were benefits to being part of Lin Yuan’s camp.","Thus, none of them wanted to cause trouble while working with Keira.","Keira personally set aside a space for the Land Imps, and the head Land Imps began dismantling the metal-type stone boards there.","A large amount of metal-type spiritual ingredients was separated from the metal-type stone boards and transformed into resources that Lin Yuan could use in any other way he wanted.","At first, the Land Imps thought that this would be a very time-consuming task.","The Land Imps were acutely aware of how terrifying the dimensional lifeforms were.","When the concentrated death aura made contact with a living creature, its muscles would immediately start to decay.","There were many Land Imps that had suffered due to the death aura emanating from the dead dimensional lifeforms.","Luckily, there were many Turning Wheel Realm Dictators stationed around the Dead Spirits Wells. Once they encountered a dead dimensional lifeform, they would kill them immediately and toss the corpse into the Dead Spirits Wells.","The vines around the Dead Spirits Wells and the Death-Cleansing Scale Snakes would then handle the rest and finally get the situation under control.","The Land Imps were already astonished that the demon insects could deal with the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms.","However, Keira expanded the area, and even with all the Land Imps working at maximum effort, they only just managed to match the rate at which the demon insects were consuming the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms.","The demon insects were moving with such ferocity that everything was progressing swiftly.","This did not mean that the insects produced by the female demon insects would be able to fully address all the dead spirits in the Startling Lines Continent. It was not so easy to clear out the dead spirits!","With the Startling Lines Continent’s long history, the number of lifeforms that had died were millions of times more than the number that was still alive. It was just that the dead spirits were being awakened in waves.","Keira just needed to keep the demon insects with Class 3 and 2 Genetic Locks at the lowest depths, and they would form a shield that also enabled the insect army to expand freely.","Meanwhile, the Land Imps would protect the surface.","As more and more dead dimensional lifeforms were consumed, Keira managed to fully examine the dead dimensional lifeforms’ powers.","Keira did not know if Lin Yuan was already aware of the dead dimensional lifeforms’ full powers, but nothing bad could come out of her reporting what she had found out to him.","“Master, these dead dimensional lifeforms have very similar auras to that of the dimensional worlds attached to a Class 3 world. Their powers and genes are similar as well.","“Didn’t you mention that you think Tower Canon is from another world? If my guess is right, Tower Canon is from a dimensional world attached to a Class 3 world. Not every Class 3 world becomes fully fused with the dimensional worlds attached to it when it is promoted. Some dimensional worlds that are sufficiently powerful can escape the fusing. These dimensional lifeforms will try to sink their world and cause it to fall into another world.","“However, this method is very dangerous. If it fails, the dimensional world will become suspended in a half-world state and will be at risk of being swallowed by dimensional storms. I think that this is what is happening to the dead spirits. If the dead dimensional world really arrived here after sinking their world, they should have landed in a world that is of a similar class to their original world.","“I have no idea how they ended up in a Class 1 world. They either used a treasure that can break through the walls between worlds, or this world already contained a presence that is beyond a Class 3 world.","“This faction has already broken past the walls between worlds. However, they decided to close one eye and did not eliminate Tower Canon, who arrived here after sinking their world. I think that there is a high chance that this faction is Epoch God Palace.","“Otherwise, there is no other reason to explain why Tower Canon lost to Epoch God Palace! Do you think this makes sense?”","Keira’s intention was to report the facts to Lin Yuan. She did not expect her words to make Lin Yuan feel as though he was seeing the truth!","Keira came from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. She might not have as many resources as him, but he could not hope to catch up to her in knowledge and experience. This was because Lin Yuan had not had the chance to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. His perception was limited to that of a Class 2 world.","Keira’s broad horizons made up for Lin Yuan’s lack of knowledge and experience. For the first time, Lin Yuan got a sense of Epoch God Palace’s level of power.","Epoch God Palace was undeniably an immense faction that Lin Yuan would struggle to match up to.","Lin Yuan could not help but worry about this.","Lin Yuan already knew everything about Tower Canon’s plan. There was a high chance that they wanted to revive the sunken dimensional world.","However, Lin Yuan was still completely oblivious to Epoch God Palace’s goal.","Epoch God Palace had come to this Class 1 world earlier than Tower Canon. Otherwise, Tower Canon would not have been able to arrive in this Class 1 world.","The real extraordinary anomaly in this world was Epoch God Palace!","“Keira, how powerful do you think Tower Canon’s strongest dimensional lifeform is?”","Keira pondered for a moment before she replied, “For a dimensional world attached to a Class 3 world to be able to sink itself, this dimensional world has to be extremely powerful. However, it won’t be stronger than a Class 3 main world.","“Otherwise, it wouldn’t have needed to sink itself. Hence, the strongest dimensional lifeforms will definitely be World Emperor grade and divine world level but won’t be stronger than World Emperor grade and pinnacle divine world level!”","Keira’s estimate was very safe. She believed that Tower Canon’s experts’ powers would not be able to reach World Emperor grade and pinnacle divine kingdom level. Otherwise, they would not have to act this cautiously.","Lin Yuan nodded.","The World Emperor grade and divine kingdom level was the standard to which lifeforms were measured in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Based on the measurement for dimensional lifeforms, it would be the Afterlife Realm.","This meant that the strongest of the real Eight Pages of Tower Canon would only be the equivalent of a pinnacle Afterlife Realm Dictator.","When Lin Yuan fused with the Abyss Red Lotus and used the ability Lotus Locks the World, he could exceed World Emperor grade and divine kingdom level.","If it truly came to blows, Tower Canon would be no match for him.","However, this conclusion was solely based on Keira’s deduction. There was no certainty that she was right.","This was because she had been asleep for numerous years. Secondly, Tower Canon had already been in the main world for many years. Who could say that the real Eight Pages had not increased their power?","While Lin Yuan was thinking, Wen Yu could not be busier.","She had delivered many demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks.","Each delivery she made exceeded the Radiance Federation’s needs.","With the demon insects’ powers, only a few of them would be sufficient to take control of a Dead Spirits Well.","This was not because Wen Yu had an optimistic view. Rather, she preferred to take a pessimistic mindset so she could always prepare for the worst. This would prevent her from panicking and being left at a loss if the worst-case scenario did come into play.","Not only would the demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks be enough to solve the Radiance Federation’s issue, but they could also become the solution for the other dimensional worlds once they were delivered there.","A thought struck Wen Yu, and she asked, “Keira, can you produce demon insects that can handle dead spirits and absorb death aura underwater?”","Keira looked at Wen Yu. She knew Wen Yu’s place by Lin Yuan’s side. Hence, she dared not show Wen Yu any disrespect and hurriedly said, “70% of the demon insects’ offspring is made up of our own genes. The other 30% comes from the genetic model of other lifeforms. As long as we can get our hands on dead dimensional lifeforms that can do battle underwater, the female insects will be able to produce demon insects with Class 2 Genetic Locks and clean up the dead spirits and death aura from the seas.","“Even if we can’t find dimensional lifeforms that are able to do battle underwater, dead spirits that can do battle underwater will be fine as well. However, the female insects will only be able to produce demon insects with Class 3 Genetic Locks from dead spirits.","“I am sure you have seen for yourself the difference in the demon insects’ powers that come from the different Genetic Locks classes. If you need such demon insects, I can send one female insect specifically to produce such demon insects.”","Wen Yu did not respond. Instead, she looked at Lin Yuan.","She had asked this question on Lin Yuan’s behalf and to give him a reminder. The main world would not be saved just by dealing with the dead spirits on land!","The seas were already contaminated by death aura. When the seawater evaporated, they would also move towards the land and spread death aura there.","Wen Yu had realized early on that saving the sea clans and water world lifeforms were also part of saving the main world and Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan instructed Keira, “Keira, send out a female demon insect. Someone will soon send over the dead dimensional lifeforms and dead spirits that can do battle underwater. For now, order the female insect to enter a reproductive state!”"]},{"number":2677,"title":"Chapter 2677 Progress of the Sped-Up Demon Insects!","paragraphs":["2677 Progress of the Sped-Up Demon Insects!","Lin Yuan had been fully focused on saving the Radiance Federation and had not stopped to consider whether the demon insects would also be effective at helping the seas.","Wen Yu’s question had indeed prompted him, and Keira’s answer excited him.","The female insects produced by Keira could produce demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks that would be able to clear death aura from the sea. This was great!","This way, not only would the problems in the water world be solved, but the water world lifeforms and sea clans would also be saved. The environment in the sea would also be cleaned up.","The sea would also become an incubator for the demon insects.","Lin Yuan could not only use the demon insects to save the world but also take advantage of the dead spirits crisis to nurture and strengthen the demon insects. The strengthened demon insects would become another secret weapon that he could utilize when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The Land Imps worked according to the areas that Keira had mapped out, and the ground of the Startling Lines Continent was slowly revealed. Previously, the ground had been brown or black. But after being contaminated by death aura, the ground had turned grayish-black. The warped soil could also release death aura.","Luckily, the demon insects were continuously consuming the death aura from underground. Otherwise, the Land Imps would have become infected, their bodies would start to decay, and their lifespans would be shortened!","It was clear that the situation had been handled. But just to be on the safe side, Lin Yuan instructed Red Thorn to station the Abyss Great Emperor by Keira’s side so he could protect her if any threats cropped up. Keira’s own body was not very strong. She would not be able to endure being attacked by an expert!","If anything happened to Keira, the demon insects would not be able to continue reproducing and expanding.","Liu Jie said with awe, “Lin Yuan, we have managed to counter Tower Canon’s second move. But I don’t think they will back down so easily! They must have other moves planned.”","Lin Yuan could not dispute Liu Jie on this and nodded.","If this was all that Tower Canon had up their sleeve, they would not be trying to take over the main world! There was no way that a dimensional world that used to be attached to a Class 3 world would be so easy to handle!","That said, the demon insects’ abilities were only just beginning to develop. From here on out, it would be a clash between the demon insects and Tower Canon.","Keira was not powerful on her own. But after the demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks absorbed death aura, they could increase their own power endlessly! All they needed was some time to develop, and their power would be able to climb rapidly.","It would not take long before the demon insects became a force to be reckoned with and turned the tide on the dead spirits crisis. The dead dimensional world saw the demon insects as threats, but the demon insects saw the dead dimensional lifeforms as food. The two sides had different stances and saw each other from different perspectives.","Since the issue had been perfectly resolved, Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan would take Keira back with him. Three of the five demon insects would be left in the Startling Lines Continent to continue expanding the insect army, while the other two would be sent to the seas to help the sea clans and water world dimensional lifeforms.","Although Lin Yuan had already done all that he could do to help, both the sea clans and water world dimensional lifeforms suffered grievous losses.","With the demon insects helping the Vast Sea Labyrinth, all of the sea clans would be saved, and they would not become extinct during the sixth epoch.","When Keira found out about Lin Yuan’s plans, she immediately made the arrangements. Doom, whom Keira was the most displeased with, was left in the Startling Lines Continent and would be in charge of covering the center territory. The other two would be sent to the north and south territories to build up their insect armies while still periodically sending demon insects to the Radiance Federation.","The remaining two female insects, who were the ones that Keira most favored, were sent to the seas. There were far more dead spirits in the sea than in the Startling Lines Continent, so the work would be very cushy there!","The two female demon insects could not be more thrilled.","Doom looked at Keira woefully. She did not understand why Keira had suddenly turned against her. Keira had picked her twice, and Doom felt that both her performances had been satisfactory.","When they were first hatched, her gene concentration had been the highest. Logically, she should be the most favored by Keira.","The center territory was almost completely empty of demon insects now. There were the least dead spirits there in the entire Startling Lines Continent. If she went there, the insect army she produced would be the smallest of all the female demon insects.","The insect queens of the demon insects competed with each other in terms of the size of their colonies. Those with larger colonies also had higher statuses!","But as wronged as Doom felt, she did not utter a word for fear of saying something that made Keira even more upset.","When Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, he went directly to the Radiant Moon Palace.","The Moon Empress was sipping tea in the inner palace while reading reports.","The demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks immediately began building colonies once they were delivered to an area. Then, they started absorbing the death aura around their colonies and feasting on the dead spirits as a means of fueling their reproduction rates.","The insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks were considered derivative female insects and were also very capable of reproduction.","Even the regions with relatively weaker defenses no longer had any other injuries or deaths once the demon insects arrived!","Almost half of the Radiance Federation’s pressure disappeared. The Radiance Federation’s troops could finally take a break.","Cicada Song immediately ordered the Radiance Federation’s troops to rest while sending the spirit qi professionals who had just been trained to heal injuries caused by death aura to treat all of the Radiance Federation’s troops.","Cicada Song and the Moon Empress came to an agreement after a discussion.","Although the demon insects provided a solution, the dead spirits crisis still posed just as much danger to the main world as it always had.","The dead dimensional lifeforms had appeared after the dead spirits crisis had progressed to a certain extent. No one could say if there would be other special dead spirits appearing in the future.","In order to overcome this obstacle, the Radiance Federation would have to boost its own power and could not rely on others for everything!","This was not because the Radiance Federation did not trust Lin Yuan enough to use his secret weapons but because they needed to set a proper position.","If they relied on Lin Yuan for everything instead of boosting themselves, the Radiance Federation would not be able to handle any external conflicts in the future.","Cicada Song had heard from the Moon Empress that Lin Yuan’s sights were not limited to the Radiance Federation or the main world but to a higher-level world.","There was no way that the main world would have access to Lin Yuan’s protection at all times.","Cicada Song knew that a large reason for the Moon Empress mentioning this was that she did not want Lin Yuan to have to bear the burden of holding up the main world on his own. Additionally, she wanted the Radiance Federation to use this opportunity to become stronger.","They had already begun rolling out the changes to the Creation Master system.","The Moon Empress intended to give out all of her resources to use this opportunity to build up the overall power of the Radiance Federation’s troops.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection that had been postponed by Liu Wencheng also had to be commenced!","The Moon Empress intended to use the next six months to breathe new life into the Radiance Federation!","When she saw Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress said, “Little Yuan, your demon insects are a godsend! Without the demon insects, the entire main world would be on the brink of ruin! For the past few days, the reports sent by the various federations have all been positive.","“Currently, the biggest problem facing the Radiance Federation is that the death aura can spread to the land from the sea. The cities next to the seas have not been fully freed from the threat yet. I sent many demon insects to the seaside to absorb death aura, but this isn’t a long-term solution!”","Lin Yuan hurriedly said, “Master, the issue that you are worried about has already been solved. You don’t have to worry about it anymore! Not only will the demon insects be able to eliminate the dead spirits from land, but they will be just as effective in the sea!","“I have already sent two female demon insects into the sea to develop and build colonies that will clean up the environment in the sea. You should be hearing of the effects in a day or two! Once the issue in the sea is solved, the territories near the sea will all benefit. Based on my estimation, the main world will be able to enjoy at least three months of peace. Even if Tower Canon comes up with other moves, they won’t be able to threaten the Radiance Federation anytime soon. The Radiance Federation can develop with a peace of mind!”","The three months that Lin Yuan estimated was not a number he had pulled out from the air.","Instead, he had communicated with Keira and learned that the demon insects were stronger than the dimensional lifeforms from a dimensional world attached to a Class 3 world.","Keira was able to control the demon insects and handle the dead spirits. Otherwise, Keira would not dare to be so confident in this matter that was so important to Lin Yuan.","Frankly, Keira’s estimate had been six months. This was because she had sensed the ley lines and deduced that there would be an explosion of death aura six months later. At that time, there would be a tsunami of dead spirits being awakened.","However, Keira was not concerned by the explosion of dead spirits because if she was able to develop the demon insects with full force during the next six months, it was likely that the demon insects would be able to cover every corner of the main world!","At that time, there might be as many demon insects as there were dead spirits.","However, Lin Yuan would never allow her to develop the demon insects with full force. If she did so, it would leave no space for the other lifeforms in the main world to live.","Lin Yuan dared not be careless when it came to safety issues. He was also worried that what he said would impact the Moon Empress’ arrangements.","Thus, Lin Yuan shortened the six-month estimate to three months. From now on, they could only observe quietly.","During this time, the Radiance Federation’s development would not be halted, nor would that of the demon insects.","This transitional period was critical.","Lin Yuan did not know when Tower Canon would receive the news.","With the demon insects consuming the waves of dead spirits and continuously reproducing, they would multiply rapidly.","The main world had just been promoted from a Class 1 to a Class 2 world, and the five dimensional worlds had been fused with the main world.","The humans from the main world only needed a very small proportion of the space to live and grow.","Lin Yuan would not permit the demon insects to take over the space meant for the humans to live in. However, he still intended for the demon insects to use the dead spirits crisis to expand.","All this activity would definitely catch Epoch God Palace’s attention and give Lin Yuan the opportunity to make contact with them.","Even if this matter did not appear on Epoch God Palace’s radar, once the demon insects occupied every corner of the main world, Lin Yuan would definitely be able to locate Epoch God Palace!","When the Moon Empress heard about the three months, she was overjoyed. The three months were a luxury for the Radiance Federation.","“Little Yuan, I will ask Liu Wencheng to proceed with the three rounds of selection. Recently, you have been running around for the main world’s sake. If you have more important things to do, you don’t need to participate!”","Lin Yuan hurriedly shook his head.","“Master, I have already made all the necessary arrangements. Only trivial matters are left. I don’t need to attend to them personally. My people can handle it. I will be there punctually to participate in the selection as a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","“I even nurtured Shiny, especially for the selection. I promised to take it into battle. If I don’t participate, I won’t be able to answer Shiny!”","Lin Yuan knew that the Moon Empress was looking out for him and was afraid that he was working too hard.","Firstly, he really wanted to participate in this selection. Secondly, he was well aware that this selection was meant to boost morale. He could not be absent!","The faith power that came from the Radiance Federation was almost half of the total amount that came from the other federations. This was enough to prove just how important Lin Yuan was to the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan did not want to break his word to Shiny, nor did he want to let down the lifeforms in the Radiance Federation who trusted and respected him.","The Moon Empress stood up and helped Lin Yuan to adjust his collar.","“Little Yuan, all of the Radiance Federation’s royalty will be present during the selection. I will be able to watch you climb to the top!”","The Moon Empress would not have said this if she did not know that Lin Yuan’s power had an advantage over Xia Qing, Zong Ze, and the rest. As things stood, his power could no longer be measured against the younger generation!","The Moon Empress had never seen Lin Yuan in battle, but she was certain that she would not have assured victory if she ever fought against him.","If Lin Yuan was not sufficiently powerful, he would not have been able to gather so many experts around him or safeguard the Radiance Federation’s peace.","The Moon Empress’ words to Lin Yuan were not one of wishes and hopes but stated facts.","Based on his contributions to the Radiance Federation and his power, he deserved to become a Radiance Envoy!","The Radiance Federation’s 13 members of royalty had not even contributed to the dead spirits crisis as much as Lin Yuan had.","Lin Yuan nodded.","The demon insects could be said to be the dead spirits’ natural enemies. Once the demon insects entered the battle, the dead spirits crisis would be shortened significantly.","The final battle between him and Tower Canon was not as far off as initially expected!"]},{"number":2678,"title":"Chapter 2678 Waves Before the Selections!","paragraphs":["2678 Waves Before the Selections!","In an office, a girl with sweet features wearing a double-breasted suit and light makeup told more than ten people sitting around a meeting table, “It’s up to our team to organize the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. Do not allow yourselves to be slack!","“If anything goes wrong, we won’t be able to answer to the citizens of the Radiance Federation! This is the biggest challenge our team will face since its establishment. It will also be a chance for us to demonstrate our skills.","“All of you are exclusive reporters for the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. You can do what you do best and communicate with the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence that you are in contact with. Do your best to bring up the spirit and enthusiasm of the selections.”","The girl who spoke was Tian Ningning.","Previously, Tian Ningning had insisted on being Black’s exclusive reporter. Later, Black and Lin Yuan were revealed to be the same person. This made Tian Ningning the exclusive reporter of Lin Yuan, who was also the Moon Empress’ disciple.","It was said that even the most mundane people are not excluded from opportunities to ascend. Lin Yuan had not especially promoted Tian Ningning. But this did not stop her from being promoted by Star Web’s managers.","Tian Ningning was also capable enough to handle the responsibility of leading this special team that had been put together by Star Web.","The few tasks that Tian Ningning had already led had been completed extremely well.","“Sister Ning, we won’t have any issues contacting the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. But you will have to be the one to get in contact with Lin Yuan! All eyes are on Lin Yuan for this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and ranking. Every citizen in the Radiance Federation is looking forward to watching him battle.”","Tian Ningning nodded and said, “I will communicate with Lin Yuan. The rest of you just need to focus on your own tasks. Don’t forget the gravity of this matter. Do not come up with false information for the sake of dramatic effect. I’m sure all of you understand what I’m getting at! If you mess this up, you can leave Star Web of your own accord!”","After she was done relaying instructions and tasks, everyone left until the only one left in the meeting room was Tian Ningning, who was still standing in front of the podium.","She was now part of Star Web’s board of directors. She was also the youngest member.","She was under immense pressure daily. Tian Ningning felt that her promotion was solely due to the fact that she was Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter. If she could not do a good job, she would be embarrassing him.","Although she did not have any close ties with Lin Yuan in real life, the people on Star Web were not aware of this.","Tian Ningning felt as though the past two years had been a dream.","Black had caught her eye, and she wanted to be his exclusive reporter because she had noticed his potential. Additionally, she admired the spirit he had exhibited when he protected Millstone Town on his own.","The power that Black later showed had shocked Tian Ningning, and she got the feeling that there was more to his background than what met the eye.","However, she never expected Black to turn out to be the Moon Empress, a Class 6 Creation Master’s disciple!","A person like this should be walking around with his chest puffed up with arrogance. But whenever she sent him a message, he was either too busy to respond or was always polite and sincere when he did.","Tian Ningning had not been in contact with Lin Yuan for a very long time.","The Moon Empress had only revealed a very small fraction of Lin Yuan’s contributions to the Radiance Federation. However, this was already enough for many people in the Radiance Federation to address him as ‘Your Excellency’.","Even now, Tian Ningning did not know if Lin Yuan would be participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Something like this should seem insignificant to Lin Yuan!","Given Tian Ningning’s status, she did not have the right to obtain a Thoughts Letter Paper. The only way she could contact Lin Yuan was through the phone. If he was not in the Radiance Federation, she would not be able to reach him.","Now that Lin Yuan was back in the Radiance Federation, he still had the habit of using his phone. However, everyone else had become accustomed to using the Thoughts Letter Paper and even used it to arrange meetings.","Thus, Lin Yuan’s phone only rang a few times, and most of these calls had come from the Moon Empress.","Lin Yuan was currently eating lunch. Liu Jie had made a fish stew that really suited Lin Yuan’s tastes.","Because of Epoch God Palace, Lin Yuan had not been able to relax. However, the might demonstrated by the demon insects allowed Lin Yuan to be more at ease, and he finally had a rare moment of rest.","When he picked up the call and saw the caller ID, he could not help but smile and raise an eyebrow. He had been expecting Tian Ningning to call in the next day or two.","Lin Yuan had a very good impression of Lin Yuan.","It was rare for a reporter to not exaggerate or come up with fake news. When Tian Ningning was reporting on him, the duel records she wrote were still very exciting.","She was a large reason why Lin Yuan was able to collect so much faith power early on.","Tian Ningning calling him was also part of her work.","Since Lin Yuan had chosen Tian Ningning to be his exclusive Star Web reporter, it was his responsibility to find work for her.","When he picked up the call, Lin Yuan heard Tian Ningning’s slightly anxious voice on the other end, “Your Excellency, I would just like to confirm if you intend to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. If you are, I need to make preparations as soon as possible!”","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he replied honestly, “Not only am I going to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection but also in the Radiance Envoy selection. As my exclusive reporter, you will be busy for some time!”","Tian Ningning was stunned, but she found it difficult to contain her delight. She did not mind being busy. Rather, she was afraid that Lin Yuan would not give her the opportunity to be busy.","Lin Yuan had not fought on Star Web using any of his identities recently. Thus, Tian Ningning had not had much work to do.","If Tian Ningning had not been chosen to become the leader of a special team in Star Web, she would be spending most of her days drinking tea and reading books in her office!","Luckily, exclusive reporters had stable incomes even if they did not have work on their hands.","This was why so many well-known reporters were willing to become exclusive reporters for the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","“Your Excellency, I am now leading a team. If there are any pressing matters to handle, my team can help out! It will be easier for me to make the proper arrangements if I know what is happening over on your end!”","This was the first time that Lin Yuan heard Tian Ningning address him as ‘Your Excellency’. At first, he thought she had misspoken. But when she addressed him like that a second time, he realized that she had not misspoken.","He hurriedly corrected her.","“Big Sister Tian, I am not a member of royalty. I am just an official member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. I won’t be worthy of being addressed like that even if I do become a Radiance Envoy.","“Don’t call me that in the future! I have a few people with me who don’t have exclusive Star Web reporters, but they will be playing large roles in the selections. Big Sister Tian, will your team be able to take on the responsibility of doing publicity for them?”","Tian Ningning knew that Lin Yuan was trying to boost her.","Tian Ningning could guess who Lin Yuan was referring to. It was likely that he was referring to Chief Guard Ye, Chef Supreme, and the Bamboo Monarch’s disciples. They were the only ones whose statuses kept Star Web reporters away.","Otherwise, any young person who was a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would have throngs of Star Web reporters trying to connect with them.","Even the famous Star Web hosts also had exclusive reporters documenting their dueling records!","If she did a good job of this opportunity, she would become the golden child of all the Star Web reporters.","However, there were only slightly more than ten people in her special team. She could not be certain that there would be enough people to complete this task to perfection.","For the sake of her future, Tian Ningning would not agree to something without full confidence. She had to answer to Lin Yuan, who was the disciple of a member of royalty!","“Lord Lin Yuan, in all honesty, my team isn’t large. With a little more than ten people, we will only be able to follow up on three people at most. How many people do you have in mind, with you included?”","Lin Yuan immediately said, “There are a total of eight of us. Big Sister Tian, why don’t you go and speak to the Star Web officials about this? I believe that they will give you more help!”","Tian Ningning became so excited that she started to shake.","If she brought up this proposal to the Star Web officials, they would never agree.","She might be Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter, but she had not been able to obtain an interview with him. The higher-ups of Star Web were always displeased at her over this. She was aware of this.","However, given Lin Yuan’s status, the higher-ups of Star Web could not act on their displeasure and still had to provide her with resources.","But this time, Lin Yuan was the one making the proposal. Once she mentioned this, Star Web’s officials would not turn down her request.","Tian Ningning always wanted to witness Lin Yuan’s growth. However, he grew at such an accelerated rate that even the Moon Empress could not track the exact trajectory, much less Tian Ningning!","Lin Yuan was not an ostentatious person. He had made this decision after careful contemplation.","Since he was going to raise the Radiance Federation’s morale, it would be a good idea for the Star Web reporters to release updated reports of the fights.","After hanging up the call, Lin Yuan rested for an entire day in the Return from Faraway Mansion and spent time with all the feys he had contracted.","On the second day, he went with Liu Jie and Wen Yu to the Radiance Sacred Hall.","The Radiance Sacred Hall had already intended on commencing the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection.","All the preparations were already complete. Once the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence arrived, this year’s selection would begin immediately.","Normally, the best way to boost the Radiance Federation’s morale would be to prolong the selection period.","However, time was tight, and raising morale was a preliminary goal. They could not afford to waste time!","The Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections would be very formal and official. The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would be settled with a few dueling stages. This was because not every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would need to be challenged.","Liu Wencheng knew that all the attention of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would be on Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, Xia Qing, and Long Tao. It was difficult for the others to compete with the four of them.","The format of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection had changed this year. A live drill would be better than a duel for testing a person’s overall capabilities. Liu Wencheng had designed a similar format for this selection.","Previously, everyone would start off dueling. But once it winnowed down to the top ten, Liu Wencheng would send them into a simulated space in Star Web where they would compete in the wilderness!","There were no other entities in this survival battle. It would only be the top ten members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence battling it out with each other.","The first to die would become Sequence #10, and the subsequent ranks would also be determined in this manner.","Firstly, it was easier to spectate a wilderness survival battle. Secondly, this would be able to test the interpersonal skills of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. There were times when connections were just as effective as power!","After ending the call with Lin Yuan, Tian Ningning went to see the manager of Star Web’s reporters and told him about the call.","The manager immediately held an emergency meeting before assigning four special teams to Tian Ningning.","She could allocate and utilize these teams as she saw fit. It was necessary that she ensured that all eight people’s reports would be done to perfection.","Liu Hao, who was the manager of Star Web’s reporters, had not paid much attention to Tian Ningning.","It was true that she was Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter. However, he felt that she had asked Lin Yuan for the job.","Liu Hao was good friends with Zuo Ming and learned about Lin Yuan’s character from him. He knew that Lin Yuan did not put on any airs and was respectful towards everyone he met. He did not have any of the arrogance that was usually associated with a young elite.","Hence, Liu Hao believed that if anyone else had asked Lin Yuan for the job, he would also have agreed.","Yet, Lin Yuan had given such a major opportunity to Tian Ningning.","Regardless of whether Lin Yuan thought highly of Tian Ningning’s abilities or because he had connections with her, Liu Hao began taking Tian Ningning seriously!","Not only did Liu Hao assign four special teams to Tian Ningning, but he also joined her to help her manage the tasks. Joining this job would also be an opportunity for him."]},{"number":2679,"title":"Chapter 2679 Selections Begin!","paragraphs":["2679 Selections Begin!","Liu Hao was not satisfied with being the manager of Star Web’s reporters for the rest of his life.","If he performed well in this job, he should be promoted to become the sixth manager of Star Web, making him the head honcho of Star Web!","“Ningning, you have been working under me for some time now. I’m sure you have noticed how I have always taken good care of you. I am assigning such an important task to you and even sent four teams to assist you","“You must do a good job. Do not disappoint me! If you encounter any problems, let me know immediately, and I’ll handle it myself! Young people are always slightly reckless. Don’t overextend yourself!”","Liu Hao knew that Tian Ningning was smart. She would definitely be able to understand his meaning. Given her intelligence, she would know what the right course of action would be.","His joining of the team did not affect Tian Ningning negatively at all. Rather, he was a form of insurance.","Tian Ningning was momentarily stunned before she said seriously, “Big Brother Hao, it is a little much for someone as young as me to be leading even one special team. Something will probably go awry while I’m leading the five special teams! I know you trust me, but I would still like for you to be present. That will give me more confidence to make bolder decisions!”","Tian Ningning had been a Star Web reporter for three years. With her talent and capabilities, it would be a breeze for her to lead a special team and complete the task. As long as she had sufficient manpower to allocate, there was nothing that was impossible.","Tian Ningning only said this because she had picked up on the hints that Liu Hao was giving her.","Given that he was the biggest boss amongst the Star Web reporters, Tian Ningning needed to extend the proper courtesies to him.","Furthermore, his joining was enough to show just how important this matter was to Star Web. It was a job that would benefit Lin Yuan.","There was no reason for Tian Ningning to refuse.","From now on, whatever happened in the future, Star Web would inject resources into her team first to ensure that they could produce the best reports.","Liu Hao glanced at Tian Ningning, and his smile widened.","She really was clever!","Liu Hao really liked communicating with smart people like Tian Ningning. He did not have to make everything explicit and only needed to raise the key points!","With Tian Ningning’s intelligence and her link to Lin Yuan, Liu Hao decided to make her his close subordinate and do his best to elevate her in the future. Her abilities had already been proven. Out of all the Star Web reporters, she was already ahead of the pack.","“Since you put it that way, I shall be the main lead for this team. However, you will have the decision-making power when it comes to following up and collating the progress of the event. Go ahead and do what you think is right. As long as you do well, the job of the manager of Star Web’s reporters will be yours next year!”","Tian Ningning did not care about these. All she wanted was to do a good job of being Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter.","The special team that she had been leading had been organizing all the information related to the dead spirits crisis. This was a job that Tian Ningning found to be very meaningful.","After the information about the dead spirits was organized, the low-rank spirit qi professionals would not be completely helpless when they faced the dead spirits.","...","Because of the high priority that the Radiance Federation placed on keeping the regular people safe, there were very few citizen casualties in the cities, even if the most remote ones, as long as no dimensional rifts opened.","But even if dimensional rifts did open, the city’s City Guards would immediately send experts to fight as well as provide medical treatment.","It could be said that the Radiance Federation had been living in relative peace and prosperity.","This did not mean much in Lin Yuan’s previous world, but this was a very rare culture in the world of feys.","In this regard, the Radiance Federation did a better job than both the Azure Federation and Freedom Federation!","Star Web, which was created by the coordinated abilities of three sacred source lifeforms, made the lives of the regular people even better and created a second world for the Radiance Federation.","The biggest change to take place in the Radiance Federation came from the opening of the Class 6 abyss dimensional rift as it led to the Radiance Federation’s royalty ordering the cities’ City Lords to build mirror cities in the Class 6 abyss dimensional rift.","People were always at least a little afraid of the unknown. This especially applied to the powerless and those who struggled to survive.","But just because they were afraid did not mean that they were stupid. It did not take long for them to understand why the members of royalty wanted to build mirror cities in the abyssal world.","The Radiance Federation’s territory was vast and had an abundance of resources. However, as adventurers continued to explore and harvest resources, the Radiance Federation’s resource endowment eventually fell. Although many of these resources were renewable, it would take time.","As the Radiance Federation’s dwindling resources continued to be harvested, the adventurers’ wages would fall, and the price of Creation Master resources would rise. Once the price of Creation Master resources increased, the cost of living for the Radiance Federation’s citizens would increase as well.","The best choice now would be to expand the territory and begin harvesting resources from the new areas.","The only issue had been the factions that made their living from fire-type spiritual ingredients. They had been severely impacted by the construction of the mirror cities in the abyssal world.","The Radiance Federation’s Cultivated Garden decided not to provide aid to these factions that were losing out due to the changing times. Rather, they opened up a new path for them by making them their business partners. As a result, they were developing better than they were before.","As the mirror cities in the abyssal world were constructed, more and more of the Radiance Federation’s citizens moved to the abyssal world. They brought with them many industries that supported even more livelihoods.","This was a positive structural change. Once the Radiance Federation crossed the initial slightly uncomfortable adjustment period, it would be able to thrive and grow in new ways.","However, the dead spirits crisis was not a structural change. It was only a catastrophe.","Although there had been warnings before this catastrophe, even rising factions struggled to deal with the dead spirits crisis, much less individual people.","Death aura poured out from the Dead Spirits Wells endlessly and claimed life after life.","This was an issue that Lin Yuan and the Radiance Federation’s royalty worked tirelessly to address.","The dead spirits had not been going on for very long, but it had already caused widespread damage that threatened to collapse the Radiance Federation.","The situation was only contained after Wen Yu sent the demon insects into battle. For now, the danger of this calamity had been mostly neutralized.","At this moment, Radiance Sacred Hall announced that they were going to hold the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. The Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections would also be brought forward.","This would be the grandest event in the Radiance Federation, and it immediately caught the attention of all of the Radiance Federation’s citizens.","Moreover, Chef Supreme had planted the Soldier Ration Radishes in various cities so the Radiance Federation’s citizens could all claim the Soldier Ration Radishes’ leaves to fill their stomachs.","Cultivated Garden had also distributed a mountain of resources while the Land Imps continued laying down the metal-type stone boards and fortifying houses.","All of this was part of rebuilding the Radiance Federation.","As Star Web continued to release reports, the Radiance Federation’s citizens became more and more excited for this selection.","Lin Yuan could sense that many of the glowing dots of faith in the fountain of faith in the divine kingdom were growing larger.","Lin Yuan had only become a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence last year. Since then, he had been extremely busy and had not participated in any of the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s meetings. Thus, many of the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members were strangers to him.","Although he did not know them, none of them were unfamiliar with him. He might only be Sequence #91, but the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence all saw him as having colossal power! He had even killed a Freedom Envoy!","Not even Chief Guard Ye’s disciple, Liu Jie, or Xia Qing possessed such abilities.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members were all very excited to watch the battle between Lin Yuan and Liu Jie, as well as between Lin Yuan and Xia Qing. It would definitely be an eye-opening experience.","All of them were the cream of the crop and had grown in the past year. They wanted to see just how large the gap between themselves and Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and the rest was.","Liu Wencheng sat on the main seat and smiled at Lin Yuan before nodding.","Next, he turned his gaze to Liu Jie.","He already knew that Night Leaning Moon wanted to use Liu Jie to unleash the ‘final weapon’ plan, but Liu Wencheng had never approved of this because Night Leaning Moon’s ‘final weapon’ plan asked too much of a spirit qi professional and it was difficult for a regular person to meet this standard.","Moreover, taking control of carcinoma feys was akin to dancing with death. If there were any accidents that caused the carcinoma feys to break free and lose control, the consequences would be unimaginable.","Many insect-species carcinoma feys did not seem scary before they had the chance to multiply and spread. But once they were able to expand into an army, they could potentially cause as much damage to the main world as the dead spirits!","It was when Liu Jie represented the Radiance Federation to battle the Freedom Envoys that Liu Wencheng found out that Liu Jie had perfectly accomplished the ‘final weapon’ plan that Night Leaning Moon had designed.","Not only could he command many carcinoma feys in battle, but he had a high degree of control over them. It was impossible for them to break free of his control.","The heart of the plan was the Insect Queen that Liu Jie had contracted. Once it died, the carcinoma feys would follow it in death.","This was both Liu Jie’s Achilles’ heel and his strength. Once he died, so would the Insect Queen, and the carcinoma feys would not be able to go rampant and bring forth a disaster!","By being willing to undertake the responsibility of turning himself into the ultimate weapon, Liu Jie truly deserved the title Heart of Insect Swarm!","Once the last members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence arrived, Liu Wencheng stood up and said solemnly, “Normally, the reranking is a private affair. But this time, it will be broadcast publicly on Star Web. All of you can make your preparations now. Later, we will enter the location specially designed by Star Web’s officials for our challenges. Every person will have three challenges.","“Mu Yan, who is Sequence #100, will go first. In the end, just like in the past, Sequence #90 to Sequence #100 will enter a simulated space to compete with the new generation of Radiance Hundred Sequence members.","“The top 90 ranks will each receive a Bronze/Legend fey that suits the Willpower Rune they have comprehended. If any of you have any secret weapons, take them out now. If you are found to be hiding them later, it will cost you a place among the top 90, and you will have to bear the losses yourselves!”","When the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence heard what Liu Wencheng said, they first bowed to him before they all entered Star Web together.","None of them expected this year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and reranking to have such prizes!","There were no prizes in the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selections and rerankings. All they received was some money and subsequent monthly wages in the form of resources. But all of the money and resources summed up would not be equivalent to the value of a Bronze/Legend fey.","Bronze/Legend feys were a specialty of Class 5 Creation Masters. Moreover, these Bronze/Legend feys would be custom-made to their individual Willpower Runes.","Many of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence came from elite families, but few had ever received such a gift!","Even Long Tao’s breathing picked up.","While Liu Wencheng was making these promises, his gaze drifted towards Lin Yuan.","It was likely that all these resources would be coming from Lin Yuan.","The Moon Empress was capable of supplying such resources, but she was fully focused on dealing with the death aura and would not have the time to tailor Bronze/Legend feys for the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Lin Yuan caught Liu Wencheng looking at him and gently pursed his lips.","It was true that Lin Yuan was the one providing these resources to the Radiance Hundred Sequence, but this was only the beginning. In the future, he would be providing even more resources to the best talents of the Radiance Federation to help them grow rapidly!","Lin Yuan intended to use his abilities and store of resources to help the Radiance Federation and main world to achieve true prosperity before he left. This was the only way he would be able to leave for the Sky Beyond the Clouds with his mind at ease.","Once the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence entered Star Web, all of them were fired up with passion. They would not allow themselves to be kicked out of the top 90 ranks!","All of them had witnessed last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence participate in the survival live drill.","In the face of the ocean of dimensional lifeforms, an individual’s strength was negligible.","A person’s power was only partly effective.","Even the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who were fully confident in their capabilities dared not be certain that they would be able to stay in the Radiance Hundred Sequence through the reranking after being pushed out from the top 90 ranks.","Moreover, every intelligent person knew that the true threat to the main world now was not dimensional lifeforms but dead spirits.","The dimensional lifeforms were now the humans’ allies in taking on the dead spirits.","So, it was unlikely that they would be facing dimensional lifeforms during this survival live drill. Instead, they would be facing dead spirits that released death aura!"]},{"number":2680,"title":"Chapter 2680 Battle in the Clouds!","paragraphs":["2680 Battle in the Clouds!","The current members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence all had a certain degree of understanding of the dead spirits.","Although Radiance Sacred Hall had not issued any tasks related to the dead spirits, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had all taken the initiative to head to the nearby Dead Spirits Wells to lend a helping hand. This was so they could train themselves and contribute to the Radiance Federation.","Every citizen of the Radiance Federation who made it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence possessed wholehearted sincerity.","Some of them were arrogant and had personality flaws, but at critical moments, they were all able to step up to the plate. Since they were models for the Radiance Federation’s younger generation, they had to take responsibility for this position.","It was because they understood the dead spirits that almost none of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence wanted to fight in a simulated environment filled with dead spirits.","It took a lot of time to build a stage in real life. It required both resources and labor.","But all that was needed to build a stage in Star Web was for the sacred source lifeforms that created Star Web to adjust the network of Star Web’s space.","Mystic Moon and the other two members of royalty had built a magnificent stage for this event.","Since they were going to boost morale, they needed the appropriate infrastructure!","After being transported, every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence arrived at their position on the glorious stone pillars that Radiance Sacred Hall had erected, specially for the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Since they were going to be competing online, all of the stone pillars were also moved to Star Web.","Lin Yuan stood on the stone pillar that had a diameter of three meters. All he could see around him were rolling clouds.","Lin Yuan could not help but raise his eyebrows at this sight.","This setting was very grand. Lin Yuan had stood on the real stone pillars in Radiance Sacred Hall before. When he looked down from the real stone pillars, he could clearly see what was happening on the ground.","But here in Star Web, the stone pillars were thousands of meters tall, and every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence felt as though they were standing among the clouds.","In order to become a powerful spirit qi professional, it was even possible to train oneself to become resistant to acrophobia.","There was a seat on the stone pillar, and Lin Yuan sat down leisurely and leaned back.","He believed that unless something abnormal happened, no one would challenge him.","He was Sequence #91. Once the nine new members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence chose their opponents, it would be Lin Yuan’s time to issue his challenges.","Liu Jie looked up and saw Long Tao, Liu Jie, and Xia Qing in the distance.","Lin Yuan did not intend to give up on the three battle challenges. He was going to make good use of them to invigorate the Radiance Federation’s morale.","It just so happened that Lin Yuan wanted to see how Long Tao, Liu Jie, and Xia Qing had improved.","Lin Yuan was aware of Long Tao’s power.","Long Tao had revealed his cards to Lin Yuan when Lin Yuan visited Coiling Dragon’s Valley. Long Tao’s main plan was to nurture the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus.","Long Tao had become an A-rank spirit qi professional. After the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus was evolved to Myth Breed, it activated the main-dragon-species bloodline that was dormant in its body and had become a highly aggressive terrifying-dragon-species fey.","After becoming a spirit qi professional but before he left the Xia Region, he never saw many large spectacles. The most astonishing and largest scale event was Dong Hai using his wolf-species fey to fend off the alien beast wave.","At that time, Lin Yuan had not been awed by the Platinum wolf-species fey but by the seemingly endless insect army that was unafraid of death.","After he left the Xia Region, Lin Yuan truly began walking down the path of a spirit qi professional.","When he arrived in the Royal Capital and saw the battle between Long Tao and Cai Cha, Lin Yuan understood for the first time what it meant to be a young elite. He also found his direction and motivation to work hard.","At that time, Long Tao had been like a shining star. Back then, with Lin Yuan’s level of power, all he could do was look up at Long Tao.","But now, Long Tao was no longer a match for Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan was the most familiar with Liu Jie, but Liu Jie had been developing in seclusion for the past six months. Lin Yuan had yet to witness the insect-species carcinoma feys that had been transformed into fairies wielding their power during battle.","As for Xia Qing, all Lin Yuan knew about her was that she was very strong. However, he was not aware of the exact degree and magnitude.","Lin Yuan was really looking forward to these three fights.","The member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence Liu Wencheng had mentioned was Mu Yan. Mu Yan was currently anxious and on the edge.","She had only been part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence for a year. She had been the last survivor in the intense and exciting insect army survival battle.","Although she was only able to make it to the end because of Lin Yuan’s protection, Mu Yan did possess real power! Otherwise, regardless of how close she was to Lin Yuan, it would be difficult for her to make it to the final ten!","Mu Yan had worked hard for the past year. Since she had made it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence and became the pride of her family, she would not allow herself to be eliminated.","But as she looked at the seniors in front of her, Mu Yan found it difficult to remain calm.","She sneaked a look at Lin Yuan.","She heard that he had only just become of age. He was five years younger than her. Yet, he was able to use his determination, resilience, and courage to push through all odds. What was there that she could not achieve?","The image of Lin Yuan had been seared into Mu Yan’s mind a year ago. He became an idol that she wanted to work towards.","There were some people who only called others their idols but did not take them seriously while others used them to motivate themselves.","Mu Yan was the latter. Although she worked hard, there were times when she slacked off. But every time she thought of Lin Yuan, her fighting spirit would be stirred, and she would push on.","As a result of this, even Mu Yan’s strict teacher had to tell her to take a break.","Mu Yan clenched her fist tightly, and a resolute expression formed on her face.","She could take small steps and try her best without putting too much pressure on herself!","She was still young. As long as she retained a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, she stood a chance of making it into the top 30 ranks by the time she reached 27 or 28 years old.","Moreover, the Radiance Federation intended to inject a large amount of resources into the Radiance Hundred Sequence. The provision of Bronze/Legend feys as prizes was enough proof of this.","A Bronze/Legend fey that would be tailored to one’s Willpower Rune was so valuable that it was also difficult for Mu Yan, who came from a Creation Master family, to digest the news easily.","At this moment, Mu Yan’s eyes met a pair of calm ones. Mu Yan instinctively started to panic, and her left hand clutched her chest.","Because of Genius, Lin Yuan had expanded his sea of spiritual energy. Thus, he was able to use his spiritual energy to acutely sense the surroundings through spiritual perception.","Even if he closed his eyes and rested, he would be able to use spiritual perception to detect who was looking at him.","Lin Yuan had some idea of who Mu Yan was. During the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Mu Yan had led 200 spirit qi professionals and moved between numerous battle lines, saving countless young people who were participating in the selection.","Compared to Mu Yan’s individual power, Lin Yuan admired her leadership skills.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence members were usually tested on their character and power. However, Lin Yuan felt that coordination and execution skills were also important qualities.","Lin Yuan smiled at Mu Yan before he turned to look at the swirling whirlpool at the center of the clouds. At this moment, the whirlpool dispersed and faded into wisps.","A suspended arena was revealed.","The arena was surrounded by moving clouds and was around twice the size of regular arenas.","There was a layer of jade covering the arena. This was not a durable material that could withstand the force of attacks. It was clear that the jade was only used for aesthetic purposes.","Since the challenge was going to be taking place in this arena amongst the clouds, the arena could not be damaged.","Liu Wencheng’s figure appeared at the center of the arena. He raised his hand and bellowed, “The fifth epoch has become another notch in history. The beginning of the dead spirits crisis has heralded the beginning of the sixth epoch.","“The Radiance Federation has not only been focused on fighting the dead spirits. We have also been saving and coordinating the main world’s humans and sea clans. We have made many achievements in our efforts against the dead spirits. We are already making progress in terms of treating the death aura and healing the injuries inflicted by the death aura.","“In the past few days, the Dead Spirits Wells had somewhat reached a state of stability. Our troops have been working hard non-stop and have shed blood, sweat, and tears for the sake of our homeland.","“The Radiance Federation’s younger generation should also be prepared to take up the mantle left by their seniors. The Radiance Hundred Sequence’s reranking will be a demonstration of the younger generation’s outstanding capabilities!","“I hereby announce the beginning of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection! The last rank will be the first to pick his challengers. Every time they defeat an opponent, they will take over their opponent’s rank. The defeated members will take on the challenger’s rank. Each person is eligible to three challenges.”","The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were all well aware of the rules. Liu Wencheng had only explained in such detail for the benefit of the spectators.","The first part of Liu Wencheng’s speech was also not directed at the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","As long as the reranking and selection proceeded smoothly, every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would be able to demonstrate their power and significantly boost the Radiance Federation’s morale!","However, this was only a temporary solution and the fiery morale would only last for a short time.","Liu Wencheng needed all the citizens of the Radiance Federation to know that the Radiance Federation’s officials and Creation Masters were constantly working hard and that their efforts were effective. Once the Radiance Federation’s citizens understood this, the fighting spirit riled up by the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and reranking would be even more explosive and long-lasting!","Unlike Cicada Song, Liu Wencheng had not gone with the Moon Empress to gain an understanding of the demon insects’ might.","However, Liu Wencheng had visited Ascending Dragon City and witnessed how the demon insects had established their armies. What Liu Wencheng saw had exceeded his comprehension. He felt as though the dead spirits that were extremely dangerous to humans were nothing more than food that had popped out from the ground to the demon insects.","Based on Liu Wencheng’s careful observations, he had not noticed the dead dimensional lifeforms employing any special methods to take on the demon insects. It was as though, just like how the dead spirits and humans could not coexist, the demon insects and dead spirits were also natural enemies.","Liu Wencheng had also considered the possible issue of the sixth epoch not being triggered by the dead spirits crisis but the demon insects crisis instead. Would the humans also end up having to battle the demon insects just like they were doing with the dead spirits?","But Liu Wencheng quickly shook this thought out of his head.","Based on Liu Wencheng’s observation, the 17th wave of offspring produced by the demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks had the intelligence of a 20-year-old human.","The demon insects might not be pleasant to look at, but they were a highly intelligent species.","Highly intelligent species were very sociable and could acclimatize easily. They were capable of using strategies and ploys during combat. There was no way that the dead insects that were driven by instinct stood a chance!","Liu Wencheng felt that he needed to have a chat with the Moon Empress and ask her if Lin Yuan had full control over the demon insects. He did not want the demon insects to stop the dead spirits crisis only to become the real enemy that destroyed the human race!","Liu Wencheng pondered over these matters while he continued to make methodical and orderly arrangements.","There were no commentators on the arena where the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking and selection was going to take place. However, on Star Web, where the event was being broadcasted, all of the Radiance Federation’s hosts and commentators for major events opened their own channels and prepared to commentate on this grand event!","Star Web’s reporters also sprung into action.","Ever since news of the dead spirits crisis broke out, the Star Web hosts’ revenue fell by at least a third. Who could be bothered with leisure on Star Web when the dead spirits crisis was taking place?","But with such a magnificent event, there was no reason for the hosts and reporters not to participate.","Liu Hao had been watching the audience numbers on Star Web. He was extremely pleased with the amount of activity and attention that was being drawn in by this event.","After thinking for a moment, Liu Hao called Tian Ningning. Tian Ningning picked up after two rings.","“Big Brother Hao, do you have any instructions for me? I have already begun writing the drafts for the battle records. Although those few battles will be the most important, the battles between the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence will also make an impact!”","Liu Hao was very happy with Tian Ningning’s work. He knew that Tian Ningning was very professional and capable. Otherwise, she would never have managed to become Liu Hao’s exclusive reporter.","Even if Lin Yuan thought highly of her, the Moon Empress would have already swapped her out if she was not sufficiently capable.","Liu Hao had heard from Zuo Ming about how Lin Yuan was the apple of the Moon Empress’ eye.","But despite knowing that Tian Ningning was very reliable, this matter was far too important, and Liu Hao needed to make sure that things were going well.","“Ningning, are all the preparations done on your end? Will there be any issues with the reporting on those high-priority matches? If you need more help, I can send the teams under me to help you. It’s better to err on the side of caution. You have a major responsibility. Not even a hint of carelessness or error will be tolerated!”"]},{"number":2681,"title":"Chapter 2681 Battle of Ice!","paragraphs":["2681 Battle of Ice!","Tian Ningning had confirmed these matters repeatedly long ago and had done many rehearsals.","She had also conducted the others aside from Lin Yuan, and they were all willing to cooperate with her.","As long as Lin Yuan and the rest were willing to cooperate with her, nothing could go wrong. This was something that Tian Ningning could guarantee!","Even if there was a kink in the process, the talented people in the teams could handle it.","Tian Ningning knew that Liu Hao was acting this way because he was worried that something would go wrong and he would have to take responsibility for it. At the same time, he wanted to remind her of the gravity of this matter.","“Don’t worry, Big Brother Hao. The Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking has begun. I need to begin working and preparing. I hope you can send another team to me. I need them to help out the hosts and commentators. This will raise the publicity of the event to the greatest extent.”","Tian Ningning had selfish reasons for saying this to Liu Hao.","Tian Ningning had not watched that youth grow up, but he hoped that she would be able to brighten up his most glorious moment. She wanted the spotlight on him to be as dazzling as possible so he could be even more astounding than he already was.","The most troubled person in the entire Radiance Federation was Mu Yan, who was Sequence #100.","According to the rules of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, she would be the first to issue her three challenges.","It did not matter if she lost these three challenges. But as long as she won one, she would be able to move up the ranks.","Those who challenged first meant that in the subsequent 200 matches, they could only be chosen to be challenged.","Given that she was Sequence #100, people naturally assumed that she was the weakest.","Mu Yan was confident in her power. She had improved her power significantly in the past year.","But if her opponent was sufficiently powerful, even if she managed to win the match, she would have to expose herself completely and reveal all her secret weapons.","Secret weapons were what struck fear into others.","Hence, Mu Yan had no idea who to pick!","Ever since she became part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Mu Yan had been preparing for the reranking a year later because she was worried that she would be eliminated.","Thus, she had been researching the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. She would only be able to improve her chances when she understood her opponents.","Eventually, she decided to set her sights on Sequence #87 Wu Ting, who was called Icy Waves.","Wu Ting was a veteran in the Radiance Hundred Sequence. She was already 29 years old this year but had never made it into the top 60. She always fluctuated around the 80s.","She was one of the main members of a B-level guild club and had a wealth of battle experience.","One of the rules of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection was that once a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had been eliminated, they could not compete again!","Wu Ting’s power and tenacity were proven by her tenure in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Wu Ting was surprised to be chosen by a rookie, and she hurriedly stood up from her seat before gallantly striding to the arena.","Mu Yan had selected Wu Ting as her opponent after all the research she had done.","Every spirit qi professional contracted many feys, so it was difficult to effectively counter them. One could only target one area to try and influence the battle.","Element-type feys battled each other in terms of the level of their elements. If a fire element was of a high enough level, water would not be able to put it out. For example, Zong Ze’s Fiery Sky Hou could instantaneously dry up a river.","Mu Yan had nurtured a new fey. Although this fey was ice-type, it could also effectively counter other ice-type feys.","This new fey was what gave Mu Yan the confidence to take on Wu Ting.","At first, one could only challenge ranks that were up to ten ranks above one’s position. But now, this restriction had been lifted. The ranking would become more flexible and fair.","Even if Mu Yan used natural countering to win one match, she would not be at an advantage for the rest of the reranking.","However, Mu Yan did not care.","All she wanted to do now was to raise her rank as quickly as possible while trying to keep as many of her secret weapons hidden as possible. This would give her the chance to use them if she was challenged by anyone else.","Although she had learned from previous information that her new fey could counter Wu Ting, Mu Yan dared not underestimate Wu Ting. It was possible that Wu Ting had significantly increased her power in the last year or still had secret weapons that she had yet to reveal.","Wu Ting smiled and nodded at Mu Yan.","“Sister Mu Yan, you can summon your fey first!”","Wu Ting’s arms hung by her sides, and she looked expectant.","It was an advantage to be able to summon one’s feys first during battle.","There was a tradition in the Radiance Hundred Sequence, which was that when those of higher ranks were challenged by those of lower ranks, those of lower ranks could summon their feys first.","Mu Yan did not stand on ceremony with Wu Ting and pointed ahead of her. Two identical ice-type feys appeared in front of her.","These two ice-type feys were two Ice Vein Frozen Bats with wingspans of less than 40 centimeters. They could absorb the coldness in the air around them to boost their combat abilities.","Wu Ting’s lips twitched. It was no wonder that this brat was challenging her!","Two of her ice-type feys were skilled at creating icy environments. The two Ice Vein Frozen Bats would be able to effectively counter these two feys.","However, Mu Yan was naive if she thought that she would be able to defeat her just with these two Ice Vein Frozen Bats!","Wu Ting leaned forward and charged ahead. While she was running, a giant creature that was more than 20 meters tall crashed to the ground ahead of her.","An aura barrelled over towards Mu Yan at the instant that his giant creature appeared.","The giant creature’s claws pierced the ground, and the arena’s ground froze solid.","When the giant creature roared, ice slabs rose from the ground, completely altering the arena’s environment.","The Shaman Ice Bear was one of Wu Ting’s signature feys. It was what enabled Wu Ting to win most of her battles.","The Shaman Ice Bear’s reputation caused the audience watching the Radiance Hundred Shaman Ice Bear reranking to let out gasps.","The Shaman Ice Bear was much more famous than Mu Yan’s two Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","However, the hosts and commentators who were analyzing the battles could not help but frown.","The Ice Vein Frozen Bat was part of textbooks and described as the perfect ice-type fey.","Those who took Fey Observer classes in university all had a certain understanding of the Ice Vein Frozen Bat.","Wu Ting and Mu Yan were both members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Although Mu Yan’s rank was lower than that of Wu Ting, it was unlikely that Wu Ting knew nothing about Mu Yan.","There had to be a special reason for Wu Ting summoning the Shaman Ice Bear in such circumstances!","Wu Ting had a fair number of feys. She had three.","The ice-type fey that was mainly in charge of attacking had restrained cold aura, so none of it leaked to be absorbed by the Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","Mu Yan instructed the Ice Vein Frozen Bats to produce two ice walls to block the fierce aura.","The cold aura within the rush of cold air was the best nourishment for the Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","As the Ice Vein Frozen Bats absorbed the cold aura, they started to divide and separate.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow.","A year ago, before the Radiance Federation had begun building mirror cities in the abyssal world, the price of relatively perfect ice-type feys was very low because it was very costly to nurture them.","But now, the Ice Vein Frozen Bat had become the most popular ice-type fey.","The Ice Vein Frozen Bat had the exclusive skill Cold Accumulation Body Split. When the frozen aura in its body reached a certain level, it would begin splitting its body to become a swarm of bats.","This was slightly less rare than the Mirror Silver Obsidian Bull’s ability Sacrifice.","Both of Mu Yan’s Ice Vein Frozen Bats’ exclusive skills were Cold Accumulation Body Split.","She had spent a lot of effort and resources to nurture these two feys.","But when Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Shaman Ice Bear, Lin Yuan shook his head slightly. He had not expected Wu Ting to be hiding such a move.","The Shaman Ice Bear’s Diamond ability Zero Degree Disintegration would allow the Shaman Ice Bear to infuse its spiritual energy and soul energy into its cold aura. It would then freeze its target and cause the target’s muscles to disintegrate.","Given that Zero Degree Disintegration required the Shaman Ice Bear to use its spiritual energy and soul energy, it was considered a restraining ability that was not commonly used in combat.","This ability was extremely costly for the Shaman Ice Bear, and Wu Ting had been significantly troubled by it.","Yet, this ability was going to become the crux of this battle!","The Ice Vein Frozen Bat’s exclusive skill, Cold Accumulation Body Split, would also use up its own energy.","Moreover, Mu Yan did not have the clarity to see all that was happening and used the Ice Vein Frozen Bats’ swarm as both her method of attack and defense.","When they clashed, the Ice Vein Frozen Bats would be immediately broken down by the Shaman Ice Bear.","The Class 3 Creation Masters had to carefully examine the Shaman Ice Bear to notice that something was different about the Shaman Ice Bear’s ability.","The Class 4 and above Creation Masters were able to see through the Shaman Ice Bear’s abilities.","There were Creation Masters amongst the Radiance Hundred Sequence, but they were only Class 3 at best. It was rare for a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to reach a higher level before they turned 30 years old.","Wu Ting saw that Mu Yan was busy ordering the Ice Vein Frozen Bats to absorb the cold aura released by the Shaman Ice Bear and did not summon any other feys.","Wu Ting intended to push Mu Yan to the brink before pushing Mu Yan to reveal her secret weapons. This would give her the advantage and enable her to assess if it would be necessary for her to use her own secret weapons.","When she saw the expression on Mu Yan’s face, she believed that Mu Yan thought of her as a moron who was enabling her to absorb as much cold aura as she wanted.","Although Mu Yan was still somewhat wary, the Ice Vein Frozen Bats continued to split up, and there were eventually tens of Ice Vein Frozen Bats flying around her. Mu Yan felt that she might be able to defeat Wu Ting without summoning that fey!","The two Ice Vein Frozen Bats had powerful control over the more than 60 Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","When she felt that there were enough of the bats, Mu Yan ordered half of the swarm to attack Wu Ting. As for the other half, they circled Mu Yan to protect her.","When Wu Ting saw that Mu Yan was beginning to attack, she issued another order to the Shaman Ice Bear.","After receiving Wu Ting’s order, the Shaman Ice Bear let out a loud roar.","Soon, three ice walls appeared in front of the Shaman Ice Bear, blocking it from sight. However, the gaps between the three walls were large enough for the swarm of bats to fly through.","Mu Yan could no longer see Wu Ting, and she immediately frowned.","Wu Ting used this opportunity to summon another two feys.","One of these feys was covered with crystalline ice and was around the size of a pet rabbit.","However, this small creature had taken Liu Jie down in a previous battle. The memory was still fresh in his mind!","The small creature rushed into the ice wall and became one with it.","Liu Jie knew that this fey called the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable would not remain in the ice wall. The entire ice-covered arena could become its dwelling.","The Ice Mirror Hunter Sable would attack Mu Yan at the right moment.","If Mu Yan could not remove the layer of ice underneath her, it would be difficult for her to survive the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable’s attack.","The other fey was a yak that was around the same size as the Shaman Ice Bear.","Once the yak appeared and stomped on the ground, the cold aura in the arena intensified.","At first, there was only ice on the ground. But now, there was snow, too. The snow shot up to the sky from the ground.","The territory of ice created by the Blizzard Wild Cow and Shaman Ice Bear was the reason that Wu Ting was called Icy Waves.","The Shaman Ice Bear produced waves of cold air continuously, and Mu Yan had no choice but to go on the defensive.","The rushing waves of cold air covered the sound of the Blizzard Wild Cow’s stomping.","Thus, Mu Yan did not know that Wu Ting had already summoned another fey.","Nonetheless, Mu Yan had sensed that she was in danger.","Because of this, Mu Yan summoned the fey she regarded as her secret weapon.","A mouse with a half-red and half-blue body appeared by Mu Yan’s feet and started squeaking. It did not look very intelligent.","At the instant that Lin Yuan saw the mouse-species fey, an amused appeared on his face.","The victor of this game was yet to be confirmed!","If this mouse-species fey’s ability was not so one-sided, Lin Yuan would have been interested in forming a contract with it.","This fey was called the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse. It could transform cold attributes into flaming hot ones.","There were two sides to every element. But most feys could only control one of them.","The opposite spectrum of the element would cause backlash to a fey that controlled the element on the other side of the spectrum.","The damage caused by such backlash was much stronger than external elemental attacks!","This was the first time that Lin Yuan was seeing a fey that could overturn the attributes of another fey.","Mu Yan’s sense of danger heightened.","She no longer cared that her secret weapon was being exposed, and she ordered the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse, “Squeaky, turn the ice into flames!”"]},{"number":2682,"title":"Chapter 2682 Turning the Tables and Strong Ice!","paragraphs":["2682 Turning the Tables and Strong Ice!","Despite knowing that her Hot Ice Boiling Mouse would be able to transform the ice elements in the arena and immediately allow her to take the upper hand in the battle, Mu Yan was not happy at all because she had been forced to reveal her secret weapon.","She could still try to target other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence she had an advantage over for the next two challenges. But once she was challenged by others, she would stand no chance of turning the tables because she had already revealed all of her secret weapons.","Mu Yan sighed softly. She might really end up pushed out from the Radiance Hundred Sequence!","If she really ended up being eliminated, she would join the Spirit Guards. They were currently recruiting young spirit qi professionals from various schools. With her background as a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, there was no way that they would reject her!","With this thought, Mu Yan looked into the distance where Lin Yuan was sitting. However, she was only able to see his silhouette.","This was when it dawned on her. Remaining a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence was not the most important component of life. The most important component of life was growing continuously.","Now that she understood this, a passionate fighting spirit lit up in Mu Yan’s eyes.","The Hot Ice Boiling Mouse was a mouse-species fey that had already undergone a special mutation. As intelligent as it was, it was also very temperamental.","After being ordered by Mu Yan to attack, icy blue flames erupted all over the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse’s body. Instead of slowly spreading outwards, the icy flames melted all the ice in the arena into a gelatinous substance in an instant.","As the icy blue flames continued burning atop the gelatinous substance, an unsettling searing heat covered the entire arena. This reminded Lin Yuan of the alcoholic cakes that burned beneath the copper hotpots from his previous life.","At the instant that the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse used its abilities to transform the elements, the Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow let out piercing howls of agony. The higher the grade of a fey, the more acute the pain of the backlash that came from two different types of ice-elemental energy clashing in its body.","Wu Ting thought that she had already secured control over the situation and had not anticipated this move from Mu Yan at all.","Now, the tide had suddenly turned, and it was Wu Ting who was forced into a corner and needed to scramble to deal with the situation.","If the Shaman Ice Bear had not tossed Wu Ting onto its back at the moment that the icy flames lit up, Wu Ting’s body would have already been burned to ashes.","It was not just members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Even spirit qi professionals who were Radiance Envoys were limited by their bodies during battle.","It was only when a spirit qi professional reached S-rank that his body would be able to condense spirit qi into a vortex that he could use to defend himself.","Once spirit qi professionals gained the ability to defend themselves, their style of combat would change drastically. The best way to tip the scales of the battle would no longer be to target the spirit qi professional directly.","Wu Ting’s reaction to the abrupt change in circumstances caused Lin Yuan’s eyes to light up. She was truly a battle-worn veteran!","Wu Ting had developed an outstanding ability to adapt in battle during the S Tournament. If she had any less battle experience, it would be difficult for her to adjust to such a sudden change.","With such an outstanding performance right out of the gate of the first battle, the rookie Mu Yan left a deep impression on many of the Radiance Federation’s citizens.","Although the fans who were familiar with Mu Yan were slightly concerned, they were not panicking because she had yet to use her actual ultimate killing move!","Although the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse had transformed the elements, Wu Ting’s Ice Mirror Hunter Sable could still use the abilities Tough Mirror Killing Claws and Mirror Surface Body to put up a defense.","Mirror Surface Body allowed the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable to enter a covert state of movement that allowed it to imitate its environment. The surface of its body would become a mirror that allowed it to absorb the elemental energy around it. This prevented its body from being damaged by elemental energy.","It was this ability that allowed Wu Ting to assassinate opponents during tournaments.","Not even a volcano environment filled with many fire-type feys could stop the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable’s movements.","Tough Mirror Killing Claws would allow the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable to use its sharp claws to work in conjunction with Mirror Surface Body to utilize the elemental energy that had gathered around the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable. It would use the elemental energy to attack a target, strengthening the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable’s deadliness and turning it into the perfect assassin.","It seemed as though Wu Ting was trying to counter and fight back, but she was still capable of being a threat to Mu Yan.","Wu Ting did not immediately instruct the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable to attack Mu Yan. Instead, she instructed the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable to use Mirror Surface Body to hide within the burning icy flames.","Mu Yan was definitely still on guard.","The Ice Mirror Hunter Sable’s chances of success would be significantly raised once Mu Yan saw the Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow were on the brink of collapse.","By delaying the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable’s attack, the strength of the ability Tough Mirror Killing Claws would also be raised.","It seemed as though Wu Ting was at a disadvantage and had no means of fighting back. But this was a performance that Wu Ting was putting on.","Battling on Star Web was different from battling in real life. On Star Web, one did not have to worry about one’s fey’s roots being damaged or death. Thus, one could fight with one’s life on the line without hesitation.","The 98 other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were all watching Mu Yan and Wu Ting’s fight intently. This was because there was a high possibility that they would end up having to battle the two of them later.","The Star Web’s hosts and commentators were currently enthusiastically analyzing the battle and giving their own insights. This event was the best chance for the Star Web hosts, commentators, and reporters to rise up and thrive.","It was fine if they made the wrong comments, but if they did well and were able to accurately predict the result of every match, their number of fans would skyrocket after the event.","The money they earned and their status in this industry would also be inflated!","Wu Ting silently sensed the Shaman Ice Bear’s condition. It could only hold on for another three minutes at most in such an environment.","Mu Yan’s two Ice Vein Frozen Bats had already absorbed the maximum amount of Ice Vein Frozen Bats and produced the maximum number of bats.","Mu Yan eventually sent the 30 bats she had been keeping by her side to join the attack.","It was clear that Mu Yan intended to finish the battle as quickly as possible and claim victory.","Wu Ting still had a gloomy expression on her face, but she was leaping for joy internally.","Once the Shaman Ice Bear used Zero Degree Disintegration, the swarm of bats would only lose their combat powers. After being disintegrated, the cold aura within the swarm of bats was released and used by the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","It was extremely draining for the Shaman Ice Bear to use its Diamond ability Zero Degree Disintegration.","The Shaman Ice Bear could not use the ability twice in such short succession. Presently, the swarm of bats was already charging towards her.","Due to the crumbling of the swarm of bats due to Zero Degree Disintegration, the cold aura that was released would lower the effects of the transformed ice elements and alleviate some of the negative impacts on the Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow.","This would allow the Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow to last for longer and defend against any secret weapons that Mu Yan might still have.","The use of precious instruments was not allowed in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. This greatly decreased the leverage that family assets could give a spirit qi professional.","However, Wu Ting, who had a plethora of battle experience, knew that staying vigilant was the true key to victory.","The Hot Ice Boiling Mouse’s transformation of ice elements had significantly impacted the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats. Although the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse had not targeted the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats, the environment would naturally restrict them.","Without the cold aura to use, the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats had no means of defending themselves against the Ice Vein Frozen Bat’s assassination!","Wu Ting pretended to be panicking and instructed the Shaman Ice Bear to retreat.","Mu Yan hurriedly instructed the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats to use the swarm of bats to launch an attack.","At this moment, Wu Ting suddenly instructed the Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow to turn and take on the more than 50 Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","Wu Ting shouted out orders to the Shaman Ice Bear and Ice Mirror Hunter Sable.","The Shaman Ice Bear used the Diamond ability Zero Degree Disintegration.","The destructive swarm of bats suddenly started falling apart from the inside out and the cold aura leaked out.","The Shaman Ice Bear and Blizzard Wild Cow let out two simultaneous roars.","The Blizzard Wild Cow created another area of blizzards to take on the area created by the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse.","This change immediately attracted Mu Yan’s attention.","At this moment, the Ice Mirror Hunter Sable that had been hiding in the layer of broken ice used Tough Mirror Killing Claws and attacked Mu Yan.","One attack was enough to kill Mu Yan and shred the Ice Vein Frozen Bats that had been blocking her.","The winds of this battle had changed again. Eventually, Wu Ting was able to retain her ranking and safeguard the glory that was attached to her title of Icy Waves!","The guild club that Wu Ting belonged to also had two other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. After the match, her teammate Feng Yao shook his head.","He had not expected this rookie to challenge Wu Ting! In actuality, Wu Ting still had another secret weapon that she had yet to reveal.","She had begun preparing this secret weapon three years ago. During last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, she had decided to keep this secret weapon under wraps.","But this year, Wu Ting intended to make it into the top 30 ranks. Mu Yan had unknowingly bitten off more than she could chew!","He hoped that Mu Yan would not lose her confidence in the next two matches because of this defeat.","As long as she still had one or two more secret weapons up her sleeve, it should not be overly difficult for her to make it into the top 90!","During the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Lin Yuan had created a sea of flowers as a shield so the participants who had gathered together could form battle lines to defend against external forces.","Mu Yan was only able to display her leadership and execution abilities when she had people around her she could lead and coordinate into teams.","Without someone like Lin Yuan, who could play the pivotal position, the participants would not be able to work unitedly even if they did gather together. This would make it difficult for Mu Yan to demonstrate her capabilities.","Hence, unless she made it into the top 90, it was unlikely that there was a spot for Mu Yan in this year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence.","After her death, Mu Yan reappeared in her seat. She had a rather defeated expression hanging off of her face.","At this moment, Liu Wencheng’s voice appeared in Mu Yan’s ear.","“Now, let us invite Sequence #100 Strong Ice Mu Yan to pick another challenger!”","Mu Yan’s expression froze momentarily when she heard what Liu Wencheng said.","Her title in the Radiance Hundred Sequence was ‘Strong Ice’. It was the name that had received the most votes on Star Web from the Radiance Federation’s citizens. She had attained this title because she had demonstrated a will as strong as ice.","Mu Yan was about to give up. But when she heard her title, she felt ashamed for entertaining thoughts of giving up.","She only had three main feys, and she had used all of their powers during the battle with Wu Ting.","Now that her opponent knew of her secret weapons, she would have no choice but to rely on brute force.","Mu Yan gnashed her teeth and said, “I pick Sequence #83, King Beast Blood Liu Hong!”","Of all the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Liu Hong relied on his feys’ bodies the most and preferred physical battles. He was the weakest member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Aside from absorbing cold aura to constrain ice-type feys, the Ice Vein Frozen Bats could also use the elements to freeze targets to lower the effectiveness of their attacks as well as agility.","Once there were enough bats, the target would become fully frozen. At that point, the Ice Vein Frozen Bats could absorb the energy within the targets to replenish and heal themselves or use the cold aura to divide themselves into even more bats.","Moreover, after using Ice Shadow Teeth to bite a target, there was also a small chance that the target would be cursed. The curse would cause the target to begin aging rapidly and lower the strength of their body.","Since she had not managed to achieve victory through skill and strategy, Mu Yan decided to use force to manage the battle instead.","Management was Mu Yan’s strong suit.","Liu Hong was not at all surprised at being picked.","Given the current circumstances, he was the best choice that Mu Yan could have made.","However, he was no sitting duck that Mu Yan would be able to take down easily.","He had also significantly increased his power in the past year. It was only a shame that he was still a little weak when it came to comprehending Willpower Runes and only had two Fantasy Breed feys.","Liu Hong leaped down and was caught by the clouds at the edge of the arena. He stepped on the clouds and descended on the arena in a dashing manner.","This caused a few members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to smirk.","Liu Hong always liked to add flair to everything that he did. This way of entering the area was rather juvenile!","It would be fine if he won. But if he lost, he would be ripped to shreds and made into a laughingstock by the Star Web reporters.","Shi Xu’s lit up when he saw Liu Hong’s actions, and he shot a look at Zhao Xiaochun.","When Zhao Xiaochun caught Shi Xu’s gaze, she hurriedly shook her head.","She knew that he now wanted to enter the arena in a similar fashion and that he wanted her to join him!","She did not want to be embarrassed alongside him!","Alas, Shi Xu seemed to be unphased by her shaking head. Zhao Xiaochun could not help but press her hand to her forehead.","It seemed that aside from spending money to treat her to meals, Shi Xu did not have any other strengths.","Nonetheless, she still liked him.","If he ended up embarrassing himself she would pull him to the Spirit Food Pavilion after the Radiance Hundred Sequence ended and eat until her stomach felt like it was going to explode!"]},{"number":2683,"title":"Chapter 2683 Lingering Death Penetrating Armor and Heavy Rock Kangaroo!","paragraphs":["2683 Lingering Death Penetrating Armor and Heavy Rock Kangaroo!","Liu Hong’s flamboyant manner of entering had the passionate air of an adolescent. This led to many comments in the live-streaming rooms.","Liu Hong’s leap brought out a happy and excited atmosphere on Star Web. They needed something entertaining to forget the stress that came with fear.","Rather than being entertained, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, aside from Shi Xu, were more interested in the impending battle between Liu Hong and Mu Yan.","Mu Yan had worked hard to increase her power over the past year and had declined to join any guild clubs.","Liu Hong had been busy battling as a member of the Fighting Fists Guild Club’s main team and had achieved many victories for them.","In order to retain Liu Hong, the Fighting Fists Guild Club even gave him 3% of shares and provided him with generous remuneration.","Liu Hong had been a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence for four years. Although he was not considered very senior, he did have a wealth of experience.","Liu Hong was very sociable and made many friends after joining the Radiance Hundred Sequence. People with similar personalities to Long Tao all got along well with Liu Hong.","Apart from battling in tournaments, Liu Hong had spent the past four years working on tasks handed out by Radiance Sacred Hall in order to accumulate points. He wanted to accumulate enough points to trade for a high-quality Bronze fey that was suitable for his Willpower Rune.","Alas, although there were such feys in Radiance Sacred Hall, they were far too expensive. Even after working and saving for four years, he still did not have enough to trade for the fey he had his eye on.","However, two months ago, Radiance Sacred Hall lowered the points required to trade for resources and offered even rarer resources for trading.","The amount of points that Liu Hong had accumulated not only allowed him to trade for Bronze/Legend fey but also for the resources that sped up its growth.","Not even Liu Hong’s teammates from the Fight Fists Guild Club, with whom he spent the bulk of his time, knew that he had already swapped out his main fey.","His previous signature fey was no longer his strongest one.","In the past, he would have been rather anxious to be picked by Mu Yan. A spirit qi professional like him, who mostly contracted feys that relied on their bodies for battle, were the most afraid of taking on feys that had strong controlling abilities and could limit the movements of their opponents.","Mu Yan’s Ice Vein Frozen Bats had already demonstrated curse-related abilities during the previous battle. They were usually the most difficult abilities for Liu Hong to counter in battle.","Whenever one had a flaw, one would always try one’s best to fix it.","Although the new fey that Liu Hong contracted also relied on its body for combat, it was the bane of feys that had controlling and curse abilities.","Liu Hong had yet to have the chance to see this new fey in action during a real battle. Now, he finally had the chance to test it out!","Liu Hong was not very good at being secretive. Mu Yan could see the excitement and hopefulness on his face.","Mu Yan’s chest tightened, but she quickly adjusted her mindset.","If she lost to Liu Hong now, it was very unlikely that she would be able to hold on to a place in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","If that truly happened, when it came to the third match, Mu Yan would not pick an opponent she would try to defeat. Rather, she would challenge Lin Yuan.","This was so she could see how large the gap was between her and her idol, and it was also a means for her to act on her urges as a fan!","With such thoughts in mind, Mu Yan summoned the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats before summoning the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse as well.","She instructed the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse to release ice-elemental energy and form a circle of boiling hot ice around her as a means of defending against close-quarter combat.","Liu Hong let out a shout of excitement when she saw Mu Yan summoning her feys and preparing to attack him.","He lifted up a hand and released a mighty kangaroo that was almost two meters tall and had bulging muscles. Its entire body was gray and brown, and its tightly knotted muscles were pulsing with powerful earth-elemental energy.","The earth-elemental energy was not released. Rather, it was stored within the muscles and formed a dark brown membrane on the kangaroo’s skin.","The membrane of earth-elemental energy significantly raised the Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s power and allowed it to take down a small hill with one punch!","After releasing the Heavy Rock Kangaroo, Liu Hong released a small creature that was less than half a meter tall and covered with thick and sharp armor pieces. This was Liu Hong’s other signature fey, the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor.","When the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor moved around at high speeds, its scales would shift randomly. Its sharp scales could cut almost anything that it came into contact with. As a result, when the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor fought, it had a strange beauty of untamed violence.","There were very few teams who liked encountering Fighting Fists Guild Club in offline guild club battles. Unless it was an important tournament, most guild clubs preferred to preserve the safety of their main team’s feys and send their second team to take on the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor instead. Some would even choose to back out of the tournament altogether.","If the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor fought with all of its force, its opponent fey’s flesh would be reduced to filet pieces. Even with a capable medical team treating it, it would take around a month for the fey to recover.","But more importantly, just like spirit qi professionals, feys were also living creatures. When they suffered pain and injury, they were left with trauma.","After suffering such serious injuries, there was a high chance that the fey’s enthusiasm in future battles would be lowered. It might even start to fear fighting.","A few of Liu Hong’s opponents had experienced this after battling him.","The Heavy Rock Kangaroo did not begin throwing fists wildly. Meanwhile, the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor had already charged towards Mu Yan.","The Lingering Death Penetrating Armor curled itself up into a ball, and the armored pieces on its back let out grinding noises as they rubbed together.","Mu Yan had already mentally prepared herself to lose and had composed her mental state.","She calmly instructed the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats to release cold aura and begin splitting up. Then, with the two original Ice Vein Frozen Bats included, she instructed the six Ice Vein Frozen Bats to use Frozen Shadow Collision on the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor.","Six dark blue bats slammed into the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s body and substantially slowed down its movement. The Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s speed was thereby reduced at least by half.","This was just the beginning of the six dark blue bats’ attack. They continued swooping down toward the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor until a thick layer of snow was formed on its body.","The Lingering Death Penetrating Armor was now even slower than a Silver fey!","The Ice Vein Frozen Bats’ ability Frozen Shadow Collision did not just have speed-reducing effects. When the ability made contact with the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s body, it began freezing from the inside out.","Liu Hong had already anticipated that the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s movements would be constrained by the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats.","Due to the lack of cold aura present to replenish the Ice Vein Frozen Bats, the advantage that came from their ability to continuously divide themselves had been sealed away! Now, the Ice Vein Frozen Bats were using the energy in their own bodies to split up because Mu Yan wanted to handle and control the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor as soon as possible.","The Ice Vein Frozen Bats had used up a significant amount of their energy to forcefully split themselves up. Moreover, Mu Yan was also using the mouse to create an area of hot ice.","Liu Hong had yet to use much energy, but Mu Yan had already spent a large amount. It would not be long before he gained the upper hand.","Liu Hong had never employed cunning ploys during battle. There were times when obvious plans were more effective than hidden tricks.","Taking this situation as an example, Mu Yan clearly knew that trying to limit the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s movements would cost her a lot of energy. Yet, she had no other choice!","The Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s iron fists would come after the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor.","The reverberations from a few slams of the Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s Gold Breaking Tremors would cause the target’s vessels to snap.","Once this crippling ability hit a target, the target’s body would be damaged.","Liu Hong had already anticipated that Mu Yan would use the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats to restrain the Heavy Rock Kangaroo. They would place curses on the Heavy Rock Kangaroo to lower its combat ability.","Even someone like Liu Hong, who usually did not take things seriously, would not reveal his secret weapons if he could help it.","But if he wanted to win this battle against Mu Yan, there was no way he could hide his secret weapons.","After understanding this, Liu Hong began using the Heavy Rock Kangaroo and Lingering Death Penetrating Armor as targets. This would attract more attacks and cause his opponent to use up more of her energy.","Mu Yan could not allow the Heavy Rock Kangaroo to get within 20 meters of her. The Ice Vein Frozen Bats could dodge the Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s attacks. All they needed to do was fly into the air, and the Heavy Rock Kangaroo would not be able to touch them. However, Mu Yan could not do the same.","The defensive area that the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse had built around Mu Yan would not be enough to withstand the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse’s attacks.","Although the Heavy Rock Kangaroo would suffer serious injuries after entering this area, it would still be able to kill Mu Yan.","Mu Yan instructed the Ice Vein Frozen Bats to use Frozen Shadow Collision again. At the same time, they used Ice Shadow Teeth continuously on the Heavy Rock Kangaroo.","Under the curse effects of Ice Shadow Teeth, the Heavy Rock Kangaroo began aging, and the strength of its body fell substantially.","The two Ice Vein Frozen Bats were also absorbing the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor’s vitality and intended to use the vitality to generate cold aura and replenish their energy.","They had used up almost all of the energy in their bodies to take control of the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor and Heavy Rock Kangaroo.","Liu Hong realized this and took the opportunity to summon a round and chubby white seal.","The white seal crawled on the ground before raising up half of its body. It used its short and tough fins to slap its stomach.","Two beams of light shot out and landed on the Lingering Death Penetrating Armor and Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s body. The cold aura was absorbed through the two lines of white light and absorbed into the fat seal’s body, taking with it the aging curse that was afflicting the Heavy Rock Kangaroo.","After taking on so many negative effects and curses, the fat seal splayed out in pain on the ground.","The member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence sitting next to Lin Yuan said, “Silly Liu Hong, who only knows how to charge ahead, has contracted a defense-type fey! It sucked away the negative effects inflicted on his two main feys. Unless Mu Yan has something else up her sleeve, it looks like the winner of this battle is settled!”","Lin Yuan shook his head. There was no way Mu Yan was holding anything back. If she did, she would have already used it in her battle with Wu Ting!","Lin Yuan was all but certain that there was no way the direction of this battle would be changing.","Mu Yan was not weak. She had only lost twice because she was not the only one who had worked hard this past year. The others had done the same. All of them were hiding even more secret weapons than they used to!","When Mu Yan saw Liu Hong summon a fey that was unknown to her and this fey had instantly released the Heavy Rock Kangaroo and Lingering Death Penetrating Armor from her control, she knew that she had lost this battle.","Nonetheless, she did not resign herself to defeat. Instead, she continued using the Ice Vein Frozen Bats and Hot Ice Boiling Mouse to continue fighting back bravely. Eventually, they were killed by one of the Heavy Rock Kangaroo’s punches.","The entire battle lasted less than three minutes. But in those three minutes, the entire audience had been riled up.","Although Mu Yan had lost, she had put up a commendable performance and demonstrated outstanding fighting spirit.","The Radiance Federation’s royalty did not turn up to watch live but were silently spectating from the Royal Capital.","Night Leaning Moon said with marvel in her voice, “Mu Yan is a good prospect. But I don’t think she will be able to stay in the Radiance Hundred Sequence! The Spirit Guards have been trying to cultivate top talents this past year. I am going to personally recruit Mu Yan later.","“The departments the rest of you manage also need to be supported by top talents. The people eliminated by Liu Wencheng can become prime candidates for our selection. But none of you better compete with me for the ones I have my eye on!”","Cicada Song shot Night Leaning Moon a look of exasperation.","The most important resources for the dead spirits crisis were finances and infrastructure. They already had sufficient troops. Who was going to fight with Night Leaning Moon over manpower now?","The dead spirits crisis’ threat on the main world had been dampened, but the Spirit Guards were still very important for defense.","The talents in the Radiance Federation were all selected and recruited by the Spirit Guards. Even the City Guards Cicada Song chose were also talents that were left over once the Spirit Guards had been chosen.","Just as Night Leaning Moon said, it was unlikely that Mu Yan had sufficient power to keep a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence. But if she was noticed by Night Leaning Moon and was employed as a Spirit Guard, it would also be a good opportunity for her!","The Moon Empress and Lin Yuan had provided a mountain of resources to the Radiance Hundred Sequence. However, they had also provided just as much resources to the Spirit Guards.","Based on what the Moon Empress said, she would be supplying even more resources to the Spirit Guards in the future to enable them to better defend against the dead spirits.","The rewards for the troops defending against the dead spirits had only just been settled. It had yet to be announced. Once the announcement was made, it was likely that many of the current members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would also try to come up with a way to join the Spirit Guards!"]},{"number":2684,"title":"Chapter 2684 Lin Yuan’s First Battle!","paragraphs":["2684 Lin Yuan’s First Battle!","At that time, Mu Yan would still have the opportunity to work with these companions!","Even after losing two battles in succession, Mu Yan did not look disappointed or sad at all.","She looked in Lin Yuan’s direction and said earnestly to Liu Wencheng, “For my last challenge, I am going to pick Sequence #91, Miracle Lin Yuan!”","Mu Yan’s words caused Liu Wencheng, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, and the audience watching on Star Web to be stunned.","Soon, the audience started breathing heavier. They were very excited to see Lin Yuan summon feys to battle Mu Yan.","At first, the audience members all thought that they would have to wait for the other eight new members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to issue their challenges in order to watch Lin Yuan fight.","This was because Lin Yuan was Sequence #91. Even if they defeated Lin Yuan, one would not be guaranteed a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Furthermore, everyone was well aware of Lin Yuan’s powers. He had killed a Freedom Envoy. There was no way any of them stood any chance of winning against him!","Liu Wencheng had already announced that those who earned a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence would gain a high-quality Bronze fey that was tailored to their Willpower Rune. No one would be able to resist such temptation.","By doing this, Mu Yan had already given up on this opportunity. She would not be able to remain a part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence this year.","Liu Wencheng nodded. Each member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had three challenges to issue.","Mu Yan could have selected any member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Liu Wencheng did not understand why she wanted to select Lin Yuan.","“Mu Yan, are you sure you want to challenge Sequence #91 Miracle Lin Yuan? If you do, you will remain in the last ten ranks regardless of whether you defeat him. You will become the first member of the current Radiance Hundred Sequence to enter this year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection!”","Mu Yan nodded seriously before saying resolutely to Liu Wencheng, “I didn’t manage to increase my power sufficiently this year and failed to win my first two challenges. I am choosing Lin Yuan because he is my idol.","“Ever since he began battling on Star Web as Black, I have noticed and paid attention to him. I want to use this battle to see how large the gap is between my idol and me. I would like to fulfill my wish of battling my idol!”","If this had been said by a Star Web host, others would think that they were trying to take advantage of Lin Yuan’s popularity. But none of them thought this when it came from Mu Yan’s lips! She was a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence and had the right to say such a thing.","Moreover, she had said what many people were thinking.","Lin Yuan stood up from the moment Mu Yan mentioned his name.","He stepped on the clouds and walked over to the arena. His footsteps were stable and did not try to act suave like Liu Hong had done.","However, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence could not help but cheer to themselves.","Lin Yuan was surprised at being chosen. He had not expected someone to pick him for such a reason.","He could decide to go easy in the match so he could rally with Mu Yan. Alternatively, he could try and make the battle into a lesson that he used to give pointers to Mu Yan.","But he did not do so. He was going to show Mu Yan his real chops and not give her any opportunity to fight back. Otherwise, every other member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would end up picking him!","When Lin Yuan arrived at the arena, he followed the unspoken rule of the Radiance Hundred Sequence and did not summon his fey first because had the higher rank.","Mu Yan looked up into his eyes. She felt that this gentlemanly Lin Yuan was completely different from the Lin Yuan she had seen a year ago!","A year ago, he still had a youthful air about him. But now, he was composed and had a calm gaze. Although he still had the appearance of a young man, his entire demeanor had matured.","Mu Yan bowed to him before summoning the Ice Vein Frozen Bats for the third time and instructing them to fly toward Lin Yuan.","The charging Ice Vein Frozen Bats did not stop releasing cold aura and already had the abilities Frozen Shadow Collision and Ice Shadow Teeth loaded. As long as Lin Yuan was within the range of attack, the attacks would make contact with him.","Mu Yan immediately launched her strongest combat techniques. The Hot Ice Boiling Mouse created an area of hot ice in a one-meter radius around Mu Yan. Mu Yan was immediately surrounded by burning icy flames.","Lin Yuan gently lifted his hand, and the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom that was on the amber-button-shaped Diamond fey storage box released a large plume of spores.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores were very small, and it was impossible to see them with the naked eye.","The spores released by the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom were like its antenna.","The spores were carried by the wind, and the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats that were flying towards Lin Yuan were affected by Seeping Flames, Body-Penetrating Flames, and Thought-Separating Flames. Their bodies immediately started burning with fiery flames.","However, none of these three abilities targeted the target’s body but their mind, spirit, and soul.","It was difficult to defend against such flames that targeted the cores that were the heart, brain, mind, spirit, and soul.","Even if they could extinguish the flames, the flames would absorb the energy within the target’s heart and brain to reignite the fire.","Due to Thought-Separating Flames, the damage inflicted on the Ice Vein Frozen Bats’ mind and soul would be extended and guided to reach Mu Yan.","The screeches of pain from within the icy flames halted quickly.","Lin Yuan gently raised his hand, and the smoke in front of Mu Yan dissipated, revealing the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse that had collapsed in a heap on the ground. Mu Yan had already vanished.","Given that this was a battle on Star Web, Mu Yan’s body reappeared on her seat 30 seconds later.","Lin Yuan nodded at Liu Wencheng and strode back to Sequence #91’s stone pillar.","The battle between Mu Yan and Wu Ting and Mu Yan and Liu Hong had left the audience’s hearts pumping, and there were strategies used during the fights. Both sides had used their secret weapons to counter each other.","Since they were all exceptional spirit qi professionals, the details of the battle had all played out beautifully. Both battles were worthy of being used as case studies in the lessons of any school.","Compared to those battles, this battle with Lin Yuan was much simpler. All he had done was raise his hand. He had not even summoned any feys.","This was enough to burn up both of Mu Yan’s Ice Vein Frozen Bats. Even Mu Yan had vanished.","No one was naive enough to think that the Hot Ice Boiling Mouse’s flames had accidentally burned up Mu Yan.","Lin Yuan and Mu Yan’s match could be described as strange. After the momentary shock, Tian Ningning scratched her head and chuckled wryly. She did not know how to begin writing about such a fight because she had no idea what she had just seen.","However, the draft needed to come out 20 minutes after the match. Tian Ningning could not wait until Lin Yuan was done with the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking to call him and ask him about what had happened.","After pondering for a moment, Tian Ningning called Liu Hao.","Once Liu Hao picked up, Tian Ningning immediately said, “Big Brother Hao, did you happen to watch the match between Lord Lin Yuan and Mu Yan?","“I don’t understand how Lord Lin Yuan managed to defeat Mu Yan. Are you able to contact a few high-class Creation Masters who can analyze the situation?”","Tian Ningning had anticipated that this task would not be easy. The difficulty came from being able to understand the techniques used by Lin Yuan and the others!","It was not just Lin Yuan. Liu Jie, Zong Ze, and the rest were all elites, and it would not be easy to see through their techniques!","However, not even the boldest person dared to make wild conjunctions.","As the manager of Star Web’s reporters, Liu Hao needed to watch all the matches on Star Web.","Tian Ningning’s phone call had come at the right time. Even if she had not called him, he would be calling her.","The smaller reporters could write the battle records as they saw fit and did not need to take responsibility for what they wrote. However, Star Web’s official reporters needed to take responsibility for every single one of their words.","Liu Hao had been afraid that the rookie Tian Ningning would forget her duty.","But now that she called him, Liu Hao praised her to himself. He really liked principled people.","“Ningning, I was afraid of such a thing happening and invited a pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master just for this. I will send him over to analyze the abilities displayed by Lin Yuan. You just continue to observe the next match.”","Tian Ningning nodded. She was really looking forward to the analysis of Lin Yuan’s abilities that the Class 4 Creation Master came up with.","This was partly because she needed to do her job but also because she was curious about Lin Yuan’s abilities.","Given that even an experienced Star Web reporter like Tian Ningning felt this way, it was unsurprising that the audience in the commentators and hosts’ live-streaming rooms had already filled the comment section with an endless stream of words. All of them were expressing their shock and amazement.","Lin Yuan’s actions were akin to that of a sun deity who had descended from the heavens and could thus set fire to entities by just raising his hand.","He truly lived up to his title of ‘Miracle’.","The battle that Mu Yan had triggered had left audiences with such overwhelming delight and astoundment!","Lin Yuan had not expected such a reaction at all.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had reached Suzerain/Myth II. It overwhelmed the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats in both quality and grade. So it was only to be expected that it would be able to kill them instantaneously.","Lin Yuan had nurtured the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom with only the best methods from the moment it was spirit locked by Morbius. It would be difficult for even other Suzerain/Myth II feys to stand toe-to-toe with it.","Lin Yuan had killed Mu Yan instantaneously because he understood her wishes. Since she wanted to see how large the gap between them was, he would show it to her. It would be much better to show her the truth than to lie to her!","Tian Ningning and the rest did not understand Lin Yuan’s methods, but some of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had guessed what Lin Yuan did.","There were a few feys that were very sensitive to the aura of vitality and elemental energy. When Lin Yuan raised his hand, he had released an aura of vitality.","This aura had been carried by the wind and spread out in all directions. It was very similar to the spores released by fungi-species fey.","It was this aura that had injected the two Ice Vein Frozen Bats and caused them to be set on fire.","Not even Liu Jie had witnessed this move before, much less Xia Qing, Zong Ze, and the rest.","All of them had their own secret weapons. This was what made these battles interesting!","Liu Jie and Xia Qing, who were Sequence #1 and Sequence #2 respectively, knew that they were about to be called to battle soon.","Once it reached Lin Yuan’s turn, he would choose to challenge both of them.","They knew that Lin Yuan’s goal was Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Both Liu Jie and Xia Qing were looking forward to battling Lin Yuan.","Xia Qing turned to Liu Jie, who was sitting next to her, and said with a grin, “Big Brother Liu, I am glad I gave up the spot of Sequence #1 to you last time. It gave me the chance to be the first to battle Lin Tuan.","“I know that you are stronger than me now. I followed the Spirit Guards while they went around to places that have been overtaken by carcinoma feys, so I am well aware of the might of a Myth Breed carcinoma fey.","“I will do my best to force Lin Yuan to reveal as many of his secret weapons as I can. The highlight of the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking will be the battle between you and Lin Yuan!”","Liu Jie looked deeply into Xia Qing’s eyes. He did not agree with what she said about giving up the spot of Sequence #1 to him.","Last year, he had already taken control of more than 20 insect-species carcinoma feys, and they had all reached Diamond grade at least. In a fight between him and Xia Qing, he stood a higher chance of winning.","After all, she had a limited number of feys. Some of his carcinoma feys’ abilities could target her feys specifically.","However, Liu Jie was very interested in what Xia Qing said about forcing Lin Yuan to reveal as many of his secret weapons as possible.","Lin Yuan would only use feys that were Myth III and below during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. There was no way he would use secret weapons that were beyond the power of the younger generation.","He was much too mysterious. Although Liu Jie was extremely close to Lin Yuan, he had no idea how deep the well of Lin Yuan’s power went.","Liu Jie only had one objective for this battle, which was to prove himself. He wanted to prove that after his two years of growth, he finally deserved the duty of being Lin Yuan’s retainer. Liu Jie had never stopped working hard with this goal in mind.","When Elegance took control of the insect-species carcinoma feys, Liu Jie had to endure the vicious attacks of the insect-species carcinoma feys before the psychotoxins came into effect and took control of the insect-species carcinoma feys’ spiritual energy and soul.","Liu Jie had only managed to grit his teeth and push on to become the main world’s true Heart of Insect Swarm because he never lost sight of this goal."]},{"number":2685,"title":"Chapter 2685 Time for Lin Yuan to Make His Move!","paragraphs":["2685 Time for Lin Yuan to Make His Move!","The battle between Lin Yuan and Mu Yan led to a torrent of comments on Star Web. The surge of comments centered around Lin Yuan did not stop even when the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were battling.","Lin Yuan had not demonstrated such abilities during his fight with the Freedom Federation envoy group. At that time, he had pulled out all the stops and used all of his secret weapons.","This meant that Lin Yuan had prepared such a powerful secret weapon in the past year.","More importantly, as more and more high-class Creation Masters offered their expertise and analysis, Lin Yuan’s method was peeled apart, and it could be confirmed that he was using a fungi-species fey that could release spores and that he had become an A-rank spirit qi professional at just 19 years of age.","Spirit qi professionals who achieved A-rank before they reached 30 years old were considered bona fide geniuses!","Lin Yuan’s current power already exceeded the comprehension of those around him.","If one could be called a genius by becoming an A-rank spirit qi professional before one reached 30 years old, what did that make Lin Yuan? A monster among geniuses?","For the next 20 matches, none of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence chose to challenge Lin Yuan.","This was not because none of them wanted to challenge their idol as a means of showing respect to him, like Mu Yan did. But after they understood Lin Yuan’s power, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had to consider one thing. Did they have the right to show respect to Lin Yuan?","After last year’s thrilling Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Mu Yan and every other member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence began viewing Lin Yuan as their idol. This even applied to Gao Feng, who was Lin Yuan’s good friend.","Lin Yuan’s leadership skills, execution skills, and control over the sea of flowers had been the picture of brilliant elegance. It had been so splendid that no one who witnessed it could forget about it.","Given that these members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence had been selected from their combined abilities and had not single-mindedly fought for power, only three of them made it into the top 80 ranks.","As the manager of Radiance Sacred Hall, Liu Wencheng had anticipated this!","They had changed the format of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. It no longer just tested their power and character. Thus, the newly selected members were weaker than previous generations when it came to power.","However, given that they managed to make it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence, they were all worth nurturing.","The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence could only retain their position for a decade at the most. Alternatively, they would have to step down once they reached 30 years old.","In less than ten years, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would all meet the criteria of the new format. This would allow the Radiance Federation to nurture a generation of more well-rounded leaders.","In the face of the calamity that was the dead spirits crisis, everything became centered around stopping the dead spirits.","The Radiance Federation could afford to wait for ten years.","At this moment, a giant dragon lizard that was three-stories tall snapped the neck of a purple-maned lion with one bite. This put the end to a bloody battle.","“Sequence #92 Violent Lizard Zheng Dui has won and will rise to the rank Sequence #76! The original Sequence #76 Beast Army Lu Huai will become Sequence #92. The challenges will continue as per the rules.”","Lu Huai looked at Zheng Dui, who had just defeated him with frustration. Zheng Dui’s fey had completely countered him and had annoyingly hit all of his weak points. Even after using his entire beast army, he had only managed to kill two lizard dragons and had not managed to take down this giant lizard dragon.","Although he had fallen to Sequence #92, he could still issue challenges as the original Sequence #76.","Lu Huai had already selected his targets and would not have a problem making it into the top 70 ranks.","Zheng Dui could counter him, but there were also others who could counter Zheng Dui. Zheng Dui might technically be Sequence #76 now, but there was always a chance of someone pushing him out of that position.","During the yearly Radiance Hundred Sequence selections, many members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence forcefully climbed the ranks, even if it meant that they had to reveal their secret weapons.","This was not just so they could secure glory for themselves but also because they hoped that this would save them from elimination in next year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence.","All of them had started as rookies and slowly grown step by step. When they were rookies, they had also eliminated veterans. Now that they were the veterans, they did not dare to underestimate the rookies.","When Zheng Dui and Lu Huai returned to their seats, all of the audience on Star Web, the reporters and commentators who had experience with such large-scale events held their breaths.","Now, it was time for Lin Yuan to pick his opponents!","All of them were looking forward to this.","Liu Wencheng fixed his fiery gaze on Liu Wencheng and raised his hand before exclaiming,","“Next, Sequence #91 Miracle Lin Yuan will pick his opponents. Lin Yuan, who will you be challenging?”","Lin Yuan stood up from his seat a second time.","He turned to look toward Long Tao, Xia Qing, and Liu Jie.","Since he was going to raise the spirits of the citizens of the Radiance Federation, he had to put on a good show in these next three matches.","While Mu Yan and the rest had been stunned by Lin Yuan during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and began viewing him as their goal, this was the way that Lin Yuan viewed Long Tao!","When Lin Yuan first left the small area that was the Xia Region, he went to the more developed area, which was Redbud City. But he did not stay there for long before he headed to the Royal Capital.","The battle between Long Tao and the tea attendants demonstrated how truly epic the world of feys could be and showed Lin Yuan the power of the upper echelon of the younger generation!","This had left a visceral impression on Lin Yuan.","Now, Lin Yuan also wanted to do the same.","During the last Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Long Tao had placed second. However, Xia Qing had given up her position of Sequence #1 to Liu Jie before defeating Long Tao, causing him to eventually take the position of Sequence #5.","Lin Yuan looked at Liu Wencheng and said loudly, “I would like to challenge Sequence #5, Vast Sea Long Tao.”","Long Tao stood up when he heard Lin Yuan call out his name. It was an honor to be selected by Lin Yuan.","Long Tao assumed that Lin Yuan would pick Liu Jie or Xia Qing first.","Long Tao had become Iron Prison’s disciple. Iron Prison’s disciplining of Long Tao was extremely strict.","It was just a shame that Long Tao had only contracted five feys, so his path had already been set.","After contracting the fey with the barren bloodline, Long Tao could not contract any more feys.","Hence, his only secret weapon was his fey with the barren bloodline.","Long Tao had the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus, two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes, Wave Halberd Killer Whale, and the Reef Sturgeon that he rarely used. He had used the water-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls he obtained from Lin Yuan to evolve these five feys’ bloodlines before he evolved them to Myth Breed.","Long Tao had only attained his current achievements and power because of Lin Yuan.","Despite knowing that he could not defeat Lin Yuan, Long Tao was going to give his all in this fight.","Long Tao walked over to the arena. After glancing at Lin Yuan in the distance, Long Tao was momentarily silent but did not summon his feys.","The Reef Sturgeon was akin to a moving fortress in battle. Long Tao just needed to climb aboard the Reef Sturgeon’s back, and it would be able to defend him.","Lin Yuan had not selected him because he wanted to defeat him. Rather, it was so they could put on a show.","Thus, there was no way that Lin Yuan would attack him directly.","Long Tao did not intend to use the Reef Sturgeon in this battle.","The two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes were skilled at attacking and controlling a large area. After they evolved to Myth Breed, one of them became more skilled at attacking while the other became more skilled at controlling. When these two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes worked alongside the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus, they would create a territory of water.","As for the Wave Halberd Killer Whale, it was the core of Long Tao’s five feys. Its abilities and exclusive skills could condense the energy from the other four feys to roll grades to do combat.","Whenever Dragon Gate Guild Club fought against powerful opponents during large tournaments and Star Web battles, Long Tao always used the Wave Halberd Killer Whale.","However, that was because Long Tao did not want to reveal the fey with the barren bloodline that he had contracted.","It required a large amount of energy to use the fey with the barren bloodline that Long Tao had contracted. If Long Tao used the Wave Halberd Killer Whale to attack Lin Yuan, he would not have enough energy left in his body to use his fey with the barren bloodline.","Thus, for this battle, Long Tao only summoned the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfish.","The Myth Breed Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus was now longer than 800 meters. The main-dragon-species bloodline in its body had been fully activated. Thus, its dragon might had transformed completely.","As a terrifying-dragon-species fey, every part of the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus was a powerful and deadly weapon.","The two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes floated in the sky, and their tentacles, which were almost 100 meters long, hung down from their caps, releasing a light shower of misty rain.","The Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus roared. In an instant, the sea gathered around the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus.","Lin Yuan did not rush to summon his feys. Instead, he used True Data to check on the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus.","[Fey Name]: Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus","[Fey Species]: Mosasaurus species/Emperor Dragon genus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (7/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Whirl Flow]: Stir up the water region and cause extreme suction flow in the water.","[Eight Dragon Shadows]: The dragon shadow moved and transformed into eight dragon shadows. Each dragon shadow possess 60% of the original body’s attributes.","[Sea Bite]: Control the flow of the sea to form a bite. The biting force is equivalent to the biting force of the original body.","[Sea Emperor’s Dragon Breath]: Shoot out a destructive breath that belongs to the emperor dragons.","[Wrath of the Ocean]: Utilize all of the innate energy within the ocean to conduct a devastating tremor. The extreme tremor within the water has the power to destroy everything within the sea region.","[Water World Block]: Condense the water-elemental energy in the territory of water created, causing the water-elemental energy to lose its attributes. An enclosed elemental space will be created, and it will block out all external energy. It can also be used to seal in the target.","[Barren Ancient Dragon Might]: The dragon might will solidify and form an entity with half the power of the main body. This entity will be able to deter and intimidate targets to a certain extent. The affected target will experience intensified elemental damage and lose its fighting spirit temporarily.","Exclusive Skill:","[Water Overseer]: Delicate control when using the power of water and can control the flow of water.","[Extremity of Sea]: Gather water elements and form rivers. Allow the rivers to flow into the sea and control a portion of the sea region.","[Reverse Rolling Sea Pressure]: With its body as the base, all of the water produced will irrigate the base before the solid territory of water will crash onto the target to restrict its movements and destroy its body. The ability can only be negated by elemental abilities of the same type. Other types of elemental energy will be absorbed by the water-elemental energy.","Now, Lin Yuan had a certain degree of understanding of the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ power.","Zhou Luo had also contracted the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus, but he had obtained it from Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","Zhou Luo’s Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus had not reached Suzerain/Myth and was only Diamond/Fantasy.","Zhou Luo had almost died alongside Lin Yuan and Liu Jie in the evolving water world dimensional rift. If it was not for him, Lin Yuan and Liu Jie might have been stuck there forever. Thus, since then, Lin Yuan always took good care of Zhou Luo and provided him with the best resources.","Thus, Zhou Luo’s Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ abilities were even more excellent than Long Tao’s Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus.","Luckily, Long Tao had used water-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls to activate the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ bloodline before he evolved it to Myth Breed. This allowed the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus to manifest strong abilities such as Barren Ancient Dragon Might and Reverse Rolling Sea Pressure.","Lin Yuan did not check on the two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes because he had already done so in the past.","The two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes had decent controlling and attacking abilities, which were precious to Fantasy Breed feys. But for Myth Breed feys, functional abilities were the most important!","Long Tao’s two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes lacked functional abilities and could not be considered the top tier of feys.","Long Tao had discussed his feys with Lin Yuan in the past.","Because he had contracted his fey when he was very young, he was now unable to match up to Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and the rest.","Nonetheless, he had no choice but to accept this. There was nothing he could do to change his circumstances.","Otherwise, he would not have contracted the Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes and Reef Sturgeon.","When Lin Yuan saw that Long Tao had not summoned the Wave Halberd Killer Whale, he knew that Long Tao had successfully nurtured his fey with the barren bloodline and that he intended to use it during this battle.","Lin Yuan smiled and raised his hand, summoning Blackie.","The dragon-species feys that Long Tao had contracted were famous. He was the only member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who only contracted feys with the dragon-species bloodline.","But when it came to feys with the dragon-species bloodline, Lin Yuan did not fear any other member of the younger generation!","When Lin Yuan evolved Blackie to Myth Breed, it had become a clawed-dragon-species/five-clawed-dragon genus dragon!"]},{"number":2686,"title":"Chapter 2686 Appearance of the Barren Beast!","paragraphs":["2686 Appearance of the Barren Beast!","It was considered a stellar dragon-species fey.","Long Tao’s Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes were a far cry from Blackie!","Blackie was now a true main dragon, and a remarkable one at that.","Blackie let out a grand and drawn-out dragon cry next to Lin Yuan as before, twisting and circling above his head.","Thick black clouds gathered above the arena.","Blackie let out another roar.","As a water-type main dragon, Blackie’s bloodline power could exert pressure on the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes.","The Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ aura lost its vigor.","Dragon-species feys competed with each other in terms of their bloodlines. Blackie promptly took control of the sea created by the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus.","The Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus could still use its abilities and exclusive skills but could not use the sea to put pressure on Blackie.","Although Blackie’s voice was very gentle, it loved battling.","However, Blackie rarely had the opportunity to do combat in the past. Lin Yuan usually used Spirit Essence Explosion to attack as though he was a fey in human form.","Now that Lin Yuan had released Blackie, it finally had the chance to take on enemies with its real body!","Most of Blackie’s abilities were support-type, but it also had controlling abilities.","Without Lin Yuan giving it an instruction, Blackie released a stream of dragon aura.","Blackie’s Diamond ability, Spirit Wrath, could dry up the spirit qi in an area and leave the target in an environment devoid of spirit qi.","In an instant, the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes lost access to the spirit qi around them.","This caused Long Tao’s chest to tighten. It had been a long time since he last felt this way.","Although he still represented the Dragon Gate Guild Club to participate in the S Tournament, Long Tao rarely met opponents that brought out such a feeling in him.","It was Lin Yuan who once again allowed him to feel the anxiousness of facing a strong enemy.","However, Lin Yuan was far too powerful, and Long Tao was momentarily at a loss about what to do next.","Lin Yuan’s pure flood-dragon-species fey had become a true main dragon. It was the five-clawed dragon, which was the rarest and most powerful type of clawed dragon.","The bloodline pressure of this fey on his three feys was already enough to overwhelm him.","The two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes had already lost their fighting spirit, and the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus could only defend but dared not advance.","Long Tao had initially intended to attack first and put some pressure on Lin Yuan.","However, Lin Yuan managed to overwhelm him by just summoning his fey.","Long Tao did not stop issuing orders to the two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes and forced them to release another shower of rain.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to give Blackie an order, Blackie said seriously, “Lin Yuan, I would like the chance to battle freely. I have the confidence to beat these three!”","Lin Yuan did not turn down Blackie’s suggestion and said softly, “Blackie, since you want to battle freely, then go ahead and do your best!”","After hearing this, Blackie used Spirit Judgment Imprisonment.","Spirit Judgment Imprisonment was directed at a target and would make a judgment about the concentration of the target’s spirit qi. If Blackie’s spirit qi was more concentrated than that of the target, the spirit qi in the target’s body would be sealed.","Once a fey’s spiritual power was sealed and was unable to sense the interaction of spirit qi in the surroundings, it would become groundless. It would not even be able to defend against elemental energy!","Long Tao was completely unfamiliar with Blackie’s abilities. After Blackie used Spirit Judgment Imprisonment on the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus, it froze.","Blackie could not be bothered with the two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes that did not even have any more desire to battle.","Blackie slowly flew over as spirit qi condensed on its claws.","It pushed its claws downwards and hit the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ back.","A terrifying-dragon-species fey’s strong suit was defense.","Blackie’s attack was not lethal, and many spectators did not think much of it. They assumed that Lin Yuan’s main dragon was just warming up.","Yet, explosions were suddenly heard from the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ back.","Because of these two attacks, the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ body shape had been altered, and it landed heavily in the water.","Blood-stained water began spreading out from where the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ body lay.","As Lin Yuan sensed Blackie’s attacks, he knew that Blackie had used Spirit Essence Explosion to explode the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus’ back and internal organs.","Although the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus still seemed to be alive, its vitality would soon run out, and it would be unable to participate in the ensuing battle!","Blackie could not be bothered with the two Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes, but it did not forget that this was Lin Yuan’s battle.","Spirit qi gathered on Blackie’s tail and slammed it on the Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes like a whip, crushing their bodies to pieces.","Lin Yuan’s lips twitched when he saw this.","Blackie was a flood-dragon-species fey, but its battle style was even more vicious than that of terrifying-dragon-species feys!","Blackie had easily eliminated three of Long Tao’s feys. If Long Tao wanted to continue battling, the only option he had left would be to summon his fey with the Barren bloodline.","Blackie was about to attack Long Tao before it was stopped by Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan believed that Long Tao wanted to summon the fey with the Barren bloodline in this battle!","Lin Yuan, who was in the midst of the battle, had no idea that Blackie’s graceful battle display had sent all the Star Web live-streaming rooms into a frenzy of comments.","As Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter, Tian Ningning smiled wryly at Blackie before asking questions to the old woman next to her.","The feys that Long Tao contracted had records as he had used them in previous battles.","However, his feys’ powers had all increased. They needed to observe the battle to discern what abilities and exclusive skills the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes had gained!","Yet, Long Tao’s three feys had not had the chance to demonstrate their abilities before they were all killed.","There could only be one possibility for this, which was that Lin Yuan’s main-dragon-species fey was Suzerain/Myth II, but its level and power exceeded that of Long Tao’s three feys!","Lin Yuan had never used this main-dragon-species fey before, but it was clearly not a fey with the Barren bloodline.","Tian Ningning asked the elderly woman respectfully, “Lordess Shen, are you able to explain Lord Lin Yuan’s fey to me so I can write the battle record?”","Shen He relaxed her furrowed brow and said with a bitter smile, “This clawed dragon killed Long Tao’s three feys with a few simple attacks. It didn’t show enough of its powers. I can’t analyze its exact abilities for you. But I can tell you one thing, which is that it is definitely extraordinary! If I hadn’t seen it for myself, I wouldn’t have believed that it only became a five-clawed dragon when it evolved to Myth Breed! I am more curious to know how Lord Lin Yuan managed to nurture this fey.”","Tian Ningning’s lips twitched, but she dared not rebuke this pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master Shen He.","However, she really wanted give Shen He a reminder.","Lordess Shen He, you have gone off-topic! Don’t forget that you are here to help our special teams write our reports!","Lin Yuan looked at Long Tao. By now, Long Tao had summoned the Reef Sturgeon and was standing on its back.","The Reef Sturgeon was just floating on the blood-soaked sea. Long Tao had only summoned three feys to start with because he wanted to conserve spiritual power.","But now, all three of them had been killed almost instantaneously by Lin Yuan! Long Tao had barely used any of the energy in his body.","Long Tao met Lin Yuan’s gaze without feeling even the slightest hint of disappointment. His eyes were filled with amazement and respect for Lin Yuan’s power.","“Ah Yuan, I have already evolved it to Suzerain X/pinnacle Myth II. I actually have you to thank for this!”","Lin Yuan knew that Long Tao was about to reveal his fey with the Barren bloodline!","Lin Yuan had also invited Long Tao to the gathering two days ago. But Long Tao had been unable to attend because he was in the middle of a critical period of evolving his fey with the Barren bloodline’s bloodline.","Lin Yuan had sent Long Tao pure water-elemental energy concocted in the Element Well as well as a water-type elemental doll.","It seemed that Long Tao had been successful!","There were strong spiritual fluctuations rippling out from Long Tao’s body. Lin Yuan immediately sensed the strong aura that was unique to feys with the Barren bloodline.","A giant fish that was six meters long and had speckled bird wings and shiny gold scales appeared in the sea with a flash.","Tens of whirlpools immediately appeared on the surface of the sea. It was as though there was an eye staring out of the center of every whirlpool.","From the fey’s graceful and swan-like appearance, Lin Yuan knew what Long Tao’s fey with the Barren bloodline was.","The Victory Fish was the most mystical water-type fey with the Barren bloodline.","The Victory Fish was recorded in the Catalog of Mountains and Seas.","“Victory Fish, with the body of a fish and wings of a bird, it has a voice of mandarin ducks, and seeing one is akin to looking at a settlement of water.”","It was said that the Victory Fish could predict fortunes but it was a beast of disaster. Water-related calamities followed it wherever it went!","At first, Blackie had managed to overwhelm the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus and Deep Blue Dragon Jellyfishes with its bloodline power, thereby taking control of the sea.","But with the appearance of the Victory Fish, Blackie’s control over the water had decreased significantly.","However, as a clawed dragon, and a five-clawed dragon to boot, there was no guarantee that Blackie would lose control of the water to the Victory Fish!","As long as the Victory Fish did not take full control of the water, its threat to Lin Yuan would be significantly discounted!","Lin Yuan did not know where the Victory Fish was hiding in the water, so he used True Data to scan through the water. He immediately discovered the Victory Fish’s location.","[Fey Name]: Victory Fish","[Fey Species]: Barren-species/winged-fish species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Mandarin Duck Voice]: In order to generate vibrations, a fish roar will be released with the voice of mandarin ducks. Those who hear this voice will become paralyzed, and there is also a chance that the listener’s soul will be put to sleep.","[Curtain of Wings]: The two wings will dissolve into the water and absorb water-elemental energy to produce an enormous curtain of wings that can defend against external damage. As long as the curtain of wings is not damaged, external damage will be absorbed and transformed into energy that can be stored.","[Sea Disaster]: The water will be flooded with curse power, and the lifeforms within the cursed water will be drained to boost the Victory Fish’s power.","[Victory Arrow]: The body will turn into a bow, and the two wings will become the string. The water will form a sharp arrow that can penetrate the target. The penetrated target will be cursed.","[Heavenly Water Stamp]: A heavenly water stamp can be formed on any target that is within a body of water that is also in contact with the Victory Fish. Each time the target’s energy is replenished, the Victory Fish’s energy will also be replenished. When the target uses up its energy, the Victory fish can choose to also use up some of its energy to lower its own drain of energy.","[Victorious Water Mist]: The Victory Fish’s energy will be used up and released via the water. The water will transform into mist. When the Victory Mist is within the mist, it will be healed by the water. Any injured targets within the mist will also be healed.","[Victorious Body Transformed Arrows]: The Victory Fish’s body will be sacrificed and transformed into arrows. The arrows will attack a target. Its curse effects will also be transformed into deadly effects and applied to the arrows.","Exclusive Skill:","[Revived Wings]: When the wings are transformed into a curtain of wings, new ones can be grown. As long as the curtain of wings exists, the energy required to grow the new wings will be lowered by half.","[Double Life Arrows]: Each time the curtain of wings and the transformation of the Victory Fish’s body into arrows to attack a target is in effect, the attacks will absorb the energy from the surroundings and split up, causing double the damage.","[Victory Forms Secret Stone]: Before the body is deconstructed, a victory stone will be formed in the fish’s stomach. The victory stone will absorb curse energy from the surroundings, and the Victory Fish can be reincarnated through the victory stone.","After reading the Victory Fish’s True Data, Lin Yuan felt that the Victory Fish’s abilities were just as impressive as that of Zong Ze’s Fiery Sky Hou!","Although it was not as well-rounded as Shiny’s’ abilities, its capability of taking on many enemies at once was the strongest that Lin Yuan had ever seen from a fey!","Mandarin Duck Voice’s paralyzing effect was rather common. It would be easy to use blessing effects to neutralize paralyzing effects.","However, its true controlling effects came from the possibility of it putting a soul to sleep.","Putting a soul to sleep was not the same as putting the spirit to sleep. When the spirit was asleep, it could be awakened by external forces. But once the soul was asleep, only the support from feys that had awakening abilities would be effective. It would be very difficult for the soul to wake up on its own.","It was just unlucky for Long Tao and the Victory Fish that Lin Yuan had two souls and that the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was able to protect his souls.","Although Lin Yuan would be paralyzed by Mandarin Duck Voice, his soul would not be put to sleep.","The abilities that Lin Yuan was truly interested in were Curtain of Wings and Revived Wings.","Curtain of Wings was an extremely strong defensive and endurance ability.","The Victory Fish only had one pair of wings, so it could only produce one Curtain of Wings.","But if it used Revived Wings as well, the Victory Fish would be able to control many Curtain of Wings."]},{"number":2687,"title":"Chapter 2687 Fearsome True Spirit Five Changes!","paragraphs":["2687 Fearsome True Spirit Five Changes!","Curtain of Wings was a defensive form produced when the Victory Fish dissolved into water and ensnared water-elemental energy.","When it is hit by external attacks, it can absorb the attack and transform it into energy that it will store.","This defensive ability also had endurance effects, enabling the Victory Fish to take on multiple opponents.","One Curtain of Wings would be enough to turn the tide in a battle.","But when it used Revived Wings, it would be able to grow more wings. When it grew more wings when it already had a pair, it would only require half of the initial amount of energy.","Given a fey with the Barren bloodline’s store of energy, it would be able to put up four Curtain of Wings in a battle without much effort.","Sea Disaster was a range-based curse ability. Other lifeforms in the water where the Victory Fish was located would all be cursed.","The Victory Fish had many curse effects and would eventually cause the other lifeforms to wither and die.","The longer the lifeforms were under the effects of the curses, the more their battle abilities would fall.","Victory Arrow would allow the Victory Fish to do combat with water elements. Every jet of water it produced was extremely powerful and would also carry curse effects when they made contact with the target.","Although the feys that flew in the sky would not be cursed by the Victory Fish that was in the sea, they would be affected by the curse once they were hit by one of the Victory Arrows.","The Platinum ability Heavenly Water Stamp was the Victory Fish’s main endurance ability.","The more lifeforms there were in the sea, the quicker the Victory Fish’s vitality would be replenished.","In a battle between Long Tao and Liu Jie, this ability would be a godsend for Long Tao. But with Lin Yuan, Heavenly Water Stamp was rather useless!","Lin Yuan was skilled at individual combat and would not send out many feys at once to engage in attrition warfare.","The Victory Fish’s Diamond ability, Victorious Water Mist, was both a lethal and healing ability. Just like Heavenly Water Stamp, it was a replenishing ability that was suited for taking on many enemies at once.","It would also be able to heal the Victory Fish when it was only facing a few enemies. However, the healing effects would be greatly discounted.","Victorious Water Mist would allow the Victory Fish’s combat techniques to extend past water regions.","The water mist would be dispersed in the air, turning the sky into the Victory Fish’s battleground as well.","Victorious Body Transformed Arrows would strengthen Victory Arrows.","Victory Arrow controlled the water in the surroundings while Victorious Body Transformed Arrows would turn the Victory Fish’s body into streams of water in the shape of arrows that would attack the enemy.","The curse effects would result in a deadly effect when the Victory Fish’s body was deconstructed. There was a chance that the attack would immediately kill the target.","The exclusive skill Double Life Arrows strengthened the effects of Victory Arrow and Victorious Body Transformed Arrows. During each attack, the energy in the surroundings would be used to cause double damage to the target.","An exclusive skill like this was very rare.","This exclusive skill could double the impact of the attack. It was likely that such an ability would only be seen in feys with the Barren bloodline.","The Victory Fish’s Myth Breed exclusive skill was called Victory Forms Secret Stone.","Victory Forms Secret Stone and the Suzerain ability Victorious Body Transformed Arrows could be linked.","Normally, due to the deconstruction effects of Victorious Body Transformed Arrows, the Victory Fish would be killed. But with the exclusive skill Victory Forms Secret Stone, the Victory Fish could be revived by eating the victory stone, allowing it to rejoin the battle.","Lin Yuan had a complete understanding of every one of the Victory Fish’s abilities.","Long Tao was currently planning on using the Victory Fish to ambush Lin Yuan and Blackie.","It went without saying that Lin Yuan would not give Long Tao the opportunity to do so. Instead, he was going to use Long Tao’s battle plans to counter him!","By now, mist was already draping over the surface of the sea. Lin Yuan knew that the Victory Fish had used Victorious Water Mist.","However, this mist would not be able to affect Blackie’s vision or cause it any damage.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and summoned Chimey. Chimey appeared next to Lin Yuan with a burst of beautiful sacred fire. All clouds in a 15-kilometer radius around Chimey were rapidly evaporated.","With a soft cry, tens of thousands of sparrows formed from musical notes appeared and began flying around Chimey.","Once he summoned the Victory Fish, Long Tao no longer had any other combat moves he could utilize. Even if he ended up losing his battle, he would put up a good fight!","Long Tao was well aware that neither Chimey nor the black-clawed dragon were Lin Yuan’s secret weapons. But he had already played his final card by summoning the Victory Fish.","Long Tao was at a disadvantage in this battle, but he was a strategy specialist.","Long Tao ordered the Victory Fish to use Victorious Body Transformed Arrows to attack Lin Yuan.","All was fair in love and war. Long Tao knew that if he could kill Lin Yuan instantaneously, he would be able to win this battle.","However, not only did Lin Yuan not give Long Tao the chance to do so, but he could even see the Victory Fish’s underwater movements with complete clarity.","Lin Yuan issued a battle order to Blackie through his mind.","Blackie used True Spirit Five Changes. It released its claws, and each claw turned into a split body.","The split bodies possessed Blackie’s full abilities and would not disappear after they were attacked. They could be considered invincible.","Each time the bodies were destroyed, Blackie could produce new ones by using spiritual power.","True Spirit Five Changes was an exclusive skill of clawed dragons. But this ability only manifested in five-clawed dragons.","With the inclusion of Blackie’s main body, there were now six five-clawed dragons flying in the sky.","The five-clawed dragons stormed the sea and used Spirit Essence Explosion while clustering around the Victory Fish.","The Victory Fish did not even have the chance to emerge from the surface of the water.","Blackie’s split bodies rushed to take on both Victory Arrow and Victorious Body Transformed Arrows without fear of death.","Once the split bodies produced by True Spirit Five Changes were destroyed, new ones formed. This left Long Tao in disbelief.","He thought that the Victory Fish was exceptionally formidable. But now, it seemed that it was not as strong as he thought!","Lin Yuan did not summon his fey with the Barren bloodline He had managed to overwhelm the Victory Fish with just a regular fey.","However, as a true five-clawed dragon, Lin Yuan’s fey was extremely valuable and had the same standard of merit as a fey with the Barren bloodline!","The longer he fought the ferocious Blackie, the braver Long Tao became. However, he also had an increasingly strong feeling that something was wrong.","The Victory Fish had already activated four Curtain of Wings. It had absorbed a significant amount of energy from the repeated attacks from Blackie’s five split bodies. But it was as though this five-clawed dragon had an endless supply of energy!","Meanwhile, the Victory Fish’s store of energy was about to run out.","The Victory Fish would only be able to handle around ten more attacks from the five-clawed dragon before it ran out of energy and could no longer put up a defense.","Star Web’s commentators and hosts were currently animatedly and passionately narrating the battle.","None of them were faking their emotions.","These Star Web hosts and commentators rarely had the chance to narrate such a high-quality battle.","Feys with the Barren bloodline were iconic of the Radiance Federation.","They were always shrouded in mystery and rarely made an appearance.","But the power demonstrated by the Victory Fish seemed to pale in comparison to Blackie.","But those who were intelligent knew that this was because the Victory Fish was battling a five-clawed dragon that belonged to Lin Yuan. Any other fey would already have been crushed to pieces by the Victory Fish’s attacks.","Poison Beauty and Lu Shuang’s live streams were exploding with popularity.","Lu Shuang was already very popular. But after the battle with Black, her popularity skyrocketed to a new level.","Poison Beauty’s popularity had been rather mild previously. But she managed to emerge as a dark horse with her eloquence and forked tongue.","However, it was difficult for small hosts to make it into the big leagues and gain popularity with the masses.","Poison Beauty only gained more attention after being matched with Lin Yuan multiple times and leveraging his popularity.","Eventually, she managed to be signed by the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce and became an auctioneer on Star Web! She was in charge of auctioning off the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce’s luxury goods on Star Web.","Listen had noticed Poison Beauty’s potential and gave her a helping hand. She also put in effort and, with opportune factors in her favor, managed to become one of the biggest hosts.","She eventually became Star Web’s biggest host that year and was specially invited by Star Web’s officials to live stream and host the battles.","Poison Beauty understood her role and knew how important this event was. She did not try to incorporate any performance effects. Rather, she stuck to doing what she did best and seriously analyzed the battles.","“Everyone, please try not to send comments while the battles are ongoing. Only post comments if you have legitimate questions! That will make it easier for me to answer all your questions! Just now, someone asked why a fey with the Barren bloodline can’t seem to beat a regular fey.","“Let me correct this perspective. The fey that Lord Lin Yuan is using is not a run-of-the-mill fey. It is a true main dragon and a five-clawed dragon to boot! Main-dragon-species feys are highly revered. It cannot be viewed as a regular fey.","“I never thought that a Myth II fey’s bloodline could reach such a level. A fey’s strength is determined by how it was nurtured. Long Tao’s fey with the Barren bloodline is very strong, and there are very few members of the younger generation who can compete with him. But it is evident that Lord Lin Yuan’s fey is slightly stronger.","“I don’t think there is any uncertainty about the outcome of this battle. Lord Lin Yuan hasn’t used his signature sparrow. All it has been doing is staying by his side to protect him.”","In Poison Beauty’s previous live streams, she had lavished praise on Lin Yuan in order to gain more attention. This eventually turned into a habit.","However, she was not trying to do that now.","The formidability that Lin Yuan had displayed was undeniable.","Long Tao laughed wryly. The Victory Fish had burned to the end of its wick while fighting the clawed dragon. It could not fight anymore!","Long Tao did not bother to push on with a meaningless battle. Instead, he raised his hand before slamming it down forcefully. This was the way that the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence signaled that they were surrendering.","If they continued fighting, it would only end with the Victory Fish being pulverized by the five-clawed dragon.","Long Tao knew of the power of a clawed dragon’s claws and tail.","Without the defense from the ability Curtain of Wings, any attack that made contact with the Victory fish would break apart its scales and leave a bloody hole in its body.","There was still one thing that Long Tao did not understand, which was how the clawed dragon managed to possessed such strong endurance. It did not show any signs of weakening even after launching repeated attacks!","Normally, a Myth II dragon-species fey would not have so much energy to spare.","Long Tao had no idea that Lin Yuan had been using Blackie as a support fey.","This battle established Blackie’s prowess.","After a vicious battle, Blackie let out a comfortable cry before flying over to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan leaped up onto Blackie’s back and rode the five-clawed dragon up to the sky before looking down at the stone pillars around him.","As the victor, Lin Yuan could pick his next opponent.","Despite being summoned by Lin Yuan, Chimey had yet to participate in the combat. It sulkily flapped its wings next to Lin Yuan and let out a woeful cry to express how it was feeling.","Lin Yuan soothed Chimey while looking over at Xia Qing.","Lin Yuan knew that Xia Qing was very strong. Zong Ze and Gu Lang both mentioned that they had lost to her in combat.","However, Lin Yuan had never fought with Xia Qing before. He did not even know what feys Xia Qing had.","Lin Yuan had no idea that while he was looking at Chimey, his action of leaping onto Blackie’s back had come across so dashing that he had stupefied many spectators. Lin Yuan was much more gallant than that member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who had tried to act suave!","Xia Qing and Lin Yuan locked eyes. She stood up before Lin Yuan even called out her name. She fixed her fiery gaze on him and waved her fists, signaling that she was going to do her best in the battle.","Lin Yuan smiled. That was exactly what he wanted.","Chimey had yet to participate in a battle since evolving to Myth Breed. Lin Yuan intended to use Chimey in the battle against Xia Qing.","If Chimey was overwhelmed during the fight with Xia Qing, Lin Yuan would send out other feys in accordance with Xia Qing’s feys.","After Xia Qing stood up, Lin Yuan yelled out Xia Qing’s name to Liu Wencheng. They still needed to go along with the process.","Just like Long Tao, Xia Qing summoned her fey after entering the arena.","Lin Yuan suddenly felt a powerful force pressing down on him. The pressure almost caused his heart to burst out of his chest!"]},{"number":2688,"title":"Chapter 2688 Chimey Attacks!","paragraphs":["2688 Chimey Attacks!","After sensing the threat from the pressure, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen released its aura. It formed a barrier of energy around Lin Yuan’s body to block out the pressure.","A dragonfly, over eight meters in length, appeared in front of Xia Qing. It was covered in fiery flames and held a large red ball with its front legs.","This was Xia Qing’s signature fey. However, Xia Qing usually only summoned the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad during battle. She rarely summoned the Star Dragonfly.","The last time that Xia Qing summoned the Star Dragonfly it was only Diamond X/Fantasy V. Now, it had reached Suzerain X/pinnacle Myth II.","Lin Yuan sensed the aura from the Star Dragonfly and realized that the pressure was coming from the ball it was holding with its front legs.","If the ball was enlarged, it would seem like a celestial body!","Liu Jie had once appraised the Star Dragonfly in a conversation with Lin Yuan. He solemnly stated that the Star Dragonfly was the strongest Myth Breed insect-species fey when it came to individual combat. It was much stronger than the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle that had yet to be boosted by the deaths of armies of feys!","Xia Qing had once used the Star Dragonfly to kill Creation Breed feys. This meant that the Star Dragonfly had an impressive ability to roll grades to do battle.","During previous battles, Lin Yuan always used True Data to check on his opponent’s feys before he began fighting. This allowed him to secure the advantage in all situations.","However, this method of combat also took the fun out of fighting.","Lin Yuan felt that he might not need to use Morbius to check on the abilities of Xia Qing’s two feys in this battle. Instead, he could battle her normally. Regardless of how many secret weapons she had, there was no chance of him unexpectedly losing, even if he did have to take a few hits.","Lin Yuan turned and said to Chimey, who was clearly ready to dive into battle, “Chimey, Blackie was the lead in the previous battle, and you didn’t get the chance to join in. Now, it’s your turn to take the lead. Go and have a good fight with these two feys. If you find yourself losing, I will send the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to help you!”","Chimey let out a soft chirp before flapping its wings in front of Lin Yuan, indicating that it did not need help from others.","While Chimey was flapping its wings, glassy flames ignited all over its body, and the sun started to shine even brighter.","Soon, a string of pleasant chirps was released from Chimey’s throat as it used Phoenix Cry.","With the power of a phoenix, Chimey combined the phoenix cry with the birds that were flying around it, imbuing the musical notes in the shape of birds with extremely strong penetrating effects.","After coming into contact with the target, the musical notes let out phoenix cries that would stun and disrupt the target. When they were hit by any impact, the musical notes would also split off to produce new birds.","The beauty from continuous attacks was akin to watching a swarm of birds paying homage to a phoenix!","Chimey’s ability Phoenix Breed Input Sound allowed Chimey to temper the soul of a phoenix-species fey to phoenix breed and inject it into the flying birds. The flying birds would then take on some of the intelligence and spiritual power of a phoenix-species fey. Their abilities would also be improved, allowing them to become partial phoenixes.","The legion of birds flew towards Xia Qing’s Suck Burst Oxygen Toad and Star Dragonfly.","In the midst of this attack, Chimey also used New Day of Light and commandeered the bloodline of a main-phoenix-species fey. The exquisite main-phoenix-species blood and sunlight formed a sun behind Chimey. Under the light of the sun, its depleted energy would be replenished.","This allowed Chimey to substantially boost its attacks.","Chimey’s appearance was just as beautiful as that of Purple Afterglow.","The two different lifeforms exemplified the greatest extent of beauty that could ever manifest in living creatures.","If the dead spirits crisis had not begun and the main world continued holding fey beauty pageants, Chimey would definitely stand a chance to place among the top three!","Xia Qing felt slightly dizzy as she looked at the endless birds swooping around in front of her. Lin Yuan’s pinnacle Myth II sparrow’s attack was almost unbelievably dense!","Xia Qing gave an order to the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, “Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, use Oxygen Bursting Flames.”","The inside of the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s body was half red and half blue. When it was Fantasy Breed, it was around the size of a small building. But now that it was Myth Breed, it was gargantuan!","The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad sucked in a forceful breath.","The air around the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad was pulled in into its mouth forcefully and rapidly.","Soon, patterns of air currents appeared on the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s body, and the flames were fanned by the patterns of air currents.","In an instant, the black flames burned up all the oxygen in the air.","Even from a distance away, Lin Yuan felt as though he was being suffocated.","To any other spirit qi professional, this might spell trouble. If they could not breathe, they would fall unconscious due to a lack of oxygen within five minutes.","However, Lin Yuan’s genetic model had been improved, and he could no longer be measured against regular humans! He could survive for more than half an hour with no issues, even in an environment without oxygen!","Chimey’s source of energy was sunlight. It did not need to breathe to transform external energy.","The burning black flames formed a giant shield of flames that covered Xia Qing, the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, and Star Dragonfly.","The birds that Chimey produced using Phoenix Cry flew straight into the black shield of flames.","Alarm bells rang in Lin Yuan’s head.","He noticed that the black flames had consumption effects.","The energy within the golden birds was absorbed by the black flames, causing the black flames to burn with an even greater flourish.","After noticing this, Lin Yuan did not give Chimey another order.","He had already made himself clear during his conversation with Chimey.","Chimey wanted to fight with its own free will!","Chimey was very talented at battling and would not allow itself to suffer unnecessarily.","Chimey must have a reason for continuing to attack after noticing that the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s black flames were absorbing the energy within the brids.","The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s shield of flames had defended against various energy-based attacks in the past.","After consuming many birds, the black flames were triggered to their maximum extent.","When the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad used the exclusive skill Consuming Fire Stimulation, it could consume flames to recover its own energy and injuries.","It could be said that Xia Qing had started the battle against Lin Yuan on a good note.","Previously, the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad needed to deplete a large amount of energy to use its ability and could not hold on for long during battle. But now, it had the confidence to sustain combat.","Chimey’s eyes were very bright. Instead of drawing back after it realized what was happening, it sent even more birds flying into the black flames.","Many of the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were confused. They did not understand why Lin Yuan allowed his fey to act foolishly. If it continued to give up energy, Xia Qing’s Suck Burst Oxygen Toad would be able to release enough flames to take control of the battle!","The narrators and hosts who were watching this were left at a slight loss about what to say. They could not say that Lin Yuan’s fey was pathetic in battle!","At this moment, the shield of black flames seemed to go out of control, and phoenix cries began ringing out from the black flames.","Chimey let out a soft chirp, and even more birds crashed into the shield of black flames.","After a moment of pondering, Lin Yuan realized what was happening.","The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s shield of black flames only absorbed energy.","When Chimey used Phoenix Breed Input Sound to temper the phoenix-species fey’s soul and inject it into the birds, this could not be absorbed.","Not only were phoenix-species feys unafraid of flames, but there were some powerful main-phoenix-species feys that could be reincarnated through flames.","The black flames expanded and grew until the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad began struggling to maintain control.","When the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s control over the black flames weakened, the partial phoenixes that were capable of individual thought captured control of the black flames.","The flaming birds that were now black in color soared down towards Xia Qing, the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, and Star Dragonfly.","Xia Qing had created this shield to protect herself from being attacked by external energy.","However, Chimey had adapted and used the phoenix bloodline to penetrate the shield.","This was akin to a fully-armored person poking a beehive. One would assume that the armor would be able to block out all damage from the bees. However, the bees were still able to penetrate the armor.","Xia Qing was being put to the test but could not express her grievances.","Chimey was still injecting energy into the shield of black flames. The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad could transform this energy, but it took time.","A pool could be drained. But if water was being poured in too quickly, the pool would still fill up even while it was being drained.","Xia Qing knew that she needed to break free of this situation as soon as possible. Otherwise, the fire birds that could penetrate the shield would only increase in quantity. Once they reached a certain number, her defeat would be sealed!","As such, Xia Qing quickly swung her fist in front of her, and a purple scorpion appeared.","This scorpion was very small. It was only around the size of Xia Qing’s palm.","The scorpion’s tail was raised, and it shone with a crystalline gleam.","After this beautiful scorpion appeared, Xia Qing cried out, “Fire Source Crystal Scorpion, use the exclusive skill Release Fire Body Transformation!”","Xia Qing’s cry could not be heard past the shield, and those outside did not know that Xia Qing was currently poised to lose her battle against Lin Yuan.","At that moment, Xia Qing felt rather ashamed. Lin Yuan had only summoned one fey so far in this battle, but she had already been forced to summon three feys.","When the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion heard Xia Qing’s command, it leaped in front of her and raised its two pincers as well as half of its body before a large amount of fire energy was absorbed into its body.","The Fire Source Crystal Scorpion’s body started to enlarge until it was as enormous as the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad!","All of the black flames had been absorbed by the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion.","It looked as though Xia Qing had just destroyed the defense she had built. But when it came to storing energy, Xia Qing had the upper hand because most of the fire energy the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion absorbed had come from Chimey.","With the ability New Light of Day to replenish it, Chimey had no lack of energy and did not mind such a depletion. After all, regardless of how much energy was used up, it would be replenished by the sun. The sun was Chimey’s charger!","Through its exclusive skill Double Sun Reins, Chimey could strengthen the link between the sun and other suns. Each time Chimey let out a soft chirp, it was singing to the suns. If Chimey wanted to, it could draw on the real sun to replenish its body.","In terms of endurance, Chimey was the strongest of all of Lin Yuan’s feys. Battling Chimey was like trying to measure up to the sun!","The recent crossing of swords was Chimey’s way of testing the waters. It now had a general understanding of its opponent’s power. Now, it was going to get serious!","But before Chimey could make its move, the giant Fire Source Crystal Scorpion that had absorbed all of the fire energy had already viciously swung its tail towards Chimey! There were hundreds of shadows clinging to the tail that would make it extremely difficult for Chimey to dodge and flee.","At the instant that the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion swung its tail towards Chimey, its two pinchers made a chopping motion and formed two dark red crosses.","Chimey felt as though it had just been nailed to the spot by two crosses. It was as though it would end up hurt by the crosses regardless of how it moved.","Chimey had no intention of fleeing. Instead, it used Falling Sky New Day.","The sun within Chimey’s body suddenly descended to the ground and formed a territory charged with the sun’s power around Chimey.","Before the sun’s power ran out, Chimey’s body would be immune to most physical and elemental damage. In such a state, it was very unlikely that Chimey would be harmed in any way.","The attacks from the shadows on the scorpion’s tail and crosses were all deflected by the sun power around Chimey.","After Chimey evolved to Myth Breed, the structure of its power changed drastically. Previously, its combat style depended on the moves it made at present. But now, it mostly relied on using speech as a medium for its spirit to do battle.","In the past, Chimey never used abilities that involved speech as a medium for its spirit.","When most Myth Breed feys used their abilities in battle, their beast states were their strongest forms.","They could only wield more power in their human form than beast form when they reached Immortal Breed.","But when it came to using abilities that involved speech as a medium for the spirit, it would be more effective to use them in human form than beast form!","Chimey had reached Myth II. Even if it did not use treasures like the Spirit Bodhi Fruit, it was still able to change into human form.","Chimey did not think this much during battle and had long forgotten about its large audience.","Chimey shot up to the sky. Soon, its body changed into that of a young girl wearing a blue and gold shawl.","Chimey trod on clumps of clouds, and languid tunes slipped from its lips.","Chimey had begun using Speak Spirit Singer.","As it tapped into its phoenix breed, a silhouette formed around Chimey. As a result, Chimey resembled a celestial maiden."]},{"number":2689,"title":"Chapter 2689 Xia Qing’s Barren Beast!","paragraphs":["2689 Xia Qing’s Barren Beast!","Chimey did not think much when it was in the midst of battle.","It completely forgot about Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ influence in Star Web.","It could be said that Chimey was currently the most famous household name in the Radiance Federation.","In the past, Chimey managed to use just its singing voice to take over the entire Star Web audience.","Ever since Chimey consumed the Spirit Bodhi Fruit and revealed its appearance in human form, it attracted even more appearance-centric fans.","Chimey’s looks were outstanding. But unlike other feys in human form, its beauty was not demonic, and it did not retain any fey features. When Chimey was in human form, even females like Wen Yu were momentarily mesmerized.","Ever since Chimey began aiming to increase its power, it had stopped live streaming on Star Web. There were many discussions ongoing on Star Web that tried to determine Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ current whereabouts.","Previously, they all knew that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess was linked to Black. But later, Black and Lin Yuan were revealed to be the same person. From that point on, they began assuming that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess was a daughter of a secret faction.","It was when Lin Yuan represented the Radiance Federation to take on the Freedom Federation envoy group that those who were close to him found out that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess was actually his fey named Chimey.","Now that Chimey had changed from a fey form to a human form, everyone was astonished. They now all knew that Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess was Lin Yuan’s fey.","The Warm Sun Fund was a blessing that Lin Yuan and Chimey jointly provided to the Radiance Federation.","Xia Qing’s three feys, the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, Star Dragonfly, and Fire Source Crystal Scorpion, all had the power to do battle in human form. However, for regular feys, doing battle in human form would significantly depress their power.","As such, spirit qi professionals rarely instructed their feys to change into human form during battle.","Chimey’s voice was like an aural celebration, and such sounds were rarely heard during battle.","Rivers began appearing one after another in front of Chimey while it sang.","As Chimey continued to sing, flood dragons occasionally rose from the rivers. These flood dragons contained a special energy. It was as though Chimey’s voice was boosting these imageries in some way.","These imageries’ attacks restrained the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion, forcing it to use the fire energy it had just absorbed to defend itself.","The imageries’ attacks were already extremely aggressive to begin with. But as Chimey continued to sing, the figures multiplied.","Chimey’s song boosted the imageries in many ways. The tens of attacks left the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion seriously injured within the short span of three minutes.","Xia Qing was very arrogant. She was filled with indignance at the fact that Lin Yuan had only summoned one fey in their battle.","Initially, she wanted to eliminate Chimey first so that Lin Yuan would have to summon more feys and take her on seriously. But now that she was about to lose this one-on-one battle against Chimey, Xia Qing had no choice but to end this battle as soon as possible.","Lin Yuan was both her idol and an imposing mountain that stood in her way.","In this battle against Lin Yuan, Xia Qing truly realized the size of the gap between her and him.","Nonetheless, the battle was still ongoing, and Xia Qing was never the type to admit defeat.","If they were dueling in real life, Xia Qing would have to restrain herself out of consideration for her and Lin Yuan’s safety.","But given that they were fighting on Star Web, she had Lin Yuan would not be tangibly affected in real life even if she used a self-sacrificing move.","With this in mind, Xia Qing issued an order to the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, “Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, use Boiling Oxygen Tubid Stream and swallow all the oxygen in this space into your stomach! Star Dragonfly, begin storing energy by absorbing the energy within the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion’s body! Fire Source Crystal Scorpion, unleash the territory of fire and change the environment of the battleground.”","Xia Qing barked out a string of instructions in quick succession.","Xia Qing’s Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, Star Dragonfly, and Fire Source Crystal Scorpion immediately sprung into action upon hearing her orders.","The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad opened its mouth and croaked twice.","Soon, the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad became a powerful filter and began gulping large amounts of air. All of the oxygen was filtered out.","According to Star Web’s rules, alterations to the battleground in a Star Web battle would only affect the battleground. As such, the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence watching the fight were still able to breathe comfortably.","Any member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who was familiar with Xia Qing knew how powerful the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s ability Boiling Oxygen Tubid Stream was.","This was a performance duel. Otherwise, Xia Qing would never speak her commands so plainly.","Once the oxygen vanished, a viscous and turbid stream of air was released in prodigious amounts from the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad.","A unique heat formed in the air, and the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion slammed its tail and pincers forcefully onto the ground.","The entire arena in the clouds was set alight by fire.","At the instant that the fire was about to reach Lin Yuan, he opened the four pairs of black wings on his back and lifted himself into the air.","The Fire Source Crystal Scorpion continued changing the environment while the Star Dragonfly moved behind the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion and pierced its tail into the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion’s armored back.","The ball that the Star Dragonfly held in its front legs turned tangerine and started to expand.","In previous battles against members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Xia Qing mostly used the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad and Star Dragonfly. But now, not only had she summoned three feys, but she was also using them to their full potential.","However, based on the current circumstances, it seemed that Xia Qing did not have the upper hand.","A sacred hall composed of musical notes appeared behind the celestial maiden-like Chimey. All of the imageries in the voices condensed into solid forms within the sacred hall.","Chimey walked into the sacred hall.","Chimey used its Myth Breed ability, Sound Spirit Sacred Hall.","Sound Spirit Sacred Hall could be perfectly linked with Speak Spirit Singer.","At the instant that Chimey entered the Sound Spirit Sacred Hall, the effects of Sound Spirit Sacred Hall resulted in Chimey’s energy spreading in all directions.","Thousands of bird lifeforms with the voices of phoenixes swooped down from the clouds to the area like a shower of rain, completely blanketing the area.","This was just the first wave of Chimey’s attacks using Sound Spirit Sacred Hall.","Chimey had already changed its bloodline into a new sun and shot it into the real sun so that it would be boosted by the sun power.","Sun Projection boosted Chimey’s power to the greatest extent.","However, there were also drawbacks to being closely linked to the sun. Once the connection was broken, Chimey would be in an extremely weak state.","It was not just Xia Qing who was preparing her final attack. Chimey was doing the same!","After the birds with voices of phoenixes passed, a sea materialized atop the territory of fire that the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion had created.","Given that the imageries contained wills, the imageries produced from Chimey’s voice were able to endure the effects of the territory of fire.","However, the territory of fire created by the Fire Source Crystal Scorpion was nothing to scoff at.","The flames penetrated the seawater and bloomed on the surface like flowers.","When Chimey saw this, it changed the tune it was singing, and frost began forming on the surface of the sea.","Chimey was using the wills in its song to battle the raging flame energy.","The battle between Lin Yuan’s Blackie and Long Tao could be said to have been a regular fey battle.","But now, the battle between Chimey and Xia Qing was like a legendary battle between mythical immortals.","Chimey was a light-type bird-species fey, but it was able to infuse wills into its singing voice.","The attacks from the imageries in Chimey’s voice were putting so much pressure on Xia Qing that she was slightly struggling to breathe.","It went without saying that this situation had also come about from Chimey using Sun Projection to connect itself to the sun and tap into the sun’s energy. Otherwise, even a Creation Breed fey would have already run out of energy after such heavy-handed attacks.","When Xia Qing first started fighting back with her three feys, Chimey had felt pushed into a corner.","The Star Dragonfly’s explosive effects were not only strong enough to harm but also kill Chimey.","However, due to the Star Dragonfly’s relatively weak body, it had been unable to attack Chimey in the midst of Chimey’s ongoing attacks.","When Chimey evolved to Myth Breed, it confirmed the path that it was going to take henceforth.","The stronger the barrage of attacks, the better defended it would be.","It looked as though Xia Qing was on her last legs. Nonetheless, her expression had not changed in the slightest.","Firstly, she already knew that she would not be able to defeat Lin Yuan. Just like Long Tao, she was just trying to get a sense of the gap between her and Lin Yuan.","Additionally, she had yet to summon her fey with the Barren bloodline.","Her fey with the Barren bloodline could not comfortably demonstrate its power in reality. But it did not have to be concerned in a battle on Star Web.","The Suck Burst Oxygen Toad, Star Dragonfly, and Fire Source Crystal Scorpion that had been completely suppressed by Chimey’s attacks to the point that they could no longer fight back would all become fuel for her fey with the Barren bloodline’s combat.","Xia Qing raised her fist and waved it in front of her again.","The vibrant aura of a fey with the Barren bloodline began permeating the air around Xia Qing.","This robust might was soon accompanied by surging fire-elemental energy.","The fire-elemental energy gathered together tightly, burning this space that was devoid of oxygen.","Oxygen was usually the fuel of fire-elemental energy. But at this moment, the flames burned a black crack into this space devoid of oxygen.","Xia Qing stood amidst the flames and fixed her unwavering gaze on Lin Yuan.","There were only two fire-type feys with the Barren bloodline.","Zong Ze had contracted the Fiery Sky Hou. The Fiery Sky Hou was skilled at brewing fire. It used fire-elemental energy to inflict harm on targets and was very compatible with Zong Ze’s sacred source lifeform.","Xia Qing had picked her fey with the Barren bloodline later than Zong Ze.","However, her fire-type fey with the Barren bloodline was not any weaker than the Fiery Sky Hou and was even stronger once it was paired with her sacred source lifeform!","During the previous battle between Lin Yuan and Long Tao, Long Tao had chosen to use all of his energy on the Victory Fish and had not used his sacred source lifeform.","Xia Qing would not be following in his footsteps.","Her sacred source lifeform and fey with the Barren bloodline might not have obvious links, but once they were used, they could work together to cause potent trouble for her opponent.","Xia Qing intended to use her sacred source lifeform to give a stab at Lin Yuan. At the very least, she wanted to defeat his sparrow-species fey. Regardless of what happened, Xia Qing would not allow herself to be beaten without taking down a single one of Lin Yuan’s feys!","Lin Yuan looked at the flaming beast that had appeared next to Xia Qing. It had the shape of a dog and did not look fierce at all. Rather, it looked cute in the same way as the shibu inu dogs from Lin Yuan’s previous life.","After this beast appeared, all the fire-elemental energy in the environment gathered towards this small beast. However, it did not absorb the fire-elemental energy. Instead, it used its aura to transform the fire-elemental energy, changing it to a beautiful purplish-red.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the dog-like beast.","[Fey Name]: Misfortune Fighter","[Fey Species]: Barren-species/furred-beast species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Fire","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Fusing Fire]: When its flames make contact with other targets, the flames will seep into the target. The targets will thus be invaded and transformed into fire-elemental energy that it will be able to manipulate.","[Misfortune Explosion]: Each time the flames are triggered to explode, the explosive effects will be transferred to the surroundings, subsequently causing the flames to explode. The targets affected by the explosive effects will be burned.","[Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames]: Transfer the transformed fire-elemental energy to the surrounding environment. Once the fire-elemental energy senses a target, it will penetrate the environment to burn the target.","[Chasing Flames Transmission]: Each time a target is burned by Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames, the Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames will be rapidly transmitted to the roots. Each transmission will be accompanied by explosive cracking.","[Misfortune Flame Lamps]: When the misfortune flames reach a certain concentration, they will turn into lamps. The lamps are able to recreate fire-elemental energy. The light released by the Misfortune Flame Lamps is also able to break through stealth effects and place a bright flame imprint on the target.","[Fury-Released Flames]: After activating the misfortune flames, the misfortune flames will fill a space and burn up everything in the space. During the burning process, the Misfortune Fighter’s own vitality will be slowly used up.","[Karma Misfortune Seed]: Each time the target is attacked, as long as the target and the Misfortune Fighter’s karma have a certain strength, a misfortune seed will be formed in the target’s body and worsen the flame damage suffered by the target.","Exclusive Skill:","[Incinerating Obliteration of the Soul]:","[Body of Fire]: Its body will become part of the flames and boost the flames. After the flames are extinguished, it will temporarily return to the state before it had fused with the flames before turning back into flames and extinguishing its life.","[Disaster Seed Judgment]: A judgment will be made of the target based on the number of disaster seeds in its body. Each disaster seed will carry an obliterating soul effect. Any injuries will also be transferred to the target through the karma link."]},{"number":2690,"title":"Chapter 2690 One Move to Determine the Outcome!","paragraphs":["2690 One Move to Determine the Outcome!","Now, Lin Yuan had an in-depth and reliable understanding of the Misfortune Fighter’s abilities.","The Misfortune Fighter was a disaster beast and could bring fire raining down from the skies.","Everything that it comes into contact with, even feces, would turn into fervent flames.","This creature that resembled a Shiba Inu was extremely deadly.","Fusing Fire allowed the Misfortune Fighter to invade enemies through fire-elemental energy.","When fire-elemental energy was injected into other targets, it would be transformed.","The most terrifying part was that the Misfortune Fighter could allocate the transformed energy so that the Misfortune Fighter could remove the ability of any target weaker than the Misfortune Fighter and which shared the same space as it. The Misfortune Fighter could allocate all of the energy contained within other lifeforms.","The Victory Fish was very skilled at group combat, but it was very weak compared to the Misfortune Fighter.","If Chimey’s grade was lower than the Misfortune Fighter and did not have the protection of Speak Spirit Singer and Sound Spirit Sacred Hall, Chimey’s body would already have begun burning.","The Misfortune Fighter used its Elite ability, Misfortune Explosion, the most when it fought feys of the same level.","The flames produced by the Misfortune Fighter were extremely brutal and triggered explosive effects every second.","Once the Misfortune Fighter used the Misfortune Explosion, sparks would explode instantaneously, burning all the targets that were being attacked.","The explosive effects could break through armor, and the burning effects could trigger Fusing Fire.","While killing a target, the Misfortune Fighter’s energy would also be replenished.","Lin Yuan looked at Xia Qing and could see the clear amazement and astonishment in her eyes.","Lin Yuan knew that Xia Qing had summoned the Misfortune Fighter so she could not only target his feys but him as well.","However, Lin Yuan had the protection of the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen, and it gave him immunity against the effects of fire elements.","With the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Stars and because it had absorbed fire-type Immortal bodies, the Misfortune Fighter would not be able to hurt Lin Yuan with fire-elemental energy as long as it had not reached Immortal Breed.","Lin Yuan had tested this ability in a previous battle with Zong Ze. Now, the ability was even stronger.","The Misfortune Fighter was unable to affect Lin Yuan in any way. Xia Qing did not immediately instruct the Misfortune Fighter to attack Lin Yuan.","Instead, the Misfortune Fighter began accumulating energy.","One after another, Misfortune Flame Lamps appeared on Xia Qing’s side of the battleground.","The Misfortune Flame Lamps were able to attract fire elements.","Given that more than ten Misfortuune Flame Lamps had appeared, Lin Yuan knew that Xia Qing intended to fight a drawn-out battle.","Misfortune Flame Lamps’ revealing abilities could not affect Lin Yuan because he did not have any feys that were skilled at stealth.","Unfortunately for Xia Qing, she was unaware of this.","When he battled anyone else, Lin Yuan could leverage the information he knew to stand on equal ground with his opponent. This would even apply when he battled Class 5 and above Creation Masters.","Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames and Chasing Flames Transmission were fire-type abilities that could be linked.","Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames allowed the Misfortune Fighter to transfer its own fire-elemental energy to its surrounding environment to alter it before using the fire-elemental energy in the environment to burn targets.","Meanwhile, for Chasing Flames Transmission, whenever a target was burned by Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames, the burning effects of Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames would be circulated around the other lifeforms in the space.","Just like Misfortune Explosion, most of the Misfortune Fighter’s abilities could intensify the burning effects.","These burning effects were compatible with the exclusive skill, Incinerating Obliteration of the Soul.","Every time the target was burned three times, the effects of Incinerating Obliteration of the Soul would be activated, and the target’s soul would be temporarily stunned. One instance of the effects might not cause much damage. But after three instances, there was a high chance that the soul would pass out.","The burning effects from the Misfortune Fighter’s abilities could be easily transferred to others.","The obliterating soul’s effects would also appear repeatedly during combat, adding variety to the battle.","If Xia Qing was battling someone else besides Lin Yuan, the obliterating soul effects could definitely tip the scales. After all, suddenly losing focus during an important battle would likely change the battle circumstances.","The deadly and controlling effects of Incinerating Obliteration of the Soul allowed the Misfortune Fighter to stand out as a fey with the Barren bloodline.","Body of Fire was an extremely strong self-preservation exclusive skill. It could also provide the Misfortune Fighter with a one-time boost.","Body of Fire enabled the Misfortune Fighter to fully fuse its body with flames, making its body a part of the flames.","Any external attacks it suffered would be absorbed by the flames to boost the flames. This raised the Misfortune Fighter’s deadliness.","When the Misfortune Fighter encountered a strong enemy and extinguished the flames, it would return to the same state from before it had fused with the flames.","Although this would use up the Misfortune Fighter’s vitality, it did give the Misfortune Fighter another chance to live and continue brandishing abilities.","Karma Misfortune Seed was a Diamond ability that could manipulate karma. It was similar to Ji Feng’s Karma Sword Lily’s abilities.","As long as two parties came into contact and sensed each other’s presence, karma would form between them. If the karma crossed a line, it would turn into misfortune.","The targets afflicted with the misfortune seed would be even more severely injured by the flames.","It could be said that Karma Misfortune Seed would boost the Misfortune Fighter once during combat, allowing it to take control of two lives.","At important junctures, when the Misfortune Fighter gained a new life through Body of Fire, it would have a large impact on a stalemate battle.","The Myth Breed exclusive skill Disaster Seed Judgment would be linked with Karma Misfortune Seed.","The misfortune seed could also place obliterating soul effects on targets. Each misfortune seed would lead to the emergence of one obliterating soul effect.","When combined with Incinerating Obliteration of the Soul, the obliterating soul effects could be stacked up.","From the Misfortune Fighter’s effects, Lin Yuan knew that Xia Qing had put a lot of effort into nurturing the Misfortune Fighter.","Otherwise, it would not have so many abilities that could be linked and complementary exclusive skills and abilities.","But regardless of how perfect the Misfortune Fighter’s abilities were, Lin Yuan had a way to deal with them.","Firstly, the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen could fully restrain the Misfortune Fighter. The Misfortune Fighter could use whatever abilities or exclusive skills it wanted. Regardless of how many explosions or burning effects it unleashed, Lin Yuan would be kept safe by the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had absorbed Fifth Page Truth’s sacred source lifeform and the source totems of Grace Sacred Hall’s two rulers.","The Sacred Sword Wielding Queen was likely a product of the two rulers, so it had the same source as the two source totems. All of this culminated in the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen currently being a step away from reaching 9 Stars.","There were very few experts from the senior generation who had sacred source lifeforms with Stars as high as Lin Yuan’s sacred source lifeform, much less experts from the younger generation.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan did not underestimate Xia Qing because she had yet to use her sacred source lifeform.","Sacred source lifeforms were able to counter each other. It was not a guarantee that low Stars sacred source lifeforms were under the thumb of high Stars sacred source lifeforms.","During the gathering at the Return from Faraway Mansion, Zong Ze mentioned that he had once suffered greatly at the hands of Xia Qing’s sacred source lifeform.","Lin Yuan was very curious about Xia Qing’s sacred source lifeform.","Chimey was sufficiently strong, especially after it began drawing on the sun’s energy.","It was just a shame that the Misfortune Fighter was skilled at endurance battles. Flames were both the Misfortune Fighter’s combat tool and safe haven.","Chimey had used up a significant amount of energy taking on Xia Qing’s three feys.","It was likely that Chimey would end up losing the battle against the Misfortune Fighter.","Lin Yuan conveyed his thoughts to Chimey.","Chimey did not insist on pressing on. It was well aware of the significance of this battle.","It would not be humiliated even if it insisted on continuing the fight and ended up losing.","But in order to boost the Radiance Federation’s morale, Lin Yuan needed to win this battle with flying colors.","With a wave of its hand, four celestial maidens appeared from within the Sound Spirit Sacred Hall. The four maidens carried the Sound Spirit Sacred Hall over to Lin Yuan, and Chimey walked out of the Sound Spirit Sacred Hall.","At this moment, Chimey stopped attacking and putting pressure on Xia Qing. Instead, it let out a soft chirp and turned back to its original form before landing on Lin Yuan’s shoulder.","Chimey was no longer battling and was now a spectator instead.","The Misfortune Fighter was skilled at flame combat. But Lin Yuan also had feys that were skilled at flame combat.","Lin Yuan thought about sending out Shiny to battle the Misfortune Fighter. But he soon gave up on the idea.","The Diamond/Fantasy Shiny could hold its own in a fight against the Misfortune Fighter.","Wind and fire elements were complementary. The burning flames would whip up air currents that stimulated wind elements.","An environment that contained wind would allow Shiny to stand its ground against the Misfortune Fighter. However, it would be a struggle for it to defeat the Misfortune Fighter.","Given that he understood Xia Qing’s power, Lin Yuan decided to put an end to this battle swiftly.","Lin Yuan was more looking forward to the battle with Liu Jie than this battle with Xia Qing.","Although Liu Jie did not have a barren beast, the insect-species carcinoma feys that had transformed into fairies that he controlled were all just as formidable as feys with the Barren bloodline. Moreover, Liu Jie had carefully and painstakingly pieced his team together so the fairies were able to work together swimmingly.","Liu Jie’s combat system was already complete. Aside from the fairies, Liu Jie had also evolved the other insect-species carcinoma feys.","Even members of royalty with Eternal Breed feys sometimes required a lot of effort and time to handle the disasters triggered by the Diamond X/Legend insect-species feys.","Lin Yuan could not say with certainty that he would be able to defeat Liu Jie without using his secret weapons.","With a wave of his hand, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom released a large amount of spores.","Once the spores entered the environment filled with fire-elemental energy, they were unaffected by the Misfortune Fighter’s abilities, and some of the weaker spores even became even more ample.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had only gently shaken its cap, but it had released hundreds of thousands of spores floating across the arena.","Xia Qing had already issued orders to the Misfortune Fighter.","“Misfortune Fighter, once you are done with Misfortune Flame Lamps, use Fusing Fire, Misfortune Explosion, Ground-Penetrating Misfortune Flames, and Chasing Flames Transmission simultaneously.”","The purple and red sea of fire that had already been boiling unleashed its might.","At this moment, Xia Qing suddenly felt her spirit being attacked by an external force.","The Misfortune Fighter let out a few pained howls.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom was a pinnacle Myth II fey that had been nurtured with perfect methods. Its attacking power could not be compared to regular Myth II feys.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had used Seeping Flames, Body-Penetrating Flames, and Thought-Separating Flames together.","When the spores invaded the Misfortune Fighter, they attacked its mind, spirit, and soul first. Once the spores took over its heart and brain, its attack on the mind, spirit, and soul became even more savage.","With its mind, spirit, and soul gravely injured, the Misfortune Fighter stopped moving forward.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s Seeping Flames allowed it to absorb the energy within the target’s heart and brain and utilize it to its own benefit. It essentially used the opponent’s energy to kill the opponent.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s Body-Penetrating Flames did not have obvious effects.","The Misfortune Fighter was not afraid of the burns on its body. The burns on its body would not affect it in any way.","Lin Yuan had instructed the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to use Body-Penetrating Flames because he wanted to use the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to inhibit the Misfortune Fighter and prevent it from fusing with the flames.","Xia Qing had sensed her own spirit, mind, and soul being attacked because of Thought-Separating Flames’ effects.","Xia Qing and the Misfortune Fighter were hit with the same injuries.","Under this torture, Xia Qing’s body was on the verge of collapse and held back a groan of agony. Nonetheless, her fighting spirit had been severely shaken.","Lin Yuan thought, Unless my opponent is of a much higher level than the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom or is able to protect their mind, spirit, and soul, it will be very difficult for them to save themselves from the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s attacks.","Since he had already made his move and his objective was to end this battle quickly, Lin Yuan ensured that the spores in the Misfortune Fighter’s body had germinated before ordering the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to use Crumbled Parasitic Cycle.","But a moment later, the germinated spores within the Misfortune Fighter and Xia Qing were sacrificed. Once they were sacrificed, they removed the energy in Xia Qing and the Misfortune Fighter’s bodies before destroying the energy.","Xia Qing had not noticed Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s intangible attacks at all.","By the time Xia Qing thought about summoning her sacred source lifeform, it was already too late.","As the disheartened Mu Yan looked down from her stone pillar at Xia Qing, she could not help but think about how terrified she would be if Lin Yuan used such methods against her.","Before she even had the time to react, her mind, spirit, and soul would have already been seriously wounded. She would not have the courage to handle the threefold anguish from her mind, spirit, and soul for a second time.","Even someone like Xia Qing had lost to Lin Yuan’s methods. It was no longer embarrassing that she had lost after going in completely unprepared!","Once Xia Qing regained consciousness, she was back on the stone pillar.","Xia Qing looked at Lin Yuan and pursed her lips tightly before saying a moment later, “With just that move, none of the members of the younger generation will be your match!”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow. He knew that Xia Qing was blowing off steam.","However, it was not true that this move would be effective against anyone. At the very least, it would not work against Liu Jie!"]},{"number":2691,"title":"Chapter 2691 Destined Battle!","paragraphs":["2691 Destined Battle!","Lin Yuan never underestimated his feys or overestimated his opponents.","He had internally rebuked Xia Qing’s words because he understood Liu Jie.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom could release hundreds of thousands of spores into the air. As long as five spores made it into the body of a Diamond insect, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom would be able to trigger its ability.","However, high-level insect-species carcinoma feys multiplied into an army much faster than was expected by the average person. This especially applied to an army created by multiple insect-species carcinoma feys.","With the neverending waves of insect armies charging at him, it would be difficult for Lin Yuan to use the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to take control of the vast number of insects within a short span of time.","There were some insect-species carcinoma feys that could even consume the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom used the effects of Thought-Separating Flames to affect the spirit, mind, and soul of entities and the main body or the body contracted to the entities.","However, the insect army produced by the insect-species carcinoma feys did not possess much intelligent thought and only knew how to follow the mother insect’s orders to kill and feed. If they were subjected to the torture of the spirit, soul, and mind, they would follow the mother insect’s orders and their innate genetic instincts. Thus, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom would not be able to trace the link back to the mother insect. Lin Yuan already tested this on Liu Jie when the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom evolved to Myth Breed.","Xia Qing had said this partially because she was slightly indignant and partially because she truly felt that the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s abilities were very strong.","But in the upcoming battle, Lin Yuan would correct Xia Qing’s thinking and show her that she had misunderstood.","There was a plethora of variations to fey abilities. It could not be said that one singular ability was better than all the rest. Lin Yuan was able to save himself from being unexpectedly tripped up because he always kept this in mind.","Lin Yuan had already used two of his three challenges. This next battle would be his last challenge for the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking.","Star Web was a cacophony of activity because of Lin Yuan’s three battles.","Lin Yuan had won his battle against Mu Yan in an extremely bizarre and startling manner.","This battle caused those who had been looking forward to watching Lin Yuan to raise their anticipation to the maximum, and those who had not been looking forward to watching him to also become excited.","Star Web returned to the same state as before the dead spirits crisis began.","As Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter, Tian Ningning continuously asked the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master, whom Liu Hao had sent to assist her in writing her draft and updating the duel record.","However, even the pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master could not make an accurate assessment of Lin Yuan’s fey.","The second battle had been between Lin Yuan and Long Tao.","When Lin Yuan fought as Black on Star Web, he had encountered opponents from the Dragon Gate Guild Club. Long Tao even publicly invited Black to join the Dragon Gate Guild Club. This formed an invisible link between Long Tao and Black.","Later, due to the incident involving Long Tao, Black, and the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence working together to fend off the wave of demons, it became public knowledge that Long Tao and Black were friends.","Long Tao’s power had been dazzling ever since he made it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","He managed to overwhelm opponents time and time again to climb the ranks into the top ten of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Once he became Sequence #3 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, he began receiving many challenges annually. However, there were very few people who could defeat him in battle.","Even if his feys were countered and he lost one or two abilities, he would be able to climb back up later.","It could be said that Long Tao was the standard for the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking.","The battle between Long Tao and Lin Yuan was highly anticipated by the Star Web audience and Long Tao had even summoned one of the legendary feys with the Barren bloodline.","In the Victory Fish’s first public appearance, it was defeated by Lin Yuan with just one main-dragon-species fey.","It was obvious that Lin Yuan had not utilized his full capabilities in the battle against Long Tao.","It was assumed that Lin Yuan would continue using the main-dragon-species fey in the battle against Xia Qing. After all, after each battle on Star Web, both spirit qi professionals and feys were fully healed.","Yet, Lin Yuan did not send out the main-dragon-species fey again. Instead, he summoned the bird that could transform into a sun that he had used in the battle against the Freedom Federation envoy group.","After the battle against the Freedom Federation envoy group, the bird had become a celebrity and was a household name.","This was because the sparrow’s beauty was eye-catching, and its voice was literally music to the ears.","Furthermore, this sparrow’s power was undeniably fearsome. No one had heard of the ability to harness to sun.","Moreover, this sparrow turned out to be the most popular idol on Star Web, Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess!","Previously, only a few people successfully guessed Chimey’s true identity. Most were unaware of it.","The battle between Chimey and Xia Qing had utterly stirred up the audience on Star Web. This especially applied to Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess’ fans.","[Beach]: I finally know why Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess has been absent all this time. Lord Lin Yuan was probably in seclusion and evolving her power!","[Look at Your Bearish Appearance]: Ah! I haven’t heard Sparrow Voice Loli Goddess sing in so long. It was such a blessing to be able to hear her sing during the match!","[Magic Mini Jie]: Will she continue to livestream after this match? When will she hold a fan meeting? I want her signature as a keepsake!","Aside from Chimey, most of the conversation surrounded Lin Yuan and Xia Qing.","Xia Qing had never summoned the Misfortune Fighter publicly in the past.","It was likely that only Lin Yuan could withstand and eventually defeat Xia Qing, who had the outstanding Misfortune Fighter and its ability to turn the entire arena of clouds into flames.","However, the method by which Lin Yuan defeated Xia Qing took Star Web’s audience by surprise.","It was similar to the method by which Lin Yuan had defeated Mu Yan.","Before this, there were some people who felt that Mu Yan had lost because she was weak.","Due to the new format of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, many powerful members of the younger generation ended up being swallowed by the sea of alien beasts before they had the chance to exhibit their strength. Some of them included members of the previous generation of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","This inevitably led to some doubting the fairness of the new selection format.","After Mu Yan lost, even more people used her as evidence for their suspicions. They felt that if she was weak enough to be beaten by a mere wave of Lin Yuan’s hand, she did not deserve to stand as a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. It went without saying that such naysayers were emboldened by the fact that she had not won a single one of her three challenges.","But now that Lin Yuan had used a similar method to defeat Xia Qing, some of the finger-pointing at Mu Yan eased.","After all, she did manage to go a few rounds with the other two members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence she challenged.","If they said Mu Yan didn’t deserve a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence because Lin Yuan beat her with a technique, it would be like saying Xia Qing, who was Sequence #1 for a long time, didn’t deserve it either.","All of the commentators and hosts on Star Web were enthusiastically expressing their opinions on the battles. All of them had different styles. A few were conservative, while others took greater leaps in logic. But they were all trying their best to explain the exhilarating battles.","It was not long before the attention of the entire Star Web shifted from the battle between Lin Yuan and Xia Qing to the one between Lin Yuan and Liu Jie.","Liu Jie stood up at the instant that Lin Yuan said his name.","From the outside, Liu Jie looked extremely calm. But people like Bai Hao and Wang Zhong, who knew him, were aware that he could not be more excited. This was because Liu Jie always balled his right fist when he was excited. He never did so at other times.","Bai Hao and Wang Zhong were not just Liu Jie’s previous teammates but were also his close friends.","Both of them knew that he was Lin Yuan’s retainer and that Lin Yuan had saved Liu Jie from the mud.","Liu Jie had been looking forward to this battle for a long time.","However, he was not trying to use his battle to prove himself but to report to Lin Yuan and show him how he had grown.","Liu Jie was under extreme pressure, and Wang Zhong and Bai Hao could tell. But at the same time, they knew that this stress could not be changed by Liu Jie himself because it came from Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan’s rapid growth placed unimaginable pressure on Liu Jie. This would happen regardless of who Lin Yuan’s retainer was.","Luckily, Liu Jie also had his own opportunities. These opportunities allowed him to have the chance to report to Lin Yuan.","Bai Hao and Wang Zhong cheered Liu Jie on internally.","The last time that Liu Jie had demonstrated his power was last year during the fight against the Freedom Federation envoy group.","Neither Bai Hao nor Wang Zhong knew how far Liu Jie had grown in the past year.","Lin Yuan and Liu Jie locked eyes, and a smile immediately spread across Lin Yuan’s face.","Just like Liu Jie, Lin Yuan had also been looking forward to this fight for a long time. He also wanted to see how ferocious Liu Jie could be when he unleashed his full power.","Night Leaning Moon was the one who had come up with the ‘final weapon’ plan for Liu Jie, but Lin Yuan was the one who had materialized it.","Without Lin Yuan, Elegance would not have gained the Blade Queen Bee’s psychotoxins and mutated. Liu Jie would also not have obtained the Firefly Demon Fetuses that transformed the insect-species carcinoma feys into fairies.","Lin Yuan had one fey that was very suited to battle against Liu Jie, and that was Source Sand!","After Lin Yuan conquered the subterranean world, the metal spiritual ingredients he obtained had enabled him to comprehensively evolve the Suzerain/Myth Source Sand.","Liu Jie walked down from the stone pillar. In front of all of the citizens of the Radiance Federation, Liu Jie stood in front of Lin Yuan and performed the rites of a retainer.","Immediately after this, Liu Jie summoned Elegance with a wave of his hand.","The Dimensional Light Moth that was close to becoming a four-winged fairy also appeared next to Elegance.","The Dimensional Light Moth was the fortress that stored Liu Jie’s insect army.","Only a few of the carcinoma feys controlled by Elegance were stored within it. Most of them were stored within the Dimensional Light Moth.","Given that Liu Jie’s intention was to show Lin Yuan how he had improved, he was in no rush to summon the insect army to attack Lin Yuan.","Instead, he instructed the Dimensional Light Moth to release a veteran fight, the Hypha Tapeworm.","Previously, the Hypha Tapeworm was a Diamond X/Legend insect-species carcinoma fey.","Liu Jie could continuously raise the grades of the insect-species carcinoma feys he controlled but not Elegance. Otherwise, Elegance would lose control over the insect-species carcinoma feys.","Liu Jie felt slightly conflicted about the Hypha Tapeworm, but he eventually used the Firefly Demon Fetus to transform it into a fairy.","Of all of his insect-species carcinoma feys, the Hypha Tapeworm was the most suited to set the stage for his combat. When the Hypha Tapeworm set the stage, it would enable the other insect-species carcinoma feys to utilize their powers to the greatest extent.","When Liu Jie had been hesitating about whether to transform the Hypha Tapeworm into a fairy, he had discussed his concerns with Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan used True Data and started reading the Hypha Tapeworm’s information.","[Fey Name]: Hypha Tapeworm (Fairy)","[Fey Species]: Fairy-species/fairy-genus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Insect/Dark","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Fluid Hypha]: A sticky fluid will be produced that can cover an area. The bacteria pockets in the sticky fluid will break apart quickly to form webs of hypha.","[Long Body Split]: The Hypha Tapeworm will tunnel into the Fluid Hypha and start to split itself. Each split section can be planted in any small insect.","[Degeneration Control]: Flesh that is dead due to bacterial infection will be covered in bacteria pockets that contain vicious poison. When the bacteria covers a degenerating surface, the tapeworms that have been created from the split sections can enter the dead host to control it.","[Decaying Bacteria]: The bodies of the hosts being manipulated will be covered in strong corrosive bacteria that will spread to the cells of healthy flesh that it comes into contact with and cause the cells of the healthy flesh to start to decay.","[Degenerating Body Integration]: When a degenerating body is damaged, the ladybugs that are produced will sacrifice their body as nutrients to feed and integrate the bacteria. The tapeworms produced from the split sections will control the degenerated body.","[Double Parasite]: When in the presence of other parasitic-type lifeforms and insects, the degenerating body, bacteria, and tapeworms formed from split sections can be sacrificed to increase the parasitic-type lifeform’s power. If the parasitic-type lifeform is injured, it can draw energy from the sacrificed entities to heal itself.","[Decaying Camp Fungal Territory]: Whenever an insect-species lifeform dies in the territory of fungi, the territory of fungi will absorb the insect-species lifeform before breaking them down into their components and turning them into nutrients for the territory of fungi. This will create an environment where insect-species lifeforms can take shelter.","Exclusive Skill:","[Degenerating Body’s Reproduction]: The bacteria will alter the reproductive and gender cells in the degenerating body to allow the degenerating body to produce new creatures by splitting its sections.","[Resilient Corded Body]: The Hypha Tapeworm’s split bodies and ability to produce hypha will be strengthened. Splitting the body excessively will not affect the main body’s resilience. The split bodies are able to produce hypha.","[Sacrificing Hypha Provision]: The hypha colonies produced by the split bodies will be sacrificed and turned into nutrients that will feed the insect-species lifeforms in contact with the hypha. This will help the insect-species targets in combat, and the insect-species targets being controlled by the split bodies will also be strengthened."]},{"number":2692,"title":"Chapter 2692 The Strongest Heart of Insect Swarm!","paragraphs":["2692 The Strongest Heart of Insect Swarm!","Lin Yuan now had a precise understanding of the Hypha Tapeworm.","Liu Jie had indeed evolved the Hypha Tapeworm to Suzerain X/Myth II.","After the Hypha Tapeworm transformed into a fairy, it became an allusive creature. It had a head of flowing white hair and a fresh cuteness.","Every time it met the gaze of someone else, its small face would flush red. It was much shyer than Elegance.","However, the Hypha Tapeworm was not careless or sloppy at all in its battle against Lin Yuan.","Under Liu Jie’s feet, the territory of fungi started to spread towards Lin Yuan at an indescribable speed.","Eight wings opened on Lin Yuan’s back, and he flew into the air, leaving the ground to Liu Jie.","Lin Yuan was in no rush to attack. He wanted to experience the pressure from Liu Jie’s carcinoma feys.","Liu Jie did not need to issue instructions to the Hypha Tapeworm. It had already used Long Body Split in the carpet of fungi.","Small tapeworms hid themselves in the carpet of fungi. Anything that touched the carpet of fungi would be attacked by the Hypha Tapeworm, and the tapeworms would reproduce in the entities’ bodies.","The sudden expansion of the carpet of fungi across the arena of clouds was shocking.","However, Liu Jie was only just getting started.","Liu Jie was battling Lin Yuan because he wanted to prove that he could perform his job as Lin Yuan’s retainer.","Just like the insect queens who wanted to report to the insect empress, Liu Jie was going to demonstrate his full power.","The Dimensional Light Moth produced the Parasite Decay Locust.","During the battle against Lu Ou and the Freedom Federation envoy group, the Parasite Decay Locust was killed by Lu Ou’s major devil’s skill, Family Clan Adjudication.","Luckily, the Radiance Federation had a second Parasite Decay Locust.","The Parasite Decay Locust did not meet Liu Jie’s standard, so he did not select it as one of the candidates to be transformed into a fairy by the Firefly Demon Fetus.","Nonetheless, Liu Jie still nurtured this insect-species carcinoma fey that could establish an army.","The Parasite Decay Locust’s female insect had a distended stomach. At the instant that it appeared, a plume of yellow smoke burst out from the Parasite Decay Locust’s abdomen. This was not because the Parasite Decay Locust had an upset stomach but because it was laying minuscule eggs.","The eggs landed on the carpet of fungi created by the Hypha Tapeworm and absorbed the energy from the carpet of fungi.","The Parasite Decay Locust’s offspring flew out from the carpet of fungi-like spring bamboo sprouting after a shower of rain.","When the audience saw this, they felt that Liu Jie was even more terrifying than a highly active Class 5 alien insect dimensional rift!","But this was still just the tip of the iceberg for Liu Jie.","Two Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects appeared after the Parasite Decay Locust. A burst of black smoke rose in the wake of the Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects’ movements.","To other feys, the barren land would be extremely toxic.","But for insect-species carcinoma feys, the barren land replenished their energy.","The two Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects worked together with the Hypha Tapeworm to strengthen Liu Jie’s formation.","Liu Jie’s army continued to grow, and it seemed to cover the entire sky.","Just as everyone thought that Lin Yuan was going to begin his counterattack, he still did not move.","Liu Jie was also in no rush to attack Lin Yuan.","Instead, he raised his left hand, and a chubby two-winged fairy with purple hair and eyes let out a strange insect cry.","Soon, the space started to fold over itself, and the Parasite Decay Locusts that filled the sky entered the folded space, fading into dim shadows.","It had not been long since Liu Jie had transformed this insect-species carcinoma fey into a fairy.","The Dimensional Light Moth was Liu Jie’s moving arsenal. The Illusionary Layer Caterpillar was a battleground-expanding tool that allowed Liu Jie to wield his maximum power in a small space.","A small space would limit the growth of the insect-species carcinoma feys.","When Liu Jie manually created a wide space, and the Illusionary Layer Caterpillar delivered the alien insects it had stored, the alien insects would rush out like water into a latrine that had been flushed.","After releasing the Illusionary Layer Caterpillar, Liu Jie released a green fairy with short hair.","Lin Yuan nodded his head to himself.","After some internal struggle, Liu Jie still decided to transform the Demon Flower Fragrance Shield Stinkbug, which was skilled at defense, into a fairy!","Lin Yuan had spent a long time urging Liu Jie to transform the Demon Flower Fragrance Shield Stinkbug into a fairy.","Previously, Liu Jie had single-mindedly focused on attack. But for an insect army, it was more important for Liu Jie to prioritize his self-preservation.","Liu Jie was the foundation of the disaster of insects. If something happened to him, the disaster would not aid the humans but would harm the humans instead!","Less than a minute had passed since Liu Jie laid out his formation. However, Long Tao, Xia Qing, and the other members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were all gripped by fear.","Long Tao and Xia Qing gulped.","They admitted to themselves that even if they brought their Barren beasts right out of the gate in a fight against Liu Jie, there was no way they would last even a minute.","Long Tao and Xia Qing were rather familiar with Liu Jie. They knew that the insect-species carcinoma feys he had summoned was just a small portion of the total number of insect-species carcinoma feys he had in his arsenal.","After Liu Jie summoned the Demon Flower Fragrance Shield Stinkbug to protect himself, he did not summon that insect-species carcinoma fey that could create special terrain.","There was no point in changing the terrain in a fight against Lin Yuan.","He had witnessed how Lin Yuan had fused with the Abyss Red Lotus to suppress all of the factions in the subterranean world and conquer it.","When he was facing Lin Yuan, the insect armies created by his insect-species carcinoma feys were useless.","Liu Jie’s current intention was to report to Lin Yuan. He summoned the Blade Queen Bee that had reached pinnacle four wings.","500 Vibrating Armor Ladybugs shot out from the Dimensional Light Moth’s body.","These Vibrating Armor Ladybugs were meant to be sacrificed so that the Blade Queen Bee could produce the Blade Worms.","It did not take long before 500 Blade Worms crawled to the front of the insect army.","Soon, Liu Jie released three Exploding Body Dung Beetles.","At first, there was only one Exploding Body Dung Beetle. But later, Liu Jie obtained one from the Freedom Federation and Azure Federation each.","The three Exploding Body Dung Beetles formed a small team and could produce thousands of egg casings in a second.","Every egg casing could produce more than 300 Exploding Body Dung Beetles.","There was a special fluid within the Exploding Body Dung Beetle. It used the energy in its body to stabilize the fluid. Once the Exploding Body Dung Beetle used up all the energy in its body, the fluid would explode.","The force of the explosion was just as powerful as that of the Flowing Plasma Electric Insect and Electromagnetic Chrysalis.","Liu Jie did not transform the three Exploding Body Dung Beetles into fairies because they were not considered functional-type insect-species carcinoma feys. Liu Jie’s power would not increase by much by transforming them into fairies.","Nonetheless, the three Exploding Body Dung Beetles were still part of Liu Jie’s main pillar of power.","All of the audience members on Star Web, the commentator, and reporters were staring with stupefaction at Liu Jie while he established his army while also looking at Lin Yuan suspiciously. They did not understand why Lin Yuan was quietly watching Liu Jie build up his combat power without doing anything.","It was likely that the power of these insect-species carcinoma feys could cause just as much damage as the dead spirits crisis.","If the insect army and dead spirits clashed, it was possible that the dead spirits would not be able to defeat Liu Jie’s alien insects.","This thought set many people at ease.","The core of Liu Jie’s insect army was decided after extended discussions with Lin Yuan. It was an insect-species carcinoma fey called the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle.","Liu Jie had transformed the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle into a fairy long ago, and he had been concentrating on nurturing it all this time.","Liu Jie was only done establishing his sensational formation after ten minutes.","He only released the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle at the end.","Once it appeared, the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle used its signature ability, Spread Wings Insect Cry.","The insect cry reverberated around the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle.","In an instant, all the insect-species carcinoma feys lit up with bright golden light. This was because the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle had covered the other insect-species carcinoma feys with metal-type.","The metal-type ability could protect the other insect-species feys as well as boost them.","After releasing the insect cry, a loud drumming noise could be heard from the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s abdomen. This was a result of the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s Insect Abdomen Battle Drum.","The drumming from within the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s abdomen would cause other insect-species lifeforms to go into a frenzied state of bloodthirstiness.","While it used Abdomen Battle Drum, a long halberd formed on the top of the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s head.","The long halberd protruded into the sky like a flagpole. This boosted the morale of the insect army and also increased their endurance.","It could be said that the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle alone had managed to raise the combat power of the insect army by at least five times.","With this boosting ability, the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle deserved to be the core of Liu Jie’s insect army.","Lin Yuan knew that the insect army was about to attack him.","Suddenly, he noticed that the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle had once again lit up with golden light.","The golden light contained a red hue, and the overall power of the insect army was raised again at least twice.","This motivation was also reflected back to the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle, allowing it to wield the power of a Creation Breed fey despite only being Suzerain/Myth II.","A strange expression came across Lin Yuan’s face when he saw this.","He used True Data to check on the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle.","[Fey Name]: Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle (Fairy)","[Fey Species]: Scarab species/large rhinoceros beetle species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Insect/Gold","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Metal Forge Angle]: It can absorb every type of metal and apply it to its horns to increase its damage power.","[Spread Wings Insect Cry]: When it flaps its wings, it can attract other insect-species feys and apply its metal characteristics to them to provide them with protection.","[Halberd Banner]: Raise the halberd high in the air, and it will become a banner amongst the army of insects that will motivate them and increase their endurance.","[Insect Abdomen Battle Drum]: The abdomen will start to move and produce a roaring noise. The insects that hear the noise will go mad with bloodthirst.","[Metal Solidification Style]: Absorb all of the metal attributes on its body and turn its legs, horns, and shell into battle attire. The metal attributes will boost its combat abilities. (The metal attributes will be used up in the process of boosting).","[Insect Soul Undestroyed]: The souls of the insects that have been protected by the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle will gather around it and form a stance. The stance of insect souls can help the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle to sustain damage while boosting its combat powers.","[Broken Halberd Fury]: When the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s energy reaches a limit, it will be forcefully shrunken by breaking the halberd. This will be followed by a frenzied state where the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle will attack the target continuously. With each unit of energy that is used up during the attack, its injuries will be healed to a certain extent.","Exclusive Skill:","[Insect Death]: Whenever an insect dies around it, its metal characteristics will change from its original defense mode to offense mode.","[Fission Halberd]: When the insect-species feys die, the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle will experience a fission effect and a halberd will be formed. The halberd can form a territory and provide metal fission effects to other insect-species feys.","[Twofold Motivation]: When boosting other insect-species feys, the other insect-species feys will be motivated, and the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle itself will also be motivated. The motivation will boost the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s various statistics.","Lin Yuan now knew the effects of the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s Myth Breed exclusive skill, Twofold Motivation.","This was the first time he saw Broken Halberd Fury and Fission Halberd.","The Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle was akin to the general of the insect army.","Apart from being able to boost the insect army, it was also extremely powerful as a singular entity. It was Liu Jie’s strongest source of combat power!","Broken Halberd Fury rose Liu Jie’s individual combat power.","Fission Halberd could boost the entire insect army. This boosting made use of the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle’s metal attributes.","Once the metal attributes formed a halberd, it created a territory that boosted the insect army. This ensured that every halberd formed from a metal would be able to boost an insect-species fey that needed to be boosted.","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie was trying to use this battle to prove his own power.","Lin Yuan saw Liu Jie as his friend. In truth, he was not concerned by Liu Jie’s power. Liu Jie’s value did not stem from his power.","Although Liu Jie was not talented at internal governance, his way of thinking was the opposite of Wen Yu. When the two of them communicated, they could come up with a comprehensive and grounded decision.","However, the power that Liu Jie was demonstrating had sincerely startled Lin Yuan. He had no idea that Liu Jie had already grown to such a degree!","Lin Yuan was very happy for Liu Jie.","If he could get his hands on more items like the Firefly Demon Fetuses, Liu Jie’s power would continue to grow.","Since Liu Jie had blown his battle trumpet, it was time for Lin Yuan to respond!"]},{"number":2693,"title":"Chapter 2693 Sand Angel!","paragraphs":["2693 Sand Angel!","Since the Source Sand evolved, Lin Yuan had not used it in battle.","Among all of Lin Yuan’s feys, the Source Sand had always been relatively more skilled at combat.","Not only did it have attacking and controlling abilities, but it could also significantly raise Lin Yuan’s defensive abilities.","After evolving to Suzerain, the Source Sand could now produce something Overlord Sand, which could serve as the control tower for the sea of sand and exert a highly precise level of control over the sea of sand.","Every grain of sand could absorb a metal. After absorbing the metal, the sea of sand under the Overlord Sand’s control would be boosted by the metal attributes.","Liu Jie’s Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle could use metals to boost the insect army, but Lin Yuan’s Source Sand could similarly utilize metals.","Chubby Pocket attained metal attributes by consuming and storing the metals in its body.","But to the Source Sand, the metals were food. It viewed any and all metals as delicious meals.","Because of this, the Source Sand could continuously replenish its metal attributes while it clashed against the insect army. The vibrations and friction from the sand granules could easily grind the insects into crumbs.","The gusts of wind would rapidly blow and push the crushed insect bones around until they became part of the sea of sand.","Normally, Lin Yuan released the Source Sand by allowing it to fall from his sleeve cuff before it began creating sand on the ground.","However, Lin Yuan went for a different course of action in this battle against the ferocious insect army.","The amber-button-shaped Source Sand transformed into the Close Guard Sand straight away.","Thousands of crystalline Overlord Sand granules formed the main area of the Close Guard Sand.","A portion of the Overlord Sand embedded itself into the four pairs of wings on Lin Yuan’s back, adding an orange tint to his black wings.","The wings also started to elongate while two pairs of auxiliary wings sprouted next to the eight wings.","Eventually, Lin Yuan had six pairs of amber wings sprouting from his back, giving him an indescribable air of godly sacredness.","After the Overlord Sand was attached to Lin Yuan’s back, the remainder of the Overlord Sand formed a sand barrier around Lin Yuan.","It was as though the granules of Close Guard Sand had found a main core as they began rapidly gathering toward and covering the barrier of Overlord Sand.","Close Guard Sand’s granules began using their own energy and producing sand at an accelerated rate.","Yellow sand flew in all directions, landing on the surface of the hypha-covered ground.","Because of the Hypha Tapeworm’s exclusive skill, Resilient Corded Body, there were countless tapeworms produced from the ability Long Body Split that were hidden within the carpet of fungi and which significantly strengthened the carpet of fungi.","The carpet of fungi that appeared to be sticky and soft could be easily consumed by insects. However, anything non-insect would not be able to break free from the tight bindings of this carpet of fungi regardless of how hard they struggled!","Alas, compared to the yellow sand, the carpet of fungi was rather weak.","With the Source Sand being Myth II, it could use Metal Consume Manifestation and Overlord Sand Control to take control of many metal-type spiritual ingredients.","However, there was a limit to the Source Sand’s endurance or rather capacity. If it consumed more high-grade metals, the sea of sand would not be able to contain as many metals as when it consumed low-grade metals.","Lin Yuan did not insist on only allowing the Source Sand to consume high-grade metal spiritual ingredients. He was striving for the best combination.","The Source Sand still retained radium, which was both sharp and durable. But while it could only absorb a small amount in the past, it could now consume a large amount and transform it into a part of its own body.","A large amount of sand was produced from the radium, and the immense force of the sea of sand sandwiched the radium against the carpet of fungi, causing the carpet of fungi to break down.","The environment that Liu Jie had put a lot of effort into building and ensuring that it would complement the insects during battle was thus destroyed by Lin Yuan.","The cloud arena that used to be blanketed by the carpet of fungi was now covered by the yellow sand that Lin Yuan had created.","There was still a portion of the carpet of fungi that had yet to be ground away by the sea of sand, but the insects within the carpet of fungi would need to exit the sea of sand in order to survive. Due to the enormous pressure within the sea of sand, no oxygen could penetrate the sand.","Naturally, Lin Yuan would not give these insects the chance to make it out of the sea of sand.","The sea of sand moved rapidly, forming thousands of giant vortexes. All of the lifeforms within the sea of sand would be swallowed to its depths by the vortexes.","The Source Sand’s sea of sand was already 800 meters deep and was still enlarging. It would be a struggle for even Creation Breed feys to make it out of the sea of sand that was thousands of meters deep.","The weight would easily crush the exoskeletons that the insects were so proud of.","Using this method of dumping heavy sand on the insects to kill them would be able to minimize the amount of energy that the Source Sand used.","Lin Yuan had noticed a chink in Liu Jie’s style long ago. He relied too much on setting the scene and building his advantage early on.","When he faced opponents who were weaker than him, this style would come across as stunning and would easily allow him to attain victory by crushing his opponent.","But when he faced stronger opponents, relying too heavily on setting the scene would limit his actions. Moreover, those stronger opponents would not always wait for him to be done with his preparations like Lin Yuan had. Even if he did manage to successfully set the scene, his opponent would be capable of destroying this advantage he had built for himself.","Liu Jie was intelligent. Through this fight, he would definitely be able to notice his issue and make the necessary adjustments to address it.","The sea of sand was growing much faster than the insect-species carcinoma feys could reproduce.","This was because the method of growth was different for the two sides.","The insect-species feys increased their numbers through the mothers’ reproductive abilities. The mothers needed to absorb energy before they could give birth to the next batch.","For example, the Blade Queen Bee needed suitable sacrifices and sufficient time to nurture powerful Blade Worms. The strong Blade Worms needed to digest the sacrifices to a certain extent before they could begin brandishing their strength.","On the other hand, the Source Sand enlarged itself by breaking down elements. All it needed was energy, and it could split up the elements.","Aside from the Source Sand expanding its own body, Close Guard Sand could also change the ground beneath it to generate even more sand.","Previously, the battle taking place in the cloud arena involved Lin Yuan taking on the staggering insect army. But now, the tables had completely turned.","The yellow sand buried everything. Even the Lonely Night Hurricane Moths produced by Elegance were also grabbed by the hand formed from the yellow sand.","Aside from the fairies transformed from the insect-species carcinoma feys that Lin Yuan had yet to target, the rest of Liu Jie’s army of insects had died in the sea of sand.","The three Exploding Body Dung Beetles under Liu Jie’s control produced millions of offspring, and they created significant turbulence under the sea of sand. However, the explosions were unable to harm the Source Sand. Rather, they helped the Source Sand to kill a large number of insects.","The Parasite Decay Locusts were so focused on producing offspring that they were unable to avoid being grabbed by the hand of sand and pushed into the sea of sand. As a result, Elegance’s link to the Parasite Decay Locusts was broken.","Aside from these insect-species carcinoma feys that had been transformed into fairies, the rest of the insect-species carcinoma feys under Liu Jie’s control were all hidden in the folded space created by the Illusionary Layered Caterpillar.","Because this battle was taking place on Star Web, Lin Yuan did not need to hold back in this battle. He did not need to be afraid of harming the feys Liu Jie had contracted.","Otherwise, he would not dare to unleash the Source Sand’s power in such an unrestrained manner.","The waves of sand barrelled through everything in the arena, and the spectators finally understood what a sea of sand looked like.","The army of insects on the surface of the sea of sand were like stones that had been tossed into the sea as they promptly sunk into the water.","Liu Jie had intended to utilize Chubby Pocket to launch a powerful counterattack on Lin Yuan. But he had not anticipated the army of insects outside of the folded space to be rampaged by Lin Yuan so swiftly.","Liu Jie gulped. He had not been caught in such a bind ever since Elegance began controlling insect-species carcinoma feys.","Now, as he was facing Lin Yuan, Liu Jie was reminded of how he felt all those years ago in Cold Frost City when he single-handedly faced the wave of alien beasts.","Liu Jie was familiar with Lin Yuan’s Source Sand.","Lin Yuan mostly used the Source Sand when he first started fighting on Star Web. Liu Jie had also accompanied Lin Yuan many times while he tested the Source Sand’s absorption of various metals.","However, he had not expected the weak Source Sand of the past to be nurtured to such a magnitude!","Liu Jie and Wen Yu had been with Lin Yuan when he traded for the Source Sand at the private trading event.","But Lin Yuan created a miracle out of the Source Sand in two years.","This was just like how Lin Yuan had created a miracle for Liu Jie when he saved him.","Liu Jie took a deep breath and let out a loud cry.","The Illusionary Layered Caterpillar’s body started to glow with blinding bursts of light.","Lin Yuan could clearly sense the vitality being slowly extracted from the Illusionary Layered Caterpillar’s body.","Soon, the folded space started spitting insects like a drunken man vomiting at the end of the night.","The Dimensional Light Moth also started releasing everything in its storage.","Liu Jie said softly, “Chubby Pocket, use these insects to reveal your strongest side! Your target is the ball of sand in the sky that looks like the sun! After this battle, I will find more of the metals you like eating.”","Liu Jie was also very gentle in his treatment of his insect-species carcinoma feys.","When a lifeform gained sufficient intelligence, it would be able to reflect on itself.","Once the insect-species carcinoma feys transformed into fairies, they all became aware that their power came from being nurtured by Liu Jie.","When Chubby Pocket received Liu Jie’s order, it immediately used Metal Forge Angle and covered its horn with all of the metal attributes in its possession.","Next, it used Spread Wings Insect Cry to distribute the metal attributes to the insects spat out by the Illusionary Layered Caterpillar to raise the defense of the army of insects.","Halberd Banner and Abdomen Battle Drum were also used.","Chubby Pocket also used Metal Solidification Style for the first time, turning its armor and horn into a full set of weaponized equipment.","Insect Soul Undestroyed was also fully activated. Once the insects under Chubby Pocket’s protection or were boosted by it died, their souls would gather around Chubby Pocket to help it to defend against damage.","This ensured that when Chubby Pocket used Broken Halberd Fury and Insect Death, the attacks would be able to hit the ball that had enveloped Lin Yuan.","However, Liu Jie had no clue that Lin Yuan was not present in the ball in the sky.","While the ball of sand was creating the sea of sand, he had already moved to the ground.","He was currently located in a secret and secure area protected by the Overlord Sand.","Since this was a battle, Lin Yuan was going to give it his best. There was no way he would allow himself to become Liu Jie’s punching bag.","It was not just power that was important in battle. Skill was just as important. As the commander of an insect army, Liu Jie should be well aware of this.","However, in this situation where he was disadvantaged, his mind was clouded over. This should never happen to the commander of an insect army.","He hoped that when Chubby Pocket slammed into the ball of sand in the sky, the rebound effect would allow Liu Jie to understand the logic of ‘all’s fair in love and war’.","The sea of insects clashed against the sea of sand and took back control over half of the area.","Soon, the waves of insects encased the sea of sand, and it looked as though they were about to suppress the sea of sand.","However, more discerning people knew that the sea of insects’ advantage was only temporary.","The sea of insects could still hold its own against the sea of sand now. But it was inevitable that the sea of insects would be swallowed and destroyed by the sea of sand.","Liu Jie did not intend to take back the advantage by using the sea of insects to overpower the sea of sand. Instead, he was going to sacrifice the army of insects so that Chubby Pocket could gather more insect souls.","The more insects died, the greater Chubby Pocket’s power would grow through Insect Death.","Chubby Pocket let out a feral bellow, indicating that it had reached its limit of the metals it could transform. Its body would not be able to handle any more.","Liu Jie was in no rush to instruct Chubby Pocket to launch its final attack. Instead, he summoned the Empress Core of All Insects.","Recently, Liu Jie had invested most of his effort into enabling the Empress Core of All Insects’ Stars to break through instead of evolving Elegance’s grade and nurturing the insect-species carcinoma feys.","During Lin Yuan’s crusade across the five dimensional worlds, he had collected many insect-related source totems and gave them to Liu Jie. The latter had selected those that were the most compatible with the Empress Core of All Insects so that it could consume them.","The Empress Core of All Insects had reached 7 Stars and gained its third ability.","Liu Jie was prepared to lay it all out on the table and use the Empress Core of All Insects’ abilities to boost Chubby Pocket.","Liu Jie tossed the Empress Core of All Insects at Chubby Pocket, and it landed on Chubby Pocket’s back.","In an instant, the might of an insect empress wrapped around Chubby Pocket, evolving its aura!","Chubby Pocket was fused with the Empress Core of All Insects through Final Weapon, and it began transforming into the Final Weapon.","This process also strengthened Chubby Pocket’s body, allowing it to contain even more insect souls and metal attributes."]},{"number":2694,"title":"Chapter 2694 The Empress Core of All Insects’ New Ability!","paragraphs":["2694 The Empress Core of All Insects’ New Ability!","The sand was Lin Yuan’s eyes.","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie had been secretly nurturing the Empress Core of All Insects.","Lin Yuan used True Data to pass through the layers of Overlord Sand and Close Guard Sand to detect the Empress Core of All Insects.","[Sacred Source Name]: Empress Core of All Insects","[Sacred Source Species]: Source genus/Sacred Source species","[Sacred Source Star Grade]: 7","[Sacred Source Type]: Insect","Abilities:","[Final Weapon]: Fuse with a lifeform related to insects. The stronger the procreative ability of the lifeform, the stronger the abilities of the fused entity will be. The lifeform’s vitality and procreative ability will be used up to become the final shield of all insects.","[Empress’s Revival]: By using up a large amount of vitality, the lifeform’s genetic model can be triggered to revive the insect empress’ genetic model and will be used on the final weapon. The empress of insects will descend. Before she disappears, the insect-species lifeform will be able to receive the benefit of the empress once.","[Providing for All Insects]: Once all of the insects in the area that were under the control of the Empress Core of All Insects died, their bodies, souls, and wills will gather around the target that is being boosted. They will eventually turn into energy for the target. The target will become stirred up, and its resistance to various elements will be raised.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow as he looked at the Empress Core of All Insects.","Lin Yuan genuinely did not like the Empress Core of All Insects and had not wanted Liu Jie to form a contract with it.","Final Weapon was suitable to be combined with Elegance.","Elegance was a powerful production entity. After the Empress Core of All Insects fused with Elegance, its power would be significantly boosted. However, it would cause Elegance to lose its reproductive abilities while continuously draining its vitality. Hence, any insect-species lifeform with reproductive abilities would not truly benefit from fusing with the Empress Core of All Insects.","Liu Jie would never use Final Weapon flippantly in real life.","Chubby Pocket was an insect-species carcinoma fey that could fight on its own. It did not have a particularly strong reproductive ability. Thus, it would not receive an impactful boost when it fused with the Empress Core of All Insects through Final Weapon.","Nonetheless, Chubby Pocket’s overall power would still be increased by at least twice.","Although Chubby Pocket did not have reproductive abilities, it did contain substantial vitality. The vitality would be continuously used up in exchange for boosting Chubby Pocket’s power.","Lin Yuan had not truly understood the Empress Core of All Insects’ Empress’ Revival the last time that he saw it. This was because the genetic model that would be activated came from the Empress Core of All Insects and not the insect-species carcinoma fey that Liu Jie controlled.","Once this genetic model was activated, the boosted Final Weapon would have the might of an empress.","It was only when Lin Yuan went to the alien insect world and witnessed the might of an alien insect empress that he understood what kind of genetic model would be activated when Empress’ Revival was used.","The Empress Core of All Insects had to have come from an alien insect empress that had died.","Although the alien insect that combined with the Empress Core of All Insects would be perpetually boosted—if Lin Yuan had not used the Jasmine Lily and opened the Vitality Imprint as well as the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen’s Sacred Sword form’s healing abilities—Liu Jie’s Insect Queen would have died while in the empress state.","Liu Jie would not have many opportunities in real life to use this ability that required healing-type spirit qi professionals to constantly be present to help sustain the effects.","Lin Yuan asked Liu Jie never to use the Empress Core of All Insects’ first two abilities unless he was with him to support him.","Presently, Liu Jie mainly relied on insect-species carcinoma feys to fight.","But as Liu Jie’s spirit qi professional rank continued to rise, by the time Elegance reached Eternal Breed, the combat power of Elegance’s insect army would be even stronger than insect-species carcinoma feys!","The insect-species carcinoma feys could not be evolved like regular feys even after being transformed into fairies. Moreover, the evolution also needed the fairy bloodline to be balanced while they were being nurtured.","If Lin Yuan summoned the eight-winged Red Thorn now, the pressure from its bloodline would already have put an end to the battle. Additionally, the pressure between fairies was stronger than dragon-species feys.","This was the first time Lin Yuan saw the Empress Core of All Insects’ Providing for All Insects.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, Providing for All Insects revitalized both Final Weapon and Empress’ Revival and lifted their restrictions.","Providing for All Insects was very compatible with Chubby Pocket’s ability Insect Soul Undestroyed.","The insects’ souls, bodies, and wills would gather toward Chubby Pocket and turn into its energy.","This energy included vitality.","When Liu Jie used a sea of insects that was composed of many types of insect-species carcinoma feys, it would be able to supply a large amount of vitality when boosted by the Empress Core of All Insects.","Lin Yuan was very happy for Liu Jie.","As long as Liu Jie could finish establishing his needed environment and estimate the amount of vitality the Empress Core of All Insects depleted while boosting targets, he could use its ability to keep the battle in the palm of his hand.","However, he would not be able to win this battle because the insect armies’ bodies had all been ground to dust by the Source Sand.","The Source Sand had a Suzerain metal spiritual ingredient called Spirit-Selling Gold. It had an extremely strong will-destroying effect.","The sea of sand completely annihilated the insect army’s will.","Hence, when Chubby Pocket was boosted by Providing for All Insects, it could only absorb the insect souls.","When the Empress Core of All Insects boosted Chubby Pocket, it became the insect species’ ultimate weapon. A jet of power that contained the might of an insect empress shot into the ball of sand in the sky that was still spewing sand.","Lin Yuan had not been idle while investigating the Empress Core of All Insects’ abilities.","He commandeered the ball of sand to be composed of a large amount of Close Guard Sand and Overlord Sand.","The ball of sand expanded as its interior was coated with layer upon layer of radium. The radium was blended with Red Lotus Soft Gold and Vibrating Gold threads.","Once Chubby Pocket broke through the radium layers, the Vibrating Gold would reflect the damage done by Chubby Pocket.","The Red Lotus Soft Gold could target the spirit and would also torment Chubby Pocket.","The moment that Vibrating Gold and Red Lotus Soft Gold were pierced by Chubby Pocket’s horn, they would wrap tightly around the horn. As a result, Chubby Pocket’s horn would be stuck in the ball of sand.","At that time, a hand formed from Overlord Sand would emerge from the ball of sand and pull Chubby Pocket in.","The Source Sand did have a main body and returned to Lin Yuan’s sleeve.","The Close Guard Sand and Overlord Sand were just a portion of the Source Sand’s strength. Regardless of how they were attacked, the Source Sand would not be impacted.","This battle was a demonstration to all the Radiance citizens of the peak of the younger generation’s power.","The impending Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections would also be thrilling. However, it was unlikely that a match of a similar caliber would be seen again.","Even the commentators with a wealth of experience had their lips tightly pursed, and their eyes widened as they silently watched what was happening.","The scales of this battle had tipped abruptly. The army of insects seemed to have secured the upper hand and was shaping up to be a devastating catastrophe centered around insect-species carcinoma feys.","With the 12 amber wings flapping behind Lin Yuan, he looked like an angel at sunset.","The army of insects caused the audience to feel extremely suffocated. However, this assault on the senses was wiped out by the sand in an instant.","Anyone could tell that Lin Yuan had the advantage.","However, the power surrounding Chubby Pocket was growing.","The capable commentators could already see Chubby Pocket’s true power and knew that it exceeded Creation Breed power. Its attack had reached Immortal Breed level.","An A-rank spirit qi professional commanded a Myth Breed fey that unleashed an attack two grades above its current one!","Would Lin Yuan, trapped within the ball of sand, be able to shield himself from such a powerful attack?","When the fairy transformed from the insect-species carcinoma fey crashed into the ball of sand, the vibrations would destroy Lin Yuan, who was hiding within.","Poison Beauty forced herself to calm down and remember that she was in the middle of a live-stream before she said, “It looks like Lord Lin Yuan underestimated his opponent this time. It’s not a good plan to seal himself within the ball of sand!”","Poison Beauty and Lu Shuang were Lin Yuan’s biggest beneficiaries. They managed to become the most popular hosts in the Radiance Federation because of him.","Lu Shuang and Poison Beauty became friends after an offline event. They decided to live-stream together this time. They connected their channels and commentated on the battles together.","Their channel had entered the Glorious Popularity Ranking and reached the sixth place. It was a big honor for Star Web hosts to made it into this ranking!","When Lu Shuang heard what Poison Beauty said, she felt that Poison Beauty’s view was too naive.","As a direct participant, Liu Jie was choosing to attack the ball of sand in the sky rather than the sand below him because his army of insects had been destroyed, and he had no other choice.","Lu Shuang had battled Lin Yuan in the past. She saw him as a hardened vault who was always hiding more moves up his sleeve.","After using the full extent of her capabilities, she had been under the impression that the Exquisite Rhino Giraffe would be able to kill Lin Yuan. However, all that had happened was that eight tails had appeared behind him.","There was no way that Lin Yuan was staying still within the ball and allowing Liu Jie to attack him at will!","The sand was raining down from the ball of sand in a waterfall that was ten meters wide. Lin Yuan could move himself at any time. There was no need for him to remain in the ball. This was unless Lin Yuan needed to seal himself away for the ball of sand resembling the sun to continue releasing sand.","The two hosts could have different opinions. The more popular the live-streaming rooms with opposing opinions, the more gifts the eventual victor would receive.","However, Lu Shuang did not end up speaking her mind.","Given that the ball of sand in the sky was expanding, it was as though Lin Yuan could tell that Liu Jie was attacking and was trying to defend himself.","Lu Shuang kept her eyes glued to the ball of sand and awaited the next attack—it would decide the result of this battle.","Poison Beauty narrowed her eyes at Lu Shuang. Normally, Lu Shuang would respond with her own opinion after she gave hers. However, Lu Shuang had not picked up and added to what she said.","Poison Beauty was concerned that she had said something wrong.","It might go unnoticed if a small host misspoke. But she was already one of the biggest hosts on Star Web. Even the slightest of slips of the tongue would result in significant negative impacts.","Poison Beauty glanced at the comments and saw that they were mostly discussing the battle. No one had mentioned her.","Poison Beauty relaxed when she saw this.","When she looked back at the battle, Chubby Pocket had slammed into the rapidly expanding ball of sand with incredible force.","Poison Beauty assumed that the powerful Chubby Pocket would shatter the ball of sand. But to her surprise, all that happened was that Chubby Pocket’s horn pierced through the ball of sand, leaving most of its body stuck outside.","After sustaining such immense force, the ball of sand’s shape had changed. But almost immediately after, a burst of energy with equal force exploded from the site where Chubby Pocket had pierced through the ball of sand. As a result, cracks appeared all over Chubby Pocket.","Chubby Pocket managed to contain the damage by swiftly absorbing insect souls into its body.","Liu Jie had not anticipated this situation.","This was not because Liu Jie had not expected Lin Yuan to be powerful. He was well aware of Lin Yuan’s true power.","However, Liu Jie also knew that Lin Yuan had only used the Source Sand so far in this battle.","The Source Sand’s counterattack on Chubby Pocket caused a bitter smile to spread across Liu Jie’s face.","He was not able to defeat the Source Sand even after using his sacred source lifeform, Elegance, and insect-species carcinoma feys.","Although Liu Jie was rather disheartened, he suddenly remembered something that Lin Yuan had said to him.","“Big Brother Liu, don’t allow your thinking to be skewed when it comes to increasing your power. A person’s value does not only come from his power. One’s combat ability also adds to his value.","“Functional attributes are always more important than individual combat. It is easy to cultivate powerful experts, but mere resources won’t be enough to produce a functional-type expert with irreplaceable skills!","“Big Brother Liu, you have already started going down a unique path that will afford you special abilities. This is an important strategic foundation for Sky City. So, there is no need for you to be overly concerned about your strength on the dueling ground.”","At the time, Liu Jie had not understood why Lin Yuan said this. But now, he did."]},{"number":2695,"title":"Chapter 2695 Crowning Glory!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2695 Crowning Glory!","Lin Yuan was setting up preventive measures for Liu Jie. He was worried that Liu Jie would end up spiraling and becoming nitpicky after he lost his battle.","Now that he understood this, a look of realization appeared on Liu Jie’s face. Perhaps the most important takeaway from this battle was a change in mindset.","Lin Yuan had used this battle to teach Liu Jie a valuable lesson.","The result of this match had been decided. Liu Jie already guessed that Lin Yuan would not remain in the ball of sand in the sky.","Every grain of sand in the sea of sand became Lin Yuan’s citizens, and he could manipulate them as he pleased.","Liu Jie had instructed Chubby Pocket to attack the ball of sand in the sky because he could no longer detect Lin Yuan’s position after so many of the insects had died.","Furthermore, Liu Jie knew that this was a performance duel. Since he was going to lose, he decided to funnel all his power into one attack rather than try to locate Lin Yuan.","Otherwise, this situation would not have taken place.","When Chubby Pocket collided with the ball of sand, Liu Jie knew that this battle had come to an end.","Once the hand of sand grabbed Chubby Pocket and pulled it into the ball of sand, Liu Jie had no moves left to play.","He had achieved the objective of his battle.","This battle allowed him to once again become aware of the distance between himself and Lin Yuan.","However, Liu Jie did not blame himself or spiral into negative thoughts surrounding how he lacked the power to protect Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie now recognized his value to Sky City.","As one of Sky City’s three founders, he would be disappointing Lin Yuan and his trust in him if he continued pedantic.","This battle, full of twists and turns between the cream of the crop of the younger generation, had effectively boosted the faith of the Radiance citizens.","The Moon Empress had been paying close attention to Lin Yuan’s battles.","After his four battles, a dazzling smile appeared on her face.","She could not help but think back to a year ago. At that time, he had fought doggedly against the members of the Freedom Federation and only just managed to win by the skin of his teeth.","He had managed to grow to such a degree in the span of a year.","In just less than three years, he was unrecognizable from the young boy who came from the Xia Region. Not only had he become famous throughout the Radiance Federation, but he had even become the protector of the main world!","Mystic Moon saw the Moon Empress’s smile and could not help but marvel at and be happy for Lin Yuan’s sake.","As one of the Moon Empress’ two Moon Envoys, he received immense blessings from Lin Yuan. Thanks to Lin Yuan’s resources, Mystic Moon managed to grow rapidly.","Mystic Moon was considered Lin Yuan’s senior, and he wanted to see the ceiling of Lin Yuan’s power.","Mystic Moon could sense that the Moon Empress was no longer focused on the main world, although she continued to manage the Radiance Federation’s affairs.","The Moon Empress’ goal was now the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He might have the chance to go with her to see worlds beyond the main world!","“Moon Empress, the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s reranking is done. Next is the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. It will take place over three days.","“The leaders of the other federations will arrive in the Radiance Federation in the next two days. They are hoping to meet with you. Do you want me to make the arrangements?”","The Moon Empress was silent for a moment before asking, “Mystic Moon, did Elder Liu really change the setting of the test to the dead spirits crisis?”","Mystic Moon pursed his lips before saying softly, “Liu Wencheng is even more ruthless than I expected. He not only simulated the environment of the dead spirits crisis but also copied various types of dead dimensional lifeforms and added them in. The test is much harder than it was last year!","“If only the newcomers are participating in the test, they might end up killed by the dead dimensional lifeforms in less than half a day. So, Liu Wencheng decided that the first ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence will also be entering the test to act as leaders that will separate the environment into ten areas.","“The participants being tested will gather around the leaders and seek their protection. Aside from providing rations, the leaders will also score the participants. Those with the highest scores will become part of the final 100 candidates, and the victors from the 100 candidates will become the last ten ranks of the newest generation of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","“The remaining 90 candidates will receive invitations from different departments like the Spirit Guards and Cultivated Garden. Although they won’t receive as many resources as the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, they will still be nurtured well.”","Mystic Moon’s sacred source lifeform was one of the main components that created and sustained Star Web. The two changes to Star Web’s format were linked to his sacred source lifeform.","As long as he wanted to, there was nothing on Star Web that Mystic Moon could not find out about.","Since the Moon Empress had asked, Mystic Moon told her everything that he knew.","The Moon Empress chuckled softly. “Elder Liu really put a lot of thought into the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection!”","To make sure the last ten members of the new generation would have enough strength, unlike the last generation, where eight out of the ten newcomers were selected again this year, Liu Wencheng devised a plan to subject the 100 candidates to an attrition battle.","However, he also considered the fact that surviving did not equate to power. Thus, he decided to send the first ten ranks of the current Radiance Hundred Sequence into the test to act as facilitators who would score the participants.","The first ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence could handle such a responsibility.","However, he would only be able to use this method once or twice before he had to do away with it. This was because it gave the first ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence too much superior authority.","This would result in the first ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence being affected by many elements.","Such authority could not be given out flippantly. Otherwise, the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would lose its purity!","The Moon Empress intended to discuss this matter with Liu Wencheng. She believed that with his experience and knowledge, he would easily be able to see this!","After the demon insects were sent to the Radiance Federation’s various areas, their effects were very obvious.","It could be said that the demon insects had controlled the dead spirits crisis.","The Moon Empress knew that Tower Canon definitely had more moves up their sleeve. Hence, she dared not take her foot off the pedal.","The Land Imps were still building bases and defenses throughout the Radiance Federation.","Given the demon insects’ rapid rate of reproduction and with Wen Yu in charge of the transportation, the Moon Empress could consider delivering the demon insects outside of the Radiance Federation.","The Moon Empress knew why the leaders of the various federations wanted to see her. They hoped that the Radiance Federation would help them again.","News of the Radiance Federation’s discovery of the Dead Decay Earthworm had spread.","Frankly, this was not the first time that the leaders of the various federations wanted to see her.","But she had not agreed to see them in the past.","This time, she was going to meet with them because she had found a way to settle the issue.","Furthermore, now that the Radiance Federation had the confidence to take on the dead spirits crisis, the Moon Empress also wanted to give the rest of the federations in the main world this confidence.","The Radiance Federation had become the core of all the human federations. It was the center around which the other federations gravitated.","The Azure Federation and Freedom Federation flanked the Radiance Federation, allowing it to come across as the moon surrounded by stars.","If she wanted to use the demon insects to change and manage the environment in the dimensional worlds as well as gradually clear out the dead spirits with the Radiance Federation at the helm, she needed to bolster the rest of the human federations as well.","Since all the federations had come to plead with the Radiance Federation, the Radiance Federation could make a gesture of their own.","The Major Federation Union meeting would once again solidify the Radiance Federation’s position as the core.","“Mystic Moon, send out an announcement to the leaders of the other federations. Tell them to come to the Radiance Sacred Hall two days later to watch the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. I will also be in attendance.","“Give the federations who haven’t arrived in the Radiance Federation a day so they have time to rush to the Radiance Federation using the Spatial Mother Shellfish’s shell pieces.”","After hearing the Moon Empress’ instruction, Mystic Moon knew that she intended to take charge of managing the entire main world.","If the demon insects were not reproducing so quickly that they were able to address the issues in the Radiance Federation, the Moon Empress would never be so impulsive as to share the resources regardless of what Mystic Moon said or how he urged her.","As a Moon Envoy, Mystic Moon was responsible for assisting the Moon Empress, and he often reminded her of such detailed affairs. The Moon Empress was usually aware of most of these affairs, but his reminders never annoyed her.","Mystic Moon’s thinking was always clear and calm. With someone like this giving her reminders, the Moon Empress could be confident that nothing would go wrong.","When the Moon Empress issued the order to Mystic Moon, all of the live-streaming rooms on Star Web began filling up with comments on Lin Yuan’s title, Miracle.","Lin Yuan’s existence was miraculous for the Radiance citizens. He churned out miracles continuously.","While Lin Yuan was basking in the glory, Shiny was protesting in his soul.","Lin Yuan knew that it wanted to make an appearance. However, the time had not been right.","If Shiny had appeared during his battle against Mu Yan, he would have been able to win easily. However, there was no need for Lin Yuan to summon a fey with the Barren bloodline that was iconic of the Radiance Federation in a battle against Mu Yan.","It was also unsuitable for Shiny to appear during his battles against Liu Jie, Long Tao, and Xia Qing.","Firstly, it would have been immediately defeated in the battle against Liu Jie.","Shiny could fuse with the wind elements in the battle against Xia Qing and the arena full of fire elements to sense Xia Qing’s position.","The wind-elemental energy would also be able to push out the sea formed from the Victory Fish’s body. But it would require a large amount of energy to propel the wind-elemental energy to the bottom of the sea to sense the Victory Fish’s position.","Because of these reasons, Lin Yuan had yet to release Shiny.","However, he had already promised Shiny that it could fight to its heart’s content.","Lin Yuan soothed Shiny, “There is still the Radiance Envoy selection after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. You will definitely have the chance to make an appearance then! Hold on a little more. You will only have to wait three more days at the most.”","Shiny had a personality that was very easily appeased. After receiving Lin Yuan’s promise, it immediately began happily cuddling up to him in his soul.","Lin Yuan shook his head vexedly. He did not know if it was because Shiny had spent a long time with Genius, but he noticed it was coquettishly in an increasingly similar way to Genius!","After acting coquettishly for some time, Shiny told Lin Yuan seriously, “Yuan, can you give me some dragon liver and phoenix blood? If you give me a little more, I will be able to evolve to Suzerain/Myth three days later! I can’t bring myself to ask you to feed me water from the Element Well daily.”","Lin Yuan frowned slightly. “Shiny, if you want to continue accumulating your power, don’t force yourself to evolve just so you can participate in battle. You will be able to participate in battle when the time is right, even if you haven’t yet evolved to Suzerain/Myth at that time!”","Shiny hurriedly said, “Yuan, if I were the anxious type, I wouldn’t have asked for a few days of rest. But now, it’s time for me to evolve to Suzerain/pinnacle Myth II. Don’t worry. I won’t joke around with increasing my power and level. It’s really time for me to increase my power! I am also ready for this!”","Lin Yuan relaxed when he heard this.","“Shiny, I am now Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. For the next three days, I will have to help the newcomers with their selection. I will place sufficient dragon liver and phoenix blood in the Return from Faraway Mansion’s breeding room so you can take as much as you need.","“Do you remember the spatial equipment I hung on your leg? It is filled with elemental pearls and spirit qi crystals. You can use them at will, too. Once I’m back, I will help you with your breakthrough!”","Lin Yuan liked watching his feys grow, and Shiny also wanted Lin Yuan to be there when it evolved.","“Yuan, I will be good and wait for you at home!”","...","Lin Yuan braved all the difficulties and finally took the position of Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","The stone pillar of Sequence #1 was much taller than the other stone pillars.","After every Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Sacred Hall created a new batch of statues for the members.","During the year that the dead spirits crisis broke out, Lin Yuan’s statue would stand in the position of Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","After the reranking ended, Lin Yuan and the rest left Star Web.","Meanwhile, Star Web was celebrating wildly over the matches.","When the dead spirits crisis began, many taverns and bars closed. Even the Spirit Food Pavilion started to limit their opening hours.","But now, due to this event that rejuvenated their confidence, all the streets of the Radiance Federation were once again filled with life.","Cicada Song, who managed the various cities, had been keeping an eye on the situation.","After receiving the report from his subordinates, all of the tension finally lifted off of Cicada Song.","“Radiance Federation, you have finally regained your vigor!”","Cicada Song prayed that this zeal and confidence would last.","However, he knew that this would be difficult because changes could crop up anything during the dead spirits crisis.","However, the vibrant zest and confidence permeating the Radiance Federation now would give the citizens more fighting spirit and unity in the days to come as they continued taking on the dead spirits crisis.","Cicada Song immediately told the other members of the Radiance Federation the good news through the Thoughts Letter Paper."]},{"number":2696,"title":"Chapter 2696 Appointing Leaders in the Selection!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2696 Appointing Leaders in the Selection!","The Radiance Federation’s circumstances had undergone tumultuous changes over the course of the dead spirits crisis. The Radiance Federation’s royalty had tried their best but were unable to make effective progress.","It could be said that most of the impactful progress stemmed from Lin Yuan.","At first, the Radiance Federation’s royalty had been somewhat confident. But after the dead dimensional lifeforms appeared and the Dead Decay Earthworms lost their effectiveness, the dead aura rampantly stole lives, and the Radiance Federation’s royalty became increasingly nervous.","But now, the demon insects had wholly changed the circumstances and gave the humans the upper hand for the first time during the dead spirits crisis.","The Moon Empress was not at all surprised by Cicada Song’s message. She already knew how capable the demon insects were at absorbing death aura.","Moreover, the demon insects were continuing to multiply underground.","The more the Moon Empress thought about it, the more terrifying she found the demon insect species to be.","On more than one instance, she had already been grateful that the crisis came from the dead spirits and not the demon insects. Otherwise, the demon insects that could consume everything and anything might end up eating the entire main world.","The Moon Empress had confirmed with Lin Yuan that he had complete control over the demon insects. It was only then that she was set at ease.","Previously, Lin Yuan was Sequence #91 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. But now, he had climbed up to Sequence #1.","Lin Yuan no longer had any chances to issue challenges. He could only be challenged by others.","After Lin Yuan, there were still 90 members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who had yet to issue challenges, and the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking had to go on.","But after Lin Yuan’s four consecutive stunning battles, the rest of the battles seemed rather tame. None of them reached the standard of Lin Yuan’s battles.","However, after the temporary cloud of disappointment passed, the excitement levels rose again.","Every member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence was a household name in the Radiance Federation. All of them had their own signature feys and battle styles.","This was the first time that the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking was being held publicly. It was a visual feast for the Radiance citizens.","So this was the true power of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation! Numerous veteran experts could not help but sigh in shame.","As the thrilling battles took place, Tian Ningning became the busiest person in the Radiance Federation.","She personally checked every dueling record to ensure that they were accurate.","At the very least, her workload would not be increased because of the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking’s dueling records.","The dueling records’ relevance and efficacy were time-sensitive. If Star Web’s officials produced the dueling records too slowly and others produced them first, Star Web’s officials would come across as lazy.","Tian Ningning immediately contacted Liu Hao. She hoped that he would be able to send more help.","In the past, Liu Hao viewed Tian Ningning with derision. He believed that she was only able to make it this far because she was Lin Yuan’s exclusive reporter.","But after working together, he got to know of her capabilities and could not help but think to himself that it was no wonder that Lin Yuan had chosen her!","Despite leading such a large team, she was still able to ensure that she performed her tasks well. Not only was she efficient, but she had yet to make a single mistake.","...","The spectators were almost vibrating with excitement as they watched the consecutive battles.","However, none of them were sad when the Radiance Federation reranking came to an end because they knew that up next was the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Radiance Knight selection, and Radiance Envoy selection.","They would be able to watch Lin Yuan in action again during the Radiance Envoy selection.","Normally, the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would only take place a few days after the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking. But due to the urgency of the matter, the selection this year would take place half a day after the reranking.","As Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Lin Yuan needed to enter the selection as a leader. Hence, he did not have time to meet with his friends.","Liu Wencheng told Lin Yuan and the rest seriously, “In your previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, you only represented yourself. But now, you will have to shoulder the responsibility of promoting members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. We are bestowing this responsibility on you, so you have to treat it with careful reverence!”","Liu Wencheng received the message from the Moon Empress half an hour ago. He understood her meaning.","In actuality, he never intended to maintain this new format for too long.","In three to five years, once the Radiance Hundred Sequence had completely new members and was no longer defined by martial force, Liu Wencheng could retract this responsibility from the first ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Ever since the Radiance Sacred Hall was established, Liu Wencheng had been in charge of it. He had even watched the Moon Empress and the rest grow up.","As a wise person, he could think comprehensively in every matter.","After speaking to Lin Yuan and the other top nine rankers of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Liu Wencheng began thinking about where to position them.","The arrangement of their positions was critical because Liu Wencheng could not allow the spectators watching the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection to think that the dead spirits crisis was trivial.","Liu Wencheng was going to simulate a realistic environment modeled after the Dead Spirits Well. Hence, the positioning was crucial. If there was an issue with the positioning, there was a high possibility that one of the top ten members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would end up dying.","This would not only be a blow to the reputation of these members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence but would also affect the confidence of the Radiance citizens.","It was known that not everything could always go as planned. Liu Wencheng needed to put a lot of careful thought into the matter if he wanted to ensure he did not hit any bumps along the road.","However, this would mean that Lin Yuan and Liu Jie had to handle the same load that was being shared among the other four.","Liu Wencheng seriously told Lin Yuan and Liu Jie, “The two of you will be sent to the most dangerous positions. It will be just as laborious as handling a Dead Spirits Well on your own. The only difference between this and an actual Dead Spirits Well was that all of these dead spirits would only have Diamond and below power.”","Lin Yuan and Liu Jie looked at each other. The two of them were unafraid of swarm battles. All Lin Yuan needed to do was release Red Thorn, and Liu Jie could release a few insect-species carcinoma feys to suppress the swarm.","“Don’t worry, Your Excellency. We will definitely take proper responsibility for this duty!” Lin Yuan paused before continuing. “There are still three hours before the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection begins. I need to leave to make preparations to evolve my feys.”","Liu Wencheng’s lips curled into a smile as he nodded. It was definitely good news that Lin Yuan’s feys could evolve again!","“Go ahead. Don’t forget to be back half an hour before it begins. The Star Web broadcast will begin half an hour before the selection begins. You will need to head in early to wait.”","Liu Wencheng was not strict with the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence when it came to such small matters. As long as the main events were not delayed, he was understanding when it came to urgent matters.","...","Lin Yuan immediately returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion and summoned Shiny to the breeding room.","Next, he laid out all the dragon liver, phoenix blood, and other spiritual ingredients that Shiny needed for its evolution before returning to the Radiance Sacred Hall.","Lin Yuan was really looking forward to this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","This was because he had yet to have many opportunities to visit the Dead Spirits Wells and personally experience the might of the waves of dead spirits.","The last time he was there, the dead spirits crisis had only just begun. But now, the situation had already changed completely.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan had participated in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection as a candidate who had to compete with the others last year. But this time, he was an invigilator.","He was more than willing to gain a detailed understanding of the power of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation now that a year had passed.","...","There was half an hour to prepare before the event actually began.","Xia Qing coughed softly to Lin Yuan before seriously saying, “In the past, Grandfather often praised your capabilities, and I am also aware that you are exceptionally strong. I saw your battle with the Freedom Federation envoy group last year. I thought that there would be a stalemate between us for some time. But I never expected to suffer such an utter defeat at your hands!”","Xia Qing’s voice was laced with bitterness, and she sounded stiff. It seemed as though she could not swallow her defeat to Lin Yuan!","But those who were familiar with her knew that she was being shy. Her voice was only coming up this way because she was panicking. Normally, her voice did not carry any emotion.","Lin Yuan hurriedly said, “You are already sufficiently strong. If your Misfortune Fighter’s bloodline takes another step forward, Chimey will be no match for it!”","Lin Yuan could clearly see the respect and admiration in Xia Qing’s eyes as she spoke. This was the same way that he used to look at seniors in his previous life.","Xia Qing pursed her lips and said pragmatically, “Lin Yuan, you don’t have to consider my feelings. Even if you don’t use your full power, you will be able to beat me very quickly as long as you are determined to do so.","“Don’t forget that you only used two feys while I used four during our battle! One of them was even my sacred source lifeform!","“I used to think that the only member of the younger generation stronger than me is you. But even Liu Jie is stronger than me! It’s true that your bird-species fey won’t be able to unleash its full potential against the army of insects.”","After she was done speaking, Xia Qing silently walked off to the side and replayed the battle between herself and Lin Yuan.","The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, including Lin Yuan and Liu Jie, did not know Xia Qing well.","This was because they were not nosy or interested in gossip and because Xia Qing was not the sociable type.","Hence, the first impression that she gave was one of arrogance.","However, after what she said today, all of their ideas of her changed completely.","Although she was arrogant, she was able to face her failures objectively and admit her issues.","These were all virtues that the elites of the younger generation rarely possessed. This showed that she was pure-hearted.","Lin Yuan walked over to Liu Jie and patted his shoulder. “Big Brother Liu, if the attack from the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle hits its mark, not even Immortal Breed feys will be able to escape without being seriously injured!","“If I was in that ball of sand, I would have died regardless of how many metals the Source Sand produced to try and protect me!”","Liu Jie had already adjusted his mindset. He no longer associated his value with his combat power. Instead, he was going to focus on the functions of his abilities.","As a result of this change in mindset, he regained his confidence. “Lin Yuan, I have a few carcinoma feys. When we return, help me to pick two of them that will be suited for my formation!”","Gao Feng had also become an A-rank spirit qi professional. The Breeze Hibiscus, two Spirit Spring Lilies, and Yellow Spring Lily had evolved to Suzerain/Myth. He was able to use the strength of his feys’ bodies to defeat opponents.","If he were still a B-rank spirit qi professional, being a pure support-type spirit qi professional might have caused him to lose and have to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection again.","Lin Yuan used to think that a spirit qi professional’s development could be skewed in one direction if he were part of a stable team. But now, he knew that the right thing for spirit qi professionals to do was to pursue well-rounded development.","An expert could go down their paths with companions, but the companions were more for encouragement rather than support.","Gao Feng was slightly laid back and did not have much motivation. His personality suited being a pure support-type spirit qi professional.","Long Tao had been focused on managing Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","Although he had adjusted his mindset, one’s mental strength was limited.","This time, he lost to Wang Fan and almost lost to Shi Xu as well.","As a result, he decided to set aside managing Coiling Dragon’s Valley and focus on increasing his individual power. He did not want his personal power to end up lagging because he devoted himself to Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s affairs for the next few years.","These peers who used to be weaker than him were now experts whom he had to struggle to catch up with. He did not even have to think of closing the gap between himself and Lin Yuan.","Nonetheless, they were all disciples of members of royalty, and he had yet to lose the chance to catch up to Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and the rest."]},{"number":2697,"title":"Chapter 2697: Epoch God Palace in Action!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2697: Epoch God Palace in Action!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Liu Wencheng looked at the time and said sternly, “All of you can go in now!","Later, the Radiance Hundred Sequence members will be sent to the various","Dead Spirits Wells to train. The ten of you will be the leaders. It will be good for you to gain a prior understanding of the dead spirits.”","The members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were all experienced. However, facing the perils of the Dead Spirits Wells on Star Web would be a shock to their systems.","Albeit, Lin Yuan would not be one of those people.","Not only had he witnessed the situation around the Dead Spirits Wells, but he had personally led the demon insects to the Dead Spirits Wells to take control of them as well.","Frankly, Liu Wencheng had thought about swapping Lin Yuan out for another member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. He knew that Lin Yuan was swamped with things to do.","He had discussed this with the Moon Empress.","She responded that it would be Lin Yuan’s decision, so Liu Wencheng asked Lin Yuan. He only sent Lin Yuan in as part of the ten people when he confirmed with Lin Yuan that he wanted this.","While Long Tao, Li Fan, and the rest had austere expressions, Lin Yuan looked excited. He looked forward to being pleasantly surprised by the Radiance Federation’s youths.","Long Tao, Wang Fan, and the rest were all veterans of the Radiance Hundred Sequence and knew Liu Wencheng well. They knew what kind of person he was. He would never repeat his warnings repeatedly unless the dangers were truly serious.","It seemed that this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection would test both the Radiance Federation’s youths and the top ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Tian Ningning was extremely busy checking the dueling record drafts and did not have the bandwidth for anything else.","Tian Ningning picked two capable spokespeople and gave them the information sent by the Radiance Sacred Hall’s staff so they could give a detailed introduction of the setting.","This was a good chance to demonstrate her capabilities to the Radiance citizens. Everyone assumed that she would make sure to grab the opportunity. No one expected her to give such a rare opportunity away.","In the past, it was not just Liu Hao who had doubted Tian Ningning. There were many members of the special teams who had done the same.","Tian Ningning first led the team in accomplishing the tasks and proved her abilities. Now, she was proving her character to all of Star Web’s departments.","It was rare for a supervisor to be willing to give away benefits that were supposed to belong to them.","The two spokespeople Tian Ningning chose were extremely grateful to her.","With her current reputation, no one would stop her from being one of the Star Web reporter spokespeople. Moreover, she had been a spokesperson for Black in the past.","Although she was only a Star Web reporter, she still caught the Moon Empress’ eye by being linked to Lin Yuan.","Tian Ningning had no idea that the Moon Empress had been observing her. She was very satisfied with Tian Ningning’s action.","Lin Yuan and the rest were delivered to the test ground.","Once they entered, Lin Yuan frowned slightly. This was because he could sense that the concentration of death aura in the environment was higher than what regular people could handle.","If a regular person got a whiff of this concentration of death aura, they would be dead in around 18 hours due to their bodies being infected and decaying. In around a week or two, they would become a dead spirit.","Although spirit qi professionals had stronger physiques than regular people, they could not last more than three days unless they had reached A-rank and their spiritual energy had concentrated to a certain degree.","Even A-rank spirit qi professionals who could concentrate their spiritual energy to defend themselves against death aura would not be able to last in this environment for more than a week.","Lin Yuan could tell from this environment that Liu Wencheng was taking the test extremely seriously.","The environment was a perfect copy of the concentration of death aura around actual Dead Spirits Wells.","Moreover, to ensure that the Radiance citizens could quickly understand the danger, dead dimensional lifeforms would also appear during the simulated dead spirits crisis.","With Lin Yuan included, there were six A-rank spirit qi professionals among the top ten members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. The other four and their feys would not be able to fend off the death aura. Despite being leaders, they would not be able to last more than three days.","When Lin Yuan entered, he noticed that Liu Wencheng gave him a profound look.","The Thoughts Letter Paper could also be used on Star Web.","The top ten members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence all received a Thoughts Letter Paper so they could communicate with each other conveniently.","Lin Yuan noticed that the four members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence who had yet to reach A-rank were nearer to him. It seemed that Liu Wencheng was hoping that he could look after the B-rank spirit qi professionals.","This selection that was being broadcast on Star Web was also meant to be somewhat performative.","Hence, Lin Yuan could not allow these four members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence to fall.","Now that he had become aware of this, Lin Yuan knew what to do later.","The selection had yet to officially begin. Lin Yuan and the rest could not set up defenses in advance, but thev could begin scanning the surrounding terrain so that it would be easier for them to lead the newcomers in navigating the dead spirits crisis later.","They also began placing the Dead Decay Earthworms they had received at the most suitable positions for defense.","It was not just the Star Web officials who had sent spokespeople to commentate on the selection. The officials also permitted reporters and other spokespeople who had been to the Dead Spirits Wells and observed the situation there to release and share information.","All of the Radiance citizens finally gained a real understanding of the dead spirits crisis. This understanding would deepen once the selection began.","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, using the dead spirits crisis as an objective test setting was not fair for many participants because those who were able to defend themselves against death aura would have a significant advantage. But this did not mean that their feys were powerful or that they were truly strong.","Nonetheless, it was said that heroes were bred from success. When Liu Wencheng realized that the dead spirits crisis might not come to an end for a few thousand years, he needed to make the best decision that suited the current circumstances.","Liu Wencheng had asked the other 12 members of royalty about this decision through the Thoughts Letter Paper. After the Moon Empress and the rest thought it over, they gave him their affirmation.","However, Liu Wencheng never expected Lin Yuan to figure out his idea immediately after entering the test ground.","Last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection had the most number of registered participants in a decade.","Liu Wencheng believed that it was unlikely that the record would be beaten in the future.","Many schools and cities sent the same number of participants each year.","There were many members of the younger generation who earned their right to participate by battling on Star Web.","This also applied to Lin Yuan. However, no one else stood out as much as he did.","Yet, to his surprise, there were more participants this year than last year!","The members of the younger generation who did not earn the chance to participate last year could not participate this year either!","Liu Wencheng was very happy that many of the Radiance Federation’s youths were willing to step up and offer their power to become its pillars.","Due to the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking broadcast that had just ended, the Radiance citizens were also paying more attention to this year’s selection than last year’s.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection’s participants were about to enter.","It was time for Liu Wencheng to head to the Radiance Sacred Hall to host the selection.","The fighting spirit of the Radiance Federation was burning fervently. However,","Towar Cnnnn c:till had nnt made anv new mnvpc:","Still, the death aura emanating from the towers on the islands was even more concentrated than before.","At that moment, the previously tightly sealed stone doors were pushed open.","Three masked and bronze armor-wearing teams walked out of the stone doors and broke the silence that had been maintained outside the stone doors for thousands of years.","There was a towering mountain behind the stone doors that pierced through the clouds.","At the mountain’s base, spring was in full bloom. Just above, there was a blend of spring and summer. Higher up, the mountain marked the transition from summer to autumn, and at its peak, endless winter prevailed.","This mountain showcased all four seasons, making it extraordinarily beautiful and enigmatic. Behind the mountain, four grand palaces stood.","Initially, these palaces were quiet. Their doors opened only once a year during the changing of the seasons, promptly closing afterward. However, this time, the four doors remained ajar.","Before these doors, dozens of people were engaged in ancient and mysterious rituals, offering prayers.","Inside each palace, a figure knelt facing the wall behind the throne, praying solemnly, their expressions filled with delight.","The wall’s images had been changing abruptly for the past two years. The transformations had accelerated recently, occurring every few days and growing more intricate, signaling the full awakening of Lord Saint.","Lord Totem God alone was not enough to cause so much change.","Lord Totem God’s awakening also confirmed that Lord Saint had landed in this world.","Epoch God Palace had been waiting for this epoch for an extremely long time, and it was finally taking place!","After completing this round of sacrificial rites, Epoch God Palace would no longer have to remain hidden. Instead, they could leave to search for Lord Saint and Lord Totem God.","Epoch God Palace’s only goal was to be followers.","Otherwise, the cold-faced woman who had been conducting sacrificial rites in the third palace would not have shown mercy!","Tower Canon had long been aware of the demon insects’ existence.","The demon insects’ existence completely exceeded First Page Crimson and the rest’s expectations.","A rare species like the demon insects that could only come from the Sky Beyond the Clouds had appeared in a world that had only recently been promoted to Class 2.","The demon insects’ existence was a pesky problem for First Page Crimson and","the rest.","However, before the demon insects fully matured, Tower Canon could interfere with them. If they could follow the trail to the female insects, they would be able to eliminate the threat that the demon insects posed. They could even attempt to turn the demon insects into dead lifeforms and use them for their own purposes.","Logically, this was the time for Tower Canon to step in.","But there was still no movement on their end because they had noticed that Epoch God Palace was showing signs of taking action.","Ever since Tower Canon landed in the Class 1 world, Epoch God Palace had not made a move aside from the time Tower Canon sought them out to cause trouble.","This caused First Page Crimson and the rest to venture a guess. Could it be that Epoch God Palace did not want this main world to be combined with the dead world?","Perhaps this guess was the only explanation for how the demon insects appeared in this world.","Epoch God Palace’s sudden awakening caused Tower Canon to feel threatened.","At times like this, inaction was better than action.","Even taking the risk of allowing the demon insects to grow and spread was better than having to face Epoch God Palace.","At first, Tower Canon had a choice. They were not stuck in this Class 1 world.","Firstly, they could not bear to leave all that they had established in this Class 1 world. The Eight Pages of Tower Canon had put a lot of effort into infecting the main world’s ley lines with death aura.","Secondly, the true Eight Pages of Tower Canon had awakened but had yet to recover their power.","If they forcefully moved to another Class 2 world, there was a possibility that they would experience backlash from that Class 2 world.","With all these considerations, Tower Canon decided not to leave the Class 1 world and to fuse the dead world’s roots with this Class 1 world.","After making this decision, there was no way out for Tower Canon.","Otherwise, when the demon insects first appeared, the Eight Pages of Tower Canon would have personally gone to the Radiance Federation to cross swords with Lin Yuan!","When First Page Crimson saw that no one had anything to say, he announced his decision, “Even if we do eventually battle it out with Epoch God Palace, now is not the time. Since Epoch God Palace is making their move, they must be planning something. What we need to be doing is finding out their goal. We will only be able to make our decision after finding out what they are after.” First Page Crimson felt extremely wronged while he spoke.","But as he thought about the power that Epoch God Palace had displayed 6,000 years ago, he believed that this was the only way.","If they clashed against Epoch God Palace again, they would not be able to slumber for another 6,000 years while the dead world’s roots were fusing with this world. In the next 6,000 years, the dead world’s roots would likely end up absorbed by this Class 2 world’s roots instead!","Even Second Page Warbler Candle, who loved arguing unnecessarily with First Page Crimson, did not oppose him this time.","The only one who frowned was Fifth Page Falling Rainbow.. This was because she had yet to locate where her Tower of Falling Rainbow and Secret of the","Dead were!"]},{"number":2698,"title":"Chapter 2698 Epoch God Palace and the Saint!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2698 Epoch God Palace and the Saint!","The material used to build the Tower of Falling Rainbow had come with Tower Canon when they landed in this Class 1 world.","They still possessed a small amount of it, and it was sufficient to build another Tower of Falling Rainbow.","However, the other seven might not be willing to give her the rest of the resources.","First Page Crimson was the one in charge of resource allocation in Tower Canon. Otherwise, he would not have been the first to awaken after they all fell asleep together.","She could accept the loss of the Tower of Falling Rainbow, but the loss of the Secret of the Dead would affect the fusing of the dead world with the main world. She would also not be able to leverage the Secret of the Dead’s role in absorbing the main world’s roots to claim benefits.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had asked to search for the Tower of Falling Rainbow and Secret of the Dead more than once, but she had been shot down by the other members of Tower Canon each time for different reasons.","This infuriated Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, and she felt that her companions were colluding against her.","It was true that she was the cause of that incident thousands of years ago, but the eight of them had made the decision together. Yet, she always took the full brunt of the blame.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow was becoming increasingly displeased with Second Page Warbler Candle.","However, with Epoch God Palace showing signs of taking action, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow did not have the courage to leave to search for the Secret of the Dead.","“Crimson, it sounds like you want us to do nothing and allow the demon insects to grow. We already caught some demon insects with Class 3 Genetic Locks. After rehabilitating them, it can be said with certainty that these female insects are insect queens, at least!","“This world lacks resources and limits the demon insects’ development. But if we give them a month or two to build up themselves, it will become challenging for us to restrain them. These demon insects have a diet made up of dead lifeforms and death aura. They will severely delay the dead world’s roots’ consumption of this Class 2 world’s roots.”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow brought up the most pressing problem before casting her gaze at First Page Crimson.","She was not trying to seek his opinion. He had already decided to be a silent observer.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow just brought up one possible result, insinuating that First Page Crimson would have to take responsibility if something like that really took place.","First Page Crimson glanced at Fifth Page Falling Rainbow before saying, “Falling Rainbow, if I suggest that you be the one to kill these demon insects, will you be willing to do it?","“If Epoch God Palace is indeed taking action all of a sudden because we are using the dead world’s roots to consume this Class 2 world’s roots, trying to deal with the demon insects will give Epoch God Palace a reason to target you. But since you’re the one who posed this possibility yet is unwilling to go, who do you think should go instead?”","It went without saying that First Page Crimson would never take on such a responsibility.","Clearly, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow was unwilling to stick her neck out. Yet, she still opposed his opinion.","This made First Page Crimson livid.","Third Page Violet Light Green, who rarely spoke, cleared her throat. “It’s not the time to assign responsibilities. But we can’t keep cowering while we wait for Epoch God Palace to make their move, either.","“I think we should send someone to make contact with Epoch God Palace. If none of you are willing to do this, I’ll do it!”","Third Page Violet Light Green sighed.","Before landing in this Class 1 world, they were divided and only looked out for their interests during key moments. If they had been more united, they might have successfully combined the dead world with that Class 3 world’s roots.","After all this time, her companions had yet to learn their lesson. How pathetic!","First Page Crimson had always been the decision-maker of the group and liked to assert his status.","Yet, he was unwilling to step forward at such a moment.","Perhaps this was the reason why the rest of them could not follow his lead wholeheartedly.","Just as First Page Crimson was done speaking, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s hand pinched her with considerable force. Clearly, he did not want Third Page Violet Light Green to take such initiative.","First Page Crimson said, “Fine. Violet Light Green, since the idea came from you, you can be the one to represent Tower Canon to make contact with Epoch God Palace.”","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Second Page Warbler Candle voiced their agreement, while Sixth Page Wave Glow, Seventh Page Concubine Winding, and Eighth Page Eye Shadow remained silent, indicating that they were neither in agreement nor opposition.","When Fourth Page Cavity Orchid saw that Third Page Violet Light Green had no intention to retract her decision, he spoke up. “I’ll go with Violet Light Green to make contact with Epoch God Palace! Having two of us will show that Tower Canon is taking this matter seriously. We’ll also be able to look out for each other.”","Once he was done speaking, Fourth Page Cavity Orchid could not be bothered to linger and immediately returned to the black coffin, where he waited for Third Page Violet Light Green to come to see him.","...","After emerging from flying under the radar for such a long time, the four rulers of Epoch God Palace met up again at the garden at the top of Four Seasons Mountain.","Normally, their knights also listened in on the meetings conducted by the four rulers. However, only the four rulers were present in the garden today.","Each of the four rulers had a flushed face full of uncontrollable elation.","“Epoch God Palace has been waiting for such a long time. Now, we can finally be certain that Lord Saint is in this world. The prophecy was right! All our waiting was worth it!","“Lord Totem God has already entered the second form, and the totem seeds have formed. This means that Lord Saint has already developed the ability to become the master of all lifeforms.","“Given the circumstances, we can now begin searching for Lord Saint. We don’t have to worry about our actions affecting Lord Saint’s growth progress.”","The tall, slim girl with cold features and a slightly bitter voice gently shook her hand, causing the fallen flowers to fly to every corner of the mountain peak.","“I called this meeting to confirm three matters with the rest of you. The first is to decide how we will deal with Tower Canon. The second is how we plan on establishing contact with Lord Saint in a way that will convince him to accept us as his followers. The third is the matter of helping Lord Saint to open a path out of this world in advance. He is in possession of one of the six sacred mountains that represent the highest authority in the four major universes!”","The other three rulers’ faces fell.","It was indeed good that Lord Saint had awoken. However, making contact with him was a big problem. If he did not accept them as his followers, their existence would be pointless.","The elderly man with white hair but a strapping body said, “The best place to open the road from the main world to the Sky Beyond the Clouds is behind my palace. Let me handle the opening of the road! I have been growing my roots all these years. It should be enough to open the road!","“Spring and Summer can be the ones to search for Lord Saint. Autumn, many things that should appear in this world have appeared. Go and search for them and observe them.","“After I find Lord Saint and report the situation to him, he can decide what to do with them. I don’t think we need to discuss how to make contact with Lord Saint. All we need to do is maintain the sincere hearts of followers!","“We can’t control whether Lord Saint accepts us. It’s up to him. We can’t sway his thinking. What we should be discussing is how to handle Tower Canon.”","The elderly man coughed softly, and a drizzle of snow fell from his lips, covering the wildflowers on the top of the mountain.","The elderly man did not have a strong impression of Tower Canon. The only interaction they had with Tower Canon was when they barged in to try to steal the Epoch Clock that tracked the changing of epochs.","He was not concerned by these stragglers and vanquished from a dimensional world that used to be attached to a Class 3 world. The best that could be produced in a Class 3 world was intermediate faeries.","Although this elderly man was unbothered by this group, they had been identified as an unstable element. Epoch God Palace could not allow the structure of this world to be changed in case it hampered Lord Saint’s reincarnation and revival.","The elderly man could not decide if these destitute, uninvited guests were a key component that sped up Lord Saint’s reincarnation and revival.","Thus, Epoch God Palace had not annihilated this group that was biting off more than they could chew even after they attacked Epoch God Palace.","Instead, they blamed Spring for being too brutal and allowing this faction to hide for this long!","Now, Tower Canon was so much commotion immediately after awakening. There was not even a moment of peace!","Winter felt that Spring was bringing up this matter because she did not know if Tower Canon was truly linked to Lord Saint and if they were friends or foes.","Epoch God Palace came from another world and would not think on behalf of this world.","If they annihilated Tower Canon and it turned out that Tower Canon had a close relationship with Lord Saint, it would mean that they were making a mistake.","Despite being his followers, they were not helping to share his burdens but were causing trouble. This was a grave sin for all followers!","Autumn flicked his short hair, and his magnetic voice gave the air of fallen leaves floating on wind.","“I am most curious to find out how the demon insects ended up in this world. They require a large amount of pure spirit qi in order to propagate their aura. It will be difficult for even a Class 4 world to produce this concentration of spirit qi, much less a Class 2 world.","“There is definitely someone nurturing these demon insects. In my opinion, the only one capable of something like this is Lord Saint! I think that rather than searching for Lord Saint, we should follow the trail of the demon insects!","“Tower Canon has been silent ever since they attacked us. It’s clear that they fear us and are unaware of our objective. It won’t be long before they make contact with us. Given that the demon insects are fending off the dead spirits and dimensional worlds and trying to keep them from impacting this Class 2 world, it isn’t difficult to guess Lord Saint’s stance.”","Autumn paused momentarily before saying seriously, “Lord Saint is still growing. It will definitely affect his growth trajectory if we appear in front of him suddenly. I think our main objective should be discovering his identity before secretly protecting him and aiding his growth. It goes without saying that this will all change if Lord Saint initiates contact with us instead!”","All of them felt that Autumn’s analysis was reasonable. However, there were many things that could not be concluded based only on analysis!","Summer said gently, “I think Autumn and Winter make good suggestions. Spring and I will immediately begin secretly searching for Lord Saint. If Tower Canon makes contact with us, Autumn can handle them!”","This meeting on Four Seasons Mountain was very simple, and the expressions of delight did not disappear from their faces even for a moment.","...","While the four of them were in discussion, Lin Yuan had chosen the locations where he would place the Dead Decay Earthworms.","Lin Yuan’s lips twitched as he watched the Dead Decay Earthworm tunnel underground and begin absorbing death aura.","Liu Wencheng’s design for this selection was rather harsh.","The thousands of Dead Decay Earthworm tunneling underground and absorbing death aura seemed to be able to effectively lower the concentration of death aura in the area. But in actuality, the Dead Decay Earthworms would lose their effectiveness once the waves of dead spirits arrived.","This was because there were far too few Dead Decay Earthworms.","The Radiance Federation supplied the Dead Decay Earthworms to the Dead Spirits Wells in the tens of millions.","Additionally, there would also be dead dimensional lifeforms appearing in the test.","The dead dimensional lifeforms produced death aura that had a concentration higher than what the Dead Decay Earthworms could handle.","This was not because the Dead Decay Earthworms were incapable of absorbing the death aura but because the Dead Decay Earthworms were limited in their ability to process death aura.","One Dead Decay Earthworm could absorb the death aura from five dead spirits.","It was likely that 1,500 Dead Decay Earthworms were needed to absorb the death aura produced by one dead dimensional lifeform.","Due to this, the Radiance Federation still suffered serious losses against the waves of dead spirits despite facing the dead spirits crisis with preparations in place.","Lin Yuan didn’t underestimate A-rank spirit qi professionals. Even Xia Qing and Long Tao would find it challenging to withstand attacks from the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms for an extended period. This difficulty remained, even when they used their feys with the Barren bloodline.","Their task was made even harder as they had to protect others and prevent the participants of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection from succumbing to the dead spirits’ attacks and getting infected by the death aura.","After investigating the environment, Lin Yuan now knew what he was going to do later.","It was likely that Liu Jie had also made his own decision.","...","Thirty minutes passed very quickly, and Liu Wencheng finished his speech in Radiance Sacred Hall.","The young elites participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection entered Star Web’s test ground, just like Lin Yuan had done a year ago.","Immediately after entering, many members of the younger generation felt stifled while drawing breath."]},{"number":2699,"title":"Chapter 2699 Death-Drawing Bladderworm!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2699 Death-Drawing Bladderworm!","The best option for them would be to rush to the leaders and seek their protection so they could set up defenses against the waves of dead spirits together!","Hence, during this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, the participants did not immediately begin cutting each other down. Instead, they tried their best to form alliances and groups with those around them so they could prevent themselves from befalling any danger before they met up with the leaders.","This was extremely different from last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, where fights started breaking out immediately after the participants entered the test ground and resulted in many strong participants being eliminated at the beginning.","Those who were weak would not brashly fight the other competitors right out of the gate.","This year’s test might seem as though the participants were safe as long as they could band together and move through the area together. However, there were no lull periods. Aside from the air being concentrated with death aura, endless waves of dead spirits appeared even before the major explosion of dead spirits that would take place a day later.","Regardless of how strong the young spirit qi professionals were, they did not have much experience with outdoor survival, especially in such extreme environments.","Each time there was a new wave, the dead spirits that had been killed would contribute to the concentration of death aura in the environment.","In actuality, there would not be many participants who would be able to make it to Lin Yuan and the other leaders before the main part of the dead spirits crisis began.","Lin Yuan was not worried because he could protect the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members in such an environment.","However, it was likely that Liu Wencheng, who designed this test, had already discovered that he had set the bar too high.","Firstly, the test ground was twice as large as the previous year’s. This would make it even more difficult for the participants to search for the leaders.","It was acceptable to fill the environment with death aura. Still, Liu Wencheng clearly had not considered that the concentration of death aura would rise rapidly as more dead spirits and dimensional lifeforms died.","The Dead Decay Earthworms placed around the main areas were far from enough to lower the concentration of death aura.","The dead dimensional lifeforms were not truly feared because of their power but because of how they could affect the environment.","Just as Lin Yuan thought, Liu Wencheng soon realized that things were going wrong.","But at the same time, he knew that he could not stop this test now. If he did, it would be a huge blow to the Radiance Federation!","All of the Radiance citizens were watching the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","If he had another week to prepare, he would definitely have figured out through his testing that such an issue would arise. However, he had given up on testing due to the tight timeline.","Liu Wencheng’s heart pounded like a drum, and he was terrified that this test would leave no survivors.","Cicada Song sent a message through the Thoughts Letter Paper to ask Liu Wencheng about how things were going, and Liu Wencheng responded honestly.","Nonetheless, Cicada Song was not overly worried because he knew of Lin Yuan’s capabilities in handling the dead spirits.","If things were truly going awry, it was likely that Lin Yuan would release demon insects into the test ground to clear out the dead spirits.","It was not just Lin Yuan. Night Leaning Moon’s disciple also controlled some insect-species carcinoma feys that could ameliorate an environment filled with death aura. Night Leaning Moon had mentioned this during a previous imperial meeting.","It seemed that the success of this test now depended on Liu Jie and Lin Yuan.","...","On the first day, even teams of hundreds or even thousands of participants had their numbers greatly reduced whenever they encountered dead spirits.","Even if they started out with light injuries, their bodies would have already been infected with death aura that would continue to decay their muscles.","Regular healing-type feys were not effective in healing such injuries. Hence, every team that had tried to fill their ranks with healing-type spirit qi professionals eventually suffered major losses.","With no medical aid, many teams composed of hundreds of people were eliminated, while those composed of thousands of people winnowed down to only a few hundred members.","This was in spite of the fact that many of the teams were even working together.","All members of the teams were in extremely bad states and had ghastly faces. Blood dripped from their noses and ears in an almost never-ending stream. Those with more serious conditions were showing signs of losing their teeth despite only being around 20 years old.","The high concentration of death aura even made breathing a challenge.","Ever since Lin Yuan entered the test ground, he instructed the Source Sand to release a large amount of Close Guard Sand and Overlord Sand before creating more sand underground. The flowing sand beneath the test ground became Lin Yuan’s eyes and helped him to detect the environment.","Once Lin Yuan used the Source Sand to check on how the other teams were doing, he saw that things had already reached a severely terrible state. He knew that he had to step in.","However, he did not summon Red Thorn’s eight-winged fairy form.","An eight-winged fairy had never been seen in the main world before. Moreover, Red Thorn had not even reached Creation Breed.","Hence, revealing Red Thorn to the rest of the world would cause too much of a shock.","Red Thorn was a secret weapon Lin Yuan kept to himself.","Regardless of what the secret weapons were, they should not be revealed without careful consideration.","Hence, Lin Yuan waved his hand and released Red Thorn’s spores.","The spores were scattered around Lin Yuan, and carnivorous plants rapidly pushed out from the ground before continuing to elongate.","There were many specially mutated plants in the flowerbed that were spreading spores. The sea of flowers spread in a semicircular formation toward the other leaders.","Red Thorn was unable to allow the sea of flowers to spread freely as it would also affect the environment and occupy the living space of other lifeforms. Otherwise, Lin Yuan would have used the sea of flowers to manage the dead spirits crisis.","Once the sea of flowers was established, the gill-shaped flower petals of the large red flowers growing on the carnivorous vines opened and closed. Consequently, the concentration of death aura in the environment started to fall.","As a result, Wang Fan, Shi Xu, and the rest noticed that the air they were breathing had become cleaner and no longer felt as suffocated as before. However, they realized that their bodies had already become weaker due to being infected by death aura.","Long Tao had already instructed the Sea King Chalk Mosasaurus to create a territory of water that enveloped him and helped him fend off the death aura.","Xia Qing also used the Suck Burst Oxygen Toad and Misfortune Fighter to create a territory of fire to burn up the death aura in the environment.","Long Tao and Xia Qing were both bringing out their unique skills, but they knew they would be unable to hold on like this for too long.","Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers would be essential in helping them break free from the death aura’s invasion.","The sea of flowers could be considered Lin Yuan’s signature. It was what he had used to capture the attention of the masses when he had been Black.","Black had used the sea of flowers to handle the wave of alien insects in Millstone Town. He had also used the sea of flowers multiple times during his battles on Star Tower.","During the last Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, the waves of dimensional lifeforms had only been restrained through the coordination of the seas of sand and flowers.","Naturally, Lin Yuan’s action immediately stoked enthusiastic debate on Star Web.","[No Wind or Rain]: Wow! Black has once again summoned the sea of flowers! With this sea of flowers, there is no way the dead spirits will be able to invade! If the participants are lucky enough to reach Black, they will definitely be able to rely on his defense to survive the dead spirits!","[Beach]: I have been waiting for the sea of flowers to appear. I have been his fan for the past two years! When I first became his fan, I was already certain that he would be able to make it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence. With the sea of flowers, all the participants need to do is hide behind it, and they will make it to the end.","[Ringing Cat]: Weren’t any of you paying attention to Lord Liu Wencheng when he read out the rules? There will be a lot of stress if they choose to stay around Black! How will they distinguish themselves if they don’t need to do anything? Dying on Star Web will not lead to dying in real life. As long as they demonstrate themselves during this test, they will likely be picked by the Spirit Guards. At the very least, they will become popular enough to become a combat host on Star Web.","[Look at Your Bearish Appearance]: I agree! The stronger the leader they join, the more difficult it will be for them to demonstrate their abilities. Look at Lord Liu Jie’s area, things are happening!","...","Like Lin Yuan, Liu Jie carefully investigated the environment and realized the irregularities. Liu Jie did not come up with a plan immediately. Instead, he asked Lin Yuan questions through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Liu Jie only began acting after he learned of Lin Yuan’s decision.","Liu Jie summoned the Hypha Tapeworm again, and the carpet of fungi began expanding rapidly in front of Liu Jie.","The carpet of fungi formed a ring and linked up with the sea of flowers, shielding the four members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence that Liu Jie was in charge of protecting.","The carpet of fungi formed by the Hypha Tapeworm only created a combat area that was suitable for the activities of the army of insects.","If any insect was injured or died, the tapeworms could immediately make use of the insect bodies.","Liu Jie had two feys that could transform death aura. They were the Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects and Death-Drawing Bladderworm.","The Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects were also insect-species carcinoma feys that could alter their environment.","The two Diamond/Legend Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects began reproducing on the carpet of fungi. They transformed the various types of energy in the air and soil into soil that was beneficial for insects.","Death aura was also considered a type of energy.","Although the Earth-Wrecking Old Burial Insects’ ability to transform energy was not strong, they did manage to significantly lower the concentration of death aura in the surrounding environment.","After all, the large-scale explosion of dead spirits had yet to happen.","But even if it did happen and the large number of dead dimensional lifeforms released death aura into the environment, Liu Jie would not panic.","In actuality, Liu Jie was even more capable at treating death aura than Lin Yuan because he had the insect-species carcinoma fey called the Death-Drawing Bladderworm.","The Death-Drawing Bladderworm was an insect-species carcinoma fey that the Spirit Guards had collected, and its danger level was only B. This meant that it had been assigned the lowest danger level possible.","The Radiance Federation began had developing the Pestilence Marsh in the west. They had intended to use the poisonous miasma and death aura from the large number of dead lifeforms that were present in the Pestilence Marsh to nurture special feys.","But before the base was built, a strange phenomenon had occurred.","All of the death aura had disappeared from the Pestilence Marsh, and only poisonous miasma had been left.","This had affected the Radiance Federation’s plan to nurture special feys.","The Spirit Guards had sent out a Guard Envoy and two special teams. Eventually, they discovered the Death-Drawing Bladderworm.","The Death-Drawing Bladderworm could absorb death aura and use the strong cystic membrane in its body to envelop the death aura. It would then compress and purify the death aura before storing it.","The Spirit Guards had not believed the Death-Drawing Bladderworm to pose significant danger.","They only collected the Death-Drawing Bladderworm because it was an insect-species carcinoma fey.","When Liu Jie and Night Leaning Moon first started selecting insect-species carcinoma feys, they had not considered the Death-Drawing Bladderworm at all.","The Death-Drawing Bladderworm only stood out from the rest of the insect-species carcinoma feys and was selected to be controlled by Elegance after the dead spirits crisis descended.","Night Leaning Moon hoped that Liu Jie would turn the Death-Drawing Bladderworm into a fairy so it could treat the death aura-concentrated environment.","After all, regular Diamond insect-species carcinoma feys could not be compared to Suzerain/Myth insect-species carcinoma feys.","However, Lin Yuan had stopped Liu Jie.","This was not because Lin Yuan did not acknowledge the Death-Drawing Bladderworm’s abilities.","The Death-Drawing Bladderworm’s ability to absorb death aura was powerful. However, it could not reproduce in large numbers.","Even when the Death-Drawing Bladderworm evolved to Myth Breed, it could only produce an army of thousands of offspring.","As a result, it would only be able to lower the concentration of death aura in a small area and would not be able to make a large impact on the dead spirits crisis.","Rather, it would be a waste of one of the Firefly Demon Fetuses.","Turning the Death-Drawing Bladderworm into a fairy would not increase Liu Jie’s power in the slightest.","A Suzerain/Myth Death-Drawing Bladderworm would only be comparable to a few thousand of the Dead Decay Earthworms.","The Dead Decay Earthworms were extremely skilled at reproducing. The army of Hundred Questions Beasts were also continuing to do research into feys that could treat death aura.","Hence, there was no need for Liu Jie to make such a sacrifice.","After listening to Lin Yuan’s suggestion, Liu Jie did not transform the Death-Drawing Bladderworm into a fairy.","However, with the size of the Star Web test ground, a Suzerain Death-Drawing Bladderworm could be extremely effective.","The Death-Drawing Bladderworm’s mother body was around the size of a palm, and its body was translucent and gray. It looked like an exquisite art piece.","When it absorbed death aura, the Death-Drawing Bladderworm’s abdomen expanded continuously.","The concentrated gray and black death aura would be compressed while the Death-Drawing Bladderworm grew until the vesicle case eventually expelled it.","Liu Jie carefully collected the vesicle filled with death aura to prevent the death aura within from contaminating the environment again."]},{"number":2700,"title":"Chapter 2700: Escalation of the Radiance Hundred Sequence Selection!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2700: Escalation of the Radiance Hundred Sequence Selection!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","When the Death-Drawing Bladderworm was purifying death aura, it did not lower the amount of death aura in the environment. All it did was extract the impurities in the dead aura.","Pure death aura was far deadlier than impure death aura.","Once the vesicle case was broken, Liu Jie would cause issues rather than be of help.","Not even Liu Jie would be able to handle being infected by pure death aura, much less the younger members participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Both Liu Jie and Lin Yuan had demonstrated their capabilities. The sea of flowers and colony of insects were akin to two impenetrable defensive nets that had wrapped around the main areas where the ten leaders were located.","Furthermore, the sea of flowers and colony of insects were expanding continuously.","Liu Wencheng’s tightly furrowed brows relaxed when he saw this.","With Lin Yuan and Liu Jie’s capabilities and the rate at which the death aura was being treated, this test of heightened difficulty could be completed successfully.","In actuality, Liu Wencheng’s decision to raise the difficulty was also related to","Liu Jie, Xia Qing, Long Tao, and the rest. Because he was aware of their powers, he was afraid that the intensity of the test would not be sufficient to achieve its intended effects.","Aside from Liu Wencheng, the other members of royalty, Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, and the rest, who were aware of how harmful death aura could be, knew that Liu Wencheng’s test design was unreasonable.","However, the Radiance Federation’s younger generation being tested had no idea.","All of them were braving the abuse and doing their best to search for the locations of the leaders. Every one of them was displaying exceptional determination.","There were even a few of them who had feys that demonstrated a resistance to death aura.","One of the participant’s light-type feys was even able to cleanse death aura!","Cleansing was a light-type ability that rarely manifested in feys. It could dispel dirt and impurities.","Venom and death aura were all deemed as dirt and impurities by light-type feys.","The contractor of the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane became a prominent figure and was seen as a shining light of hope by all of the participants.","However, Yang Nuanxin was completely unaware of this.","Being in the midst of the test, she did not have a bird-eye view and did not know that a spotlight was now shining on her because of the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane. Famous Star Web hosts had already mentioned her name and commentators multiple times.","If she did know, she would definitely be overjoyed.","However, at that moment, Yang Nuanxin was in a state of conflict.","Two teams were fighting over her. One was a team formed by her schoolmates. The other was a team formed by a distant cousin from the main branch of her family.","Yang Nuanxin had an indecisive personality, especially when it involved emotional matters.","She did not want to abandon her schoolmates when she could be of help to them. However, there was more to consider aside from emotions when it came to her cousin. It related to the direct benefits and status within her family.","Although the main branch of a middle-sized faction could not control the lives of the collateral branches, it could supervise them and restrict their inflow of resources.","Yang Nuanxin could not guarantee that she would be able to stand out during the selection and become a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Hence, she could not afford to burn the bridge between herself and her cousin.","Before she could make her decision, the young man on her left grabbed her arm and growled, “Nuanxin, why are you hesitating? What are you doing just standing there when I need you? There are only 300 to 400 people left in your team. There’s no way they can protect you.","“After encountering the dead spirits twice, there are still more than 800 people left in my team. We also have two spirit qi professionals with feys that had similar abilities to the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane.","“If you join me, the three of you will receive the team’s full protection. You won’t have to clear the dead spirits. All you need to do is cleanse the death aura in the surroundings.”","A vicious glint appeared in this short-haired young man’s eyes.","Everyone knew that it was best not to get into conflicts with the other participants during this test that involved fighting dead spirits. In this environment where the humans and dead spirits were battling for dominance, any cracks in their unity would negatively impact the humans.","However, killing intent had taken form in Yang Wenpeng’s mind. This was not only directed toward Yang Nuanxin’s schoolmates but Yang Nuanxin as well.","This brat from the collateral branch had the gall to step on his pride. Even after extending repeated invitations to her, she continued to be wishy-washy. This was a blow to his clout.","He had invested a lot of thought and effort before gathering his teammates and securing the team’s leader position.","Once his clout was compromised, he would be replaced as the leader.","Many people in the team were gunning for this.","Frankly, there was another course of action that Yang Wenpeng could take, which was to invite Yang Nuanxin’s schoolmates as well. The issue would be resolved as long as he could convince them to join his team.","However, Yang Wenpeng despised Yang Nuanxin’s schoolmates.","A tall and skinny man whose hair reached his earlobes said mockingly, “Wenpeng, isn’t this your cousin from a collateral branch of the family? Who knew that you have so little sway as a member of the family’s main branch? A member of the collateral branch isn’t even willing to listen to you!”","The tall and skinny young man whose hair reached his earlobes was one of","Yang Wenpeng’s rivals and had been secretly working against him in the team.","Yang Wenpeng had managed to hold his ground in their past few confrontations. Still, his rival was now seizing his window of opportunity and was trying to use this situation to disparage Yang Wenpeng’s formidability.","The tall and skinny young man was well aware that a large-scale clash between the two teams would definitely affect one of the participants’ evaluations.","Yang Wenpeng was irritable and could not handle being provoked.","If he could trigger a fight between Yang Wenpeng and the other team, Yang Wenpeng might be able to retain his clout, but his impression in the eyes of the members of royalty would be blemished.","This would allow Wei Haodong to kick one of his threatening rivals out of the running.","Wei Haodong thought himself to be extremely intelligent, but he had no idea that two members of royalty were already frowning at his provocative behavior.","Wei Haodong might have failed to deduce the members of royalty’s perspectives, but he had successfully grasped Yang Wenpeng’s character.","Yang Wenpeng was already on the brink of exploding with anger. His grip on Yang Nuanxin’s wrist increased in strength, and she felt pain shoot up her wrist.","Yang Nuanxin was not very familiar with Yang Wenpeng.","The Yang family’s main branch rarely interacted with the collateral branches, and it was difficult for the collateral branches to catch the attention of the main branch.","Nonetheless, Yang Nuanxin had heard rumors about the Yang family’s Eldest Young Master Yang Wenpeng. He was bad-tempered and easily agitated. Many members of collateral branches had met with horrible ends after offending him.","If she did not agree to his invitation, her parents and sister would end up suffering!","At the thought of her parents and sister, Yang Nuanxin made her decision. She had no choice but to abandon her schoolmates and join her cousin.","Just as she was about to make her decision known, the leader of her schoolmates’ team stepped out.","“Haha, your team is still left with so many people after encountering the dead spirits twice while we lost many of our members to just one wave of the dead spirits. If we didn’t have Nuanxin with us to help us cleanse the air, at least 40 more of our team members would have died.","“The dead spirits are our common enemy. We still don’t know where the ten leaders are. We don’t even know if we are headed in the right direction. Why don’t we join forces? There is power in numbers.","“Since you have more people on your team, you can have the decision-making power. We only want to retain the right to separate from you if we don’t agree with your opinions. What do you think of this proposition?”","The person who spoke was a young man with a buzz cut. He was rotund and had a very contagious smile.","This tempted Yang Wenpeng. After this team of more than 300 people joined him, his team would comprise more than 1,200 members. They would be able to hold on even after encountering another two waves of dead spirits.","The young man’s statements were true.","Yang Wenpeng did not know where the ten members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence were selected or if he was even going in the right direction.","Given the situation, the more power he controlled, the better.","After the team of more than 300 people joined, all Yang Wenpeng needed to do was suggest that they reform teams, and he would be able to disrupt them. Even if he gave them the autonomy to leave when they wanted, they could not use it!","“Go and inform your subordinates then. We will join forces and head north!”","While Yang Wenpeng and Du Xing were communicating, Wei Haodong frowned and glared at Du Xing.","This fatty was ruining his plan!","He had already agitated Yang Wenpeng and was a hair’s breadth away from his goal.","As the leader of a team with more than 1,200 members, Yang Wenpeng had to have hidden skills.","Wei Haodong did not know that Night Leaning Moon had already eliminated him and Yang Wenpeng despite not having died yet.","Rather, Du Xing, who was able to sacrifice some of his profits for the team’s sake, showed more leadership qualities.","Night Leaning Moon decided to keep an eye on Du Xing.","Yang Nuanxin looked at Du Xing gratefully. His decision meant that she did not need to explicitly choose Yang Wenpeng and abandon her schoolmates.","The team of more than 1,000 people would allow Yang Nuanxin to unleash the","Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s abilities to a greater extent and allow her to stand out even more in the test.","Du Xing gave his team simple instructions before they joined forces with the other team.","Du Xing’s expression had not changed. It still carried amicability and a smile.","But in actuality, he was complaining to himself. This feeling of being coerced was not pleasant at all. However, it was the only choice that his team could take.","This Radiance Hundred Sequence selection was a miniature version of a society living in the dead spirits crisis. With every passing second, there were teams fighting each other, as well as others that were joining forces.","There were constantly capable, intelligent, and powerful people distinguishing themselves during this test and capturing the audience’s attention on Star Web.","In such an environment, power, character, and other qualities that made up a person were being displayed through the constant clashes and cooperation.","Those in the midst of the test had no idea that every one of their actions was being broadcast.","The Moon Empress nodded to herself. She approved of this broadcasting method and conducted the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","The Radiance Federation already intended to turn the members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence into the standard and the pillars of the Radiance Federation.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members needed to be supervised.","The Radiance citizens were all judges of the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s members.","The Moon Empress did not observe the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection from the beginning.","She had just finished participating in the second meeting of the Major Federation Union.","The main theme of the last Major Federation Union meeting was for the Radiance Federation to inform the other federations of the imminent arrival of the dead spirits crisis.","The main theme of this Major Federation Union meeting was the other federations asking the Radiance Federation for help.","The Moon Empress had already decided to help them.","The demon insects were reproducing at a rate that was beyond the Moon Empress’ imagination. They could now be delivered to the other parts of the main world.","Due to the urgency of the matter, the Moon Empress decided not to try to control the federation leaders and directly announced that the Radiance Federation would be helping the other federations.","During the last Major Federation Union meeting, the other federations were afraid of the Radiance Federation’s power. But this time, they were reliant on the Radiance Federation and saw them as their last hope.","The Moon Empress could sense this.","As the Radiance Federation continued supplying help to the other federations, this attitude would become the norm, and the Radiance Federation would become the true head of all the federations!","The Mirror God and God of Fools had had conflicted emotions throughout the entire Major Federation Union meeting. They were the strongest experts in all the federations, after all.","Although the Spacetime Elder had also set his spirit fire alight, his soul was tied to the Radiance Federation, so he could never leave and had to protect the federation forever.","As long as they did not enter the Radiance Federation, they would not have to worry about being bothered by the Spacetime Elder.","But the sudden explosion of dimensional lifeforms from the Class 6 marsh dimensional rift into the Freedom Federation had left them in dire straits, and they had had no choice but to ally with the Radiance Federation.","Yet, it turned out that the Radiance Federation had commandeered the marsh dimensional lifeforms and had turned them into captives.","Even now, the Mirror God and God of Fools felt as though they were dreaming.","However, too many things had happened recently. The Radiance Federation’s saving of the main world caused the Mirror God and God of Fools to submit to the Moon Empress, as well as her all-powerful disciple.","The Mirror God and God of Fools did their best to help the Moon Empress with the Major Federation Union’s affairs and alleviated a significant portion of her burdens.","The two of them dutifully allowed the Moon Empress and the rest of the Radiance Federation’s royalty to have the decision-making power.","They also resolved to change the Freedom Federation.","With the dead spirits crisis as a form of cleansing, the Freedom Federation would become a completely new federation.","The Azure Federation’s 12 aristocratic families had all arrived in the Radiance Federation in order to express their respect for the Moon Empress and noticed the Mirror God and God of Fools’ changes.."]}]);
